E["item:altered-snapjaw-shell"] = {t="item",n="Altered Snapjaw Shell",z="barrens",s="At the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases, snapjaws bear altered shells that draw a druid’s attention. Their carapaces may reveal what the fissures beneath the Barrens are doing to local wildlife.",h="At the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases, snapjaws bear altered shells that draw a druid’s attention.",sec={{t="Signs of Corruption",b="Oasis snapjaws have changed in ways that trouble those who study the land. The freshwater turtles of Lushwater and Stagnant Oases are believed to drink from springs fed by mysterious underground fissures. Their altered carapaces have caught the attention of researchers at the Crossroads. Tonga Runetotem, a tauren druid, gathers the shells as he seeks to understand the land’s health. He wants to learn whether energies rising from deep below are an unnatural blight or something stranger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes these turtle shells altered?",a="The snapjaws live in springs at the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases, fed by deep subterranean fissures. Strange energies rising into the water have changed the creatures that drink there, leaving their carapaces visibly warped.",al={"why are shells altered","what is altered snapjaw shell","snapjaw shell mutation"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants these shells and why?",a="Tonga Runetotem, a druid at the Crossroads, asks hunters to gather the shells. He believes changes in native beasts can help reveal what power or corruption is affecting the Barrens’ water supply.",al={"who needs altered snapjaw shells","tonga runetotem shells","altered beings quest turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these snapjaws found?",a="Oasis snapjaws live in the waters and muddy shores of Lushwater Oasis and Stagnant Oasis, south and southeast of the Crossroads.",al={"oasis snapjaw location","where to get altered shells","snapjaw shell locations"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Where do altered snapjaw shells come from?",a="These carapaces belong to the oasis snapjaws dwelling around the freshwater springs of the Barrens, notably the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases. Rather than normal turtle carapaces, their strange state stems from drinking water contaminated or empowered by mysterious fissures beneath the oases, physically mutating the creatures who live there.",al={"where do altered snapjaw shells come from","altered snapjaw shell source","who made altered snapjaw shells"},it="origin",add="1549c45f"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can study the twisted carapaces of oasis beasts to help identify the hidden imbalance disturbing the Barrens’ waters."},kw={"altered beings","altered snapjaw shell","barrens","lushwater oasis","oasis snapjaw","stagnant oasis","tonga runetotem"},rel={"quest:880","npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},src={"Altered Snapjaw Shell","Altered Beings (Classic)"}}
E["item:baron-longshore-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Baron Longshore's Head",z="barrens",s="Along the Merchant Coast, Baron Longshore's Head proves the pirate captain's death. Gazlowe posted a public bounty for Longshore's identifiable remains to protect Ratchet's commercial shipping.",h="Along the Merchant Coast, Baron Longshore's Head proves the pirate captain's death.",sec={{t="A Price on a Buccaneer",b="Baron Longshore led Southsea Freebooter raids from camps along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet. His flagship, the Heedless, threatened goblin trade lanes between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Gazlowe, Ratchet's Chief Engineer, offered a bounty for identifiable proof of Longshore's death. The port authority pays a monetary reward when the pirate's head is delivered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Baron Longshore?",a="Baron Longshore was a pirate captain from the human kingdom of Gilneas. He led Southsea Freebooters from camps along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet and terrorized shipping lanes aboard the Heedless.",al={"baron longshore","who is longshore","captain longshore"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Baron Longshore's head?",a="Gazlowe, Ratchet's goblin leader, posted a public bounty for Baron Longshore's identifiable remains. The Southsea Freebooters preyed on Ratchet's merchant vessels, and Gazlowe wanted the harbor's trade to remain uninterrupted.",al={"who wants the head","who turned in to","gazlowe bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Baron Longshore found?",a="Baron Longshore patrols three Southsea pirate encampments on the coastline south of Ratchet, just north of Northwatch Hold along the Merchant Coast.",al={"where is longshore","longshore location","baron longshore spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What ship did Baron Longshore command?",a="Baron Longshore captained the Heedless, which raided merchant ships on the Great Sea off the Barrens coast.",al={"longshore ship","the heedless","heedless ship"},it="history"},{q="What is Baron Longshore's Head?",a="It is the gruesome, severed head of Baron Longshore, a notorious pirate captain from Gilneas who commands vessels for the Southsea Freebooters. You take it as irrefutable proof of his death to fulfill the bounty posted against him in Ratchet, ensuring that the Steamwheedle Cartel knows the infamous raider will trouble their merchant shipping lanes no longer.",al={"baron longshore head item","what is this head","longshore head lore"},it="item",add="0986c9c0"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can trace Baron Longshore's origins to Gilneas, the isolationist nation he left before joining the Southsea Freebooters."},kw={"baron longshore","bounty","gazlowe","gilneas","heedless","merchant coast","ratchet","southsea freebooters"},rel={"quest:895","subzone:merchant-coast","subzone:ratchet","quest:887","zone:barrens"},src={"Baron Longshore's Head","WANTED: Baron Longshore"}}
E["item:bristleback-quilboar-tusk"] = {t="item",n="Bristleback Quilboar Tusk",z="barrens",s="Across the northern and central Barrens, Bristleback Quilboar Tusks are taken from slain quilboar. Mankrik gathers them as proof of slaughter and tokens of vengeance.",h="Across the northern and central Barrens, Bristleback Quilboar Tusks are taken from slain quilboar.",sec={{t="Trophies of Vengeance",b="Bristleback quilboar defend their territory across the Barrens against Horde expansion. Their jagged ivory tusks serve as weapons in close combat. Mankrik, a veteran orc warrior stationed at the Crossroads, lost his wife in a vicious quilboar ambush. He gathers dozens of tusks as retribution, a bloody count of the suffering he means to return to the Bristlebacks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants these tusks?",a="Mankrik, an orc warrior at the Crossroads in the Barrens, wants the tusks. He seeks vengeance against the Bristleback quilboar after an ambush separated him from his wife.",al={"who needs bristleback tusks","who takes bristleback quilboar tusk","tusk turn in"}},{q="Why does Mankrik want so many tusks?",a="After quilboar raiders overwhelmed Mankrik and left him for dead, he was consumed by grief and fury. Sixty tusks give him proof that the Bristleback tribe is being culled in return.",al={"why 60 tusks","why does mankrik want tusks","mankrik revenge"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which quilboar carry these tusks?",a="Members of the Bristleback tribe carry these tusks in the northern and central scrublands and bramble camps of the Barrens.",al={"where do bristleback tusks drop","who drops bristleback quilboar tusk"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Do these tusks serve any purpose other than Mankrik's vendetta?",a="Mankrik gathers these trophies solely for vengeance. Quilboar tusks can sometimes become tribal trinkets or trade goods, but these are not put to those uses.",al={"bristleback tusk uses","can you craft with quilboar tusks"},it="item"},{q="What is a Bristleback Quilboar Tusk?",a="These are the severed tusks taken from slain Bristleback quilboar roaming the Barrens. To the quilboar, they are natural features and marks of ferocity, but to hunters in the plains, they serve as gruesome physical proof of another dead beast.",al={"bristleback quilboar tusk","what is bristleback quilboar tusk","bristleback tusk"},it="identity",add="a893c973"},{q="Where does a Bristleback Quilboar Tusk come from?",a="They are harvested directly from the jaws of Bristleback quilboar throughout the Barrens. Quilboar naturally grow these sharp tusks, and taking them requires cutting them from fallen enemies after battle.",al={"where do bristleback tusks come from","who drops bristleback quilboar tusk","source of bristleback quilboar tusk"},it="origin",add="fe8719fb"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The quilboar threaten the Crossroads and supply trails across the Barrens. Gathering tusks serves Mankrik's vendetta and the Horde's effort to pacify the region.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the weight of blood debts and a warrior's grief. Mankrik's pursuit of sixty quilboar trophies touches a shared sense of honor."},kw={"barrens","bristleback","consumed by hatred","crossroads","mankrik","quilboar","tusk"},rel={"npc:mankrik","quest:899","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads"},src={"Bristleback Quilboar Tusk","Consumed by Hatred (Classic)"}}
E["item:broken-samophlange"] = {t="item",n="Broken Samophlange",z="barrens",s="In the northern Barrens, a broken samophlange draws the notice of curious engineers. Its gears and shifting parts hint at a purpose no one has uncovered.",h="In the northern Barrens, a broken samophlange draws the notice of curious engineers.",sec={{t="A Baffling Mechanism",b="The broken samophlange is a baffling contraption from the northern Barrens. Its moving assemblies and fine gears show careful workmanship, even in ruin. Sputtervalve, a goblin in Ratchet, damaged the delicate device by accident before anyone could document how it worked. The finder hoped to send working results to curious colleagues in Undermine, so they sought someone able to repair it. Wenikee Boltbucket, a clever tinkerer near the border outpost of Mor'shan Rampart, was the one they turned to.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Tinkerer's Hands",b="Wenikee Boltbucket cannot tell what a samophlange is meant to do, even after examining its ruined parts. Its clockwork sounds and shifting motion catch her interest, though. Rather than discard it as junk, she sets out to repair the device and see its mechanisms working at full capacity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a samophlange?",a="Even the tinkerers trying to repair a samophlange cannot say what it does. Its name offers no answer, but its intricate gears and moving parts point to some unknown industrial purpose.",al={"samophlange purpose","what does a samophlange do","samophlange definition"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the samophlange broken?",a="Sputtervalve, the goblin in Ratchet, damaged the delicate machinery while tampering with the device brought to him. The samophlange seized before its secrets could be shared with colleagues in Undermine, so they sought an expert to get it working again.",al={"how did it break","broken samophlange lore"}},{q="Who is Wenikee Boltbucket?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket is an inquisitive tinkerer in the northern Barrens, just south of Mor'shan Rampart on the Ashenvale border. Her engineering curiosity leads her to inspect and rebuild strange contraptions.",al={"where is wenikee","boltbucket location"}},{q="Why are goblins in Undermine interested in it?",a="Goblin engineers and entrepreneurs are eager to study unusual mechanical technology. Word of the device reached contacts in Undermine, who were intrigued by whatever advantages it might offer.",al={"undermine interest","why do goblins care"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For an engineer, the samophlange is an irresistible puzzle: a machine with delicate inner gears whose purpose may emerge only by taking it apart and getting it running.",["faction:Horde"]="The device turns up in Horde territory in the Barrens, bringing local outposts, tinkerers, and neutral trading contacts into cooperation."},kw={"barrens","broken samophlange","gears","mor'shan rampart","samophlange","undermine","wenikee boltbucket"},rel={"quest:3921","quest:894","subzone:mor-shan-rampart","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},src={"Broken Samophlange","Wenikee Boltbucket (Classic)"}}
E["item:bundle-of-hides"] = {t="item",n="Bundle of Hides",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, a Bundle of Hides travels toward Thunder Bluff with the Horde’s wind riders. The cured skins are a straightforward courier shipment for the leatherworkers, and their delivery introduces travelers to the wind rider network.",h="Across the Barrens, a Bundle of Hides travels toward Thunder Bluff with the Horde’s wind riders.",sec={{t="Frontier Trade",b="Hunters skin the beasts of the Barrens for cured hides. The plains hold vast herds of kodo, prowling lions, and roving raptors. These skins supply the leatherworkers of Thunder Bluff, who turn them into gear, pouches, armor, and bindings for the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Skyward Freight",b="Couriers carry the bundle from the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff on Devrak’s trained wyverns. Overland travel through the Barrens and into Mulgore is slow and dangerous, with roaming quilboar and centaur raiders. Handing the hides to a wind rider courier shows how swiftly air travel can cross Kalimdor’s fractured terrain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Bundle of Hides used for?",a="The Bundle of Hides carries skins gathered from animals across the Barrens to Ahanu, a leatherworker in Thunder Bluff. He makes leather goods and armaments for the tauren and their Horde allies.",al={"bundle of hides purpose","why transport hides","what are hides for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who receives the shipment in Thunder Bluff?",a="Ahanu receives the parcel at Hewa’s Armory, directly at the base of Thunder Bluff’s wind rider roost.",al={"who gets the hides","bundle of hides recipient","where is ahanu"}},{q="Why send this bundle via a wind rider?",a="The Crossroads-to-Thunder Bluff journey on foot takes days and risks ambush by centaur or quilboar. Devrak, the Crossroads flight master, carries the goods atop a wind rider so they arrive swiftly and safely.",al={"why fly hides","crossroads flight hides","devrak wind rider"},it="purpose"},{q="Who prepared the bundle in the Barrens?",a="Jahan Hawkwing prepared the bundle from animals of the Barrens. He is a leather and mail armor merchant at the Crossroads and a colleague of Ahanu.",al={"who gave the hides","jahan hides","who gathered the pelts"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Bundle of Hides?",a="The Bundle of Hides is a packaged shipment of raw pelts gathered from the wild beasts roaming the Barrens. Collected and prepared locally near the Crossroads, it serves as crucial crafting material intended for export to Thunder Bluff, where skilled leatherworkers turn tough frontier skins into armor, clothing, and essential trade goods.",al={"what is bundle of hides","bundle of hides item","bundle of hides lore"},it="identity",add="2b9c2280"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Simple shipments like pelts cross the sky on wyvern flight paths, binding isolated Horde outposts directly to sovereign capital cities.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you rely on natural materials and reverent hunting, turning hides from the neighboring savanna into armor and crafts sold in Mulgore’s stalls."},kw={"ahanu","barrens","bundle of hides","crossroads","devrak","hewa's armory","jahan","leatherworking","thunder bluff","wind rider"},rel={"quest:6361","quest:6362","npc:ahanu","npc:devrak","subzone:crossroads","zone:thunderbluff","zone:barrens"},src={"Bundle of Hides","A Bundle of Hides (Classic)","Ride to Thunder Bluff (Classic)"}}
E["item:cats-eye-emerald"] = {t="item",n="Cats Eye Emerald",z="barrens",s="In the northern Barrens, the Cats Eye Emerald has drawn the eye of Ratchet's Wharfmaster Dizzywig. Venture Company bosses keep the fist-sized gem under guard at Boulder Lode Mine.",h="In the northern Barrens, the Cats Eye Emerald has drawn the eye of Ratchet's Wharfmaster Dizzywig.",sec={{t="A Fist-Sized Fortune",b="Venture Company laborers struck a massive emerald at Boulder Lode Mine, northeast of the Sludge Fen. Word of the find spread quickly across the savanna. In goblin country, rare gemstones seldom stay secret. Trade gossip carried news from Ratchet's docks to Booty Bay, and Wharfmaster Dizzywig heard of the prize. He began plotting to send it to the open market in Undermine.",sp=0},{t="Company Possession",b="Venture Company management keeps the emerald inside the mine under heavy guard. Overseers, Enforcers, and chief operators such as Boss Copperplug defend it from rival cartels and fortune-hunters. Dizzywig has promised a fifty-percent cut to those who help him secure the gem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Cats Eye Emerald?",a="The Cats Eye Emerald is an unusually huge emerald, about the size of a fist, found by miners in the northern Barrens. Its clarity and size make it worth a fortune on the global market.",al={"what is cats eye emerald","cats eye gem","what kind of gem is this"},it="identity"},{q="Where was the gem discovered?",a="Venture Company miners unearthed the gem inside Boulder Lode Mine, northeast of the Sludge Fen in the northern Barrens.",al={"where was it found","gem location","boulder lode mine emerald"},it="place"},{q="Who wants the emerald in Ratchet?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig, who oversees shipping and cargo at Ratchet's docks, wants the stone for wealthy buyers through Undermine trading connections.",al={"who buys the emerald","dizzywig emerald","who gives quest for emerald"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who holds onto the stone inside the mine?",a="Senior Venture Company supervisors hold the emerald inside Boulder Lode Mine. One of the Venture Co. overseers or enforcers carries it.",al={"who drops the emerald","who has the cats eye emerald","where to find cats eye emerald"},it="target"},{q="Where did the Cats Eye Emerald come from?",a="The Cats Eye Emerald is a natural, fist-sized gemstone unearthed deep within the Boulder Lode Mine, a Venture Company excavation northeast of the Sludge Fen in the Barrens. Rather than an artifact forged or cut by an artisan, it was recently dug out of the earth by one of the goblin company's luckier miners.",al={"cats eye emerald origin","where was cats eye emerald found","who made cats eye emerald"},it="origin",add="24f13ef4"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, finding a pristine, fist-sized gem in an industrial dig like Boulder Lode Mine is the lucky strike every miner dreams of.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, stealing an immense gem from under the noses of corrupt Venture Company taskmasters is a chance for opportunism."},kw={"boss copperplug","boulder lode mine","cats eye emerald","emerald","ratchet","sludge fen","venture company","wharfmaster dizzywig"},rel={"quest:896","subzone:boulder-lode-mine","subzone:ratchet","topic:venture-company","subzone:sludge-fen","quest:1492","zone:barrens","subzone:booty-bay"},src={"Cats Eye Emerald","Miner's Fortune (Classic)"}}
E["item:centaur-bracers"] = {t="item",n="Centaur Bracers",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, Centaur Bracers are stripped from slain Kolkar warriors. Regthar Deathgate gathers them west of the Crossroads as proof that centaur raiders have been culled.",h="Across the Barrens, Centaur Bracers are stripped from slain Kolkar warriors.",sec={{t="A Gritty Bounty",b="Kolkar raiders threaten the Horde’s foothold across the Barrens. Their fallen warriors leave behind leather and iron bracers, proof that a raider has been removed from the trade roads. Regthar Deathgate, an orc scout stationed on the bluffs west of the Crossroads, offers a standing bounty for these trophies to curb the tribe’s aggression.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants these bracers?",a="Regthar Deathgate, a Horde scout camped on a rise west of the Crossroads in the Barrens, accepts the bracers as proof of your efforts against the local Kolkar centaur.",al={"who takes centaur bracers","regthar deathgate turn in","who buys centaur bracers"},gp=true},{q="Which centaur carry these bracers?",a="Kolkar warriors wear these bracers as they roam the northern Barrens’ oases and encampments, including the Forgotten Pools and Lushwater Oasis.",al={"where to farm bracers","kolkar bracers drop","centaur bracers source"},gp=true},{q="Why does Regthar want them collected?",a="Regthar wants the Kolkar numbers reduced to protect Horde territory. The bracers show that warriors have killed marauders instead of merely driving them off.",al={"why collect bracers","regthar deathgate motive","purpose of centaur bracers"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are Centaur Bracers?",a="These bracers are pieces of crude armor worn by centaur warriors across the Barrens. Stripped from the arms of slain Kolkar marauders, they serve the Horde as grim physical proof of a hunter's success in culling their aggressive warbands.",al={"what are centaur bracers","centaur bracer lore","what is centaur bracers"},it="identity",add="2b8929fb"},{q="Where do Centaur Bracers come from?",a="They are forged or crafted by the centaur clans that roam the arid plains of Kalimdor, specifically the hostile Kolkar tribe. Warriors equip them for battle as rudimentary protection against the blades, arrows, and claws of their many enemies.",al={"who made centaur bracers","centaur bracers origin","where do centaur bracers come from"},it="origin",add="e954048b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect caravan supply lines between Durotar, Mulgore, and the Crossroads when you take down Kolkar raiders.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know your people have endured generations of brutal harassment by centaur clans. Clearing Kolkar from the Barrens brings retribution and security."},kw={"barrens","bounty","bracers","centaur","crossroads","deathgate","kolkar","regthar"},rel={"quest:855","quest:1361","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},src={"Centaur Bracers","Centaur Bracers (Classic)"}}
E["item:console-key"] = {t="item",n="Console Key",z="barrens",s="At the Venture Company digsite in the Barrens, Tinkerer Sniggles holds the Console Key. It unlocks the main control terminal and lets the samophlange be removed once the apparatus is shut down.",h="At the Venture Company digsite in the Barrens, Tinkerer Sniggles holds the Console Key.",sec={{t="Securing the Apparatus",b="The Venture Company runs an industrial outpost in the northern Barrens. Its steam-driven machinery depends on a device called a samophlange. The console is locked against unauthorized hands, and only Tinkerer Sniggles, the chief technician on site, carries the Console Key. The key opens the terminal casing so the rig can be powered down.",sp=0},{t="Shutting Down the Rig",b="After the auxiliary valves are turned and the apparatus cools to a stop, the Console Key cuts the final circuits. Turning it drains the terminal's remaining power and unlocks its housing, letting the samophlange be pried from the machinery.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does the Console Key unlock?",a="The Console Key unlocks the main control console at the Venture Company rig in the northern Barrens. Once the machinery is idle, it drains power from the terminal and exposes the samophlange.",al={"what is console key for","what does console key open","console key use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries the Console Key?",a="Tinkerer Sniggles carries the Console Key. The Venture Company engineer stays in a hut just northeast of the main console apparatus.",al={"who drops console key","where to get console key","tinkerer sniggles key"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the console locked in the first place?",a="The Venture Company locks the terminal to keep rivals and unruly workers from interfering with its machinery or taking valuable parts like the samophlange.",al={"why do i need a key","why is samophlange locked"},it="motive"},{q="Can you use the key before shutting down the valves?",a="Use the Console Key after the valves are shut down and the gauges read zero. Trying the active console risks a mechanical backfire.",al={"use key first","can i just unlock console"},gp=true},{q="What is the Console Key?",a="The Console Key is a mechanical security key held by the Venture Company tinkerer overseeing the control console in the Barrens. It fits into the locked housing that encloses the samophlange, ensuring that only authorized personnel can access the delicate machinery and terminal internals.",al={"console key","what is console key","what is the console key"},it="identity",add="4424a0fd"},{q="Why does anyone want the Console Key?",a="Once the apparatus has been shut down and power has drained from the control console, the housing remains locked tight. You need the Console Key to unlock the control panel itself, which is the final step required to safely dislodge and recover the samophlange from the terminal.",al={"why get console key","why do i need console key","console key purpose why"},it="why_wanted",add="81c16021"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Venture Company uses custom keyed locks to protect delicate engineering prototypes like the samophlange from competitors.",["faction:Horde"]="Taking the Console Key from Tinkerer Sniggles helps disrupt the Venture Company's exploitative industrial work in the heart of the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","console key","control console","samophlange","tinkerer sniggles","venture company"},rel={"quest:894","zone:barrens"},src={"Console Key","Samophlange (Classic 3)"}}
E["item:control-console-operating-manual"] = {t="item",n="Control Console Operating Manual",z="barrens",s="At the Venture Company site southwest of Sludge Fen, the Control Console Operating Manual guides workers through the machinery. It explains how to close the valves and disengage the samophlange.",h="At the Venture Company site southwest of Sludge Fen, the Control Console Operating Manual guides workers...",sec={{t="Deciphering Goblin Machinery",b="Southwest of Sludge Fen, the Venture Company runs a drilling and research site in the northern Barrens. Its machinery links gauges, pressurized valves, and mechanisms to a device called a samophlange. Without the right instructions, working the volatile controls can cause a dangerous failure or lock the system. The manual gives the valve sequence for disengaging the core apparatus without triggering an explosive failure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Control Console Operating Manual used for?",a="The Control Console Operating Manual explains how to work the Venture Company console southwest of Sludge Fen. It guides you through closing the valves so the samophlange can be disengaged.",al={"what does the manual do","manual use","why do i have operating manual"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is a samophlange?",a="Even the researchers outside the Venture Company do not fully understand what a samophlange does. It appears to be a goblin-engineered core mechanism tied to drilling and industrial work in the Barrens.",al={"what does samophlange do","samophlange lore","what is this machine"}},{q="Who wrote this manual?",a="Venture Company technicians overseeing the research outpost drafted the manual. It was meant to help workers operate the console and keep pressure levels across its control valves at their intended levels.",al={"who made the manual","manual author"},it="origin"},{q="What happens if I lose the manual?",a="The console has gauges and readouts showing valve pressure. A skilled adventurer can read its face and operate the switches without the manual in hand.",al={"lost manual","deleted operating manual"},gp=true},{q="What is the Control Console Operating Manual?",a="It is an instructional guide recovered from the Venture Company detailing the operation of the control console at their research facility southwest of the Sludge Fen. It outlines how their machinery functions so a technician can safely manipulate its valves and disengage the apparatus.",al={"what is control console manual","control console manual","venture co manual"},it="identity",add="4b9f7b43"},{q="Why is the Control Console Operating Manual wanted?",a="The manual provides the exact operational steps required to shut down and disengage the Venture Company's mysterious samophlange. Without deciphering its instructions, tampering blindly with the erratic levers, buttons, and pressurized control valves on the console would be nearly impossible.",al={"why want control console manual","why need manual","why is manual useful"},it="why_wanted",add="5e9de40e"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The manual shows a goblin approach to engineering: highly pressurized, marginally safe systems run by a chaotic array of levers and valves instead of balanced failsafes.",["faction:Horde"]="The manual gives Horde investigators a look inside the Venture Company's invasive industrial operations across the northern Barrens."},kw={"barrens","control console","goblin engineering","operating manual","samophlange","sludge fen","venture company"},rel={"quest:894","topic:venture-company","subzone:sludge-fen","zone:barrens"},src={"Control Console Operating Manual","Samophlange (Classic)"}}
E["item:corrupt-manifestation-s-bracers"] = {t="item",n="Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers",z="barrens",s="Tainted bracers lie on the coast of Silverpine Forest, remnants of a corrupted water elemental. Shaman initiates recover them during the Call of Water and cast them into the Brazier of Everfount with pure water to cleanse the shrine and summon a pure water spirit.",h="Tainted bracers lie on the coast of Silverpine Forest, remnants of a corrupted water elemental.",sec={{t="A Cleansing Offering",b="The Scourge's plague reached the spirits of Lordaeron. Along Silverpine Forest's misty coast, west of the Sepulcher, a sacred water shrine fell to corruption. Its water manifestation became an aggressive shade. Shaman initiates must defeat it and recover its bracers. At the Brazier of Everfount, they cast the bindings into the flame with pure water, lifting the corruption and calling forth an unblemished water spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are these bracers used for?",a="The bracers are cast into the Brazier of Everfount with pure water during a cleansing rite. The rite purges corruption from the Silverpine shrine and calls forth a pure water spirit.",al={"what do bracers do","call of water bracers","corrupt bracers use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do the bracers come from?",a="The bracers come from a Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water near a tainted elemental shrine on the Silverpine Forest coast, west of the Sepulcher.",al={"where do i get bracers","corrupt manifestation location"},it="origin"},{q="Why did the water elemental become corrupt?",a="The plague and dark powers that blighted Lordaeron warped the elemental and severed the local spirits from communion with shamans.",al={"why is water tainted","silverpine water corruption"}},{q="What are the Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers?",a="These bracers are physical remnants bound to a corrupted minor manifestation of water found along the tainted coastline of Silverpine Forest. Like many elemental beings bound to the mortal plane, the manifestation wears bracers that anchor and shape its watery form. Even after the creature is destroyed, the bracers retain the spiritual residue of the elemental's tainted existence, making them vital catalysts for ritual cleansing.",al={"what are corrupt manifestation's bracers","corrupt manifestation bracers","what are these bracers"},it="identity",add="0d8aeb2f"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, recovering and purifying these bracers is the final trial of the Call of Water. It proves your power to soothe and restore distorted elements."},kw={"brazier of everfount","call of water","corrupt manifestation's bracers","shaman quest","silverpine forest","water elemental"},rel={"quest:63","item:remaining-drops-of-purest-water","npc:minor-manifestation-of-water","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","npc:brine","zone:barrens"},src={"Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers","Call of Water (7)"}}
E["item:crossroads-supply-crate"] = {t="item",n="Crossroads Supply Crate",z="barrens",s="Stolen provisions for the Crossroads lie scattered among Razormane camps in the Barrens. A raided caravan left the settlement short of food, tools, and necessities.",h="Stolen provisions for the Crossroads lie scattered among Razormane camps in the Barrens.",sec={{t="Plundered Provisions",b="Razormane quilboar raided a caravan carrying supplies to the Crossroads. The crates were dragged into nearby camps among the underbrush and dirt dens. Thork, the settlement's commander, seeks their return before the outpost runs dangerously low on food, tools, and necessities.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are these supply crates?",a="The crates hold food, tools, and other provisions meant for the Horde settlement of the Crossroads. A Razormane attack scattered them after the quilboar raided a supply caravan on the Barrens roads.",al={"crossroads supplies","what is in the crates","supply crate info"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole the supply crates?",a="The Razormane quilboar attacked the caravan and hauled the crates to their nearby thorned camps to feast and hoard the spoils.",al={"who took the crates","who raided the caravan","quilboar thieves"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is looking for these crates?",a="Thork, an orc officer stationed at the Crossroads, seeks the stolen crates so the garrison and local inhabitants remain supplied.",al={"who wants the crates","turn in supply crates","thork supplies"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the crates located?",a="The crates lie scattered across Razormane quilboar camps in the surrounding Barrens.",al={"crate locations","where to find supply crates","crossroads supply crate spots"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Crossroads links Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern wildlands. Its supplies help protect Horde travel and logistics across Kalimdor."},kw={"crossroads","crossroads supply crate","quilboar","razormane","supplies for the crossroads","the barrens","thork"},rel={"quest:5041","subzone:crossroads","npc:thork","zone:barrens","topic:quilboar","topic:horde"},src={"Crossroads Supply Crate","Supplies for the Crossroads (Classic)"}}
E["item:deepmoss-egg"] = {t="item",n="Deepmoss Egg",z="barrens",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Deepmoss Eggs draw goblin merchants from Ratchet. Deepmoss spiders lay clustered clutches in the crags and canyons, and Booty Bay pirates prize them for omelettes.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, Deepmoss Eggs draw goblin merchants from Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Delicacy of the Crags",b="Deepmoss spiders nest across the Stonetalon Mountains, especially in Sishir Canyon and beneath the surviving trees of Windshear Crag. They leave clustered clutches of viable eggs in thick webbed sacks, sheltered by damp mountain moss. Most travelers have little use for them, but goblin traders see a chance to profit.",sp=0},{t="Booty Bay's Culinary Fad",b="Booty Bay has taken to spider egg omelettes, an eccentric culinary fad among wealthy pirates and adventurous diners. Local supplies cannot satisfy their appetite, so Mebok Mizzyrix of Ratchet arranges shipments through Wharfmaster Dizzywig. Collectors brave Stonetalon's venomous broods for fresh clutches, which become valuable cargo.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Deepmoss Eggs found?",a="Deepmoss Eggs are found in the Stonetalon Mountains, northwest of the Barrens. Clutches gather beneath the surviving trees of Windshear Crag and deeper in the venomous dens of Sishir Canyon.",al={"egg locations","where to get deepmoss eggs","deepmoss egg location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants to collect these eggs?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin merchant in Ratchet, hires collectors to gather Deepmoss Eggs. He arranges for Wharfmaster Dizzywig to ship the clutches across the sea.",al={"who needs deepmoss eggs","who buys deepmoss eggs","mebok mizzyrix quest"},it="people"},{q="What are the eggs actually used for?",a="The eggs go to Booty Bay, where spider egg omelettes have become a popular, if bizarre, culinary fad among pirates and other diners.",al={"spider egg use","why collect spider eggs","spider omelettes"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Sishir Canyon warned about when gathering them?",a="Sishir Canyon is a breeding ground crowded with mature spiders, webs, and devoured prey. Mebok advises anyone with a delicate stomach to gather eggs beneath Windshear Crag's sparse trees instead.",al={"sishir canyon warning","weak stomach sishir"},it="threat"},{q="What is a Deepmoss Egg?",a="A Deepmoss Egg is the clutch-laid egg of the deepmoss spiders native to the Stonetalon Mountains. Clustered beneath trees and nestled deep within mountain canyons, these silk-wrapped eggs are primarily harvested by bold adventurers looking to cash in on bizarre culinary markets across the sea.",al={"what are deepmoss eggs","deepmoss egg","deepmoss eggs"},it="identity",add="19ff336a"},{q="Where do Deepmoss Eggs come from?",a="These eggs are laid by the deepmoss spiders that infest the crags and valleys of the Stonetalon Mountains, particularly Windshear Crag and the perilous Sishir Canyon. They are naturally laid in clutches near surviving tree roots and arachnid nests rather than manufactured by any thinking mortal.",al={"deepmoss egg origin","where do deepmoss eggs come from","who lays deepmoss eggs"},it="origin",add="80df5d4f"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you may hesitate to use spider eggs, but Booty Bay diners prize whipped eggs as an adventurous delicacy and pay goblin prices for them."},kw={"booty bay","deepmoss egg","deepmoss spider","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","sishir canyon","stonetalon","windshear crag"},rel={"quest:1069","npc:mebok-mizzyrix","zone:stonetalon","subzone:ratchet","subzone:sishir-canyon","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:booty-bay","quest:1492"},src={"Deepmoss Egg","Deepmoss Spider Eggs"}}
E["item:dried-seeds"] = {t="item",n="Dried Seeds",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem gives travelers Dried Seeds to test the life-giving power beneath the Barrens' waters.",h="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem gives travelers Dried Seeds to test the life-giving power beneath the...",sec={{t="The Seeds and the Oasis",b="Tonga Runetotem studies the strange vents beneath the Barrens' waters. At the Forgotten Pools, he found fissures below the surface and now wants to learn whether one lies beneath the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast. He gives travelers Dried Seeds, which appear lifeless, to place in the bubbling fissure. Their response can show whether the energy beneath the oases can stir life in dead seeds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Dried Seeds used for?",a="You use Dried Seeds to test the bubbling fissure beneath the Stagnant Oasis. Place them in its waters and see whether the energy there can revive them.",al={"dried seeds use","what do i do with dried seeds","dried seeds purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Dried Seeds?",a="Tonga Runetotem, a tauren druid at the Crossroads, gives travelers the Dried Seeds. He studies the Barrens' sudden bursts of plant growth.",al={"who gives dried seeds","where do dried seeds come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where is the fissure to use them on?",a="The fissure lies beneath the waters of the Stagnant Oasis, southeast of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"where to plant dried seeds","stagnant oasis fissure location","bubbling fissure dried seeds"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when the seeds are exposed to the fissure?",a="Tonga asks you to place the dead seeds in the bubbling fissure and observe them. Their response reveals the result of his experiment.",al={"do the seeds grow","dried seeds result"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="What are the Dried Seeds?",a="These are completely dead and infertile plant seeds provided to you for an ecological experiment. On their own, they have withered beyond any natural hope of germination, making them an ideal control subject to test whether the mysterious bubbling fissures in the Barrens' oases possess unnatural, life-giving properties.",al={"what are dried seeds","dried seeds item","dried seeds lore"},it="identity",add="aa7d6cee"},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem want you to test the Dried Seeds?",a="Tonga Runetotem seeks to uncover the true nature of the strange fissures bubbling beneath the waters of the Barrens' oases. By exposing lifeless, infertile seeds directly to the fissure at the Stagnant Oasis, he hopes to observe whether the waters can stimulate growth where natural life has entirely failed.",al={"why dried seeds","why use dried seeds","tonga seeds purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="f2970934"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can use the dead seeds to study the strange energies rising from the Barrens' earth.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you can help Tonga Runetotem investigate the changes in the Barrens' dry soils."},kw={"barrens","bubbling fissure","crossroads","dried seeds","stagnant oasis","tonga runetotem"},rel={"quest:877","subzone:stagnant-oasis","subzone:crossroads","quest:870","zone:barrens","subzone:forgotten-pools"},src={"Dried Seeds","The Stagnant Oasis (Classic)"}}
E["item:echeyakee-s-hide"] = {t="item",n="Echeyakee's Hide",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn awaits the pale hide of Whitemist, the legendary white lion of the Barrens. Tauren honor the beast as an embodiment of mercy and death, while hunters bring the pelt as proof of their prowess.",h="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn awaits the pale hide of Whitemist, the legendary white lion of the...",sec={{t="Trophy of Whitemist",b="Echeyakee means Whitemist in the Taur-ahe tongue. The lion earned that name among the savannah's predators for his stealthy white coat and swift kills, ending prey's lives before fear or pain could take hold. A hunter summons the elusive cat near the giant kodo bones northeast of the Crossroads with a ceremonial horn, then claims his pelt. Bringing it to Sergra Darkthorn proves martial skill and honors Whitemist's silent, merciful end.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Echeyakee's Hide come from?",a="Echeyakee's Hide comes from the white lion Echeyakee, who lairs among giant kodo skeletons northeast of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Sergra Darkthorn provides the Horn of Echeyakee to summon him.",al={"where do i get echeyakee's hide","how to get echeyakee hide","echeyakee pelt location"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Echeyakee's Hide?",a="Sergra Darkthorn, an orc huntress at the Crossroads, wants Echeyakee's Hide. She sends rising Horde hunters to track the great cat and return with his pelt as proof of their connection to the wild.",al={"who turns in echeyakee hide","turn in echeyakees hide","who needs echeyakee hide"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does the name Echeyakee mean?",a="Echeyakee means Whitemist in the tauren language. The name honors the cat's pale pelt and the belief that he moved across the savannah like rolling mist, killing without lingering terror or agony.",al={"echeyakee translation","meaning of echeyakee","tauren name echeyakee"},it="name"},{q="What is Echeyakee's Hide?",a="It is the pelt of Echeyakee, the revered white lion known to the tauren as Whitemist. Considered the king of the savannah cats in the Barrens, Echeyakee hunts with unmatched stealth and swiftness, regarded as both mercy and death. Taking his hide serves as physical proof that a hunter possessed the skill and courage to summon and overcome the legendary predator.",al={"what is echeyakees hide","echeyakee hide","white lion hide"},it="identity",add="718fd4d1"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor Whitemist's swift spirit when you hunt Echeyakee, a sacred test of mercy and stealth rather than mere conquest.",["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, you take the pelt of the savannah's apex stalker as an early rite of passage, learning the subtleties of the wild as a Horde tracker."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","echeyakee","echeyakee's hide","sergra darkthorn","white lion","whitemist"},rel={"quest:881","item:horn-of-echeyakee","quest:860","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:tauren"},src={"Echeyakee's Hide","Echeyakee (Classic)"}}
E["item:empty-blue-waterskin"] = {t="item",n="Empty Blue Waterskin",z="barrens",s="Brine sends the Empty Blue Waterskin north from the Barrens to gather sacred water. The liquid will help her prepare the draught needed to summon and appease the water spirit.",h="Brine sends the Empty Blue Waterskin north from the Barrens to gather sacred water.",sec={{t="A Sacred Vessel",b="Brine gives the Empty Blue Waterskin to a shaman initiate at her hilltop hut in the southern Barrens. The vessel marks the final and most perilous gathering task of early training. To commune with the spirit of water, the initiate must seek pure, undisturbed sources across Kalimdor. The waterskin is meant for a secluded fountain deep within the Ruins of Stardust, along Ashenvale's contested borderlands.",sp=0},{t="The Forest Fountain",b="The initiate must leave the safety of Horde territory and travel into ancient groves guarded by nature beasts and night elves. At a fountain in the ruined sanctuary deep within the Ruins of Stardust, the waterskin is filled and becomes a Filled Blue Waterskin. With water samples from the Barrens and Tarren Mill, its contents let Brine brew the draught needed to summon and appease the elemental spirit of water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Empty Blue Waterskin used for?",a="The Empty Blue Waterskin carries water from the fountain deep within the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale back to Brine, who uses it to brew a draught of pure water.",al={"what does empty blue waterskin do","empty blue waterskin use","why do i have empty blue waterskin"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who gives you this waterskin?",a="Brine gives you the waterskin at her hut in the southern Barrens, south of Camp Taurajo near the Razorfen border.",al={"who gives empty blue waterskin","where do you get blue waterskin"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Where must the waterskin be filled?",a="Fill it at the central fountain deep within the Ruins of Stardust in south-western Ashenvale, just past Lake Mystral near the Stonetalon mountain ridge.",al={"where to fill empty blue waterskin","blue waterskin location","where do i fill it"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Brine need water from Ashenvale?",a="Brine seeks to make the purest vial of water known on Kalimdor. The untouched sacred wellsprings of the night elven ruins provide the pristine final component for communing with the elemental spirits of water.",al={"why ashenvale water","why ruins of stardust water"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Empty Blue Waterskin?",a="The Empty Blue Waterskin is a ritual vessel entrusted to shaman initiates during their trials. Given by the hermit Brine in the southern Barrens, it is fashioned to safely gather and carry pristine water from sacred places without corrupting its spiritual potency.",al={"empty blue waterskin","what is blue waterskin","blue waterskin purpose"},it="identity",add="6fa6361d"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you carry and fill the waterskin as a vital step in mastering the spirits of water. Its pure liquid is needed to craft your permanent Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you must travel from the Barrens into hostile night elf territory in western Ashenvale to retrieve the water."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","brine","call of water","empty blue waterskin","ruins of stardust","water totem"},rel={"item:filled-blue-waterskin","quest:63","npc:brine","subzone:ruins-of-stardust","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","topic:shaman"},src={"Empty Blue Waterskin","Call of Water (5)"}}
E["item:empty-brown-waterskin"] = {t="item",n="Empty Brown Waterskin",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Brine gives an empty waterskin to a shaman initiate.",h="In the Barrens, Brine gives an empty waterskin to a shaman initiate.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Scarcity",b="Brine gives a shaman initiate an empty leather skin for the opening trial of the Call of Water. The initiate must carry it to the watering hole beneath her dwelling and return with it full. The pool is guarded by local quilboar, who prize its water. In the Barrens, where water is scarce, even a small oasis can sustain life and spark violence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Empty Brown Waterskin used for?",a="Shaman initiates use the empty waterskin to draw water from the natural pond beneath Brine's hut in the Barrens. Filled, it is needed to prepare elemental sapta.",al={"waterskin purpose","what does brown waterskin do","use of empty brown waterskin"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides this waterskin?",a="Brine, a hermit in the southern Barrens, gives the waterskin to shamans undertaking their elemental pilgrimage to commune with the spirits of water.",al={"who gives the waterskin","brown waterskin quest giver","where to get empty waterskin"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the quilboar defending the water source?",a="Rain is rare throughout the Barrens, and water is scarce. To the quilboar, even a small watering hole means wealth and survival, so they guard it and attack anyone who draws from it.",al={"why quilboar attack","quilboar water","why is the pool guarded"},it="motive"},{q="What happens once the skin is filled?",a="Dipped into the oasis beneath Brine's hill, the skin becomes a Filled Brown Waterskin. Returning it to Brine lets her test your understanding of nature's balance before she sends you across the world for rarer waters.",al={"what to do after filling","turn in waterskin","filled brown waterskin turn in"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Empty Brown Waterskin?",a="The Empty Brown Waterskin is a simple vessel given to aspiring shaman by the hermit Brine in the southern Barrens. It serves as an instructional tool on the path to communing with the spirits of water. To earn the water sapta, you must carry this vessel to a nearby watering hole guarded by fierce quilboar, filling it with pure liquid while observing how life and conflict revolve around scarce moisture in the arid plains.",al={"what is empty brown waterskin","empty brown waterskin lore","brown waterskin"},it="identity",add="805e4eda"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, carrying this waterskin is a rite of passage on the way to your Water Totem. It shows the balance between reverence for the elements and the harsh struggle to survive."},kw={"barrens","brine","call of water","quilboar","sapta","shaman","waterskin"},rel={"item:filled-brown-waterskin","npc:brine","quest:63","zone:barrens","topic:quilboar"},src={"Empty Brown Waterskin","Call of Water (3)"}}
E["item:empty-dreadmist-peak-sampler"] = {t="item",n="Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler",z="barrens",s="At Dreadmist Peak, druids seek tainted water in an empty Cenarion vessel. The sample may help diagnose and cure the blight spreading among wildlife in the northern Barrens.",h="At Dreadmist Peak, druids seek tainted water in an empty Cenarion vessel.",sec={{t="Tracing the Blight",b="Dendrite Starblaze suspects the pools atop Dreadmist Peak are at the heart of a sickness afflicting gazelles and unsettling the northern Barrens. The pools influence the weather, and the druid fears they are tied to the spreading blight. He sends druid initiates with empty samplers to brave the mountain heights and draw water from the peak. The Burning Blade, a demon-worshipping cult, now infests the mountain.",sp=0},{t="A Crucial Specimen",b="Druids carry the empty sampler up Dreadmist Peak to collect water from its pool. They take the sample to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads, where it can help him devise a cure and protect the native wildlife.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler?",a="The Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler is an empty container, a specialized Cenarion vessel druids use to draw water from the tainted pool atop Dreadmist Peak. They bring the sample to Tonga Runetotem to help devise a cure for sickened wildlife.",al={"what does this item do","dreadmist sampler use","why do i have this sampler"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this sampler need to be taken?",a="Carry the sampler to the high pool atop Dreadmist Peak, northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens, and draw a water sample.",al={"where do i fill the sampler","sampler location","how to fill empty dreadmist peak sampler"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who provides the sampler?",a="Dendrite Starblaze provides the sampler on behalf of the Cenarion Circle, then sends the druid to coordinate with Tonga Runetotem.",al={"who gives the sampler","who started this quest"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the water on Dreadmist Peak so important to sample?",a="The pools atop Dreadmist Peak influence regional weather and mist. The Burning Blade cult has corrupted the summit, and tainted runoff spreads across the plains and poisons local creatures.",al={"why dreadmist peak pool","why is the water bad"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler?",a="It is a specialized vessel entrusted to Horde druids by Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle. Its sole purpose is to securely hold and transport water drawn from the elevated pools atop Dreadmist Peak, allowing it to be safely analyzed without spilling or further contaminating the sample.",al={"what is dreadmist peak sampler","empty dreadmist peak sampler item","dreadmist peak sampler"},it="identity",add="cf2d7f72"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, collecting a sample with this vessel is part of learning to cure poisons and to diagnose and ease suffering in the wild.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry this sampler to aid Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads as he works to stop ecological decay across the Barrens' northern plains."},kw={"barrens","burning blade","dendrite starblaze","dreadmist peak","empty dreadmist peak sampler","the principal source","tonga runetotem"},rel={"item:filled-dreadmist-peak-sampler","quest:6122","subzone:dreadmist-peak","npc:tonga-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:6125","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},src={"Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler","The Principal Source (Horde)"}}
E["item:empty-red-waterskin"] = {t="item",n="Empty Red Waterskin",z="barrens",s="In Tarren Mill, an empty red waterskin is bound for a well untouched by blight. Brine gives it to shaman initiates for their elemental trials.",h="In Tarren Mill, an empty red waterskin is bound for a well untouched by blight.",sec={{t="A Vessel for Pure Water",b="Brine gives shaman initiates this plain red skin for the Call of Water trials. They carry it across the sea to Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. The Forsaken occupy the town, but its central well still draws fresh spring water. The filled skin brings a sample to Brine, who blends the water into a vial of purest water for the initiate’s trial.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Empty Red Waterskin used for?",a="Shaman use the skin during the Call of Water trials to gather spring water from Tarren Mill’s well. The water turns it into a Filled Red Waterskin.",al={"empty red waterskin use","what to do with red waterskin"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides this waterskin?",a="Brine, an orc shaman hermit on a hill in the southern Barrens, gives the waterskin to shaman initiates undergoing elemental trials.",al={"who gives red waterskin","red waterskin questgiver"},it="origin"},{q="Why gather water from Tarren Mill specifically?",a="Tarren Mill is under Forsaken control, yet its central well remains uncorrupted. Brine sees the pure spring as a sign of hope and life enduring in an unhallowed land.",al={"why tarren mill water","tarren mill well lore"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after the waterskin is filled?",a="After filling the skin at the well, you bring it back to Brine in the Barrens. He blends its water with other rare samples into a vial of purest water, which Islen Waterseer uses to create the Water Sapta.",al={"what next red waterskin","filled red waterskin turn in"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Empty Red Waterskin?",a="It is an empty container entrusted to shaman initiates undergoing the Call of Water trials. Crafted to safely transport liquid across vast distances, its specific purpose is to collect and preserve pure well water from the Hillsbrad Foothills so that it can later be brewed into an elemental sapta.",al={"what is empty red waterskin","red waterskin item","empty red waterskin lore"},it="identity",add="29d0aa45"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you carry and fill this waterskin as a first step toward mastering the Water Totem and attuning your senses to water’s resilient spirits.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you hear Brine compare the pure well in Tarren Mill to Warchief Thrall, a beacon of strength and hope enduring immense suffering."},kw={"brine","call of water","empty red waterskin","hillsbrad foothills","tarren mill","water sapta"},rel={"item:filled-red-waterskin","quest:63","npc:brine","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:barrens","topic:forsaken","npc:thrall"},src={"Empty Red Waterskin","Call of Water (4)"}}
E["item:explosive-stick-of-gann"] = {t="item",n="Explosive Stick of Gann",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Gann Stonespire turns stolen dwarven plans against Bael Modan. He built the charge to sabotage the dwarves’ flying machine.",h="In the southern Barrens, Gann Stonespire turns stolen dwarven plans against Bael Modan.",sec={{t="A Weapon of Retribution",b="When Prospector Khazgorm led the Ironforge excavation into southern Kalimdor, the dwarves drove the Stonespire tauren from their ancestral village and razed their sacred grounds to build Bael Modan. Gann Stonespire reclaimed Khazgorm’s blueprints to avenge his displaced and fallen kin. He studied the plans and assembled a charge with enough force to wreck heavy machinery.",sp=0},{t="Targeting the Sky Machine",b="Gann made the explosive stick for the dwarven flying machine on an observation tower above the excavation. To him, the machine is more than transport or a weapon of war. It marks Alliance dominion over sacred tauren soil. Destroying it cripples the dwarven outpost and strikes a blow for the lost Stonespire tribe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Explosive Stick of Gann?",a="Gann Stonespire crafted the explosive charge from recovered dwarven schematics to sabotage the Prospectors’ machinery on his ancestral lands.",al={"explosive stick of gann","ganns explosive stick","gann bomb"},it="identity"},{q="Who made this explosive?",a="Gann Stonespire assembled the explosive to avenge his tribe after the Ironforge dwarves at Bael Modan destroyed their village and desecrated their homeland in the southern Barrens.",al={"who made this","who is gann","gann stonespire"},it="origin"},{q="What is the explosive supposed to blow up?",a="The charge is meant to destroy the dwarven flying machine on a tower above the excavation at Bael Modan. Its destruction cripples the site's reconnaissance and brings symbolic revenge for the Stonespire tribe.",al={"what do i bomb","flying machine target","where do i use it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did a tauren learn to make dwarven explosives?",a="Gann built the stick from engineering blueprints recovered from Prospector Khazgorm, leader of the dwarven dig at Bael Modan. He turned the invaders’ own technology against them.",al={"how did gann build it","explosive schematics","khazgorm plans"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, using this weapon avenges the displaced Stonespire tribe and strikes back at the Prospectors who dug into sacred Kalimdor soil.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how stolen blueprints turned against the dwarven machinery."},kw={"bael modan","explosive stick of gann","flying machine","gann stonespire","prospector khazgorm","stonespire tribe","the barrens"},rel={"quest:846","npc:gann-stonespire","subzone:bael-modan","quest:843","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff","topic:tauren"},src={"Explosive Stick of Gann","Revenge of Gann (2)"}}
E["item:filled-blue-waterskin"] = {t="item",n="Filled Blue Waterskin",z="barrens",s="Shamans gather water for their trials at the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale. The Filled Blue Waterskin carries a pristine sample from the ancient fountain.",h="Shamans gather water for their trials at the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Sacred Spring of Ashenvale",b="Call of Water initiates cross north from the Barrens into Ashenvale's dense forests. Beyond Lake Mystral, the Ruins of Stardust lie against the mountains dividing Ashenvale from Stonetalon. Fierce forest beasts guard the secluded elven sanctuary. At the center of its lake, an untouched fountain holds water untainted by corruption or drought. A blue waterskin filled from its basin carries the sample sought by shaman masters for ritual attunement.",sp=0},{t="A Rite of Harmony",b="Brine, a hermit and water expert, lives on a hill in the southern Barrens and needs this final sample. He combines it with water from contrasting wells and springs, then distills the pure essence into an offering. The offering can manifest and soothe the elemental spirits of water, completing an initiate's trial.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the water gathered to fill this waterskin?",a="The water comes from a small fountain at the center of the lake in the Ruins of Stardust, in southwestern Ashenvale beyond Lake Mystral.",al={"where do i fill it","ruins of stardust fountain","water location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who requires this water?",a="Brine, a hermit living in the southern Barrens, requires the water for the Call of Water trials he gives novice shaman.",al={"who wants the blue waterskin","brine water","call of water npc"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of collecting this sample?",a="Brine needs this final sample to brew a draught of extraordinarily pure water, allowing an aspiring shaman to commune with and honor the elemental spirits of water.",al={"why do i need it","what is filled blue waterskin used for"},it="purpose"},{q="Is the area where the water is gathered dangerous?",a="Yes. Hostile wildlife, including local elementals and fierce beasts, inhabit the Ruins of Stardust and defend the ancient elven glade.",al={"ruins of stardust danger","is ashenvale fountain safe"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Filled Blue Waterskin?",a="The Filled Blue Waterskin is a leather vessel filled with pure spring water collected from a fountain in the Ruins of Stardust, located deep within the forests of Ashenvale. It serves as one of the essential elemental samples required for a shaman undertaking the sacred Call of Water trials.",al={"what is filled blue waterskin","filled blue waterskin item"},it="identity",add="031dd284"},{q="Where does the Filled Blue Waterskin come from, and who made it?",a="The waterskin itself is an empty pouch provided to you by Brine, a hermit dwelling in the southern Barrens. It becomes the Filled Blue Waterskin once you travel north into the ancient elven territory of Ashenvale and scoop fresh water from the sacred fountain resting in the center of the lake at the Ruins of Stardust.",al={"where does filled blue waterskin come from","who made filled blue waterskin","source of filled blue waterskin"},it="origin",add="eff34fc2"},{q="Why does Brine want the Filled Blue Waterskin?",a="Brine requires this sample as the final component in a three-part collection of pure waters from across Azeroth. By combining it with the other sources you have gathered, she crafts a vial of unblemished, pure water necessary for the next phase of your shamanistic rite of passage.",al={"why does brine need filled blue waterskin","why is filled blue waterskin wanted","filled blue waterskin purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="320c16da"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you gather this water as the final step in mastering water, crossing hostile faction borders to commune with nature's purest reservoirs.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde initiate, you venture north into Ashenvale's contested woods and ancestral night elven territory to complete sacred rites, facing real danger along the way."},kw={"ashenvale","brine","call of water","filled blue waterskin","lake mystral","ruins of stardust","shaman quest"},rel={"quest:63","npc:brine","subzone:ruins-of-stardust","item:empty-blue-waterskin","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","topic:shaman"},src={"Filled Blue Waterskin","Call of Water (5)"}}
E["item:filled-brown-waterskin"] = {t="item",n="Filled Brown Waterskin",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, the Filled Brown Waterskin carries fresh water from the pond below Brine's hut. Aspiring shaman bring it to her to begin brewing sapta, used to commune with water spirits.",h="In the Barrens, the Filled Brown Waterskin carries fresh water from the pond below Brine's hut.",sec={{t="A Life-Giving Drought",b="The pond beneath Brine's hut is a rare source of fresh water in the Barrens. Nearby quilboar fight fiercely over it, and a novice shaman sees how scarce water can drive creatures to defend what sustains them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Filled Brown Waterskin used for?",a="You bring the water to Brine at her hut in the southern Barrens. She uses it to begin preparing sapta, a draught that lets shaman perceive and commune with water spirits.",al={"brown waterskin use","what is filled brown waterskin","what do i do with filled brown waterskin"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this water come from?",a="The water comes from a small freshwater pool just down the ridge beneath Brine's isolated hut. Local quilboar fiercely contest the pool.",al={"where to get water","pond location","where is the watering hole"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the quilboar fight over this water source?",a="Rain is exceedingly rare in the arid Barrens, so the quilboar hold feasts when it comes. They guard natural springs against outsiders, even to the death.",al={"why quilboar attack","quilboar water","why is water sacred to quilboar"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Filled Brown Waterskin?",a="It is a simple waterskin filled from the freshwater pond nestled below Brine's hut in the arid Barrens. Drawn as part of a shaman's trial, this water serves as a pure elemental sample, demonstrating how even a humble pool of moisture can sustain life and breed conflict in a parched desert.",al={"filled brown waterskin","what is filled brown waterskin","what is the brown waterskin"},it="identity",add="52b5cef0"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you fetch this water as Brine's first practical test during the Call of Water. It teaches you to respect the balance and fierce passions surrounding water."},kw={"barrens","brine","brown waterskin","call of water","filled brown waterskin","quilboar","sapta","shaman quest"},rel={"npc:brine","item:empty-brown-waterskin","quest:63","zone:barrens","topic:quilboar"},src={"Filled Brown Waterskin","Call of Water (3)"}}
E["item:filled-dreadmist-peak-sampler"] = {t="item",n="Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler",z="barrens",s="At Dreadmist Peak, a filled sampler holds water gathered by Horde druids from the summit pools. The Cenarion Circle studies the sample to learn what is poisoning wildlife in the northern Barrens.",h="At Dreadmist Peak, a filled sampler holds water gathered by Horde druids from the summit pools.",sec={{t="A Tainted Source",b="Dreadmist Peak’s high crags hold pools whose mists shape weather and rainfall across the northern Barrens. The Burning Blade, who worship demons, made their coven atop the summit, and the water soon soured. Cenarion druids suspect demonic rites poisoned the vapors that feed the surrounding savanna. They send initiates to collect a sample in a special sampler. The foul liquid confirms their fears: its corruption can sicken the herds below.",sp=0},{t="Curing the Savanna",b="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem uses the sample to help find an antidote. The Burning Blade are suspected of tainting the water, and its properties help the Cenarion Circle understand the poison. By studying the taint in the vial, druids make herbal remedies for dying gazelles and learn to wield their own natural power over poison.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is this water sample obtained?",a="The sample comes from a pool at Dreadmist Peak’s summit, northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"where do i get the sample","dreadmist sampler location","where to fill sampler"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the water on Dreadmist Peak tainted?",a="The Burning Blade cult has taken over Dreadmist Peak’s heights to worship demons. Dendrite Starblaze suspects the cult tainted the summit’s natural waters.",al={"why is dreadmist water poisoned","who poisoned dreadmist peak","burning blade water"},it="threat"},{q="Who needs the filled sampler?",a="Tonga Runetotem needs the filled sampler. He is a Cenarion druid at the Crossroads, investigating the sudden sickness among wildlife in the Barrens.",al={"who do i bring the sampler to","tonga runetotem sampler","turn in dreadmist water"},it="people",gp=true},{q="How does this poisoned water affect the Barrens?",a="Dreadmist Peak’s airy heights and pools influence local weather and mist. Once poisoned, the vapors settle over the savanna north of the main road and make the native gazelles sick.",al={"what does the water do","sick gazelles barrens","dreadmist mist effect"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the sampler used for after it is collected?",a="Tonga Runetotem studies the foul liquid to learn the nature of its demonic taint, then uses that knowledge to make a curative salve for druids to treat afflicted gazelles.",al={"what does tonga do with it","cure for the poison","power over poison research"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler?",a="It is a specialized vial containing a drawn sample of tainted water taken directly from the high pool atop Dreadmist Peak. Handed to druid initiates by the Cenarion Circle, it serves as critical physical evidence of the foul corruption currently seeping through the high mountain springs and ruining the wildlife across the northern plains.",al={"what is filled dreadmist peak sampler","dreadmist sampler","filled sampler druid"},it="identity",add="f843c928"},{q="Where does the Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler come from, and who made it?",a="The empty glass sampling phial is provided by the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade to young druids studying the art of curing maladies. You fill it personally at the summit pool of Dreadmist Peak in the Barrens, where the demon-worshipping Burning Blade cultists gather and pollute the natural headwaters that affect the surrounding climate.",al={"who made dreadmist sampler","where does dreadmist sampler come from","origin dreadmist sampler"},it="origin",add="2e934816"},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem want the Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler?",a="Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads urgently needs the water to study the blight affecting the northern Barrens. Gazelles and local fauna are falling violently ill, and by analyzing this foul source material from the peak, Tonga hopes to isolate the unnatural poison and concoct an effective herbal remedy to heal the land.",al={"why does tonga want the sampler","tonga runetotem dreadmist sample","why get the filled dreadmist sampler"},it="why_wanted",add="cb57b91c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Horde druid, you gather this sample as a rite of passage. It teaches you how corruption spreads through natural waterways and prepares you to master curative magic.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see the Burning Blade cult’s threat growing within Horde territory in the Barrens."},kw={"burning blade","cenarion circle","dreadmist peak","druid","filled dreadmist peak sampler","the barrens","the principal source","tonga runetotem"},rel={"quest:6127","item:empty-dreadmist-peak-sampler","subzone:dreadmist-peak","npc:tonga-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:6130","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},src={"Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler","The Principal Source (Horde)"}}
E["item:filled-red-waterskin"] = {t="item",n="Filled Red Waterskin",z="barrens",s="In Tarren Mill, a well gives clear spring water for a shaman’s trial. The Filled Red Waterskin carries water drawn from the village well, amid ruins held by the Forsaken.",h="In Tarren Mill, a well gives clear spring water for a shaman’s trial.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Blighted Lands",b="Brine, a hermit in the Barrens, sends shaman initiates to Tarren Mill for water training. The journey leads to the Hillsbrad Foothills, where decay and the dead surround the town. Yet the central well still draws clear spring water. Brine sees this pure water as a sign of endurance in an unhallowed land. She compares the uncorrupted spring with Warchief Thrall’s resolve through hardship. Gathering the water tests an initiate’s respect for its purity, even in hostile surroundings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Red Waterskin?",a="The Filled Red Waterskin holds pure spring water drawn from the public well in the center of Tarren Mill.",al={"what water is in it","tarren mill water","red waterskin contents"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Brine want water from Tarren Mill?",a="Brine sees Tarren Mill’s fresh spring as a rare sign of purity amid Forsaken decay. She needs the water to brew sapta for a shaman’s water trials.",al={"why tarren mill","why brine needs this","purpose of red waterskin"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does the well stay clean in an undead town?",a="No one knows why the spring has remained untouched by the plague around it. Brine says the Forsaken in Tarren Mill may not recognize or value the purity of the holy spring among them.",al={"why isn't the well blighted","is tarren mill well poisoned","holy well tarren mill"},it="place"},{q="How does Thrall relate to this quest?",a="Brine compares the clean well in a ruined town to Thrall. He endured great suffering and captivity, then emerged strong and untainted to guide the orcish people through dark times.",al={"thrall comparison","why mention thrall"},it="history"},{q="Where does the Filled Red Waterskin come from?",a="You obtain it by carrying an Empty Red Waterskin—given to you by Brine in the Barrens—all the way to the Hillsbrad Foothills and drawing pure water from the village well in Tarren Mill. Brine remembers the well as an astonishing pocket of fresh spring water persevering in the middle of a Forsaken settlement.",al={"filled red waterskin origin","where to get filled red waterskin","who made filled red waterskin"},it="origin",add="c913c28c"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, carrying this water tests your ability to find and honor life-giving balance in the world’s most decayed and sorrowful corners.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion from Kalimdor, you travel to Tarren Mill, where the Forsaken struggle against Alliance forces across the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"brine","call of water","empty red waterskin","filled red waterskin","sapta","shaman","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:63","item:empty-red-waterskin","npc:brine","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","npc:thrall","topic:forsaken","zone:barrens"},src={"Filled Red Waterskin","Call of Water (4)"}}
E["item:forged-steel-bars"] = {t="item",n="Forged Steel Bars",z="barrens",s="In the northern Barrens, Thun'grim Firegaze's steel bars are missing. Recovering them will prove a warrior's resolve to reclaim stolen property.",h="In the northern Barrens, Thun'grim Firegaze's steel bars are missing.",sec={{t="Stolen Metal",b="Thun'grim Firegaze, a visually impaired orc smith, keeps a camp in the northern Barrens. Razormane quilboar took his iron chest during a night raid, distracting him with grunts and snorts while thieves slipped away. Unable to work fine steel, the quilboar left the unopened chest near a ruined wagon in their encampment to the northwest. The bars remain intact for warriors willing to recover them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns these forged steel bars?",a="The bars belong to Thun'grim Firegaze, an orc armorer and weaponsmith who lives in a camp in the northern Barrens.",al={"who owns the bars","thungrim steel","whose steel is this"},it="origin"},{q="Why did the quilboar steal them?",a="The Razormane quilboar stole them to pillage Thun'grim's valuables. Knowing his eyesight was poor, they taunted and distracted him while others carried off his iron chest.",al={"why steal steel","quilboar motive","razormane theft"}},{q="Did the quilboar use the steel?",a="No. The Razormanes lacked the skill to work such finely refined steel. They left the chest unopened beside a broken wagon in their camp.",al={"did quilboar forge anything","what did quilboar do with steel"}},{q="What will Thun'grim offer in return for them?",a="Thun'grim offers aspiring warriors a crafted weapon in exchange for braving the quilboar camps and returning all the bars.",al={"forged steel reward","what do i get for the steel"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are the Forged Steel Bars?",a="These bars are a cache of refined, high-quality metal belonging to the blacksmith Thun'grim Firegaze. Kept securely locked in an iron chest at his camp, they represent fine materials meant for forging sturdy weapons. While raw and unworked into finished arms, their craftsmanship far surpasses the crude scrap typical of the Barrens.",al={"what are forged steel bars","forged steel bars info","stolen steel bars"},it="identity",add="4e666297"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Recovering Thun'grim's stolen steel proves a warrior can track down thieves and face dangerous quilboar packs. In return, Thun'grim offers custom weaponry.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The refined bars show the difference between crude tribal scrap metal and the quality steel made by trained Horde smiths."},kw={"barrens","forged steel","forged steel bars","iron chest","razormane","stolen iron chest","thun'grim firegaze"},rel={"quest:1503","quest:1502","zone:barrens","topic:quilboar"},src={"Forged Steel Bars","Forged Steel"}}
E["item:fungal-spores"] = {t="item",n="Fungal Spores",z="barrens",s="Around the Barrens' oases, Fungal Spores gather in swollen mushrooms. The waters quicken the life around them, and the Royal Apothecary Society seeks the spores for its alchemy.",h="Around the Barrens' oases, Fungal Spores gather in swollen mushrooms.",sec={{t="Vitality of the Oases",b="The Barrens' oases bring unusual life to the dry plains. At the Forgotten Pools, the Lushwater Oasis, and the Stagnant Oasis, the water does more than ease thirst. It quickens and changes the plants and wildlife nearby. Mushrooms along the damp shores swell with spores, carrying the waters' concentrated power to spur growth. Naturalists study this change, while the Royal Apothecary Society gathers the mushrooms for its alchemy.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Alchemy",b="Apothecaries abroad gather unusual local ingredients for their laboratories and colleagues. At the Crossroads, Apothecary Helbrim sends such reagents onward, including to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff. The spores are valuable for brewing potent chemical mixtures. Their natural properties have already been altered by the mysterious forces beneath Kalimdor's soil, making them useful to the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are these spores found?",a="You find Fungal Spores in swollen mushrooms along the shores of the Barrens' major oases: the Forgotten Pools, the Lushwater Oasis, and the Stagnant Oasis.",al={"spore locations","where to find fungal spores","laden mushroom locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken interested in them?",a="The oasis waters have altered the spores with vibrant life energy. Apothecary Helbrim uses them in potent mixtures for the Royal Apothecary Society and his colleague Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff.",al={"why does helbrim want spores","apothecary spores use","what are spores used for"},it="motive"},{q="Why do the mushrooms around the oases grow so large?",a="The waters at the Barrens' oases carry unusual life energy that changes nearby plants and animals. Fungi along the shores swell with altered spores.",al={"why are the mushrooms mutated","oasis water effect","oasis mystery"},it="origin"},{q="Who asks for the spores?",a="Apothecary Helbrim, a Forsaken alchemist at the Crossroads in the Barrens, asks adventurers to gather spores for his research.",al={"who needs fungal spores","spore quest giver","apothecary helbrim"},it="target"},{q="What are these fungal spores?",a="These are potent spores harvested from the laden mushrooms that sprout around the oases of the Barrens, such as the Forgotten Pools. Nourished by the strange, altered life energies flowing through the oasis waters, the fungi produce spores imbued with unusual biological properties that intrigue alchemists.",al={"what is fungal spores","fungal spores info","what are the spores"},it="identity",add="3c4c96db"},{q="Why does Apothecary Helbrim want the fungal spores?",a="Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads seeks the spores for the Royal Apothecary Society. He finds the altered properties of the oasis fungi particularly useful for compounding an experimental concoction, which he intends to deliver to his associate, Apothecary Zamah, in Thunder Bluff.",al={"why does helbrim want spores","why want fungal spores","who needs fungal spores"},it="why_wanted",add="02f1bc1b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Royal Apothecary Society values rare regional ingredients for its research. Kalimdor's altered fungi offer a different choice from Lordaeron's blighted plants.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can see how the life-giving waters of the Barrens' oases change the mushrooms growing nearby."},kw={"apothecary helbrim","apothecary society","barrens","crossroads","forgotten pools","fungal spores","laden mushroom","lushwater oasis","stagnant oasis"},rel={"quest:848","npc:apothecary-helbrim","quest:853","subzone:forgotten-pools","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","subzone:lushwater-oasis","subzone:stagnant-oasis"},src={"Fungal Spores","Fungal Spores (Classic)"}}
E["item:gazlowe-s-ledger"] = {t="item",n="Gazlowe's Ledger",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Gazlowe checks his trade records against the harbor manifest when a shipment from Booty Bay goes missing.",h="In Ratchet, Gazlowe checks his trade records against the harbor manifest when a shipment from Booty Bay goes...",sec={{t="Ratchet's Commercial Records",b="Gazlowe tracks trade goods in Ratchet with a personal ledger. It records imported crates, outbound cargo, and warehouse stores. When a shipment from Booty Bay is missing, Gazlowe compares his expected inventory with the dock records kept by Wharfmaster Dizzywig.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Theft",b="Gazlowe and the other goblins compare the ledger with Dizzywig's harbor logs and find that the cargo never reached the port warehouse. The mismatch confirms Gazlowe's suspicion that the crates were taken before they came ashore. The Southsea Freebooters along the nearby Merchant Coast are to blame.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Gazlowe's Ledger?",a="Gazlowe's Ledger records goods expected and stored in Ratchet. Gazlowe sends it to the docks so its entries can be checked against the wharf records when a shipment is missing.",al={"gazlowes ledger","ratchet ledger","gazlowe inventory book"},it="identity"},{q="Who needs to inspect the ledger?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig reviews Gazlowe's Ledger against his shipping logs. He oversees the Ratchet docks and can determine whether missing goods were misplaced or never unloaded.",al={"who do i take the ledger to","ledger recipient","dizzywig ledger"}},{q="What cargo was missing in the ledger?",a="Gazlowe was waiting for his latest shipment from Booty Bay. Dizzywig finds nothing amiss in his logs, though he says goods from Undermine are waiting for Gazlowe to pick up.",al={"what is gazlowe missing","missing shipment cargo"}},{q="What happens after the ledger is checked?",a="Dizzywig checks whether the shipment passed through the docks. When he finds it did not, the ledger goes back to Gazlowe, confirming that Southsea Freebooters likely intercepted the cargo at sea.",al={"what happens to the ledger","after dizzywig checks"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does Gazlowe's Ledger come from, and who keeps it?",a="This ledger belongs to Gazlowe, the goblin boss overseeing the port town of Ratchet. It serves as his personal inventory record, documenting inbound and outbound cargo shipped across the Great Sea between Ratchet and other goblin trading hubs like Booty Bay.",al={"who made gazlowes ledger","where does gazlowes ledger come from","origin of gazlowes ledger"},it="origin",add="d44950a4"},{q="Why is Gazlowe's Ledger needed right now?",a="Gazlowe suspects that a long-overdue shipment from Booty Bay was stolen by the Southsea Freebooters. Before jumping to conclusions, he needs you to carry his ledger down to Wharfmaster Dizzywig on the docks to compare inventory records against the harbor logs and rule out a clerical error.",al={"why want gazlowes ledger","why need gazlowe ledger","what is gazlowes ledger for"},it="why_wanted",add="c4547cde"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can trade at Ratchet, a neutral port. Helping Gazlowe trace stolen shipments keeps good standing with the local Steamwheedle authorities.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can glimpse the flow of contraband, valuable imports, and piracy around the Barrens coast in a goblin boss's private trade ledger."},kw={"booty bay","dizzywig","freebooters","gazlowe","ledger","ratchet","shipment","steamwheedle"},rel={"quest:890","subzone:ratchet","quest:1492","quest:888","quest:887","subzone:booty-bay","topic:pirate","zone:barrens"},src={"Gazlowe's Ledger","The Missing Shipment","The Missing Shipment (2)"}}
E["item:harpy-lieutenant-ring"] = {t="item",n="Harpy Lieutenant Ring",z="barrens",s="In the Dry Hills, Harpy Lieutenant Rings mark the Witchwing Slayers who command the flock. Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads asks for them as proof of death.",h="In the Dry Hills, Harpy Lieutenant Rings mark the Witchwing Slayers who command the flock.",sec={{t="Tokens of Rank",b="Witchwing Slayers direct attacks on Horde travelers in the Barrens. Their rings mark their place among the flock’s leaders, above the ordinary raiders who fight with little coordination. At the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger and the defenders need the rings taken from fallen slayers to confirm that this part of the harpies’ leadership has been broken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who carries these rings?",a="Witchwing Slayers wear the rings as lieutenants among the Witchwing flock in the Dry Hills.",al={"who drops harpy lieutenant ring","witchwing slayer rings","which harpies have rings"},it="target"},{q="Where can Witchwing Slayers be found?",a="Witchwing Slayers roost in the Dry Hills, northwest of the Crossroads in the northern Barrens.",al={"witchwing slayer location","where are harpy lieutenants","dry hills harpies"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Darsok Swiftdagger want them?",a="Darsok wants the rings as proof that the Witchwing Slayers have been killed. Their deaths break part of the flock’s leadership.",al={"why collect harpy rings","darsok swiftdagger rings"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Do regular harpy raiders carry these rings?",a="No. The rings mark the Witchwing Slayers, while ordinary harpy raiders are lower-ranking underlings.",al={"can raiders drop rings","do witchwing raiders have rings"},gp=true},{q="What is a Harpy Lieutenant Ring?",a="These rings are distinctive adornments carried by the Witchwing slayers of the Dry Hills. Within their roosts, the slayers act as lieutenants, commanding the lesser harpy underlings on behalf of their matriarchs. To the Horde scouts watching the Barrens, these trinkets serve as identifiable proof of rank among the vicious flock.",al={"what is harpy lieutenant ring","harpy ring identity","harpy lieutenant ring lore"},it="identity",add="105f77c8"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face Witchwing harpies that harass supply lines between Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern outposts. Breaking their leadership helps secure passage for Horde caravans across the Barrens.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may favor the precise strikes Darsok Swiftdagger seeks: slipping into harpy roosts to kill their commanders."},kw={"crossroads","darsok swiftdagger","dry hills","harpy lieutenant ring","the barrens","witchwing","witchwing slayer"},rel={"quest:875","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","subzone:dry-hills","quest:867","quest:876","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Harpy Lieutenant Ring","Harpy Lieutenants (Classic)"}}
E["item:heart-of-isha-awak"] = {t="item",n="Heart of Isha Awak",z="barrens",s="Hunters seek Isha Awak’s heart along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet. Mahren Skyseer wants it as proof that the Deep Doom has been overcome.",h="Hunters seek Isha Awak’s heart along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Deep Doom",b="Isha Awak prowls the sea off the Merchant Coast, south of Ratchet. Sailors and coastal folk revere and fear the massive thresher, known as the Deep Doom. It has killed many human trespassers along the shore. Mahren Skyseer, a tauren mystic, sees an honorable predator, not a mindless menace. She believes its fierce spirit dwells in its heart. Mahren charges brave hunters to plunge into the waves, defeat Isha Awak in its own domain, and claim the heart as both trophy and spiritual offering.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Heart of Isha Awak?",a="The Heart of Isha Awak is the heart of the giant thresher that prowls the waters south of Ratchet. Hunters claim it as proof of overcoming the Deep Doom for Mahren Skyseer.",al={"heart of isha awak","isha awak heart","what is this heart"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the Heart of Isha Awak?",a="Mahren Skyseer, a tauren seer camped along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet, wants hunters to retrieve the heart. She seeks to honor the beast’s power and absorb its spirit.",al={"who takes the heart","who do i give the heart to","mahren skyseer"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Isha Awak found?",a="Isha Awak dwells in the ocean off the Merchant Coast in the eastern Barrens, south of Ratchet.",al={"isha awak location","where is isha awak","where to find isha awak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Mahren Skyseer want the heart?",a="Mahren Skyseer considers Isha Awak an honorable hunter and worthy adversary. By slaying the beast and holding its heart, a hunter takes the sea creature’s spirit into themselves.",al={"why kill isha awak","why does mahren want the heart"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the Heart of Isha Awak come from?",a="The heart is not a crafted artifact, but an organ claimed directly from Isha Awak, the mighty sea beast known as the Deep Doom. The creature haunts the waters off the Barrens coast south of Ratchet, feared by the local humans whose kin it has consumed. Striking down this primal predator of the sea and carving out its heart is the only way to obtain it.",al={"heart of isha awak origin","where did heart of isha awak come from","who made heart of isha awak"},it="origin",add="1c3e01c4"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter, you pursue Isha Awak as an act of spiritual communion with nature’s fiercest predators, guided by the elder Mahren Skyseer.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face an ultimate test of courage when tracking and conquering the Deep Doom beneath the Merchant Coast’s waves."},kw={"deep doom","heart of isha awak","isha awak","mahren skyseer","merchant coast","ratchet","the barrens"},rel={"quest:873","quest:874","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","topic:human"},src={"Heart of Isha Awak","Isha Awak (quest)"}}
E["item:heartswood"] = {t="item",n="Heartswood",z="barrens",s="Heartswood is timber harvested from a sacred tree rooted within the Ruins of Ordil'Aran in northwestern Ashenvale. Born from the final resting place of two ancient lovers, its resonance with undying devotion makes it an essential lure for summoning a succubus.",h="Heartswood is timber harvested from a sacred tree rooted within the Ruins of Ordil'Aran in northwestern...",sec={{t="A Monument to Devotion",b="The Heartswood grows among the elven stones of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran in northwestern Ashenvale. According to legend, two lovers named Anathera and Latherion fell side by side during the catastrophic War of the Ancients thousands of years ago. On the very earth where they breathed their last, a peculiar tree took root, blossoming as an eternal testament to their devotion. Even millennia later, the wood cut from this tree hums with the memory of undying passion, making it an object of great curiosity for those who study emotional and spiritual bonds.",sp=0},{t="A Tool of Subjugation",b="While born of pure sentiment, Heartswood attracts darker attention. Succubi—demons that thrive on passion, longing, and emotional exploitation—are intensely drawn to artifacts imbued with genuine, undying love. Human and gnome warlocks under the instruction of Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind seek out this rare timber specifically to construct a ritual lure. By using the innate resonance of the lovers' sacrifice, a practitioner can bait a succubus across the Nether, draw her into a summoning circle, and bind her to their will.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Heartswood?",a="Heartswood is the wood taken from a tree that sprouted in Ashenvale's Ruins of Ordil'Aran, marking the spot where two ancient night elf lovers perished together during the War of the Ancients.",al={"heartswood tree","what is heartswood","heartswood lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who were Anathera and Latherion?",a="Anathera and Latherion were lovers who fought side by side during the War of the Ancients. When they both fell in battle, their final embrace nourished the earth, giving rise to the Heartswood tree as an enduring symbol of their devotion.",al={"anathera and latherion","lovers of heartswood","who died at heartswood"}},{q="Why do warlocks need Heartswood?",a="Succubi are demonic creatures of desire and emotional manipulation. Because the Heartswood resonates powerfully with the essence of unyielding, eternal love, warlocks use it as a potent psychic bait to tempt and summon a succubus into the physical world.",al={"why do warlocks want heartswood","heartswood succubus","heartswood purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Heartswood be found?",a="Heartswood is found within the Ruins of Ordil'Aran, located in the northwestern reaches of the Ashenvale forest near the border of Darkshore.",al={"heartswood location","where is heartswood","ruins of ordil'aran heartswood"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Heartswood come from, and who made it?",a="Heartswood is not crafted by mortal hands, but harvested from a solitary tree that sprouted in the ruins of Ordil'Aran in northwestern Ashenvale. During the catastrophic War of the Ancients millennia ago, two lovers named Anathera and Latherion fell together in battle. Where they took their final breaths, the tree took root and grew, standing as a living monument to their eternal devotion.",al={"heartswood origin","where does heartswood come from","how was heartswood created"},it="origin",add="61f35e8f"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For Alliance warlocks, securing Heartswood is a critical rite of passage directed by Gakin the Darkbinder, providing the emotional bait required to compel and bind a succubus minion.",["race:NightElf"]="The tree represents a tragic, sacred memorial from the War of the Ancients, making its desecration by warlocks and cultists a bitter offense against the memory of fallen ancestors."},kw={"anathera","ashenvale","gakin the darkbinder","heartswood","latherion","ordil'aran","succubus"},rel={"quest:1738","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","subzone:ruins-of-ordil-aran","zone:ashenvale","topic:war-of-the-ancients","quest:1685","quest:1739"},src={"Heartswood","Heartswood (quest)"}}
E["item:hezrul-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Hezrul's Head",z="barrens",s="At Lushwater Oasis, Hezrul Bloodmark leads the Kolkar centaur in the Barrens. His head is carried to Regthar Deathgate west of the Crossroads as proof their chieftain has fallen.",h="At Lushwater Oasis, Hezrul Bloodmark leads the Kolkar centaur in the Barrens.",sec={{t="Decapitating the Kolkar",b="Hezrul Bloodmark leads his Kolkar centaur clan from Lushwater Oasis, south of the Crossroads. The Kolkar hold the Barrens' oases and threaten Horde supply routes and young settlements. Regthar Deathgate, an orc veteran charged with securing the land west of the Crossroads, sees their fierce rage but little discipline. He demands Hezrul's severed head to break the clan's command and throw its surviving fighters into disarray, weakening their attacks on the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who does this head belong to?",a="The head belongs to Hezrul Bloodmark, the leader of the Kolkar centaur clan in the central Barrens.",al={"who is hezrul","hezrul identity","whose head is this"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Hezrul Bloodmark found?",a="Hezrul leads his band around Lushwater Oasis, south of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"hezrul location","where is hezrul","find hezrul"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Hezrul's Head?",a="Regthar Deathgate, an orc at a military outpost on the road west of the Crossroads, wants the head as proof Hezrul has been defeated.",al={"turn in hezrul head","who takes hezrul head","regthar deathgate"},it="target"},{q="Why does the Horde require his head instead of just driving him away?",a="The Horde needs certainty that Hezrul is dead. The centaur are volatile and prone to infighting, and removing their chieftain breaks their command and weakens their threat to the Crossroads.",al={"why kill hezrul","why take his head","centaur threat"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does Hezrul's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken from Hezrul Bloodmark, a cunning and brutal centaur chieftain found at the Lushwater Oasis south of the Crossroads. Hezrul leads the Kolkar tribe in the region, orchestrating their aggression against Horde outposts and neighboring settlements until struck down.",al={"origin of hezruls head","where did hezruls head come from","who did hezruls head come from"},it="origin",add="67b3da29"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, claiming the Kolkar chieftain's head secures vital water rights at Lushwater Oasis and protects Horde travelers crossing the Barrens.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may see the Kolkar as undisciplined ruffians whose fury yields to orcish battle discipline. Regthar sees the trophy as proof of martial honor."},kw={"bloodmark","centaur","crossroads","deathgate","hezrul","kolkar","lushwater","regthar"},rel={"quest:852","quest:851","quest:850","quest:4021","quest:1361","subzone:lushwater-oasis","subzone:crossroads","topic:centaur"},src={"Hezrul's Head","Hezrul Bloodmark (Classic)"}}
E["item:horn-of-echeyakee"] = {t="item",n="Horn of Echeyakee",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn gives hunters the Horn of Echeyakee. Sounded among the ancient kodo remains northeast of the settlement, it calls the legendary white predator of the Barrens.",h="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn gives hunters the Horn of Echeyakee.",sec={{t="Calling the Whitemist",b="Hunters who are being tested in the hunt receive the horn. Its call summons Echeyakee, whose name means “Whitemist” in Taur-ahe. Taure n hunters revere the king of the savannah cats as both mercy and death. He strikes so swiftly that his quarry feels neither terror nor suffering. The horn belongs at the predator’s lair, among giant kodo bones behind the hills northeast of the Crossroads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Horn of Echeyakee do?",a="The horn draws out Echeyakee, the elusive white savannah cat. Sound it near the giant kodo bones northeast of the Crossroads, and the beast appears for a hunter to face.",al={"use horn of echeyakee","what is horn of echeyakee for"},it="power"},{q="Where does the horn come from?",a="Sergra Darkthorn, an orc huntress at the Crossroads in the Barrens, gives the horn to adventurers seeking to prove their subtlety and tracking skill.",al={"who gives the horn","horn of echeyakee source"},it="origin"},{q="What does the name Echeyakee mean?",a="In Taur-ahe, the Tauren tongue, Echeyakee means “Whitemist.” The name honors the beast’s pale coat and his silent way of stalking through dry grasses undetected.",al={"echeyakee meaning","whitemist meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where do you blow the horn?",a="Sound the horn among the giant kodo ribs and skeletal remains behind the hills northeast of the Crossroads, where the white lion roams.",al={"where to use horn","echeyakee location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Horn of Echeyakee?",a="The Horn of Echeyakee is a ritual hunting instrument given to promising hunters at the Crossroads by Sergra Darkthorn. Blown among the giant kodo bones northeast of the settlement, its call draws out Echeyakee himself—the white lion revered by the tauren as the king of the savannah cats.",al={"horn of echeyakee","what is this horn","what is the horn of echeyakee"},it="identity",add="eb6b337d"},{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn give you the Horn of Echeyakee?",a="Sergra Darkthorn provides the horn as a vital tool for testing your prowess. Echeyakee stalks the plains unseen like a white mist, making him nearly impossible to track by sight alone. The horn's blast challenges the great predator, coaxing him out to fight so you may claim his hide and prove your hunting skill.",al={"why do i need the horn of echeyakee","why echeyakee horn","purpose of horn of echeyakee"},it="why_wanted",add="5884ea69"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face Echeyakee in a legendary rite of passage, testing your senses against a predator renowned across the Barrens for near-flawless stealth.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know Echeyakee’s hunt carries spiritual weight. Your people see his swift, painless kill as both mercy and the harsh necessity of death."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","echeyakee","horn","kodo bones","sergra darkthorn","whitemist"},rel={"quest:881","quest:860","item:echeyakee-s-hide","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},src={"Horn of Echeyakee","Echeyakee (Classic)"}}
E["item:ignition-key"] = {t="item",n="Ignition Key",z="barrens",s="At Sludge Fen, the Ignition Key is held by Supervisor Lugwizzle at the Venture Company drilling operation. Wizzlecrank needs it to unlock an advanced shredder's movement column and activate its controls.",h="At Sludge Fen, the Ignition Key is held by Supervisor Lugwizzle at the Venture Company drilling operation.",sec={{t="A Missing Piece of Espionage",b="Sputtervalve of Ratchet sent an operative to steal a Venture Company shredder from Sludge Fen, but the plan stalled. The undercover pilot, Wizzlecrank, climbed into the cockpit and found the movement column locked. He pretended the machine had mechanical trouble so the foremen would not grow suspicious while he waited for someone to fetch the Ignition Key. Supervisor Lugwizzle keeps the key high atop the central oil derrick, where access to the shredder's arm, speed, and rotation controls is held.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can the Ignition Key be found?",a="Supervisor Lugwizzle keeps the Ignition Key in the control room atop the oil derrick in Sludge Fen, where he oversees the drilling work.",al={"ignition key location","who drops ignition key","how to get ignition key"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizzlecrank need this specific key?",a="The advanced Venture Company shredder has a locked movement column. Without its ignition key, Wizzlecrank cannot control its rotation, speed, stability, or arm well enough to drive it away.",al={"why need key","what does key do","shredder key purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wants the shredder stolen?",a="Sputtervalve, a goblin engineer in Ratchet, arranged the theft to obtain the Venture Company's superior engineering designs.",al={"who sent wizzlecrank","why steal shredder","ratchet shredder"},it="motive"},{q="What happens once the key is delivered?",a="With the key, Wizzlecrank unlocks the movement column and starts the shredder's engine. He must then race through Sludge Fen's hostile laborers to escape toward Ratchet.",al={"after turning in key","the escape","what next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Ignition Key?",a="The Ignition Key is an operational key used to unlock the movement column of an advanced Venture Company shredder at the Sludge Fen. Without it, the heavy logging machine's controls remain locked, leaving the pilot unable to steer or drive.",al={"what is ignition key","ignition key use","shredder key"},it="identity",add="762c90b7"},{q="Where does the Ignition Key come from?",a="The key belongs to the Venture Company's drilling and logging operations in the Sludge Fen. It is held by Supervisor Lugwizzle, who oversees the site from the control room atop the central oil derrick.",al={"who made ignition key","origin of ignition key","where did the key come from"},it="origin",add="8801ec8f"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Ignition Key unlocks a shredder with advanced controls, including speed regulation and fine arm movement that outclass typical goblin designs."},kw={"ignition key","shredder","sludge fen","sputtervalve","supervisor lugwizzle","venture company","wizzlecrank"},rel={"quest:858","quest:114","subzone:sludge-fen","npc:sputtervalve","topic:venture-company","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Ignition Key","Ignition (Classic)"}}
E["item:intact-raptor-horn"] = {t="item",n="Intact Raptor Horn",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens savannas, raptors are hunted for their intact horns. Mebok Mizzyrix of Ratchet wants them for a scheme built on rumors of raptor intelligence.",h="Across the Barrens savannas, raptors are hunted for their intact horns.",sec={{t="A Questionable Ingredient",b="Hunters prize raptor hides, talons, and trophies, but whole horns are harder to take in the field. Mebok Mizzyrix, an eccentric goblin alchemist in Ratchet, believes the Barrens raptors are more cunning than their kin elsewhere. He suspects their intellect lies in their horns. By grinding whole horns and brewing them into tonics, Mebok hopes to bottle that supposed genius in commercial drinks.",sp=0},{t="Stalking the Prides",b="A horn fit for brewing must come from a particularly vicious predator, not just any young raptor. Sunscale Scytheclaws prowl the southern plains and the northern borders near Ashenvale. Takk the Leaper and the elusive Ishamuhale are notable terrors of the veldt, and their stout horns can survive the clash of the hunt intact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants these intact raptor horns?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin merchant and aspiring brewer in Ratchet, seeks intact horns. He believes they hold the key to his next get-rich-quick product.",al={"who needs raptor horns","horn buyer","who buys raptor horn"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do the horns need to be intact?",a="Mebok plans to grind whole horns into a fine powder for ingestion. Hunters discard chipped or broken horns, or consider them spent, because they lack the full potency he hopes to harness for his recipes.",al={"why intact","shattered horns"}},{q="Which raptors carry them?",a="Mature Sunscale Scytheclaws carry them in the northern and southern extremes of the Barrens. Notorious unique raptors, including Ishamuhale and Takk the Leaper, bear them too.",al={"where do horns drop","which raptors","who drops intact horn"},gp=true},{q="Do raptor horns actually make you smarter?",a="Barrens raptors show unusual pack cunning and coordination, but no one has proved their intelligence rests in their horns or can pass to someone through a drink.",al={"do smart drinks work","are raptors smart","raptor intelligence"},it="power"},{q="What is an Intact Raptor Horn?",a="An Intact Raptor Horn is an undamaged cranial horn harvested from the predatory raptors stalking the Barrens. These horns are valued by enterprising locals who believe their pristine condition preserves the natural essence and cunning of the beasts.",al={"intact raptor horn what is it","what is raptor horn"},it="identity",add="41f89fc5"},{q="Where do intact raptor horns come from?",a="These horns grow naturally upon the heads of Barrens raptors, notably sunscale scytheclaws as well as notorious beasts like Ishamuhale and Takk the Leaper. They are biological trophies taken directly from fallen raptors throughout the savannas.",al={"where do raptor horns come from","who drops intact raptor horn"},it="origin",add="b3ef4089"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, taking a trophy horn whole calls for a clean kill against some of the savannas' fiercest predators.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you may hear Mebok plans to pulverize the horns for wine infusions. Practical survivalists favor raptor parts for toolcrafting over palatable cuisine."},kw={"intact horn","ishamuhale","mebok mizzyrix","raptor horn","ratchet","smart drinks","sunscale scytheclaw","takk the leaper"},rel={"quest:865","quest:1491","npc:mebok-mizzyrix","quest:882","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Intact Raptor Horn","Raptor Horns"}}
E["item:ishamuhale-s-fang"] = {t="item",n="Ishamuhale's Fang",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Jorn Skyseer awaits Ishamuhale's Fang from the feared sunscale raptor Speartooth of the Barrens. The tooth proves the hunter bested one of Kalimdor's deadliest natural predators.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Jorn Skyseer awaits Ishamuhale's Fang from the feared sunscale raptor Speartooth of the...",sec={{t="Trophy of Speartooth",b="Across the central savanna, hunters fear Ishamuhale, the fiercest sunscale raptor alive. Some say the apex hunter kills from predatory passion, not hunger. Fresh zhevra meat draws the beast into the open beside a withered tree northwest of Ratchet, where it gives no quarter. Taking its massive fang proves to the Horde's hunting instructors that a traveler has overcome the savagery of the plains.",sp=0},{t="A Lesson in Temperance",b="At Camp Taurajo, Jorn Skyseer sees more than ivory and blood in Ishamuhale's fang. To the tauren there, taking it passes the predator's fierce strength to the hunter who bested him. The test that follows is temperance: the hunter must master that savage fury instead of letting it rule the soul.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Ishamuhale's Fang?",a="Ishamuhale's Fang is a trophy taken from Ishamuhale, the infamous Speartooth sunscale raptor that prowls the Barrens.",al={"ishamuhale tooth","speartooth fang","raptor fang barrens"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Ishamuhale's Fang?",a="Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo wants the fang, as part of the hunting trials that begin with Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.",al={"who do i give ishamuhale fang to","turn in ishamuhale fang","where does ishamuhale fang go"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How is the beast Ishamuhale found?",a="Ishamuhale is lured from hiding with a fresh zhevra carcass placed near a dead tree northwest of Ratchet.",al={"how to get ishamuhale to spawn","summon ishamuhale","where is ishamuhale"},gp=true},{q="What does claiming the fang represent to the tauren?",a="To the tauren, claiming Ishamuhale's Fang means the raptor's legendary strength now lives within the hunter, who must use that power with temperance and honor.",al={"meaning of the fang","tauren hunter ritual ishamuhale"},it="for_you"},{q="Where does Ishamuhale's Fang come from?",a="The fang is taken directly from the jaws of Ishamuhale, also known as Speartooth. He is the fiercest sunscale raptor roaming the Barrens, a natural predator who kills purely out of his savage instinct. It was not crafted by mortal hands, but grew naturally as a deadly weapon of the beast.",al={"ishamuhale fang origin","where did ishamuhale fang come from","who made ishamuhale fang"},it="origin",add="aa73e2a3"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, taking Speartooth's fang is a rite of passage across the Barrens. It tests your skill at baiting, facing, and overcoming a cunning predator.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, claiming the tooth means taking in a predator's raw power while keeping discipline and balance."},kw={"barrens","fang","ishamuhale","jorn","raptor","sergra","speartooth","sunscale","taurajo"},rel={"quest:882","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","quest:860"},src={"Ishamuhale's Fang","Ishamuhale (quest)"}}
E["item:kadrak-s-flag"] = {t="item",n="Kadrak's Flag",z="barrens",s="At the edge of the Barrens and Ashenvale, Kadrak gives the Horde a mark to carry into enemy ground. The flag is planted in the Talon Den after Keymaster Rynthariel is killed.",h="At the edge of the Barrens and Ashenvale, Kadrak gives the Horde a mark to carry into enemy ground.",sec={{t="A Mark of Defiance",b="Kadrak sends the Horde flag into the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak. The dryad Rynthariel, Keymaster of the Den, has sent communications across the border, and Kadrak decides her death alone will not answer them. He gives you the crimson banner to plant deep inside the Den. The Horde colors there carry a warning to the night elves and dryads: incursions across the Barrens will meet retaliation on Alliance soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Kadrak's Flag used for?",a="Plant Kadrak's Flag inside the Talon Den atop Stonetalon Peak after killing Rynthariel the Keymaster. The Horde banner warns the night elves against sending more scouts and messengers into the Barrens.",al={"flag purpose","why plant flag","what does flag do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you the flag?",a="Kadrak, an orc scout at the border watchpost between the northern Barrens and Ashenvale, gives you the banner as he works to secure the region.",al={"who gives flag","where to get flag","kadrak location"},it="origin"},{q="Where is the flag planted?",a="Plant the banner inside the Talon Den, a cavern sanctuary on the western slopes of Stonetalon Peak in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where do i plant flag","flag location","talon den flag spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Rynthariel?",a="Rynthariel is a dryad and Keymaster of the Talon Den. She sends messengers into Horde territory until Kadrak intercepts her communications and orders her killed.",al={"rynthariel dryad","who is rynthariel","keymaster"},it="target"},{q="What is Kadrak's Flag?",a="Kadrak's Flag is an emblem of the Horde, entrusted to you by the orc outpost commander Kadrak at the border between the Barrens and Ashenvale. Bearing the colors and sigil of the Horde, it serves as an unmistakable territorial marker meant to claim ground and broadcast an uncompromising message of defiance to Alliance forces venturing south.",al={"what is kadraks flag","kadrak flag","about kadraks flag"},it="identity",add="555b344d"},{q="Why does Kadrak want his flag planted in the Talon Den?",a="Kadrak wants the banner driven directly into the heart of the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak after the dryad leader Rynthariel is slain. Planting the Horde's standard within their sanctuary ensures that any surviving outrunners or Alliance sympathizers understand that trespassing into Horde territory will be met with decisive, lethal retaliation.",al={"why plant kadraks flag","why does kadrak want the flag placed","purpose of planting flag"},it="why_wanted",add="52bd9818"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Planting the banner deep inside the Talon Den declares the Horde's strength and shows it will strike night elf sanctuaries when provoked.",["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, the Horde banner inside the Talon Den is a direct insult to the protectors of Stonetalon Peak."},kw={"barrens","horde presence","kadrak","kadrak's flag","rynthariel","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","talon den"},rel={"quest:3514","npc:kadrak","zone:stonetalon","subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:barrens","quest:3513","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Kadrak's Flag","Horde Presence"}}
E["item:khazgorm-s-journal"] = {t="item",n="Khazgorm's Journal",z="barrens",s="At Bael Modan, Prospector Khazgorm leads the Ironforge dwarven excavation in the southern Barrens. His field ledger records the Explorers' League's work on lands claimed by the Stonespire tauren.",h="At Bael Modan, Prospector Khazgorm leads the Ironforge dwarven excavation in the southern Barrens.",sec={{t="A Record of Destruction",b="Prospector Khazgorm directs the heavy machinery and blasting that cut into the southern Barrens hillsides. His notes show an excavation far from the Explorers' League's promised search for knowledge: its work has displaced the Stonespire tribe. The tauren tried to settle matters peacefully, but the dwarves refused. Gann Stonespire wants the journal to understand the Ironforge presence in his homeland and find a way to break it.",sp=0},{t="A Shift in Tactics",b="Gann Stonespire finds the journal among Khazgorm's remains, near the tents and pillars of the digsite. The notes show him how the dwarf expedition is organized, what equipment it uses, and where it is vulnerable. With that knowledge, Gann turns from driving back laborers to striking the excavation's machinery. The journal changes the struggle over Bael Modan.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who does the journal belong to?",a="The journal belongs to Prospector Khazgorm, a leader of the Ironforge dwarven excavation at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens.",al={"who owns the journal","khazgorm","prospector khazgorm"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gann Stonespire want this book?",a="Gann Stonespire wants the journal to study the plans and secrets of the dwarves who displaced his tribe. Khazgorm's notes help him plan further strikes against the Bael Modan encampment.",al={"why gann wants journal","gann quest journal","ganns reclamation book"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can the journal be found?",a="Prospector Khazgorm carries the journal among the tents and rock pillars of the active excavation just south of Bael Modan.",al={"where is khazgorms journal","find khazgorms journal","khazgorm location"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What does the journal reveal about the dwarves?",a="The journal shows the Explorers' League's pursuit of buried relics and Titan heritage comes at the direct, violent expense of tribes such as the Stonespire tauren.",al={"explorers league barrens","dwarf digsite secrets","bael modan purpose"}},{q="Where does Khazgorm's Journal come from, and who made it?",a="The journal was penned by Prospector Khazgorm, a leader among the dwarven excavators of the Explorers' League stationed at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens. Khazgorm kept the book to record his expedition's findings and daily affairs while tearing through the ancestral lands of the Stonespire tauren.",al={"khazgorm journal origin","who wrote khazgorm's journal","where did khazgorm journal come from"},it="origin",add="6ed76dba"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see the journal as evidence of the Ironforge invaders' disregard for the Stonespire tribe as they blast its ancestral lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help Gann Stonespire defend Kalimdor from Alliance expeditions pressing into Horde territory."},kw={"bael modan","barrens","dwarf","explorers' league","gann stonespire","journal","khazgorm","prospector"},rel={"npc:gann-stonespire","quest:843","quest:846","subzone:bael-modan","topic:explorers-league","topic:tauren","zone:barrens","topic:dwarf"},src={"Khazgorm's Journal","Gann's Reclamation"}}
E["item:kodo-horn"] = {t="item",n="Kodo Horn",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Kodo Horns are gathered from the roaming kodos. Tonga Runetotem uses them in herbal remedies for poisoned wildlife.",h="In the Barrens, Kodo Horns are gathered from the roaming kodos.",sec={{t="A Reagent of the Plains",b="Across the Barrens, Tonga Runetotem uses intact kodo horns in his herbal remedies. He works from the Crossroads, where the horns help strengthen his salves. Chips and fragments lack the strength he needs, so he gathers whole horns from mature kodos wandering the plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Kodo Horns used for?",a="Tonga Runetotem uses Kodo Horns with Earthroot and pure water to brew a salve for poisoned gazelles across the Barrens. Making the remedy is part of a druid's training in natural cures for poison.",al={"kodo horn purpose","why gather kodo horns","use of kodo horn"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these horns collected?",a="You can gather them from Barrens Kodos and Lost Barrens Kodos in the northern Barrens, between the Crossroads and the surrounding scrubland.",al={"where to find kodo horns","kodo horn location","which kodos drop horns"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why can't druids use horn fragments instead?",a="Tonga Runetotem says chips and fragments lack the potency to balance the salve. He needs intact horns to make a remedy strong enough to counter virulent toxins.",al={"why not broken horns","horn chips"}},{q="Is hunting kodos considered respectful for a druid?",a="Yes. Druids hunt kodos when it serves nature's balance, taking what they need to heal larger blights, such as the mysterious poisoning afflicting the native gazelle herds.",al={"druid hunting kodos","balance and kodos"}},{q="What is a Kodo Horn?",a="It is an intact horn harvested from the massive kodos roaming the northern savannas of the Barrens. While often utilized in tribal crafts or tools, whole and sturdy horns are prized by shamans and druids as potent alchemical reagents, capable of infusing medicinal mixtures with strong natural fortitude.",al={"what is kodo horn","kodo horn","about kodo horn"},it="identity",add="f5876d60"},{q="Where do Kodo Horns come from?",a="These horns come directly from the Barrens kodos that graze across the arid plains. Bringing down one of these formidable beasts allows hunters and druids to claim an intact horn, provided it has not been shattered or worn down into mere chips and fragments.",al={"where does kodo horn come from","kodo horn origin","how to get kodo horn"},it="origin",add="062d3e91"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Horde druid, you gather horns under Tonga Runetotem's guidance as you learn to master nature's poisons.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you hold kodos in high reverence and take from them with care and purpose, here to safeguard the Barrens' delicate ecosystem."},kw={"barrens","cenarion","earthroot","gazelle","kodo horn","poison","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","quest:6123","quest:6125","topic:druid","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:horde"},src={"Kodo Horn","Gathering the Cure (Horde)"}}
E["item:kodo-liver"] = {t="item",n="Kodo Liver",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Brewmaster Drohn needs Kodo Liver for a strange ale. He learned to brew trogg ale from the wandering brewmaster Chen Stormstout.",h="In Ratchet, Brewmaster Drohn needs Kodo Liver for a strange ale.",sec={{t="A Bizarre Brewing Reagent",b="Kodos roam the Barrens, where tauren and predators hunt them for their hides and meat. In Ratchet, Brewmaster Drohn uses a fresh Kodo Liver with thunderhawk saliva glands and lightning glands to make trogg ale. Chen Stormstout taught Drohn the recipe, and Drohn says the blend packs a potent kick for adventurous travelers. The ingredients come from the wilds of central Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Kodo Liver used for?",a="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet uses Kodo Liver in trogg ale. Chen Stormstout taught him the recipe.",al={"kodo liver purpose","why need kodo liver","what is kodo liver for"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Which creatures yield a Kodo Liver?",a="Kodo Liver comes from kodos in the Barrens, including common, wooly, lost, and greater kodos, as well as Lakota'mani and Brontus.",al={"where to get kodo liver","who drops kodo liver","kodo liver source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why would anyone put animal organs in ale?",a="Brewmaster Drohn follows the eccentric recipes Chen Stormstout taught him. In trogg ale, raw organs such as Kodo Liver and elemental glands give the drink its kick and sharp flavor.",al={"why liver in beer","kodo liver in alcohol"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Kodo Liver?",a="It is an internal organ harvested from the massive, thick-skinned kodos that roam the plains of the Barrens. While not typical tavern fare, its potent nature makes it a prized component for eccentric brewmasters who craft concoctions with a truly legendary bite.",al={"what is kodo liver","kodo liver lore","kodo liver"},it="identity",add="a4c717e9"},{q="Where does a Kodo Liver come from?",a="It is gathered directly from the wild kodos roaming the savannah of the Barrens, from common wandering beasts to ancient behemoths like Lakota'mani and Brontus. Hunters and adventurers carve it out after felling the massive creatures.",al={"where do you get kodo liver","who drops kodo liver","kodo liver source"},it="origin",add="c325e464"},{q="Why does Brewmaster Drohn want a Kodo Liver?",a="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet seeks a fresh liver to brew an unconventional trogg ale recipe taught to him by the wandering pandaren brewmaster, Chen Stormstout. Combined with lightning glands and thunderhawk saliva, the liver gives the potent beverage its distinctive kick.",al={"why does drohn need kodo liver","who wants kodo liver","kodo liver quest use"},it="why_wanted",add="328036a8"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Kodo meat feeds people across central Kalimdor, but Kodo Liver is considered too foul and pungent for ordinary cooking. Its use in Ratchet's trogg ale has made it notorious.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren honor every part of the kodo they hunt. Even seasoned plainsrunners look askance at goblins and foreigners who make novelty ale from kodo innards in Ratchet."},kw={"barrens","brewing","chen stormstout","drohn","kodo","kodo liver","ratchet","trogg ale"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","quest:819","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","quest:883","item:lightning-gland","item:thunderhawk-saliva-gland","topic:trogg"},src={"Kodo Liver","Chen's Empty Keg (3)"}}
E["item:kodobane-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Kodobane's Head",z="barrens",s="Near the Forgotten Pools, Barak Kodobane's severed head proves the cunning chieftain's death. The orc warlord Regthar Deathgate receives it as proof that the centaur threat there has been broken.",h="Near the Forgotten Pools, Barak Kodobane's severed head proves the cunning chieftain's death.",sec={{t="A Trophy of War",b="Kolkar bands in the Barrens have long been divided, but ambitious warlords now threaten to gather them into an army. Barak Kodobane made his camp by the lush waters of the Forgotten Pools, where the oasis offers vital resources and nearby paths lie open to raids. Regthar Deathgate, stationed in a bunker west of the Crossroads, demands Kodobane's severed head as proof that this commander can no longer rally his kin against the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Barak Kodobane?",a="Barak Kodobane was a prominent chieftain among the Kolkar centaur. Cunning and commanding where many of his kin were undisciplined, he organized warbands and camped around the Forgotten Pools to assert Kolkar dominance over the northern Barrens.",al={"barak kodobane","who is kodobane","barak lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Regthar Deathgate want his head?",a="Regthar Deathgate is tasked with securing Horde territory in the Barrens. The centaur are usually fractious, so leaders with tactical vision are singled out. Regthar demands Kodobane's head to make certain the chieftain is dead, not merely displaced.",al={"why get head","regthar deathgate head","kodobane bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Barak Kodobane found?",a="Barak Kodobane camps near the Forgotten Pools, the northern oasis just northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"barak location","where is kodobane","barak spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does killing Barak stop the Kolkar threat?",a="No. Barak Kodobane is the first of several warlords rallying the Kolkar. His death disrupts their presence at the Forgotten Pools, but Verog the Dervish and Hezrul Bloodmark continue to direct centaur aggression across the Barrens.",al={"are centaurs defeated","what happens after barak dies"},it="threat"},{q="What is Kodobane's Head?",a="It is the severed head of Barak Kodobane, one of the prominent chieftains among the Kolkar centaur in the Barrens. Kept as physical proof of the chieftain's demise, it signifies a decisive blow struck against the coordinated centaur threat menacing Horde settlements near the Forgotten Pools.",al={"what is kodobanes head","barak kodobane head item","baraks head lore"},it="item",add="891c4b09"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For generations, the centaur drove the nomadic tauren across Kalimdor to the brink of extinction. Killing Barak Kodobane avenges centuries of bloodshed and protects the pastures of Mulgore and the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="The Barrens crossroads link Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff by land. Suppressing centaur leaders like Kodobane helps keep caravan trails safe."},kw={"barak","barrens","centaur","crossroads","deathgate","forgotten pools","kodobane","kolkar","regthar"},rel={"quest:850","quest:1361","subzone:forgotten-pools","quest:851","quest:852","topic:centaur","topic:tauren","zone:barrens"},src={"Kodobane's Head","Kolkar Leaders (Classic)"}}
E["item:kreenig-snarlsnout-s-tusk"] = {t="item",n="Kreenig Snarlsnout's Tusk",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Thork seeks proof that Kreenig Snarlsnout has fallen. His tusk marks the end of the Razormane leader's attacks on Horde caravans in the northern Barrens.",h="At the Crossroads, Thork seeks proof that Kreenig Snarlsnout has fallen.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Severed Ambition",b="Horde caravans traveling west from Durotar face constant attacks in the Barrens. Those raids grew bolder under Kreenig Snarlsnout, a fierce Razormane leader. Thork, commander of the Crossroads watch, ordered Kreenig killed to disrupt the quilboars' coordination. His tusk offers proof that the leader is dead and insults the Razormane, weakening their resolve and leaving their fighters without central direction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Kreenig Snarlsnout?",a="Kreenig Snarlsnout led the Razormane quilboar encamped northeast of the Crossroads. He organized attacks on Horde caravans traveling along the main road from Durotar, making the supply route dangerous until his death.",al={"kreenig snarlsnout","who is kreenig","snarlsnout lore"},it="people"},{q="Why does Thork want the tusk specifically?",a="Thork wants the tusk as proof that Kreenig is dead and as an insult to the Razormane. Taking a fallen chieftain's tusk wounds their pride and demoralizes the surviving raiders.",al={"why tusk","why bring tusk to thork","thork tusk"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where was this tusk taken?",a="The tusk comes from Kreenig Snarlsnout's camp northeast of the Crossroads, near the mountain foothills just south of the main road crossing from Durotar into the Barrens.",al={"where is kreenig","where to get tusk","snarlsnout location"},it="origin"},{q="What effect does taking Kreenig down have on the Barrens?",a="Thork believes the Razormane raiders will falter without Kreenig's leadership. His death throws their ranks into disarray and curbs further attacks on vital supply shipments.",al={"did raids stop","consequences of kreenig death"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Kreenig Snarlsnout's Tusk?",a="It is a severed quilboar tusk claimed as a grim trophy from Kreenig Snarlsnout, the leader of the Razormane raiders northeast of the Crossroads. Thork demanded it both as undeniable proof of the chieftain's death and to add bitter insult to the quilboars' injury, demonstrating to the remaining tribe that their raid leader has fallen.",al={"what is kreenigs tusk","kreenig snarlsnout tusk item"},it="identity",add="4371b9f1"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Caravans carry weapons, provisions, and settlers from Durotar, sustaining the Horde's expansion into the Barrens. Bringing Thork this tusk helps protect those lifelines.",["race:Orc"]="For an orc of the Crossroads, taking a trophy from a defeated commander is practical warfare: it shows strength and sows panic among the enemy."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","kreenig","quilboar","razormane","snarlsnout","thork","tusk"},rel={"quest:872","npc:thork","topic:quilboar","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","quest:5041"},src={"Kreenig Snarlsnout's Tusk","The Disruption Ends"}}
E["item:kuz-s-skull"] = {t="item",n="Kuz's Skull",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Kuz's Skull marks the end of a feared Razormane raider. Kuz came from Razorfen Kraul and helped lead attacks on Horde outposts before a captive former kin sought vengeance.",h="In the southern Barrens, Kuz's Skull marks the end of a feared Razormane raider.",sec={{t="A Bitter Feud",b="Kuz, Nak, and their chieftain Lok Orcbane led Razormane attacks across the southern Barrens. Sent from Razorfen Kraul, the three raiders struck travelers and settlements such as the Crossroads. Their betrayal of Mangletooth, a fellow quilboar, turned one of their own against them. They left Mangletooth to rot in a cage at Camp Taurajo. From that cage, he revealed Kuz's location to Horde champions willing to kill the raider and take her head.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Retribution",b="Kuz's Skull proves to Mangletooth that one of the three leaders of the southern warband is dead. For him, the head brings satisfaction against the tribe that abandoned him. Across the Barrens, Kuz's death breaks the command behind the Razormane attacks and gives the supply roads across the plains a brief respite.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Kuz?",a="Kuz was one of three Razormane quilboar sent from Razorfen Kraul into the southern Barrens. With Nak and Lok Orcbane, she directed ambushes and raids against Horde encampments and supply lines.",al={"who is kuz","kuz lore","kuz razormane"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mangletooth want Kuz's skull?",a="Mangletooth wants Kuz's skull because Kuz and the other Razormane left him to die in a cage at Camp Taurajo. Seeking vengeance before his own death, he points Horde champions toward his rivals and asks for their skulls as proof.",al={"why mangletooth wants kuz dead","mangletooth revenge"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Kuz found in the Barrens?",a="Kuz is found in the southern Barrens, with the Razormane quilboar south of Camp Taurajo near the thorny border regions.",al={"kuz location","where to find kuz"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Kuz is slain?",a="When Kuz's Skull and the heads of Nak and Lok Orcbane reach Mangletooth, they break the leadership behind the Razormane attacks and help secure the southern trade routes.",al={"kuz quest reward","betrayal from within outcome"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does Kuz's Skull come from?",a="The skull is taken directly from the remains of Kuz, a prominent Razormane quilboar operating in the southern Barrens. Emerging from Razorfen Kraul alongside her fellow raiders, Kuz helped orchestrate violent attacks against the Horde before being hunted down.",al={"where did kuz skull come from","who made kuz skull","kuz skull origin"},it="origin",add="9baef7d0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, taking Kuz's head helps protect settlements such as the Crossroads and Camp Taurajo from organized quilboar attacks."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","kuz","kuz's skull","lok orcbane","mangletooth","nak","razormane"},rel={"quest:879","npc:mangletooth","item:nak-s-skull","item:lok-s-skull","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:barrens","npc:thork","topic:horde"},src={"Kuz's Skull","Betrayal from Within (1)"}}
E["item:large-soran-ruk-fragment"] = {t="item",n="Large Soran'ruk Fragment",z="barrens",s="The Large Soran'ruk Fragment rests in Shadowfang Keep, far from the other shards. Its broken orb once held a disgraced demon of the Burning Legion.",h="The Large Soran'ruk Fragment rests in Shadowfang Keep, far from the other shards.",sec={{t="The Legacy of Soran'ruk",b="Disgraced demons of the Burning Legion may be condemned to imprisonment in enchanted orbs. Mages and warlocks aligned with the Legion receive these vessels and draw on the fel forces trapped within. Even when an orb is shattered, its bound fiend's lingering essence still radiates power. Each fragment draws ambitious practitioners of shadow magic.",sp=0},{t="The Shard in Shadowfang",b="The orb of Soran'ruk was cracked into two halves long ago. Cultists elsewhere scattered one half into smaller pieces. A sorcerer in the cursed Shadowfang Keep claimed the larger half. The Shadowfang Darksouls carry the Large Soran'ruk Fragment, which holds the bound spirit until someone seeks to reforge the ancient vessel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Large Soran'ruk Fragment?",a="The Large Soran'ruk Fragment is the larger half of the Orb of Soran'ruk, an ancient vessel holding the bound spirit of a disgraced Burning Legion demon.",al={"large soranruk fragment","soranruk large fragment","what is this fragment"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the fragment found?",a="The Shadowfang Darksouls hold the fragment in Shadowfang Keep, a haunted fortress in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where do i find the large fragment","large fragment location","who drops large soranruk fragment"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the orb broken?",a="The original orb was split into two main pieces. The smaller half was broken into shards and carried to the coastal caverns of Blackfathom Deeps, while dark wizards kept the larger half in Shadowfang Keep.",al={"how did the orb break","why is the orb fragmented","orb of soranruk history"},it="history"},{q="Who wants to reassemble it?",a="Doan Karhan, a reclusive hermit in the southern Barrens, has devoted his life to studying and reconstructing the lost orbs of the Burning Legion.",al={"who needs the large fragment","who reassembles the orb"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the Large Soran'ruk Fragment come from, and who made it?",a="The fragment was once part of the Orb of Soran'ruk, an artifact created by the Burning Legion. When Legion demons fall out of favor, their spirits are bound inside orbs and given to mortal mages and warlocks. Soran'ruk was one such demon, its essence imprisoned to fuel demonic magic. The orb was later split into two pieces, with this larger shard falling into the hands of a dark spellcaster within Shadowfang Keep.",al={"soranruk fragment origin","who made orb of soranruk","where did soranruk come from"},it="origin",add="0cdd1dfd"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Reclaiming the Large Soran'ruk Fragment lets you master the trapped demonic spirit inside and aid Doan Karhan in reconstructing a potent weapon for demonic arts."},kw={"burning legion","doan karhan","large soran'ruk fragment","orb of soran'ruk","shadowfang keep","soran'ruk"},rel={"quest:1740","item:soran-ruk-fragment","npc:doan-karhan","zone:shadowfang","topic:burning-legion","topic:warlock"},src={"Large Soran'ruk Fragment","The Orb of Soran'ruk"}}
E["item:lightning-gland"] = {t="item",n="Lightning Gland",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Lightning Glands are taken from stormhides roaming the plains. Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet needs them for trogg ale, a fiery brew Chen Stormstout taught him to make.",h="In the Barrens, Lightning Glands are taken from stormhides roaming the plains.",sec={{t="A Shocking Ingredient",b="Stormhides roam the Barrens savannas among other predators touched by the elements. Their flesh holds lightning glands, organs charged with latent electricity. These glands are poor fare on their own, but brewers prize them for the sting they bring to a brew.",sp=0},{t="Drohn's Trogg Ale",b="Brewmaster Drohn keeps Chen Stormstout’s brewing traditions alive in Ratchet. To make trogg ale, a potent brew, Drohn needs five lightning glands, a thunderhawk saliva gland, and a fresh kodo liver. The finished drink has a sharp kick that adventurers find invigorating and potent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures carry lightning glands?",a="Stormhides roaming the Barrens savannas carry lightning glands.",al={"where to get lightning gland","who drops lightning gland","stormhide lightning gland"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants lightning glands and why?",a="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet wants lightning glands for trogg ale, a recipe taught to him by the wandering brewmaster Chen Stormstout.",al={"who needs lightning gland","lightning gland turn in","lightning gland purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What else is needed alongside the lightning gland?",a="Drohn needs five lightning glands, a thunderhawk saliva gland from greater thunderhawks, and a fresh kodo liver from the beasts of the Barrens.",al={"drohn trogg ale ingredients","chen's keg 3 items"},gp=true},{q="What is a lightning gland?",a="A lightning gland is an organ harvested from stormhide beasts roaming the Barrens. Imbued with the natural electrical energies that surge through these creatures, the gland holds a potent elemental charge that makes it prized as an exotic brewing ingredient.",al={"what is lightning gland","lightning gland lore","what is a lightning gland"},it="identity",add="f0cc18d7"},{q="Where does a lightning gland come from?",a="Lightning glands are not crafted by mortal hands; they are biological organs taken directly from the stormhides that stalk the savannas of the Barrens. These wild beasts naturally develop the glands to channel crackling electrical energy.",al={"where do lightning glands come from","lightning gland origin","how are lightning glands made"},it="origin",add="ba679c5d"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can see how Brewmaster Drohn and Chen Stormstout use raw beast organs in spirits, though lightning glands are not ordinary food."},kw={"barrens","brewmaster drohn","chen stormstout","lightning gland","ratchet","stormhide","trogg ale"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","quest:819","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","item:thunderhawk-saliva-gland","item:kodo-liver","topic:trogg"},src={"Lightning Gland","Chen's Empty Keg (3)"}}
E["item:lok-s-skull"] = {t="item",n="Lok's Skull",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Lok's Skull marks the fall of a feared Razormane leader. Lok Orcbane led fierce quilboar raids against Horde supply routes, and the skull is his severed head.",h="In the southern Barrens, Lok's Skull marks the fall of a feared Razormane leader.",sec={{t="A Chieftain's Fall",b="Lok Orcbane led aggressive Razormane assaults on Horde supply lines in the southern Barrens. He emerged from Razorfen Kraul with his lieutenants Nak and Kuz. After betraying Mangletooth and leaving him captive at Camp Taurajo, Lok became known to orcish defenders for ruthless raids they struggled to contain. Mangletooth directs Horde champions to Lok's camp, where claiming Lok's skull avenges the captive and strikes at the leadership driving the Razormane offensive.",sp=0},{t="Proof for the Crossroads",b="Mangletooth demands the skulls of all three conspirators for his vengeance, then sends Lok's skull north to Thork at the Crossroads. Thork and the Horde command suspected another quilboar led the raids. Lok's skull came as a grim surprise, and proved that the threat to the Barrens' central trade routes had been cut down.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Lok Orcbane?",a="Lok Orcbane was a formidable Razormane warrior who emerged from Razorfen Kraul to lead quilboar raiding parties across the southern Barrens. He hated orcs and led aggressive assaults on Horde caravans and outposts with his trusted allies Nak and Kuz.",al={"who is lok","lok orcbane lore","who was lok orcbane"},it="people"},{q="Why does Mangletooth want Lok's Skull?",a="Lok Orcbane and his companions betrayed Mangletooth and left him to be captured and caged by the tauren at Camp Taurajo. Certain his own death is near, Mangletooth seeks vengeance on those who abandoned him and directs Horde adventurers to kill his former comrades.",al={"why mangletooth want skull","mangletooth revenge","why kill lok"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the skull brought to Thork at the Crossroads?",a="Thork oversees the Crossroads' defense and works to protect Horde supply routes from quilboar attacks. Lok's Skull proves to the orc commander that the leader of the southern raids has been slain, bringing safety to travelers in the region.",al={"why bring skull to thork","thork lok skull","who gets loks skull"},it="next_step"},{q="Who were Nak and Kuz?",a="Nak and Kuz led raids alongside Lok Orcbane in the southern Barrens. Mangletooth says one was a spellcaster and the other a tracker, backing Lok's strength as a warrior in raids against the Horde.",al={"nak and kuz","lok orcbane lieutenants","kuz and nak"},it="people"},{q="What is Lok's Skull?",a="Lok's Skull is the severed head of Lok Orcbane, a fierce warrior who led ruthless Razormane quilboar raids against Horde supply routes across the southern Barrens. Taken as grim proof of his death, it serves both as an instrument of vengeance for a betrayed tribesman and as undeniable evidence for the defenders of the Crossroads that the menace has been ended.",al={"what is loks skull","lok skull item","what is this skull"},it="identity",add="a8e2f7c2"},{q="Where does Lok's Skull come from?",a="It is taken directly from the slain body of Lok Orcbane in the southern Barrens. Lok and his lieutenants emerged from Razorfen Kraul to organize raiding parties against the Horde, until Mangletooth, an outcast quilboar held at Camp Taurajo, revealed their stronghold so that Lok could be brought down.",al={"where did lok skull come from","who made loks skull","source of loks skull"},it="origin",add="4d726f58"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, taking Lok Orcbane's skull breaks the southern quilboar leadership that harasses supply caravans between Camp Taurajo and the Crossroads.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, displaying the severed head of a quilboar chieftain named 'Orcbane' brings deep satisfaction and safety to those defending the Barrens."},kw={"betrayal from within","camp taurajo","crossroads","lok orcbane","lok's skull","mangletooth","razormane","thork"},rel={"quest:879","npc:mangletooth","npc:thork","item:nak-s-skull","item:kuz-s-skull","subzone:crossroads","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:quilboar"},src={"Lok's Skull","Betrayal from Within (1)","Betrayal from Within (2)"}}
E["item:nak-s-skull"] = {t="item",n="Nak's Skull",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Nak leads Razormane warbands against the Horde. His skull proves his defeat and gives Mangletooth a means to avenge betrayal by his former kin.",h="In the southern Barrens, Nak leads Razormane warbands against the Horde.",sec={{t="A Token of Vengeance",b="Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane lead raids from Razorfen Kraul across the Barrens. Their warbands strike Horde settlements and roads, while defenders at the Crossroads do not know the three commanders are planning attacks beyond ordinary tribal skirmishing. At Camp Taurajo, the captive Razormane Mangletooth has been left to die in a cage by his own people. He now seeks revenge against those former brethren. Mangletooth demands proof that Nak and his companions are dead: their severed skulls, delivered by Horde adventurers. He means to use that proof to break the southern raiding parties.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Nak?",a="Nak is a Razormane quilboar commander who leads raids with Kuz and Lok Orcbane. The three emerged from Razorfen Kraul and strike Horde travelers and settlements across the southern Barrens.",al={"who is nak","nak lore","nak barrens"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Nak's Skull?",a="Mangletooth, a captive Razormane quilboar at Camp Taurajo, wants Nak's Skull. His own kin abandoned him, and he seeks revenge on the leaders who betrayed him.",al={"who wants the skull","who do i give naks skull to","mangletooth skull"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Mangletooth want the skulls of his own people?",a="Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane abandoned Mangletooth to die in captivity. He retaliates by helping the Horde find them and demanding their severed heads as proof they are dead.",al={"why betray his tribe","mangletooth motive","why does mangletooth want skulls"},it="motive"},{q="Does collecting Nak's Skull help protect the Crossroads?",a="Yes. Mangletooth says Nak and his partners direct Razormane raids against the Crossroads and the central trade routes. Their defeat weakens the tribe's coordinated attacks.",al={"crossroads safe","stop quilboar raids"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Nak's Skull come from?",a="The skull is taken directly from the remains of Nak, a prominent Razormane quilboar who emerged from Razorfen Kraul. Nak and his brethren traveled far into the southern reaches of the Barrens to orchestrate ruthless raids against Horde encampments. When you hunt down Nak among the southern brambles and defeat him, his severed skull serves as indisputable proof that this dangerous quilboar raider has been eliminated.",al={"nak skull origin","where does nak skull come from","who has naks skull"},it="origin",add="96a0c2b0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can ease pressure on supply lines between Camp Taurajo and the Crossroads by taking the heads of Razormane warlords like Nak."},kw={"barrens","betrayal from within","camp taurajo","kuz","lok orcbane","mangletooth","nak","nak's skull","quilboar","razormane"},rel={"quest:879","npc:mangletooth","subzone:camp-taurajo","item:kuz-s-skull","item:lok-s-skull","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Nak's Skull","Betrayal from Within (1)"}}
E["item:nitroglycerin"] = {t="item",n="Nitroglycerin",z="barrens",s="At Bael Modan, Nitroglycerin helps the dwarves drive their excavation through tauren lands. Their soldiers and officers carry the volatile chemical, which can also be used against the fortress.",h="At Bael Modan, Nitroglycerin helps the dwarves drive their excavation through tauren lands.",sec={{t="Industrial Demolition",b="Bael Modan's dwarves dig into the ancestral lands of the Stonespire tauren with heavy drillers and volatile chemicals. At the excavation site and its fortified keep, they keep nitroglycerin close to blast deep holes and break apart hills. Soldiers and officers, including Lord Cyrik Blackforge, carry vials of the fluid as the digging continues.",sp=0},{t="A Taste of Their Own Medicine",b="After Prospector Khazgorm dies, Gann Stonespire seeks to destroy the encroaching fortress. The displaced tauren brave studies dwarven engineering plans and learns that nitroglycerin combined with wood pulp and sodium nitrate makes a charge strong enough to strike Bael Modan's military garrison.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does nitroglycerin come from?",a="Dwarven forces at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens carry nitroglycerin, including Bael'dun Soldiers, Riflemen, Officers, and Lord Cyrik Blackforge in the keep.",al={"where to find nitroglycerin","who drops nitroglycerin","nitroglycerin source"},it="origin"},{q="What is the nitroglycerin used for?",a="Gann Stonespire combines nitroglycerin with wood pulp and sodium nitrate to make a powerful charge against the military fortress at Bael Modan.",al={"what is nitroglycerin for","nitroglycerin purpose","revenge of gann ingredients"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why were the dwarves carrying it in the first place?",a="The Bael Modan prospectors and garrison use explosives, steam engines, and volatile chemicals to open the earth at their archaeological dig site.",al={"why do dwarves have nitroglycerin","bael modan explosives"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Gann Stonespire?",a="Gann Stonespire is an exiled tauren warrior whose tribe lost its ancestral lands when the dwarves built the Bael Modan excavation site and keep, driving them out through industrial destruction.",al={"who is gann","gann stonespire"},it="people"},{q="What is Nitroglycerin?",a="Nitroglycerin is a volatile chemical substance carried by the dwarven forces entrenched at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens. The Bael'dun expedition relies on heavy engineering and blasting materials to excavate ancestral tauren lands and tear open the earth. In volatile mixtures, it serves as a critical component in constructing high-yield explosive charges.",al={"what is nitroglycerin","nitroglycerin item lore","what does nitroglycerin do"},it="identity",add="9ba54f78"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers know nitroglycerin as a compounding explosive. Wood pulp absorbs it, and sodium nitrate helps make it stable and detonable.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the volatile chemicals around Bael Modan as a bitter mark of the destruction inflicted on the Stonespire tribe."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun","barrens","explosives","gann stonespire","nitroglycerin","revenge of gann"},rel={"quest:846","npc:gann-stonespire","subzone:bael-modan","item:sodium-nitrate","item:wood-pulp","quest:843","zone:barrens"},src={"Nitroglycerin","Revenge of Gann"}}
E["item:nugget-slug"] = {t="item",n="Nugget Slug",z="barrens",s="Nugget slugs are specialized 17.5-gauge mechanical fasteners used in industrial engineering. Stockpiled in tool buckets by the Venture Company at the Sludge Fen, they are coveted by tinkerers attempting to repair volatile machinery.",h="Nugget slugs are specialized 17.5-gauge mechanical fasteners used in industrial engineering.",sec={{t="Industrial Fasteners of the Sludge Fen",b="Nugget slugs are heavy-duty metallic fasteners manufactured for demanding industrial assemblies. Specifically sized at 17.5 gauge, these components are an essential part of the heavy equipment deployed across Venture Company extraction sites. While useless as ordinary trade goods, they are indispensable to tinkerers dealing with customized goblin hardware.",sp=0},{t="Tinkering with the Samophlange",b="Wenikee Boltbucket requires a substantial collection of nugget slugs to overhaul an unstable samophlange recovered from the Barrens. Because the Venture Company routinely leaves tool buckets scattered across their drilling operations at the Sludge Fen, salvage operations prove lucrative for scavengers—even if Wenikee's eventual repairs result in sudden, explosive failure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a nugget slug?",a="A nugget slug is a specialized 17.5-gauge metallic fastener or slug used in heavy-duty machinery. They serve as structural hardware inside complex industrial mechanisms, such as oil drills and samophlanges.",al={"what are nugget slugs","nugget slug lore","slug fastener"},it="identity"},{q="Where are nugget slugs found?",a="They are stored in tool buckets scattered around the Sludge Fen, a Venture Company drilling camp located in the northeastern Barrens.",al={"where do i find nugget slugs","nugget slug location","sludge fen tool buckets"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Wenikee Boltbucket need them?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket wants to tinker with and repair a recovered samophlange. Having run out of seventeen-point-five gauge fasteners herself, she sends adventurers to salvage them from the nearby Venture Company camp.",al={"who needs nugget slugs","why wenikee wants slugs","samophlange repair"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does using the nugget slugs fix the samophlange?",a="Not successfully. Once Wenikee fits the machine with the salvaged slugs and begins her maintenance work, the samophlange abruptly detonates in front of her.",al={"does the machine work","samophlange explosion","wenikee repair result"},sp=1},{q="Where do nugget slugs come from, and who makes them?",a="These particular seventeen-point-five gauge slugs are industrial hardware utilized by the Venture Company at the Sludge Fen. Their laborers and engineers keep them stockpiled in tool buckets scattered around their drilling and excavation works in the eastern Barrens.",al={"where do nugget slugs come from","who makes nugget slugs","nugget slug origin"},it="origin",add="f3aea894"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Every engineer knows that mixing proprietary seventeen-point-five gauge hardware with an unstable goblin-engineered samophlange is an invitation for a rapid, explosive dismantling."},kw={"barrens","nugget slug","samophlange","sludge fen","tool bucket","venture company","wenikee boltbucket"},rel={"quest:3922","quest:3921","quest:894","subzone:sludge-fen","topic:venture-company","zone:barrens"},src={"Nugget Slug","Nugget Slugs (Classic)"}}
E["item:piece-of-krom-zar-s-banner"] = {t="item",n="Piece of Krom'zar's Banner",z="barrens",s="At Regthar Deathgate's bunker west of the Crossroads, a torn banner marks the broken assault. Warlord Krom'zar led the Kolkar retaliatory force from Desolace.",h="At Regthar Deathgate's bunker west of the Crossroads, a torn banner marks the broken assault.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Centaur Incursion",b="Warlord Krom'zar led a warband east from Desolace to strike back. Kolkar chieftains across the Barrens had fallen, and the furious centaurs attacked the defensive bunkers west of the Crossroads. A strip cut from Krom'zar's fallen standard gives Regthar Deathgate proof that the assault was crushed and the southern trade routes were preserved for the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this banner piece used for?",a="Bring the torn cloth to Regthar Deathgate at his bunker west of the Crossroads. It proves Warlord Krom'zar was slain and his raiding force shattered, ending the defense of the northern Barrens.",al={"banner purpose","why keep banner","what do i do with banner piece"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who was Warlord Krom'zar?",a="Krom'zar was a Kolkar commander from Desolace. He led a direct counterattack against Horde outposts after local Kolkar leaders were killed.",al={"who is kromzar","krom'zar lore","warlord krom'zar"},it="leader"},{q="Why did the Kolkar attack the bunker?",a="After Barak, Verog, and Hezrul and the other local chieftains fell, the enraged centaur gathered reinforcements from Desolace to take vengeance on the Horde presence west of the Crossroads.",al={"why counterattack","kolkar invasion why","barrens counterattack reason"},it="motive"},{q="Does Thrall hear of this victory?",a="Yes. Regthar Deathgate promises to send word directly to Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar, praising the defenders who broke the invasion.",al={"thrall reward","does thrall know"},it="fame"},{q="What is the Piece of Krom'zar's Banner?",a="It is a torn scrap retrieved from the battle standard of Warlord Krom'zar, commander of the vengeful Kolkar centaur army that marched from Desolace into the Barrens. To the Horde forces defending the western bunkers, it serves as undeniable physical proof that the warlord has fallen in battle and his invasion has been broken.",al={"what is piece of kromzars banner","kromzars banner piece","what is the banner fragment"},it="identity",add="92115071"},{q="Where does the Piece of Krom'zar's Banner come from?",a="The banner was carried into the Barrens by Warlord Krom'zar and his Kolkar host, who traveled all the way from their homeland in Desolace to exact vengeance on the Horde. When Krom'zar takes the field outside the western bunkers and falls in combat, his banner is left standing on the battlefield, where this remnant can be torn away.",al={"where did kromzars banner come from","who made kromzars banner","origin of kromzars banner"},it="origin",add="caa193f6"},{q="Why does Regthar Deathgate want a Piece of Krom'zar's Banner?",a="Regthar Deathgate needs concrete proof that the invading Kolkar army has been decisively crushed. Presenting this torn banner confirms that Warlord Krom'zar was slain in front of the Horde bunkers, allowing Regthar to officially declare the invasion over and send word of your valor directly to Warchief Thrall.",al={"why does regthar want the banner","why bring kromzars banner to regthar","why is kromzars banner needed"},it="why_wanted",add="7a980ed6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Defeating Krom'zar and taking his banner stops a major centaur offensive. The northern routes between Durotar, Mulgore, and the Crossroads are secure.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know centaur aggression has long troubled the nomadic tribes. Krom'zar's vanguard is destroyed, and the trails toward Mulgore are safer."},kw={"banner","centaur","counterattack","crossroads","deathgate","kolkar","krom'zar","regthar"},rel={"quest:4021","quest:1361","quest:852","quest:851","quest:850","zone:barrens","zone:desolace","npc:thrall"},src={"Piece of Krom'zar's Banner","Counterattack! (Classic)"}}
E["item:plainstrider-beak"] = {t="item",n="Plainstrider Beak",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, hunters bring Plainstrider Beaks back to the Crossroads. Huntmasters use them as proof that birds threatening local provisions have been culled.",h="Across the Barrens, hunters bring Plainstrider Beaks back to the Crossroads.",sec={{t="A Measure of the Hunt",b="Plainstriders forage around the Crossroads and threaten its supplies. Greater, fleeting, and ornery plainstriders roam the surrounding savannah. Sergra Darkthorn asks arriving hunters to bring back their beaks as proof that the flocks have been culled away from supply lines and storehouses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn want Plainstrider Beaks?",a="Sergra Darkthorn asks hunters to cull plainstriders because the birds harass food supplies around the Crossroads. Their beaks show that the hunt has reduced the threat to local supplies.",al={"why collect beaks","sergra plainstrider beak quest","why beaks"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which creatures yield these beaks?",a="Hunters take the beaks from greater, fleeting, and ornery plainstriders roaming the Barrens savannah.",al={"what drops plainstrider beaks","plainstrider beak sources","where to get beaks"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why don't all plainstriders provide a beak when slain?",a="In the struggle, swift, thrashing birds can leave a beak cracked, shattered, or unusable as a clean trophy. Hunters gather only intact beaks.",al={"why bad drop rate","plainstrider beak not dropping"},gp=true},{q="What is a Plainstrider Beak?",a="A Plainstrider Beak is the severed bill taken from the flightless tallstrider birds that roam the savanna of the Barrens. Hard and pointed, these beaks are collected by hunters as tangible proof that nuisance birds threatening local supplies have been culled.",al={"plainstrider beak item","what is plainstrider beak","plainstrider beaks"},it="identity",add="7e2762f5"},{q="Where does a Plainstrider Beak come from?",a="These beaks come directly from the various breeds of plainstriders—such as greater, fleeting, and ornery plainstriders—native to the Barrens. They are harvested by hunters across the arid plains as trophies and proof of a successful cull.",al={"where to get plainstrider beak","who drops plainstrider beak","plainstrider beak source"},it="origin",add="6978f6b2"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, taking down plainstriders and gathering their beaks gives you an early lesson in stalking and securing prey across Kalimdor’s open plains.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, culling the nuisance flocks east of the Crossroads helps protect the trade and supply routes that feed the outpost."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","plainstrider beak","plainstrider menace","sergra darkthorn","tallstrider"},rel={"quest:844","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads"},src={"Plainstrider Beak","Plainstrider Menace (Classic)"}}
E["item:plainstrider-kidney"] = {t="item",n="Plainstrider Kidney",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, hunters harvest Plainstrider Kidney for Kalimdor's unusual brewing traditions. The organ is unappetizing to most travelers, yet essential to an exotic brew.",h="Across the Barrens, hunters harvest Plainstrider Kidney for Kalimdor's unusual brewing traditions.",sec={{t="An Unorthodox Brewing Ingredient",b="The vast, arid plains of the Barrens are home to tall, flightless plainstriders. Hunters often take their feathers and meat for tools and simple rations, while Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet seeks their internal organs for another purpose. Drohn says plainstrider kidneys are needed to recreate Chen Stormstout's legendary potent ale. He claims the kidneys give the brew a unique kick, in a tradition passed down through an unconventional line of brewmasters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Plainstrider Kidney used for?",a="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet needs plainstrider kidneys to recreate a legendary batch of Stormstout ale. He says his mentor learned the recipe directly from Chen Stormstout, the wandering pandaren Brewmaster.",al={"plainstrider kidney use","why do i need plainstrider kidneys","plainstrider kidney purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why would someone brew ale with animal organs?",a="Kalimdor's exotic brews often use parts from rugged local wildlife to give them strong, memorable flavors and distinct kicks. Brewmaster Drohn says making such potent, wild recipes reminds him fondly of unorthodox creations like trogg brew.",al={"kidney in beer","why kidney in stormstout","animal parts in alcohol"}},{q="Which creatures yield these kidneys?",a="Various species of plainstriders that run across the Barrens yield these kidneys, including fleeting, ornery, and greater plainstriders.",al={"where do plainstrider kidneys drop","who drops plainstrider kidney","plainstrider kidney source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What other ingredients are needed alongside the kidneys?",a="Brewmaster Drohn asks for five plainstrider kidneys, five savannah lion tusks, and one thunder lizard horn to complete his concoction.",al={"other brew ingredients","what else does drohn need","stormstout ingredients"},gp=true},{q="What is a Plainstrider Kidney?",a="It is an internal organ harvested from the large, flightless plainstriders that roam the savannas of the Barrens. While most hunters discard such entrails or leave them to scavengers, certain eccentric brewers prize them as potent and unconventional additions to exotic spirits.",al={"what is plainstrider kidney","plainstrider kidney info","tell me about plainstrider kidney"},it="identity",add="d14d143c"},{q="Where does a Plainstrider Kidney come from?",a="These organs are taken directly from the wild plainstriders native to the Barrens, including greater, ornery, and fleeting varieties. They are naturally occurring parts of the birds' anatomy rather than manufactured goods, though securing one requires hunting down the swift and aggressive avian beasts across the plains.",al={"plainstrider kidney source","where to get plainstrider kidney","plainstrider kidney origin"},it="origin",add="4fd58422"},{q="Why does Brewmaster Drohn want Plainstrider Kidneys?",a="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet seeks these kidneys to recreate Chen Stormstout's legendary, potent namesake brew. Chen passed the unconventional recipe down to Drohn's mentor, and Drohn requires the kidneys alongside lion tusks and a thunder lizard horn to craft the stout with its signature, fierce kick.",al={"why are plainstrider kidneys needed","who wants plainstrider kidneys","plainstrider kidney purpose drohn"},it="why_wanted",add="53f4067b"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you may balk at fermenting avian kidneys into fine spirits. In Kalimdor's wilderness, survival often means making full use of every part of the kill.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you must dress plainstriders carefully across the savanna to keep their internal organs intact for trade with Ratchet's brewmasters."},kw={"brewmaster drohn","chen stormstout","plainstrider","plainstrider kidney","ratchet","stormstout","the barrens"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","quest:819","item:savannah-lion-tusk","item:thunder-lizard-horn","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:trogg"},src={"Plainstrider Kidney","Chen's Empty Keg (2)"}}
E["item:powdered-azurite"] = {t="item",n="Powdered Azurite",z="barrens",s="In Hillsbrad Foothills, Powdered Azurite is taken from the Azurelode Mine. Thun'grim Firegaze needs it to forge brutal armor for rising Horde warriors.",h="In Hillsbrad Foothills, Powdered Azurite is taken from the Azurelode Mine.",sec={{t="A Rare Mineral Compound",b="Powdered Azurite comes from the mineral veins beneath Hillsbrad Foothills. Human workers dig the blue stone from Azurelode Mine, then grind and pack it for trade and metalworking. A skilled smith mixes the dust with dense metals to make armor more durable and resilient.",sp=0},{t="Forging Brutal Armor",b="Horde blacksmiths prize Powdered Azurite for its strength in metalworking, though it comes from human-held tunnels across the Great Sea. Thun'grim Firegaze, an aging orc armorer in the Barrens, asks for small amounts alongside refined iron and fiery reagents. Mixed into the smelt, the powder helps him hammer out the heavy plating of his Brutal Armor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Powdered Azurite used for?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze uses Powdered Azurite with iron ingots and volatile reagents to forge pieces of Brutal Armor for Horde champions.",al={"powdered azurite use","what is powdered azurite"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Powdered Azurite be found?",a="Human miners gather Powdered Azurite in Azurelode Mine, along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"where to find powdered azurite","powdered azurite location","who drops powdered azurite"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does an armorer in the Barrens require reagents from Hillsbrad?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze seeks fine materials for armor worthy of legendary warriors. Iron is easy to find, but the tempering qualities of Azurelode mineral make it worth sending his champions across the sea to obtain.",al={"why hillsbrad","thungrim mineral source"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Powdered Azurite?",a="Powdered Azurite is a crushed blue mineral reagent extracted from deep veins in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Revered by master armorers for its unique metallurgical properties, the fine powder can be alloyed or tempered into base metals during smithing. It is particularly valued by the Horde armorer Thun'grim Firegaze, who uses it alongside exotic reagents to craft heavy, resilient mail armor worthy of renowned warriors.",al={"what is azurite powder","powdered azurite lore","powdered azurite item"},it="identity",add="139f7c50"},{q="Where does Powdered Azurite come from, and who mined it?",a="The substance is mined from the Azurelode Mine nestled along the southern hills of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Human miners working the subterranean shafts of Azurelode unearth the raw azurite ore and grind it down into a refined powder. Because the mine remains under the firm control of Hillsbrad's human laborers, obtaining the powder requires taking it directly from the miners working beneath the earth.",al={"where to get powdered azurite","who mines powdered azurite","powdered azurite source"},it="origin",add="720f3d61"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, gathering Powdered Azurite tests your endurance abroad and brings Thun'grim Firegaze the reagents he needs to forge your armor of savage strength.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, claiming this refined dust means striking deep into the Eastern Kingdoms and taking resources from Alliance hands in Hillsbrad Foothills."},kw={"azurelode mine","azurite","brutal armor","hillsbrad","powdered azurite","reagent","thun'grim firegaze"},rel={"quest:1838","quest:1502","subzone:azurelode-mine","zone:hillsbrad","item:smoky-iron-ingot","item:vial-of-phlogiston","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Powdered Azurite","Brutal Armor"}}
E["item:prowler-claws"] = {t="item",n="Prowler Claws",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, Prowler Claws are carried back to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads. They show that a hunter can track and defeat the prowlers stalking the plains.",h="Across the Barrens, Prowler Claws are carried back to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.",sec={{t="Trophies of the Stalker",b="Savannah Prowlers hide in the Barrens’ tall grass, waiting to strike with patience and cunning. These large cats ambush creatures that enter their hunting grounds, unlike grazing plainstriders and zhevra. Taking their curved claws means facing predators that rely on stealth and defend their territory. For Horde warriors and scouts, the hunt tests whether they can track a stalker through its own ground and make it the prey.",sp=0},{t="Proof for the Huntress",b="Sergra Darkthorn, the huntress at the Crossroads, asks initiates to bring back Prowler Claws before facing greater trials. The claws show that a hunter can follow tracks through the savannah grass and withstand a predator’s attack. Those who return with them have proved they can stay alert among the dangerous beasts of the plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I get Prowler Claws?",a="Savannah Prowlers roam the central Barrens grasslands, especially the plains southwest of the Crossroads. Take their claws and bring them back.",al={"prowler claw location","how to get prowler claws","where to find prowler claws"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants these claws and why?",a="Sergra Darkthorn, an experienced huntress at the Crossroads, wants seven Prowler Claws. Bringing them to her tests your tracking and fighting against dangerous predators.",al={"who needs prowler claws","turn in prowler claws","sergra claws quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are Savannah Prowlers considered a significant hunt?",a="Savannah Prowlers are stealthy carnivores that stalk travelers and prey from the tall brush. Hunting them tests whether you can avoid an ambush and defeat a cunning, lethal beast.",al={"why hunt prowlers","prowlers dangerous"}},{q="What are Prowler Claws?",a="Prowler Claws are the razor-sharp talons taken from the paws of savannah prowlers, the deadly feline predators that stalk the tall savannah grass of the Barrens. To the hunters of the Crossroads, taking these trophies proves you can track and best a sly, lethal beast without becoming prey yourself.",al={"what are prowler claws","prowler claws item","about prowler claws"},it="identity",add="551eb0e2"},{q="Where do Prowler Claws come from?",a="These claws come directly from the savannah prowlers wandering the plains of the Barrens, particularly in the grasslands to the southwest of the Crossroads. They are natural trophies harvested from the carcasses of the big cats by hunters skilled enough to bring them down.",al={"where do prowler claws come from","prowler claws source","how to get prowler claws"},it="origin",add="c8bad4fe"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking down savannah prowlers and taking their claws tests your skill at stealth, tracking, and handling beasts at close range.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, helping cull prowlers around the Crossroads protects messengers, caravans, and settlers on the central roads of Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","prowler claws","prowlers of the barrens","savannah prowler","sergra darkthorn"},rel={"quest:903","quest:860","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:845"},src={"Prowler Claws","Prowlers of the Barrens"}}
E["item:raptor-head"] = {t="item",n="Raptor Head",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, Raptor Head trophies answer a bounty from Gazrog at the Crossroads. The guard payroll vanished from a watchtower, and a wild raptor was caught in the theft.",h="Across the Barrens, Raptor Head trophies answer a bounty from Gazrog at the Crossroads.",sec={{t="Bounty of the Crossroads",b="A stolen chest of guard payroll has left the Crossroads watchtower without its silver. The defenders caught a wild raptor red-handed, to their disbelief. Gazrog has put a bounty on the cunning reptiles prowling the Barrens. Bring their severed heads to the outpost, and the predators will be culled before they can pilfer more Horde supplies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gazrog want raptor heads?",a="A shipment of silver meant as payroll for the Crossroads guards was stolen from their tower in a chest. To everyone's disbelief, a raptor was caught in the act. Gazrog wants the beasts hunted across the Barrens so they cannot raid the settlement again.",al={"why collect raptor heads","gazrog raptors","raptor head bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why would wild raptors steal silver?",a="Gazrog admits he has no idea why wild beasts would want metal coins. Raptors in Kalimdor are notorious for their unnerving cunning, and the theft leaves the Crossroads guards embarrassed and eager for retribution.",al={"why do raptors want silver","raptors stealing coins","raptor thieves mystery"},it="motive"},{q="Which raptors carry these heads?",a="Heads come from Sunscale raptors roaming the central and southern Barrens, including Sunscale Lashtails, Screechers, and Scytheclaws. Notorious beasts such as Ishamuhale and Takk the Leaper also yield heads.",al={"where to get raptor heads","which raptors drop heads","barrens raptors"},gp=true},{q="What happens after turning in the heads?",a="Once Gazrog receives twelve heads and the raptor menace is thinned, attention turns to tracking down where the stolen silver shipment was actually taken.",al={"what follows raptor thieves","after collecting raptor heads"},it="next_step"},{q="What is a Raptor Head?",a="A Raptor Head is the severed trophy and bounty proof taken from raptors roaming the Barrens, including local Sunscale packs and notorious beasts like Ishamuhale or Takk the Leaper. The Crossroads authorities require these gruesome tokens as verifiable evidence that the cunning predators troubling their supply lines and guards have been put down.",al={"what is raptor head","raptor head item","what are raptor heads"},it="identity",add="f6102aac"},{q="Where does a Raptor Head come from?",a="These heads come directly from the predatory raptors stalking the savannas and ridges of the Barrens. Sunscale Lashtails, Screechers, Scytheclaws, and notable hunters across the plains yield them once slain. As biological remains harvested in the field, they are not crafted by anyone, but rather claimed as trophies of a successful hunt.",al={"where do raptor heads come from","raptor head origin","who made raptor head"},it="origin",add="377da5ba"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Crossroads is the heart of Horde travel in central Kalimdor. Clearing the thieving predators secures the garrison's supplies and payroll.",["class:Hunter"]="Tracking Sunscale raptors across the Barrens' dry scrub tests your skill against some of the savannah's most aggressive and cunning pack hunters."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","gazrog","raptor head","raptor thieves","stolen silver","sunscale"},rel={"quest:869","npc:gazrog","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:3281","quest:882"},src={"Raptor Head","Raptor Thieves"}}
E["item:reconstructed-tome"] = {t="item",n="Reconstructed Tome",z="barrens",s="In warlocks’ hands, the Reconstructed Tome gathers the scattered teachings of the cabal. Its pages hold the rites for summoning and binding a felhunter from the Twisting Nether.",h="In warlocks’ hands, the Reconstructed Tome gathers the scattered teachings of the cabal.",sec={{t="A Grimoire Reassembled",b="Warlocks of the Alliance and Horde search for the torn leaves of the Tome of the Cabal. They piece the grimoire back together and consult occult scholars, who are eager to glimpse its rare teachings before the finished book is surrendered.",sp=0},{t="Key to the Felhunter",b="Strahad Farsan, a summoning master near Ratchet’s port in the Barrens, receives the restored tome and rods of channeling taken from Dragonmaw spellcasters. Its rituals give his acolytes the incantations to help a warlock summon a ravenous felhunter, overcome it, and bind it to their will.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Reconstructed Tome used for?",a="The Reconstructed Tome holds cabal teachings and rituals for summoning and binding a felhunter. A warlock brings it with rods of channeling to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet for the ritual.",al={"purpose of reconstructed tome","why need reconstructed tome","reconstructed tome use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Strahad Farsan?",a="Strahad Farsan is an expert summoner who dwells above Ratchet’s port in the Barrens. He oversees trials for warlocks seeking to enslave more dangerous demons.",al={"who is strahad","strahad farsan role"}},{q="Why do the scholars examining the book want a copy?",a="The scholars helping decipher the torn pages find the cabal’s occult texts rare and fascinating. Dwarven and Forsaken researchers covet the demonic knowledge, which surpasses their usual reading.",al={"who translated it","scholars reconstructed tome"},it="motive"},{q="What else is needed alongside the tome for the ritual?",a="Strahad requires three rods of channeling so his acolytes can sustain the summoning ritual. Dragonmaw spellcasters in the Wetlands hold the rods.",al={"other items needed","what goes with reconstructed tome"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the Reconstructed Tome?",a="The Reconstructed Tome is the pieced-together version of the Tome of the Cabal, a forbidden grimoire containing esoteric demonic rituals. After its scattered pages and binding materials are gathered from across the world, scholars painstakingly reassemble the fragmented text so its dark knowledge can be deciphered and put to use.",al={"what is reconstructed tome","reconstructed tome lore","tome of the cabal book"},it="identity",add="a9385a16"},{q="Where does the Reconstructed Tome come from, and who made it?",a="The book is the recovered form of the ancient Tome of the Cabal. Warlock scholars reassemble its torn chapters and worn binding after adventurous practitioners retrieve its scattered components from dangerous locations across the continents.",al={"reconstructed tome origin","who made reconstructed tome","where did reconstructed tome come from"},it="origin",add="d276d405"},{q="Why is the Reconstructed Tome wanted?",a="Warlocks and dark scholars seek the tome for the potent, forbidden secrets recorded across its recovered pages. Strahad Farsan requires its specific rites to guide an aspiring warlock through summoning and binding a vicious demonic felhunter, while local scholars crave a copy purely for its rare and fascinating magical lore.",al={"why want reconstructed tome","why does strahad want reconstructed tome","purpose of reconstructed tome"},it="why_wanted",add="04500ccd"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, assembling the Reconstructed Tome opens the dark rites for dominating a felhunter. Its hunger for magic can be turned against opposing spellcasters."},kw={"binding","dragonmaw","felhunter","ratchet","reconstructed tome","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","quest:1758","quest:1471","item:rod-of-channeling","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:warlock","topic:dragonmaw-clan"},src={"Reconstructed Tome","Tome of the Cabal (Alliance, 3)","Tome of the Cabal (Horde, 3)"}}
E["item:recruitment-letter"] = {t="item",n="Recruitment Letter",z="barrens",s="Takrin Pathseeker sends promising adventurers from Durotar west to serve in the Barrens. His letter directs able-bodied volunteers to the border outpost run by Kargal Battlescar.",h="Takrin Pathseeker sends promising adventurers from Durotar west to serve in the Barrens.",sec={{t="Enlistment for the Frontier",b="Takrin Pathseeker watches young warriors and scouts prove themselves around Razor Hill. He chooses those who seem strong enough for frontline service and gives them a letter for duty in the Barrens. Across the Southfury River bridge, recruits leave Durotar’s sheltered red dirt and join the Horde’s guard against quilboar, centaur, and Alliance scouts.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Battlescar",b="Kargal Battlescar receives the recruits at the outpost just across the river. The grizzled veteran manages the post and evaluates each conscript before signing off on their enlistment. A signed recruit is soon sent farther west to the Crossroads, where the frontier outposts are stretched thin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wrote this recruitment letter?",a="Takrin Pathseeker hands out the letter. The orc scout is posted along the road from Razor Hill and watches for capable recruits heading west.",al={"who gives recruitment letter","who wrote it","takrin pathseeker letter"},it="origin"},{q="Where does this letter need to go?",a="You take the letter to Kargal Battlescar at the orc watchpost just across the Southfury River bridge, on the border of Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"where do i take recruitment letter","turn in recruitment letter","who do i give it to"},it="target"},{q="What happens once the letter is signed?",a="Kargal signs the document to formalize your enlistment, then orders you deeper into the plains to report for duty at the Crossroads, where reinforcements are urgently needed.",al={"what happens after kargal signs","next quest after recruitment letter"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde conscripting adventurers in the Barrens?",a="The Horde conscripts adventurers because the Barrens is a sprawling, dangerous land that connects major Horde settlements. Centaur clans, aggressive Bristleback quilboar, and Alliance operations keep the threat constant, and frontline commanders need every able hand.",al={"why are they recruiting","why conscription barrens"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Recruitment Letter?",a="The Recruitment Letter is an official conscription document issued to capable adventurers in Durotar. Scout Takrin Pathseeker hands it to those who look strong enough to assist the Horde's expanding presence in the harsh frontier of the Barrens, commending them to military outpost commanders.",al={"what is recruitment letter","recruitment letter purpose","what is this letter"},it="identity",add="e6a35429"},{q="Why does Kargal Battlescar want the Recruitment Letter?",a="Kargal Battlescar commands the border outpost safeguarding the bridge into the Barrens and desperately needs capable recruits to reinforce the frontier. The signed letter verifies that you have been vetted by Scout Takrin Pathseeker and are ready to be assigned where the Horde needs you most.",al={"why does kargal want the letter","why turn in recruitment letter","recruitment letter turned in"},it="why_wanted",add="6a5949ec"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, carrying this letter marks your move from local defense in Durotar to active military service across the Kalimdor frontier.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc, presenting a signed letter of service to a veteran like Kargal Battlescar is an early step toward earning honor under Warchief Thrall’s new Horde."},kw={"barrens","conscript of the horde","crossroads","kargal battlescar","razor hill","recruitment letter","takrin pathseeker"},rel={"quest:840","quest:842","npc:kargal-battlescar","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","subzone:razor-hill","topic:horde"},src={"Recruitment Letter","Conscript of the Horde (Classic)"}}
E["item:remaining-drops-of-purest-water"] = {t="item",n="Remaining Drops of Purest Water",z="barrens",s="Across Kalimdor and Lordaeron, shaman gather what Brine needs for a draught. Its last drops wait for a perilous journey.",h="Across Kalimdor and Lordaeron, shaman gather what Brine needs for a draught.",sec={{t="A Remedy for Defiled Waters",b="Brine prepares a water draught in the Barrens from water gathered across Kalimdor and Lordaeron. Part of it gives shaman vision of distant elements. The remaining drops are kept for a harder purpose. Shaman carry them to the coast of Silverpine Forest, near the Sepulcher, where the Brazier of Everfount stands. There, the drops are burned with the bracers of a fallen, tainted elemental. The pure water cuts through the undead plague’s corruption, calling an untainted water spirit to commune with the shaman and complete their communion with the element.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are these drops used for?",a="The drops go onto the Brazier of Everfount on Silverpine Forest’s coast with the bracers of a corrupt water manifestation. The ritual cleanses the corrupted elemental shrine and summons an uncorrupted water spirit.",al={"what do remaining drops do","remaining drops purpose","use purest water"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did the liquid come from?",a="They are the leftover portion of a purifying draught prepared by Brine, an orc shaman who lives on a hill in the southern Barrens. He makes it during the spiritual trials of aspiring shaman.",al={"who made purest water","origin of drops","brine water drops"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the ritual performed all the way in Silverpine Forest?",a="A water shrine on the Silverpine coast, west of the Sepulcher, was corrupted by the plague of undeath. Its elemental spirits became hostile and twisted. Cleansing that pool tests a shaman’s devotion and mastery across great distances.",al={"why silverpine","why travel to silverpine","silverpine water shrine"},it="place"},{q="What happens when they touch the brazier?",a="Poured onto the brazier’s flames with the corrupted bracers, the drops crackle in the fire. The incantation cleanses the lingering plague and summons a pure water manifestation.",al={"brazier ritual","what happens on brazier","brazier of everfount ritual"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Remaining Drops of Purest Water?",a="This small vial contains the last remnants of the cleansing draught brewed by the hermit Brine in the southern Barrens. Infused with water gathered from the Barrens, Tarren Mill and Ashenvale, the potent liquid possesses immense purifying properties. Though just a few drops remain, its concentrated purity is enough to cut through lingering corruption when offered in elemental rites.",al={"what is remaining drops of purest water","what is purest water drops","drops of purest water lore"},it="identity",add="db79eea5"},{q="Why does Islen Waterseer want you to use the Remaining Drops of Purest Water?",a="Islen Waterseer requires you to pour the drops upon the Brazier of Everfount in Silverpine Forest. A sacred water shrine there has succumbed to the undead plague, deafening its local spirits to shamanic communion. By offering these remaining drops alongside the bracers of a fallen corrupt manifestation, the brazier can ignite a cleansing ritual potent enough to summon a pure water spirit.",al={"why use drops of purest water","why is remaining drops of purest water needed","why do you need drops of purest water"},it="why_wanted",add="55d7092f"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you carry the drops from the arid Barrens to Silverpine’s blighted coast as part of your trials to master water. This pilgrimage is essential to earning your Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel from Horde territory in Kalimdor to the precarious Forsaken holdings in Silverpine. The pilgrimage carries spiritual restoration against the Scourge blight across that distance."},kw={"brazier of everfount","brine","call of water","corrupt manifestation","purest water","silverpine","water totem"},rel={"quest:63","npc:brine","item:corrupt-manifestation-s-bracers","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","zone:barrens"},src={"Remaining Drops of Purest Water","Call of Water (7)"}}
E["item:rod-of-channeling"] = {t="item",n="Rod of Channeling",z="barrens",s="In the Wetlands, the Rod of Channeling is carried by Dragonmaw spellcasters. Warlocks seeking to summon a felhunter gather three for Strahad Farsan's acolytes to steady the ritual circle in Ratchet.",h="In the Wetlands, the Rod of Channeling is carried by Dragonmaw spellcasters.",sec={{t="Instruments of Binding",b="Warlocks need more than willpower to bind a volatile felhunter. Strahad Farsan asks for three matched rods so his acolytes can channel magic together and steady the summoning circle while the warlock binds the beast. Dragonmaw darkcasters carry these rods for their own workings. Bonewarders and shadowwarders bear them at Angerfang Encampment and in the surrounding Wetlands ruins. Combat leaves the rods worn and nicked, but they still focus chaotic nether energy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rod of Channeling used for?",a="The rods go to Strahad Farsan above Ratchet. His acolytes use them to channel and steady the circle needed to summon and bind a hostile felhunter.",al={"what is rod of channeling","rod of channeling purpose","why do i need rod of channeling"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Rods of Channeling be found?",a="Dragonmaw spellcasters carry the rods in the Wetlands, especially Dragonmaw Bonewarders and Shadowwarders around Angerfang Encampment.",al={"where to get rods of channeling","who drops rod of channeling","rod of channeling location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Strahad need three rods?",a="Strahad's acolytes assist with the felhunter summoning ritual. Each needs a focus to hold the conduit steady while the warlock subdues the beast.",al={"why three rods","why 3 rods of channeling"},it="motive"},{q="Why are the Dragonmaw using these rods?",a="The Dragonmaw clan uses the rods in its dark shamanism and shadowcraft, remnants of the Old Horde. Its bonewarders and shadowwarders channel curses, necromancy, and shadow magic in their ongoing territorial wars in the Wetlands.",al={"dragonmaw rods","why do dragonmaw have them"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Rod of Channeling?",a="A Rod of Channeling is an arcane focus utilized by spellcasters to focus and harness volatile magical energies. While originally wielded by the dark casters of the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands, these rods are potent ritual instruments capable of stabilizing high-order summonings when handled by experienced warlocks.",al={"what is rod of channeling","rod of channeling lore","about rod of channeling"},it="identity",add="af4e8f1c"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you gather three Rods of Channeling during the Tome of the Cabal trials. They help contain the ritual as you bind your first felhunter."},kw={"angerfang encampment","bonewarder","dragonmaw","felhunter","rod of channeling","shadowwarder","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","quest:1758","item:reconstructed-tome","quest:1471","topic:dragonmaw-clan","zone:wetlands","subzone:angerfang-encampment","zone:barrens"},src={"Rod of Channeling","Tome of the Cabal (Alliance, 3)","Tome of the Cabal (Horde, 3)"}}
E["item:samophlange-item"] = {t="item",n="Samophlange (item)",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Samophlange is hidden inside an automated control console. Goblin mechanics cannot explain what the strange component does.",h="In the Barrens, Samophlange is hidden inside an automated control console.",sec={{t="A Baffling Contraption",b="Samophlange lies inside a control console in the Barrens, behind a maze of wiring and hollow tubes. It takes careful searching to free the component from its housing. It looks like a vital part of clockwork and steam machinery, but goblin tinkerers cannot make sense of its purpose. They mean to send it to the Tinkers' Union in Undermine, though the fragile piece may not survive rough handling.",sp=0},{t="Curiosity and Catastrophe",b="Sputtervalve, an engineer in Ratchet, plans to send Samophlange to senior minds in the Tinkers' Union for study. Goblin curiosity gets in the way of that plan. When Sputtervalve sets the delicate device down to examine its inner workings, it often shatters into scrap.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a samophlange?",a="Samophlange is a strange mechanical component taken from a control console in the Barrens. Its purpose is unknown, and the console around it is crowded with tubes and wires that seem to do nothing useful.",al={"what does a samophlange do","samophlange purpose","what is this item"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the samophlange?",a="Sputtervalve, an engineer in Ratchet, wants Samophlange brought to him so he can study it and send it to the Tinkers' Union.",al={"who needs the samophlange","who do i give the samophlange to"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does Sputtervalve do with it?",a="Sputtervalve plans to send Samophlange to Undermine for study by the Tinkers' Union. He sets it down to inspect it first, and the fragile mechanism breaks.",al={"sputtervalve samophlange","what happens to the samophlange"},sp=1},{q="Where did the samophlange come from?",a="Samophlange is housed inside an operating console in the northern Barrens, behind layers of confusing, seemingly useless machinery.",al={"samophlange location","where is it found"},it="origin"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may recognize Samophlange as an overcomplicated design. Its intricate exterior hides a mechanism so fragile that it breaks when set on the floor."},kw={"barrens","console","ratchet","samophlange","sputtervalve","tinkers union","undermine"},rel={"quest:894","npc:sputtervalve","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Samophlange (item)","Samophlange (Classic 4)"}}
E["item:sample-snapjaw-shell"] = {t="item",n="Sample Snapjaw Shell",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, Sample Snapjaw Shells carry lingering vitality from freshwater oases. Tauren druids send them across the Great Sea to help heal Silverpine Forest.",h="Across the Barrens, Sample Snapjaw Shells carry lingering vitality from freshwater oases.",sec={{t="A Spark of Oasis Life",b="Snapjaws thrive in the lush, strange oases of the Barrens. Their durable shells keep a faint inner glow and pulse with energy long after separation from the creature. Tauren druids watching the land's swift changes see in these carapaces the resilient spark of Kalimdor's wilderness. Their vigor shows how life can flourish even in harsh, arid surroundings.",sp=0},{t="Healing Distant Lands",b="Tauren naturalists send couriers across the sea with shells for Mura Runetotem at the Sepulcher. Stationed in Silverpine Forest's blighted expanses, Mura seeks ways to help the Forsaken heal the northlands. She studies the life-force preserved in the snapjaw's armor, hoping to find what can renew an ailing forest and bring growth back to dying soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes this snapjaw shell special?",a="A Sample Snapjaw Shell keeps a faint inner glow and pulse of life long after collection. It comes from snapjaws around the Barrens' strange freshwater oases, where natural energies run unusually high.",al={"why is shell special","what is snapjaw shell","glowing shell"},it="power"},{q="Who needs this sample?",a="Mura Runetotem, a tauren druid, needs the shell at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. She is there to help the Forsaken find ways to heal dying lands.",al={"who wants the shell","where do i bring shell","mura runetotem quest"},it="target"},{q="Why send a Barrens shell all the way to Silverpine?",a="Silverpine's woodland is ailing and blighted, while life has suddenly surged at the Barrens oases and persisted. Druids hope the vitality in Kalimdor's beasts can teach them how to heal Lordaeron's damaged soil.",al={"why send to silverpine","shell connection to silverpine"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is the shell dangerous or tainted?",a="No. The shell radiates pure vitality rather than dark magic. The druids find the lingering energy in the Barrens' mysterious sudden growth natural resilience worth cultivating.",al={"is shell evil","is the shell corrupted"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Sample Snapjaw Shell?",a="It is a specimen taken from the carapace of a snapjaw turtle found in the arid reaches of the Barrens. Imbued with a strange, pulsing vitality, this shell is carefully preserved so its unusual life energy can be examined far from Kalimdor's plains.",al={"what is sample snapjaw shell","snapjaw shell item","sample snapjaw shell identity"},it="identity",add="6161673b"},{q="Where does the Sample Snapjaw Shell come from?",a="It originates from the wild snapjaws dwelling around the oases and waterways of the Barrens. The natural shell was gathered by Horde adventurers in Kalimdor and chosen by the tauren druids as a representative sample of the flourishing life force found within the sun-drenched wasteland.",al={"snapjaw shell origin","where did the snapjaw shell come from","who made sample snapjaw shell"},it="origin",add="c3ef5b23"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of the Cenarion Circle, studying oasis snapjaws offers crucial lessons in how life perseveres and how blighted ground might be healed.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see this shell's journey as a commitment to the Earth Mother. Your people carry aid and natural healing across the sea, even to their undead allies."},kw={"barrens","mura runetotem","oasis","sample snapjaw shell","sepulcher","silverpine","snapjaw","turtle shell"},rel={"quest:3301","subzone:sepulcher","zone:barrens","quest:6381"},src={"Sample Snapjaw Shell","Mura Runetotem (quest)"}}
E["item:savannah-lion-tusk"] = {t="item",n="Savannah Lion Tusk",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Savannah Lion Tusks go from hunting trophies to ingredients in Chen Stormstout's legendary potent ale.",h="In the Barrens, Savannah Lion Tusks go from hunting trophies to ingredients in Chen Stormstout's legendary...",sec={{t="A Curious Brewing Ingredient",b="The great cats roaming the Barrens carry sharp, heavy tusks. Prowlers, huntresses, prides ruled by patriarchs, and beasts like Humar the Pridelord all bear them. Travelers often take the teeth as proof of a successful hunt. Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet uses the tusks with plainstrider kidneys and thunder lizard horns to recreate Chen Stormstout's famous namesake brew, a potent ale with a legendary kick few mortal gullets can withstand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Brewmaster Drohn need Savannah Lion Tusks?",a="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet needs the tusks to recreate Chen Stormstout's namesake brew. His mentor passed the recipe down to him, and the tusks are one of three Barrens ingredients needed to reproduce the stout's distinct flavor and kick.",al={"why tusks for beer","drohn lion tusks","brewmaster drohn recipe"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which beasts carry Savannah Lion Tusks?",a="Savannah lion pride members across the Barrens carry the tusks. They include Savannah Highmanes, Patriarchs, Matriarchs, Huntresses, Prowlers, and rare beasts like Dishu and Humar the Pridelord.",al={"where do lion tusks drop","who drops lion tusk","savannah lion tusk source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Do lions actually have tusks?",a="Savannah big cats have oversized canine fangs that grow prominent and thick in Kalimdor's rugged wilds. Local hunters and frontiersmen call them tusks.",al={"why are lion teeth called tusks","lion tusks vs fangs","lion tusk anatomy"}},{q="What is a Savannah Lion Tusk?",a="A Savannah Lion Tusk is a sharp canine tooth harvested from the predatory cats prowling the sun-baked plains of the Barrens. While called tusks, they are the formidable fangs of the savannah lions that dominate the local hunting grounds. Beyond serving as grim trophies of wilderness survival, these resilient parts find peculiar uses among locals who know how to extract their essential qualities.",al={"what is savannah lion tusk","savannah lion tusk lore","lion tusk"},it="identity",add="98d362c4"},{q="Where does a Savannah Lion Tusk come from?",a="These tusks are taken directly from the savage pride cats that hunt the central savannas of Kalimdor. Every breed of lion stalking the Barrens—from prowlers and huntresses to mighty patriarchs and highmanes—possesses these sharp fangs, relying on them to bring down plainstriders and defend their territory against competing predators.",al={"where do lion tusks come from","who drops lion tusks","lion tusk source"},it="origin",add="ea601034"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking the fierce prides across the Barrens tests your skill. Their dangerous fangs can prove deadly in battle and valuable to local brewers."},kw={"barrens","brewmaster drohn","chen stormstout","dishu","humar","ratchet","savannah lion tusk"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","quest:819","item:plainstrider-kidney","item:thunder-lizard-horn","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Savannah Lion Tusk","Chen's Empty Keg (2)"}}
E["item:secure-crate"] = {t="item",n="Secure Crate",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, a Secure Crate waits for a traveler to carry it to Ratchet. Potions and alchemical goods inside are bound for the Eastern Kingdoms.",h="In the Barrens, a Secure Crate waits for a traveler to carry it to Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Courier's Cargo",b="Couriers, caravans, and goblin ships carry trade between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. When a Barrens caravan misses its departure, travelers take fragile cargo like this Secure Crate down to the coast. It holds potions, alchemical goods, and reagents for associates across the Great Sea. The crate is sealed against the Barrens trails and the sea spray on its voyage.",sp=0},{t="Through the Port of Ratchet",b="The crate’s land journey ends at the Ratchet docks, where Wharfmaster Dizzywig oversees shipping. Ratchet is a neutral port for goods crossing the sea, including cargo bound for Blackwater Cove. Dizzywig works under the Steamwheedle Cartel’s ledger, recording parcels and freight before loading them onto the next departing vessel. Ratchet links the Old World with the frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Secure Crate?",a="The Secure Crate holds potions, alchemical reagents, and other supplies for associates in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"crate contents","what is in the crate","secure crate items"},it="item"},{q="Where is the crate being sent?",a="Carry it to Wharfmaster Dizzywig on the Ratchet docks. He will book it onto a merchant vessel bound for Blackwater Cove in the Old World.",al={"crate destination","where does secure crate go"},it="next_step"},{q="Why was the crate given to an adventurer instead of a caravan?",a="The sender could not make the journey to Ratchet in time, and the scheduled trade caravan had already left. A hired courier must get the crate to the docks in time for the tide.",al={"why do i have the crate","missed caravan"},it="motive"},{q="Who takes the crate at Ratchet?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig receives the crate on the Ratchet docks and records it in his shipping ledger before loading it onto the next ship sailing with the tide.",al={"who gets the crate","dizzywig crate"},it="target"},{q="What is the Secure Crate?",a="The Secure Crate is a tightly packed shipment containing an assortment of potions, reagents, and other valuable supplies. It is packaged securely so that its delicate contents survive a long journey by caravan and vessel across the sea to the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"what is secure crate","secure crate lore","about secure crate"},it="identity",add="e5dd21c1"},{q="Where does the Secure Crate come from, and who made it?",a="The crate originates in the Barrens, packed and sealed by an apothecary or scholar who urgently needed to export their alchemical supplies. Lacking the time to travel to the coast personally after missing the regular trade caravan, they prepared the crate to be carried by hand directly to the port at Ratchet.",al={"who made secure crate","where did secure crate come from","secure crate origin"},it="origin",add="4df2d75b"},{q="Why is the Secure Crate wanted?",a="Associates in the Eastern Kingdoms across the sea are awaiting these essential reagents and potions. Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet needs the crate delivered to his docks so he can log it into his trade ledger and stow it aboard the next outbound vessel sailing for Blackwater Cove.",al={"why want secure crate","who needs secure crate","why does dizzywig want secure crate"},it="why_wanted",add="b7ad6ca4"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can see how cross-sea alchemists and herbalists rely on frontier trade routes to exchange raw ingredients.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you know Ratchet’s neutral port links Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms through goblin shipping."},kw={"barrens","blackwater cove","potions","ratchet","reagents","secure crate","shipping","wharfmaster dizzywig"},rel={"quest:1492","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Secure Crate","Wharfmaster Dizzywig (Barrens)"}}
E["item:serena-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Serena's Head",z="barrens",s="At the Dry Hills in the northern Barrens, Serena Bloodfeather's head is sought as proof of her death. Darsok Swiftdagger plans to display it on a Horde supply wagon as a warning against further harpy raids.",h="At the Dry Hills in the northern Barrens, Serena Bloodfeather's head is sought as proof of her death.",sec={{t="A Warning on the Road",b="Serena Bloodfeather led the Witchwing harpies of the Dry Hills in attacks on trade through the northern Barrens. Her assaults on Horde supply lines grew vicious because her sister had fallen to the beastmaster Rexxar. Darsok Swiftdagger, an orc rogue, ordered Serena hunted to break the flock's morale. He wants her severed head mounted on an outbound caravan, where harpies watching from the crags will see the warning.",sp=1,bt={"q867.3"}}},faq={{q="Why does Darsok Swiftdagger want Serena's head?",a="Darsok wants proof that Serena Bloodfeather is dead, and plans to mount her head on a Horde supply caravan. He hopes the display will frighten the surviving Witchwing harpies away from travelers.",al={"why take serenas head","darsok serena head","what does darsok do with the head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why was Serena Bloodfeather attacking Horde caravans?",a="Serena Bloodfeather attacked Horde caravans to avenge her sister, whom the half-ogre champion Rexxar had slain. She struck Horde supply lines and wayfarers across the Barrens.",al={"why did serena attack caravans","serena bloodfeather motive","harpy attacks barrens"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"q867.3"}},{q="Where does this trophy come from?",a="The trophy is taken from Serena Bloodfeather, the matriarch who roosts among the Dry Hills crags in the far northwestern Barrens.",al={"where to find serena's head","serena bloodfeather location","how to get serenas head"},it="origin"},{q="What is Serena's Head?",a="Serena's Head is the severed head of Serena Bloodfeather, the vengeful matriarch of the Witchwing harpy flock in the northern Barrens. Taking it marks an end to her raids against Crossroads supply routes and serves as irrefutable proof that the harpy menace has been struck at its very top.",al={"what is serenas head","serena bloodfeather head","serena head item"},it="identity",add="29e11954"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde caravans connect Durotar to Mulgore and the distant outposts. Displaying Serena's head on a supply wagon declares Horde dominance over the wild wastes.",["class:Rogue"]="Darsok Swiftdagger values clean, ruthless work. He praises mercenaries who slip behind enemy perches and execute a target without flinching."},kw={"crossroads","darsok swiftdagger","dry hills","harpy","rexxar","serena bloodfeather","serena's head","witchwing"},rel={"quest:876","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","quest:875","quest:867","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:harpy","topic:horde"},src={"Serena's Head","Serena Bloodfeather (Classic)"}}
E["item:shard-of-water"] = {t="item",n="Shard of Water",z="barrens",s="Along the Barrens coast, Islen Waterseer receives the Shard of Water from a shaman who has faced corruption.",h="Along the Barrens coast, Islen Waterseer receives the Shard of Water from a shaman who has faced corruption.",sec={{t="Token of Elemental Purity",b="Shamans must understand balance, life, and preservation to master water. In the Call of Water, they travel to corrupted springs, even crossing the sea to blighted Silverpine Forest. After purifying the tainted waters, a shaman receives the Shard of Water. Returning the crystal token to Islen Waterseer on the rocky Barrens shore proves the initiate's worth and provides the final key to forge a Water Totem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shard of Water used for?",a="You bring the shard to Islen Waterseer on the Barrens' eastern shore as proof of your trial. Presenting it completes your communion with water and earns you a Water Totem.",al={"shard of water purpose","what does shard of water do","why do i have shard of water"},it="purpose"},{q="Who requires this item?",a="Islen Waterseer, a shaman in a hut south of Ratchet along the Merchant Coast, asks for the shard to confirm you purified tainted water.",al={"who wants shard of water","where to turn in shard of water","islen waterseer shard"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why was the trial set as far away as Silverpine?",a="Water means healing and preservation, while corruption halts life. Silverpine's tainted waters test whether you can restore elemental harmony amid deep decay.",al={"silverpine water quest","why silverpine forest","shaman silverpine"},it="place"},{q="What is the Shard of Water?",a="The Shard of Water is a sacred elemental fragment granted to shamans undertaking the trials of water. It serves as tangible proof that you carried out the ritual to purify corrupt waters and understand water's true nature as a giver and protector of life.",al={"what is shard of water","shard of water item","what is this shard"},it="identity",add="aaf07767"},{q="Where does the Shard of Water come from, and who made it?",a="You receive the shard at the end of your spiritual journey in Silverpine Forest, bestowed upon completing your ritual to cleanse the corrupted waters of the region. It embodies the elemental power of pure water awakened through that rite.",al={"where do you get shard of water","who gives shard of water","origin of shard of water"},it="origin",add="47314211"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, obtaining the shard completes your attunement to water spirits and the long journey to earn your Water Totem."},kw={"barrens","call of water","islen waterseer","shard of water","silverpine","water totem"},rel={"quest:63","npc:islen-waterseer","topic:shaman","zone:barrens"},src={"Shard of Water","Call of Water (9)"}}
E["item:shipment-of-boots"] = {t="item",n="Shipment of Boots",z="barrens",s="Off the Barrens coast, Shipment of Boots lies in a Southsea encampment south of Ratchet. Drizzlik sent the crate from Booty Bay for Gazlowe's trade network, but the pirates seized it before it reached port.",h="Off the Barrens coast, Shipment of Boots lies in a Southsea encampment south of Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Plundered Cargo",b="Gazlowe arranged for Drizzlik, a clothing merchant in Booty Bay, to send boots to Ratchet. Southsea Freebooters patrolling the Merchant Coast ambushed the ship and carried the crates to their beach encampments south of the harbor. They scattered the stolen goods among their tents and shanties, and the shipment remains there, far from Ratchet's docks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent this shipment of boots?",a="Drizzlik, a goblin merchant in Booty Bay, sent the boots from the southern port.",al={"who made the boots","where did the boots come from","drizzlik boots"},it="origin"},{q="Who was supposed to receive the boots?",a="Gazlowe ordered the boots for Ratchet. He is the chief engineer and overseer there, and the shipment was meant to support his local workforce and trade.",al={"who owns the boots","gazlowe boot shipment"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did the boots end up with the pirates?",a="Southsea Freebooters ambushed the cargo ship along the Barrens coast, plundered it, and carried the crates to their encampments south of Ratchet.",al={"why do southsea pirates have boots","who stole the boots"},it="history"},{q="Where can the shipment be found?",a="The shipment is in the Southsea pirate encampment along the coast south of Ratchet, among their plundered goods.",al={"boots location","where is shipment of boots","find boot shipment"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Shipment of Boots?",a="The Shipment of Boots is a crate of footwear sent across the Great Sea from Booty Bay to Ratchet. Dispatched by the goblin merchant Drizzlik, it was meant directly for Gazlowe before the Southsea Freebooters intercepted the cargo ship carrying his trade goods.",al={"what is shipment of boots","shipment of boots item","what are the boots"},it="identity",add="06b396e7"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can slip through the Southsea camps along the coast. Their pirate patrols are dense, so a silent approach is the safest way to reclaim Gazlowe's stolen freight."},kw={"booty bay","drizzlik","gazlowe","ratchet","shipment of boots","southsea freebooters","stolen booty"},rel={"quest:888","subzone:ratchet","subzone:booty-bay","quest:887","quest:890","item:telescopic-lens","topic:pirate","zone:barrens"},src={"Shipment of Boots","Stolen Booty"}}
E["item:signed-recruitment-letter"] = {t="item",n="Signed Recruitment Letter",z="barrens",s="Kargal Battlescar sends the Signed Recruitment Letter west from the Far Watch Post. His mark directs new recruits to report for duty at the Crossroads.",h="Kargal Battlescar sends the Signed Recruitment Letter west from the Far Watch Post.",sec={{t="A Conscript's Transfer",b="At the Far Watch Post, Kargal Battlescar prepares recruits for service in the Barrens. The post stands east of the Southfury River, where newcomers cross from Durotar. When a conscript proves ready to Kargal, he stamps and signs a letter of introduction. The orders send recruits west along the road to the Crossroads. There, Sergra Darkthorn coordinates supplies and the defense of the dry plains.",sp=0},{t="Tension at the Outposts",b="Kargal's orders carry his personal contempt for the officer who awaits the recruit. He calls Sergra Darkthorn an abrasive shaman who talks in circles around soldiers. Kargal openly questions Warchief Thrall's high opinion of her. Even so, the dispatch must reach Sergra's hands before any further assignments at the Crossroads are granted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Signed Recruitment Letter?",a="The Signed Recruitment Letter transfers you from Kargal Battlescar at the Far Watch Post to duty in the Barrens. It shows Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads that Kargal has judged you ready.",al={"what does this letter do","recruitment letter use","signed letter barrens"},it="purpose"},{q="Who signed the letter?",a="Kargal Battlescar signs the letter. The orc veteran oversees the Far Watch Post on the border between Durotar and the Barrens, and signs after a recruit completes initial duties there.",al={"who wrote the letter","kargal letter","who signed this"},it="origin"},{q="Who do I deliver the letter to?",a="You deliver the letter to Sergra Darkthorn, an influential orc shaman stationed at the Crossroads' central intersection.",al={"where do i take the letter","who gets the letter","letter recipient"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Kargal speak poorly of Sergra Darkthorn?",a="Kargal calls Sergra sharp-tongued and difficult, and thinks she wastes time talking when work needs doing. Warchief Thrall holds her in high regard, but Kargal doubts her leadership.",al={"kargal sergra feud","why does kargal hate sergra"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Signed Recruitment Letter?",a="It is an official Horde conscription document handed to recruits arriving in the Barrens from Durotar. Drafted and endorsed by Kargal Battlescar at the Far Watch Post, it serves as formal certification that you have been vetted, enlisted, and dispatched to assist the settlement at the Crossroads.",al={"what is signed recruitment letter","recruitment letter","what is this letter"},it="identity",add="ea3ee62a"},{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn want the Signed Recruitment Letter?",a="Sergra Darkthorn oversees operations at the Crossroads and relies on incoming manpower to secure the Barrens for the Horde. The letter confirms your enlistment under Kargal's authority, proving you are ready to take orders, prove your worth, and tackle the pressing labor and threats facing the settlement.",al={"why does sergra want the letter","why deliver recruitment letter","who needs recruitment letter"},it="why_wanted",add="ea22ddb8"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry this letter from basic service in Durotar into the Horde's wider frontier forces.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you report to Sergra Darkthorn, an orc shaman whom Thrall has entrusted with helping secure the Barrens."},kw={"conscription","crossroads","far watch post","kargal battlescar","sergra darkthorn","signed recruitment letter","the barrens","thrall"},rel={"quest:842","quest:840","npc:kargal-battlescar","subzone:crossroads","subzone:far-watch-post","zone:barrens","topic:horde","npc:thrall"},src={"Signed Recruitment Letter","Crossroads Conscription"}}
E["item:silithid-egg-the-barrens"] = {t="item",n="Silithid Egg (The Barrens)",z="barrens",s="Across the Field of Giants, silithid eggs lie buried beneath the soil. Horde researchers gather them to learn about the swarm spreading through the southern Barrens.",h="Across the Field of Giants, silithid eggs lie buried beneath the soil.",sec={{t="A Mysterious Swarm",b="Silithid mounds rise from the Field of Giants as strange insect-like creatures churn the earth. Their eggs lie beneath the hardened soil, guarded by territorial silithid. The Horde knows little about these creatures, but scouts at the Crossroads have seen signs of coordination and intelligence beyond that of ordinary wild beasts. Unhatched eggs may help scholars in Orgrimmar learn about the silithid’s life cycle and nature.",sp=0},{t="Excavation and Danger",b="Silithid eggs must be dug from the mounds with an adapted digging claw. The creatures defend their underground nurseries fiercely, swarming anyone who threatens their unhatched young. Korran, a troll researcher, needs intact specimens for study before the swarm spreads farther across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Silithid Eggs?",a="Silithid Eggs are unhatched clutches buried in earthen mounds in the southern Barrens, especially around the Field of Giants.",al={"silithid egg","what is silithid egg","silithid mounds"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants these eggs collected?",a="Korran, a troll researcher at the Crossroads, gathers the eggs for his masters in Orgrimmar, who want to study silithid biology and behavior.",al={"who needs eggs","korran quest","egg hunt questgiver"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the silithid being studied?",a="The Horde knows little about the silithid. Korran has seen signs of intelligence and coordination beyond those of typical wild animals, troubling Horde leaders as the creatures appear in the Barrens.",al={"why study silithid","silithid threat","are silithid smart"},it="motive"},{q="How are the eggs gathered?",a="An adapted digging claw is used to pry eggs from silithid mounds, while the aggressive swarm defends its nests.",al={"how to get eggs","digging claw","harvest silithid eggs"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where do Silithid Eggs come from?",a="These eggs are laid by the strange, insect-like silithid deep within their earthen mounds in the southern Barrens, particularly throughout the Field of Giants. The silithid carefully bury and guard their clutches inside these towering dirt mounds, fiercely attacking anyone daring enough to disturb the nests.",al={"silithid egg origin","where do silithid eggs come from","who laid the silithid eggs"},it="origin",add="04f05afd"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, intelligent insect swarms near the Crossroads threaten trade routes and territory in central Kalimdor."},kw={"crossroads","digging claw","egg hunt","field of giants","korran","mounds","silithid","silithid egg","the barrens"},rel={"quest:868","npc:korran","subzone:field-of-giants","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Silithid Egg (The Barrens)","Egg Hunt (Classic)"}}
E["item:singed-scale"] = {t="item",n="Singed Scale",z="barrens",s="In Durotar, Singed Scale comes from the charred plates of electrified thunder lizards. Horde warriors bring the scales to prove their endurance and learn defensive combat.",h="In Durotar, Singed Scale comes from the charred plates of electrified thunder lizards.",sec={{t="A Test of Endurance",b="Horde veterans judge a warrior by the blows they can bear while shielding allies. In Thunder Ridge, a canyon in western Durotar, lightning hides and thunder lizards crackle with storm energy. Hunting these beasts means enduring relentless electrical shocks and crushing blows. Their blackened scales show that a fighter can withstand punishing assaults and hold firm under pressure.",sp=0},{t="The Way of the Shield",b="At the Far Watch Post, on the border between Durotar and the Barrens, the veteran warrior Uzzek asks initiates for five scales before teaching them. He believes they need physical toughness before they can learn stances and tactical defense. Bringing the scales proves they have the fortitude to join thick hide, heavy armor, and careful footwork into a firm defense against the Horde’s enemies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are singed scales used for?",a="Singed scales prove martial endurance. Uzzek, a warrior trainer, requires five before teaching an initiate advanced defensive techniques.",al={"singed scale use","who wants singed scales","singed scale quest"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where do you find singed scales?",a="You find singed scales on thunder lizards and lightning hides in Thunder Ridge, a canyon in western Durotar across the river from the Barrens.",al={"singed scale location","where to get singed scales","how to get singed scale"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why are the scales singed?",a="Thunder lizards channel lightning and electrical storms through their bodies. The persistent crackle of elemental energy scorches and blackens their outer hide, giving the scales their charred texture.",al={"why singed","why are the scales burnt"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Uzzek and why does he care about these scales?",a="Uzzek is a veteran warrior at the Far Watch Post in the eastern Barrens. He trains rising Horde warriors in defensive combat and requires them to prove their resilience against deadly beasts first.",al={"who is uzzek","uzzek"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Singed Scale?",a="A Singed Scale is a tough reptilian scale taken from the fierce thunder lizards and lightning hides dwelling in Thunder Ridge. Constantly crackling with natural electrical energy, these creatures bear plates blackened and scarred by their own violent lightning discharges, leaving behind charred but remarkably resilient armor.",al={"what is singed scale","singed scale lore","singed scales info"},it="identity",add="c263d0cb"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a developing warrior, bringing the scales to Uzzek marks a core milestone in learning protection and standing as an impenetrable shield for the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="At the Far Watch Post, trials ensure that guards and vanguards on the Durotar and Barrens frontiers possess unyielding stamina."},kw={"far watch post","lightning hide","path of defense","singed scale","thunder lizard","thunder ridge","uzzek"},rel={"quest:1498","npc:uzzek","subzone:far-watch-post","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:durotar","zone:barrens","topic:warrior","topic:horde"},src={"Singed Scale","Path of Defense"}}
E["item:smoky-iron-ingot"] = {t="item",n="Smoky Iron Ingot",z="barrens",s="At the Windshear dig sites, kobolds smelt Smoky Iron Ingots from ore they pull from the Stonetalon Mountains. Orcish armorers prize the bars as raw material for sturdy mail gear for Horde warriors.",h="At the Windshear dig sites, kobolds smelt Smoky Iron Ingots from ore they pull from the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Crude Kobold Metallurgy",b="Kobolds smelt Smoky Iron Ingots in the Windshear Crag tunnels of the Stonetalon Mountains. They dig ore from the rocky slopes and heat it over crude, smoking fires. Residue and charcoal cling to the bars, but the metal remains dense and strong.",sp=0},{t="Forging the Brutal Armor",b="Thun'grim Firegaze, a near-blind orc armorer, works from a rugged camp overlooking the Barrens. He asks for these ingots to make armor for proven Horde warriors. Alongside refined iron bars, powdered azurite, and volatile phlogiston, the smoky metal forms a resilient core for Brutal Hauberks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Smoky Iron Ingots come from?",a="Kobolds in the Windshear dig sites and tunnels of eastern Stonetalon Mountains carry Smoky Iron Ingots. They include diggers, stonecutters, vermin, geomancers, and their overlords.",al={"where to find smoky iron ingot","smoky iron ingot location","who drops smoky iron ingots"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What are Smoky Iron Ingots used for?",a="Warriors answering Thun'grim Firegaze's call collect Smoky Iron Ingots. The master armorer lives on the peaks near Crossroads in the Barrens and needs fifteen ingots to forge the Brutal Hauberk.",al={"smoky iron ingot use","what is smoky iron ingot for","brutal armor quest item"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Why are the ingots described as 'smoky'?",a="Kobolds use crude, low-burning smelting fires in their dim tunnels. Soot, charcoal dust, and ash cling to the metal instead of leaving it with a clean shine.",al={"why is it smoky","smoky iron lore"},it="identity"},{q="Can any blacksmith craft with these ingots?",a="No. The irregular, soot-caked bars are not fit for standard trade blacksmithing. Only smiths such as Thun'grim Firegaze know how to work them into custom combat gear.",al={"can players smith smoky iron","is smoky iron a trade good"},gp=true},{q="What is a Smoky Iron Ingot?",a="Smoky Iron Ingots are roughly smelted bars of dark, soot-streaked iron found in the hands of the Windshear kobolds tunneling deep within the Stonetalon Mountains. Crude compared to refined metalwork, they nonetheless possess the resilient strength needed by skilled smiths looking to forge heavy, enduring armor.",al={"what is smoky iron ingot","smoky iron ingot info","tell me about smoky iron ingot"},it="identity",add="18404e72"},{q="Where does Smoky Iron Ingot come from, and who made it?",a="These ingots are mined and smelted by the kobolds of the Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Deep in their subterranean tunnels, diggers and vermin unearth the raw ore and cast it into serviceable iron ingots to reinforce their subterranean operations and arm their warbands.",al={"smoky iron ingot source","where do smoky iron ingots come from","who makes smoky iron ingot"},it="origin",add="9ee5c553"},{q="Why does anyone want Smoky Iron Ingot?",a="The near-blind orc master smith Thun'grim Firegaze, who resides atop the bluffs of the Barrens, requires fifteen of these ingots to fashion Brutal Armor for worthy Horde warriors. Combined with other rare alchemical and mineral agents, the crude metal serves as foundational material for a suit built to withstand brutal warfare.",al={"why get smoky iron ingot","who wants smoky iron ingot","smoky iron ingot use lore"},it="why_wanted",add="8ab45f92"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="For Horde warriors, gathering these ingots tests endurance in Stonetalon. They are needed to forge the Brutal Hauberk.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="These ingots show the crude smelting methods kobold diggers use beside the refined techniques of trained smiths."},kw={"brutal armor","kobold","smoky iron ingot","stonetalon","thun'grim firegaze","warrior","windshear"},rel={"quest:1838","quest:1502","zone:stonetalon","topic:kobold","zone:barrens","item:powdered-azurite","item:vial-of-phlogiston","topic:horde"},src={"Smoky Iron Ingot","Brutal Armor"}}
E["item:sodium-nitrate"] = {t="item",n="Sodium Nitrate",z="barrens",s="At Bael Modan, Sodium Nitrate helps the dwarves blast through the southern Barrens’ stone. Gann Stonespire seeks the chemical for charges against the fortress.",h="At Bael Modan, Sodium Nitrate helps the dwarves blast through the southern Barrens’ stone.",sec={{t="Industrial Demolition",b="Dwarven excavators at Bael Modan use Sodium Nitrate to break through the southern Barrens’ rock. The Bael'dun expedition entered the Stonespire tribe’s ancestral lands with earthmovers and blasting reagents. Riflemen, soldiers, and officers carry the chemical inside the excavation works and nearby fortress.",sp=0},{t="Turnabout and Retribution",b="Gann Stonespire watched the invaders after they devastated his tribe’s homeland and scavenged their engineering schematics. Unable to breach the defended keep with ordinary attacks, the exiled tauren turns their blasting supplies against them. He mixes looted Sodium Nitrate with nitroglycerin and wood pulp to make charges meant to shake Bael Modan’s foundations.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Sodium Nitrate used for in the Barrens?",a="The Ironforge dwarves use Sodium Nitrate in explosives to blast rocky ground at their dig site. Gann Stonespire mixes it with nitroglycerin and wood pulp to make charges against Bael Modan.",al={"sodium nitrate purpose","what does sodium nitrate do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Sodium Nitrate come from?",a="Dwarven forces stationed at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens carry Sodium Nitrate. Riflemen, soldiers, officers, and commanders such as Lord Cyrik Blackforge keep it on hand.",al={"who drops sodium nitrate","where to get sodium nitrate"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Gann Stonespire need this chemical?",a="Gann Stonespire lost his ancestral village to the dwarven excavation. Without heavy siege equipment, he studied their schematics and set out to make charges that could break their fortified positions with their own supplies.",al={"why does gann want sodium nitrate","gann stonespire explosives"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is Sodium Nitrate dangerous on its own?",a="On its own, sodium nitrate is an oxidizer and chemical salt, not an instant explosive. Mixed with a fuel source and shock-sensitive chemicals such as nitroglycerin, it becomes dangerous and volatile.",al={"is sodium nitrate an explosive"},it="danger"},{q="What is Sodium Nitrate?",a="Sodium nitrate is a volatile chemical agent stocked by the dwarven expeditionary forces stationed at Bael Modan. While relatively stable when stored, the dwarves rely on it as a core component for compounding high-grade explosive charges used to blast through solid stone at their excavation sites. In the hands of a clever saboteur, however, it can just as easily be repurposed to dismantle the fortress itself.",al={"what is sodium nitrate","sodium nitrate lore","sodium nitrate barrens"},it="identity",add="caaef0db"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers recognize sodium nitrate, nitroglycerin, and wood pulp as the recipe for stabilized dynamite, the basis of Gann’s improvised charges.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, Gann Stonespire turns to dwarven chemicals to strike back for the destruction of his ancestral territory."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun","blackforge","gann stonespire","nitroglycerin","revenge of gann","sodium nitrate","wood pulp"},rel={"quest:846","npc:gann-stonespire","item:nitroglycerin","item:wood-pulp","subzone:bael-modan","quest:843","zone:barrens"},src={"Sodium Nitrate","Revenge of Gann"}}
E["item:soran-ruk-fragment"] = {t="item",n="Soran'ruk Fragment",z="barrens",s="In Blackfathom Deeps, cultists hold shards of Soran'ruk, a shattered prison orb. The pieces still carry fel energy from the demon once bound inside.",h="In Blackfathom Deeps, cultists hold shards of Soran'ruk, a shattered prison orb.",sec={{t="A Shattered Prison",b="Soran'ruk's prison orb was broken apart after the demon fell from favor with the Burning Legion. Demons who displease their masters may have their spirits sealed in orbs, then given to fel spellcasters as sources of power. The Twilight's Hammer cultists in the submerged ruins of Blackfathom Deeps possess smaller shards from one half of the orb. They draw on the lingering demonic essence for their own workings.",sp=0},{t="Reconstruction in the Barrens",b="Each fragment still holds a trace of the imprisoned demon's vitality. Doan Karhan, a reclusive scholar in the southern Barrens, has spent a lifetime studying demonic vessels and owns a similar orb, the Orb of Zargain. An ambitious warlock can bring him three small fragments and the larger piece held in Silverpine. He can forge the relic whole again as an instrument of power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Soran'ruk?",a="Soran'ruk was a demon of the Burning Legion who fell from favor with its leaders. As punishment, its spirit was drawn out and trapped in a crystalline orb, where it served mortal warlocks and mages as a source of energy.",al={"who is soranruk","soran'ruk lore","is soranruk a demon"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these fragments found?",a="Twilight Acolytes carry the smaller shards through the cavernous halls of Blackfathom Deeps along the Zoram Strand.",al={"where to get soranruk fragment","who drops soran'ruk fragments","soranruk fragment location"},gp=true},{q="Why does the Twilight's Hammer have these shards?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cultists gather the shards because they retain the trapped demon's magical essence. They use corrupt artifacts to fuel their dark rituals and channel forbidden magic.",al={"why do cultists have it","twilights hammer soranruk"}},{q="Who can restore the Orb of Soran'ruk?",a="Doan Karhan can restore the Orb of Soran'ruk. The solitary hermit lives in the southern Barrens near the border of Thousand Needles and studies and reforges the Burning Legion's demonic orbs.",al={"who fixes the orb","where to turn in soranruk fragment","doan karhan orb"}},{q="Where do the Soran'ruk Fragments come from, and who made them?",a="They are shattered remnants of the Orb of Soran'ruk, a demonic vessel forged by the Burning Legion. When demons fall out of favor, the Legion imprisons their spirits inside such orbs and entrusts them to their mages and warlocks. The orb of Soran'ruk was later broken into pieces, with these smaller shards ending up in the hands of the Twilight's Hammer acolytes within Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"soranruk fragment origin","who made soranruk fragments","where did soranruk fragments come from"},it="origin",add="49c59cce"},{q="Why does anyone want Soran'ruk Fragments?",a="Even broken into shards, the fragments still hum with the essence and power of the trapped demon. The hermit warlock Doan Karhan in the Barrens has dedicated his life to studying and reconstructing Legion orbs. If you bring him these smaller shards along with the large fragment from Shadowfang Keep, he can reforge the Orb of Soran'ruk into a potent implement for your craft.",al={"why gather soranruk fragments","who wants soranruk fragments","why do you need soranruk fragments"},it="why_wanted",add="5e1e8c12"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can use demonic prison vessels like the Orb of Soran'ruk to channel raw fel energy without directly subjugating a demon."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","doan karhan","fel","orb of soran'ruk","soran'ruk","soranruk","twilight acolyte"},rel={"quest:1740","item:large-soran-ruk-fragment","npc:doan-karhan","zone:blackfathom","zone:barrens","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:burning-legion","topic:warlock"},src={"Soran'ruk Fragment","The Orb of Soran'ruk"}}
E["item:southsea-treasure"] = {t="item",n="Southsea Treasure",z="barrens",s="The Southsea Treasure is a valuable hoard kept deep within the hold of the Southsea Freebooter vessel, the Tide Razor. Sought by Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet, retrieving it tests the lockpicking and infiltration skills of fledgling thieves.",h="The Southsea Treasure is a valuable hoard kept deep within the hold of the Southsea Freebooter vessel, the...",sec={{t="A Deadly Heist",b="Anchored along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet, the pirate vessel Tide Razor serves as a forward base and training ground for the Southsea Freebooters. Stashed deep in its lowest hold lies a coveted stash of plunder known as the Southsea Treasure. Wrenix the Wretched, a goblin scoundrel operating out of Ratchet, considers it the ultimate test for aspiring pickpockets. According to Wrenix, the last five operatives sent to filch the chest returned in pieces, owing to the alert pirates aboard and a surprisingly ferocious guardian guarding the hold.",sp=0},{t="Polly's Keepsake",b="Thieves who manage to bypass the pirate trainers and pick the lock on the target chest find a vicious surprise waiting for them. Rather than sitting loose inside the coffer, the true Southsea Treasure is watched over by Polly, an unnaturally hostile parrot. Overcoming the vicious avian—often with the aid of goblin engineering such as Wrenix's E.C.A.C. device—is the only way to pry the treasure loose and bring it back to Ratchet intact.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Southsea Treasure located?",a="The treasure is held aboard the Tide Razor, a Southsea Freebooter ship anchored along the coast south of Ratchet in the Barrens. It rests in the lowest hold beneath the pirates' training quarters.",al={"where is the treasure","tide razor location","how to find southsea treasure"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Southsea Treasure?",a="Wrenix the Wretched, an unscrupulous goblin stationed in Ratchet, hires covert operatives to infiltrate the ship and recover the loot on his behalf.",al={"who gives the quest","who is wrenix","who wants it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the chest empty when picked?",a="Picking the lock on the treasure chest triggers the appearance of Polly, a monstrously aggressive parrot guarding the hold. Defeating Polly is what actually yields the Southsea Treasure.",al={"where did polly come from","why did polly spawn","why isn't the treasure in the box"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="What is an E.C.A.C. and why is it needed?",a="The E.C.A.C. is an experimental goblin device provided by Wrenix the Wretched. It is designed to weaken unusually ferocious airborne threats—specifically the lethal guardian parrot Polly lurking inside the pirate ship's hold.",al={"what is ecac","how to beat polly","hostile parrot"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What do the Southsea Freebooters use the ship for?",a="The Tide Razor serves as a staging ground and thieves' den for the Southsea Freebooters, featuring practice lockboxes on the second level where the crew trains their cutpurses.",al={"what is tide razor","pirate den barrens","southsea ship hold"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Southsea Treasure?",a="The Southsea Treasure is the plundered payoff hoarded by the Southsea Freebooters aboard their vessel, the Tide Razor, anchored off the coast of the Barrens. Kept deep within the ship's hold and guarded by a notoriously ferocious pirate parrot named Polly, it represents the ill-gotten gains accumulated by the corsairs from their raids along the Merchant Coast.",al={"what is southsea treasure","southsea treasure item","what kind of treasure is southsea treasure"},it="identity",add="c9f033cd"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Recovering the Southsea Treasure represents a rite of passage for developing rogues, providing both real-world lockpicking practice and an introduction to the shadowy syndicate known as the Shattered Hand.",["faction:Horde"]="Southsea Freebooters routinely harass trade around the Barrens and the Port of Ratchet, making any theft of their central stash a welcome disruption for local authorities."},kw={"e.c.a.c.","lockpicking","polly","ratchet","shattered hand","southsea treasure","tide razor","wrenix the wretched"},rel={"quest:2381","npc:wrenix-the-wretched","quest:2378","quest:1858","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:pirate","topic:rogue"},src={"Southsea Treasure","Plundering the Plunderers"}}
E["item:stolen-silver"] = {t="item",n="Stolen Silver",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, a strongbox of Horde silver has gone missing from the guard tower. Sunscale raptors carried the coins to their nests at the Raptor Grounds south of Ratchet.",h="At the Crossroads, a strongbox of Horde silver has gone missing from the guard tower.",sec={{t="A Beastly Heist",b="Sunscale raptors carried a strongbox of silver from the Crossroads guard tower. The coins were meant as pay for the garrison guards. The raptors dragged the lockbox to their communal nests at the Raptor Grounds, south of Ratchet. Gazrog and the other overseers cannot explain why the predators took it. The theft leaves them wondering whether the raptors prize shiny things or possess a cunning beyond that of ordinary wild beasts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Stolen Silver?",a="The Stolen Silver is a heavy lockbox of coins meant to pay the Crossroads guards. Raptors stole it from the guard tower and carried it to their nesting grounds.",al={"what is stolen silver","what is the silver"},it="identity"},{q="Why did raptors steal a lockbox of coins?",a="Even Gazrog cannot explain why the raptors took the lockbox. They may have been drawn to its shiny metal, or their unusual cunning may have led them to carry it deep into their lair.",al={"why do raptors want silver","raptor intelligence","why silver"},it="motive"},{q="Where was the silver taken?",a="The raptors took the lockbox to the Raptor Grounds, a rugged canyon of nests south of Ratchet in the eastern Barrens.",al={"stolen silver location","where is the silver"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is looking for the Stolen Silver?",a="Gazrog, an orc stationed at the Crossroads, is looking for the chest. The silver is a full month's pay for the outpost's hard-pressed defenders.",al={"who wants the silver","who turns in stolen silver"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Crossroads is the heart of the Horde's presence in the Barrens. Recovering the pay keeps the local grunts fed, paid, and ready to hold the line against centaur and Alliance incursions."},kw={"barrens payroll","crossroads","gazrog","raptor grounds","silver lockbox","stolen silver","sunscale raptor"},rel={"quest:3281","quest:869","npc:gazrog","subzone:raptor-grounds","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet"},src={"Stolen Silver","Stolen Silver (quest)"}}
E["item:tear-of-the-moons"] = {t="item",n="Tear of the Moons",z="barrens",s="At Bael Modan in the southern Barrens, dwarven excavators have unearthed the Tear of the Moons. Its strange power draws Feegly into obsession, while General Twinbraid fears what the crystal can do.",h="At Bael Modan in the southern Barrens, dwarven excavators have unearthed the Tear of the Moons.",sec={{t="A Unearthed Relic",b="Dwarven excavators unearthed the Tear of the Moons during the first digging at Bael Modan. The crystal's strange radiance captivated the miners, especially Feegly. He claimed it gave him great strength, then grew unstable and turned against his comrades. General Twinbraid, commander of the expedition, feared the relic's influence and declared it cursed. He took the crystal and locked it in his personal strongbox at Bael'dun Keep. Then he cast Feegly out into the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Obsession",b="Exiled Feegly cannot master his craving for the crystal's power. He asks passing Horde travelers to help break into the dwarven fortress and take it from Twinbraid's vault. When Feegly gets the Tear and rubs it, strange grunts escape him. The crystal falls from his hands and shatters on the ground. Feegly turns into a trogg and dies shortly afterward.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where did the Tear of the Moons come from?",a="Dwarven Prospectors and excavators unearthed the Tear of the Moons at Bael Modan, an archaeological dig site in the southern Barrens.",al={"tear origin","where was the tear found","tear of the moons background"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the crystal locked inside Bael'dun Keep?",a="General Twinbraid feared the crystal was cursed after Feegly grew obsessed with it and turned against his fellow miners. He locked it in his strongbox at Bael'dun Keep to protect the expedition.",al={"why locked up","twinbraid strongbox tear","why did twinbraid take it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when Feegly gets the Tear back?",a="Feegly rubs the crystal, which falls from his hands and shatters. He turns into a trogg and dies shortly afterward.",al={"feegly turning trogg","what happens to feegly","trogg transformation feegly"},sp=1},{q="Can the Tear of the Moons be saved or repaired?",a="The Tear shatters when Feegly gets it back. The account gives no word of anyone repairing it afterward.",al={"can you keep the tear","shattered tear","repair tear of the moons"},sp=1},{q="What is the Tear of the Moons?",a="The Tear of the Moons is a mysterious, glowing crystal unearthed by dwarven excavators during their delve into Bael Modan in the southern Barrens. Though celebrated as the site's first great discovery, the artifact proved deeply unstable, radiating a corrupting power that warped the mind of the dwarf who held it and prompted the expedition's leadership to lock it away.",al={"tear of the moons","what is tear of the moons","what is the tear"},it="identity",add="f703febe"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Feegly's fate warns of the danger the Bael'dun expedition risks waking beneath Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help recover the relic from Bael'dun Keep, disrupting the Ironforge military presence encroaching on ancestral tauren lands."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun keep","barrens","excavation","feegly","tear of the moons","trogg","twinbraid"},rel={"quest:857","npc:feegly-the-exiled","subzone:bael-dun-keep","subzone:bael-modan","topic:trogg","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Tear of the Moons","The Tear of the Moons"}}
E["item:telescopic-lens"] = {t="item",n="Telescopic Lens",z="barrens",s="Gazlowe needs the Telescopic Lens to finish the observatory telescope above Ratchet’s harbor. Southsea pirates took it from a ship, and the lens remains in their camp south of town.",h="Gazlowe needs the Telescopic Lens to finish the observatory telescope above Ratchet’s harbor.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Sky",b="Ratchet is known chiefly for ruthless commerce, but its overseer and chief engineer, Gazlowe, has greater mechanical ambitions. His observatory rises above the harbor to house a telescope for watching maritime traffic and the stars. The larger lens came safely overland from Durotar. The smaller, vital lens traveled by sea, where Southsea Freebooters prey on merchant lanes off the Barrens coast.",sp=0},{t="Pirate Plunder",b="The Southsea Freebooters took anything of value when they raided the transport ship, including the delicate optics. The pirates may have left the lens among the clutter of their beachside camp south of Ratchet because they could not appreciate its craft or did not know how to pawn it. Gazlowe needs the unblemished glass brought back so his observation deck can come into focus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gazlowe need this lens?",a="Gazlowe needs the Telescopic Lens to finish the telescope in Ratchet’s observatory. The larger lens arrived overland from Durotar, but the smaller lens was lost at sea.",al={"gazlowe lens","what is the lens for","why telescope lens"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who stole the Telescopic Lens?",a="Southsea Freebooters stole the Telescopic Lens. They are opportunistic human and goblin pirates who prey on merchant ships near the Merchant Coast, and they keep the lens in a marked crate at their coastal camp south of Ratchet.",al={"who took the lens","who has the lens","telescopic lens location"}},{q="Where did the lens originally come from?",a="The Telescopic Lens was shipped by sea to Ratchet, while its counterpart came overland from Durotar. Inbound shipments to the port often come from across the Great Sea or from southern goblin holdings such as Booty Bay.",al={"where was lens made","lens origin","where did gazlowe order lens"},it="origin"},{q="Is the lens undamaged despite being stolen?",a="Miraculously, the lens survived unharmed. A crate marked “Fragile - Do Not Drop” protected the precision glass from the pirates’ rough handling.",al={"is the lens broken","fragile do not drop crate"}},{q="What is the Telescopic Lens?",a="It is a precision-crafted optical lens designed for an observatory telescope. Gazlowe commissioned two specialized lenses to complete the telescope atop his tower in Ratchet, and this smaller secondary piece was shipped overseas before being intercepted by Southsea Freebooters.",al={"what is telescopic lens","telescopic lens item","what is this lens"},it="identity",add="ddcd39c0"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the fine optical craft in this lens. It is needed to focus long-range observation mechanisms without spherical aberration.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may scoff at goblin rocketry, but Gazlowe’s devotion to optical astronomy shows goblin engineering is not all about high explosives."},kw={"crate","gazlowe","observatory","ratchet","southsea freebooters","stolen booty","telescopic lens"},rel={"quest:888","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:pirate","item:shipment-of-boots","quest:887","quest:890"},src={"Telescopic Lens","Stolen Booty"}}
E["item:theramore-medal"] = {t="item",n="Theramore Medal",z="barrens",s="At Northwatch Hold, Theramore Medal marks service among the marines and officers defending the outpost along the Merchant Coast. The insignia bears Theramore’s mark and identifies the Alliance garrison.",h="At Northwatch Hold, Theramore Medal marks service among the marines and officers defending the outpost along...",sec={{t="Tokens of Northwatch",b="Marines, marksmen, commandos, and officers serving from Northwatch Hold carry stamped medals bearing Theramore’s mark. The soldiers are loyal to Lady Jaina Proudmoore’s realm. For the human troops on the cliffs above the Barrens, the medals show that their service is legitimate and their authority comes from Theramore. Others see the tokens as trophies from an overzealous foreign garrison, one that treats every vessel approaching the coast as a mortal threat.",sp=0},{t="Pirate Vengeance",b="Northwatch Hold’s gun batteries menace ships along the Merchant Coast, often bombarding privateers and merchantmen alike. After losing ships to the guns, Ratchet privateer Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun seeks the medals. He wants proof that Northwatch’s trigger-happy ranks have paid in blood for sinking his ships, and that the soldiers responsible have been slain in retribution.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Theramore Medal?",a="A Theramore Medal is an insignia carried by Theramore military personnel serving at Northwatch Hold. It identifies the bearer as an active marine, sailor, or officer in the Alliance garrison in the Barrens.",al={"theramore medal","what are theramore medals","northwatch medal"},it="identity"},{q="Who carries these medals?",a="Marines, sharpshooters, deck hands, commandos, senior cannoneers, and officers serving at Northwatch Hold carry these medals along the Merchant Coast.",al={"who has theramore medals","who drops theramore medals","where do theramore medals come from"},it="people"},{q="Why does Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun want them?",a="Northwatch Hold’s artillery has bombarded passing ships, including vessels belonging to Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun’s fleet. He demands the medals as proof that the soldiers responsible have been slain in retribution.",al={"why does ratchet want medals","brightsun medals","why collect theramore medals"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Northwatch Hold attacking passing ships?",a="Northwatch Hold’s garrison is paranoid on the edge of Horde territory. Its cannoneers have grown reckless and trigger-happy, firing on nearly any vessel that approaches their coastal enclave.",al={"why is northwatch shooting ships","northwatch aggression","why does northwatch attack ratchet"},it="conflict"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance loyalists, medals of Theramore gathered as blood bounties show how isolated and aggressive Northwatch Hold has become on Kalimdor’s frontier.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde adventurers, these medals are proof of the growing Alliance military presence on the shores of the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","captain fairmount","merchant coast","northwatch hold","thalo'thas brightsun","theramore medal"},rel={"quest:891","npc:captain-thalo-thas-brightsun","subzone:merchant-coast","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:alliance","topic:human"},src={"Theramore Medal","The Guns of Northwatch (Classic)"}}
E["item:thunder-lizard-blood"] = {t="item",n="Thunder Lizard Blood",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, hunters bring back Thunder Lizard Blood as proof of survival. The blood comes from the great beasts that roam the plains.",h="In the southern Barrens, hunters bring back Thunder Lizard Blood as proof of survival.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Hunt",b="Thunder lizards go by the names Stormsnouts, Stormhides, and Thunderheads across the plains. Their heavy steps shake the earth, and their crushing weight can flatten unwary hunters. Bringing back their blood shows the skill to hunt them and the endurance to survive beneath their thundering feet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures provide this blood?",a="Stormsnouts, Stormhides, and Thunderheads provide the blood. These mature thunder lizards roam the savannah around Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens.",al={"who drops thunder lizard blood","where to get thunder lizard blood","which thunder lizards"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why is Thunder Lizard Blood sought after?",a="Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo asks hunters to gather the blood as part of trials across the Barrens. Bringing it back unbroken proves a hunter can face Kalimdor's largest stomping beasts.",al={"who wants thunder lizard blood","thunder lizard blood purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these thunder lizards usually found?",a="Thunder lizards roam the grasslands north, east, and south of Camp Taurajo, grazing alongside the other large animals of the southern Barrens.",al={"thunder lizard locations","where are stormsnouts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Thunder Lizard Blood?",a="Thunder Lizard Blood is a vital fluid harvested from the massive thunder lizards that roam the southern Barrens. These towering beasts shake the plains with every stride, and taking their blood serves as irrefutable proof that a hunter possessed the skill and resilience to bring down such formidable creatures without being crushed underfoot.",al={"what is thunder lizard blood","thunder lizard blood item","about thunder lizard blood"},it="identity",add="25735f1e"},{q="Where does Thunder Lizard Blood come from, and who made it?",a="This blood is naturally drawn from the mighty thunder lizards inhabiting the southern Barrens, specifically the breeds known as Stormsnouts, Stormhides, and Thunderheads. It is not manufactured or crafted by mortal hands, but taken directly from these colossal beasts by hunters who dare to face their trampling hooves across the savanna.",al={"where does thunder lizard blood come from","who made thunder lizard blood","thunder lizard blood origin"},it="origin",add="d2820178"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you need steady footing and agility to best a thunder lizard. Taking its blood proves your mastery of the savannah's largest beasts.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter from Camp Taurajo, you face thunder lizards in a traditional test of survival alongside the formidable giants of your homeland."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","jorn skyseer","stormhide","stormsnout","thunder lizard blood","thunderhead"},rel={"quest:907","quest:3261","subzone:camp-taurajo","quest:860","zone:barrens"},src={"Thunder Lizard Blood","Enraged Thunder Lizards"}}
E["item:thunder-lizard-horn"] = {t="item",n="Thunder Lizard Horn",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Brewmaster Drohn seeks a Thunder Lizard Horn for Chen Stormstout's legendary brew.",h="In the Barrens, Brewmaster Drohn seeks a Thunder Lizard Horn for Chen Stormstout's legendary brew.",sec={{t="A Potent Brewing Reagent",b="Thunder lizards roam the Barrens, their crested bodies crackling with lightning. Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet values their horns as an ingredient for Stormstout ale. His mentor learned the recipe from the wandering pandaren Brewmaster Chen Stormstout and passed it down to Drohn. The horn gives the drink its potent kick.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the horn used for?",a="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet uses the horn as an ingredient in the brew Chen Stormstout made famous.",al={"thunder lizard horn use","what uses thunder lizard horn","why do i need thunder lizard horn"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which beasts yield a thunder lizard horn?",a="Thunderheads, stormsnouts, thunderstomps, stormhides, and the elusive Owatanka can yield a thunder lizard horn.",al={"where to get thunder lizard horn","who drops thunder lizard horn","thunder lizard horn sources"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who is Brewmaster Drohn?",a="Brewmaster Drohn brews in Ratchet. His former mentor learned the Stormstout recipe from Chen Stormstout and passed it down to him.",al={"who is drohn","brewmaster drohn lore","drohn ratchet"},it="people"},{q="Are thunder lizards dangerous to hunt for their horns?",a="Thunder lizards can discharge lightning and unleash thunderous stomps when provoked, making them dangerous to hunt alone.",al={"how tough are thunder lizards","hunting thunder lizards"},it="danger"},{q="What is a Thunder Lizard Horn?",a="A thunder lizard horn is a sturdy natural trophy harvested from the great thunder lizards roaming the plains of the Barrens. These imposing, storm-attuned reptiles channel electrical energy through their massive bodies, making their horns a potent natural component prized by rare artisans with unconventional recipes.",al={"what is thunder lizard horn","thunder lizard horn info","about thunder lizard horn"},it="identity",add="6ace69b3"},{q="Where does a Thunder Lizard Horn come from?",a="It is not an artificial creation, but a horn taken directly from the formidable thunder lizards of the Barrens, including creatures like stormsnouts, thunderheads, and the elusive Owatanka. Slaying one of these massive beasts allows you to claim the horn intact.",al={"where do thunder lizard horns come from","who makes thunder lizard horn","thunder lizard horn source"},it="origin",add="1dc3a738"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you may find Drohn's recipe unusual: it combines plainstrider organs, predator tusks, and a beast's horn into an intoxicating drink.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, take care when tracking thunder lizards across the open savannah. Their lightning makes them deadlier than ordinary Barrens kodo or plainstriders."},kw={"barrens","brewmaster drohn","chen stormstout","owatanka","ratchet","stormsnout","stormstout","thunder lizard horn","thunderhead"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","quest:819","quest:884","item:savannah-lion-tusk","item:plainstrider-kidney","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet"},src={"Thunder Lizard Horn","Chen's Empty Keg (2)"}}
E["item:thunderhawk-saliva-gland"] = {t="item",n="Thunderhawk Saliva Gland",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, greater thunderhawks yield a gland prized by Brewmaster Drohn. He needs it to recreate Chen Stormstout's fiery Trogg Ale.",h="Across the Barrens, greater thunderhawks yield a gland prized by Brewmaster Drohn.",sec={{t="A Wild Ingredient",b="Greater thunderhawks hunt across the Barrens' arid savannas. These winged serpents are known for harnessing storms, and the older, more dangerous ones produce a saliva gland charged with natural potency. Travelers keep clear of the deadly beasts, but brewmasters value the gland as a rare base for exotic drinks.",sp=0},{t="Chen's Secret Recipes",b="Brewmaster Drohn settled outside Ratchet after Chen Stormstout traveled through Kalimdor. Drohn studies the wandering brewmaster's fermentation methods and needs a fresh thunderhawk saliva gland, stormhide lightning glands, and kodo liver to brew Trogg Ale. The fiery spirit has an unmistakable kick and is meant to fortify hardy adventurers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do you find a Thunderhawk Saliva Gland?",a="Greater thunderhawks hunt across the open savannas of the Barrens, and their saliva glands are harvested there.",al={"thunderhawk saliva gland drop","where to get saliva gland","thunderhawk gland location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the saliva gland used for?",a="Brewmaster Drohn outside Ratchet needs the gland to brew Trogg Ale, a potent recipe Chen Stormstout left behind.",al={"saliva gland use","what is thunderhawk saliva gland for","thunderhawk saliva purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Brewmaster Drohn?",a="Brewmaster Drohn lives near Ratchet's port. He learned exotic brewing from the wandering traveler Chen Stormstout and trades powerful ales to adventurers who brave local wildlife for ingredients.",al={"drohn ratchet","who is drohn","brewmaster drohn lore"},it="people"},{q="What is Trogg Ale?",a="Chen Stormstout conceived Trogg Ale as a fiercely potent drink. Brewmaster Drohn makes it with a greater thunderhawk's saliva gland, lightning glands, and kodo liver.",al={"trogg ale lore","what is trogg ale","chen's trogg ale"},it="item"},{q="What is a Thunderhawk Saliva Gland?",a="It is an organ harvested from the mature, predatory greater thunderhawks that soar above the arid plains of the Barrens. Imbued with the natural energies and venomous fluids native to these avian beasts, the gland provides a sharp, volatile secretion prized by daring brewers who seek untraditional concoctions with an unmistakable kick.",al={"what is thunderhawk saliva gland","thunderhawk saliva gland lore","about thunderhawk saliva gland"},it="identity",add="bfe8bf39"},{q="Where does a Thunderhawk Saliva Gland come from?",a="It is not a manufactured good, but a biological organ taken from the greater thunderhawks roaming the open skies and crags of the Barrens. Hunters must track down these powerful winged predators and carefully extract the gland intact from their carcasses.",al={"thunderhawk saliva gland origin","where do thunderhawk saliva glands come from","who made thunderhawk saliva gland"},it="origin",add="dda65d1e"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you may balk at using saliva glands, but inventive brewmasters prize strange animal essences for their zest and potency.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can prove yourself by hunting fierce thunderhawks across the Barrens as you travel through Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","drohn","gland","keg","ratchet","saliva","thunderhawk","trogg ale"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","quest:819","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","item:lightning-gland","item:kodo-liver"},src={"Thunderhawk Saliva Gland","Chen's Empty Keg (3)"}}
E["item:thunderhawk-wings"] = {t="item",n="Thunderhawk Wings",z="barrens",s="Across the central and southern Barrens, hunters claim Thunderhawk Wings from the wind serpents that soar overhead. At Camp Taurajo, Jorn Skyseer receives them as proof of a hunter’s strength, cunning, and endurance.",h="Across the central and southern Barrens, hunters claim Thunderhawk Wings from the wind serpents that soar...",sec={{t="Trophy of the Hunt",b="Hunters stationed at Camp Taurajo prize a pair of intact Thunderhawk Wings. Wind serpents, whom local hunters call thunderhawks, are fierce winged reptiles that strike swiftly from above. Tracking them across the open plains and claiming their wings in combat tests a hunter’s skill. For an initiate, bringing back the wings proves readiness to follow the lifelong path of an accomplished hunter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Thunderhawk Wings found?",a="Thunderhawk Wings come from thunderhawks gliding above the ridges and plains of the central and southern Barrens, especially around Camp Taurajo.",al={"where get wings","thunderhawk wings location","how to get thunderhawk wings"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants these wings?",a="Jorn Skyseer, a seasoned tauren hunter stationed at Camp Taurajo, asks for the wings as proof that an initiate has mastered the savanna’s hunting rites.",al={"who takes thunderhawk wings","turn in thunderhawk wings","jorn skyseer wings"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="What does claiming the wings signify?",a="Bringing the wings to Jorn Skyseer completes a challenging rite of passage. It shows the hunter has the strength, courage, and patience to face fierce aerial predators.",al={"why hunt thunderhawk","wings purpose","significance of thunderhawk hunt"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are Thunderhawk Wings?",a="These wings are harvested from thunderhawks, the majestic feathered wind serpents that soar above the plains of the southern Barrens. Fierce and proud predators, thunderhawks are revered by the tauren as symbols of strength and wild majesty. Taking the creature's wings is not done lightly; they serve as a physical testament of a hunter's skill, courage, and respect in confronting one of the sky's most formidable beasts.",al={"what are thunderhawk wings","thunderhawk wings lore","wings of thunderhawk"},it="identity",add="1074baa7"},{q="Where do Thunderhawk Wings come from?",a="The wings are taken directly from slain thunderhawks roaming the open skies around Camp Taurajo. Naturally gifted with lightning and agility, these winged serpents are native aerial predators of the Barrens, making the wings purely natural trophies taken at the climax of a demanding hunt.",al={"where do thunderhawk wings come from","thunderhawk wings source","who drops thunderhawk wings"},it="origin",add="dd263964"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, claiming a soaring thunderhawk’s wings marks a rite of passage. It tests your tracking, patience, and marksmanship against swift aerial beasts.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor the savanna’s spirit by harvesting these wings and showing respect for the Earthmother’s fierce creatures."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","jorn skyseer","sergra darkthorn","thunderhawk","wind serpent","wings"},rel={"quest:913","quest:3261","subzone:camp-taurajo","quest:860","zone:barrens","topic:hunter"},src={"Thunderhawk Wings","Cry of the Thunderhawk"}}
E["item:tome-of-the-cabal-quest-item"] = {t="item",n="Tome of the Cabal (quest item)",z="barrens",s="Warlocks in Ratchet receive the Tome of the Cabal from Strahad Farsan after gathering dangerous components. Its pages hold the incantations for drawing a felhunter across the Twisting Nether and binding it.",h="Warlocks in Ratchet receive the Tome of the Cabal from Strahad Farsan after gathering dangerous components.",sec={{t="A Gateway to the Nether",b="A felhunter is a vicious beast from the chaotic Twisting Nether, feared for devouring mana. Subduing one marks a passage for seasoned warlocks. The Tome of the Cabal holds the rites for opening a path to such a demon. Strahad Farsan, an experienced conjurer in Ratchet, gives the tome to an aspirant only after they gather the rare and dangerous components its magic requires.",sp=0},{t="The Summoning Ritual",b="Strahad Farsan establishes the primary summoning circle in his sanctum, while his acolytes use rods of channeling to form a greater protective boundary. The warlock recites the tome's exact incantations and drags the felhunter into our world. The demon must be battled at once and subdued, binding it to the warlock's will.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of the Cabal used for?",a="The Tome of the Cabal holds the incantations for summoning a felhunter from the Twisting Nether into a prepared circle in Ratchet, where a warlock can face and bind the demon.",al={"what does tome of the cabal do","tome of cabal purpose","tome felhunter"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Tome of the Cabal?",a="Strahad Farsan, a warlock mentor living in the hills above Ratchet in the Barrens, provides the tome after a practitioner completes the arduous preparations.",al={"who gives tome of the cabal","where to get tome of the cabal","strahad book"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Do you keep the tome after completing the ritual?",a="No. After defeating the summoned felhunter and proving your mastery, you return the Tome of the Cabal to Strahad Farsan as proof of your success.",al={"do i keep the book","tome of the cabal reward","keep tome of cabal"},gp=true},{q="Can you summon the felhunter anywhere in the world?",a="No. You must read the incantations in Strahad Farsan's sanctuary above Ratchet, where he and his acolytes maintain the greater and lesser summoning circles needed to contain the arriving beast.",al={"summon felhunter anywhere","where to read tome","tome ritual location"},gp=true},{q="What is the Tome of the Cabal?",a="The Tome of the Cabal is an esoteric grimoire containing specialized demonic rituals and incantations. Entrusted to seasoned warlocks by Strahad Farsan above Ratchet, the book details the dangerous rites required to breach the Nether and compel a vicious felhunter to your bidding.",al={"what is tome of the cabal","tome of the cabal lore","about tome of the cabal"},it="identity",add="42bf8406"},{q="Where does the Tome of the Cabal come from, and who made it?",a="The tome was written by the first group of warlocks to summon a felhunter unaided. Once held in Lordaeron, it was vandalized and split into a Moldy Tome and a Tattered Manuscript. A warlock recovers these portions from the Hillsbrad coast and the centaur of Thousand Needles, then brings the reconstructed volume to Strahad Farsan.",al={"who made the tome of the cabal","where does tome of the cabal come from","creator tome cabal"},it="origin",add="a251072b"},{q="Why does anyone want the Tome of the Cabal?",a="Aspiring warlocks seek out the Tome of the Cabal because it holds the precise incantation needed to draw forth a felhunter into a prepared summoning circle. Without the tome's exact words, subduing one of these dangerous mana-devouring fiends would be virtually impossible.",al={"why want tome of the cabal","why do warlocks want the tome of the cabal","purpose of tome cabal"},it="why_wanted",add="03fa6157"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you must master this tome to claim a felhunter companion and gain dominion over demonic magic."},kw={"felhunter","ratchet","strahad farsan","summoning circle","the binding","tome of the cabal"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","quest:1471","quest:1758","topic:warlock","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Tome of the Cabal (quest item)","The Binding (Felhunter)"}}
E["item:twitching-antenna"] = {t="item",n="Twitching Antenna",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, silithid antennae still twitch after they are cut free. Ruga Ragetotem at Camp Taurajo seeks them as proof of a young warrior’s speed and skill in combat before the nerves go still.",h="In the southern Barrens, silithid antennae still twitch after they are cut free.",sec={{t="Proof of the Hunt",b="Silithid Grubs, Swarmers, Harvesters, and Creepers carry antennae that twitch after they are cut from the head. The spasms fade soon after the insects are slain. A young warrior must hunt silithid in the southern wastes and hurry back across the scrublands while the antennae still twitch. Bringing them back in time tests both speed and skill, making the hunt a rite of passage for Horde warriors.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the South",b="The silithid antennae also point to a threat that troubles Camp Taurajo’s hunters. Silithid are not native to the Barrens, and their new burrowing mounds at the Field of Giants unsettle the camp. Ruga Ragetotem wants the specimens to study the danger and prepare Horde warriors for the alien menace moving into the plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures drop Twitching Antennae?",a="Silithid Grubs, Harvesters, Swarmers, and Creepers around the Field of Giants in the southern Barrens carry the antennae.",al={"where do twitching antennae drop","who drops twitching antenna","silithid antenna source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why do the antennae have to be twitching?",a="The twitching shows the antennae were freshly cut. Ruga Ragetotem uses how quickly they go still to test an aspirant’s speed and combat skill across the wild terrain.",al={"why twitching","why the rush for antennae","trial at field of giants timer"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is looking for these antennae?",a="Ruga Ragetotem, a tauren warrior at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, seeks the antennae for the Trial at the Field of Giants.",al={"who wants twitching antenna","who turns in antennae"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Field of Giants?",a="The Field of Giants lies south of Camp Taurajo in the Barrens. Massive skeletal remains rise from the earth there, with silithid hives around them.",al={"where is field of giants","field of giants location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a Twitching Antenna?",a="A Twitching Antenna is a freshly severed sensory organ harvested from one of the silithid infesting the southern Barrens. These bizarre insectoid appendages continue to spasm and twitch with nervous energy for a short period after being carved away from grubs, swarmers, and harvesters.",al={"what is twitching antenna","twitching antenna lore","silithid antenna"},it="identity",add="47f6f8c0"},{q="Where does a Twitching Antenna come from?",a="These antennae come from the bizarre silithid swarm that has recently emerged around the Field of Giants in the southern Barrens. Severed directly from creatures like grubs, swarmers, creepers, and harvesters, they are organic biological matter rather than crafted tools.",al={"where do twitching antennae come from","who drops twitching antenna","silithid parts"},it="origin",add="057f3d5d"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you track and slay silithid, then gather their antennae while they still twitch. The trial tests your speed, tracking, and skill in the field.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know Camp Taurajo’s hunters see the silithid’s sudden arrival as a disturbance to the plains’ natural balance. Young braves must stay vigilant."},kw={"antennae","barrens","camp taurajo","field of giants","ruga ragetotem","silithid","twitching antenna"},rel={"quest:1824","npc:ruga-ragetotem","subzone:field-of-giants","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:barrens","npc:grub"},src={"Twitching Antenna","Trial at the Field of Giants"}}
E["item:unrefined-ore-sample"] = {t="item",n="Unrefined Ore Sample",z="barrens",s="In Thousand Needles, an unusual ore draws the Horde's attention. Tatternack Steelforge seeks a sample to judge whether the raw mineral can strengthen the weapons of Warchief Thrall's armies.",h="In Thousand Needles, an unusual ore draws the Horde's attention.",sec={{t="Mined by the Vermin",b="South of the Barrens, Gravelsnout kobolds dig through the stone beneath the canyon walls of Thousand Needles. Travelers returning north found a curious mineral among slain vermin, unlike the usual veins of Kalimdor. They refused to surrender their prize to the Horde. The kobolds who dig and survey the depths carry raw chunks of the ore from their excavations.",sp=0},{t="Forging for the Warchief",b="At Camp Taurajo, weaponsmith Tatternack Steelforge works under orders from Warchief Thrall to improve the Horde's arms. Travelers who kept knowledge of the deposit angered him; he saw their refusal as an insult to the Horde's war effort. With a raw sample, Tatternack plans to test the mineral's strength and temper, then smelt it and forge a prototype blade for Orgrimmar's approval.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this unrefined ore come from?",a="Gravelsnout kobolds carry the ore from the canyon depths of Thousand Needles, south of the Barrens. Their diggers, surveyors, and leader Gibblesnik live there.",al={"ore location","where get unrefined ore sample","who drops unrefined ore"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Tatternack Steelforge want a sample?",a="Tatternack works under the Warchief's orders to improve Horde weapons. He wants to inspect and smelt the ore to learn whether it can be forged into stronger arms.",al={"why tatternack want ore","ore purpose taurajo","what is ore for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why were the travelers reluctant to part with it?",a="Horde travelers crossing from Thousand Needles found the ore on a kobold and kept it as a trophy or curiosity. They refused to sell it, even when asked to help the Horde's smithing efforts.",al={"who were the travelers","travelers ore barrens"},it="motive"},{q="Is this ore found anywhere in the Barrens?",a="No. Camp Taurajo lies in the southern Barrens, but the ore must be recovered from kobolds farther south in Thousand Needles.",al={"ore in barrens","can you mine it in barrens"},it="place"},{q="What is an Unrefined Ore Sample?",a="It is a piece of raw, unusual mineral dug up from the earth by the kobolds of Thousand Needles. Unlike standard veins worked throughout the Barrens, this unfamiliar ore catches the eye of smiths for its potential durability, though it requires smelting and proper study before anyone can judge whether it is fit for forging.",al={"what is unrefined ore sample","unrefined ore sample","what is the ore sample"},it="identity",add="5c1fb5e1"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can understand Tatternack's frustration. Testing new ore for strength and durability helps smiths outfit warriors with blades that will not shatter in combat.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know each new mineral vein in southern Kalimdor could help Thrall's young nation supply its own arms as it secures its borders."},kw={"camp taurajo","gibblesnik","gravelsnout","kobold","ore","tatternack steelforge","thousand needles","unrefined ore sample"},rel={"quest:1153","npc:tatternack-steelforge","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens","quest:893","topic:kobold","topic:horde"},src={"Unrefined Ore Sample","A New Ore Sample"}}
E["item:verog-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Verog's Head",z="barrens",s="Regthar Deathgate seeks Verog's Head as proof of the Kolkar leader's death. The chieftain commands forces around the Stagnant Oasis, and his defeat is meant to weaken the tribes threatening the Barrens.",h="Regthar Deathgate seeks Verog's Head as proof of the Kolkar leader's death.",sec={{t="A Trophy of the Oasis",b="The Kolkar centaur threaten Horde travelers and supply routes across the northern Barrens. Verog the Dervish roams the arid scrubland, leaving his command tent at the Stagnant Oasis vulnerable. Horde operatives attack his forces around the pavilion until an alarm sounds. Verog rushes back to defend his camp, where he is slain and decapitated. Regthar Deathgate receives his head as proof that another dangerous Kolkar chieftain has fallen. Barak Kodobane's head is already on display beside it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Verog the Dervish?",a="Verog the Dervish was a Kolkar centaur warlord based at the Stagnant Oasis in the Barrens. He roamed the arid plains and commanded the hostile forces around the oasis tent.",al={"who is verog","verog lore","verog the dervish"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Verog's head?",a="Regthar Deathgate, an orc veteran at an encampment west of the Crossroads, wants Verog's head. He collects trophies from slain Kolkar warlords to weaken their warbands and morale.",al={"who takes verog head","regthar deathgate verog","turn in verog head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Verog found?",a="Verog's encampment and command tent are at the Stagnant Oasis, southeast of the Crossroads. He returns to defend his post when centaur guards are slain and an alarm is raised.",al={"where is verog","verog location","stagnant oasis tent"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to the head after it is turned in?",a="Regthar Deathgate places Verog's head beside Barak Kodobane's. The heads mark the Horde's campaign against Kolkar leaders.",al={"what does regthar do with the head","centaur heads display"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Verog's Head?",a="It is the severed head of Verog the Dervish, one of the prominent Kolkar centaur leaders operating out of the Stagnant Oasis. It serves as gruesome physical proof of his demise, taken to reassure the Horde garrison west of the Crossroads that the threat posed by this elusive commander has been permanently extinguished.",al={"verog head item","what is verogs head"},it="item",add="f5f2a432"},{q="Where does Verog's Head come from?",a="The head is claimed directly from Verog the Dervish himself. The nomadic Kolkar leader roams the plains of the Barrens, but when his encampment at the Stagnant Oasis comes under direct attack, he returns to defend his command tent, allowing you to strike him down and claim his head as a trophy.",al={"where does verog head come from","who drops verog head"},it="origin",add="7da1755c"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Defeating Verog and taking his head helps secure Horde routes between the Crossroads and the southern Barrens against centaur raids.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the weight of the Kolkar defeat: your people have endured generations of brutal warfare against the centaur tribes of Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","centaur","kolkar","regthar deathgate","stagnant oasis","verog","verog the dervish","verog's head"},rel={"quest:851","quest:850","quest:852","quest:1361","subzone:stagnant-oasis","zone:barrens","topic:centaur"},src={"Verog's Head","Verog the Dervish (Classic)"}}
E["item:vial-of-purest-water"] = {t="item",n="Vial of Purest Water",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Brine blesses a vial of pure water for a shaman initiate. Its contents help Islen Waterseer prepare a water sapta for seeing elemental spirits.",h="In the southern Barrens, Brine blesses a vial of pure water for a shaman initiate.",sec={{t="A Purified Offering",b="Brine guides the initiate through trials of patience and cleansing before sealing the water in the vial. The water holds an uncorrupted elemental purity. Carry it across the Barrens to Islen Waterseer, who keeps watch on a solitary shore. She needs it to brew a water sapta. Without such pure water, a shaman cannot commune with spiritual guardians in places far from the sunbaked flats.",sp=0},{t="Path to the Water Totem",b="Islen uses the blessed water to test the initiate’s dedication and open their senses to hidden elements. She blends some into a sapta, which reveals spirits at a distant shrine in Silverpine Forest. She keeps the remaining drops for confronting and cleansing a rogue manifestation elsewhere. Carrying the vial marks a turning point: the initiate moves from humble chores to facing elemental realities directly.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Vial of Purest Water used for?",a="The vial holds water cleansed and blessed for a shaman initiate. Islen Waterseer uses it to brew a water sapta, which grants the spiritual sight needed to perceive water elementals, and for further ritual trials required to earn the Water Totem.",al={"vial of purest water purpose","what does the vial do","use of purest water"},it="purpose"},{q="Who prepares the water inside the vial?",a="The shaman gathers the water under Brine’s direction. Brine is an orc shaman hermit deep in the southern Barrens; after the initiate’s trials, Brine blesses and seals the purified water in the vial for transport.",al={"who made the vial","who fills the vial","brine water"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the vial need to be taken?",a="Carry the vial to Islen Waterseer on the Barrens’ eastern shore, just south of Ratchet and overlooking the Great Sea.",al={"who do I give the vial to","where to deliver vial","turn in purest water"},gp=true},{q="Where does the ritual lead after delivering the vial?",a="After receiving the vial and brewing the sapta, Islen Waterseer sends the shaman across the sea to the Eastern Kingdoms. The shrine lies in Silverpine Forest, south of the Undercity.",al={"where do I go next","next step after vial","silverpine water shrine"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Vial of Purest Water?",a="The Vial of Purest Water is a sacred vessel containing pristine liquid blessed and prepared by the water seer Brine. Entrusted to developing shaman, it holds water gathered from pure sources across the land, purified through ritual to attune you to the spirits of water.",al={"vial of purest water","what is vial of purest water"},it="identity",add="3774bd18"},{q="Why does Islen Waterseer want the Vial of Purest Water?",a="Islen Waterseer requires the blessed water within the vial to brew a water sapta for you. Drinking this special draught grants you spiritual sight, allowing you to commune directly with water elementals at their shrine in Silverpine Forest.",al={"why does islen want the vial","why need vial of purest water","vial of purest water purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="273b8475"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, delivering this purified water brings you through the final steps toward communing with water spirits and claiming your Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde shaman, you cross Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms during the vial’s trials, deepening your bond with the elements."},kw={"barrens","brine","call of water","islen waterseer","silverpine","vial of purest water","water sapta"},rel={"quest:63","npc:islen-waterseer","npc:brine","topic:shaman","zone:barrens","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Vial of Purest Water","Call of Water (6)"}}
E["item:warsong-outrider-update"] = {t="item",n="Warsong Outrider Update",z="barrens",s="Along Ashenvale’s eastern border, a Warsong Outrider prepares a dispatch for the Horde. Stationed there, the outrider records frontline intelligence for couriers serving the Horde to carry, helping secure the crossing toward Azshara and strengthen the orcish foothold against night elf resistance.",h="Along Ashenvale’s eastern border, a Warsong Outrider prepares a dispatch for the Horde.",sec={{t="Frontier Intelligence",b="Beyond Splintertree Post, the eastern road runs toward the ancient ruins of Azshara through Ashenvale’s volatile borderlands. Mounted orcish vanguards patrol this frontier and record tactical sightings, patrol movements, and resource evaluations. They send their field notes to Kadrak at the northern watchtower, which guards the Barrens border. The reports give Horde commanders a clear view of enemy troop concentrations and territorial threats beneath the forest canopy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this update?",a="The update reports night elf activity and conditions along the eastern Ashenvale road toward Azshara. Kadrak uses the intelligence to coordinate Horde troop deployments and strengthen defenses along the Barrens’ northern border.",al={"warsong outrider update purpose","why outrider update","what is this report"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries and delivers this dispatch?",a="A Warsong Outrider patrolling the highway between Splintertree Post and the border of Azshara carries the dispatch. The outrider delivers it to Kadrak and receives fresh strategic orders.",al={"who writes outrider update","where does outrider update come from"},it="people"},{q="Where does this report need to go?",a="Bring the update directly to Kadrak at the northern watchtower, which guards the Barrens border and the southern entrance to Ashenvale.",al={"where do i take outrider update","who wants outrider update"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Warsong so invested in Ashenvale?",a="The Warsong Clan logs Ashenvale’s ancient forests for lumber and construction materials needed in Orgrimmar. Their resource gathering brings them into conflict with the defending night elves and Silverwing Sentinels.",al={"why are orcs in ashenvale","warsong interest ashenvale"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Warsong Outrider Update?",a="It is a field report compiled by a Warsong outrider patrolling the roads of eastern Ashenvale toward the Azshara border. It documents local reconnaissance, troop movements, and observations critical to maintaining the Horde's foothold across the contested forest.",al={"what is warsong outrider update","warsong outrider update item","what is the outrider report"},it="identity",add="0cc42a69"},{q="Where does the Warsong Outrider Update come from, and who made it?",a="It is written and handed over by a Warsong outrider stationed along the forest road between Splintertree Post and the border of Azshara. The outrider drafts these field updates in response to fresh orders delivered from the northern Barrens.",al={"who wrote warsong outrider update","where did warsong outrider update come from","who gave the outrider update"},it="origin",add="2fb6b9e4"},{q="Why does Kadrak want the Warsong Outrider Update?",a="Kadrak coordinates the Horde's frontier presence from the northern watchtower on the Barrens border. He needs the outrider's frontline observations alongside dispatches from other scouts to gauge enemy strength and strategically plan the Warsong clan's next moves deeper into Ashenvale.",al={"why does kadrak need outrider update","why is warsong outrider update needed","why collect outrider update"},it="why_wanted",add="aa3bba6b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on frontline reports to protect supply routes between the Barrens and Ashenvale. Those routes carry lumber needed to expand Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you rely on vigilant scouts and swift couriers to hold Warsong honor and territory against the night elf sentinels disputing your clan’s forestry claims."},kw={"ashenvale","azshara","barrens","kadrak","splintertree post","warsong outrider","warsong outrider update"},rel={"quest:6543","npc:kadrak","npc:warsong-outrider","zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:barrens","zone:azshara","quest:6545"},src={"Warsong Outrider Update","The Warsong Reports"}}
E["item:warsong-runner-update"] = {t="item",n="Warsong Runner Update",z="barrens",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Warsong Runner Update carries reports from western Ashenvale to Kadrak.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Warsong Runner Update carries reports from western Ashenvale to Kadrak.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Western Front",b="The Warsong runner at Zoram'gar Outpost watches the coast and nearby threats in western Ashenvale. The dispatch records observations gathered by scouts at the outpost and reports on local activity. It travels to Kadrak's watchtower on the Barrens border, helping Horde leaders strengthen their position and plan their movements into the elves' ancestral woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Warsong Runner Update?",a="Warsong Runner Update is a written military dispatch from the Warsong runner at Zoram'gar Outpost in western Ashenvale. It carries frontline observations to Horde leaders at the Barrens border.",al={"runner update","what is warsong runner update","warsong report zoram"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this dispatch come from?",a="The dispatch comes from the Warsong runner at Zoram'gar Outpost, on Ashenvale's far western coast near the Zoram Strand.",al={"runner location","where is warsong runner","who gives runner update"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives this update?",a="Kadrak, the Warsong commander in the watchtower along the northern Barrens border, receives the update.",al={"who do i turn this in to","kadrak update","deliver runner update"},it="target"},{q="Why does Kadrak need this dispatch?",a="Kadrak coordinates the Warsong clan's military movements into Ashenvale. Dispatches from outposts such as Zoram'gar tell him about enemy resistance, naval approaches, and control of local territory.",al={"why runner update","warsong reports purpose"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The report shows the difficulty of maintaining distant outposts in hostile night elf territory. Couriers keep communications open between Ashenvale and the Barrens.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know Warsong scouts and couriers risk their lives in dense forests to bring tactical reports to Kadrak and advance the clan's territorial claims."},kw={"ashenvale","kadrak","the barrens","the warsong reports","warsong clan","warsong runner update","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"quest:6543","quest:6545","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:zoram-strand","npc:kadrak","quest:6546","quest:6547","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Warsong Runner Update","The Warsong Reports"}}
E["item:warsong-scout-update"] = {t="item",n="Warsong Scout Update",z="barrens",s="At Splintertree Post, a Warsong scout records what the Horde needs to know about Ashenvale.",h="At Splintertree Post, a Warsong scout records what the Horde needs to know about Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Ancient Forest",b="Warsong scouts watch the woods as the Horde seeks timber and supply routes through Ashenvale. From Splintertree Post, a fortified encampment, they track night elf sentinels and movements across the territory. Their observations reach Kadrak at the Barrens-Ashenvale border among routine orders. He uses them to judge troop readiness and coordinate supplies and travel through the contested woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Warsong Scout Update?",a="The Warsong Scout Update gathers a Warsong scout’s observations from Splintertree Post in eastern Ashenvale for commanders on the border.",al={"scout update","scout report","warsong scout dispatch"},it="identity"},{q="Who requires this update?",a="Kadrak needs the update. The Horde officer watches the border between the northern Barrens and Ashenvale from a watchtower, and uses it to plan military maneuvers.",al={"who wants this","kadrak report","who gets the update"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Warsong Scout located?",a="The scout is stationed inside Splintertree Post, the Horde stronghold along the main road through eastern Ashenvale.",al={"where is scout","scout location","find warsong scout"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are these dispatches so important to the Horde?",a="Night elves fiercely defend Ashenvale. Scout reports warn Horde leaders of ambushes and troop movements, helping keep supply routes and logging camps secure.",al={"why care","warsong logistics","ashenvale intelligence"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the Warsong Scout Update come from, and who made it?",a="This written report is compiled by a Warsong scout stationed within Ashenvale, based out of Splintertree Post to the north. Tasked with observing enemy movements and surveying the contested forest, the scout records vital field intelligence and hands it over in exchange for fresh orders dispatched from the Barrens border.",al={"who wrote warsong scout update","warsong scout update source","who made scout update"},it="origin",add="ed4a3567"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Warsong dispatches keep the Horde’s forward camps in Ashenvale in contact with supply bases in the Barrens as the Horde expands into the forest.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Warsong clan bears the brunt of the logging campaign in Ashenvale. Swift scouts help hold its forest outposts."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","kadrak","report","scout","splintertree","update","warsong"},rel={"quest:6543","quest:6547","npc:kadrak","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","quest:6546","quest:6545","zone:barrens"},src={"Warsong Scout Update","The Warsong Reports"}}
E["item:witchwing-talon"] = {t="item",n="Witchwing Talon",z="barrens",s="In the northwestern Barrens, Witchwing Talons mark dead harpy raiders. Horde scouts at the Crossroads seek them as proof while they work to secure vital caravan routes.",h="In the northwestern Barrens, Witchwing Talons mark dead harpy raiders.",sec={{t="Trophies from the Roosts",b="Witchwing harpies raid Horde supply caravans from their roosts northwest of the Crossroads. Scout Darsok Swiftdagger coordinates strikes against the flock's hierarchy. Darsok requires physical proof of each dead scavenger, and the talons provide it. With proof that raiders have fallen, the scouts can weaken the flock's ranks before striking higher in its command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants Witchwing Talons and why?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger, an orc scout at the Crossroads, collects them. He plans a campaign against the Witchwing brood and requires eight talons as proof that its frontline raiders have been slain.",al={"who needs talons","witchwing talon quest giver","darsok swiftdagger talons"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which harpies carry these talons?",a="Witchwing Talons come from harpies in the northwestern Barrens, including common harpies and Witchwing Roguefeathers that nest along the cliffs and dry ridges.",al={"what drops witchwing talons","which harpies have talons"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why are the Witchwing harpies being targeted?",a="The Witchwing flock has grown increasingly bold, attacking Horde supply lines and trade caravans across the Barrens. Darsok aims to thin its lower ranks before striking its lieutenants and matriarch.",al={"why kill witchwing harpies","harpy raiders purpose"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Witchwing Talon?",a="A Witchwing Talon is a sharp claw harvested directly from the avian feet of the Witchwing harpies infesting the northwestern reaches of the Barrens. To the Horde scouts stationed at the Crossroads, these severed claws serve as undeniable, physical proof of dead raiders.",al={"witchwing talon","what are witchwing talons","witchwing claw"},it="identity",add="5a3e0f86"},{q="Where do Witchwing Talons come from?",a="These talons are naturally grown by the Witchwing harpies dwelling in the canyons of the northwest Barrens. They are taken from the fallen bodies of common Witchwing harpies and Roguefeathers by hunters sent to cull the flock.",al={"witchwing talon origin","where do witchwing talons come from","who drops witchwing talons"},it="origin",add="98111910"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Caravans connect Kalimdor's scattered Horde outposts, so clearing the harpy roosts helps secure the frontier.",["class:Rogue"]="Darsok Swiftdagger values quiet, precise attacks. To him, these sharp claws mark the work of a skilled killer against aerial predators."},kw={"barrens","caravans","crossroads","darsok swiftdagger","harpy","talon","witchwing"},rel={"quest:867","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","topic:harpy","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:875","quest:876","quest:1060"},src={"Witchwing Talon","Harpy Raiders (Classic)"}}
E["item:wolf-heart-sample"] = {t="item",n="Wolf Heart Sample",z="barrens",s="Wolf Heart Sample is bound for the Crossroads, carrying diseased wolf tissue from Lordaeron to Kalimdor. The Royal Apothecary Society seeks to learn what northern toxins do to the Barrens’ native beasts.",h="Wolf Heart Sample is bound for the Crossroads, carrying diseased wolf tissue from Lordaeron to Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Toxic Export",b="Wolf Heart Sample began with plagued wolves in Lordaeron’s ruins. Apothecary Renferrel gathered the hearts, and they were packed for the journey across the Great Sea. The Forsaken’s Royal Apothecary Society seeks greater knowledge of venom, blights, and biological reagents. A courier carries the parcel to the Crossroads in the Barrens, linking Undercity’s experiments in the scarred Eastern Kingdoms with Kalimdor’s frontier outposts.",sp=0},{t="Helbrim's Research",b="At the Crossroads, Apothecary Helbrim receives Wolf Heart Sample. Helbrim studies how toxins from Lordaeron’s Scourge-ravaged lands affect the native wildlife of Kalimdor. The toxicity preserved in the wolf hearts may reveal properties that can improve Forsaken poisons and elixirs far from home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Wolf Heart Sample?",a="Wolf Heart Sample is tissue preserved from blighted wolves in Lordaeron. Its lingering toxicity from the northern plagues gives the Royal Apothecary Society material for studying virulent poisons.",al={"wolf heart sample","what is the sample","what is in the package"},it="identity"},{q="Who sent this sample to the Barrens?",a="Apothecary Zinge sent the sample from Undercity, using wolf hearts Apothecary Renferrel had sent her from Silverpine Forest.",al={"who sent wolf heart","who gave me this","origin of wolf heart sample"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Apothecary Helbrim want it?",a="Helbrim studies how toxins from Lordaeron affect Kalimdor’s native beasts. He plans to examine the sample’s venomous properties to advance Forsaken alchemical compounds and poisons.",al={"why does helbrim want it","helbrim research","purpose of wolf heart"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the sample need to be delivered?",a="Bring the sample to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads, a major Horde settlement in the heart of the Barrens.",al={"where to bring wolf heart","where is helbrim","delivery location"},it="target",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you carry the Royal Apothecary Society’s research into Kalimdor, where it tests northern concoctions against unfamiliar wildlife.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help carry research reagents across the sea, linking Undercity with Horde outposts in the Barrens."},kw={"apothecary helbrim","apothecary renferrel","barrens","crossroads","lordaeron","royal apothecary society","toxins","wolf heart sample"},rel={"npc:apothecary-helbrim","quest:1358","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:lordaeron","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Wolf Heart Sample","Sample for Helbrim"}}
E["item:wood-pulp"] = {t="item",n="Wood Pulp",z="barrens",s="At Bael Modan, Wood Pulp helps the dwarves prepare their blasting charges. The dwarven personnel stationed in the southern Barrens carry it as an absorbent base for stabilizing liquid explosives.",h="At Bael Modan, Wood Pulp helps the dwarves prepare their blasting charges.",sec={{t="A Volatile Recipe",b="At Bael Modan, Ironforge dwarves use earth-moving equipment and chemical explosives to tear into ancestral tauren hunting grounds. Liquid nitroglycerin is unstable on its own, so dwarven engineers soak it into porous wood pulp with sodium nitrate to make stable charges for excavation and combat. Riflemen, soldiers, and officers carry bundles for sapping and field munitions.",sp=0},{t="Turned Against the Keep",b="After Prospector Khazgorm fell, Gann Stonespire recovered the dwarves' blasting schematics. The displaced tauren warrior uses those practices against the invaders encroaching on his tribe's lands. From the Bael'dun garrison, Gann reclaims wood pulp, nitroglycerin, and nitrates to make a charge intended to destroy the dwarves' flying machine at Bael Modan.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is wood pulp used for in Bael Modan?",a="At Bael Modan, dwarven engineers use wood pulp as an absorbent base for munitions. They soak unstable liquid nitroglycerin into it, making demolition charges safer for sappers to carry and handle.",al={"why do dwarves have wood pulp","wood pulp purpose","what does wood pulp do"}},{q="Who carries wood pulp in the Barrens?",a="Dwarven forces stationed at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens carry wood pulp. They include Bael'dun soldiers, riflemen, officers, and their commanding lord, Cyrik Blackforge.",al={"where to get wood pulp","who drops wood pulp","wood pulp location"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gann Stonespire need this wood pulp?",a="Gann Stonespire uses wood pulp to turn the dwarves' destructive methods against them. Following their demolition schematics, he combines it with recovered nitroglycerin and sodium nitrate to make a charge meant to destroy the dwarves' flying machine at Bael Modan.",al={"who wants wood pulp","gann stonespire wood pulp","why collect wood pulp"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does wood pulp explode by itself?",a="No. Raw wood pulp is shredded wood fiber; it becomes dangerous only when combined with volatile chemicals such as nitroglycerin and an oxidizer such as sodium nitrate.",al={"is wood pulp explosive","can wood pulp blow up"}},{q="What is Wood Pulp?",a="Wood pulp is processed plant fiber that the dwarves of Bael Modan keep on hand at their dig site. While innocuous on its own, it serves as a porous, absorbent stabilizer when mixed with volatile liquids like nitroglycerin, turning dangerous chemicals into manageable solid explosives.",al={"what is wood pulp","wood pulp item","wood pulp description"},it="identity",add="1f614fe2"},{q="Where does Wood Pulp come from, and who made it?",a="This pulp is manufactured and stocked by the Ironforge dwarves of the Bael'dun excavation. Soldiers, riflemen, and officers stationed at Bael Modan carry bundles of it through the fortress to supply their blasting operations and artillery works.",al={"where does wood pulp come from","who made wood pulp","wood pulp origin"},it="origin",add="1f0d889e"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers know wood pulp can absorb nitroglycerin and a nitrate oxidizer, stabilizing the volatile liquid in durable dynamite.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren of the Stonespire tribe, you see the invaders' munitions turned against Bael Modan as justice for the destruction of your ancestral home."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun","barrens","gann stonespire","nitroglycerin","revenge of gann","sodium nitrate","wood pulp"},rel={"quest:846","item:nitroglycerin","item:sodium-nitrate","npc:gann-stonespire","subzone:bael-modan","quest:843","zone:barrens"},src={"Wood Pulp","Revenge of Gann"}}
E["item:zargh-s-meats"] = {t="item",n="Zargh's Meats",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Zargh prepares fresh meat for Gryshka in Orgrimmar. The parcel gives young Horde travelers a reason to learn the wind rider route.",h="At the Crossroads, Zargh prepares fresh meat for Gryshka in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Courier's Cargo",b="Zargh, an orc butcher and hunter at the Crossroads in the Barrens, prepares fresh cuts for Gryshka, the innkeeper in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. The heat across the savannas can spoil fresh game quickly, so the parcel goes with couriers bound for the Crossroads roost. Wind Rider Master Devrak arranges a wyvern flight to Orgrimmar's Skytower, sparing travelers the long overland journey through Durotar.",sp=0},{t="A Way to the Heart",b="Zargh's delivery carries a personal sentiment along with its provisions. When Gryshka receives the meat, she recognizes Zargh's knack for winning a lady's favor with quality game. She is eager to prepare the cuts for the inn's patrons and guests. For newly arrived orc and troll travelers, the delivery offers an introduction to long-distance flight between Kalimdor's Horde settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who prepared Zargh's Meats?",a="Zargh, an orc butcher and hunter at the Crossroads in the Barrens, prepares and packs the meat.",al={"who made zarghs meats","who is zargh","where does the meat come from"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the recipient of the meats?",a="Gryshka, the innkeeper in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, receives the cuts.",al={"who gets the meat","who is gryshka","where do i deliver zarghs meats"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why must the meat be taken by wind rider?",a="Fresh meat spoils quickly in the heat of the Barrens and Durotar. Zargh sends couriers to Devrak at the Crossroads roost, where a wyvern can carry the parcel to Orgrimmar before it spoils.",al={"why fly the meat","devrak wind rider meat"}},{q="Why can only certain races deliver this package?",a="Orc and troll travelers carry Zargh's parcel to Orgrimmar. Tauren adventurers carry animal hides to Thunder Bluff, while Forsaken couriers take supplies back to the Sepulcher.",al={"why cant tauren get this quest","undead zarghs meats","who can deliver zarghs meats"},gp=true},{q="What is Zargh's Meats?",a="Zargh's Meats is a parcel of choice raw cuts bundled up in the Crossroads. Rather than ordinary butcher scraps, these fine cuts are sent as a gift to Gryshka, the innkeeper of Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength.",al={"what is zarghs meats","zarghs meats item","zargh meat parcel"},it="identity",add="a104b0f9"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, carrying Zargh's cuts to Gryshka introduces you to the Valley of Strength, the heart of your capital, and to the need for aerial travel by wyvern.",["profession:Cooking"]="Gryshka values these fresh cuts. They show the orcish preference for rare meat, lightly cooked and taken straight from the wild beasts of the Barrens."},kw={"crossroads","devrak","gryshka","meats","orgrimmar","valley of strength","wind rider","zargh"},rel={"quest:6365","quest:6384","npc:zargh","npc:devrak","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-strength","zone:barrens"},src={"Zargh's Meats","Meats to Orgrimmar (Classic)","Ride to Orgrimmar (Classic)"}}
E["item:zhevra-hooves"] = {t="item",n="Zhevra Hooves",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, zhevras graze in the open savannah. Their hooves prove a hunter can face swift, powerful prey.",h="Across the Barrens, zhevras graze in the open savannah.",sec={{t="Trophies of the Hunt",b="Zhevras graze across the Barrens, but their compact, muscular legs can strike hard. Sergra Darkthorn, the orc shaman in charge of the Crossroads, sends aspiring Horde scouts to gather hooves from zhevra runners. The hunt sharpens a fledgling hunter's instincts and resilience. A panicked runner can kick even a sturdy tauren flat. Intact hooves show a hunter can handle swift, kicking quarry before taking on Kalimdor's deadliest predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants Zhevra Hooves?",a="Sergra Darkthorn, an orc shaman at the Crossroads in the Barrens, asks hunters to bring her four Zhevra Hooves to prove they are ready for tougher game.",al={"who needs hooves","who takes zhevra hooves","sergra hooves"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do Zhevra Hooves come from?",a="Zhevra Hooves come from zhevra runners grazing across the open savannah north and south of the Crossroads.",al={"where to get hooves","zhevra runner location","find zhevra"},it="origin"},{q="Why are zhevra dangerous to hunt?",a="Zhevras can strike with great force using their hind legs. A sprinting zhevra can kick an adult tauren off their feet, though zhevras are less aggressive than raptors or prowlers.",al={"are zhevras strong","zhevra kick strength","zhevra danger"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Sergra have hunters track zhevra rather than fiercer beasts?",a="Sergra sees zhevras as a step up from plainstriders. They give newcomers firm but safe practice before they face truly lethal creatures.",al={"why hunt zhevra","sergra training purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What are Zhevra Hooves?",a="Zhevra hooves are the sturdy, solid footings taken from the striped wild equines that gallop across the savannas of the Barrens. They pack tremendous power—enough in a single kick to stagger a full-grown tauren—and serve as physical proof of a hunter's growing skill and endurance under the harsh sun.",al={"what is zhevra hooves","zhevra hooves","about zhevra hooves"},it="identity",add="51f26e7e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a new Horde recruit arriving in the Barrens, you can prove your fitness to defend the Crossroads by harvesting hooves for Sergra Darkthorn.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking zhevras across the savannah teaches you to handle swift herd animals that can turn and strike with powerful kicks."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","darkthorn","hooves","hunt","runner","sergra","zhevra"},rel={"quest:845","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","quest:860","topic:tauren"},src={"Zhevra Hooves","The Zhevra (Classic)"}}
E["npc:apothecary-helbrim"] = {t="npc",n="Apothecary Helbrim",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Apothecary Helbrim studies the Barrens for the Royal Apothecary Society. Sent to Kalimdor, he gathers unfamiliar reagents for the Forsaken.",h="At the Crossroads, Apothecary Helbrim studies the Barrens for the Royal Apothecary Society.",sec={{t="Apothecary in the Dust",b="Apothecary Helbrim works beneath the harsh sun at the Crossroads, far from the Royal Apothecary Society's quarters in the damp undercity of Undercity. Sent across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, he searches the Barrens for useful plants, fungi, and other natural specimens. He depends on travelers to bring him samples, including local fungal spores, and works with Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff. Through Helbrim, the Forsaken's alchemists reach beyond the ruined borders of Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Helbrim?",a="Helbrim is a Forsaken alchemist and agent of the Royal Apothecary Society. He is stationed at the Crossroads to gather and study natural reagents from across the Barrens.",al={"who is helbrim","helbrim lore","crossroads apothecary"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a Forsaken apothecary stationed in the Barrens?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks new compounds, toxins, and reagents for its research. Helbrim was sent to central Kalimdor to study local specimens, including fungal spores unlike those found in the plague-scarred lands of Lordaeron.",al={"why is he at crossroads","what is helbrim doing here","why forsaken in barrens"},it="why_here"},{q="What does he do with the fungal spores players bring him?",a="Helbrim studies the fungal spores for their toxicity, medicinal value, and other properties. He packages samples for couriers to carry to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff for further experiments.",al={"fungal spores helbrim","what are spores for","fungal spore quest"},it="wants"},{q="Who does Helbrim work with?",a="Helbrim answers to the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity. In Kalimdor, he works with Apothecary Zamah at the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff and sometimes does business through goblin intermediaries such as Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.",al={"helbrim allies","who does helbrim answer to"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Apothecary Helbrim on?",a="Helbrim is a member of the Forsaken and answers directly to the Royal Apothecary Society of the Undercity. As part of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's people, he stands with the Horde, though the Society often pursues its own secretive alchemical agendas even while operating in allied territories like the Barrens.",al={"helbrim faction","who does helbrim serve","is helbrim horde"},it="side",add="d7b2fd88"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, you can see how your people contribute to the Horde in Kalimdor: Helbrim turns the wilderness into material for the Society's research.",["faction:Horde"]="Helbrim works near orcish guards and tauren wayfarers, but his drive to gather spores and toxins leaves even his allies uneasy."},kw={"apothecary","barrens","crossroads","fungal spores","helbrim","royal apothecary society","zamah"},rel={"topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:848","quest:853","quest:1358","quest:1492","topic:forsaken"},src={"Apothecary Helbrim"}}
E["npc:apothecary-zinge"] = {t="npc",n="Apothecary Zinge",z="barrens",s="Beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, Apothecary Zinge works for the Forsaken. She studies biological specimens and arranges research shipments across Horde lands.",h="Beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, Apothecary Zinge works for the Forsaken.",sec={{t="In Service to the Society",b="Apothecary Zinge works in the Apothecarium beneath the Undercity. Under Master Apothecary Faranell, she searches for chemical and biological compounds that can advance the Forsaken's aims. Her work connects her with field researchers and scouts far beyond Tirisfal Glades, including at distant outposts in Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Cross-Continental Experiments",b="Apothecary Zinge depends on couriers and adventurers to carry test materials across the sea. She regularly writes to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads in the Barrens. She sends him toxic wolf heart samples from Silverpine Forest so he can study how Lordaeron's toxins affect Kalimdor's beasts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Apothecary Zinge be found?",a="Apothecary Zinge works in the Apothecarium, the alchemical quarter on the southeastern tier of the Undercity.",al={"zinge location","where is apothecary zinge","apothecary zinge spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What organization does she belong to?",a="Apothecary Zinge belongs to the Royal Apothecary Society, a company of Forsaken alchemists who create concoctions, plagues, and antidotes in service to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"zinge faction","who does zinge work for"},it="ties"},{q="Why does she need samples from the Barrens?",a="The samples go from Silverpine Forest to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads. Zinge has adventurers carry toxic wolf hearts to her colleague, who studies how Lordaeron's toxins affect Kalimdor's beasts.",al={"why barrens samples","helbrim sample","zinge barrens delivery"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Apothecary Zinge?",a="Apothecary Zinge is a Forsaken alchemist and an active member of the Royal Apothecary Society based in the Undercity. Dedicated to advancing the research and concoctions of her order, she coordinates field research, sends toxin samples to colleagues in distant lands like the Barrens, and maintains close ties with friends such as Fenstad Argyle.",al={"who is zinge","apothecary zinge lore","who is apothecary zinge"},it="identity",add="55fc7dbb"},{q="Whose side is Apothecary Zinge on?",a="Zinge serves the Forsaken and the Royal Apothecary Society, aligning herself directly with Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and by extension the Horde. Her loyalties lie firmly with the research efforts of the Undercity, aiding any Horde adventurers willing to assist her experiments.",al={"zinge faction","who does zinge serve","apothecary zinge loyalty"},it="side",add="b56b8970"},{q="Why is Apothecary Zinge involved in the Barrens?",a="While Zinge herself remains stationed in the Apothecarium within the Undercity, she has couriers carry toxic wolf heart samples from Silverpine Forest to her colleague Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads, who is studying how Lordaeron's toxins affect the beasts of Kalimdor.",al={"why is zinge interested in barrens","zinge barrens connection","why send for barrens samples"},it="why_here",add="d8143764"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see researchers like Zinge at the forefront of your people's scientific independence. They work tirelessly on solutions meant to secure the Forsaken's survival and supremacy.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you rely on open supply routes and trusted runners crossing the sea between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms to keep your front lines supplied."},kw={"apothecarium","apothecary zinge","crossroads","helbrim","royal apothecary society","samples","undercity","zinge"},rel={"subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:1358","quest:1359","zone:barrens","topic:forsaken","npc:master-apothecary-faranell"},src={"Apothecary Zinge"}}
E["npc:brewmaster-drohn"] = {t="npc",n="Brewmaster Drohn",z="barrens",s="Above Ratchet's docks, Brewmaster Drohn tends his brewing craft. The orc lives just uphill from the port, making potent drinks with methods tied to the wandering pandaren Chen Stormstout. Travelers who find discarded kegs across Kalimdor are sent to Drohn's porch.",h="Above Ratchet's docks, Brewmaster Drohn tends his brewing craft.",sec={{t="A Master of the Craft in Ratchet",b="Brewmaster Drohn brews from his home on the hill above Ratchet's goblin docks. Rather than devote himself to combat, the orc has given his craft to brewing. He lives peacefully in the neutral haven established by Gazlowe's Steamwheedle cartel. While many orcs favor coarse grog or simple spirits, Drohn works with rare ingredients, carefully balanced flavors, and methods seldom practiced among his kin.",sp=0},{t="The Pandaren Connection",b="Brewmaster Drohn learned brewing through a mentor who studied under Chen Stormstout, the pandaren wanderer who fought beside Rexxar and the Horde during the founding of Durotar. Chen also taught Drohn to make Trogg Ale. When travelers find Chen's discarded kegs in the wilds, Drohn is the only local authority who can identify their ingredients and recreate the wanderer's potent brews.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brewmaster Drohn?",a="Brewmaster Drohn brews in Ratchet, in the Barrens. The orc is known for exotic ales and ties to the brewing traditions of the wandering pandaren Chen Stormstout.",al={"drohn lore","who is drohn","ratchet brewmaster"},it="identity"},{q="How does Drohn know Chen Stormstout?",a="Drohn learned from a mentor who was taught to brew Stormstout by Chen Stormstout. Chen later taught Drohn how to make Trogg Ale.",al={"chen connection","how does he know chen","drohn and chen"},it="ties"},{q="What should I do if I find Chen's Empty Keg?",a="Take Chen's Empty Keg to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet. He recognizes Chen's handiwork and sends you to find the rare local ingredients needed to recreate the brew.",al={"chens empty keg","found empty keg","keg quest"},gp=true},{q="Is Brewmaster Drohn aligned with the Horde?",a="Yes. Drohn is an orc of the Horde, though he lives and brews in Ratchet, a neutral goblin port. Attacking him harms an Alliance adventurer's standing with Ratchet and the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"is drohn horde","is drohn neutral","drohn faction"},it="side"},{q="What kind of drinks does Drohn make?",a="Drohn makes potent brews, including Trogg Ale and Chen Stormstout's namesake Stormstout. They call for tusks, glands, and other parts from beasts found across the Barrens.",al={"drohn recipes","drohns distillery brews"}},{q="Where exactly is Drohn located?",a="Find Drohn outside his house on the hill overlooking Ratchet, just northwest of the main docks in the Barrens.",al={"drohn location","where is drohn","find brewmaster drohn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Brewmaster Drohn want?",a="Drohn is dedicated to mastering his craft and perfecting exotic, potent recipes. When travelers come across empty kegs left behind by the wandering pandaren Chen Stormstout, Drohn seeks rare ingredients across the Barrens—such as savannah lion tusks, plainstrider kidneys, and a thunder lizard horn—to recreate the legendary brews and honor the brewing traditions passed down to him.",al={"what does drohn want","drohn goals","why help drohn"},it="wants",add="2bb5b883"},{q="Why is Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet?",a="Drohn operates his distillery on the outskirts of Ratchet, taking full advantage of the bustling goblin port. The town's neutrality and bustling trade bring travelers, exotic supplies, and curious patrons from across Azeroth right to his doorstep, providing both an eager market for his ale and access to the Barrens' wilderness for brewing ingredients.",al={"why is drohn here","why is drohn in ratchet","drohn location reason"},it="why_here",add="e385fb6c"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="If you practice cooking, Drohn's skill lies in blending rare flora and fauna into fine drinks in the desert.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may see Drohn's brewing as one way to turn the peace of Durotar and the Barrens into a craft, unlike the fortresses many warriors built after following Thrall to Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, know that Steamwheedle protects Drohn in Ratchet. Attack him, and the local goblin authorities will turn against you."},kw={"barrens","brewmaster","chen stormstout","drohn","ratchet","trogg ale"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","quest:819","zone:barrens","topic:trogg","topic:alliance"},src={"Brewmaster Drohn"}}
E["npc:brine"] = {t="npc",n="Brine",z="barrens",s="On Blackthorn Ridge, Brine guides shaman initiates toward the spirits of water. This orc shaman teaches them to commune with the tides and earn their Water Totem.",h="On Blackthorn Ridge, Brine guides shaman initiates toward the spirits of water.",sec={{t="Hermit of the Ridge",b="Brine lives on a hill in northern Blackthorn Ridge, far from the Barrens' trading posts. Though dry savannas surround her, she has devoted her life to understanding water. Shaman across the Horde seek her wisdom after mastering earth and fire. She teaches that water calls for patience and perspective, qualities few understand as deeply as she does.",sp=0},{t="Memories of the Eastern Kingdoms",b="In her youth, Brine marched with her orc companions across the Hillsbrad Foothills and fought against human settlements. During the campaign, she came to Tarren Mill and found a humble well fed by fresh spring water. The well stayed in her memory as a sign of life amid devastation. It strengthened a lesson she had learned as a child: even in the darkest sorrow, a small token of hope can still be found.",sp=0},{t="The Call of Water",b="Brine tests aspiring shaman with pilgrimages to gather pure droplets from varied sources. Her trials teach that water can be gentle yet unyielding. In her rituals, shaman commune with the elemental spirits and bind water's restorative essence to their totemic focus.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Brine?",a="Brine is an experienced orc shaman who lives alone on a hill in northern Blackthorn Ridge, in the southern Barrens. She guides initiates seeking communion with water spirits.",al={"brine lore","who is brine","orc on blackthorn ridge"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a water shaman living in a desert?",a="The Barrens are dry, but Brine's solitude lets her commune deeply with the elements, away from the noise of settlements.",al={"why in the barrens","why does brine live in the desert"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Brine's connection to Tarren Mill?",a="Years ago, Brine fought alongside Horde warriors in the Hillsbrad Foothills and entered Tarren Mill. There she found a small well of pure spring water, a lasting sign of life and hope amid the ruin of war.",al={"tarren mill well","brine hillsbrad","brine backstory"},it="history"},{q="What role does Brine play in shaman training?",a="Brine guides initiates through stages of the Call of Water trials. She sends them to gather pure water from varied sources and teaches them humility and resilience before they gain the insight needed for their Water Totem.",al={"brine shaman quest","how to get water totem","call of water brine"},it="purpose"},{q="Where exactly is Brine located?",a="Brine lives atop a high bluff in northern Blackthorn Ridge, in the southern Barrens, just north of Razorfen Kraul.",al={"brine location","where is brine","find brine barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What philosophy guides her teachings?",a="Brine teaches that even in pain and sorrow, hope and renewal can be found. Water represents life and perseverance through harsh trials.",al={"brine philosophy","lessons of water"}},{q="Whose side is Brine on?",a="Brine is loyal to the Horde, sharing her deep spiritual wisdom with budding Horde shamans seeking mastery over the elements. Though she dwells in isolation among the hills of the southern Barrens rather than within a bustling fortress, she acts as a vital mentor for the shamanic traditions nurtured by Thrall's new realm.",al={"brine faction","is brine horde","who does brine serve"},it="side",add="452ad9e3"},{q="What does Brine want?",a="Brine seeks to guide aspiring shamans toward understanding the dual nature of water—both its serene, life-giving clarity and its furious, unyielding power. Rather than simply handing down power, she expects travelers to undertake rigorous pilgrimages to pure water sources across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms to learn resilience and communion with the elemental spirits.",al={"brine goal","what is brine doing","why help shamans"},it="wants",add="a90c6b58"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Brine guides you through trials of endurance and spirit before you can commune with water and claim your Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="A veteran of the wars in Hillsbrad, Brine serves the Horde by passing the spiritual heritage of the elements to new generations."},kw={"barrens","blackthorn ridge","brine","call of water","shaman","tarren mill","water totem"},rel={"quest:63","subzone:blackthorn-ridge","zone:barrens","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Brine"}}
E["npc:captain-shatterskull"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Shatterskull",z="barrens",s="At Mor'shan Base Camp, Captain Shatterskull commands the Horde's northern border defense. A seasoned orc commander, he coordinates efforts to repel night elf forces contesting the border near Warsong Gulch.",h="At Mor'shan Base Camp, Captain Shatterskull commands the Horde's northern border defense.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Northern Border",b="At Mor'shan Base Camp, Captain Shatterskull guards the Horde's foothold at the edge of Ashenvale. He works beside fellow officers such as Kadrak against night elf sentinels and Silverwing forces seeking to reclaim the borderlands. The struggle over Ashenvale's timber and ancient lands keeps the Barrens frontier under constant threat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Shatterskull?",a="Captain Shatterskull is a seasoned orc commander at Mor'shan Base Camp, overseeing the Horde's defense against night elf forces.",al={"shatterskull identity","who is captain shatterskull","shatterskull npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Captain Shatterskull be found?",a="You can find Captain Shatterskull at Mor'shan Base Camp on the northern edge of the Barrens, before Ashenvale.",al={"shatterskull location","where is captain shatterskull","morshan camp shatterskull"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his role at Mor'shan Base Camp?",a="At Mor'shan Base Camp, Captain Shatterskull commands the defense of the Horde's northern frontier and rallies warriors against the Alliance's Silverwing Sentinels.",al={"what does shatterskull do","shatterskull purpose","mor'shan commander"},it="purpose"},{q="Who does Captain Shatterskull work with?",a="Captain Shatterskull works alongside frontline officers such as Kadrak, coordinating defense and recruitment for border skirmishes.",al={"shatterskull allies","kadrak and shatterskull"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Captain Shatterskull on?",a="Captain Shatterskull serves the Horde with fierce loyalty. Stationed at Mor'shan Base Camp on the tense frontier between the Barrens and Ashenvale, he stands as a bulwark against the night elves and the Alliance, organizing forces to defend Horde interests in the region.",al={"captain shatterskull faction","who does shatterskull serve","shatterskull horde or alliance"},it="side",add="4e979652"},{q="What does Captain Shatterskull want?",a="Shatterskull seeks total control over the disputed northern border. He directs Horde champions to quell the Silverwing Sentinels encroaching from Ashenvale, demanding military sacrifice and honors of war to ensure the Mor'shan ramparts remain impenetrable to their enemies.",al={"captain shatterskull goals","what does shatterskull need","why does shatterskull want silverwing dead"},it="wants",add="3a9b17d5"},{q="Why is Captain Shatterskull here?",a="He is stationed at the Mor'shan Base Camp to oversee the Horde's front-line defenses against the night elves. Because the border with Ashenvale is an active flashpoint for territorial skirmishes, Shatterskull was assigned here to coordinate reinforcements and drive back Alliance incursions.",al={"why is shatterskull at morshan","captain shatterskull post","why is captain shatterskull in the barrens"},it="why_here",add="0393c0a4"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde warriors arriving from the southern Barrens, Captain Shatterskull guards the northern frontier against night elf incursions from Ashenvale.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Captain Shatterskull's defense of the Horde's hard-won lands reflects the martial spirit of a people others view as invaders."},kw={"barrens","captain shatterskull","kadrak","mor'shan base camp","orc captain","shatterskull","silverwing","warsong"},rel={"npc:kadrak","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Captain Shatterskull"}}
E["npc:captain-thalo-thas-brightsun"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun",z="barrens",s="At Ratchet's docks, Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun keeps a cordial face toward Alliance travelers. The privateer serves the Steamwheedle Cartel and resents the Theramore forces at Northwatch Hold for firing on his vessels.",h="At Ratchet's docks, Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun keeps a cordial face toward Alliance travelers.",sec={{t="Privateer of Ratchet",b="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun leads the Thalo'dan Privateers from Ratchet's docks under the Steamwheedle Cartel's banner. Ratchet welcomes merchants of every flag if they bring coin, but danger shadows trade along the Barrens coast. Northwatch Hold lies just south of the port, where its heavy cannons threaten neutral sea lanes. Brightsun stays cordial toward visiting travelers, yet the garrison's attacks on his fleet have tried his patience.",sp=0},{t="A Private War with Northwatch",b="An open assault on Northwatch Hold could endanger Ratchet's neutrality, so Brightsun cannot send his fleet against the fort. He turns instead to capable Horde mercenaries to settle the score. Their strikes aim to silence the cannons and free his captured crew. By using Horde auxiliaries, Brightsun protects his shipping interests without provoking direct Alliance retaliation against the cartel or entering the conflict openly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun?",a="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun commands the Thalo'dan Privateers from Ratchet in service to the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"thalothas brightsun","who is brightsun","ratchet captain"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he angry at Northwatch Hold?",a="Northwatch Hold's Alliance forces have repeatedly fired heavy cannons at Brightsun's merchant vessels and imprisoned his sailors, disrupting trade along the coast.",al={"why attack northwatch","brightsun northwatch issue","why hate alliance"},it="wants"},{q="Why does he only hire the Horde to attack Northwatch?",a="Brightsun remains diplomatic toward Alliance travelers in Ratchet, but cannot ask Alliance loyalists to attack their own stronghold. The Horde has reason to weaken Theramore's military outpost.",al={"can alliance do his quest","why horde only","brightsun alliance quests"},it="motive"},{q="Does he belong to the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Brightsun belongs to neither faction. His allegiance lies with the Steamwheedle Cartel and his privateers, though his current grievances bring his interests in line with the Horde.",al={"brightsun faction","is brightsun horde","is brightsun neutral"},it="side"},{q="Why is Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun in Ratchet?",a="Captain Brightsun uses the neutral port of Ratchet as a safe haven and base of operations for his crew, the Thalo'dan Privateers. Operating under the shelter of the Steamwheedle Cartel allows him to trade, repair his vessels, and recruit outside muscle along the merchant sea lanes of the Barrens.",al={"why is brightsun here","why is captain thalothas in ratchet","thalothas ratchet why"},it="why_here",add="30395239"},{q="Who is Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun tied to?",a="Brightsun commands his own crew, known as the Thalo'dan Privateers, and operates in close alignment with Gazlowe's Steamwheedle Cartel in Ratchet. While he maintains neutrality toward Alliance visitors in town, his fierce maritime grudge against Northwatch Hold has led him to seek assistance from Horde fighters.",al={"brightsun affiliations","who does thalothas work for","thalothas brightsun allies"},it="ties",add="8eff1400"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Brightsun gives the Horde a reason to strike Northwatch Hold and cripple Alliance naval artillery along central Kalimdor's coast.",["faction:Alliance"]="Brightsun speaks cordially with you in port, but Northwatch Hold's Theramore forces have driven him to conspire in secret with your enemies."},kw={"barrens","brightsun","northwatch hold","ratchet","steamwheedle cartel","thalo'dan privateers","thalo'thas brightsun"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","quest:891","quest:898","topic:steamwheedle-cartel","zone:barrens","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun"}}
E["npc:darsok-swiftdagger"] = {t="npc",n="Darsok Swiftdagger",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger watches the northern trails for threats. The orc scout directs Horde fighters against Witchwing harpies in the Dry Hills, whose raids endanger travelers and settlements. He is also an old friend of Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in Malaka'jin.",h="At the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger watches the northern trails for threats.",sec={{t="A Watcher at the Crossroads",b="Darsok Swiftdagger watches the northern scrubland from the Crossroads. The roads linking Durotar, Mulgore, and the Barrens’ northern reaches face raiders and centaur, as well as organized hunters from the sky. Darsok’s anger falls on the Witchwing harpies. Their roosts lie in the Dry Hills, northwest of the Forgotten Pools, where they threaten caravans traveling north.",sp=0},{t="The War on the Witchwing",b="Darsok directs strikes into Witchwing territory, beginning with the Harpy Raiders. He then sends seasoned fighters after the harpies’ lieutenants and, at last, their matriarch, Serena Bloodfeather. By breaking their command in stages, he seeks to leave the flock scattered across the crags.",sp=1},{t="Connections in the Scrub",b="Darsok has an old friend far northwest of the Barrens: Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, a troll who lives at Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, the land the harpies come from. Darsok sends Jin'Zil a letter with news of the harpy campaign. The two friends have not been in touch for many years.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Darsok Swiftdagger located?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger is stationed at the Crossroads, the central Horde settlement in the Barrens. He directs travelers toward threats in the north.",al={"darsok location","where is darsok swiftdagger","find darsok","darsok swiftdagger spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Darsok hunting harpies?",a="Witchwing harpies roost in canyons northwest of the Forgotten Pools and threaten Horde caravans, travelers, and scouts on the Barrens’ northern trails.",al={"why kill harpies","darsok harpy grudge","witchwing harpies barrens"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Serena Bloodfeather?",a="Serena Bloodfeather leads the Witchwing harpies of the Dry Hills. Darsok sends fighters to kill her and break the flock’s command.",al={"serena bloodfeather","harpy leader barrens","witchwing leader"},it="target"},{q="What is Darsok's connection to Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, a troll living at Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, is Darsok's old friend. Darsok sends a traveler to Jin'Zil with a letter about the harpy campaign, his first word to him in many years.",al={"jin'zil letter","darsok and jin'zil","witch doctor jin'zil connection"},it="ties"},{q="Does Darsok report to Sergra Darkthorn or Thork?",a="Darsok organizes his harpy campaign from the Crossroads. No Classic source identifies Sergra Darkthorn or Thork as his direct superior.",al={"darsok thork","who does darsok answer to","crossroads leadership"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where do the Witchwing harpies nest?",a="The Witchwing harpies roost in the Dry Hills, jagged ravines and cliffs northwest of the Forgotten Pools in the Barrens’ north.",al={"witchwing location","dry hills harpies","where to find harpies barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Darsok Swiftdagger?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger is an orc scout and warrior of the Horde stationed at the Crossroads. Dedicated to securing the Barrens against local threats, he has earned a fearsome reputation specifically for his relentless campaign against the Witchwing harpies infesting the region.",al={"who is darsok","darsok swiftdagger who","about darsok"},it="identity",add="c43e4047"},{q="Whose side is Darsok Swiftdagger on?",a="Darsok stands firmly with the Horde. Operating out of the Crossroads, he serves the defense of Kalimdor and aids the settlement by neutralizing threats that prey upon travelers and trade caravans.",al={"darsok faction","is darsok horde","darsok allegiance"},it="side",add="cbab4453"},{q="What does Darsok Swiftdagger want?",a="Darsok wants nothing less than the eradication of the Witchwing threat in the northern Barrens. He enlists capable adventurers to cull the flock's raiders, eliminate their field lieutenants, and ultimately slay their vicious matriarch, Serena Bloodfeather.",al={"darsok goal","what does darsok want","darsok harpies why"},it="wants",add="bc228dd6"},{q="Why is Darsok Swiftdagger here?",a="Stationed at the Crossroads, Darsok serves as a vital vanguard against the dangers menacing the northern trade routes. He remains posted here to monitor the aggression of the nearby harpies and organize military efforts to drive them back from Horde lands.",al={"why is darsok in crossroads","darsok crossroads reason","why is darsok here"},it="why_here",add="aac9a722"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you can rely on Darsok’s early, tactical missions to help secure the crossroads trade routes against attacks from above.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Darsok’s focused martial approach to securing Kalimdor’s dangerous frontier.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can recognize Darsok’s preference for precise, lethal strikes against enemy leaders, aimed at taking their heads."},kw={"barrens","bloodfeather","crossroads","darsok","harpy","jin'zil","serena","swiftdagger","thork","witchwing"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","quest:876","quest:875","quest:867","npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","npc:thork","subzone:forgotten-pools","zone:barrens"},src={"Darsok Swiftdagger"}}
E["npc:devrak"] = {t="npc",n="Devrak",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Devrak keeps the Horde’s wind riders ready for the roads across Kalimdor. The orc flight master carries couriers and supplies between Durotar, Mulgore, frontier outposts, and the Horde’s capitals.",h="At the Crossroads, Devrak keeps the Horde’s wind riders ready for the roads across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Crossroads Roosts",b="At the Crossroads, Devrak tends the wind riders that link the Horde’s far-flung holdings. The outpost stands where Kalimdor’s major trade routes meet, exposed beneath the sun and vulnerable to quilboar, centaur, and Alliance scouts. Quick flights matter here. Devrak pairs seasoned travelers and new messengers with trained wind riders that cross the savannah and reach Mulgore’s mountains or Durotar’s stone canyons.",sp=0},{t="Supplies for the Warchief and the Chieftain",b="Devrak also helps move supplies from the frontier. Barrens hunters bring in meat and pelts, and he helps send them to Orgrimmar’s cooking fires and Thunder Bluff’s tanners. He introduces new couriers to flight masters across the continents, keeping an aerial route open to the Horde’s heartlands.",sp=0},{t="A Deadly Roost",b="Devrak tends more than beasts at the Crossroads. When the settlement comes under attack, he calls enraged wyverns to strike intruders with venomous stingers and talons. His roost is a dangerous target for anyone who attacks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Devrak's role at the Crossroads?",a="Devrak is the Horde flight master at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He tends the outpost’s wind riders, grants flight paths to connected settlements across Kalimdor, and coordinates the transport of couriers, soldiers, and trade goods.",al={"who is devrak","what does devrak do","devrak job","crossroads flight master"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Devrak fly me?",a="From the Crossroads, Devrak connects you to capitals such as Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff, and to frontier outposts in Ashenvale, Stonetalon Mountains, Dustwallow Marsh, Thousand Needles, and the southern frontiers. You must have spoken to those flight masters first.",al={"devrak flight paths","where can i fly from crossroads","crossroads flight routes"},gp=true},{q="What quests does Devrak offer?",a="Devrak helps young Horde adventurers learn the flight network by sending them with fresh meat to Gryshka in Orgrimmar and bundles of hides to Thunder Bluff.",al={"devrak quests","crossroads flight quest"},gp=true},{q="How does Devrak defend himself if the Crossroads is attacked?",a="If Alliance raiders or hostile beasts attack the Crossroads, Devrak can call enraged wyverns to aid him. The creatures drive attackers off with tooth and talon.",al={"can devrak fight","killing devrak","devrak defense"},gp=true},{q="Why is having a flight master at the Crossroads so critical?",a="The Barrens is central Kalimdor’s connective spine. With the Crossroads linking Durotar, Mulgore, Ashenvale, and Stonetalon, Devrak’s roost lets the Horde move forces quickly and coordinate supplies without days of travel on foot.",al={"why is crossroads flight master important","crossroads location significance"},it="why_here"},{q="What creatures does Devrak handle?",a="Devrak handles wind riders, also called wyverns. These winged, draconic predators of Kalimdor’s peaks and mesas were befriended by the Horde as reliable flying mounts across rough terrain.",al={"what mounts does devrak have","crossroads mounts"}},{q="Whose side is Devrak on?",a="Devrak is a proud member of the Horde. Stationed in the heart of Kalimdor at the Crossroads, he serves the warchief by keeping the vital aerial supply routes open between orcish and tauren territories, transporting couriers, supplies, and warriors throughout the Barrens and beyond.",al={"is devrak horde","devrak faction","who does devrak serve"},it="side",add="a0427f27"},{q="What does Devrak want?",a="Devrak is focused on maintaining the Horde's vital supply lines across central Kalimdor. He relies on travelers to deliver essential goods—such as cured hides and preserved meats—to major capitals like Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff, ensuring the settlement's wind riders remain primed and the war effort well-supported.",al={"what is devrak's goal","devrak objective","what does devrak need"},it="wants",add="bd507e24"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde adventurers navigating Kalimdor, Devrak is an indispensable ally and a central link between the orcs, trolls, and tauren territories.",["race:Orc"]="In the dry heart of the Barrens, Devrak shows an orc’s talent for working with Kalimdor’s wind riders, bonding with the fierce beasts to secure aerial dominance."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","flight master","orgrimmar","thunder bluff","wind rider","wyvern"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:6365","quest:6384","quest:6361","quest:6362","zone:orgrimmar","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Devrak"}}
E["npc:doan-karhan"] = {t="npc",n="Doan Karhan",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Doan Karhan studies the Burning Legion’s demonic artifacts. A human scholar and practitioner of the dark arts, he lives alone to pursue his research, especially into the enigmatic Orb of Soran'ruk.",h="In the southern Barrens, Doan Karhan studies the Burning Legion’s demonic artifacts.",sec={{t="The Hermit of the Barrens",b="Doan Karhan keeps a solitary camp in the southern Barrens, far from the Alliance’s civilized bastions. He withdrew into the wilderness to study dangerous demonic relics without disturbance. He knows much about powerful fel vessels, possesses the Orb of Zargain, and is absorbed by the legendary Orb of Soran'ruk. Warlocks seeking knowledge of artifact crafting and dark rituals often come to him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Doan Karhan located?",a="Doan Karhan camps in the southern Barrens, east of Camp Taurajo and the main road. He lives alone in a small clearing that is easy to overlook.",al={"doan karhan location","where is doan karhan","doan karhan southern barrens"}},{q="Why is a human living alone in the Barrens?",a="Doan Karhan chose exile in the hostile wilderness to research the Burning Legion's magical relics. Civil Alliance lands forbid or closely scrutinize such studies of demonic orbs.",al={"why is doan here","why is there a human in barrens","doan karhan lore"}},{q="What is the Orb of Soran'ruk?",a="The Orb of Soran'ruk is an ancient, potent Legion relic imbued with dark power. Doan Karhan knows much about its construction and the similar Orb of Zargain, and guides warlocks seeking to reconstruct it.",al={"soranruk orb","orb of soran'ruk","what is orb of soran'ruk"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a seasoned warlock, you can turn to Doan Karhan for arcane knowledge to uncover, mend, and wield legendary demonic orbs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though Doan Karhan is human, he lives far from Stormwind or Theramore, choosing lonely exile in Kalimdor's heartland over the constraints of the Grand Alliance."},kw={"barrens","doan karhan","orb of soran'ruk","orb of zargain","warlock"},rel={"quest:1740","zone:barrens","topic:burning-legion","topic:alliance"},src={"Doan Karhan"}}
E["npc:feegly-the-exiled"] = {t="npc",n="Feegly the Exiled",z="barrens",s="Near the Bael Modan excavation in the southern Barrens, Feegly the Exiled lurks alone. Once praised as one of the expedition’s finest diggers, he was driven off by General Twinbraid after claiming an uncovered relic’s power as his own.",h="Near the Bael Modan excavation in the southern Barrens, Feegly the Exiled lurks alone.",sec={{t="A Digger's Ruin",b="Feegly the Exiled once ranked among Bael Modan’s finest diggers. The Tear of the Moons was the first great discovery at the site, and Feegly claimed its power for himself. General Twinbraid called the gem cursed, locked it away in Bael'dun Keep and drove Feegly off. Now Feegly broods alone, desperate to reclaim the gem that dooms him. When he finally holds it again, the Tear shatters, and Feegly twists into a hideous, hunched trogg.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Feegly the Exiled?",a="Feegly is an exiled dwarf excavator from the Bael Modan dig, where he covets the Tear of the Moons.",al={"who is feegly","feegly lore","feegly the exiled"},it="origin"},{q="Why was Feegly exiled from Bael Modan?",a="Feegly grew obsessed with the Tear of the Moons, the first great discovery at Bael Modan. General Twinbraid called the gem cursed, locked it away in Bael'dun Keep and drove Feegly off.",al={"why exiled","what did feegly do","feegly banishment"},it="history"},{q="Why is Feegly willing to talk to Horde adventurers?",a="Betrayed and cast out by his fellow dwarves, Feegly has no loyalty to the Alliance expedition. Desperate to retrieve the relic he covets, he seeks aid from Horde travelers.",al={"why is feegly friendly to horde","feegly horde friendly"},it="side"},{q="What is the Tear of the Moons?",a="The Tear of the Moons is a gem uncovered by the excavators at Bael Modan, their first great discovery there. Feegly claims it gave him power, but General Twinbraid deemed it cursed and locked it away in Bael'dun Keep.",al={"tear of the moons","feegly gem","feegly artifact"},it="item"},{q="Who is Feegly the Exiled?",a="Feegly is an exiled dwarven digger from the Bael Modan excavation in the southern Barrens. He lingers outside the dig, obsessed with recovering a relic known as the Tear of the Moons.",al={"who is feegly","feegly identity","feegly lore"},it="identity",add="21513985"},{q="What does Feegly the Exiled want?",a="Feegly seeks the Tear of the Moons, a relic he covets for its strange power. He recruits willing wanderers to retrieve it from Bael'dun Keep so he can possess it once again.",al={"what does feegly want","feegly motive","why does feegly need the tear"},it="wants",add="ed9ce58e"},{q="Why is Feegly the Exiled out in the Barrens?",a="Feegly lingers in the hills outside Bael Modan because General Twinbraid drove him out and locked away the Tear of the Moons. Desperate to recover the gem, he remains near his former excavation.",al={"why is feegly here","where does feegly stay","why is feegly outside bael modan"},it="why_here",add="7eaaafaa"},{q="Who is Feegly the Exiled tied to?",a="Feegly is tied to the dwarven expedition of Bael Modan, where he was formerly one of their foremost diggers before being banished. Now estranged from his kin, he relies on passing Horde wanderers to do his bidding against the excavation.",al={"feegly ties","who does feegly work with","feegly connections"},it="ties",add="0b854105"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Feegly is a tragic and terrifying warning: an accomplished digger whose obsession with an unearthed relic cost him his place among his kin.",["faction:Horde"]="Feegly’s bitter grudge against the Bael Modan excavators makes him an unexpected ally for Horde wanderers seeking to sabotage the dwarven expedition in the Barrens."},kw={"bael modan","barrens","digger","excavation","exiled","feegly","tear of the moons","trogg"},rel={"subzone:bael-modan","quest:857","zone:barrens","topic:dwarf","topic:trogg","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Feegly the Exiled"}}
E["npc:gann-stonespire"] = {t="npc",n="Gann Stonespire",z="barrens",s="Along the southern Barrens road near Bael Modan, Gann Stonespire seeks retaliation for his people’s displacement. The tauren nomad’s tribe hunted on land now occupied by a dwarven excavation.",h="Along the southern Barrens road near Bael Modan, Gann Stonespire seeks retaliation for his people’s...",sec={{t="Displaced from Bael Modan",b="Gann Stonespire camps beside the southern Barrens road after the dwarven expedition arrived from Ironforge and built Bael Modan. The surrounding land had been his tribe’s ancestral territory and hunting grounds. Dwarven miners drove the tauren from their soil with pickaxes, firearms, and heavy machinery, and refused peaceful overtures. Gann will not surrender his heritage quietly. He calls on travelers to strike back at the excavators.",sp=0},{t="Reclamation and Sabotage",b="Gann directs Horde operatives to break the dwarves’ hold over the dig site after peaceful diplomacy fails. His retaliation targets expedition leaders, including Prospector Khazgorm. He then has dwarven blasting powder and ordnance made into an explosive charge. Gann intends to detonate it beneath the dwarven flying machine, crippling their technological advantage and reclaiming honor for his displaced people.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gann Stonespire?",a="Gann Stonespire is a tauren warrior whose tribe once lived on the lands now occupied by Bael Modan. The dwarves displaced them when they established their dig site, and Gann now waits by a roadside in the southern Barrens, seeking vengeance and the reclamation of his people’s homeland.",al={"who is gann","gann stonespire lore","tauren outside bael modan"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gann fighting the dwarves of Bael Modan?",a="The Bael'dun dwarven expedition arrived in the southern Barrens and forced local tauren from their ancestral hunting grounds to build an excavation fortress. After the dwarves rejected diplomatic efforts, Gann chose to dismantle their operation by force.",al={"why does gann hate dwarves","why attack bael modan","gann bael modan conflict"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Gann's plan against the excavation?",a="Gann commissions the deaths of dwarven overseers, including Prospector Khazgorm, to seize excavation records. Then he has stolen dwarven ordnance and blasting supplies made into a bomb intended to destroy the expedition’s flying machine and disrupt its technological dominance.",al={"gann's revenge plan","what does gann do","bael modan bomb"},sp=1,it="wants"},{q="Where does Gann Stonespire make his camp?",a="Gann Stonespire wanders the road just west of Bael Modan in the southern Barrens, outside the excavation site’s perimeter.",al={"where is gann","gann stonespire location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gann Stonespire on?",a="Gann stands with the Horde and his fellow tauren. He seeks aid from Horde champions passing through the Southern Barrens to strike back against the Bael'dun dwarves encroaching on his people's sacred grounds.",al={"is gann stonespire horde","gann stonespire faction","who does gann fight for"},it="side",add="60933082"},{q="Who is Gann Stonespire tied to?",a="Gann belongs to a tauren tribe whose ancestral home spanned the lands now seized by Bael Modan. He acts on behalf of his displaced people, who were driven out when the dwarven excavation began.",al={"gann stonespire tribe","who are gann's people","gann stonespire clan"},it="ties",add="59c620b8"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share the plight of nomads whose ancestral ranges and sacred earth are repeatedly desecrated by foreign Alliance expeditions.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help Gann blunt Alliance expansionism entrenched in the southern Barrens."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun","gann stonespire","prospector khazgorm","southern barrens","stonespire"},rel={"subzone:bael-modan","quest:843","quest:846","topic:tauren","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Gann Stonespire"}}
E["npc:gazrog"] = {t="npc",n="Gazrog",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Gazrog keeps watch over the Horde’s roads and supply lines. He calls on passing Horde travelers to face threats in the Barrens and search for lost patrols.",h="At the Crossroads, Gazrog keeps watch over the Horde’s roads and supply lines.",sec={{t="A Sentinel of the Crossroads",b="Gazrog watches over the Crossroads and the roads beyond it. Marauders and beasts threaten the supplies moving through this isolated settlement, so he works with its defenders to keep cargo, coin, and couriers moving. The wilderness demands constant attention, and Gazrog depends on passing travelers to answer trouble beyond the outpost’s stockades.",sp=0},{t="Savannah Hazards",b="Gazrog’s watch extends across trails where raptors prey on travelers and quilboar clans ambush scouts. He coordinates responses to highway robberies, including the recovery of stolen Horde shipments. He also keeps track of missing soldiers, among them the grunt Dogran, who is injured and held by the quilboar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Gazrog be found?",a="Gazrog can be found at the Crossroads, where the Barrens’ northern, southern, and eastern routes meet.",al={"gazrog location","where is gazrog","gazrog crossroads"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Gazrog play for the Horde?",a="Gazrog coordinates operations and guards the Crossroads. He directs Horde travelers to protect supply lines, recover stolen shipments, and search for missing personnel.",al={"gazrog job","who is gazrog","what does gazrog do"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the stolen silver Gazrog asks about?",a="Raptors and opportunists on the Barrens trails often target Horde coin convoys. Gazrog sends champions after the beasts to recover the stolen cargo.",al={"stolen silver quest","who stole the silver","barrens stolen shipment"}},{q="Who is Dogran?",a="Dogran is a Horde grunt posted to the Crossroads to work with Gazrog. Gazrog has heard that Dogran is alive, injured, and held by the quilboar, but would rather keep the news from Dogran’s mate, Zankaja.",al={"news of dogran","where is dogran","gazrog dogran"},it="ties"},{q="Is Gazrog affiliated with Ratchet or the goblins?",a="Gazrog serves the Horde from the Crossroads. He maintains security for orc, tauren, and troll interests across the central Barrens.",al={"is gazrog ratchet","gazrog faction","gazrog goblin"},it="side"},{q="Why are raptors stealing supplies in the Barrens?",a="No one knows why the raptors steal supplies. They hid the silver in nests at the Raptor Grounds south of Ratchet, and Gazrog wonders if the stories of their intelligence are true.",al={"raptor thieves why","do raptors steal things","raptors shiny"}},{q="What does Gazrog want?",a="Gazrog seeks to secure critical supplies and maintain order across the Barrens for the Horde. He tasks adventurers with recovering the silver shipment stolen by local raptors, while also seeking word on the fate of his missing comrade, Dogran.",al={"gazrog wants","what does gazrog need","gazrog objectives"},it="wants",add="fdfa6042"},{q="Why is Gazrog here at the Crossroads?",a="Stationed at the strategic outpost of the Crossroads, Gazrog oversees operations vital to the Horde's foothold in central Kalimdor. He is here to tackle local threats disruptively attacking caravans, tracking down missing Horde scouts, and recovering stolen resources essential for the outpost's defense.",al={"why is gazrog here","gazrog crossroads purpose","why gazrog in barrens"},it="why_here",add="d6aec43d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler leaving Durotar or Mulgore, you can find work with Gazrog to secure travel routes across Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know Gazrog as a veteran holding the Crossroads, where keeping the frontier safe takes grit and resolve."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","dogran","gazrog","horde outpost","raptor thieves","stolen silver"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:3281","quest:869","quest:1509","topic:horde"},src={"Gazrog"}}
E["npc:gilthares-firebough"] = {t="npc",n="Gilthares Firebough",z="barrens",s="Gilthares Firebough waits in a tower at Northwatch Hold, held captive by Theramore. Once a deckhand on a moonshine transport between Ratchet and Booty Bay, he seeks a chance to escape.",h="Gilthares Firebough waits in a tower at Northwatch Hold, held captive by Theramore.",sec={{t="A Smuggler Behind Bars",b="Gilthares Firebough is held in a tower at Northwatch Hold. His ship carried illicit cargo between Ratchet and Booty Bay when naval forces from Theramore blasted it to splinters. The sole survivor, Gilthares was dragged ashore in chains and locked away. He wears vivid red and bears little affection for the Alliance zealots who slaughtered his crew. Still, he cares little who helps him break free, so long as they can fight their way down from the ramparts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gilthares Firebough?",a="Gilthares is an elven deckhand affiliated with the Thalo'dan Privateers. Northwatch forces captured him after intercepting and sinking his merchant vessel off the coast of the Barrens.",al={"who is gilthares","gilthares lore","who is this elf"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he imprisoned in Northwatch Hold?",a="Gilthares served aboard a transport carrying moonshine between Ratchet and Booty Bay. Theramore soldiers sank the ship, killed the rest of the crew, and imprisoned him at Northwatch Hold with the contraband as a prisoner of war.",al={"why is he in jail","why in a cage","northwatch prisoner"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Gilthares a high elf or a blood elf?",a="Gilthares is an elf who sails independently, serving neither the Alliance nor the rulers of Silvermoon. His red clothing is often associated with the sin'dorei, but he serves privateers rather than a national faction.",al={"what kind of elf is gilthares","high elf or blood elf","gilthares race"},it="origin"},{q="Who are the Thalo'dan Privateers?",a="The Thalo'dan Privateers are an independent maritime outfit involved in smuggling across the Great Sea. Their ventures include the profitable moonshine run between Ratchet and Booty Bay.",al={"thalodan privateers","who does he work for","gilthares crew"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Gilthares Firebough on?",a="Gilthares aligns with neither the Horde nor the Alliance. He is an independent sailor affiliated with the Thalo'dan Privateers, a free-sailing outfit operating along the trade routes between Ratchet and Booty Bay. While he harbors no particular love for the Horde, his violent capture and harsh enslavement at the hands of Theramore zealots have made him openly hostile toward the Alliance forces occupying Northwatch Hold.",al={"gilthares firebough faction","is gilthares horde or alliance","gilthares allegiance"},it="side",add="4d14e07a"},{q="What does Gilthares Firebough want?",a="Gilthares wants nothing more than to break free from his cage in Northwatch Hold and escape the zealots who captured him. Having survived the violent destruction of his moonshine transport only to be locked away in a coastal tower, he is desperate for someone capable of clearing a path through the garrison so he can flee their captivity.",al={"gilthares firebough goal","what does gilthares want","gilthares firebough objective"},it="wants",add="84aa2a4b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Helping Gilthares escape Northwatch strikes a blow against Theramore's aggression along the Barrens coastline.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gilthares is initially indifferent to passersby, but he harbors intense hostility toward the Alliance sailors who destroyed his vessel and locked him in a cell."},kw={"booty bay","free from the hold","gilthares firebough","northwatch hold","ratchet","thalo'dan privateers"},rel={"quest:898","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","subzone:booty-bay","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Gilthares Firebough"}}
E["npc:grish-longrunner"] = {t="npc",n="Grish Longrunner",z="barrens",s="At the Great Lift, Grish Longrunner watches the boundary between the southern Barrens and Thousand Needles. The tauren scout carries messages for the Horde and tracks movement across the crossing.",h="At the Great Lift, Grish Longrunner watches the boundary between the southern Barrens and Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="Watcher at the Lift",b="Grish Longrunner keeps watch beside the Great Lift in the southern Barrens. Its platform connects the dry southern Barrens with the canyons of Thousand Needles. Quilboar packs roam nearby, and rival groups threaten the crossing. Grish watches travelers and keeps the Horde informed, so reinforcements can be called where they are needed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grish Longrunner?",a="Grish Longrunner is a tauren scout for the Horde, stationed at the rim of the Great Lift. The platform descends from the Barrens into Thousand Needles.",al={"who is grish","grish longrunner identity","what does grish do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Grish Longrunner?",a="Find Grish Longrunner in the southern Barrens, beside the mechanical entrance to the Great Lift that leads down to Thousand Needles.",al={"grish longrunner location","where is grish","find grish"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play in the area?",a="Grish receives Horde messengers and travelers, and helps rally and direct local reinforcements through requests such as Calling in the Reserves.",al={"grish purpose","grish quests","calling in the reserves grish"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Grish Longrunner on?",a="Grish is a proud member of the tauren tribes and is loyal to the Horde. Operating around the borders of the Barrens and the descent into Thousand Needles, he serves as a point of contact for Horde travelers navigating the dangerous passages between regions.",al={"grish longrunner faction","is grish horde","grish longrunner allegiance"},it="side",add="0053ed11"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde courier or warrior, you can find Grish watching the Great Lift on the route south to Thousand Needles or north into the Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share Grish's Longrunner name and the vigilance his people bring to the routes through their ancestral lands."},kw={"barrens","calling in the reserves","great lift","grish","longrunner","tauren","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:great-lift","quest:5881","zone:barrens","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:quilboar"},src={"Grish Longrunner"}}
E["npc:grub"] = {t="npc",n="Grub",z="barrens",s="At a hut east of the Crossroads, Grub runs a roadside eatery with a cook and a baker. He is known for teaching travelers to cook with the Barrens' local vermin.",h="At a hut east of the Crossroads, Grub runs a roadside eatery with a cook and a baker.",sec={{t="A Frontier Appetite",b="East of the Crossroads, Grub shares a hut with Duhng, his cook, and Tarban Hearthgrain, a baker. Grub makes use of the Barrens' dig rats instead of letting them go to waste. He offers travelers a recipe for simmering the rodents into stew.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grub?",a="Grub is an orc who lives in a hut east of the Crossroads in the Barrens. He runs a small eatery with Duhng, his cook, and Tarban Hearthgrain, a baker, for travelers passing through.",al={"grub","who is grub","orc east of crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Grub?",a="Find Grub in a small hut at the foot of the mountains, just east of the Crossroads in the Barrens, off the main path.",al={"grub location","where is grub","grub hut"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Grub need help with?",a="Grub needs travelers to gather dig rats from the Barrens for his Dig Rat Stew. He shares the recipe with cooks who prepare it.",al={"grub quest","dig rat stew quest"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Grub on?",a="Grub is an orc allied with the Horde, operating peacefully just outside the Crossroads in the Barrens. He welcomes Horde travelers to his small homestead, doing business with fellow cooks, bakers, and passing adventurers without getting entangled in military strife.",al={"grub faction","is grub horde","grub alliance or horde"},it="side",add="1dd1f89b"},{q="Why is Grub here?",a="Grub has set up a small domestic settlement east of the Crossroads at the base of the mountains. Rather than serving on the front lines, he runs a culinary dwelling alongside his cook Duhng and the baker Tarban Hearthgrain, sourcing and preparing local frontier fare.",al={"why is grub in the barrens","grub hut crossroads","what is grub doing here"},it="why_here",add="bef281f8"},{q="Who is Grub tied to?",a="Grub shares his roadside hut with Duhng, who handles the cooking, and Tarban Hearthgrain, who manages the baking. Together, this unlikely gathering of companions manages their small hearth in the rugged plains of the Barrens.",al={"who does grub work with","grub companions","grub associates"},it="ties",add="c7807b4d"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn Grub's Dig Rat Stew recipe by gathering its ingredients.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you can find Grub's roadside kitchen just outside the Crossroads, where he offers travelers food and a lesson in making use of what the plains provide."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","dig rat stew","duhng","grub","tarban hearthgrain"},rel={"quest:862","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},src={"Grub"}}
E["npc:islen-waterseer"] = {t="npc",n="Islen Waterseer",z="barrens",s="Beside the Tidus Stair, respected tauren shaman Islen Waterseer guides Horde initiates through the trials of water. She lives by a quiet fishing hut and teaches shamans to attune to water spirits as they seek their Water Totem.",h="Beside the Tidus Stair, respected tauren shaman Islen Waterseer guides Horde initiates through the trials of...",sec={{t="The Hermit of Tidus Stair",b="On the Barrens coast, Islen Waterseer keeps to the craggy Tidus Stair, where arid plains meet the Great Sea. Water spirits are raw and near along this shore. Islen chooses this quiet outpost over thunderous halls and busy cities, spending her days listening to the tides. Shamans seeking communion with water come to her for guidance.",sp=0},{t="Mistress of the Water Sapta",b="To know water, a shaman needs inner harmony and spiritual sight as well as study. Islen guides seekers in preparing the Water Sapta, a sacred brew that pierces the veil between mortal senses and elemental manifestations. She teaches that water can be unyielding and deep, yet fluid and restorative. Anyone who calls on its aid must show it great respect.",sp=0},{t="Bonds Across the Wilds",b="Though Islen lives quietly on the coast, her spiritual ties reach across Kalimdor. She shares a close, enduring friendship with Greta Mosshoof, another wise tauren skilled in the restorative arts. Islen's knowledge of water's purifying nature reaches beyond the Barrens, bringing spiritual aid to lands afflicted by deep corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Islen Waterseer?",a="Along the Barrens coast, Islen Waterseer guides shamans who seek their Water Totem. The respected tauren shaman has a rare, deep bond with the elemental spirits of water and mentors those who travel to learn from her.",al={"islen waterseer lore","who is islen","tidus stair tauren"},it="identity"},{q="Why do shamans travel to see her?",a="During the Call of Water trials, shaman trainers in Durotar, Orgrimmar, and Thunder Bluff direct their students to Islen. She tests their understanding of water and teaches them to craft the Water Sapta, which lets them perceive water elementals directly.",al={"why visit islen","call of water npc","shaman quest barrens coast"},it="wants"},{q="Where is Islen Waterseer located?",a="Islen sits outside a small fishing hut on the Tidus Stair, on the Barrens' eastern shore south of the Merchant Coast.",al={"islen location","where is islen waterseer","find islen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Water Sapta she speaks of?",a="The Water Sapta is a spiritual draught brewed with elemental components. Drinking it lets a shaman's sight pierce the physical plane and reveal water spirits dwelling in sacred springs and tides.",al={"water sapta meaning","what does the sapta do"},it="item"},{q="Who is Islen's friend Greta Mosshoof?",a="Greta Mosshoof is Islen's old tauren companion and fellow practitioner of spiritual crafts. They share an enduring friendship and consult one another about spiritual cleansing and water's restorative nature.",al={"greta mosshoof connection","islen friend"},it="ties"},{q="Does Islen belong to a specific faction or tribe?",a="No tribe is named for Islen. She lives alone on the coast and welcomes travelers from both the Horde and the Alliance. She helps cleanse Felwood's corrupted waters, while Horde shaman trainers send their orc, troll, and tauren students to her.",al={"islen faction","is islen horde"},it="side"},{q="Why is Islen Waterseer here?",a="Islen dwells by the Great Sea along the Tidus Stair, living quietly in solitude near the open water. Here, attuned directly to the tides and natural flows, she serves as a spiritual anchor for young shamans across the Horde who must learn to attune themselves to the elusive spirits of water.",al={"why is islen here","why is islen by the ocean","islen waterseer tidus stair"},it="why_here",add="6d5841da"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you learn from Islen the elemental rites that bind you to water spirits and teach you to commune with them as you seek your Water Totem.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see Islen's reverence for the Earth Mother's gifts in her solitary life by the sea, where she stays attuned to the wild's subtle currents.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find a tranquil spiritual anchor in Islen along the Barrens coast. She welcomes travelers from Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff."},kw={"barrens","call of water","greta mosshoof","islen","shaman","tidus stair","water sapta","waterseer"},rel={"subzone:tidus-stair","quest:63","quest:972","npc:greta-mosshoof","zone:barrens","topic:tauren","zone:thunderbluff","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Islen Waterseer"}}
E["npc:jahan-hawkwing"] = {t="npc",n="Jahan Hawkwing",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Jahan Hawkwing keeps Horde travelers supplied with armor. The tauren armorer works from this outpost in the Barrens, where predators roam the plains.",h="At the Crossroads, Jahan Hawkwing keeps Horde travelers supplied with armor.",sec={{t="Armorer of the Crossroads",b="Jahan Hawkwing tends to the armor needs of Horde travelers and defenders at the Crossroads. In the Barrens, durable gear can mean survival against centaur, quilboar, and wild beasts. Jahan works with local leatherworkers, sending cured hides for delivery so his shop stays stocked with dependable tanned leather and sturdy chainmail.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jahan Hawkwing?",a="Jahan Hawkwing is a tauren merchant and armorer stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He supplies passing adventurers and Horde guards with protective leather and mail equipment.",al={"jahan hawkwing lore","who is jahan","crossroads armor vendor"},it="identity"},{q="What goods does he sell?",a="Jahan sells basic sets of tanned leather and chainmail armor, including jerkins, boots, belts, bracers, and gloves. The gear suits novice warriors, hunters, and scouts.",al={"what does jahan sell","jahan hawkwing inventory","jahan armor"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does he offer to travelers?",a="Jahan depends on nearby artisans to supply his wares. He asks travelers to carry raw or prepared materials to local tanners, then waits for the finished goods to return.",al={"jahan quests","bundle of hides quest","crossroads hide delivery"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Jahan Hawkwing on?",a="Jahan Hawkwing stands firmly with the Horde and his fellow tauren. Stationed at the Crossroads, a vital hub connecting the Horde's territories across central Kalimdor, he provides essential provisions and sturdy armor to those defending these lands from centaur, quilboar, and rival factions.",al={"jahan hawkwing faction","is jahan hawkwing horde","jahan hawkwing alliance or horde"},it="side",add="34a83622"},{q="Why is Jahan Hawkwing in the Crossroads?",a="Jahan Hawkwing makes his living as a leather and mail armor merchant at the Crossroads. Because the outpost sees countless scouts, hunters, and travelers passing through the Barrens every day, his craft supplies them with durable gear needed to survive the harsh wilderness.",al={"why is jahan hawkwing here","jahan hawkwing location","jahan hawkwing crossroads"},it="why_here",add="f61d6720"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="At the Crossroads, where Kalimdor's major trails meet, Jahan helps keep Horde warriors and scouts armored against centaur raids and local wildlife.",["race:Tauren"]="Jahan reflects the shu'halo's practical, self-reliant ways. He uses hidecraft and sturdy materials to protect travelers in the Barrens, the ancestral lands of the tauren."},kw={"armorer","bundle of hides","chainmail","crossroads","jahan hawkwing","leather armor","tauren","the barrens"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:6361","quest:6364","topic:tauren"},src={"Jahan Hawkwing"}}
E["npc:jorah-annison"] = {t="npc",n="Jorah Annison",z="barrens",s="In the Magic Quarter, Jorah Annison helps spellcasters find knowledge scattered across Azeroth. The Forsaken cartographer knows both the land and the ancient texts warlocks seek.",h="In the Magic Quarter, Jorah Annison helps spellcasters find knowledge scattered across Azeroth.",sec={{t="A Scholar of Darkened Lands",b="Jorah Annison makes maps in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, but the work does not hold his interest. He would trade every map in the shop for one good book. Jorah knows more about ancient texts than almost anyone, and warlocks share his taste for a scholar's work.",sp=0},{t="The Cabal's Trail",b="Warlocks seeking the elusive Tome of the Cabal are often sent to Jorah Annison. His knowledge reaches beyond the ruins of Lordaeron, and he can point them toward places where ancient texts and remnants of dark sects might be found. He joins the study of old lore to the geography of distant lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jorah Annison?",a="Jorah Annison is an undead cartographer in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, where he helps Horde travelers with geography and knowledge of historical places.",al={"jorah annison who","who is jorah","undercity cartographer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Jorah Annison?",a="You can find Jorah Annison in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"jorah annison location","where is jorah annison","find jorah"},gp=true},{q="Why do warlocks need to speak with him?",a="Strahad Farsan sends warlocks seeking the ancient Tome of the Cabal to Jorah because Jorah knows more about ancient texts than anyone Strahad knows. Jorah points them toward the tome's lost halves, rumored to be with the centaur of Thousand Needles and lost in transit on the coast west of Southshore.",al={"jorah warlock quest","tome of the cabal jorah","why talk to jorah"},it="why_here"},{q="What faction does Jorah Annison belong to?",a="Jorah Annison belongs to the Forsaken and is loyal to the Horde, serving his people from their capital city.",al={"is jorah horde","jorah annison faction"},it="side"},{q="Does Jorah Annison sell maps directly to players?",a="Jorah Annison mainly advises travelers about forgotten landmarks rather than selling goods directly.",al={"does jorah sell maps","jorah merchant"},gp=true},{q="Is Jorah Annison ever found outside the Undercity?",a="Jorah Annison remains in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, though his mapmaking and guidance concern distant places such as the Barrens.",al={"jorah in barrens","jorah outside undercity"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you can turn to Jorah for directions to the lost pages of the Tome of the Cabal.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you share Jorah's home in the Undercity, where his cartography helps serve the survival of the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can draw on Jorah's mapmaking knowledge to navigate unfamiliar lands and recover valuable relics."},kw={"annison","cartographer","jorah","magic quarter","maps","tome of the cabal","undercity","warlock"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1758","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","zone:barrens"},src={"Jorah Annison"}}
E["npc:kaal-soulreaper"] = {t="npc",n="Kaal Soulreaper",z="barrens",s="In the Undercity, orc warlock Kaal Soulreaper trains apprentices and keeps close ties with practitioners of the dark arts across the Horde. Among the Forsaken, he guides students toward mentors in distant lands.",h="In the Undercity, orc warlock Kaal Soulreaper trains apprentices and keeps close ties with practitioners of...",sec={{t="A Practitioner in the Shadows",b="Kaal Soulreaper works in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, where Horde warlocks come to learn from his mastery of demonic entities and curses. Thrall's Horde strictly regulates and monitors fel magic within Orgrimmar, while the subterranean sanctums of Lordaeron offer practitioners like Kaal ample harbor. Beyond teaching, Kaal connects those seeking greater power with mentors across the sea, including Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaal Soulreaper?",a="Kaal Soulreaper trains warlocks in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He teaches warlock spells and guides practitioners seeking specialized dark artifacts and rituals.",al={"who is kaal","kaal soulreaper lore","kaal undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an orc warlock living in the Undercity?",a="Warlocks face heavy suspicion and scrutiny in orcish society under Warchief Thrall. The Undercity offers a more tolerant place to study shadow magic and demonology alongside the Forsaken.",al={"why is an orc in undercity","why is kaal in undercity"},it="why_here"},{q="Where does Kaal Soulreaper send his apprentices?",a="When his students reach sufficient mastery, Kaal sends them across the Great Sea to the Barrens to study under Menara Voidrender, or introduces them to other prominent Horde warlocks.",al={"kaal quests","who does kaal send you to"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kaal Soulreaper on?",a="Kaal Soulreaper stands firmly with the Horde. Though an orc residing in the Undercity alongside the Forsaken, he trains warlocks who swear allegiance to the Horde's cause. He maintains direct ties with other Horde practitioners across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, including warlocks in the Barrens and Ratchet, ensuring that those who practice dark arts still direct their fel power toward aiding their allies.",al={"kaal soulreaper faction","who does kaal soulreaper serve","is kaal soulreaper horde"},it="side",add="17865f78"},{q="What does Kaal Soulreaper want?",a="Kaal seeks to guide aspiring warlocks along the perilous path of demonic mastery. Rather than letting inexperienced practitioners succumb to the corrupting powers of the Twisting Nether, he ensures they learn the necessary rites to summon and bind demons, such as the felsteed, and directs promising students to skilled masters like Menara Voidrender to deepen their craft.",al={"kaal soulreaper motive","kaal soulreaper goal","what is kaal soulreaper doing"},it="wants",add="78b7a2d4"},{q="Who is Kaal Soulreaper tied to?",a="Kaal maintains close ties with fellow warlock mentors across the continents. He regularly directs capable practitioners to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens for specialized training, advanced rituals, and the procurement of artifacts like the Orb of Orahil.",al={"kaal soulreaper connections","who does kaal soulreaper work with","kaal soulreaper allies"},it="ties",add="0c3c6935"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can learn demonic arts from Kaal Soulreaper, whose essential training sets ambitious warlocks on the paths to craft the Orb of Orahil and bind a Felsteed.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can find Kaal Soulreaper working openly in the Forsaken capital, away from Orgrimmar's watchful shamanic leadership and the hidden coven in the Cleft of Shadow."},kw={"demonology","felsteed","kaal soulreaper","magic quarter","menara voidrender","undercity","warlock trainer"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","npc:menara-voidrender","quest:4736","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Kaal Soulreaper"}}
E["npc:kadrak"] = {t="npc",n="Kadrak",z="barrens",s="At the Mor'shan Rampart, Kadrak guards the northern frontier between the Barrens and Ashenvale. He directs dispatches and reinforcements into the contested forest, where the Horde fights the night elves.",h="At the Mor'shan Rampart, Kadrak guards the northern frontier between the Barrens and Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Rampart",b="At the Mor'shan Rampart, Kadrak guards the main route between the Barrens and Ashenvale. The barricade marks a hard border: Horde-held plains lie to the south, and night elf-guarded woods stretch north. Kadrak keeps watch against Sentinels and hostile woodland creatures, holding the perimeter against incursions.",sp=0},{t="Frontline Logistics",b="Kadrak also handles military reports between the Barrens and logging camps deeper in Ashenvale. Couriers bring him combat reports from the Warsong Outriders, and he directs supplies and reinforcements to outposts such as Splintertree Post. Those who report to Kadrak are sent onward into the struggle for the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kadrak?",a="Kadrak is an orc officer at the Mor'shan Rampart. He oversees the border and directs Horde forces traveling between the Barrens and the fighting in Ashenvale.",al={"kadrak identity","who is the orc at the wall","mor'shan rampart commander"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Kadrak be found?",a="Kadrak can be found at the Mor'shan Rampart, a fortified wooden barricade at the northern edge of the Barrens, where the road leads into Ashenvale.",al={"kadrak location","find kadrak","where is kadrak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Kadrak's role in the Horde?",a="Kadrak commands the border defenses and gathers military reports from scout runners. He briefs Horde travelers heading north to reinforce outposts such as Splintertree Post.",al={"kadrak duties","what does kadrak do","kadrak role"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Mor'shan Rampart heavily defended?",a="The Mor'shan Rampart guards the northern approaches to the Barrens and Durotar against night elf incursions in response to the Horde's logging operations in Ashenvale.",al={"why is mor'shan rampart fortified","purpose of the rampart","why guard ashenvale border"},it="conflict"},{q="What quests does Kadrak provide or complete?",a="Kadrak receives reports carried from the Barrens and sends adventurers on assignments involving Warsong scouting reports and strengthening the Horde presence along the forest frontier.",al={"kadrak quests","report to kadrak","the warsong reports"},gp=true},{q="Does Kadrak have ties to other notable Horde figures?",a="Kadrak keeps in regular contact with the Warsong Outriders in Ashenvale and receives their scouting reports at the Rampart.",al={"kadrak connections"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Kadrak on?",a="Kadrak is a loyal warrior of the Horde. Stationed on the rugged border between the Barrens and the contested forests of Ashenvale, he serves under the banner of the Warchief, dedicated to securing orcish interests and defending Horde outposts against night elf incursions.",al={"kadrak faction","is kadrak horde","who does kadrak serve"},it="side",add="e1636f20"},{q="What does Kadrak want?",a="Kadrak aims to hold the northern frontier of the Barrens and push the Horde's presence deeper into Ashenvale. Facing fierce resistance from the night elves, he looks to enlist capable Horde champions to carry reports, relieve beleaguered scouts, and protect vital supply lines across the Mor'shan Rampart.",al={"what is kadrak's goal","kadrak motive","what does kadrak need"},it="wants",add="4dfee007"},{q="Why is Kadrak here at the Mor'shan Rampart?",a="Kadrak stands guard at the Mor'shan Rampart because it is the vital choke point guarding the Barrens from the hostile forests of Ashenvale. As hostilities with the night elves flare up, he coordinates defenses, monitors enemy activity, and directs scouts to reinforce the Warsong outposts to the north.",al={"why is kadrak at the rampart","kadrak location reason","why is kadrak stationed here"},it="why_here",add="86a4d862"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Kadrak to direct warriors north to defend lumber operations and claim Horde territory in Ashenvale.",["faction:Alliance"]="If you fight for the Alliance and try to enter the Barrens from Ashenvale, Kadrak's rampart blocks the road into the Horde heartland.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Kadrak's defense of the Ashenvale border as part of the Warsong Clan's effort to claim territory.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the discipline it takes to hold a fortified choke point against woodland fighters and guerrilla raids."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","kadrak","mor'shan rampart","orc","rampart","splintertree post","warsong"},rel={"subzone:mor-shan-rampart","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","quest:6541","quest:6543","quest:3514","subzone:splintertree-post"},src={"Kadrak"}}
E["npc:kargal-battlescar"] = {t="npc",n="Kargal Battlescar",z="barrens",s="At the Far Watch Post, Kargal Battlescar guards the eastern edge of the Barrens. He watches the crossing from Durotar, judges incoming recruits, and sends capable fighters west to strengthen Horde defenses.",h="At the Far Watch Post, Kargal Battlescar guards the eastern edge of the Barrens.",sec={{t="Sentinel of the Border",b="Kargal Battlescar watches the road into the Barrens from the Far Watch Post. Travelers and new adventurers cross the bridge over the Southfury River, leaving the Valley of Trials behind. The Barrens is a dangerous, contested land, where aggressive wildlife, centaur raiders, and quilboar tribes threaten the frontier. Kargal inspects those who pass and gathers willing recruits for the Horde. He sends them onward to the Crossroads, where they can aid local commanders in securing the frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kargal Battlescar?",a="Kargal Battlescar commands the Far Watch Post, guarding the eastern road from Durotar into the Barrens.",al={"kargal battlescar","kargal","who is kargal"},it="identity"},{q="What is the purpose of the Far Watch Post?",a="The Far Watch Post warns of threats near the Durotar border and along the Southfury River, and helps defend the Barrens.",al={"far watch post purpose","why far watch post","what is this outpost"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Kargal send new recruits?",a="Kargal directs recruits west along the main road to the Crossroads, the Barrens' central military hub.",al={"kargal quest destination","where to go after kargal","where does kargal send you"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Kargal Battlescar on?",a="Kargal Battlescar stands squarely with the Horde. Guarding the eastern border of the Barrens where Durotar meets the open plains, he ensures incoming recruits and travelers safely make the crossing under the Warchief's banner.",al={"kargal battlescar faction","is kargal horde"},it="side",add="81d05e56"},{q="What does Kargal Battlescar want?",a="Kargal wants capable warriors to secure the frontier and aid the growing settlement at the Crossroads. He directs fresh conscripts arriving from Durotar to bolster the Barrens' defenses against threats lingering along the plains.",al={"kargal battlescar goal","what does kargal want"},it="wants",add="ffbc81ca"},{q="Why is Kargal Battlescar stationed here?",a="Kargal oversees the Far Watch Post, the fortified entryway connecting Durotar and the Barrens across the Southfury River. He is stationed here to receive new conscripts journeying westward and direct them toward where the Horde needs them most.",al={"why is kargal at far watch post","kargal battlescar location purpose"},it="why_here",add="e589e5e9"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a fresh Horde adventurer leaving Durotar, you meet Kargal Battlescar at the edge of the wider struggles across Kalimdor. He gathers recruits for the conflicts in the Barrens.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can see Kargal's battle hardened experience in the marks of combat he bears. He shows the resilience expected of Horde frontline fighters in the frontier."},kw={"barrens","battlescar","conscript","crossroads","durotar","far watch post","kargal"},rel={"subzone:far-watch-post","quest:840","quest:842","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Kargal Battlescar"}}
E["npc:kelm-hargunth"] = {t="npc",n="Kelm Hargunth",z="barrens",s="At Mor'shan Base Camp, Kelm Hargunth keeps the Warsong Outriders supplied. He equips Horde champions fighting night elves in Warsong Gulch with care packages and provisions.",h="At Mor'shan Base Camp, Kelm Hargunth keeps the Warsong Outriders supplied.",sec={{t="Quartermaster of Mor'shan",b="At Mor'shan Base Camp, Kelm Hargunth manages supplies for the Warsong Outriders. The camp stands on the northern edge of the Barrens, beside the border with Ashenvale. Scouts and raiders skirmish beyond its stockade while Kelm sees that weapons, armor, and rations reach the fighters. The Warsong Outriders face the Silverwing Sentinels, and a steady flow of provisions matters as much as fury in battle.",sp=0},{t="Supplying the Front",b="Kelm gives specialized supplies to warriors who have proven themselves in Warsong Gulch. His stores include care packages with field dressings and iron rations, along with armaments marked with the Warsong clan's crimson insignia. These supplies go to fighters serving the Horde's campaign in the forests to the north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kelm Hargunth?",a="Kelm Hargunth is an orc supply officer for the Warsong Outriders. At Mor'shan Base Camp in the northern Barrens, he distributes weapons, armor, and provisions to Horde soldiers fighting in Warsong Gulch.",al={"kelm hargunth","who is kelm","mor'shan vendor","warsong vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Kelm Hargunth located?",a="Kelm Hargunth is stationed at Mor'shan Base Camp, at the far northern edge of the Barrens beside the rampart divide leading into Ashenvale.",al={"kelm location","where is kelm hargunth","mor shan supply officer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What faction does Kelm Hargunth serve?",a="Kelm Hargunth serves the Warsong Outriders, the Horde vanguard seeking lumber and territory in southern Ashenvale against the night elves.",al={"kelm faction","warsong outriders quartermaster","who does kelm work for"},it="side"},{q="What are the care packages Kelm offers?",a="Kelm Hargunth offers Basic, Standard, and Advanced Care Packages to frontline fighters. They contain battlefield sundries, bandages, and rations for Horde combatants in the gulch.",al={"outrider care package","kelm care package","warsong care package"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is Mor'shan Base Camp so important to the Warsong?",a="Mor'shan Base Camp is a fortified staging ground and checkpoint between the Barrens and Ashenvale. It lets the Warsong clan move supplies, reinforcements, and harvested timber safely into Horde lands.",al={"why morshan base camp","morshan purpose","base camp lore"},it="place"},{q="What kind of gear does Kelm Hargunth provide?",a="Kelm Hargunth provides proven fighters with Warsong battle tabards, specialized weapons such as the Scout's Blade and Legionnaire's Sword, tailored armor sets, rings, and battlefield draughts for close-quarters skirmishing.",al={"kelm pvp gear","warsong rewards","what does kelm sell"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is Kelm Hargunth stationed at Mor'shan Base Camp?",a="Kelm Hargunth serves as the supply officer for the Warsong Outriders right at the border of Ashenvale. Stationed at Mor'shan Base Camp, he ensures that Horde champions heading into Warsong Gulch are properly equipped to fight the Silverwing Sentinels and secure vital lumber and territory.",al={"why is kelm hargunth here","kelm hargunth purpose","why kelm at morshan"},it="why_here",add="1810d113"},{q="What does Kelm Hargunth want?",a="Kelm wants nothing less than total Horde victory against the night elves in Warsong Gulch. As the Outriders' quartermaster, he demands proof of your valor on the battlefield, offering armaments, supplies, and care packages to those who strike hard against the Alliance.",al={"what does kelm hargunth want","kelm hargunth goal","what does kelm want"},it="wants",add="c16a55e1"},{q="Who is Kelm Hargunth tied to?",a="Kelm answers directly to the Warsong Outriders, the Horde vanguard contesting the dense forests of Ashenvale. Operating under the banner of the Warsong clan and the wider Horde, he works in lockstep with the frontline forces defending Mor'shan Base Camp.",al={"kelm hargunth affiliation","who does kelm hargunth work for","kelm hargunth faction"},it="ties",add="bced0f9b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde soldier, you can take up arms against the night elves in Warsong Gulch, and Kelm Hargunth provides the tools of war.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see Grom Hellscream's legacy in Ashenvale carried on as Hargunth keeps the Warsong clan armed and fed.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you rely on Hargunth's sturdy plate leggings, heavy blades, and combat rations to hold the line against the Alliance."},kw={"barrens","care package","kelm hargunth","mor'shan base camp","pvp vendor","quartermaster","warsong gulch","warsong outriders"},rel={"npc:warsong-outrider","zone:barrens"},src={"Kelm Hargunth"}}
E["npc:kirge-sternhorn"] = {t="npc",n="Kirge Sternhorn",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Kirge Sternhorn guides travelers crossing central Kalimdor. The tauren keeps watch over the southern trails and sends new Horde adventurers north to the Crossroads.",h="In the Barrens, Kirge Sternhorn guides travelers crossing central Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Wayfarer in the Barrens",b="New wanderers often find the sun-baked Barrens daunting. Kirge Sternhorn watches over travelers south of the central trails, between the southern camps and the heart of Kalimdor. Marauding quilboar and fierce predators roam the savanna, and Kirge helps young adventurers find their footing. He ensures they seek out the greater Horde presence gathering to the north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kirge Sternhorn?",a="Kirge Sternhorn is a tauren wanderer and guide in the southern Barrens. He aids Horde travelers as they cross the dusty plains.",al={"kirge sternhorn lore","who is kirge","kirge npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Kirge send travelers?",a="Kirge directs travelers north to the Crossroads, the Barrens’ central junction. Horde forces coordinate defense and exploration across the region there.",al={"kirge quest","journey to the crossroads kirge","where does kirge send you"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What faction does Kirge Sternhorn serve?",a="Kirge is loyal to the Horde and his fellow tauren. He offers guidance and assistance to all Horde members traveling through the territory.",al={"is kirge horde","kirge allegiance"},it="side"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see Kirge’s grounded, welcoming spirit in the way he guides fellow tribal kin and allies through the harsh frontier of their adopted homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Kirge as an early waypoint from the southern reaches, pointing you toward the greater Horde community at the Crossroads."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","kirge","southern barrens","sternhorn","taurajo","tauren"},rel={"zone:barrens","quest:854","subzone:crossroads","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Kirge Sternhorn"}}
E["npc:klannoc-macleod"] = {t="npc",n="Klannoc Macleod",z="barrens",s="On Fray Island, Klannoc Macleod puts warriors to the test. The human warrior welcomes fighters from both the Alliance and the Horde who seek mastery of combat stances. Those who earn his respect are sent inland to face greater trials of strength.",h="On Fray Island, Klannoc Macleod puts warriors to the test.",sec={{t="The Master of Fray Island",b="Klannoc Macleod puts seasoned fighters through their paces on Fray Island, off the Merchant Coast in the Barrens. Though human, he leaves Alliance and Horde quarrels aside. He judges each contender by grit, blade work, and resolve under fire.",sp=0},{t="The Affray",b="Klannoc Macleod's trial on Fray Island is called the Affray. Contenders climb onto raised iron grating and face relentless waves of eager brawlers as he watches. Those who endure the onslaught and defeat his chosen champion earn his approval and prove they have the temperament for berserker training.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Klannoc Macleod?",a="Klannoc Macleod trains warriors and tests their limits on Fray Island off the Barrens coast. Fighters come to him to prove themselves and learn new techniques.",al={"who is klannoc","klannoc macleod lore","fray island guy"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Klannoc Macleod?",a="You can find Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island, a rocky isle off the eastern Barrens coast, southeast of the Merchant Coast and Ratchet. Swim across open water to reach his camp.",al={"klannoc location","where is fray island","how to get to klannoc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does a human talk to Horde players on Fray Island?",a="Klannoc Macleod keeps apart from the Alliance and Horde conflict. He judges contenders by their martial discipline and warrior's resolve, and tests those who arrive with a proper recommendation.",al={"is klannoc hostile horde","why is klannoc neutral","horde klannoc"},it="side"},{q="What is the Affray?",a="The Affray is an endurance trial on Fray Island. You stand on Klannoc's combat platform and defeat waves of challengers, ending with a fight against Big Will, to prove your ferocity for advanced warrior techniques.",al={"the affray quest","fray island trial","klannoc trial"}},{q="Why send warriors to Klannoc Macleod?",a="Warrior trainers across Azeroth send their most promising students to Klannoc Macleod for a trial of martial fortitude. The trial prepares you for the fierce focus of the Berserker Stance.",al={"warrior quest fray island","why visit klannoc","berserker stance quest"},it="why_here"},{q="Who does Klannoc send you to after the Affray?",a="After you prove yourself in the Affray, Klannoc Macleod sends you north to the Alterac Mountains, near Tarren Mill, to seek guidance from Bath'rah the Windwatcher.",al={"after klannoc","the windwatcher quest","who is the windwatcher"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What does Klannoc Macleod want?",a="Klannoc oversees the combat trials on Fray Island, seeking only capable brawlers worthy of stepping into the ring for the Affray. He pays no mind to faction politics or personal origins, demanding only that those who seek his counsel prove their raw mettle and endurance in grueling battle before directing them onward to greater martial training.",al={"klannoc macleod wants","what does klannoc want","klannoc purpose"},it="wants",add="bf19a78f"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Klannoc Macleod's test of endurance and ferocity in the Affray before he guides you toward the Berserker Stance.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde fighter, you can seek trial and honor with Klannoc Macleod, who sets faction rivalries aside on his island.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance warrior, you must travel far into the waters off the Barrens coast to find Klannoc Macleod and prove your combat readiness on Fray Island."},kw={"barrens","berserker","fray island","islander","klannoc","macleod","the affray","warrior"},rel={"subzone:fray-island","quest:1719","quest:1718","quest:1791","zone:barrens","quest:887"},src={"Klannoc Macleod"}}
E["npc:korran"] = {t="npc",n="Korran",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Korran watches the Barrens for threats to the Horde. The Darkspear troll serves Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar and studies the silithid emerging across the scrublands.",h="At the Crossroads, Korran watches the Barrens for threats to the Horde.",sec={{t="A Scout at the Crossroads",b="At the Crossroads, Korran watches for threats beyond the quilboar and centaur clans. Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar stationed the troll scout there to observe changes in the land. Korran coordinates the gathering of intelligence for the Horde's leadership.",sp=0},{t="The Silithid Incursion",b="Korran now focuses on the Field of Giants in the southern Barrens. Strange, aggressive insectoid creatures called silithid have begun burrowing into the earth. To learn where the swarm came from and what danger it poses to the young Horde, Korran asks passing adventurers to dig up intact eggs with his claw tool.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Korran?",a="Korran is a Darkspear troll who watches and studies the Barrens from the Crossroads. He reports to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.",al={"who is korran","korran troll","crossroads troll"},it="identity"},{q="What is Korran investigating in the Barrens?",a="Korran is investigating the strange, aggressive insectoid creatures called silithid at the Field of Giants in the southern Barrens. Similar swarms have also been reported farther south in Thousand Needles.",al={"what does korran study","korran research","field of giants insects"},it="why_here"},{q="Who does Korran work for?",a="Korran serves Belgrom Rockmaul, a seasoned warrior in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. Belgrom monitors emerging threats across Kalimdor for the Horde.",al={"who sent korran","korran superior","belgrom rockmaul"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Korran need silithid eggs?",a="Korran needs intact silithid eggs to study the swarm's life cycle and origins. He hopes to learn what the creatures are and how great a threat they pose to Horde territory.",al={"why silithid eggs","egg hunt quest","korran claw"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Korran on?",a="Korran is a loyal scout of the Horde stationed in the Crossroads. He reports directly to Belgrom Rockmaul, a prominent officer in Orgrimmar, keeping the warchief's command informed of strange disturbances across the Barrens.",al={"korran faction","is korran horde","korran allegiance"},it="side",add="b07b8377"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, Korran watches Kalimdor's changing ecology for new threats like the silithid while Orgrimmar secures its borders.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you bring scouting and survival instincts to the arid Barrens, where Korran studies strange, alien beasts with practical cunning."},kw={"barrens","belgrom rockmaul","crossroads","egg hunt","field of giants","korran","silithid"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","subzone:field-of-giants","zone:barrens","quest:868","zone:orgrimmar","zone:thousandneedles","topic:troll","topic:horde"},src={"Korran"}}
E["npc:mangletooth"] = {t="npc",n="Mangletooth",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth faces execution in a Horde cage and bargains with those who visit him. He offers knowledge of his rivals and Agamaggan's ancient lore in return for their help.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth faces execution in a Horde cage and bargains with those who visit him.",sec={{t="A Hostage in Chains",b="Tauren hunters and orc sentries keep Mangletooth in a cage at Camp Taurajo. The captured Razormane quilboar awaits execution, but he still tries to sway his captors and visiting Horde adventurers. He urges them to strike at the enemies of his tribe, hoping to prove his worth or win his freedom.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal from Within",b="Mangletooth first tries to earn his clan's gratitude by directing Horde fighters against the rival Bristleback tribe. Then he learns that Razormane leaders Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane have abandoned him. Enraged, he turns against his own kin and sends adventurers to execute his former allies.",sp=1},{t="The Power of Blood Shards",b="Mangletooth knows the religious history of his people. During the ancient War of the Ancients, Agamaggan's spilled blood gave rise to the Barrens' massive thorns. Mangletooth gathers red crystalline Blood Shards from fallen Bristlebacks and channels the lingering divine power within them, granting ancient blessings to those who help him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mangletooth?",a="Mangletooth is a captured Razormane quilboar held in a cage at Camp Taurajo. Facing execution, he bargains with adventurers, offering guidance and ancient blessings in return for their help.",al={"mangletooth","who is mangletooth","caged quilboar taurajo"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Mangletooth in a cage?",a="Mangletooth was captured during clashes between the Horde and quilboar in the southern Barrens. Tauren and orc guards at Camp Taurajo keep him caged as they await his execution.",al={"why is mangletooth captive","why in cage","why taurajo prisoner"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Mangletooth ask you to attack other Razormane quilboar?",a="Mangletooth asks you to attack other Razormane quilboar because Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane left him to die instead of trying to rescue him. Enraged, he wants travelers to execute them out of spite.",al={"why attack razormane","betrayal from within lore","why kill nak kuz"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="What are Blood Shards?",a="Blood Shards are crystals formed where Agamaggan's blood soaked into the earth when he fell during the War of the Ancients. Bristleback quilboar often carry them.",al={"blood shards","blood shards lore","agamaggan blood"},it="item"},{q="What can you do with Blood Shards at Mangletooth?",a="When you bring Mangletooth Blood Shards, he channels Agamaggan's sacred power into temporary blessings. They grant greater strength, agility, resilience, spirit, or swiftness.",al={"blood shard buffs","blood shard turn in","what does mangletooth give"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where does Mangletooth say Agamaggan died?",a="Mangletooth says Agamaggan fell in battle during the War of the Ancients. His spilled blood gave rise to the massive thorn spires, and his colossal skull lies enshrining a cavern to the south.",al={"agamaggan lore","where did agamaggan fall","boar god skull"},it="origin"},{q="Whose side is Mangletooth on?",a="Mangletooth serves only himself. Though born of the Razormane quilboar, he holds no true love for the Horde that imprisoned him, nor lingering loyalty to his own tribe once he realizes his clanmates have abandoned him. He cooperates with Horde adventurers solely as a desperate bargain to survive and strike back at his rivals.",al={"mangletooth side","who is mangletooth loyal to","is mangletooth horde"},it="side",add="d88e6e26"},{q="What does Mangletooth want?",a="Facing execution at Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth initially aims to survive and prove his tribe's supremacy over their Bristleback rivals, hoping his people will rescue him. When he realizes his fellow Razormane leaders—Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane—have abandoned him, his desires turn to bitter revenge and gathering the sacred power of Blood Shards.",al={"what does mangletooth want","mangletooth goal","what is mangletooth trying to do"},it="wants",add="7791b01e"},{q="Who is Mangletooth tied to?",a="Mangletooth belongs to the Razormane quilboar of the southern Barrens. His fate is intertwined with his tribal rivals Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane, whose betrayal drives his anger. He also reveres the ancient boar god Agamaggan, whose scattered essence allows Mangletooth to bestow blessings upon those who bring him relics of the fallen god's blood.",al={"mangletooth connections","who does mangletooth know","mangletooth tribe"},it="ties",add="1234667b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="At Camp Taurajo, Horde guards keep Mangletooth caged, yet the Horde uses his bitter grievances to strike at quilboar strongholds across the Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the plains' constant clashes between tauren hunters and quilboar. Mangletooth's willingness to turn on his own kind makes him a valuable, if unsettling, military asset."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","blood shards","bristleback","camp taurajo","mangletooth","quilboar","razormane"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","quest:5052","quest:878","quest:879","zone:barrens","topic:war-of-the-ancients"},src={"Mangletooth"}}
E["npc:mankrik"] = {t="npc",n="Mankrik",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Mankrik carries grief and a thirst for vengeance. A quilboar ambush separated him from his wife, Olgra, and he now hunts the bristled beasts across the Barrens.",h="At the Crossroads, Mankrik carries grief and a thirst for vengeance.",sec={{t="Ambush in the Dust",b="Mankrik and his wife Olgra traveled through the Barrens when quilboar swarmed them during a skirmish at a small tauren settlement. The fighting tore them apart, and Mankrik saw Olgra vanish beneath tusks and thorn-woven weapons. Fury drove him to fight recklessly until a blow left him unconscious. Along the Gold Road, a passing tauren druid found Mankrik bleeding out and bound his injuries. He survived the ambush, but Olgra was gone.",sp=0},{t="Consumed by Vengeance",b="At the Crossroads, Mankrik recovers, paralyzed by grief and consumed by bloodlust. Thork and other local leaders warn that hatred has clouded his judgment, and they refuse to send official war parties. Mankrik refuses to move on. Uncertain of Olgra's fate, he calls on any willing Horde travelers to search the Barrens for signs of his lost mate and slaughter any quilboar they meet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mankrik?",a="At the Crossroads in the Barrens, Mankrik is an orc warrior consumed by grief and rage. A quilboar ambush separated him from his wife, and he now seeks vengeance.",al={"mankrik lore","who is mankrik","mankrik story"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Mankrik's wife?",a="A swarm of quilboar cut Mankrik and Olgra off from each other during a clash at a tauren settlement. Mankrik was beaten down in the chaos, and Olgra disappeared amid the fighting.",al={"mankriks wife","where is mankriks wife","what happened to olgra","olgra fate"}},{q="How did Mankrik survive the battle?",a="A tauren druid found Mankrik bleeding out along the Gold Road after he fell unconscious beneath the quilboar swarm. The druid bound his injuries and brought him to safety.",al={"how did mankrik survive","who saved mankrik"},it="history"},{q="Why does Thork refuse to help Mankrik?",a="Thork, the leader at the Crossroads, believes Mankrik's rage and thirst for vengeance have clouded his judgment and left him unable to act rationally.",al={"why wont thork help","thork and mankrik"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Mankrik on?",a="Mankrik is loyal to the Horde. Operating out of the Crossroads in the Barrens, he relies on Horde travelers and adventurers to aid him in his desperate search and to strike back against the quilboar threatening their lands.",al={"mankrik faction","is mankrik horde","mankrik alliance or horde"},it="side",add="63979fed"},{q="What does Mankrik want?",a="Mankrik wants to learn the fate of his lost wife, Olgra, and to slaughter as many quilboar as possible. After being separated from her during an ambush, he is consumed by grief, rage, and a need for vengeance against the bristled marauders.",al={"what is mankrik looking for","mankrik goal","what does mankrik need"},it="wants",add="20b8339c"},{q="Why is Mankrik here at the Crossroads?",a="Following a quilboar assault that left him grievously wounded, a passing tauren druid dragged Mankrik along the Gold Road to safety. Mankrik now remains at the Crossroads because his injuries and lingering uncertainty keep him anchored near where he last saw his wife.",al={"why is mankrik at crossroads","mankrik location reason","why is mankrik in the barrens"},it="why_here",add="5eb75604"},{q="Who is Mankrik tied to?",a="Mankrik is bound by love and sorrow to his wife, Olgra, whom he fought beside before they were overrun by quilboar. He also owes his life to the wandering tauren druid who tended his wounds on the Gold Road.",al={"mankrik relationships","who is mankrik connected to","mankrik family"},it="ties",add="d34d6f35"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know family and honor are constantly tested against the threats on Kalimdor's wild frontiers.",["faction:Horde"]="At the Crossroads, you face the unrelenting threat of the bristled quilboar packs across the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","gold road","mankrik","olgra","quilboar","thork"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","quest:899","topic:quilboar","npc:thork","subzone:gold-road","zone:barrens","topic:tauren","topic:druid"},src={"Mankrik"}}
E["npc:mebok-mizzyrix"] = {t="npc",n="Mebok Mizzyrix",z="barrens",s="Mebok Mizzyrix is an enterprising goblin entrepreneur residing in the port town of Ratchet. Ever eager to turn bizarre wilderness reagents into profit, he hires passing adventurers to gather unusual flora and fauna from across the Barrens and beyond. His most notorious project involves concocting a commercial intellect-enhancing beverage out of raptor horns.",h="Mebok Mizzyrix is an enterprising goblin entrepreneur residing in the port town of Ratchet.",sec={{t="An Enterprising Alchemist",b="Operating out of the bustling, neutral port of Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix embodies the classic Steamwheedle spirit of relentless opportunism. While Ratchet caters to sailors, pirates, and merchants of all stripes, Mebok focuses his keen eye on Kalimdor's wilderness. Rather than mining standard ore or trading mundane cloth, he seeks out rare biological curiosities that he believes can be refined into highly lucrative concoctions and commodities.",sp=0},{t="The Quest for Smart Drinks",b="Mebok's premier commercial endeavor is a proprietary 'smart drink' intended to artificially boost the intellect of whoever consumes it. Convinced that the natural cunning and ferocity of local raptors stems from the horns crowning their snouts, Mebok commissions hunters to harvest intact horns across the Barrens. To him, ethics and taste take a backseat to raw market potential, so long as paying customers believe the brew delivers results.",sp=0},{t="Exotic Reagents and Flora",b="Beyond raptor-derived elixirs, Mebok maintains a constant demand for other bizarre specimens. From collecting volatile Deepmoss spider eggs to commissioning the retrieval of rare Blueleaf tubers buried deep within the brambles of Razorfen Kraul, his pursuits consistently push intrepid mercenaries into perilous territory. If an organism possesses strange properties, Mebok is certain there is a way to bottle and sell it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is a goblin merchant and alchemical schemer located in the neutral port town of Ratchet in the Barrens. He contracts adventurers to gather strange wildlife and plant parts to fuel his commercial projects.",al={"who is mebok","mebok mizzyrix lore","ratchet goblin mebok"},it="identity"},{q="What are Smart Drinks?",a="Smart Drinks are experimental intellect-boosting tonics Mebok Mizzyrix hopes to brew and sell. He believes grinding down the horns of clever Barrens raptors will impart their sharp instincts and cunning to the drinker.",al={"smart drink","smart drinks quest","raptor horn potion"}},{q="Where can Mebok Mizzyrix be found?",a="He can be found standing among the buildings in the port city of Ratchet, on the eastern coast of the Barrens, accessible to both Horde and Alliance travelers.",al={"mebok location","where is mebok","find mebok mizzyrix"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Mebok want raptor horns?",a="Mebok hypothesizes that the cunning intelligence of the raptors roaming the Barrens is concentrated within their horns. He plans to pulverize them as the primary active ingredient in his intellect-enhancing beverages.",al={"why raptor horns","raptor horn purpose","what does mebok do with horns"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Mebok send people to Razorfen Kraul?",a="He enlists adventurers to delve into Razorfen Kraul to dig up Blueleaf tubers using a trained sniffer, seeking the rare plant for its valuable and unusual botanical properties.",al={"why razorfen kraul","mebok rfk quest","blueleaf tubers rfk"},it="motive"},{q="Does Mebok work for the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Mebok is an independent member of the Steamwheedle Cartel in neutral Ratchet. He is loyal to coin and will happily trade and contract with members of either faction.",al={"is mebok horde","is mebok alliance","mebok faction"},it="side"},{q="What does Mebok Mizzyrix want?",a="Mebok is driven by concocting strange new alchemical creations—most notably his experimental 'smart drink.' To perfect his bizarre recipes, he sends adventurers scouring the Barrens and its perilous depths for peculiar ingredients, ranging from intact raptor horns to rare root samples and spider eggs.",al={"mebok wants","what does mebok need","mebok mizzyrix goal"},it="wants",add="55f078f0"},{q="Why is Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet?",a="Ratchet is the prime port town for ambitious goblins who need ready access to the wild resources of Kalimdor. From his base here, Mebok can easily hire arriving sellswords of either faction to venture into the dangerous savannah and harvest the wild specimens he requires for his experiments.",al={"why is mebok here","mebok ratchet why","mebok mizzyrix barrens"},it="why_here",add="c521482b"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Mebok's fascination with odd specimens like Blueleaf tubers showcases the wilder, commercial side of gathering Kalimdor's unique flora.",["profession:Cooking"]="Culinary adventurers will find Mebok's culinary and beverage recipes questionable at best, given his insistence on brewing ground raptor horn.",["faction:Horde"]="Passing through Ratchet on the way across the Barrens offers Horde travelers an easy source of coin clearing out dangerous beasts nearby.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stepping off the boat from Booty Bay into neutral Ratchet gives Alliance explorers access to Mebok's tasks without fear of hostile guards."},kw={"barrens","blueleaf tubers","mebok","mizzyrix","raptor horns","ratchet","smart drinks","steamwheedle"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","quest:1491","quest:865","quest:1221","quest:1069","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},src={"Mebok Mizzyrix"}}
E["npc:menara-voidrender"] = {t="npc",n="Menara Voidrender",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Menara Voidrender teaches warlocks from both factions the dark arts. The human warlock shares her knowledge of demon-binding artifacts and arcane craft from a refuge in Kalimdor, far from orthodox authorities.",h="In Ratchet, Menara Voidrender teaches warlocks from both factions the dark arts.",sec={{t="A Refuge in Ratchet",b="Menara Voidrender works from Ratchet, the neutral goblin port in the Barrens. Many warlocks in the Eastern Kingdoms study in cellars or hidden slaughterhouses beneath their cities, but Ratchet keeps Menara away from the Kirin Tor, Stormwind's guards, and Orgrimmar's overseers. There, she can pursue occult studies in plain sight. She teaches any capable apprentice, whatever their faction, making her a rare meeting point for practitioners of the dark arts.",sp=0},{t="Mistress of Binding",b="Veteran conjurers know Menara as an authority on orbs that imprison and harness demonic spirits. She works with intricate reagents and guides apprentices through demanding rituals to make enchanted attire and binding implements. Her skill is known as far as Ironforge and the Undercity, and senior warlocks across Azeroth send their most promising students across the sea to seek her counsel.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Marsh",b="Menara Voidrender shares an old history with Tabetha, a hermit mage living in deep isolation in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh. Tabetha pursues the arcane, while Menara studies fel bindings and demonology. When powerful relics such as the Orb of Orahil need restoration or special knowledge, their shared past bridges the wilderness of Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Menara Voidrender?",a="Menara Voidrender is a human warlock in Ratchet, the neutral port in the Barrens. She instructs developing warlocks in crafting rituals and demon-binding sorcery.",al={"who is menara","menara voidrender lore","who is the warlock in ratchet"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a human warlock living in the Barrens?",a="Ratchet gives Menara neutrality and distance from the watchful eyes of major governments. From the goblin port, she practices forbidden arts and teaches students from both factions without interference from paladins, mages, or city guards.",al={"why is menara in ratchet","why is she in the barrens","why ratchet warlock"},it="why_here"},{q="What kind of magic does Menara specialize in?",a="Menara specializes in demonology, enchanted dark fabrics, and vessels that trap demonic entities. She is especially known for creating and restoring binding orbs such as the Orb of Orahil.",al={"what does menara teach","menara voidrender powers","what is menara good at"},it="power"},{q="What is Menara's connection to Tabetha?",a="Menara and Tabetha share a past connection. Tabetha lives in seclusion in Dustwallow Marsh and practices traditional wizardry; warlocks seeking knowledge of the Orb of Orahil find that the two women know each other's talents.",al={"menara and tabetha","how does she know tabetha","tabetha connection"},it="ties"},{q="Does Menara favor the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Menara operates neutrally from Ratchet. She teaches and offers crafting work to capable, ambitious warlocks from both the Alliance and the Horde who can handle fel energies.",al={"is menara alliance or horde","menara faction","who does menara work for"},it="side"},{q="What major artifacts does she help create?",a="Menara guides apprentices in weaving the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe, a garment imbued with demonic power. She also helps advanced practitioners recover and assemble components for the Orb of Orahil.",al={"menara quests","what does she make","enchanted gold bloodrobe menara"}},{q="What does Menara Voidrender want?",a="Menara seeks to tutor aspiring warlocks who show enough promise and ambition to seek her out. She is dedicated to crafting and perfecting specialized dark artifacts, such as binding orbs and enchanted robes, and relies on capable practitioners to gather the rare, dangerous reagents needed to complete them.",al={"menara voidrender goals","what does menara want","menara voidrender purpose"},it="wants",add="63c53201"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can learn from Menara, who teaches practitioners from both factions to forge enchanted robes and bind demons into focus orbs.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Menara pursuing the dark arts in neutral territory, away from Stormwind's catacombs and kingdom loyalties.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can learn how Menara combines advanced tailoring materials with fel reagents to weave durable vestments that channel demonic power."},kw={"barrens","bloodrobe","demonology","menara","orahil","ratchet","tabetha","voidrender","warlock"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","quest:4736","quest:1796","npc:tabetha","zone:barrens","zone:ironforge"},src={"Menara Voidrender"}}
E["npc:monte-gazlowe"] = {t="npc",n="Monte Gazlowe",z="barrens",s="At Ratchet, Monte Gazlowe keeps a neutral port open to traders from every side. He founded the town with the fortune he earned as the Horde’s chief engineer during the building of Durotar and Orgrimmar.",h="At Ratchet, Monte Gazlowe keeps a neutral port open to traders from every side.",sec={{t="The Mastermind of Ratchet",b="At Ratchet, Monte Gazlowe runs a port where rivals can trade under the Steamwheedle Cartel. He founded the town on the barren coast after earning a handsome payday for his engineering work with the new Horde. Horde, Alliance, and independent traders may barter there, so long as they keep their weapons sheathed and their purses heavy.",sp=0},{t="Engineer for the Horde",b="After the Third War, Warchief Thrall hired Monte Gazlowe as Durotar’s chief engineer to solve urgent problems for the new orc capital. Gazlowe took on the dangerous work of securing freshwater for Orgrimmar. His tunnels broke into underground kobold dens, but the wandering beastmaster Rexxar arrived in time to help blast the caverns shut. Gazlowe finished his assignments and remains a favored contractor and friend to Thrall. He has even sent his foreman, Rezlak, to keep helping with orc construction across Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Trouble on the Merchant Coast",b="Trade brings good earnings to Ratchet, but maritime rivals and thieves trouble Monte Gazlowe’s business. The Southsea Freebooters have camps along the nearby Merchant Coast, where they seize cargo bound for Ratchet and steal goods from raw ore to Gazlowe’s custom-ordered boots. To protect his profits, the port boss often hires passing sellswords of any allegiance to clear pirate camps, recover stolen shipments, and settle scores with troublemakers at the docks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gazlowe?",a="Monte Gazlowe runs Ratchet, the main trading port on the Barrens coast. He made his fortune as the chief engineer overseeing Orgrimmar’s construction, then founded Ratchet as an open, neutral harbor under the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"who is monte gazlowe","gazlowe lore","ratchet boss"},it="identity"},{q="Is Gazlowe loyal to the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Monte Gazlowe operates Ratchet under the Steamwheedle Cartel and opens its docks to Alliance and Horde travelers. He also shares a close bond and a profitable history with Warchief Thrall, having engineered key parts of Durotar’s settlements.",al={"is gazlowe horde","is ratchet neutral","gazlowe faction"},it="side"},{q="What did Gazlowe build in Durotar?",a="During Durotar’s founding, Warchief Thrall hired Monte Gazlowe as his chief engineer. Gazlowe oversaw tunnels dug to find an underground water supply for Orgrimmar. When the miners unleashed hostile kobolds, Gazlowe hired Rexxar to help sappers seal the tunnels.",al={"gazlowe orgrimmar","gazlowe thal","gazlowe water supply"},it="fame"},{q="Why is Gazlowe hiring adventurers in Ratchet?",a="Monte Gazlowe hires private muscle against the Southsea Freebooters, who camp along the Merchant Coast and plunder cargo meant for Ratchet’s docks. He pays bounty hunters to eliminate the pirates, recover stolen cargo manifests, and retrieve missing shipments.",al={"gazlowe quests","southsea freebooters ratchet","gazlowe problems"},it="wants"},{q="What is Gazlowe's connection to the Mirage Raceway?",a="Monte Gazlowe is an avid admirer of engineering and speed. He sponsors goblin teams racing gnomes in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles, helped build their racing rig, and is trying to find prototype fuel regulators.",al={"gazlowe shimmering flats","gazlowe thousand needles","gazlowe racing"}},{q="Why is Gazlowe in Ratchet?",a="After earning a fortune helping Thrall build Orgrimmar, Gazlowe invested his profits into founding Ratchet. Situated at the mouth of the Southfury River on the Barrens coast, it serves as the premier neutral trading port in Kalimdor for the Steamwheedle Cartel, letting him oversee maritime commerce, regional engineering ventures, and lucrative contracts across the continent.",al={"why did gazlowe come to ratchet","why is gazlowe here","gazlowe ratchet purpose"},it="why_here",add="cabfa558"},{q="Who are Gazlowe's main allies and business partners?",a="Gazlowe maintains close ties with Warchief Thrall and the Horde, having served as their chief engineer during Durotar's founding. Within the Steamwheedle Cartel, he deals with Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay. He also sponsors the goblin racing team at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats.",al={"gazlowe allies","who is gazlowe tied to","gazlowe connections","gazlowe partners"},it="ties",add="0afdf6f5"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Gazlowe asks for your coin like any goblin, yet he has been a steadfast ally of Thrall since the Third War. He helped dig the foundations of your capital.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gazlowe cares little for Stormwind’s throne or the quarrels you bring from the Eastern Kingdoms. Ratchet welcomes you if your gold is real and your blade stays sheathed.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gazlowe is one of Kalimdor’s leading goblin engineers. He coordinates projects from city water grids to high-speed racing rigs at the Mirage Raceway.",["race:Orc"]="Orgrimmar’s water supply came from tunnels dug by Gazlowe’s sappers. He still stations goblin mechanics in Durotar to help with heavy construction."},kw={"barrens","durotar","freebooters","gazlowe","monte","orgrimmar","pozzik","ratchet","steamwheedle"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","npc:thrall","topic:steamwheedle-cartel","quest:887","quest:890","npc:rezlak","subzone:mirage-raceway","quest:959"},src={"Monte Gazlowe"}}
E["npc:mupsi-shacklefridd"] = {t="npc",n="Mupsi Shacklefridd",z="barrens",s="Outside Ratchet in the Barrens, Mupsi Shacklefridd helps travelers repair ties with the Steamwheedle Cartel.",h="Outside Ratchet in the Barrens, Mupsi Shacklefridd helps travelers repair ties with the Steamwheedle Cartel.",sec={{t="On the Outskirts of Ratchet",b="Mupsi Shacklefridd works along the coastal road just outside Ratchet. Steamwheedle guards patrol the port town's edge as merchants come and go. Travelers on poor terms with the goblins can seek a way back into the cartel's good graces through Mupsi, if they bring the supplies and labor it demands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mupsi Shacklefridd?",a="Mupsi Shacklefridd is a goblin stationed just outside Ratchet in the Barrens. She helps travelers restore their standing with the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"mupsi","who is mupsi","ratchet mupsi"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find her?",a="You can find Mupsi just outside Ratchet in the Barrens, where port guards and patrols sometimes pass by.",al={"mupsi location","where is mupsi shacklefridd","find mupsi"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why would someone talk to Mupsi Shacklefridd?",a="If you have angered the Steamwheedle Cartel, Mupsi can help you repair your reputation with supplies. This often follows trouble with goblins or siding with pirates.",al={"mending old wounds ratchet","ratchet reputation turn in","mupsi quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Mupsi Shacklefridd on?",a="Mupsi Shacklefridd aligns with the Steamwheedle Cartel, operating under the port authority of Ratchet. Like most goblins in the settlement, she maintains business neutrality toward both the Alliance and the Horde, prioritizing commerce, materials, and coin over political warfare.",al={"mupsi shacklefridd faction","who does mupsi work for","is mupsi shacklefridd neutral"},it="side",add="8798c45f"},{q="What does Mupsi Shacklefridd want?",a="Mupsi is seeking help for the many sailors wounded in an encounter with the Bloodsail Buccaneers, offering individuals a chance to earn favor and mend strained standing with the Steamwheedle Cartel by bringing linen cloth for bandages and empty vials for potions.",al={"what does mupsi want","mupsi shacklefridd motive","why help mupsi"},it="wants",add="a81ff16f"},{q="Why is Mupsi Shacklefridd stationed outside Ratchet?",a="She is stationed along the outskirts of Ratchet to handle outreach and logistics for travelers approaching the busy port. Operating just beyond the central docks allows her to intercept traders, outcasts, and adventurers who need to barter supplies or repair their relations with the cartel.",al={"why is mupsi here","mupsi shacklefridd location reason","why is mupsi outside ratchet"},it="why_here",add="8b7e7b21"}},kw={"barrens","goblin","mupsi","ratchet","reputation","shacklefridd","steamwheedle"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:goblin"},src={"Mupsi Shacklefridd"}}
E["npc:ruga-ragetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Ruga Ragetotem",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Ruga Ragetotem trains warriors for the Horde. He tests them against the silithid in the southern Barrens before sending the proven toward custom armor.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Ruga Ragetotem trains warriors for the Horde.",sec={{t="A Mentor in Camp Taurajo",b="At Camp Taurajo, Ruga Ragetotem trains warriors who want to prove their strength in Kalimdor. Silithid have suddenly appeared to the south, carving hives into the Field of Giants. Ruga sends young fighters to hunt the insectoids and cut off their antennae. Those who endure the trial earn his respect and a recommendation to Thun'grim Firegaze, a renowned armorsmith.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ruga Ragetotem?",a="Ruga Ragetotem trains warriors at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He tests fighters who hope to prove themselves to the Horde.",al={"who is ruga","ruga ragetotem lore","ruga taurajo"},it="identity"},{q="What trial does Ruga give to warriors?",a="Ruga sends warriors south to the Field of Giants to fight the newly emerged silithid. They must slay the aggressive insectoids and bring back their antennae to prove their bravery and skill in battle.",al={"ruga trial","trial at the field of giants","what does ruga want"},it="wants"},{q="Who does Ruga send you to after his trial?",a="After a warrior proves themselves against the silithid, Ruga sends them north to Thun'grim Firegaze, an orc armorsmith who crafts specialized armor for worthy fighters.",al={"where after ruga","ruga next quest","thun'grim ruga"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Ruga interested in the Field of Giants?",a="Silithid have recently invaded the Field of Giants, carving hives into the earth. Ruga uses the nearby threat to test warriors who may defend the Horde.",al={"why field of giants","ruga bugs","silithid taurajo"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Ruga Ragetotem on?",a="Ruga Ragetotem stands firmly with the Horde and his fellow tauren. Stationed in Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, he aids young warriors proving their mettle for the Horde's cause, testing their courage against emerging threats in Kalimdor.",al={"ruga ragetotem faction","who does ruga fight for","is ruga horde"},it="side",add="561e0961"},{q="Why is Ruga Ragetotem here in Camp Taurajo?",a="Ruga makes his camp at Taurajo to keep watch over the southern Barrens and test promising Horde warriors. From here, he monitors dangerous incursions like the silithid swarming near the Field of Giants, sending proven fighters to confront the threat before sending them onward.",al={"why is ruga in camp taurajo","ruga ragetotem location why","why is ruga in the barrens"},it="why_here",add="97d42651"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face the silithid to prove your skill before Ruga sends you to Thun'grim Firegaze for forged armor.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you find Ruga Ragetotem at Camp Taurajo, guarding the southern ranges with the strength and vigilance of the Earthmother's children."},kw={"camp taurajo","field of giants","ruga ragetotem","silithid","taurajo","thun'grim firegaze","warrior trial"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:field-of-giants","quest:1824","quest:1825","quest:1502","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},src={"Ruga Ragetotem"}}
E["npc:sputtervalve"] = {t="npc",n="Sputtervalve",z="barrens",s="Under pressure in Ratchet, Sputtervalve races to finish shredder research for the Tinkers' Union. Director Riddlevox holds him to crushing deadlines, and he hires adventurers to steal designs from the rival Venture Company.",h="Under pressure in Ratchet, Sputtervalve races to finish shredder research for the Tinkers' Union.",sec={{t="Industrial Pressure",b="In Ratchet, Sputtervalve answers to Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union. The goblin engineer oversees shredder development and has found the work brutal. Modern mechanization moves fast, the Venture Company presses hard, and his own prototypes are few. With the deadline closing in, Sputtervalve fears admitting failure to the Union. He turns to a familiar goblin practice: stealing better designs from those who built them first.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Venture Company",b="The Venture Company's drilling operation at the Sludge Fen, to the northwest, is Sputtervalve's chief target. Its latest shredders have interchangeable hands, refined control grips, and advanced inner workings, including the elusive samophlange. Sputtervalve sent his associate Wizzlecrank into the Fen for field research, but Wizzlecrank became trapped. Now Sputtervalve hires wandering mercenaries to recover the stolen technology and rescue his partner.",sp=0},{t="A Fixer in Ratchet",b="Sputtervalve also helps with strange curiosities that pass through the Barrens. Adventurers sometimes bring him bizarre artifacts infused with corruption from the Wailing Caverns, such as a glowing shard. He knows the local landscape well enough to point them away from machinery and toward the isolated druids encamped above the caverns.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin engineer in Ratchet and a member of the Tinkers' Union. Director Riddlevox put him in charge of shredder research and development, and he scrambles to meet the strict deadlines.",al={"who is sputtervalve","sputtervalve ratchet","sputtervalve lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Sputtervalve targeting the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company is building advanced shredders at the Sludge Fen, with interchangeable hands and refined control grips. Unable to match their designs, Sputtervalve turns to espionage to steal their plans and machinery.",al={"why attack venture co","sputtervalve sludge fen","sputtervalve venture company"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a samophlange?",a="A samophlange is an advanced mechanism found inside Venture Company shredders. Sputtervalve hires adventurers to retrieve and examine one so he can learn their technology.",al={"what is a samophlange","samophlange quest","what does samophlange do"},it="item"},{q="Who is Wizzlecrank?",a="Wizzlecrank is Sputtervalve's associate and operative. Sent into the Sludge Fen for field research, Wizzlecrank became trapped, so Sputtervalve hires help to recover him and the stolen technology.",al={"wizzlecrank","who is wizzlecrank","sputtervalve partner"},sp=1},{q="Why does Sputtervalve care about the Glowing Shard?",a="Sputtervalve does not study organic curiosities, but he knows the Barrens well. When shown the shard recovered from the Wailing Caverns, he directs adventurers to the druids encamped above the caves.",al={"the glowing shard sputtervalve","glowing shard wailing caverns","shard quest ratchet"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Director Riddlevox?",a="Director Riddlevox leads the Tinkers' Union. He put Sputtervalve in charge of shredder innovation and holds him to strict production deadlines.",al={"riddlevox","director riddlevox","tinkers union boss"},it="leader"},{q="Whose side is Sputtervalve on?",a="Sputtervalve answers to the Tinkers' Union and operates out of the neutral goblin port of Ratchet. While he remains neutral toward travelers of all stripes, his primary allegiances and business interests are tied strictly to goblin enterprise and his Union superiors rather than the Horde or Alliance.",al={"sputtervalve faction","who does sputtervalve work for","is sputtervalve horde"},it="side",add="8cc08011"},{q="What does Sputtervalve want?",a="Sputtervalve desperately needs to meet a tight engineering deadline imposed by Director Riddlevox. Because his own shredder designs have stalled, he wants to steal schematics and components—particularly from the superior models fielded by the Venture Company at the Sludge Fen—to salvage his research and keep his job.",al={"what is sputtervalve trying to do","sputtervalve goal","sputtervalve shredder plans"},it="wants",add="a7196ac5"},{q="Why is Sputtervalve in Ratchet?",a="Sputtervalve is stationed in Ratchet to oversee shredder development and research for the Tinkers' Union. The port's proximity to the Sludge Fen provides him with an ideal vantage point to monitor rival engineers and deploy operatives to swipe industrial secrets from the nearby Venture Company operations.",al={"why is sputtervalve here","sputtervalve barrens why","sputtervalve ratchet location"},it="why_here",add="a4a50e43"},{q="Who is Sputtervalve tied to?",a="Sputtervalve reports directly to Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union. In the field, he works closely with his partner Wizzlecrank, whom he sent into the Sludge Fen to steal Venture Company prototypes, and relies on willing adventurers to make contact with local informants across the Barrens.",al={"sputtervalve connections","who does sputtervalve know","sputtervalve partners"},it="ties",add="dc6c348a"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Sputtervalve shows the ruthless side of goblin engineering: when invention stalls, take the schematics from a rival.",["faction:Horde"]="Ratchet is neutral, but Sputtervalve depends on Horde travelers crossing the Barrens to disrupt Venture Company operations and smuggle machine parts."},kw={"ratchet","riddlevox","samophlange","shredder","sludge fen","sputtervalve","tinkers union","venture company","wizzlecrank"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","subzone:sludge-fen","topic:venture-company","quest:894","quest:114","quest:6981","zone:barrens","zone:wailing"},src={"Sputtervalve"}}
E["npc:strahad-farsan"] = {t="npc",n="Strahad Farsan",z="barrens",s="Above Ratchet, Strahad Farsan teaches warlocks to bind demons. The human warlock lives in a stone tower in the Barrens, beyond the reach of ordinary Alliance and Horde politics. Students of fel magic come from Stormwind, Orgrimmar, and the Undercity to learn from him.",h="Above Ratchet, Strahad Farsan teaches warlocks to bind demons.",sec={{t="The Tower Above Ratchet",b="Strahad Farsan keeps to a stone tower on the bluffs above Ratchet. The goblin port's neutral ground lets him practice dangerous summonings away from Alliance magistrates and Horde shamans. His acolytes gather around him as he studies the Twisting Nether, apart from the struggles over territory below.",sp=0},{t="Master of Demonic Binding",b="Strahad learned the danger of demonic binding firsthand. His first attempt to bind a felhunter nearly cost him his life, leaving him cautious and exacting. Despite being human, he has earned the respect of Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind and demonic scholars in the Undercity and Orgrimmar. Warlocks of either faction seeking to command felhunters or fiery steeds are sent to his tower.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Strahad Farsan?",a="Strahad Farsan teaches warlocks in a stone tower above Ratchet. He is part of the inner circle of Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind, and warlocks of both factions seek his skill in demonic summoning.",al={"strahad lore","who is strahad","strahad farsan info"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a human warlock living in the Barrens?",a="Strahad lives above Ratchet, a neutral port run by the Steamwheedle Cartel. The bluffs let him perform dangerous summoning rituals beyond the laws of the Alliance and the watch of the Horde.",al={"why is strahad in ratchet","human in the barrens","strahad location"},it="why_here"},{q="Why do Horde warlocks visit Strahad?",a="Strahad's skill with demons draws warlocks from the Horde. Mentors in Orgrimmar and the Undercity recognize his knowledge of binding demons such as felhunters and send promising pupils across the sea to study with him.",al={"horde visiting strahad","can horde talk to strahad","why do orcs go to strahad"}},{q="What happened to Strahad when he summoned his first felhunter?",a="Strahad's first attempt to bind a felhunter nearly cost him his life. He barely survived, and the ordeal taught him the precision needed to subdue such magic-consuming predators.",al={"strahad felhunter encounter","strahad backstory felhunter"},it="history"},{q="Is Strahad related to Godrick Farsan?",a="Strahad and Godrick Farsan share the uncommon surname Farsan, which suggests a family connection. Strahad says nothing about family and remains devoted to his dark craft.",al={"godrick farsan connection","godrick farsan relative","is strahad related to godrick"}},{q="Who are the acolytes around his tower?",a="Strahad's acolytes include Magaz, Fenrick, and Wytula. They help maintain protective wards, prepare summoning circles, and tend to the tower's rituals.",al={"strahad acolytes","acolytes in tower ratchet"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Strahad Farsan on?",a="Strahad remains strictly neutral, operating outside the political squabbles of the Alliance and Horde. Residing above the goblin port of Ratchet, he deals equally with practitioners from both factions. His allegiance lies with dark sorcery and his fellow practitioners rather than the flags of Stormwind or Orgrimmar.",al={"strahad farsan faction","is strahad alliance or horde","strahad allegiance"},it="side",add="b2638750"},{q="What does Strahad Farsan want?",a="Strahad seeks to advance the boundaries of demonic summoning and test the mettle of fellow practitioners. He tests and guides ambitious warlocks who seek to master formidable entities like felhunters, ensuring they possess the resolve and knowledge to bind creatures that once nearly took his own life.",al={"what does strahad want","strahad farsan goal","strahad motive"},it="wants",add="62896d38"},{q="Who is Strahad Farsan tied to?",a="Strahad is a prominent member of Gakin the Darkbinder's inner circle, maintaining close ties with fellow masters of the shadow across the world. In his tower above Ratchet, he oversees his own acolytes—Magaz, Fenrick, and Wytula—while training promising summoners sent to him by mentors from Ironforge, Stormwind, Orgrimmar, and the Undercity.",al={"strahad farsan connections","who does strahad work with","strahad allies"},it="ties",add="a370ddda"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can learn from Strahad how to bind felhunters and summon steeds from the Nether.",["faction:Horde"]="Though born to the Alliance, Strahad deals with Horde practitioners in neutral Ratchet.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gakin the Darkbinder sends Alliance warlocks from the crypts of the Slaughtered Lamb to Kalimdor to study under Strahad.",["race:Human"]="As a human, Strahad shows that masters of the dark arts seek greater power beyond Stormwind."},kw={"barrens","cabal","farsan","felhunter","gakin","ratchet","strahad","summoner","warlock"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","npc:menara-voidrender","quest:1471","quest:1758","quest:1798","npc:godrick-farsan"},src={"Strahad Farsan"}}
E["npc:takar-the-seer"] = {t="npc",n="Takar the Seer",z="barrens",s="East of Camp Taurajo, Takar the Seer keeps a lone camp in the Barrens. Though surrounded by Horde lands, he remains loyal to the Alliance and shares occult knowledge with certain travelers.",h="East of Camp Taurajo, Takar the Seer keeps a lone camp in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Recluse in the Savannah",b="Takar the Seer lives alone beneath a simple tent east of Camp Taurajo. Tauren braves and orc patrols watch the surrounding Barrens, yet leave his remote clearing undisturbed. He distrusts curious Horde visitors but rarely starts a fight, keeping watch on the horizon and to himself. His camp lies far from Stormwind's politics.",sp=0},{t="Occult Counsel",b="Takar the Seer shares his knowledge with a few visitors from beyond his camp. Alliance warlocks who come from the Eastern Kingdoms seek his cryptic counsel when they try to bind dangerous beings from beyond this world. His understanding of hidden forces and the craft of souls draws these practitioners to his remote, perilous camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a human seer living alone in the Barrens?",a="Takar has never said why he lives alone. His camp lies east of Camp Taurajo, far from any Alliance outpost, and warlocks visit for his knowledge of demons rather than his story.",al={"why is takar in the barrens","what is takar doing here","takar backstory"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Takar hostile to Horde players?",a="Yes. Takar is aligned with the Alliance, so Horde adventurers find him hostile. He rarely attacks unless provoked or approached too closely.",al={"is takar friendly","can horde talk to takar","takar horde reaction"},it="hostile"},{q="What brings Alliance adventurers to his camp?",a="Alliance seekers, especially warlocks, come to Takar for guidance in binding powerful demons such as the Succubus. He offers cryptic instructions and insight into the reagents needed to summon and dominate them.",al={"takar quests","why visit takar","who talks to takar"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Takar the Seer?",a="Takar the Seer is a solitary human mystic dwelling far from human settlements in the heart of Kalimdor. Camped in the dry wilderness east of Camp Taurajo, he maintains a quiet vigil in the Barrens despite being surrounded by lands claimed by the Horde and native tribes.",al={"who is takar","who is takar the seer","takar identity"},it="identity",add="e39a8e5b"},{q="Whose side is Takar the Seer on?",a="Takar remains loyal to the Alliance. Though he resides far from friendly outposts and deep within Horde territory, he welcomes Alliance travelers who seek him out while regarding passing Horde champions with cold hostility.",al={"is takar alliance","takar alliance or horde","takar faction"},it="side",add="bed67aa2"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As an Alliance warlock, you can turn to Takar in Kalimdor for guidance through the dangerous rites that summon and bind a succubus to your service.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find a friendly human far within Horde territory, though Takar keeps to his solitary camp in central Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens hermit","camp taurajo","devourer of souls","heartswood","succubus quest","takar the seer"},rel={"quest:1472","quest:1738","zone:barrens","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Takar the Seer"}}
E["npc:tatternack-steelforge"] = {t="npc",n="Tatternack Steelforge",z="barrens",s="On the Barrens frontier, Tatternack Steelforge offers work to travelers who can handle raw metal and dangerous wildlife. The orc smith studies local ores and seeks to arm Horde forces against threats across the plains.",h="On the Barrens frontier, Tatternack Steelforge offers work to travelers who can handle raw metal and...",sec={{t="An Orc at the Forge",b="Across the Barrens, Horde outposts need weapons to face wild beasts, centaur raiders, and hostile quilboar. Tatternack Steelforge brings his people's metalworking knowledge to the frontier. He seeks practical weapons and unusual geological specimens to strengthen the Horde's foothold against those threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tatternack Steelforge?",a="Tatternack Steelforge is an orc weaponsmith stationed in the Barrens. He helps supply Horde defenders by inspecting minerals, studying local ores, and putting reliable weapons into nearby warriors' hands.",al={"who is tatternack","tatternack steelforge lore","what does tatternack do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Tatternack Steelforge be found?",a="Tatternack operates in the Barrens, residing among Horde camps along the central savanna trails.",al={"where is tatternack","tatternack steelforge location","tatternack coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of tasks does Tatternack offer?",a="Tatternack asks travelers to recover weapons and bring him fresh ore samples from around the Barrens for his forging work.",al={"tatternack quests","weapons of choice quest giver","ore sample quest"},it="purpose",gp=true}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="For smiths traveling through the Barrens, Tatternack understands the need for good ore and quality steel in a lawless borderland.",["faction:Horde"]="Tatternack helps keep Horde forces armed and supplied against threats such as quilboar and centaur."},kw={"barrens","blacksmith","camp taurajo","crossroads","ore","steelforge","tatternack"},rel={"quest:893","quest:1153","subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},src={"Tatternack Steelforge"}}
E["npc:thork"] = {t="npc",n="Thork",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Thork keeps watch over the settlement’s defenses. He sends Horde adventurers against raiders and works to keep supply routes open.",h="At the Crossroads, Thork keeps watch over the settlement’s defenses.",sec={{t="Commander of the Crossroads",b="Thork commands the defenses at the Crossroads, where roads link Durotar, Mulgore, and lands beyond. The town faces threats from every side. Quilboar raids, centaur attacks, and harpies on the prowl stretch his forces thin. Thork calls on capable travelers to meet dangers his guards cannot handle alone.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borders",b="Thork’s watch reaches beyond the Crossroads walls. He sends scouts and messengers north to the Mor’shan Rampart, where they report to Kadrak. The northern and eastern routes carry supplies through the Barrens. Keeping those roads open sustains the Horde’s presence across the scrublands.",sp=0},{t="Threats Inside and Out",b="Thork thanks travelers who strike at the leaders behind the Razormane raids. Mangletooth, a captive quilboar, betrays his tribe by helping them attack its leaders. When travelers bring Lok Orcbane’s head to the Crossroads, Thork thanks them for weakening the assaults on Horde supply routes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thork?",a="Thork commands the Crossroads defenses in the Barrens. He organizes the town’s protection and works to keep supply caravans safe.",al={"thork lore","who is thork","thork crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Thork located?",a="Thork stands outside near the center of the Crossroads, coordinating guards and giving defense orders.",al={"thork location","find thork","where is thork standing"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Crossroads so vulnerable to attack?",a="The Crossroads lies at an open meeting of major trade routes in the Barrens, with little stone fortification. Hostile Razormane quilboar, Kolkar centaur, and Alliance scouts threaten its borders, so the settlement needs constant watch.",al={"crossroads under attack","why crossroads dangerous"}},{q="What is Thork's relationship with Mankrik?",a="When Mankrik asked for soldiers to hunt quilboar and search for his lost wife, Thork refused. His limited troops had to guard the outpost and its supply caravans.",al={"mankrik and thork","did thork help mankrik"}},{q="How does Thork coordinate with other Horde posts?",a="Thork sends messengers and fighters to Kadrak at the Mor’shan Rampart to report on the northern border and watch Ashenvale’s border.",al={"thork and kadrak","thork morshan rampart"}},{q="What threats does Thork deal with?",a="Thork faces marauding quilboar warbands that disrupt trade and steal supply crates. He also thanks travelers who defeat the leaders behind the raids.",al={"crossroads enemies","thork quests info"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Thork on?",a="Thork is a steadfast officer of Thrall's Horde. Stationed in the heart of Kalimdor, he commands the local defenses of the Crossroads to secure vital supply routes, shield arriving travelers, and safeguard orcish and tauren holdings across the central Barrens.",al={"thork faction","thork horde or alliance","who does thork serve"},it="side",add="3a5917fe"},{q="What does Thork want?",a="Thork wants security for the Crossroads. His focus is on maintaining order, keeping supply caravans flowing safely across the arid plains, and repelling hostile raiders who threaten the settlement's survival.",al={"thork goal","what is thork trying to do","thork objective"},it="wants",add="0b2cf0f5"},{q="Why is Thork here?",a="The Crossroads serves as the vital junction connecting Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern frontiers. Thork was appointed to lead the defenses of this vulnerable hub, coordinating patrols, marshaling arriving champions, and ensuring the trade veins of the young Horde do not collapse under constant wilderness raids.",al={"why is thork at the crossroads","thork duty barrens","why was thork posted here"},it="why_here",add="56f2bf7a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="If you come from Durotar or Mulgore as a member of the Horde, reporting to Thork is an important step in proving yourself a protector of Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the hard duty of defending the Horde’s newly conquered lands in Kalimdor from hostile neighbors.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can value Thork’s focus on supply routes, sound patrols, and stopping physical threats before they reach the town walls."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","kadrak","mankrik","mor'shan","orc","supplies","thork"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:854","quest:871","quest:872","quest:879","quest:5041","npc:kadrak"},src={"Thork"}}
E["npc:tonga-runetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Tonga Runetotem",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem watches the Barrens' oases grow sick. Sent from Thunder Bluff, the tauren druid studies a corruption harming the region's wildlife and seeks its source before the fragile ecosystem fails.",h="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem watches the Barrens' oases grow sick.",sec={{t="Watcher at the Crossroads",b="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem studies the Barrens' changing land. His elders in Thunder Bluff sent him from Mulgore, and he knows the dry savannah well. Where travelers see scrub and predators, Tonga watches for signs of the land's health. Lately, those signs have turned troubling. He seeks travelers who can help him investigate the scattered oases, the heart of life across the savannah.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Waters and Warped Beasts",b="Water is scarce in the Barrens, and the Forgotten Pools and Stagnant Oasis have turned volatile. Strange magical vapors bubble up, and creatures that drink from the waters are changing into aggressive, unnatural forms. Tonga gathers plant and creature samples to learn whether the sickness comes from natural decay or an outside power. His findings point toward deep fissures beneath the ground, linking the poisoned pools to the passages of the Wailing Caverns.",sp=1},{t="The Runetotem Lineage",b="Tonga bears the Runetotem clan name and the druidic heritage championed by Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. Hamuul keeps ties with the Cenarion Circle and studies in Moonglade's sacred groves, while scouts like Tonga serve on the frontier. Tonga draws on Moonglade's botanical wisdom to prepare healing salves and counter poisons. His work puts the young tauren druidic tradition to use within the fledgling Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tonga Runetotem?",a="Tonga Runetotem is a tauren druid near the inn at the Crossroads in the Barrens. His elders in Thunder Bluff sent him to investigate strange corruption spreading across the savannah.",al={"tonga runetotem","who is tonga","crossroads druid"},it="identity"},{q="What is Tonga investigating in the Barrens?",a="Tonga investigates strange vapors, mutated beasts, and tainted waters in the Barrens' oases, including the Forgotten Pools and the Stagnant Oasis.",al={"what is tonga doing","tonga quest goal","why investigate oases"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Tonga believe the corruption is coming from?",a="Tonga's study of altered creatures and water fissures leads him to believe the magical taint comes from deep underground in the Wailing Caverns.",al={"source of oasis corruption","where is the taint from","wailing caverns connection"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Is Tonga related to Hamuul Runetotem?",a="Tonga and Hamuul Runetotem share the Runetotem name, but whether they are related is unknown. Tonga sends word of the Barrens' troubles to Archdruid Hamuul, the elder druid on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise.",al={"is he related to hamuul","runetotem family","hamuul relation"},it="ties"},{q="What does Tonga do for the poisoned wildlife?",a="Tonga uses teachings from Moonglade and local reagents to prepare salves for poisoned gazelles and counter toxins from sources such as Dreadmist Peak.",al={"gazelle cure","tonga curing sick","dreadmist peak poison"}},{q="Why is Tonga stationed at the Crossroads instead of Camp Taurajo or Thunder Bluff?",a="The Crossroads sits at the northern Barrens' central hub, close to the affected oases. From there, Tonga can reach travelers able to venture into dangerous country for him.",al={"why crossroads","why is tonga here"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Tonga Runetotem on?",a="Tonga stands firmly with the Horde and his fellow tauren of Thunder Bluff. Dispatched directly by his people's leadership, he works to heal the land and safeguard travelers passing through the Crossroads, cooperating closely with druidic allies from Moonglade to protect the balance of nature in Kalimdor.",al={"tonga runetotem faction","who does tonga serve","is tonga runetotem horde"},it="side",add="5ac3f48e"},{q="What does Tonga Runetotem want?",a="Tonga seeks to uncover and purge the unnatural taint spreading through the Barrens' water sources. He enlists capable adventurers to inspect the local oases, sample mutated flora and fauna, and administer remedies to poisoned wildlife, striving to halt the corruption before it completely ravages the surrounding territory.",al={"what does tonga want","tonga runetotem goal","tonga runetotem purpose"},it="wants",add="8af7bcfa"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid learning your craft, you can see how Cenarion teachings help diagnose and cleanse blighted lands far from Moonglade.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share Tonga's duty to the Earth Mother as he works to protect the scarce waters that sustain life across the dry plains.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on Tonga's study to help keep the Barrens' main road habitable and safe from magical threats below ground."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","druid","forgotten pools","oases","runetotem","stagnant oasis","tonga","wailing caverns"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:886","quest:870","quest:877","zone:wailing","quest:1489","topic:tauren"},src={"Tonga Runetotem"}}
E["npc:ula-elek"] = {t="npc",n="Ula'elek",z="barrens",s="In Sen'jin Village, Ula'elek works armor for warriors across the Horde. The Darkspear smith joins forces with Thun'grim Firegaze, shaping specialized gear from traditional troll craft and trophies gathered across Kalimdor.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Ula'elek works armor for warriors across the Horde.",sec={{t="Smith of the Darkspear",b="Ula'elek is a skilled armorsmith serving the Darkspear in Sen'jin Village. Nearby quilboar and sea crawlers threaten the coastal settlement, so the tribe needs sturdy armor and working blades. Ula'elek's skill also draws seasoned warriors from across the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Forging the Brutal Armor",b="Young warriors who visit Thun'grim Firegaze at his overlook in the Barrens are sent south to Sen'jin Village. The veteran trusts Ula'elek to forge Brutal Gauntlets for battle-hardened fighters. To make them, Ula'elek calls for rare materials, especially swollen, uncloven hooves from the satyrs draining the forest's magic in northeastern Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a Darkspear troll armorsmith in Sen'jin Village. Horde veterans trust him to forge specialized armor for promising frontline fighters.",al={"who is ula'elek","ula'elek lore","ulaelek background"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Ula'elek be found?",a="Ula'elek can be found in Sen'jin Village, on Durotar's southeastern coast, south of Razor Hill.",al={"ula'elek location","where is ula'elek","find ulaelek"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze send warriors to Ula'elek?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze sends warriors to Ula'elek because he trusts the troll smith to make Brutal Gauntlets for warriors who have earned the veteran's respect.",al={"thungrim and ulaelek","why go to ula'elek"},it="motive"},{q="What materials does Ula'elek need to make the gauntlets?",a="Ula'elek requires warriors to hunt satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale and harvest their swollen, uncloven hooves for the Brutal Gauntlets.",al={"ula'elek materials","brutal gauntlets ingredients"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What kind of gear does Ula'elek craft?",a="Ula'elek specializes in heavy combat armor. He makes the Brutal Gauntlets, part of the Brutal Armor set for promising Horde warriors.",al={"what does ula'elek make","ula'elek rewards"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do the gauntlets require satyr hooves?",a="Satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale drain the forest's magic, and the most potent among them have swollen, uncloven hooves. Ula'elek draws that power from the hooves and puts it into the gauntlets.",al={"why satyr hooves","hooves for gauntlets"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Ula'elek on?",a="Ula'elek is a Darkspear troll loyal to the Horde. Based out of Sen'jin Village on the coast of Durotar, he plies his craft for the benefit of Horde champions, partnering with orcish smiths like Thun'grim Firegaze to forge sturdy armor for warriors who defend their shared lands.",al={"ulaelek faction","is ulaelek horde","ulaelek allegiance"},it="side",add="3fd6027c"},{q="What does Ula'elek want?",a="Ula'elek wants capable materials to practice his craft and fashion sturdy armor. When called upon by Thun'grim, he tasks rising warriors with gathering exotic components—such as satyr hooves—so that he can forge brutal gauntlets worthy of proven fighters.",al={"ulaelek goal","what does ula'elek need","what does ulaelek want"},it="wants",add="c0ac20d7"},{q="Why is Ula'elek here in Sen'jin Village?",a="Ula'elek resides in Sen'jin Village to serve his tribe and the Horde as an armorsmith. Working by the coast of Durotar, he remains close to his Darkspear kin while lending his forge to train and equip the Horde's frontline warriors.",al={"why is ulaelek in senjin","ulaelek location reason","why is ula'elek here"},it="why_here",add="a7c1ab84"},{q="Who is Ula'elek tied to?",a="Ula'elek is closely allied with Thun'grim Firegaze, an accomplished orc armorsmith stationed in the Barrens. Thun'grim trusts Ula'elek's skill enough to send promising warriors straight to his anvil in Sen'jin Village to have their gauntlets crafted.",al={"ulaelek connections","who does ulaelek know","ula'elek allies"},it="ties",add="e890a681"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you rely on Ula'elek to assemble your Brutal armor set, shaping hard-won satyr hooves into rugged gauntlets at Thun'grim Firegaze's direction.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see how Darkspear smiths help equip the young Horde, forging frontline gear on Sen'jin Village's open shores.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you see how Horde smiths put beast and demon trophies to practical use in warrior armor, beyond traditional foundries."},kw={"brutal gauntlets","darkspear","durotar","satyr hooves","sen'jin village","smith","thun'grim firegaze","ula'elek"},rel={"quest:1839","quest:1842","quest:1843","quest:1502","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:satyr","topic:troll"},src={"Ula'elek"}}
E["npc:uzzek"] = {t="npc",n="Uzzek",z="barrens",s="Uzzek watches the eastern Barrens from southwest of Far Watch Post. The battle-hardened orc survived many skirmishes across Kalimdor and now tests and trains promising Horde warriors crossing the plains.",h="Uzzek watches the eastern Barrens from southwest of Far Watch Post.",sec={{t="Veteran of the Plains",b="Uzzek trains young warriors southwest of Far Watch Post, near the eastern edge of the Barrens. He endured brutal combat in the recent wars and now tests those learning to defend themselves. To prove their skill, they face the savage wildlife and raiders that trouble the crossing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Uzzek?",a="Uzzek is a veteran orc warrior stationed in the eastern Barrens, just southwest of Far Watch Post. He guides aspiring Horde warriors learning defensive combat.",al={"who is uzzek","uzzek lore","uzzek npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Uzzek?",a="You can find Uzzek along the bluffs southwest of Far Watch Post, overlooking the road from Durotar into the Barrens.",al={"uzzek location","where is uzzek","find uzzek"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Uzzek play for Horde warriors?",a="Uzzek tests young warriors' stamina and resolve with trials such as the Path of Defense. Then he directs them to seasoned masters like Thun'grim Firegaze.",al={"uzzek warrior quest","path of defense uzzek"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Uzzek on?",a="Uzzek is loyal to the Horde. As an orc veteran standing vigil near the Far Watch Post on the border of the Barrens and Durotar, he serves the young nation founded by Thrall, testing and mentoring promising warriors who seek to defend Horde territory.",al={"is uzzek horde","uzzek faction","who does uzzek serve"},it="side",add="a0e5656a"},{q="What does Uzzek want?",a="Uzzek seeks to test aspiring Horde warriors in the fundamentals of discipline and defense. Having seen countless battles himself, he ensures that young fighters understand resilience, survival, and the tactical mastery needed to protect the Horde before sending them on to further training.",al={"what does uzzek need","uzzek purpose","what does uzzek ask for"},it="wants",add="6cff12ed"},{q="Why is Uzzek stationed near the Far Watch Post?",a="Uzzek keeps watch in the rugged expanse just southwest of the Far Watch Post, right along the crossing between Durotar and the Barrens. Positioning himself near the frontier allows him to intercept and evaluate Horde warriors venturing out into the wider world, preparing them for the harsher conflicts ahead.",al={"why is uzzek here","why is uzzek in the barrens","uzzek location reason"},it="why_here",add="f99df2aa"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Uzzek's tests of grit and defensive skill as you leave your first training grounds for the wider Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Uzzek near Far Watch Post, among the veteran defenders watching the vulnerable border between Durotar and the untamed savanna."},kw={"barrens","far watch post","path of defense","thun'grim firegaze","uzzek","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:far-watch-post","zone:barrens","quest:1498","quest:1502"},src={"Uzzek"}}
E["npc:velora-nitely"] = {t="npc",n="Velora Nitely",z="barrens",s="In the Undercity's Trade Quarter, Velora Nitely works the forge for the Forsaken and the Horde. Once among Lordaeron's finest armorsmiths, she now makes dry jokes that rarely land.",h="In the Undercity's Trade Quarter, Velora Nitely works the forge for the Forsaken and the Horde.",sec={{t="A Smith of Lordaeron",b="Velora Nitely works near the anvils in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, where she makes armor for the Horde. Before the Third War devastated the north, Lordaeron celebrated her as an exceptional armorsmith. Undeath took her life and warmth, but left her technical skill untouched. She works with Horde crafters across continents, including Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens. Her craft includes reinforcing heavy battle plate and forging the formidable Brutal Legguards from hardened materials such as Dragonmaw shinbones.",sp=0},{t="Deadpan Humor",b="Velora Nitely keeps trying to make jokes at the forge, though her humor rarely lands. Many of her somber Forsaken kin brood over their cursed fate, but she still makes room for levity. Death seems to have ruined her comedic timing: her quips sound flat, morbid, and thoroughly unfunny to the living and the dead alike. She keeps cracking them undeterred.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Velora Nitely?",a="Velora Nitely works as a Forsaken armorsmith in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. In life, she was renowned throughout Lordaeron for her extraordinary metalworking skills.",al={"velora nitely lore","who is velora","velora nitely npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Velora Nitely be found?",a="Velora Nitely works near the forges and armor stands in the Undercity's Trade Quarter.",al={"velora nitely location","where is velora nitely","velora nitely map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is her connection to Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="Velora Nitely is a Horde smith who aids the orc armorsmith Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens. She crafts Brutal Legguards for warriors who bring her Dragonmaw shinbones.",al={"velora and thungrim","thungrim firegaze armor","brutal armor questline"},it="ties"},{q="Why are her jokes so bad?",a="Velora Nitely enjoys trying to make people laugh, but death took a toll on her delivery. Since rising into undeath, her jokes have been awkward and deadpan, and rarely funny.",al={"velora sense of humor","velora jokes","why does velora tell jokes"}},{q="Whose side is Velora Nitely on?",a="Velora is loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed within the Undercity, she puts her exceptional metalworking skills to work assisting the Horde's warriors, collaborating with fellow Horde craftsmen across the seas to forge mighty equipment for their champions.",al={"velora nitely faction","who does velora nitely serve","velora horde or alliance"},it="side",add="af55a704"},{q="What does Velora Nitely want?",a="Velora seeks rare materials worthy of her craftsmanship, specifically dragonmaw shinbones from the Wetlands, to forge the formidable Brutal Legguards. She also enjoys trying to tell jokes to visitors, even if undeath has left her comedic delivery rather dry and flat.",al={"what does velora want","velora nitely goal","what does velora nitely need"},it="wants",add="71b2c071"},{q="Why is Velora Nitely in the Undercity?",a="As a former citizen of Lordaeron who was raised into undeath, Velora found a home among Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken. She plies her trade in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, where she can forge armor and aid travelers seeking her legendary smithing talents.",al={"why is velora nitely here","why is velora in undercity","velora nitely trade quarter"},it="why_here",add="dd304cfc"},{q="Why is Velora Nitely famous?",a="In life, Velora was renowned as one of the finest armorsmiths in all of Lordaeron. Even in undeath, her reputation for masterwork plate remains intact, prompting smiths like Thun'grim Firegaze to direct promising warriors to seek out her legendary craft.",al={"is velora famous","velora nitely reputation","why is velora nitely well known"},it="fame",add="97d7ef33"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Horde warrior seeking the legendary Brutal Armor, you are directed north to Velora in the Undercity. She forges sturdy legguards from Dragonmaw orc bones.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see Lordaeron's armorsmithing tradition in Velora's precise metalworking, which endures long into undeath."},kw={"armorsmith","brutal legguards","dragonmaw shinbones","lordaeron","thun'grim firegaze","trade quarter","undercity","velora nitely"},rel={"zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","quest:1841","quest:1846","quest:1838","quest:1502","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Velora Nitely"}}
E["npc:wizzlecrank-s-shredder"] = {t="npc",n="Wizzlecrank's Shredder",z="barrens",s="In Sludge Fen, Wizzlecrank's Shredder sits trapped among Venture Company operators. Pilot Wizzlecrank climbed inside the machine to steal it, but it will not move without a key. Its engine must be started before the goblin can try to escape.",h="In Sludge Fen, Wizzlecrank's Shredder sits trapped among Venture Company operators.",sec={{t="Trapped in the Sludge",b="Deep in Sludge Fen, Wizzlecrank waits inside a motionless shredder. The Venture Company machine is surrounded by hostile mercenaries in the polluted basin. Wizzlecrank climbed aboard to steal it, then learned he needed a key to unlock its movement column. When another shredder operator asked if all was well, he panicked and blamed a mechanical problem. Now he remains sealed inside, with guards and overseers nearby, hoping someone will fetch the key before the Venture Company grows suspicious.",sp=0},{t="A Clattering Breakout",b="With the ignition key from the supervisor in the control room atop the derrick, the shredder clatters back to life. Pilot Wizzlecrank drives the lumbering machine through the mercenaries around him, its blades whirling and metal plating taking the blows. Passersby who sympathize with the trapped pilot escort the vulnerable contraption out of the basin and toward safety.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is inside Wizzlecrank's Shredder?",a="Pilot Wizzlecrank, a goblin, is inside the mechanical walker. He climbed into the Venture Company machine to steal it, then found himself trapped in their territory without its key.",al={"who pilots the shredder","pilot wizzlecrank","who is in wizzlecranks shredder"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the shredder stranded at Sludge Fen?",a="Wizzlecrank climbed into the shredder without knowing it needed a key to unlock its movement column. Surrounded by Venture Company laborers, drillers, and guards, he told a suspicious operator the machine had a mechanical problem. Now he waits inside for someone to fetch the key from the supervisor atop the derrick.",al={"why is shredder stuck","wizzlecrank stuck","what happened to the shredder"},it="why_here"},{q="Why is the shredder sometimes missing?",a="When the shredder is missing from Sludge Fen's northern depression, another traveler has started the ignition and is escorting Wizzlecrank to safety. It returns to its starting place shortly after the escort ends.",al={"shredder despawned","where is wizzlecranks shredder","shredder missing"},gp=true},{q="What is the Venture Company doing at Sludge Fen?",a="The Venture Company is exploiting the northern Barrens for crude oil, tar, and timber. Its work has turned a natural water source into a toxic, oily quagmire crowded with hired goons and foremen.",al={"what is sludge fen","venture co sludge fen"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Wizzlecrank on?",a="Pilot Wizzlecrank is no Venture Company operative. He works with Sputtervalve of Ratchet and climbed into the Venture Co. shredder to steal it. Stuck deep within hostile Venture Co. territory at Sludge Fen, he relies on passing adventurers of either faction to fetch the key and escort him out to safety.",al={"wizzlecrank faction","is wizzlecrank horde","who does wizzlecrank work for"},it="side",add="8b008c47"},{q="What does Wizzlecrank want?",a="Wizzlecrank wants nothing more than to fire up the stolen shredder and make a clean getaway from Sludge Fen. Trapped amidst aggressive Venture Company workers and deadly machinery, he needs someone to fetch the machine's key and escort him through enemy lines to safety.",al={"what does wizzlecrank need","wizzlecranks shredder goal","wizzlecrank motive"},it="wants",add="0d614a8d"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The goblin shredder uses crude steam and piston technology. Pilot Wizzlecrank's predicament shows how easily a proprietary ignition system can fail in the field.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde usually despises the Venture Company's deforestation and toxic exploitation of the Barrens. Helping a stranded pilot gives you a chance to smash up their drilling operations."},kw={"barrens","ignition","pilot wizzlecrank","sludge fen","the escape","venture company","wizzlecrank","wizzlecranks shredder"},rel={"subzone:sludge-fen","quest:858","quest:863","zone:barrens","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},src={"Wizzlecrank's Shredder"}}
E["npc:wrenix-the-wretched"] = {t="npc",n="Wrenix the Wretched",z="barrens",s="Beside his strange apparatus in Ratchet, Wrenix the Wretched helps crack tough locks. The goblin tinker offers tools to open secure caches.",h="Beside his strange apparatus in Ratchet, Wrenix the Wretched helps crack tough locks.",sec={{t="A Tinker in Ratchet",b="Wrenix the Wretched works beside his machinery in Ratchet, the goblin port on the Barrens coast. As a tinker of the Steamwheedle Cartel, he knows mechanisms and contraptions, and how to bypass locks and salvage what lies beyond them. Rogues and scouts working the coast can turn to him for help.",sp=0},{t="The Gizmotronic Apparatus",b="Wrenix keeps his gizmotronic apparatus close at hand. He uses it and his mechanical skill to supply thieves' tools and lock-picking instruments. Those seeking to recover stolen Southsea pirate contraband along the Merchant Coast can put them to use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wrenix the Wretched?",a="Wrenix is a goblin tinker in Ratchet, in the Barrens. He works beside his gizmotronic apparatus and deals in contraptions and lock-picking tools.",al={"wrenix","who is wrenix","wrenix the wretched"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Wrenix be found?",a="Wrenix can be found beside his large mechanical device in Ratchet, the port town on the eastern coast of the Barrens.",al={"wrenix location","where is wrenix","wrenix ratchet"},gp=true},{q="What is the gizmotronic apparatus next to him?",a="Wrenix's gizmotronic apparatus is a goblin-made machine for tinkering and diagnostic work. He uses it to craft specialized instruments such as precision thieves' tools.",al={"gizmotronic apparatus","wrenix machine","what is that machine"}},{q="Why is he helping adventurers against the Southsea Freebooters?",a="Southsea pirates along the Barrens coast keep valuable plunder in locked lockboxes. Wrenix's mechanical tools help resourceful rogues open them, for mutual profit.",al={"why southsea","plundering the plunderers lore","wrenix pirates"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Wrenix the Wretched on?",a="Wrenix aligns himself with the Steamwheedle Cartel operating out of Ratchet. Like most goblins in the port, his primary allegiance is to commerce, practical enterprise, and his own skin rather than the broader war between the Alliance and the Horde. He remains neutral to any traveler willing to do business or lend a capable hand with local trouble.",al={"wrenix faction","who does wrenix serve","wrenix loyalty"},it="side",add="6e51c7f3"},{q="Why is Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet?",a="Wrenix makes his living amid the bustling docks of Ratchet, working alongside his bizarre gizmotronic apparatus. Ratchet provides a steady stream of gullible adventurers, scavengers, and scoundrels, making it the ideal frontier haven for an eccentric goblin inventor looking to hire out dirty work and protect his trade interests against nearby coastal threats.",al={"why is wrenix here","wrenix ratchet reason","what brought wrenix to ratchet"},it="why_here",add="eba18045"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can get tools from Wrenix and practice bypassing Southsea pirate lockboxes.",["profession:Engineering"]="Wrenix's gizmotronic apparatus shows Steamwheedle gadgetry at work: noisy, temperamental, and effective at precision work."},kw={"barrens","gizmotronic","goblin","lockpicking","pirates","ratchet","wrenix","wretched"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","quest:2382","quest:2381","topic:goblin","zone:barrens"},src={"Wrenix the Wretched"}}
E["npc:zargh"] = {t="npc",n="Zargh",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads in the Barrens, Zargh sells meat and sends choice cuts to Orgrimmar.",h="At the Crossroads in the Barrens, Zargh sells meat and sends choice cuts to Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Butcher of the Crossroads",b="At the Crossroads, Zargh sells cured meat, shank, and game from the surrounding plains. Travelers heading into the wilderness can find provisions at his shop. He also sends choice cuts across Durotar to Innkeeper Gryshka in the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="A Courier's Errand",b="Zargh sends fresh meat to Innkeeper Gryshka in Orgrimmar by wind rider, so it reaches her before it spoils. A letter from Gryshka recalls that Zargh lost a finger in a mishap. After receiving word from her, Zargh hints that a wedding invitation may be in the traveler's future.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zargh?",a="You can find Zargh at the Crossroads, the central Horde settlement in the Barrens. He sells meat among the camp's merchants.",al={"zargh location","where is zargh","zargh npc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Zargh's connection to Innkeeper Gryshka?",a="Zargh supplies Innkeeper Gryshka in Orgrimmar with choice meats from the Barrens. Their letters suggest a warm, personal bond, and after one arrives, Zargh hints that a wedding invitation may be coming.",al={"zargh gryshka","zargh relationship","who is zargh marrying"},it="ties"},{q="What happened to Zargh's finger?",a="A letter from Gryshka says Zargh lost a finger in a butchering accident. The mishap remains an inside joke between them about the contents of his meat cuts.",al={"zargh lost finger","zargh accident"},it="history"},{q="What does Zargh sell?",a="Zargh sells provisions including haunches of meat, cured ham steaks, wild hog shanks, and a recipe for Hot Lion Chops.",al={"zargh vendor items","zargh goods"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Zargh?",a="Zargh is an orc butcher and meat vendor stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He provides provisions and choice cuts of local game to travelers, guards, and allies across Horde territory.",al={"who is zargh","zargh lore","zargh crossroads"},it="identity",add="84a718e2"},{q="Whose side is Zargh on?",a="Zargh is a loyal member of the Horde, operating out of the pivotal settlement of the Crossroads. He regularly coordinates trade and deliveries with Horde settlements, including the capital city of Orgrimmar.",al={"is zargh horde","zargh faction","zargh allegiances"},it="side",add="9d177987"},{q="What does Zargh want?",a="Zargh aims to run his butchery trade smoothly and ensure his shipments reach their destinations. He enlists reliable couriers to deliver prime Barrens meat to his close friend, Innkeeper Gryshka, at the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.",al={"what does zargh want","zargh quest goal","zargh motives"},it="wants",add="db26839a"},{q="Why is Zargh in the Crossroads?",a="The Crossroads serves as the vital trade and travel hub of the Barrens, making it the ideal spot for a butcher. Surrounded by abundant wild game, Zargh can readily prepare and export choice meats to distant settlements.",al={"why is zargh here","why is zargh at the crossroads","zargh location reason"},it="why_here",add="a9ecc79a"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can buy Zargh's recipe for Hot Lion Chops, one of the few such recipes sold in the Barrens. It lets you prepare local predator meat.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see how the route between the Crossroads and Orgrimmar uses wind riders to carry messengers between the Barrens and Durotar."},kw={"barrens","butcher","crossroads","gryshka","hot lion chops","meat","zargh"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-gryshka","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:6365","quest:6384","quest:6386","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Zargh"}}
E["quest:1069"] = {t="quest",n="Deepmoss Spider Eggs",z="barrens",s="Mebok Mizzyrix sees a chance to sell Deepmoss Spider Eggs to Booty Bay. Spider egg omelettes have become a craze there, and he sends travelers into the Stonetalon Mountains to gather fresh clutches for the overseas trade.",h="Mebok Mizzyrix sees a chance to sell Deepmoss Spider Eggs to Booty Bay.",sec={{t="A Taste for Luxury",b="Booty Bay’s wealthy patrons and eccentric pirates have taken to spider egg omelettes, driving demand for rare ingredients across the Great Sea. Ratchet merchant Mebok Mizzyrix sees a chance to make a fortune by supplying the southern port. The Eastern Kingdoms have no supply of these spiders, so Mebok looks to Kalimdor’s wilderness for the eggs.",sp=0},{t="Nests in the Mountains",b="Deepmoss spider eggs lie in the Stonetalon Mountains, where the Venture Company has cut timber. You can find clutches beneath the trees still standing at Windshear Crag, or farther into the web covered depths of Sishir Canyon. Gathering them means facing venomous bites and thick infestations. Even seasoned scavengers may find the swarms hard to stomach.",sp=0},{t="The Steamer Clam Express",b="Fresh eggs must cross the sea before they spoil or hatch. Mebok works with Ratchet’s Wharfmaster Dizzywig to book freight on goblin merchant ships bound for the docks of Stranglethorn Vale. Once the eggs are packed into crates, Mebok earns a tidy profit from the high seas trade in fine food.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix want spider eggs?",a="Booty Bay has developed a taste for spider egg omelettes, but lacks a local supply of the eggs. Mebok Mizzyrix sees a chance for Ratchet’s goblin traders to profit by supplying the port.",al={"why spider eggs","mebok spider eggs","what are eggs for"},it="motive"},{q="Where can the deepmoss spider eggs be found?",a="Deepmoss spider eggs can be found in the Stonetalon Mountains, northwest of the Barrens. Gather them beneath the remaining trees at Windshear Crag or deeper inside Sishir Canyon.",al={"where are deepmoss eggs","egg locations","stonetalon spider egg locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Mebok warn against Sishir Canyon?",a="Sishir Canyon holds massive spider swarms, dense cobwebs, and partially digested prey. Mebok warns that anyone with a weak stomach should gather eggs beneath the trees at Windshear Crag instead.",al={"sishir canyon warning","weak stomach sishir"},it="danger"},{q="Who ships the eggs once collected?",a="Mebok works with Wharfmaster Dizzywig at the Ratchet docks to send the eggs by merchant ship across the sea to Booty Bay.",al={"who ships the eggs","wharfmaster shipping","dizzywig eggs"},it="allies"},{q="Are the eggs eaten raw or cooked?",a="The eggs are made into omelettes, an eccentric luxury dish for wealthy patrons and adventurers visiting Booty Bay’s taverns.",al={"how are spider eggs eaten","spider omelettes"},it="item"},{q="Can players of both factions complete this task?",a="Yes. Ratchet is an open port run by the Steamwheedle Cartel, and Mebok Mizzyrix offers the work to both Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"is this quest neutral","horde or alliance spider eggs"},gp=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can see how port city diners make status symbols of strange, daring foods such as deepmoss spider eggs.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler crossing the Barrens toward Stonetalon, you can earn quick coin in Ratchet to fund efforts against local harpies and Venture Company loggers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout traveling between the Barrens and Stonetalon’s night elven enclaves, you can use Ratchet’s goblin neutrality to earn traveling expenses."},kw={"booty bay","deepmoss","dizzywig","mebok mizzyrix","omelette","ratchet","sishir canyon","spider eggs","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","quest:1492","subzone:ratchet","zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:sishir-canyon","subzone:booty-bay","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="20",id=1069,ri={"Deepmoss Egg"}},src={"Deepmoss Spider Eggs"}}
E["quest:1153"] = {t="quest",n="A New Ore Sample",z="barrens",s="Tatternack Steelforge seeks new ore in Thousand Needles to strengthen the Horde’s arms. The blacksmith in Camp Taurajo sends you south to bring back a sample for testing.",h="Tatternack Steelforge seeks new ore in Thousand Needles to strengthen the Horde’s arms.",sec={{t="A Smith's Ambition",b="Tatternack Steelforge works as a blacksmith in Camp Taurajo, under Orgrimmar’s direct scrutiny. He has already supplied weapons made from local centaur armaments, but still wants to prove his craft to Warchief Thrall. Travelers passing through showed him a strange piece of ore taken from a kobold to the south. When they refused to sell it, Tatternack took their refusal as an insult to his craft and the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Venture into Thousand Needles",b="You leave the flat plains of the southern Barrens for the towering canyon mazes of Thousand Needles. Kobold diggers tunnel through its crags and cliffs. Bring back unrefined chunks taken directly from them, and Tatternack can judge whether the raw mineral can be forged into weapons worthy of Thrall’s war effort.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tatternack Steelforge?",a="Tatternack Steelforge is an orc weaponsmith stationed at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He crafts weapons for the Horde’s frontier defense and seeks new materials to impress Warchief Thrall.",al={"tatternack","camp taurajo smith","who is tatternack"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this ore sample come from?",a="Kobolds carry the unrefined ore through the winding canyons of Thousand Needles, south of the Great Lift at the Barrens’ border.",al={"where is the ore","ore location","thousand needles ore"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Tatternack angry at the passing travelers?",a="Travelers from the south showed Tatternack a strange mineral chunk taken from a slain kobold, then refused to sell it. He saw their hoarding of vital materials as an unpatriotic insult to the Warchief and cursed them as cowards.",al={"why is tatternack mad","travelers ore","tatternack travelers"},it="motive"},{q="What will Tatternack do with the ore?",a="Tatternack plans to analyze the ore’s metallurgical properties and test its strength. If it proves durable enough, he intends to forge a prototype weapon and present it directly to Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar.",al={"what happens to the ore","why does he want ore"},it="item"},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before this task?",a="First, you complete Weapons of Choice by gathering specific weapons from the various centaur tribes threatening Camp Taurajo, proving that local armaments can be repurposed.",al={"prereq quest","prior quest","weapons of choice"},gp=true},{q="Why are kobolds in Thousand Needles carrying this ore?",a="Kobolds compulsively burrow and mine, tunneling through crags and subterranean veins. In Thousand Needles, their digging has uncovered unusual deposits that surface-dwellers have rarely touched.",al={"kobold mining","thousand needles kobolds"},it="target"},{q="Why does Tatternack need you to gather the ore sample?",a="Tatternack is stationed at Camp Taurajo attending to his forge and crafting armaments for the Horde under direct orders from the Warchief. Bound to his duties at the anvil and insulted by traveling mercenaries who refused to share their find, he turns to an adventurer who has already earned his trust and proven capable in battle.",al={"why me a new ore sample","why does tatternack need me","why cant tatternack get the ore"},it="why_me",add="ecf3b4be"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a Horde smith, you help secure new metal deposits to keep the frontier armed against surrounding threats.",["faction:Horde"]="At Camp Taurajo, you can contribute materials to the Warchief’s military preparations from the Horde’s southern bastion.",["profession:Mining"]="As a prospector, you know the value of raw, unrefined veins unearthed by burrowing creatures in unexplored southern canyons."},kw={"camp taurajo","kobold","tatternack steelforge","thousand needles","thrall","unrefined ore sample","weapons of choice"},rel={"quest:893","npc:tatternack-steelforge","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens","topic:kobold","topic:horde"},m={start="Tatternack Steelforge",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1153,ri={"Unrefined Ore Sample"}},src={"A New Ore Sample"}}
E["quest:1358"] = {t="quest",n="Sample for Helbrim",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Apothecary Helbrim awaits a wolf heart from across the sea. Apothecary Zinge sends it from the Undercity to support the Forsaken's research in central Kalimdor.",h="At the Crossroads, Apothecary Helbrim awaits a wolf heart from across the sea.",sec={{t="A Contagion Across the Sea",b="Apothecary Zinge sends a Wolf Heart Sample from the Undercity to Apothecary Helbrim in the Barrens. The Royal Apothecary Society's experiments reach beyond the ruins of Lordaeron. After Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine sent tainted organs, Zinge sought to extend their research across the world. Now a courier carries the sample overseas to Helbrim, an alchemist stationed in the Barrens' dry savanna.",sp=0},{t="Helbrim's Ambition",b="At the Crossroads, Apothecary Helbrim studies how Kalimdor's native beasts react to compounds from the Plaguelands. The wolf heart could show how those toxins affect local creatures. Helbrim believes that dissecting and testing it alongside them will help the Forsaken master poisons and unnatural afflictions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the package being delivered to Helbrim?",a="The package holds a Wolf Heart Sample, harvested by Apothecary Renferrel from Silverpine Forest's corrupted wolves and analyzed by Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.",al={"what is the sample","wolf heart package","what did zinge give me"},it="item"},{q="Why does Apothecary Helbrim want a tainted wolf heart?",a="Helbrim studies how toxins from Lordaeron affect Kalimdor's wildlife. He hopes the heart's extreme toxicity will help develop stronger concoctions and poisons for the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"why does helbrim need wolf heart","helbrim research","helbrim purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Apothecary Helbrim located?",a="Apothecary Helbrim is stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens, on the upper exterior deck of the central watchtower overlooking the settlement.",al={"where is helbrim","helbrim location","find helbrim"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does a traveler get from Undercity to the Crossroads?",a="Take the zeppelin from the tower outside Undercity to Orgrimmar in Durotar. Travel south through Durotar, cross the Southfury River into the Barrens, then follow the main road west to the Crossroads.",al={"travel to crossroads","how to get to helbrim","undercity to barrens"},gp=true},{q="Who are Apothecary Renferrel and Apothecary Zinge?",a="Apothecary Renferrel and Apothecary Zinge are researchers in the Royal Apothecary Society. Renferrel works from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, while Zinge studies in the Apothecarium in the Undercity.",al={"who is renferrel","who is zinge","zinge and renferrel lore"},it="identity"},{q="What faction does this research serve?",a="The research serves the Forsaken and the Royal Apothecary Society under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. It advances their effort to create deadly chemical and biological weapons.",al={"who benefits","is this for sylvanas","apothecary goal"},it="side"},{q="Why does Apothecary Zinge want this sample delivered to Helbrim?",a="Apothecary Zinge seeks to aid the broader research of the Royal Apothecary Society across both continents. Her colleague Apothecary Helbrim is stationed in Kalimdor studying how Lordaeron's blighted toxins react with indigenous beasts. Believing the tainted wolf hearts sent from Silverpine could advance their shared knowledge of virulent poisons, Zinge dispatches you to ensure Helbrim receives the material for his experiments.",al={"why send sample to helbrim","zinge motive sample","why does zinge want this delivered"},it="motive",add="d2670c0d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you carry the Royal Apothecary Society's tainted specimens across the world, part of its far-reaching effort to secure Forsaken dominance through chemical supremacy.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see orcs and tauren welcome Forsaken aid in defending the Crossroads. The apothecaries' quiet study of plagued remains brings an unsettling presence to the peaceful Barrens."},kw={"apothecary helbrim","apothecary zinge","crossroads","royal apothecary society","sample for helbrim","the barrens","undercity","wolf heart sample"},rel={"npc:apothecary-helbrim","npc:apothecary-zinge","quest:1359","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:orgrimmar","zone:durotar","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Apothecary Zinge",["end"]="Apothecary Helbrim",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1358},src={"Sample for Helbrim"}}
E["quest:1362"] = {t="quest",n="The Kolkar of Desolace",z="barrens",s="The Kolkar threaten Horde lands from their stronghold in Desolace. Regthar Deathgate sends Horde champions west across the mountains to reinforce scout Felgur Twocuts at Ghost Walker Post.",h="The Kolkar threaten Horde lands from their stronghold in Desolace.",sec={{t="A Threat Across the Mountains",b="Centaur raiders keep pressing into the Barrens, and Regthar Deathgate knows that fighting them there will not end the threat. The Kolkar clan draws its strength from the rugged lands on Kalimdor's western coast. While their ancestral stronghold remains beyond Horde control, raiders will keep pouring through the mountain passes. To stop them, the Horde must strike at their home.",sp=0},{t="Ghost Walker Post",b="Ghost Walker Post gives the Horde a foothold deep in Desolace. Scout Felgur Twocuts watches the rival centaur clans from the outpost. Regthar sends seasoned fighters from the Barrens to serve under Felgur, carrying the Horde's campaign west from defense to direct action.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="Regthar Deathgate, an orc warrior at the bunker west of the Crossroads in the Barrens, directs you to carry the fight into the Kolkar's ancestral lands.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","regthar"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is Ghost Walker Post located?",a="Ghost Walker Post is an isolated Horde camp along the rugged paths of Desolace, west of the Kalimdor mountain ridge.",al={"where is ghost walker post","felgur twocuts location","desolace camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde focusing on Desolace?",a="The Kolkar who raid the Barrens come from the larger centaur clans rooted in Desolace. Regthar knows defense alone cannot stop the invasions while the Kolkar stronghold remains intact.",al={"why go to desolace","why fight kolkar in desolace","centaur connection"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Felgur Twocuts?",a="Felgur Twocuts is a Horde scout at Ghost Walker Post. He watches the rival centaur clans in Desolace and organizes strikes against them.",al={"felgur twocuts","who is felgur"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest involve combat?",a="No. You carry a message from the Barrens into Desolace, where harder challenges await Horde adventurers.",al={"combat in quest","fighting quest"},gp=true},{q="Which centaur clan does this quest target?",a="The Kolkar clan is the target. Its centaur raiders come from Desolace and have pushed into the Barrens and Durotar.",al={"which centaur","what clan","kolkar clan"},it="target"},{q="Why does Regthar Deathgate need you to travel to Desolace?",a="Regthar Deathgate is coordinating frontline defense and reconnaissance against the Kolkar within the Barrens, keeping local Horde forces occupied with immediate threats to the oases. To strike at the root of the problem, he needs an able, mobile adventurer to venture beyond the borders into the wastes of Desolace and link up with scout Felgur Twocuts directly.",al={"why send me desolace","why regthar needs me","why me kolkar of desolace"},it="why_me",add="4557df46"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, this marks a shift from guarding young settlements in Durotar and the Barrens to taking the fight into hostile lands.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know centaur aggression brought your nomadic tribes close to extinction before your alliance with Thrall. Fighting them in their Desolace homelands carries a personal cost.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you have secured a foothold in eastern Kalimdor. The untamed centaur clans still threaten Horde supply lines."},kw={"centaur","desolace","felgur twocuts","ghost walker post","horde","kolkar","regthar deathgate","the barrens"},rel={"quest:1361","npc:felgur-twocuts","subzone:ghost-walker-post","zone:desolace","zone:barrens","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Regthar Deathgate",["end"]="Felgur Twocuts",level="32",faction="Horde",id=1362},src={"The Kolkar of Desolace"}}
E["quest:1492"] = {t="quest",n="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",z="barrens",s="At Ratchet's pier, a crate of alchemy supplies waits for passage across the sea. Wharfmaster Dizzywig arranges its journey to the Old World aboard a ship bound for Blackwater Cove.",h="At Ratchet's pier, a crate of alchemy supplies waits for passage across the sea.",sec={{t="A Courier to the Port",b="A crate of potions and reagents waits at the Barrens port, bound for colleagues in the Old World. Caravans that might have carried it have already departed, so you are asked to take the secure shipment to Ratchet's water's edge. The port offers a route across the Great Sea between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="Ratchet's Docks",b="Wharfmaster Dizzywig handles cargo on Ratchet's wooden piers. He tracks shipments in ledgers and manifests, then finds space aboard vessels sailing east across the Great Sea. This crate is booked for a ship bound for Blackwater Cove.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig is the goblin harbor official on Ratchet's main pier. He manages ship manifests, cargo holds, and passages between Kalimdor and ports across the sea.",al={"wharfmaster dizzywig","who is dizzywig","where is dizzywig"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the crate being sent?",a="The crate of potions and reagents is bound for the Old World, aboard the next ship sailing from Ratchet to Blackwater Cove.",al={"where does crate go","blackwater cove","destination of crate"},it="place"},{q="Where is Ratchet located?",a="Ratchet lies on the eastern coast of the Barrens, in a sheltered bay directly east of the central crossroads.",al={"ratchet location","how do i find ratchet"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why send cargo through a goblin port?",a="Ratchet is a neutral port open to Horde and independent traders. Its regular routes cross the Great Sea and avoid military blockades and political hostilities.",al={"why ratchet","why use goblin port"},it="purpose"},{q="What is inside the secure crate?",a="The secure crate holds prepared potions, crafting reagents, and other alchemical goods for associates in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"crate contents","what is in the box"},it="item"},{q="Who sends the shipment to Dizzywig?",a="An alchemical practitioner in the Barrens sent the shipment after missing the departing caravan. A reliable runner is needed to reach the pier before the next tide.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Apothecary Helbrim need this crate delivered to Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads must send a crate of potions, reagents and other items to his associates in the Old World. He has little time to see it down to the docks at Ratchet himself, and the last caravan has already left. Handing the crate to you ensures it makes the next boat to Blackwater Cove.",al={"why send the secure crate","ak'zeloth motive dizzywig","why deliver crate ratchet"},it="motive",add="14e5c3eb"},{q="Why does Apothecary Helbrim ask an adventurer instead of handling the delivery himself?",a="Apothecary Helbrim has too little time to make the trek from the Crossroads to the coast himself. Because the last caravan has already left, he cannot rely on routine transport. Enlisting a traveler is his only reliable way to get the crate to the docks before the ship sails with the next tide.",al={"why send me dizzywig","why can't ak'zeloth deliver the crate","why doesn't akzeloth go to ratchet"},it="why_me",add="c036c897"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer crossing the Barrens, you can carry cargo to Ratchet and learn the sea routes linking Kalimdor with the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"blackwater cove","docks","pier","ratchet","secure crate","shipping","the barrens","wharfmaster dizzywig"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={level="11",faction="Horde",id=1492},src={"Wharfmaster Dizzywig (Barrens)"}}
E["quest:1498"] = {t="quest",n="Path of Defense",z="barrens",s="At the Far Watch Post, Uzzek prepares young Horde warriors to defend those who cannot defend themselves. He sends them to Thunder Ridge to prove their endurance against its electric beasts.",h="At the Far Watch Post, Uzzek prepares young Horde warriors to defend those who cannot defend themselves.",sec={{t="The Shield of the Horde",b="At the Far Watch Post, Uzzek teaches young warriors that defense is part of the Horde's duty. The post lies on the border between the Barrens and Durotar. Uzzek says a warrior's highest calling is to stand between danger and those unable to defend themselves, taking the blows so the Horde can endure.",sp=0},{t="Trial of Thunder",b="Uzzek sends the novices to Thunder Ridge, north across the Southfury River in Durotar, to test their stamina and resolve. Thunder lizards and lightning hides roam the canyon. The initiates must survive the beasts' jolts and harvest their singed scales to show they have the fortitude to hold the front line.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Path of Defense quest?",a="Veteran Uzzek gives the trial at the Far Watch Post, which guards the border between Durotar and the eastern Barrens.",al={"quest giver","who starts path of defense","uzzek location"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Thunder Ridge located?",a="Thunder Ridge lies in western Durotar, north of the main road, across the bridge over the Southfury River. Aggressive thunder lizards and lightning hides roam its ravine.",al={"thunder ridge location","where are thunder lizards","singed scales location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Uzzek demand singed scales specifically?",a="Uzzek asks for singed scales from the shock-wielding beasts of Thunder Ridge. Enduring their electrical attacks proves a warrior has the toughness and resilience to learn advanced defensive techniques.",al={"why singed scales","purpose of scales"},it="item"},{q="What is the philosophical lesson behind this trial?",a="Uzzek teaches that being a warrior is not merely about slaughter, but about shielding others. Surviving the beasts' fury helps initiates learn to protect weaker allies.",al={"warrior philosophy","lore behind path of defense","defensive stance lore"},it="motive"},{q="What comes next after completing Path of Defense?",a="After you prove your defensive mettle to Uzzek, he directs you to continue your martial training with Thun'grim Firegaze.",al={"next quest","what after path of defense","follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Can non-warriors undertake this trial?",a="No. This rite is for warriors, and tests and teaches recruits the basics of guard duty and defensive combat.",al={"is this warrior only","who can do this quest"},gp=true},{q="What creatures are you sent to hunt in Thunder Ridge?",a="Uzzek sends you against the thunder lizards and lightning hides dwelling within Thunder Ridge in Durotar. These formidable beasts wield crackling electrical attacks capable of blasting through ordinary defenses. Facing them forces you to endure relentless physical and elemental assault, demonstrating that your constitution and resolve are sturdy enough to shield the Horde.",al={"what do you fight in thunder ridge","path of defense targets","thunder lizards and lightning hides"},it="target",add="47a57f01"},{q="Why does Uzzek test you instead of handling tasks himself?",a="Uzzek is an instructor stationed at Far Watch Post whose duty is vetting aspiring warriors, not gathering trophies for himself. A warrior's primary calling in the Horde is serving as a living shield for weaker brethren. Uzzek cannot simply hand down defensive techniques to anyone who asks; you must personally demonstrate the resilience required to endure punishing blows before he deems you worthy of his teachings.",al={"why send me","why does uzzek need me","why must i hunt the lizards"},it="why_me",add="3d8ed519"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you begin learning defensive discipline: true martial strength lies in shielding your allies from devastation.",["faction:Horde"]="At the Far Watch Post, Horde guards protect the road into the Barrens, so their resilience matters to Horde security."},kw={"barrens","durotar","far watch post","path of defense","singed scales","thunder lizards","thunder ridge","uzzek"},rel={"npc:uzzek","subzone:far-watch-post","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Uzzek",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1498,ri={"Singed Scale"}},src={"Path of Defense"}}
E["quest:1502"] = {t="quest",n="Thun'grim Firegaze",z="barrens",s="Atop Thorn Hill, Thun'grim Firegaze keeps to a reclusive life and a solitary forge. After their first lessons in defense, Horde warriors cross the Barrens to find him and seek steel fit for their growing skill.",h="Atop Thorn Hill, Thun'grim Firegaze keeps to a reclusive life and a solitary forge.",sec={{t="The Hermit on the Ridge",b="After you show skill in the defensive arts under veteran trainers like Uzzek, you are sent to sharpen your fighting with suitable steel. Ordinary armories can carry a frontline fighter only so far. True mastery calls for a personal weapon from a smith of renown. In the Barrens, Thun'grim Firegaze is that smith, an aging orc who has left settlement life behind to keep an isolated forge high above the plains.",sp=0},{t="A Life in the Forge Fire",b="Thun'grim Firegaze lives atop Thorn Hill, a jagged rise east of the Crossroads where wild raptors and hostile quilboar roam. He spends his solitary hours shaping metal, far from the protection of town walls. Decades of gazing into blistering forge flames have ruined his eyesight, though his instincts remain sharp. When you climb the heights and disturb his solitude, Firegaze knows why: a warrior has come seeking forged steel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends warriors to find Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="Uzzek, a warrior trainer along the road near the Far Watch Post in the eastern Barrens, sends you after you demonstrate your defensive training.",al={"who gives this quest","who starts thun'grim firegaze","quest giver"},gp=true},{q="Where is Thun'grim Firegaze located?",a="Thun'grim lives at an isolated campsite atop Thorn Hill, a high ridge directly east of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"thun'grim location","where is thun'grim","find firegaze"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim live out in the hills alone?",a="Thun'grim has devoted his life to metalcraft, away from town distractions. He works alone at his anvil atop Thorn Hill despite the dangerous beasts and quilboar on the surrounding ridges.",al={"why is thun'grim a hermit","firegaze hermit"},it="why_here"},{q="What happened to Thun'grim Firegaze's eyes?",a="Decades of relentless work over glowing coals and exposure to intense forge heat have largely ruined Thun'grim Firegaze's vision.",al={"is thun'grim blind","firegaze eyes"},it="history"},{q="What comes after meeting Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="After you report to Thun'grim, he recognizes your need for arms and asks you to gather raw materials so he can craft a weapon.",al={"next quest","what after thun'grim","forged steel follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. This path is for Horde warriors seeking specialized arms.",al={"is this warrior only","who can do thun'grim firegaze"},gp=true},{q="Why does Uzzek send you to Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="Uzzek knows that martial training alone will not keep a warrior alive without proper armament. A warrior's weapon must be forged to the highest standard, and Thun'grim Firegaze is renowned among the Horde for his master craftsmanship. Uzzek sends you to seek him out so you can earn a weapon worthy of your growing strength.",al={"why find thungrim","uzzek motive thungrim","why see thungrim firegaze"},it="motive",add="65de68fe"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a young Horde warrior, you are sent into the wilds to find Thun'grim and earn a signature forged weapon to complement your battle training.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Thun'grim follows a solitary orcish tradition of blacksmithing, enduring isolation and blindness to shape hot metal into lethal tools.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde depends on seasoned artisans whose quality steel arms the frontline soldiers defending Kalimdor."},kw={"blacksmith","crossroads","forged steel","the barrens","thorn hill","thun'grim firegaze","uzzek","warrior weapon"},rel={"npc:uzzek","quest:1498","quest:1503","subzone:thorn-hill","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:1825"},m={start="Uzzek",["end"]="Thun'grim Firegaze",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1502},src={"Thun'grim Firegaze (quest)"}}
E["quest:1503"] = {t="quest",n="Forged Steel",z="barrens",s="Thun'grim Firegaze waits in the eastern Barrens for the steel stolen from his camp. He offers to forge a weapon for the warrior who brings it back.",h="Thun'grim Firegaze waits in the eastern Barrens for the steel stolen from his camp.",sec={{t="A Blind Spot Exploited",b="Thun'grim Firegaze keeps a smithy in the eastern Barrens, far from Orgrimmar. Years at the forge have dimmed his sight. The nearby Razormane quilboar used that weakness to steal an iron chest from his camp. Some snorted and made noise on one side to draw his gaze while others slipped in from the other and carried off his forged steel bars.",sp=0},{t="Priceless Metal, Clueless Thieves",b="Thun'grim is angry at the theft, but doubts the Razormanes can use the steel. Quilboar craft with stone, tusks, and thorny roots, not refined metal. The heavy chest remains near a broken wagon in their camp, untouched and useless to them. For Thun'grim, its steel is the stock he needs to forge weapons for young Horde warriors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze is an orc armorer and weaponsmith in the eastern Barrens. Though his eyesight is failing, he keeps working and arms young Horde warriors.",al={"thungrim firegaze","who is the smith","thungrim"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the quilboar steal the steel?",a="The Razormane quilboar stole the iron chest from Thun'grim's camp in a nighttime diversion. They lack the skill to work the forged steel inside.",al={"why steal metal","why quilboar stole","what did razormane want"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the forged steel bars kept?",a="The forged steel bars are locked in the Stolen Iron Chest near a broken wagon in the Razormane grounds northwest of Thun'grim's camp.",al={"where is the chest","stolen iron chest location","where are the bars"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What weapon does Thun'grim offer in return?",a="Thun'grim offers young warriors a choice of freshly forged weapons in exchange for recovering his steel.",al={"reward weapon","what do i get","forged steel reward"},it="item"},{q="How did the Razormanes manage to trick Thun'grim?",a="The Razormanes exploited Thun'grim's failing eyesight. Some raiders snorted and made noise to draw his attention while others slipped into his camp and took the chest.",al={"how did they rob him","how was thungrim robbed","distracted thungrim"},it="history"},{q="Why is Thun'grim living out in the Barrens instead of Orgrimmar?",a="Thun'grim keeps a solitary outpost in the eastern Barrens, where he arms and mentors warriors traveling from Durotar.",al={"why is thungrim here","why barrens camp"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze want the steel bars recovered?",a="Thun'grim is a master smith, and fine worked metal like these forged steel bars is vital to his craft. Having his supplies stolen right out from under his nose by thieving quilboar wounded his pride, but worse, it stripped him of the materials he needs to forge arms. He refuses to part with one of his crafted weapons until his stolen stock is restored.",al={"why recover forged steel","thungrim motive","why does thungrim want the steel back"},it="motive",add="46a881ef"},{q="Why does Thun'grim need you to retrieve the steel instead of going himself?",a="Thun'grim's eyesight has deteriorated severely in his old age, a weakness the Razormane quilboar exploited when they robbed him. Unable to see clearly enough to track them into their thorn-choked dens or fight them on equal footing, he relies on a capable warrior like you to venture into the quilboar encampments and retrieve the stolen chest.",al={"why cant thungrim get the steel","why send me thungrim","why does thungrim need help"},it="why_me",add="4f2d7c31"},{q="Who are the Razormanes holding the steel?",a="The thieves belong to the Razormane quilboar tribe, savage porcine humanoids native to the Barrens. Aggressive and fiercely territorial, they cluster in bristling bramble camps across the plains and frequently raid travelers and solitary camps for scavenged supplies, despite often having little understanding of how to work refined materials like forged steel.",al={"who are the razormanes","quilboar northwest","who stole the iron chest"},it="target",add="758f9f11"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you recover stolen steel and prove your worth before Thun'grim forges you a weapon.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you see why refined steel matters to the Horde in Kalimdor's harsh frontier.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face Razormane raids on camps and supply lines across the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","firegaze","forged steel","iron chest","quilboar","razormane","steel bars","thun'grim","warrior weapon"},rel={"quest:1502","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Thun'grim Firegaze",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1503,ri={"Forged Steel Bars"}},src={"Forged Steel"}}
E["quest:1515"] = {t="quest",n="Dogran's Captivity",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, a warlock faces a vital trial in Horde training: rescue a captured orc warrior. With Ken'zigla's Draught, you must find battered Grunt Dogran in a quilboar camp and give him strength to escape.",h="At Camp Taurajo, a warlock faces a vital trial in Horde training: rescue a captured orc warrior.",sec={{t="A Lonely Rescue",b="Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo will not risk Horde soldiers in a costly attack on the entrenched quilboar. Dogran's fate rests with you, an aspiring warlock armed only with Ken'zigla's Draught. Travel north through the brambles and hostile camps to find where the quilboar hold him captive.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Blood",b="Grunt Dogran lies badly battered among hostile quilboar in huts north of Taurajo. Ken'zigla's Draught gives him enough vigor to hobble to safety, but his injuries leave him permanently maimed. He loses an arm and a leg.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Grunt Dogran held?",a="Grunt Dogran is held in a small cluster of two quilboar huts directly north of Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.",al={"dogran location","where is dogran","find dogran barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why won't Grunt Logmar send soldiers to help?",a="Grunt Logmar cannot spare troops from Camp Taurajo's defense. He considers a rescue in heavily guarded quilboar territory too dangerous to risk more military lives.",al={"why no horde guard help","logmar soldiers","taurajo reinforcements"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Ken'zigla's Draught?",a="Ken'zigla's Draught is a potent, foul-tasting restorative tonic brewed to give the gravely injured Dogran enough strength to stand and escape quilboar captivity.",al={"kenzigla potion","what is the draught","dogran medicine"},it="item"},{q="What condition is Dogran in when found?",a="Dogran is on the brink of death, with extensive wounds and torture at the quilboar's hands. Even after drinking the draught, his arm and leg are damaged beyond repair.",al={"dogran injuries","is dogran alive","dogran arm leg"},sp=1},{q="How does this rescue relate to summoning a succubus?",a="Dogran carries a token tied to love and mortal devotion, emotions and ideas warlocks exploit to summon and bind a succubus.",al={"why do warlocks do this","succubus quest connection","warlock quest dogran"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who captured Dogran?",a="Dogran was captured by quilboar tribes living in the brambles north of Camp Taurajo.",al={"who took dogran","dogran captors","barrens kidnappers"},it="target"},{q="Why does Grunt Logmar want Dogran found?",a="Grunt Dogran is one of Logmar's comrades, captured by the quilboar while on patrol in the Barrens. While Logmar cannot spare Horde soldiers or risk a military assault to stage a rescue, he is unwilling to abandon his fellow grunt entirely. Having seen your determination to reach this point, Logmar permits you to attempt a solo mercy run with Ken'zigla's draught to give Dogran a fighting chance at survival.",al={"why help dogran","grunt logmar motive","why save dogran"},it="motive",add="b38341a7"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face a vital step toward understanding mortal passion and sacrifice, which are needed to summon a succubus.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know quilboar endanger patrols and outposts throughout the central Barrens.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Dogran's endurance through maiming and torture as the fierce resilience expected of an orcish grunt."},kw={"barrens","dogran","draught","ken'zigla","logmar","quilboar","succubus","taurajo","warlock"},rel={"quest:1511","quest:1512","quest:1471","quest:1509","npc:grunt-dogran","npc:grunt-logmar","topic:quilboar","subzone:camp-taurajo"},m={start="Grunt Logmar",["end"]="Grunt Dogran",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1515},src={"Dogran's Captivity"}}
E["quest:1524"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, an aspiring shaman begins the second trial in the search for communion with fire. Kranal Fiss sends the initiate across the Southfury River to a secluded mountaintop shrine in Durotar, carrying the unlit Torch of the Dormant Flame.",h="In the Barrens, an aspiring shaman begins the second trial in the search for communion with fire.",sec={{t="A Test of Readiness",b="Kranal Fiss entrusts the shaman with the Torch of the Dormant Flame. Raw mystical strength alone cannot meet fire’s demands; the trial calls for temperance, focus, and respect. The torch is both ritual instrument and proof to the shrine’s keeper that the bearer has been judged ready to attempt the trial.",sp=0},{t="The Hidden Peak",b="The shrine lies across the Southfury River, among Durotar’s southern crags. A weathered stone carved with a fire rune marks an obscure path that climbs toward one of the region’s highest peaks. At the summit, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is watched by Telf Joolam, a troll hermit. He turns away curious travelers and treasure hunters, keeping the sacred brazier from ordinary eyes until a petitioner arrives with the unlit torch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="Kranal Fiss gives the unlit torch as a token of intent. It identifies its bearer to Telf Joolam, keeper of the shrine, as a shaman initiate judged ready for the trial.",al={"why carry torch","dormant flame torch","torch meaning"},it="item"},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is a shamanic hermit of the Horde who watches over the Shrine of the Dormant Flame atop southern Durotar’s peaks. He guards the brazier from those who do not understand or respect the spirits.",al={"telf joolam","shrine keeper","who is the troll at the shrine"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the hidden path located?",a="The hidden trail begins in Durotar, south of the bridge over the Southfury River. Near the riverbank, where the mountains meet the coastline, a standing stone marked with a flame rune signals the narrow ascent up the high ridge.",al={"hidden path location","how to find shrine of the dormant flame","path up the mountain"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must the torch be brought unlit?",a="The torch is brought unlit because fire must be awakened and mastered through ritual, not simply claimed. Its dormant flame marks the state the shaman must kindle through communion.",al={"why is torch unlit","dormant torch ritual","why dormant flame"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after reaching Telf Joolam?",a="After Telf Joolam verifies the torch, he directs the initiate to harsher, more dangerous rites to kindle its dormant flame and prove mastery of elemental fire.",al={"next step call of fire","what after telf joolam"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is this shrine kept secret from the rest of the Horde?",a="The shrine is kept apart because elemental forces are volatile and dangerous in untrained hands. Shamanic traditions place sacred sites away from everyday settlements, so the curious and treasure hunters do not disturb resting spirits or invite calamity.",al={"why secret shrine","is the shrine hidden"}},{q="Why does Kranal Fiss send you to the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="Kranal Fiss recognizes that while your spirit possesses the raw strength to wield fire, raw power alone is not enough. Fire is dangerous, destructive, and untamed; to grant you its totem prematurely would risk catastrophe. As a mentor, his duty is to ensure you undergo the sacred trials of preparation and respect. He sends you to Telf Joolam so that you may prove your discipline and earn the right to carry the flame before the elements themselves.",al={"why does kranal fiss want this done","kranal fiss motive","why kranal sends you"},it="motive",add="10005cfa"},{q="Why must you make this journey instead of someone else?",a="This pilgrimage is not a simple errand or a matter of military defense—it is an intensely personal spiritual rite of passage. The Shrine of the Dormant Flame is kept strictly hidden from mundane members of the Horde and ordinary guards. Only an initiate pursuing communion with the fire elements can carry the dormant torch, seek Telf Joolam's guidance, and prove their worthiness to wield the element's power.",al={"why me call of fire","why send me shrine dormant flame","why can't guards go"},it="why_me",add="b8cc7d40"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you seek the Fire Totem by communing with Kalimdor’s elemental forces. That path takes you to remote shrines, beyond simple instruction.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share shamanic teachings with orcs, tauren, and trolls. Those traditions send disciples from the Barrens’ plains to Durotar’s sacred cliffs."},kw={"barrens","call of fire","durotar","fire totem","kranal fiss","shrine of the dormant flame","southfury river","telf joolam"},rel={"npc:telf-joolam","subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame","subzone:hidden-path","subzone:southfury-river","zone:durotar","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},m={start="Kranal Fiss",["end"]="Telf Joolam",level="11",faction="Horde",id=1524},src={"Call of Fire (2)"}}
E["quest:1530"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="barrens",s="Islen Waterseer sends Horde shamans south through the Barrens to seek Brine. There, they learn what water can cleanse and heal.",h="Islen Waterseer sends Horde shamans south through the Barrens to seek Brine.",sec={{t="Lessons of the Tide",b="Islen Waterseer teaches that water brings rebirth. Its flow can carve rock, wash away impurities, and mend flesh, but its healing depends on purity. Polluted water brings blight instead of life. Every shaman must understand this balance before seeking communion with water.",sp=0},{t="A Recluse in the Dust",b="You travel far south through the arid Barrens to find Brine. Quilboar raids trouble the wastes, yet Brine lives alone without guards or fear. She holds the knowledge and trials that help you bind yourself to water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Islen Waterseer?",a="Islen Waterseer is a shaman master on the Barrens coast, south of the Merchant Coast. She guides Horde shamans through the trials of communion with water spirits.",al={"islen","waterseer","who sends this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why live in the southern Barrens surrounded by quilboar?",a="Brine lives alone in the southern wastes despite constant quilboar harassment. She knows the danger seems foolish to outsiders, but keeps her reasons private and tests whether you have the fortitude to find her.",al={"why does brine live there","brine quilboar","brine location"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the purpose of the water sapta?",a="A sapta is a ceremonial mixture that changes a shaman’s perception, letting them see and speak with elemental spirits invisible to mortal eyes.",al={"sapta","water sapta use","why get water sapta"},it="item"},{q="What core lesson does water represent to a shaman?",a="Water brings rebirth, cleansing, and renewal. Pure water can heal, but tainted or stagnant water brings decay and devastation.",al={"lesson of water","elemental meaning water","water rebirth"},it="purpose"},{q="Who can undertake this journey?",a="Horde shamans who have proved their dedication and attuned to earth and fire are sent to undertake the Call of Water trials.",al={"who gets call of water","is call of water horde only"},gp=true},{q="What threats lie on the path to Brine?",a="The southern Barrens are dangerous, with aggressive quilboar tribes defending thorned dens and beasts hunting wanderers far from the safety of Crossroads or Camp Taurajo.",al={"dangers southern barrens","path to brine"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Islen Waterseer send you to Brine?",a="Islen Waterseer seeks to guide you through the sacred trials of communion with water. She teaches that water embodies rebirth, healing, and devastating corruption if left impure. To prepare the water sapta needed to pierce the veil and perceive the elemental spirits, she directs you to Brine, who holds the practical knowledge and ingredients required for your next rite of passage.",al={"why send to brine","islen waterseer motive","why seek brine"},it="motive",add="c40eecf4"},{q="Why does Islen Waterseer have you undertake this journey alone?",a="Communing with the elements is a deeply personal spiritual journey that every aspiring shaman must walk for themselves. Neither guards nor elders can undertake a trial of understanding on your behalf. Seeking out Brine through the hostile southern Barrens tests your resolve, self-reliance, and dedication to earning the favor of the water spirits.",al={"why must i go to brine","why me call of water","why send the player alone"},it="why_me",add="d6b5acd2"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, communion with water marks a key step in your growth. It joins the strength of earth and the force of fire with water’s healing power.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel across Kalimdor to master the elements and honor the spirits that grant the Warchief’s shamans their vital magic."},kw={"barrens","brine","call of water","islen waterseer","quilboar","rebirth","shaman","water sapta"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","npc:brine","quest:972","zone:barrens","topic:quilboar"},m={start="Islen Waterseer",["end"]="Brine",level="22",faction="Horde",id=1530},src={"Call of Water (2)"}}
E["quest:1534"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="barrens",s="A shaman travels from the Barrens to the Ruins of Stardust for the final gathering trial in the journey to earn Call of Water. Brine sends the initiate north into Ashenvale to draw pure water from its ancient fountain.",h="A shaman travels from the Barrens to the Ruins of Stardust for the final gathering trial in the journey to...",sec={{t="Journey Into the Twilight Grove",b="After gathering water from the pool below Brine’s hut in the Barrens and the pure well of Tarren Mill, the shaman needs one final essence. Brine sends the initiate north across the dry plains and into Ashenvale, an ancient woodland sacred to the night elves. The dry Barrens give way to Ashenvale’s deep canopy, where water takes another form. A shaman must understand this variety to live in harmony with the element.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Stardust",b="Beyond the shimmering waters of Mystral Lake, near the mountain pass between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains, lie the Ruins of Stardust. An ancient fountain rests among quiet waters and old stones in this secluded elven sanctum. Untamed elemental and nature spirits guard the ruins and resent intruders. The shaman must tread carefully to draw water from the fountain.",sp=0},{t="The Draught of Purest Water",b="Brine receives the filled blue waterskin after the shaman’s pilgrimage across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. She combines the pure fountain water with the samples from the Barrens watering hole and Tarren Mill, then prepares a vial of the purest water. This draught prepares the shaman for the next trial: communion with water elemental spirits through the seer Islen Waterseer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the Ruins of Stardust located?",a="The Ruins of Stardust lie in southwestern Ashenvale. From the Barrens, travel north, then follow the roads west past Mystral Lake toward the foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"ruins of stardust location","where is stardust","how to get to ruins of stardust"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Brine need water from an elven ruin?",a="A shaman gathers water from different expressions of the element to commune with the water spirits. The fountain in the Ruins of Stardust holds ancient, magically pure water untouched by the Barrens’ dry blight, completing the three essences Brine needs for her ritual mixture.",al={"why ashenvale water","why ruins of stardust","reason for stardust water"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What threats exist around the Ruins of Stardust?",a="Protective beasts and nature spirits guard the ruins and nearby waters. Territorial water elementals and beasts native to Ashenvale attack those who disturb the grove.",al={"stardust enemies","is stardust dangerous","who guards the fountain"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Brine and why is she helping?",a="Brine is an ascetic orc shaman who lives in a lone hut in the southern Barrens. As an elder guide assisting Islen Waterseer, she tests prospective shamans’ patience, endurance, and understanding of water before bestowing the element’s blessings.",al={"who is brine","brine lore","what is brine's role"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after bringing this water to Brine?",a="When Brine receives the third sample, she combines the waters to make a draught of the purest water. Then she sends the shaman to Islen Waterseer on the eastern Barrens coast for visionary communion with the elementals.",al={"next step call of water","what happens next","where do i go after brine"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is Ashenvale safe for low-level Horde shamans?",a="Ashenvale is contested territory where night elves and the Horde clash. The route through the southern woods avoids major night elf settlements such as Astranaar, but wandering wildlife, aggressive elementals, and Alliance patrols are hazards for an initiate.",al={"is ashenvale dangerous","level for ashenvale quest"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="Why does Brine want this done?",a="Brine guides aspiring shamans through their water trial. By gathering pure samples from distant and sacred places, you prove your dedication to understanding the element. Once you secure water from the ancient fountain at the Ruins of Stardust, she can combine all your gathered waters into a draught of utmost purity, completing her part in your rite of passage and preparing you to return to Islen Waterseer.",al={"why does brine help","brine motive call of water","why gather stardust water"},it="motive",add="d600fc8e"},{q="What is the Filled Blue Waterskin for?",a="The skin holds the pristine water drawn from the sacred fountain within the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale. It serves as the third and final pure water component Brine needs to concoct a vial of unblemished water for your shamanic trials.",al={"what does filled blue waterskin do","filled blue waterskin use","why fill blue waterskin"},it="item",add="bc32fa0f"},{q="Why does Brine send you rather than getting the water herself?",a="This journey is an integral part of your rite of passage as a shaman. Seeking out distant, sacred waters tests your endurance, respect for the elements, and devotion. Brine remains at her pond to prepare the rituals, but the pilgrimage itself must be undertaken with your own hands.",al={"why do i have to get the water","why doesn't brine go to ashenvale","why send me call of water"},it="why_me",add="d1cea88a"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you cross dangerous borders in search of balance and gather the final fluid essence needed to bind the Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you enter ancient Kaldorei lands, where the Warsong Outriders wage an ongoing timber war against hostile night elf sentinels.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you travel from the arid homelands of central Kalimdor to sacred groves remembered in myth and elder songs."},kw={"ashenvale","blue waterskin","brine","call of water","islen waterseer","mystral lake","ruins of stardust","shaman"},rel={"npc:brine","subzone:ruins-of-stardust","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","quest:1034"},m={start="Brine",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1534,ri={"Filled Blue Waterskin"}},src={"Call of Water (5)"}}
E["quest:1535"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="barrens",s="Brine sends shamans into the Barrens to gather water for a sapta. The trial begins with a sample from the guarded pool below her hill, where water means survival.",h="Brine sends shamans into the Barrens to gather water for a sapta.",sec={{t="A Lesson in the Desert",b="Brine asks shaman initiates to study water in all its forms before she grants the water sapta that lets them commune with the spirits. In the arid Barrens, water means the difference between survival and starvation. She asks them to notice what water makes possible: forests flourish where it flows, deserts starve where it is absent, and living beings will kill to protect even the humblest spring.",sp=0},{t="The Quilboar's Hoard",b="Native quilboar fiercely guard the watering hole beneath Brine's hill. They treat every pool as a priceless hoard and feast whenever rain comes. Brine regrets the violence their hoarding brings, but their insular greed and divided clans keep their threat contained. For the other races surviving on the plains, that leaves a precarious balance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of collecting water for Brine?",a="Brine needs samples of pure water from distinct corners of the world to brew a ceremonial water sapta. The draught opens an initiate's perception, allowing communion with elemental water spirits.",al={"why get water","brine water task","call of water quest 3 purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Why is the watering hole below Brine so heavily contested?",a="In the parched Barrens, water is the most precious resource. Local quilboar treat every pool as sacred treasure and fight fiercely against anyone who tries to draw from it.",al={"why are quilboar guarding water","quilboar pond","water hole barrens"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Brine?",a="Brine is an orc shaman and hermit who lives in a lonely hut overlooking the southern Barrens. Her deep wisdom about water and elemental spirits guides Horde shamans toward communion.",al={"who is brine","brine barrens","brine npc"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after returning the filled brown waterskin?",a="After you return with a sample from the watering hole, Brine sends you farther afield to gather pristine water from very different places, including the well of Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"what next call of water","after watering hole","next step brine"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Brine remark on the quilboar's division?",a="Brine sees the quilboar's territorial ways and clan rivalries as causes of their misery. If they united instead of fighting over isolated springs, they would threaten the rest of the Barrens far more.",al={"brine quilboar commentary","why quilboar fighting each other"},it="people"},{q="What is a sapta?",a="A sapta is a mystical elixir shamans prepare from gathered reagents and waters aligned with the elements. Drinking it expands spiritual sight, revealing elemental beings usually hidden from mortal eyes.",al={"what is sapta","water sapta meaning"},it="power"},{q="What is the Filled Brown Waterskin for?",a="The Filled Brown Waterskin holds a sample of water gathered from the disputed pond below Brine's hill. Brine requires you to collect this water not merely as an ingredient to brew the Water Sapta, but as an object lesson in your shamanic trials. By fetching it, you witness firsthand the fierce attachment and bloodshed that scarce, life-giving liquid provokes among the local quilboar.",al={"filled brown waterskin purpose","why filled brown waterskin","filled brown waterskin"},it="item",add="6eca6e0d"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you learn that water brings healing and restoration, but also sparks conflict and the desperate struggle to survive.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the challenge of controlling and sharing water in the Barrens, where tribes and beasts constantly fight over every trickle."},kw={"barrens","brine","brown waterskin","call of water","quilboar","sapta","watering hole"},rel={"npc:brine","zone:barrens","topic:quilboar"},m={start="Brine",level="22",faction="Horde",id=1535,ri={"Filled Brown Waterskin"}},src={"Call of Water (3)"}}
E["quest:1536"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="barrens",s="You set out from the Barrens for a pure spring in Forsaken-held Tarren Mill. The water will help Brine prepare the Water Sapta, and its survival offers a lesson in hope.",h="You set out from the Barrens for a pure spring in Forsaken-held Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Miraculous Spring",b="Brine sends you across the sea to Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills for water to prepare the Water Sapta. Human resistance and the newly allied Forsaken surround the town, yet its small central well gives pure spring water. To Brine, the spring is a sacred remnant of cleanliness in an unhallowed land.",sp=0},{t="Endurance in Darkness",b="Brine sees the pure well in Tarren Mill as more than an ingredient. She compares its endurance to Warchief Thrall, who bore hardship, captivity, and sorrow before rising to lead the orcish people. Thrall gives the Horde hope, and the well shows that life and purity can endure through tragedy and corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the water sample collected?",a="You draw the sample from the well in the center of Tarren Mill, an old human settlement in Hillsbrad Foothills now held by the Forsaken.",al={"tarren mill water","where is the well","call of water well location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Brine send you so far away for water?",a="Brine needs distinct water essences to brew the Water Sapta, which lets shamans perceive elemental spirits. She found this spring on an earlier journey into Hillsbrad and values its purity amid Forsaken decay as both potent and instructive.",al={"why tarren mill","why hillsbrad water","why brine wants this water"},it="motive"},{q="What is Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is a modest human town in northern Hillsbrad Foothills, now held by Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken as a fortified Horde outpost against local human forces.",al={"tarren mill history","who owns tarren mill"},it="place"},{q="How does this quest connect to Thrall?",a="Brine compares the pure well to Warchief Thrall. Though enslaved and made to suffer, Thrall kept the strength and vision to lead the new Horde, as the well keeps its freshness amid plague and death.",al={"brine thrall dialogue","thrall connection"},it="history"},{q="What happens after returning the filled waterskin?",a="Brine accepts the filled red waterskin and tells you she needs one more distinct water sample to finish the reagent mixture for your Water Sapta.",al={"what next call of water","after tarren mill water"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is the well's purity considered unusual?",a="Much of Lordaeron was defiled by the Scourge's plague of undeath, and Forsaken settlements are rarely linked with fresh springs. The central well in Tarren Mill still gives pristine water, a rare uncorrupted remnant.",al={"why is tarren mill water pure","forsaken polluted well"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Filled Red Waterskin for?",a="The Filled Red Waterskin holds pure spring water drawn from the well at Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad. Brine requires this untainted sample alongside others to brew a special reagent for your Water Sapta. Drinking that draught will grant you the spiritual sight needed to commune directly with water spirits.",al={"filled red waterskin use","why filled red waterskin","water sample tarren mill"},it="item",add="05ee6a54"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you travel far for water, learning to seek harmony and life amid the bitter lands of the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior or shaman born in Kalimdor, you visit Tarren Mill and meet your uneasy new allies, the Forsaken, at the front line against Hillsbrad's human defenders.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can reflect on Thrall's legacy of survival and strength, and the heavy price paid for your freedom."},kw={"barrens","brine","call of water","hillsbrad","sapta","shaman","tarren mill","thrall","waterskin"},rel={"npc:brine","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:barrens","npc:thrall","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Brine",level="22",faction="Horde",id=1536,ri={"Filled Red Waterskin"}},src={"Call of Water (4)"}}
E["quest:1716"] = {t="quest",n="Devourer of Souls",z="barrens",s="An Alliance warlock crosses the sea to seek Takar the Seer’s counsel on summoning a succubus. Gakin the Darkbinder sends Stormwind initiates into the Barrens for the wisdom they need.",h="An Alliance warlock crosses the sea to seek Takar the Seer’s counsel on summoning a succubus.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Journey West",b="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter, Gakin the Darkbinder guides promising warlocks toward summoning a succubus. The demon devours souls, destroys hearts, and dominates minds, so it cannot be called blindly into Azeroth. A warlock needs a potent lure: an object tied to pure love. That token draws the succubus from the Twisting Nether, where the warlock can defeat and bind it. Stormwind’s covens cannot teach them where to find such an object.",sp=0},{t="The Seer in Hostile Territory",b="Gakin sends his pupils across the Great Sea to Kalimdor in search of the needed catalyst. Takar the Seer waits in the arid Barrens, near the Horde settlement of Camp Taurajo. To reach him, an Alliance warlock must cross wilderness patrolled by hostile centaur, quilboar, and Horde warriors. The journey tests whether a summoner can survive before the ritual even begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="You travel from Stormwind to Kalimdor to learn how to summon and bind a succubus under your absolute command.",al={"why do devourer of souls","succubus quest goal","warlock succubus questline"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do I have to go all the way to the Barrens?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder sends you to the Barrens because Takar the Seer has the occult knowledge you need to find a symbol of pure love, the lure required to summon a succubus.",al={"why kalimdor","why go to the barrens","why send me so far"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Gakin the Darkbinder?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder is a master summoner who works in the catacombs beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind. He teaches novice warlocks demonic pacts, bindings, and the dark arts away from the city guard’s eyes.",al={"gakin darkbinder lore","who gives quest devourer of souls"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Takar the Seer?",a="Takar the Seer is a mystic who lives in the central Barrens, just outside the tauren outpost of Camp Taurajo. He points traveling warlocks toward relics that can tempt demons into Azeroth.",al={"where is takar the seer","takar seer lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does a succubus require a symbol of love to summon?",a="A succubus is drawn to genuine, pure affection and devours it. As Gakin explains, the demon corrupts hearts and dominates minds, so a romantic relic can lure it from the Twisting Nether.",al={"why love for succubus","succubus lure lore","bait for succubus"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is the Barrens safe for an Alliance character?",a="No. The Barrens is Horde territory, with hostile beasts, quilboar tribes, and settlements such as Camp Taurajo. Keep a low profile and avoid guards while seeking Takar.",al={"is barrens dangerous","will horde attack me in barrens"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder want this done?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder is training you to bend more dangerous demonic entities to your will. To advance your mastery as a warlock, he requires you to summon, overcome, and bind a succubus—a cruel devourer of souls and dominator of minds. Because such an entity cannot be lured across the Twisting Nether without a potent emotional lure, Gakin sends you on this long path to prepare the ritual bait necessary to bend the creature to your service.",al={"why does gakin send me","gakin motive devourer of souls","why summon succubus gakin"},it="motive",add="25fde1fe"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, binding a succubus marks your passage toward mastering mental manipulation and seduction magic. Reaching exotic ritual reagents takes physical daring.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance spellcaster, you travel deep into contested Horde lands, across the sea and the continent."},kw={"camp taurajo","gakin the darkbinder","heartswood","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","succubus","takar the seer","the barrens","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","npc:takar-the-seer","quest:1685","quest:1738","quest:1471","zone:barrens","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Gakin the Darkbinder",["end"]="Takar the Seer",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1716},src={"Devourer of Souls (Stormwind)"}}
E["quest:1719"] = {t="quest",n="The Affray",z="barrens",s="On Fray Island, warriors face a trial before Klannoc Macleod will train them. The Affray pits them against island challengers and their champion.",h="On Fray Island, warriors face a trial before Klannoc Macleod will train them.",sec={{t="A Proving Ground in the Great Sea",b="Fray Island lies apart from the mainland, drawing brawlers, outcasts, and combat instructors. Klannoc Macleod does not teach every wanderer who arrives by boat. Aspiring warriors must first enter the Affray, where stamina and awareness in battle prove who can fight beyond mere boasting.",sp=0},{t="The Circle of Iron and Blood",b="A warrior begins the Affray by stepping onto the central iron grate among the spectators. Ringmaster Twiggy Flathead then sends challengers into the ring one after another. Those who survive face the island's heavyweight champion, Big Will. Defeating him is the only way to earn Klannoc's respect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Affray?",a="The Affray tests aspiring warriors in a series of arena fights on Fray Island. Klannoc Macleod uses it to judge whether they are ready for advanced combat training.",al={"affray trial","what is the affray","fray island arena"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Affray take place?",a="The Affray takes place on Fray Island, off the eastern coast of the Barrens in the Great Sea.",al={"where is the affray","affray location"},it="place"},{q="Who organizes the trial?",a="Warrior trainer Klannoc Macleod oversees the island's fighters and sets the trial. Twiggy Flathead directs the bouts from the edge of the pit.",al={"who runs the affray","affray organizer"},it="in_charge"},{q="How does the combat in the ring work?",a="A warrior steps onto the central iron grate to signal readiness. Twiggy Flathead sends Affray Challengers into the pit in waves, then releases the island champion, Big Will.",al={"how does the fight work","affray waves","starting the affray"},gp=true},{q="Who is Big Will?",a="Big Will is the reigning champion of Fray Island's brawlers. Defeating him is the final requirement to pass the Affray.",al={"big will","who is big will","fray island champion"},it="target"},{q="Why must warriors complete this trial?",a="Klannoc Macleod will not teach his martial techniques until a warrior proves their toughness in combat against multiple opponents.",al={"why do the affray","affray purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Klannoc Macleod require you to fight instead of testing you himself?",a="Klannoc Macleod does not waste his advanced combat instruction on every boastful brawler who sails to Fray Island. The Affray exists specifically as an endurance trial for rising warriors. By throwing you into the pit against waves of seasoned challengers and the champion Big Will, Klannoc can watch from a distance and judge your grit, crowd control, and stamina under genuine pressure before taking you on as a student.",al={"why me klannoc","why does klannoc test me","why fight the affray"},it="why_me",add="0df51000"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face the Affray as a trial of your battle stances and endurance. Proving yourself there opens the way to deeper mastery of your craft."},kw={"affray","barrens","big will","fray island","klannoc macleod","twiggy flathead","warrior trial"},rel={"npc:klannoc-macleod","quest:1718","quest:1791","subzone:fray-island","zone:barrens"},m={start="Klannoc Macleod",level="30",id=1719},src={"The Affray"}}
E["quest:1738"] = {t="quest",n="Heartswood",z="barrens",s="In the years since the Third War, Heartswood draws warlocks toward an old night elf tragedy. Takar the Seer sends them into Ashenvale for Gakin the Darkbinder, who needs the wood to lure and subjugate a succubus in Stormwind.",h="In the years since the Third War, Heartswood draws warlocks toward an old night elf tragedy.",sec={{t="A Monument to Tragic Love",b="Takar the Seer says Heartswood grew where the night elf lovers Anathera and Latherion fell during the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago. Their last breaths and devotion nourished the tree. To mortal eyes, it marks a tragic love; to practitioners of the dark arts, its concentrated emotion is potent magical fuel.",sp=0},{t="Baiting the Succubus",b="Succubi feed on mortal passion, desire, and torment. Takar knows ordinary temptations cannot match an artifact filled with thousands of years of devotion. A piece of Heartswood gives Gakin the Darkbinder the catalyst he needs to draw a cunning demon through the Nether and into a summoning circle in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Ordil'Aran",b="The Heartswood tree grows among the Ruins of Ordil'Aran in northwestern Ashenvale. Wild beasts, hostile lands, and Dark Strand cultists who have occupied the elven ruins stand in the way. Once recovered, the wood must cross the sea to the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, where the ritual of subjugation begins.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do warlocks need Heartswood to summon a succubus?",a="Succubi are drawn to passion, desire, and strong emotional bonds. Heartswood grew where two devoted night elf lovers died together ten thousand years ago, and their lingering passion fills the wood. That makes it ideal bait to draw a succubus through the Nether.",al={"why heartswood","succubus bait","why wood for succubus"},it="item"},{q="Where does the Heartswood tree grow?",a="The Heartswood tree grows in the Ruins of Ordil'Aran, in northwestern Ashenvale, not far south of Darkshore. Sinister cultists have taken control of the area.",al={"heartswood location","where is the heartswood","where to find heartswood"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who were Anathera and Latherion?",a="Anathera and Latherion were night elves who fought side by side during the War of the Ancients. They fell together on the battlefield, and Heartswood grew where they drew their last breaths, marking their enduring love.",al={"anathera and latherion","who were the lovers","lovers of ashenvale"},it="history"},{q="Who is Takar the Seer?",a="Takar the Seer is a human seer allied with Stormwind's warlocks. He lives as a hermit in the southern Barrens near Camp Taurajo, using his sight to look into the past and find forgotten relics for Gakin the Darkbinder.",al={"who is takar","takar the seer","barrens hermit"},it="identity"},{q="How does an Alliance warlock travel safely to Ashenvale from the Barrens?",a="Alliance travelers crossing the Barrens must avoid the Horde outpost at the Mor'shan Rampart, where guards watch closely. Warlocks can slip through an unguarded breach just east of the main gate, take the high road through Stonetalon, or swim the border river.",al={"how to get to ashenvale","bypassing morshan","avoiding horde rampart"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What happens after Gakin receives the Heartswood?",a="Gakin uses the wood to prepare a ritual in the catacombs beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind. He draws a summoning circle to pull a succubus from the Twisting Nether, then tasks the warlock with defeating and subjugating her.",al={"what next after heartswood","what does gakin do with heartswood"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Takar the Seer send you to find the Heartswood?",a="Takar acts as a far-seeing ally to Gakin the Darkbinder and his circle in Stormwind. He prepared for your arrival by scouring the mists of time with his mystical sight, locating an artifact potent enough to snare and entice a succubus across the planes. Assisting aspiring warlocks in their trials is his role within their clandestine brotherhood.",al={"takar motive heartswood","why does takar help","why is takar having me get heartswood"},it="motive",add="bf8a48f3"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you need Heartswood to summon and enslave a succubus, whose powers can turn your enemies' minds against them on the battlefield.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance spellcaster, you cross contested wilderness and face hostile Horde outposts among ancient night elf ruins in Kalimdor.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you may rely on far-flung scouts like Takar the Seer to find relics from old Kalimdor, beyond what human arcanists have recorded."},kw={"anathera","ashenvale","barrens","dark strand","gakin the darkbinder","heartswood","latherion","ordil'aran","succubus","takar the seer"},rel={"npc:takar-the-seer","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1472","quest:1471","quest:1685","subzone:ruins-of-ordil-aran","zone:ashenvale","topic:war-of-the-ancients"},m={start="Takar the Seer",["end"]="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1738,ri={"Heartswood"}},src={"Heartswood (quest)"}}
E["quest:1740"] = {t="quest",n="The Orb of Soran'ruk",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Doan Karhan sets warlocks to gather the scattered pieces of Soran'ruk. They seek to rebuild an orb that holds a disgraced demon's essence.",h="In the southern Barrens, Doan Karhan sets warlocks to gather the scattered pieces of Soran'ruk.",sec={{t="Vessels of the Disgraced",b="Failure within the Burning Legion brings an eternal sentence. When lesser demons lose favor with their masters, their spirits are bound inside crystal orbs. The Legion gives these prisons to mortal conjurers and warlocks as vessels for power under demonic control. Shattering an orb does not free its captive; even the shards hold potent magic.",sp=0},{t="Scattered Across Continents",b="Soran'ruk's orb lies in pieces across two continents. Twilight's Hammer cultists hold smaller fragments in the damp caverns of Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale. A sorcerer in the haunted ruins of Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine Forest claimed the larger, mostly intact half. Doan Karhan has spent his life studying Legion orbs and assembled the Orb of Zargain before. With the recovered pieces, he can restore Soran'ruk as a working implement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Orb of Soran'ruk?",a="Soran'ruk was a demon of the Burning Legion who fell out of favor. By demonic custom, its spirit was imprisoned in a magical orb and given to mortal practitioners. The orb was later shattered, but its fragments still hold the demon's power.",al={"soranruk lore","what is soranruk","who was soranruk"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Doan Karhan?",a="Doan Karhan is a reclusive warlock who lives in the southern Barrens and has devoted his life to studying and rebuilding the Burning Legion's orbs. He spent many years assembling the Orb of Zargain and helps new warlocks piece together Soran'ruk.",al={"who is doan karhan","doan karhan backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the orb broken across two different dungeons?",a="The orb was split into two main pieces. Twilight's Hammer cultists hold smaller fragments in Blackfathom Deeps, while a wizard claimed the larger remnant in Shadowfang Keep.",al={"why are pieces in bfd and sfk","where are soranruk fragments"},it="history"},{q="Who can undertake this task?",a="Warlocks seeking to advance their craft and master artifacts made from imprisoned demonic spirits can pursue this rite.",al={"who can do this quest","is orb of soranruk warlock only"},gp=true},{q="What does Doan Karhan do with the recovered fragments?",a="Doan Karhan studies the recovered fragments to further his research into Legion relics, then rebuilds them as a magical implement shaped to the warlock's choosing.",al={"what happens after collecting shards","reforming soranruk"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Orb of Zargain?",a="The Orb of Zargain is a prison for a demon of the Legion who fell out of favor. Doan Karhan tracked it down and spent many years rebuilding it for his own use.",al={"orb of zargain","zargain lore"},it="item"},{q="Why does Doan Karhan want the fragments of the Orb of Soran'ruk?",a="Doan Karhan has dedicated his life to studying the demonic orbs forged by the Burning Legion and mastering the art of their recreation. Recovering the dispersed shards of the Orb of Soran'ruk allows him to examine the vessel of a disgraced demon's imprisoned spirit firsthand, putting his deep research into practice.",al={"why doan karhan wants orb","doan karhan motive","why gather fragments"},it="motive",add="f1114029"},{q="What is the Soran'ruk Fragment?",a="The Soran'ruk Fragments are small shards from the shattered Orb of Soran'ruk, a vessel binding the spirit of a demon who fell out of favor with the Burning Legion. Cultists of the Twilight's Hammer carried these pieces into Blackfathom Deeps to harness their lingering demonic power.",al={"soranruk fragment use","what are soran'ruk fragments","blackfathom deeps fragments"},it="item",add="32900559"},{q="What is the Large Soran'ruk Fragment?",a="The Large Soran'ruk Fragment is the primary remaining piece of the Orb of Soran'ruk. It retains enough concentrated demonic essence that a dark sorcerer within the haunted halls of Shadowfang Keep claimed it to fuel his own spellcraft.",al={"large soranruk fragment","shadowfang keep fragment","large fragment use"},it="item",add="321416b0"},{q="Who holds the fragments of the orb?",a="The fragments were split between two dangerous factions seeking demonic power. The smaller shards fell into the hands of the Twilight's Hammer acolytes scheming beneath the waves of Blackfathom Deeps, while the larger remnant was seized by a cunning sorcerer lurking inside Shadowfang Keep.",al={"who has the fragments","where are soranruk pieces","who holds the orb pieces"},it="target",add="120120b9"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Rebuilding Soran'ruk marks a major milestone for you as a warlock. It teaches how the Legion disciplines its own kind and how bound demons can be harnessed in working implements.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find Doan Karhan in the harsh southern Barrens. Traveling conjurers come to these plains to seek advanced dark lore."},kw={"blackfathom","demon","doan karhan","orb of soran'ruk","orb of zargain","shadowfang","soranruk","warlock"},rel={"npc:doan-karhan","zone:barrens","zone:blackfathom","zone:shadowfang","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:burning-legion"},m={start="Doan Karhan",level="25",id=1740,ri={"Large Soran'ruk Fragment","Soran'ruk Fragment"}},src={"The Orb of Soran'ruk"}}
E["quest:1758"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of the Cabal",z="barrens",s="Above Ratchet, Strahad Farsan sends an aspiring Alliance warlock to the Library of Ironforge. A felhunter’s hunger can overwhelm an unprepared summoner, and the Tome of the Cabal holds the knowledge needed to summon and bind the demon.",h="Above Ratchet, Strahad Farsan sends an aspiring Alliance warlock to the Library of Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Beast That Feeds on Magic",b="An imp, a voidwalker, or a succubus can be subdued through ritual, but a felhunter brings a different hazard. Felhunters serve the Burning Legion and hunt down arcane energy to devour it. A standard summoning circle will crumble before one, draining the summoner’s magic before a binding can take hold. From his redoubt in the Barrens, Strahad Farsan watches over Ratchet and knows an amateur must not attempt the binding unprepared.",sp=0},{t="The First Binding",b="An acolyte needs the arcane formulas in the Tome of the Cabal to draw forth and bind a felhunter safely. The earliest mortal cabal of warlocks who successfully broke a felhunter without outside aid authored the manuscript. Its pages detail the geomancy, materials, and binding runes needed to withstand the creature’s hunger. The copy was lost long ago, leaving Strahad and his circle without the masterwork.",sp=0},{t="The Hoarder of Dun Morogh",b="Strahad sends Alliance warlocks across the Great Sea to the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge, since he cannot provide the text himself. Krom Stoutarm, an itinerant dwarven warlock, resides there and spends his twilight years combing through ancient manuscripts and library records. If any trace of the lost grimoire remains recorded in the Eastern Kingdoms, it rests buried in Krom’s meticulous catalogs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I need to find the Tome of the Cabal?",a="The Tome of the Cabal holds precise instructions from the first mortal warlocks who summoned and subdued a felhunter without outside aid. Ordinary summoning rituals cannot entrap a demon that actively feeds on magical energy.",al={"what is tome of cabal","why find book","tome of cabal purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Krom Stoutarm?",a="Krom Stoutarm is a wandering dwarven warlock who resides in the Library of the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. He spends his days holed up among dusty tomes, cataloguing ancient historical records.",al={"where is krom","who is krom stoutarm","krom ironforge"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Strahad Farsan in the Barrens?",a="Strahad Farsan is an accomplished human warlock with a quiet, neutral redoubt on the bluffs above Ratchet. Outside the watchful eyes of the Kirin Tor and Stormwind’s authorities, he trains both Alliance and Horde practitioners in powerful demonology.",al={"strahad location","why ratchet","who is strahad"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after I speak to Krom Stoutarm?",a="Krom Stoutarm recalls references to the tome in old cataloguing registers. He charges you with tracking down its lost parts and recovering the rare reagents needed to reconstruct the grimoire.",al={"next quest","after krom","tome of cabal next step"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can Horde warlocks do this quest?",a="This journey to Ironforge is for Alliance warlocks. Strahad gives Horde warlocks an equivalent task, sending them to find knowledgeable contacts within Horde territory.",al={"horde version","is this alliance only"},gp=true},{q="What demon does this questline unlock?",a="Completing the Tome of the Cabal chain brings ritual combat against a summoned felhunter. The warlock learns to summon and bind one as a permanent minion.",al={"which demon","felhunter quest","what pet do i get"},gp=true},{q="Why does Strahad Farsan want me to find the Tome of the Cabal?",a="Strahad Farsan is guiding your growth as a warlock, preparing you to command one of the Nether's most ferocious predators: a felhunter. Summoning such a beast requires intricate, hazardous rituals far beyond standard magic circles. The lost Tome of the Cabal holds the original rites crafted by the first warlocks who successfully bound a felhunter without aid. Strahad and his acolytes stand ready to weave the summoning circles above Ratchet, but without the specific lore preserved in the Tome, the ritual cannot safely begin.",al={"why does strahad want the tome","strahad farsan motive","strahad cabal tome reason"},it="motive",add="8ce24f0c"},{q="Why does Strahad send me instead of retrieving the Tome himself?",a="Subjugating a demonic minion is a deeply personal trial that tests your resourcefulness and resolve. Strahad provides the expertise, ritual sanctum, and acolytes to anchor the magic, but the burden of securing the necessary knowledge rests entirely on you. Moreover, Strahad remains entrenched above Ratchet managing dangerous arcane forces, whereas you can travel freely to Ironforge's Hall of Explorers to consult scholars like Krom Stoutarm and recover the scattered relics yourself.",al={"why does strahad send me","why cant strahad get the tome","why send player to ironforge"},it="why_me",add="327d5815"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, obtaining the Tome of the Cabal is a rite of passage toward mastery over felhunters, taking you beyond lesser servants into anti-magic demonology.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance practitioner, you cross back from the frontier of Kalimdor to the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge to seek illicit dark texts.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see that not everyone buried in the Hall of Explorers digs up Titan artifacts; Krom Stoutarm privately compiles demonic lore."},kw={"felhunter","hall of explorers","ironforge","krom stoutarm","ratchet","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal","warlock"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","npc:krom-stoutarm","quest:1798","quest:1471","subzone:library-ironforge","zone:ironforge","zone:barrens","topic:alliance"},m={start="Strahad Farsan",["end"]="Krom Stoutarm",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1758},src={"Tome of the Cabal (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:1791"] = {t="quest",n="The Windwatcher",z="barrens",s="Warriors who have mastered the berserker stance are sent north to find The Windwatcher. After the Affray on Fray Island, Klannoc Macleod points them toward a weapon worthy of their fury.",h="Warriors who have mastered the berserker stance are sent north to find The Windwatcher.",sec={{t="A Weapon for a Berserker",b="You have survived the Affray on Fray Island and learned the berserker stance from Klannoc Macleod. Now Klannoc sends you far from the Barrens coast, across continents, to find a solitary craftsman who can forge an exceptional weapon.",sp=0},{t="The Hermit on the Riverbank",b="Bath'rah the Windwatcher lives beside the river that runs north past Tarren Mill. His camp rests among stone ruins in the contested land between the Alterac Mountains and the blighted Western Plaguelands. The troll hermit crafts weapons and commands potent elemental shamanism. He waits for warriors determined to forge a weapon of great power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Windwatcher?",a="Klannoc Macleod sends you north after you survive the Affray on Fray Island and learn the berserker stance.",al={"quest giver","who gives the windwatcher","klannoc macleod quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Bath'rah the Windwatcher?",a="Bath'rah is a troll hermit, master weaponsmith, and powerful shaman living in the wilderness between the Alterac Mountains and the Western Plaguelands.",al={"who is bathrah","bathrah the windwatcher lore","bath'rah identity"},it="identity"},{q="Where exactly is Bath'rah located?",a="Bath'rah camps near ancient ruins on the eastern bank of the river that flows north past Tarren Mill, near the border of Alterac and the Western Plaguelands.",al={"where is bath'rah","bathrah location","find bathrah"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Klannoc send warriors to Bath'rah?",a="Klannoc sends warriors to Bath'rah because those who master the berserker stance need an exceptional weapon, and Bath'rah knows both smithing and elemental shamanism.",al={"why go to bathrah","what is the purpose of this quest","windwatcher purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What comes after speaking with Bath'rah?",a="After you speak with Bath'rah, you face the elemental Cyclonian and gather rare materials to craft a potent weapon.",al={"what is next after the windwatcher","cyclonian next quest","windwatcher continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is this journey safe for a traveler coming from the Barrens?",a="The journey is perilous. You travel through the Hillsbrad foothills into contested northern lands, where Syndicate hideouts, aggressive mountain predators, and the deadly blight of the Western Plaguelands threaten you.",al={"is it dangerous","tarren mill river danger"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Klannoc send you to Bath'rah instead of going himself?",a="Klannoc Macleod is not seeking a legendary armament for himself; he serves as a seasoned mentor on the Fray Island proving grounds. Having witnessed you survive the Affray and master the berserker stance, he believes you are ready for a weapon worthy of your newly unlocked fury. The long pilgrimage to the distant hermit Bath'rah is a test of a warrior's own resolve and growth.",al={"why me the windwatcher","why send the warrior","why klannoc sends player"},it="why_me",add="ff43a27e"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you have mastered the berserker stance on Fray Island and now seek a powerful weapon forged through elemental craft.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can see how troll shamans and weapon crafters preserve mystical knowledge amid Lordaeron's broken ruins, knowledge warriors of every heritage revere."},kw={"alterac mountains","bath'rah","berserker stance","cyclonian","fray island","klannoc macleod","tarren mill","the affray","the windwatcher"},rel={"npc:bath-rah-the-windwatcher","npc:klannoc-macleod","quest:1719","zone:barrens","zone:alterac","zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:troll"},m={start="Klannoc Macleod",["end"]="Bath'rah the Windwatcher",level="30",id=1791},src={"The Windwatcher"}}
E["quest:1795"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="barrens",s="Above Ratchet, warlocks face the rite that binds a felhunter to their will. Strahad Farsan oversees the summoning with the restored Tome of the Cabal, drawing an aggressive demon from the Nether to be subdued in combat.",h="Above Ratchet, warlocks face the rite that binds a felhunter to their will.",sec={{t="The Cabal's Circle",b="On Kalimdor's bluffs above Ratchet, the goblin port, Strahad Farsan conducts dangerous trials in demon summoning. After a warlock gathers the fragments and reagents needed to restore the ancient Tome of the Cabal, Strahad prepares the binding grounds. He lays an inner glyph of containment while his acolytes channel power through enchanted rods to complete the outer circle. The circles keep whatever emerges isolated from the settlement below.",sp=0},{t="Subjugating the Hunter",b="The Tome of the Cabal holds the incantations that open a bridge into the Twisting Nether. Felhunters are ravenous demonic hounds that hunger for arcane power and feast on magical energy. No gentle enthrallment or persuasion will bind one. The warlock must violently subdue and break the summoned beast in combat before it recognizes its rightful master. Surviving the clash proves the summoner can wield the hound against enemy spellcasters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this ritual?",a="The ritual lets a warlock summon a felhunter and bind it to their will. Reading from the completed Tome of the Cabal inside Strahad Farsan's summoning circle draws the demon from the Nether. The warlock must defeat it in battle, winning its permanent service.",al={"why do this quest","felhunter quest goal","binding purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Strahad Farsan?",a="Strahad Farsan is an accomplished human warlock who works from a tower above Ratchet in the Barrens. His vast knowledge of dark summoning arts leads mentors from both the Alliance and the Horde to quietly send their most promising practitioners to study advanced binding rites under his tutelage.",al={"who is strahad","strahad farsan lore","quest giver strahad"},it="identity"},{q="Why does a warlock have to kill the demon instead of enslaving it?",a="A felhunter is an aggressive predator that devours magic and respects absolute dominance. The practitioner must best it in physical and magical combat, breaking its ferocity and imprinting their authority over its spirit so it obeys future summonings.",al={"why kill felhunter","can i enslave felhunter","felhunter combat"}},{q="Can both Horde and Alliance warlocks perform this ritual here?",a="Yes. The steps to reconstruct the Tome of the Cabal differ by faction, but both Alliance and Horde warlocks are eventually directed to Strahad Farsan above Ratchet for the final summoning.",al={"is this horde only","is this alliance only","who gets this quest"},it="side"},{q="What happens if the felhunter defeats the summoner?",a="If the summoner falls, the felhunter is banished to the Nether and the ritual fails. Warlocks who survive defeat can reclaim a fresh copy of the Tome of the Cabal from Strahad and try again when properly prepared.",al={"what if i die","failing the binding","can i retry the ritual"},it="threat"},{q="What makes felhunters unique compared to other demons?",a="Felhunters are demonic hounds that hunt by sensing magical emanations. They rely less on brute force or shadow spells, instead smelling out sorcery, devouring active enchantments, and disrupting enemy spellcasters. This makes them valuable companions against rival magic users.",al={"what does a felhunter do","felhunter lore","why felhunters"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Strahad Farsan want you to summon the felhunter?",a="Strahad Farsan is not using you to run an errand—he is training you to master greater demonic magic. He believes every warlock should have a felhunter at their command, as the creature's disruptive powers vastly outweigh the danger of binding one. Having guided your collection of the materials and the Tome of the Cabal, his stake is in testing your potential and seeing whether you can survive the trial to stand among the era's most formidable practitioners.",al={"why does strahad want this","strahad farsan motive","why summon felhunter for strahad"},it="motive",add="b1095368"},{q="Why must you face the felhunter yourself instead of Strahad doing it?",a="A summoned demon cannot simply be conquered on your behalf. Subjugating a minion of the Twisting Nether requires proving your personal will and dominance over the creature; having Strahad or his acolytes defeat it would establish no bond of servitude to you. Strahad and his assistants channel the greater summoning circles to contain the breach, but breaking the beast's feral strength in combat is a test that only the prospective master can endure.",al={"why cant strahad fight it","why do i have to kill the felhunter","why must i fight the demon alone"},it="why_me",add="44d888c5"},{q="What is the summoned felhunter, and where does it come from?",a="You are facing a vicious, predatory demon pulled directly from the Twisting Nether using the incantations within the Tome of the Cabal. Felhunters are monstrous beasts drawn to the taste of arcane and magical energies, which they eagerly track, drain, and disrupt. Because they are ravenous fiends by nature, the creature pulled into the summoning circle will immediately attack you upon materializing, demanding that you overpower it in combat before its spirit can be bound to your service.",al={"what is the summoned felhunter","what am i fighting","felhunter lore"},it="target",add="6bf7b15d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, binding a felhunter marks a crucial milestone. The hound is a specialized anti-magic predator that can devour spells and shut down hostile casters.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance warlock, you travel from Stormwind across the sea to neutral Ratchet, where Strahad oversees the perilous summoning ritual.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warlock, you journey into the heart of the Barrens to prove your dominion over the Nether and bind the hound before Strahad on neutral ground."},kw={"barrens","felhunter","ratchet","strahad farsan","summoning","the binding","tome of the cabal","warlock"},rel={"quest:1758","npc:strahad-farsan","quest:1798","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","quest:1471","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},m={start="Strahad Farsan",level="30",id=1795},src={"The Binding (Felhunter)"}}
E["quest:1796"] = {t="quest",n="Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Menara Voidrender asks warlocks to find Robes of Arcana for a garment meant to bear powerful enchantments.",h="In Ratchet, Menara Voidrender asks warlocks to find Robes of Arcana for a garment meant to bear powerful...",sec={{t="A Vessel of Arcana",b="Menara Voidrender asks warlocks seeking greater power to bring her a set of Robes of Arcana. She wants a garment strong enough to hold dark magic. The strength of a magical relic depends on the skill, rarity, and effort put into its materials. Ordinary rags would fail under deep enchantments, so the robe must be finely made and ready to receive them.",sp=0},{t="Craft and Ambition",b="Menara admires warlocks who can weave the robe themselves, but ambition matters more to her than pride. You can sew the silk, commission a skilled artisan, or buy the robe at market. However you obtain it, the finished garment is ready to become a specialized tool of fel mastery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Menara Voidrender need Robes of Arcana specifically?",a="Powerful enchantments need a garment made with skill and rare materials. Menara uses the Robes of Arcana as a receptive foundation for the forces she plans to bind into it.",al={"why robes of arcana","why this robe","robe purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where is Menara Voidrender located?",a="Menara Voidrender lives in Ratchet, the goblin port in the Barrens. She instructs warlocks who want to advance their craft and make specialized gear.",al={"menara voidrender location","where is menara","menara voidrender where"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do I have to tailor the Robes of Arcana myself?",a="No. Menara respects the work of making the robe yourself, but accepts one acquired through trade or bought from another craftsman. You can secure it by any practical means.",al={"do i need tailoring","can i buy the robes","tailoring required"},gp=true},{q="Where does the pattern for Robes of Arcana come from?",a="The pattern is rare and can be found among cultists and dark casters. Dark Strand Voidcallers at the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore and Defias Enchanters in Duskwood are among those who carry it.",al={"robes of arcana pattern","how to get pattern","tailoring recipe location"},gp=true},{q="What happens to the Robes of Arcana after handing them in?",a="Menara takes the robes as material for the imbuing ritual that follows. If you wear them when you bring them to her, she removes them at once, leaving you without a chestpiece until the later steps are complete.",al={"do i lose the robes","robe gone","what happens to robe"}},{q="What is the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe?",a="The Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe is a specialized garment for mid-ranking warlocks. Dark components and protective enchantments strengthen its wearer's resilience and reserves of dark energy.",al={"what is bloodrobe","bloodrobe lore","enchanted gold bloodrobe"},it="item"},{q="Why does Menara Voidrender want this done?",a="Menara Voidrender serves as a mentor guiding ambitious warlocks into greater mastery of dark arts. She is not seeking robes for her own wardrobe; rather, she is testing your dedication and resourcefulness while teaching you how to forge powerful warlock vestments. Guiding promising practitioners to channel fel powers through tailored focuses strengthens the ranks of their shadowy craft.",al={"why is menara helping me","menara voidrender motive","why make the robes"},it="motive",add="44990969"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, making the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe teaches you to build powerful artifacts on a strong, carefully prepared foundation.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you need the rare pattern for Robes of Arcana and skill with spider's silk and many bolts of fine silk.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may travel far to the sun-bleached Barrens to learn from Menara and strengthen your frail mortal husk against your volatile arts.",["race:Orc"]="As an Orc warlock, gathering materials for subtle robes offers you a quieter way to master fel energy, away from prying eyes and the shadow of your race's demonic past."},kw={"barrens","bloodrobe","enchanted gold bloodrobe","menara voidrender","robes of arcana","tailoring","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:menara-voidrender","zone:barrens","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","zone:duskwood","quest:99141"},m={start="Menara Voidrender",level="31",id=1796,ri={"Robes of Arcana"}},src={"Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe"}}
E["quest:1798"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking Strahad",z="barrens",s="Warlocks leave Stormwind City for Ratchet, where Strahad Farsan can teach them to summon felhunters. Beneath the goblin port, his knowledge offers a path into more dangerous demon summoning.",h="Warlocks leave Stormwind City for Ratchet, where Strahad Farsan can teach them to summon felhunters.",sec={{t="A Summons Across the Sea",b="Gakin the Darkbinder sends you from Stormwind to seek help with summoning a felhunter. He guides warlocks in the Slaughtered Lamb, below the Mage Quarter, but the rites call for knowledge beyond what he can offer there. Your journey carries you across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, where another warlock may know the way.",sp=0},{t="The Hermit of Ratchet",b="Strahad Farsan lives in the arid hills above Ratchet, the goblin harbor. He is a human warlock and a peer of Gakin's in their secret cabal. From neutral territory, Strahad can work beyond the notice of Alliance magistrates, church inquisitors, and Horde sentries. Warlocks come to him hoping to master demons that drain mana.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find Strahad?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder sends you from the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter when you are ready to learn to summon a felhunter.",al={"who gives seeking strahad","quest giver","gakin"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Strahad Farsan located?",a="Strahad Farsan lives in the Barrens, in the heights overlooking Ratchet, the goblin port.",al={"strahad location","where is strahad","find strahad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does an Alliance warlock have to travel all the way to the Barrens?",a="Gakin cannot provide the lore and materials needed for the felhunter summoning rites in Stormwind. Strahad Farsan has that knowledge and works from neutral territory near Ratchet, away from local scrutiny.",al={"why go to barrens","why kalimdor","why ratchet"},it="why_here"},{q="What ability does this quest lead to unlocking?",a="Speaking with Strahad begins a chain that leads to the Tome of the Cabal and the binding ritual for summoning a felhunter companion.",al={"what pet is this for","what do i get","felhunter quest"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Is Strahad Farsan hostile to the Horde?",a="No. Strahad lives in neutral goblin territory and instructs Alliance and Horde warlocks in summoning felhunters, while keeping ties with various cabals.",al={"is strahad alliance only","horde strahad"},it="hostile"},{q="What happens after you speak to Strahad?",a="Strahad asks you to gather the components for a binding ritual, beginning a chain involving the Tome of the Cabal.",al={"next quest","what after seeking strahad","tome of the cabal"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder want you to seek Strahad?",a="Gakin judges that your power has grown enough to command a felhunter, but he lacks the arcane reagents and ritual components required to instruct you beneath Stormwind. Rather than let your training stall, he sends you to Strahad Farsan, a trusted peer in their inner circle who possesses the necessary lore and materials across the sea.",al={"why send to strahad","gakin darkbinder motive","why gakin sends you"},it="motive",add="034d02a4"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you reach a milestone when you leave basic fiends and succubi behind and learn to summon the cunning, magic-draining felhunter.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance warlock, you cross the Great Sea into Kalimdor's rugged, Horde-dominated heartland to reach Strahad."},kw={"felhunter","gakin the darkbinder","ratchet","seeking strahad","stormwind","strahad farsan","the barrens","warlock"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1758","quest:1471","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="Gakin the Darkbinder",["end"]="Strahad Farsan",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1798},src={"Seeking Strahad (Stormwind)"}}
E["quest:1801"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of the Cabal",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Strahad Farsan sends Horde warlocks east in search of a lost grimoire. The Tome of the Cabal holds rites for summoning and binding a felhunter, and the search begins with cartographer Jorah Annison in the Undercity.",h="In the Barrens, Strahad Farsan sends Horde warlocks east in search of a lost grimoire.",sec={{t="A Hunt for Ancient Knowledge",b="Strahad Farsan says a felhunter takes more than ordinary fel magic to summon. These predators feed on magical energies and resist standard summoning circles. An initiate needs specialized circles and an ancient grimoire called the Tome of the Cabal. The first order of warlocks to bind a felhunter without outside aid wrote the book. Its rites and seals show how to enslave such a dangerous demon.",sp=0},{t="The Cartographer of Undercity",b="Copies of the Tome of the Cabal have long been lost to warlocks in Kalimdor, so Strahad sends his student across the sea to Jorah Annison in the Undercity. Annison works as a royal cartographer, mapping Lordaeron, but knows a great deal about ancient and obscure texts. He admits that he despises mapmaking and hungers for rare histories, occult narratives, and treatises on dark magic.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of the Cabal?",a="The Tome of the Cabal is a rare occult grimoire written by the first warlocks to summon and bind a felhunter without outside help. Its precise instructions, wards, and rites allow one of these magic-devouring beasts to be brought safely into Azeroth.",al={"tome of the cabal lore","what is this book","tome of cabal"},it="item"},{q="Why does Strahad Farsan send you to the Undercity?",a="Strahad and his acolytes in the Barrens have no copy of the Tome of the Cabal. He sends you to Jorah Annison, an Undercity cartographer and scholar of rare, ancient books who may know where to recover the Tome.",al={"why go to undercity","strahad farsan undercity","why see jorah"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Jorah Annison?",a="Jorah Annison is a Forsaken scholar who works in the Undercity. His official trade is cartography, but his passion lies in obscure texts, necromantic treatises, and ancient literature.",al={"who is jorah","jorah annison lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a special book needed to summon a felhunter?",a="Felhunters feed on arcane and other magical energies, making them dangerous to summon through ordinary demonic circles. The Tome of the Cabal details safeguards that bind them before they consume the summoner.",al={"why felhunter need book","why is felhunter hard to summon"},it="power"},{q="Why does Strahad Farsan want this done?",a="Strahad Farsan oversees your progression as an ambitious warlock worthy of wielding greater demonic power. Summoning and subjugating a felhunter is a perilous rite of passage that tests whether a practitioner can master a creature designed to feed on raw magical essence. Strahad is prepared to lend his acolytes and magic circles to the binding ritual, but you must first procure the ancient knowledge required to make the summoning possible.",al={"strahad farsan motive","why does strahad help","strahad reason"},it="motive",add="9f4798be"},{q="Why does Strahad Farsan send you instead of going himself?",a="The trial is entirely yours to prove. A warlock must demonstrate resourcefulness, resilience, and personal dominion over the dark arts to bind a beast as dangerous as a felhunter. Strahad and his acolytes must also remain at the summoning circle above Ratchet to prepare the complex wards and rituals needed when you return with the recovered text.",al={"why send me","why doesn't strahad go","why must I go to undercity"},it="why_me",add="5aabed1a"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you must complete this rite of passage to tame a felhunter. It takes you between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms to gather forgotten ritual components.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Kalimdor's dark casters work with Forsaken occult scholars beneath the ruins of Lordaeron."},kw={"barrens","felhunter","jorah annison","ratchet","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal","undercity","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","npc:jorah-annison","quest:1758","zone:undercity","zone:barrens"},m={start="Strahad Farsan",["end"]="Jorah Annison",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1801},src={"Tome of the Cabal (Horde)"}}
E["quest:1804"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of the Cabal",z="barrens",s="In the Barrens, Strahad Farsan waits for a warlock to bring him the Tome of the Cabal and channeling rods. Together, they prepare the way to bind a felhunter.",h="In the Barrens, Strahad Farsan waits for a warlock to bring him the Tome of the Cabal and channeling rods.",sec={{t="A Grudging Hand-Off",b="In Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, Krom Stoutarm binds the Tome of the Cabal's tattered, mouldering remnants back together. The dwarf scholar reluctantly parts with this rare work of dark scholarship, but first secures a promise of a copy. He also passes along a fresh missive from Strahad Farsan. The tome holds the rites for breaching the Nether, though parchment alone cannot conduct the ritual.",sp=0},{t="Stolen Relics of the Dragonmaw",b="Strahad's acolytes need focus implements to steady the energies summoned to bind a felhunter. Krom sends the warlock to the Wetlands, where Dragonmaw spellcasters carry rods of channeling. Taking the rods from the hostile orcs gives Strahad's circle the conduit it needs to control the rift and stabilize the summoned energies.",sp=0},{t="Back to the Barrens",b="At Strahad's tower high above Ratchet, the reconstructed tome and channeling rods complete the grueling assembly. With the instruments secured and the text translated, Strahad prepares the dangerous binding rite. The summoner's willpower will be tested against a hound of the Burning Legion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Strahad need rods of channeling?",a="Strahad's acolytes use the rods to focus and steady the energies needed to summon and bind a felhunter. Their work helps keep the portal from collapsing or running wild.",al={"why rods of channeling","rods of channeling purpose","what are the rods for"},it="item"},{q="Where are the rods of channeling found?",a="Dragonmaw orc spellcasters in the Wetlands hold the rods of channeling, especially around the marshes and ruins they occupy.",al={"where to get rods of channeling","who drops rods of channeling","rods of channeling location"},gp=true},{q="Why was Krom Stoutarm involved in a warlock ritual?",a="Krom Stoutarm is a master researcher in Ironforge, skilled at translating, preserving, and rebuilding ancient damaged manuscripts. His interest in rare antiquities led him to restore the Tome of the Cabal's corrupted pages.",al={"why krom","why is an ironforge dwarf helping a warlock","krom stoutarm warlock"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after giving the tome and rods to Strahad?",a="After you give Strahad the tome and rods, he begins the binding rite atop his tower. You face the summoned felhunter and try to subdue it.",al={"what happens next","next quest after tome of the cabal 3","what does strahad do"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Strahad Farsan?",a="Strahad Farsan is a powerful warlock in a solitary tower on the cliffs above Ratchet in the Barrens. Experienced practitioners across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms defer to his mastery of demonology.",al={"strahad farsan lore","who is strahad","guy above ratchet"},it="identity"},{q="Is the Tome of the Cabal used by the Horde as well?",a="Horde warlocks follow their own Tome of the Cabal rites, with leads to different contacts across Kalimdor and the Undercity rather than to Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge.",al={"horde tome of the cabal","do orcs do this quest"}},{q="Why must you hunt down the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands?",a="The Dragonmaw clan remnant entrenched in the Wetlands still wields potent dark magic left over from their past dominion. Krom knows their spellcasters carry the specialized rods of channeling needed to anchor Strahad's summoning circle. To claim the focuses, you must pry them directly from these hostile orc casters.",al={"why dragonmaw orcs","wetlands dragonmaw warlocks","who has rods of channeling"},it="target",add="7a279078"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, subduing a felhunter marks a passage from pacts with imps and voidwalkers to mastering predatory demons made to devour arcane magic.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance summoner, you travel between Ironforge, the misty bogs of the Wetlands, and Ratchet, the neutral goblin port in Kalimdor.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the value of careful preservation. In Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, Krom Stoutarm pieces ruined relics back together."},kw={"barrens","dragonmaw","felhunter","krom stoutarm","ratchet","rods of channeling","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal","wetlands"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","npc:krom-stoutarm","quest:1471","quest:1758","quest:1798","topic:dragonmaw-clan","zone:wetlands","subzone:ratchet"},m={start="Krom Stoutarm",["end"]="Strahad Farsan",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1804,ri={"Rod of Channeling"}},src={"Tome of the Cabal (Alliance, 3)"}}
E["quest:1805"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of the Cabal",z="barrens",s="A warlock's work with the Tome of the Cabal now leads into hostile territory. After helping Jorah Annison restore the tome, you must claim three Rods of Channeling and bring them to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.",h="A warlock's work with the Tome of the Cabal now leads into hostile territory.",sec={{t="Secrets of the Reconstructed Tome",b="In the Undercity, Jorah Annison studies the recovered fragments of the Tome of the Cabal. The Forsaken scholar pieces together its eldritch passages and welcomes the rare knowledge they offer. Then Jorah delivers an urgent directive from Strahad Farsan. Knowledge alone cannot bind a felhunter. A warlock needs precise instruments to focus demonic power into a binding circle.",sp=0},{t="Venture into the Wetlands",b="Strahad needs three Rods of Channeling, carried by renegade orcs of the Dragonmaw clan. They dwell among the ruins of Angerfang Encampment in the Wetlands, far from Horde lands. You must enter contested territory and face clan remnants who hate the modern Horde as much as they butcher Alliance explorers.",sp=0},{t="Return to Ratchet",b="With the rods and the Reconstructed Tome secured, you return across the sea to Strahad Farsan's tower above Ratchet. Strahad greets you with grim satisfaction. The ritual's components are assembled, and a dangerous test of will against a beast from the Twisting Nether lies ahead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This is the third step in the Horde warlock chain to learn to summon a felhunter. You deliver the restored Tome of the Cabal and three Rods of Channeling to Strahad Farsan above Ratchet.",al={"why do this quest","quest purpose","what is tome of the cabal for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Jorah Annison?",a="Jorah Annison is a Forsaken warlock and scholar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Jorah studies esoteric and dark texts, helping fellow practitioners piece together shattered grimoires such as the Tome of the Cabal.",al={"who is jorah","jorah annison lore"},it="people"},{q="Why are Rods of Channeling needed?",a="The rods give a warlock precise control when summoning and compelling a felhunter. They focus the ritual, stabilizing and shaping the summoning circle so the warlock can subdue the demon rather than be devoured.",al={"why rods of channeling","rods purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where are the Dragonmaw orcs located for this quest?",a="The Dragonmaw clan holds Angerfang Encampment in the Wetlands, across the sea in Khaz Modan. Their bonewarders carry the channeling rods.",al={"where to find dragonmaw","dragonmaw location wetlands","angerfang encampment"},gp=true},{q="Who is Strahad Farsan?",a="Strahad Farsan is a human warlock allied with the Horde's dark spellcasters. He works from a lone tower on the bluffs above Ratchet, the goblin port in the Barrens.",al={"who is strahad","strahad farsan ratchet"},it="people"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Your delivery leads into 'The Binding'. Strahad then instructs you to draw a summoning circle and face a summoned felhunter in magical combat to master the beast.",al={"what comes next","next quest after tome"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Jorah Annison helping you?",a="Jorah Annison is a Forsaken cartographer in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, starved for arcane and esoteric reading material after long exhausting the sparse selection of geography texts at hand. In exchange for granting him the opportunity to study the reconstructed Tome of the Cabal, he passes along instructions from Strahad Farsan and reveals where you can acquire the rare channeling rods needed for your training.",al={"why does jorah help","jorah annison motive","what does jorah want"},it="motive",add="9475dbd0"},{q="Why do the Dragonmaw orcs have the Rods of Channeling?",a="The renegade Dragonmaw Clan maintains strongholds across the Wetlands, harboring dark spellcasters and bonewarders who practice sinister magics separate from the modern Horde. They utilize powerful channeling rods to focus and bind raw magical energies, making their encampments the prime place to recover the arcane foci Strahad requires for summoning rituals.",al={"dragonmaw orcs wetlands","who has the rods of channeling","why dragonmaw orcs"},it="target",add="cff1ec65"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face a trial of resolve: securing dangerous ritual reagents in hostile lands takes the knowledge and nerve to bind a predatory felhunter to your service.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face Dragonmaw renegades in the Wetlands, bitter enemies of Thrall's Horde. Taking their channeling rods is a victory for Horde interests.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, striking down rogue Dragonmaw in the Wetlands recalls the dark, unrepentant path the Horde fought to leave behind.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see Jorah Annison's work in the Undercity: Forsaken warlocks study forbidden arcane texts for practical supremacy."},kw={"angerfang encampment","dragonmaw","felhunter","jorah annison","ratchet","rod of channeling","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal","wetlands"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","npc:jorah-annison","topic:dragonmaw-clan","subzone:angerfang-encampment","zone:wetlands","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Jorah Annison",["end"]="Strahad Farsan",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1805,ri={"Rod of Channeling"}},src={"Tome of the Cabal (Horde, 3)"}}
E["quest:1824"] = {t="quest",n="Trial at the Field of Giants",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Ruga Ragetotem sends warrior aspirants south to face an unfamiliar foe. They must slay silithid in the Field of Giants and return with several twitching antennae within half an hour.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Ruga Ragetotem sends warrior aspirants south to face an unfamiliar foe.",sec={{t="A Test of Speed and Steel",b="At Camp Taurajo, Ruga Ragetotem challenges growing warriors to prove themselves against an unfamiliar adversary. The Horde's warrior trainers test more than combat skill: aspirants must slay the creatures and bring back fresh antennae within half an hour. The run across the southern Barrens tests their speed and resolve, while the antennae must still twitch when they reach Taurajo.",sp=0},{t="Unwelcome Intruders",b="Silithid hives rise in the Field of Giants, beneath massive fossilized ribcages. The bizarre, crawling insects are recent arrivals in the Barrens, disturbing tauren hunters and shamans who watch the savannas. Ruga says their presence bodes ill for Kalimdor. The trial tests a young warrior's instincts in combat and gathers intelligence on a growing threat to the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a time limit on the antennae?",a="Ruga Ragetotem requires the antennae to still twitch when warriors bring them to Camp Taurajo, giving them only thirty minutes for the hunt and return. Their freshness proves the aspirant slew a silithid in direct combat rather than scavenging a dead one.",al={"why timed","twitching antennae timer","how much time"},it="item"},{q="What creatures live at the Field of Giants?",a="Bizarre, aggressive silithid burrowers live in the Field of Giants. They have excavated massive mounds and hives beneath ancient fossils, disturbing the local ecology and alarming the Horde.",al={"what are the bugs","field of giants mobs","what are silithid"},it="target"},{q="Who is Ruga Ragetotem?",a="Ruga Ragetotem is a tauren warrior trainer at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He oversees trials for Horde warriors seeking to advance their standing, testing their skill, resilience, and speed.",al={"ruga","who gives quest","ruga ragetotem lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Field of Giants located?",a="The Field of Giants lies directly south of Camp Taurajo, beside the road before the southern pass toward Thousand Needles. Towering skeletal ribcages and silithid mounds mark the field.",al={"where is field of giants","field of giants location","where do i find the bugs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does this training chain lead next?",a="After the warrior returns the twitching antennae in time, Ruga sends them to Thun'grim Firegaze, an elder orc blacksmith who lives atop a hill east of the Crossroads. Thun'grim will craft armor for proven warriors.",al={"next quest","what comes after","warrior chain continuation"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the tauren concerned about the insects?",a="Ruga says the silithid are unnatural newcomers to the Barrens and that their arrival bodes ill for the land. He suspects their aggressive burrowing and expansion point to a greater danger beneath the sands.",al={"why do tauren care","insect herald","silithid threat"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Ruga Ragetotem want this done?",a="Ruga Ragetotem tests your martial mettle as part of your warrior training while keeping an eye on an emerging threat. Strange insectoid creatures have recently surfaced at the Field of Giants, unsettling the local tauren. By sending you to swiftly cull them and bring back fresh trophies before they cease twitching, Ruga tests your combat prowess, speed, and endurance in the field.",al={"ruga ragetotem motive","why trial at the field of giants","why does ruga send you"},it="motive",add="5312a899"},{q="Why does Ruga Ragetotem need you instead of camp guards?",a="This mission is a personal rite of passage designed specifically for an aspiring warrior under Ruga's tutelage. The camp guards are committed to defending Camp Taurajo and watching the nearby frontiers, whereas surviving harsh solitary trials against dangerous predators is how you prove yourself ready to walk the greater warrior's path.",al={"why me trial of giants","why send an adventurer ruga"},it="why_me",add="2d3c0cc0"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face this rite of passage around level twenty. It tests how quickly you can overcome swarming foes and endure a strict time limit.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren defender, you help protect the hunting grounds around Camp Taurajo by confronting the desecration at the Field of Giants and its unnatural, invasive hive.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the expanding silithid presence in the southern Barrens. These trials also gather information about a creeping threat."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","field of giants","ruga ragetotem","silithid","twitching antenna","warrior trial"},rel={"subzone:field-of-giants","npc:ruga-ragetotem","subzone:camp-taurajo","quest:1825","zone:barrens"},m={start="Ruga Ragetotem",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1824,ri={"Twitching Antenna"}},src={"Trial at the Field of Giants"}}
E["quest:1825"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Thun'grim",z="barrens",s="This errand directs rising Horde warriors to Thun'grim Firegaze, an acclaimed orc blacksmith camping in the Barrens. Having proved themselves through demanding physical trials, warriors are invited to have custom armor forged in recognition of their valor. The quest serves as the crucial bridge connecting general warrior testing with the crafting of Brutal Armor.",h="This errand directs rising Horde warriors to Thun'grim Firegaze, an acclaimed orc blacksmith camping in the...",sec={{t="The Call of the Smith",b="After proving their mettle against the silithid hives during the Trial at the Field of Giants, Horde warriors earn more than simple praise from Ruga Ragetotem. Word of their endurance and martial prowess quickly reaches Thun'grim Firegaze, a renowned orc smith who maintains a camp perched on a ridge east of the Crossroads. Recognizing a warrior worthy of his craft, Thun'grim sends word that he wishes to fashion them an exceptional suit of battle mail.",sp=0},{t="A Master's Standard",b="Thun'grim Firegaze does not forge for ordinary soldiers. For an armorsmith of his reputation, steel must match the spirit of the one who carries it into battle. Reaching his camp signifies that a warrior has advanced past simple militia drills and is ready to undertake the grueling, specialized tasks required to gather rare crafting reagents across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze is an esteemed orc blacksmith camped atop a rocky ridge just east of the Crossroads in the Barrens. He crafts custom, formidable armor for Horde warriors who have proven their valor through dangerous trials.",al={"who is thungrim","thungrim lore","thungrim firegaze"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Ruga Ragetotem send me to him?",a="Ruga Ragetotem recognizes that you have outgrown basic trials after surviving the silithid in the southern Barrens. He directs you to Thun'grim so the master smith can reward your service to the Horde by forging a specialized set of armor.",al={"why speak with thungrim","ruga sending me"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Thun'grim's camp?",a="Thun'grim makes his camp on the high bluffs east of the Crossroads in the Barrens, looking out over the dry savanna.",al={"where is thungrim","thungrim location","find thungrim firegaze"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after speaking with Thun'grim?",a="Meeting Thun'grim begins the Brutal Armor questline, sending warriors across distant lands to collect tough materials such as smoky iron ingots and iron bars to fashion a bespoke mail harness.",al={"next quest after thungrim","what does thungrim want"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest available to all classes?",a="No. This quest and its associated armor chain are strictly part of the martial training regimen reserved for Horde warriors.",al={"can non warriors do this","is this warrior only"},gp=true},{q="What trial was required before this meeting?",a="Prior to this errand, warriors had to travel to the southern Barrens to complete the Trial at the Field of Giants, gathering twitching silithid antennae to demonstrate their combat stamina.",al={"prerequisite quest","what did i do before this"},it="history"},{q="Why is Ruga Ragetotem sending you instead of going himself?",a="Ruga Ragetotem oversees the training and testing of rising Horde warriors from his post at Camp Taurajo. Thun'grim Firegaze specifically reached out seeking you, having heard of your valor and trials across the Barrens. Ruga merely passes along the summons so you can claim armor forged to your personal measure.",al={"why send me ruga","why me ruga ragetotem","why does ruga need me"},it="why_me",add="2df90612"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This quest marks an important rite of passage, elevating you from a novice fighter to a recognized champion deserving of custom-forged armor.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde armorsmiths take pride in arming their fiercest defenders, ensuring that those fighting on the frontier wear gear that matches their battlefield deeds.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Thun'grim Firegaze represents traditional orcish smithing philosophy, where mastercrafted armor must be earned through martial trials rather than mere coin."},kw={"barrens","brutal armor","crossroads","firegaze","ragetotem","ruga","thun'grim","warrior"},rel={"quest:1824","quest:1838","quest:1502","npc:ruga-ragetotem","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},m={start="Ruga Ragetotem",["end"]="Thun'grim Firegaze",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1825},src={"Speak with Thun'grim"}}
E["quest:1838"] = {t="quest",n="Brutal Armor",z="barrens",s="A warrior in the northern Barrens faces Thun'grim Firegaze's test. The near-blind smith sends seasoned Horde warriors across distant lands for rare ingredients and smelting agents. Fulfilling his scroll begins the forging of a full set of brutal battle gear.",h="A warrior in the northern Barrens faces Thun'grim Firegaze's test.",sec={{t="A Master's Calling",b="In the northern Barrens, Thun'grim Firegaze listens for news of war. The veteran orc smith's eyesight is failing, but his skill at the forge remains unmatched. Rumors reach him of a warrior whose strength and valor exceed those of ordinary soldiers. Thun'grim sets out to craft mail that can withstand the fiercest battles across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="A Cross-Continental Search",b="Thun'grim's armor calls for more than common ore. By firelight, his failing eyes guide him as he writes a precise scroll for the core chestpiece. Its ingredients include refined iron, smoky iron ingots carried by burrowing kobolds, powdered azurite worked by miners across the sea, and a volatile vial of phlogiston. Only a warrior ready to face trials across distant lands can bring the required materials together.",sp=0},{t="The First Strike of the Hammer",b="Thun'grim's rare materials begin a much larger undertaking. When they arrive, he fires his furnace and forges the Brutal Hauberk. The old smith sees that he cannot complete such an ambitious armory alone. The full set calls for expert craftsmen of the other Horde races: a Tauren helm-shaper, a Troll gauntlet-maker, and an Undead greave-smith, each found across the continents.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze is a veteran orc blacksmith who lives on a hill overlooking the northern Barrens. Though his eyesight is failing, his instincts at the anvil remain sharp, and he crafts powerful custom battle mail for Horde warriors renowned for valor.",al={"who is thungrim","thun'grim firegaze lore","thungrim backstory"},it="identity"},{q="What is Brutal Armor?",a="Brutal Armor is a set of battle-forged mail for seasoned Horde warriors. Horde smiths bring their skills together to make it, and each piece calls for dangerous journeys to find rare alchemical reagents, purified ores, and ancient techniques.",al={"what is brutal armor","brutal armor set lore","warrior armor chain"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Thun'grim need such unusual ingredients?",a="Thun'grim needs unusual ingredients because standard iron is too brittle to endure the heavy blows faced by a frontline champion. He uses powdered azurite, smoky iron ingots, and volatile phlogiston as flux and tempering agents to give the metal greater resilience and strength.",al={"why powdered azurite","why phlogiston","what are the reagents for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does Thun'grim forge the entire set himself?",a="No. Thun'grim forges the central hauberk, while fellow Horde smiths craft the matching helm, gauntlets, and legguards. They include Orm Stonehoof, Ula'elek, and Velora Nitely.",al={"does thungrim make all of it","who makes the brutal armor pieces"},sp=1},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="The trial leads to the forging of the Brutal Hauberk and opens the way to consult smiths in Thunder Bluff, Sen'jin Village, and the Undercity for the rest of the brutal battle mail.",al={"what comes after brutal armor","brutal armor follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does a warrior have to travel so far for these materials?",a="The journey tests a warrior's martial tenacity and resourcefulness. To prove worthy of master-forged armor, a warrior must cross enemy territory, enter hazardous mines, and gather components beyond ordinary reach.",al={"why travel to eastern kingdoms","why so many materials"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze want to make this armor?",a="Thun'grim has heard of your growing renown across the Horde and wishes to craft a suit worthy of your strength. To the aging, near-blind smith, forging legendary armor to accompany a rising warrior on their journey is an honor and a testament to his own craft.",al={"why does thungrim help me","thungrim firegaze motive","why make brutal armor"},it="motive",add="31952f55"},{q="Why does Thun'grim need you to collect the materials?",a="Thun'grim is an elderly orc whose eyesight is nearly gone; he struggled over several nights just to pen your instructions. Gathering dangerous reagents from distant mines and wild beasts is far beyond his physical capabilities, requiring a proven warrior to undertake the journey.",al={"why do i have to get the materials","why me brutal armor","why does thungrim need my help"},it="why_me",add="8131a754"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Horde warrior, you prove your valor and endurance across multiple continents to earn custom-forged battle armor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Orc, Tauren, Troll, and Forsaken smiths bring their distinct craft traditions together in one battle set.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how Thun'grim's scroll blends smoky iron, powdered azurite, and phlogiston to refine standard iron smelting."},kw={"barrens","brutal armor","brutal hauberk","phlogiston","powdered azurite","smoky iron ingot","thun'grim firegaze","warrior quest"},rel={"quest:1825","quest:1502","zone:barrens","topic:horde","topic:kobold"},m={start="Thun'grim Firegaze",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1838,ri={"Iron Bar","Powdered Azurite","Smoky Iron Ingot","Vial of Phlogiston"}},src={"Brutal Armor"}}
E["quest:1839"] = {t="quest",n="Ula'elek and the Brutal Gauntlets",z="barrens",s="Thun'grim Firegaze sends you from the Barrens to Sen'jin Village for the Brutal Gauntlets. There, Darkspear craftsman Ula'elek will forge them.",h="Thun'grim Firegaze sends you from the Barrens to Sen'jin Village for the Brutal Gauntlets.",sec={{t="A Journey to the Coast",b="Thun'grim Firegaze sends you east after you prove your valor in the Barrens and begin assembling the Brutal Armor set. The veteran orc smith relies on skilled artisans across Horde lands instead of forging every piece at his mountain perch. For the heavy mail gauntlets, he directs you to Durotar's rocky southern shores.",sp=0},{t="The Eyes of the Loa",b="In Sen'jin Village, troll armorsmith Ula'elek works among his Darkspear kin. Thun'grim has already told him of your deeds, and Ula'elek says the spirits have watched your triumphs in battle. For a warrior earning a place among the Horde's elite, fine craft and spiritual acknowledgement go hand in hand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Ula'elek and the Brutal Gauntlets?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze, an orc armorer atop the mountains in the Barrens, gives you the task.",al={"quest giver","who starts ula'elek and the brutal gauntlets","thun'grim firegaze quest"},it="people",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Ula'elek?",a="You can find Ula'elek in Sen'jin Village on Durotar's southern coast.",al={"ula'elek location","where is ula'elek","ulaelek senjin"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Brutal Armor set?",a="Brutal Armor is a custom mail set for seasoned Horde warriors around their thirtieth season. Allied smiths across Kalimdor craft its pieces.",al={"brutal armor","what are brutal gauntlets","warrior class armor 30"},it="item"},{q="What happens after reaching Ula'elek?",a="After welcoming you and acknowledging your deeds in battle, Ula'elek asks you to gather the exotic materials for the Brutal Gauntlets, starting with Satyr Hooves.",al={"next quest","after speaking to ula'elek","satyr hooves quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim send you to a troll armorsmith?",a="Thun'grim shares the Brutal Armor set's forging among the Horde's finest specialized smiths, including Darkspear craftsman Ula'elek, who makes the gauntlets.",al={"why ula'elek","why go to sen'jin village","troll smith brutal armor"},it="motive"},{q="Do Alliance players have an equivalent to this quest?",a="Alliance warriors undertake a similar martial trial to craft class-specific armor, but the Brutal Armor chain and Ula'elek's work belong to the Horde.",al={"alliance brutal gauntlets","alliance equivalent"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze need you to travel to Sen'jin Village?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze is guiding your growth as a rising warrior of the Horde. While he oversees your training, the ancient art of forging Brutal Armor calls upon the specialized talents of fellow craftsmen across Horde lands. Ula'elek in Sen'jin Village is a skilled Darkspear armorsmith attuned to the spirits and suited to hammer out the gauntlets. Thun'grim sends you in person not only to commission the piece, but to prove your dedication and earn the armorsmith's trust directly.",al={"why me ulaelek","why cant thungrim craft gauntlets","why send warrior to durotar"},it="why_me",add="a664db53"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Horde warrior, assembling the Brutal Armor marks your passage toward becoming a battle-hardened frontline champion.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, Ula'elek's work shows how Darkspear smithing and spiritual attunement aid the Horde war effort.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see orc smiths in the Barrens and troll smiths in Durotar work together, binding Thrall's young coalition."},kw={"brutal gauntlets","darkspear","durotar","sen'jin village","the barrens","thun'grim firegaze","ula'elek","warrior"},rel={"npc:ula-elek","quest:1838","quest:1842","quest:1843","quest:1502","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Thun'grim Firegaze",["end"]="Ula'elek",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1839},src={"Ula'elek and the Brutal Gauntlets"}}
E["quest:1841"] = {t="quest",n="Velora Nitely and the Brutal Legguards",z="barrens",s="Thun'grim Firegaze sends Horde warriors across the Great Sea for Velora Nitely's Brutal Legguards. In the Undercity, the Forsaken smith draws on the craft she kept from her mortal life to forge the armor. Her work helps assemble a durable suit for the Horde's warriors.",h="Thun'grim Firegaze sends Horde warriors across the Great Sea for Velora Nitely's Brutal Legguards.",sec={{t="A Journey Across the Sea",b="Thun'grim Firegaze sends you east across the Great Sea to find a smith for the Brutal Legguards. You've proved your mettle to the veteran smith at his vigil in the Barrens, and now he points you toward the fabled Brutal Armor. Thun'grim cannot make the whole suit alone, so he relies on skilled allies across the Horde. The greaves call for an artisan whose work was revered before northern humanity fell, in the Forsaken's underground kingdom.",sp=0},{t="The Artistry of Velora Nitely",b="Velora Nitely works in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, where her old craft still serves the Horde. Before the Scourging of the north ended her mortal life, she was one of the Kingdom of Lordaeron's foremost armorsmiths. Her homeland was corrupted, and she became one of the Forsaken, but death did not take her mastery of metal. She now turns her human skill toward the Horde's warriors, with a dry, macabre wit about being undead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Velora Nitely?",a="Velora Nitely was once celebrated as one of the finest armorsmiths in the kingdom of Lordaeron. After the Third War, she rose again as one of the Forsaken and made her home in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, where she still practices her craft for the Horde.",al={"velora nitely lore","who is velora","forsaken smith velora"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thun'grim send me to Undercity?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze sends you to the Undercity because the full Brutal Armor set calls for skilled artisans across the Horde. He knows Velora's reputation for armor and dispatches you to Lordaeron to commission the legguards from her.",al={"why go to undercity","thun'grim undercity quest","barrens to undercity warrior"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Velora Nitely in the Undercity?",a="Velora Nitely works in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, at the forges among smiths and other master crafters serving Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"velora nitely location","where is velora nitely","find velora nitely"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after speaking to Velora Nitely?",a="Velora asks you to gather shinbones from Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands for your Brutal Legguards.",al={"next quest after velora","dragonmaw shinbones quest","what does velora want"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does Velora have any dialogue about being undead?",a="Yes. Velora dryly jokes about whether she is making the armor for you or the other way around. She says she lost her sense of humor around the time she lost her sense of smell and stopped breathing.",al={"velora jokes","undead smith dialogue","velora humor"}},{q="Is Brutal Armor only for warriors?",a="Yes. The Brutal Armor trials, including seeking Velora Nitely for the legguards, are for Horde warriors advancing through the seasoned ranks.",al={"can other classes get brutal armor","warrior only quest brutal armor"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze want this done?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze is helping you forge your full suit of Brutal Armor, a rite of martial progression for promising warriors of the Horde. While Thun'grim can craft several components himself, the specialized craftsmanship required for the legguards exceeds his personal forge techniques, prompting him to direct you to Velora Nitely, renowned as one of Lordaeron's finest armorsmiths.",al={"thungrim firegaze motive","why make brutal legguards","why send to velora nitely"},it="motive",add="7eb107f7"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you reach a milestone in the Horde's armor trials around level thirty, traveling beyond Kalimdor for specialized class armor.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see Velora Nitely carrying on the refined skills and artistic legacy of fallen Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you join a line of work that brings orcs, trolls, and tauren from Kalimdor together with Forsaken craftsmen in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"brutal armor","brutal legguards","lordaeron","thun'grim firegaze","trade quarter","undercity","velora nitely","warrior quest"},rel={"quest:1838","quest:1846","npc:velora-nitely","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","topic:lordaeron","zone:barrens"},m={start="Thun'grim Firegaze",["end"]="Velora Nitely",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1841},src={"Velora Nitely and the Brutal Legguards"}}
E["quest:1848"] = {t="quest",n="Brutal Hauberk",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, Horde warriors face a trial before Thun'grim Firegaze will forge their mail. They gather rare materials and prove themselves against dangerous foes across the lands, then bring their bounty to the reclusive smith. He hammers it into armor built for battle.",h="Across the Barrens, Horde warriors face a trial before Thun'grim Firegaze will forge their mail.",sec={{t="A Smith's Masterpiece",b="In the northern Barrens, Thun'grim Firegaze forges armor only for warriors who meet his demands. The reclusive orc sends them far and wide to gather tough beast parts, rare metal, and alchemical reagents before he lights his bellows. The finished hauberk offers protection and marks the endurance and grit its wearer has shown, earning recognition from veteran fighters throughout the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Forged in Hardship",b="Thun'grim makes his demands punishing by design. Horde arms and armor are expected to carry the sweat and blood of their wearer from the moment they are made. When you hand over the finished Brutal Hauberk, the smith offers no praise. He expects you to prove the armor in brutal combat and return with stories of blood and honor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Brutal Hauberk?",a="The Brutal Hauberk is a sturdy chestpiece crafted by the orc blacksmith Thun'grim Firegaze. Horde warriors earn it by proving their combat prowess and gathering rare materials across several dangerous lands.",al={"what is brutal hauberk","brutal hauberk quest","who makes brutal hauberk"},it="item"},{q="Who is Thun'grim Firegaze?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze is a reclusive veteran smith who lives atop a mountain spur in the northern Barrens, just east of the road between the Crossroads and Orgrimmar. He tests emerging warriors and forges them specialized armor when they prove their worth.",al={"who is thun grim","thungrim firegaze","where is thungrim"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thun'grim require so much effort before crafting the armor?",a="Horde warrior tradition prizes hardship alongside martial skill. Thun'grim believes fine mail belongs to those who have shed their own blood and labored to gather the rare components needed to forge it.",al={"why gather so many materials","brutal armor requirements","thungrim trials"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="After Thun'grim presents you with the finished hauberk, his work for you is complete. You can wear the armor into battle across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"what comes after brutal hauberk","next quest after brutal hauberk","is there a follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Is the Brutal Hauberk quest available to the Alliance?",a="No. The Brutal Hauberk is a Horde trial. Alliance warriors undergo a separate martial rite with the smiths of Ironforge and the surrounding dwarven territories to forge their own signature armor.",al={"can alliance get brutal hauberk","alliance equivalent","is this horde only"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Where in the Barrens can Thun'grim be found?",a="Thun'grim lives on a high ridge in the northern Barrens, just south of Thorn Hill and east of the Crossroads.",al={"thungrim location","where is thungrim in barrens","how to find thun grim"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze forge this hauberk for you?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze does not forge his brutal armor for just anyone. As an honored master armorer testing promising Horde warriors, he demands proof of endurance, strength, and raw tenacity before striking his hammer. By gathering the necessary materials and braving perils on his behalf, you proved yourself worthy to bear his finest craftsmanship into battle.",al={"why me brutal hauberk","why does thungrim make the armor","why give brutal hauberk"},it="why_me",add="a5674fab"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a young Horde warrior, you earn the Brutal Hauberk as you pass from raw recruit to hardened combatant outfitted in custom mail.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see its virtues of martial self-reliance and strength reflected in a hauberk made from trophies won in Kalimdor's wilds.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can learn from Thun'grim's traditional orcish craft, where martial spirit and resilience are hammered into steel."},kw={"brutal armor","brutal hauberk","crossroads","orcish smithing","the barrens","thun'grim firegaze","warrior mail"},rel={"quest:1838","quest:1502","zone:barrens"},m={start="Thun'grim Firegaze",["end"]="Thun'grim Firegaze",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1848},src={"Brutal Hauberk (quest)"}}
E["quest:1946"] = {t="quest",n="Nether-lace Garment",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Kil'hala weaves dryad hair into enchanted cloth for spellcasters. The finished garment marks the end of his specialized work in the Barrens.",h="At the Crossroads, Kil'hala weaves dryad hair into enchanted cloth for spellcasters.",sec={{t="Weaving the Nether-Lace",b="At the Crossroads in the Barrens, Kil'hala weaves nether-lace from the locks of laughing sisters. The dryads live in Ashenvale, and their hair is harvested for this work. Kil'hala binds the woodland enchantment in those rare, magically resonant locks into cloth that is comfortable and durable.",sp=0},{t="Favors for Orgrimmar",b="Kil'hala wants more than fine work from his trade. He hopes to win favor with Deino, a respected troll mage who lives in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. By making exceptional garb for aspiring practitioners, he hopes to earn and keep Deino's good graces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is nether-lace?",a="Nether-lace is an enchanted fabric Kil'hala weaves from the tresses of laughing sisters. The cloth is resilient and carries their woodland enchantment.",al={"nether lace cloth","what is nether lace garment"},it="item"},{q="Who crafts the Nether-lace Garment?",a="Kil'hala crafts the garment at his station in the Crossroads in the Barrens, once he has the needed dryad hair from Ashenvale.",al={"who makes nether lace","kil hala nether lace"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Kil'hala mention Deino?",a="Deino is an influential troll mage trainer in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. Kil'hala hopes to keep her favor, and believes your satisfaction with his tailoring will reflect well on him.",al={"who is deino","why mention deino"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the materials for the garment come from?",a="The garment's core material is hair gathered from the elusive laughing sisters, dryads found across Ashenvale's forests.",al={"nether lace materials","dryad hair cloth"},it="origin"},{q="Who is this garment made for?",a="The garment is made chiefly for spellcasters, especially mages in training who need robes that channel arcane energies without hindering movement.",al={"who uses nether lace garment","nether lace class"},it="for_you"},{q="Where is Kil'hala located?",a="Kil'hala lives at the Crossroads, the central crossroads settlement in the heart of the Barrens.",al={"kil hala location","where is kil hala"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you receive a garment that bridges wilderness trials in Ashenvale with Kil'hala's craftsmanship under Deino's guidance.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see how exotic reagents such as dryad hair become cloth with innate magical protection.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help equip its spellcasters with materials from Kalimdor's sacred woods, part of the ongoing contest between the Horde and Ashenvale's woodland defenders."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","crossroads","deino","kil'hala","laughing sisters","mage","nether-lace"},rel={"quest:1945","npc:kil-hala","npc:deino","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},m={start="Kil'hala",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1946},src={"Nether-lace Garment"}}
E["quest:220"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="barrens",s="Brine's water reaches Islen Waterseer on the eastern Barrens coast, where the next part of the shamanic trial begins. The vial holds water Brine prepared and blessed, the base for a sapta that lets an initiate see water spirits in Silverpine Forest.",h="Brine's water reaches Islen Waterseer on the eastern Barrens coast, where the next part of the shamanic trial...",sec={{t="Return to the Shore",b="After the trials in the southern Barrens, Brine gives the shaman initiate a Vial of Purest Water. The water comes from pure springs and has been consecrated by Brine's rites. The initiate carries it back to the eastern coast, where Islen Waterseer keeps watch. The water links Brine's teachings with the rites of the totem.",sp=0},{t="The Purpose of the Sapta",b="Islen explains that mortal eyes cannot easily see water spirits. To meet them, an initiate drinks a brew called a sapta. The water from Brine will form the base of that draught and open the shaman's senses to what ordinary sight cannot find. Seeing the spirits is only part of the journey; they will test the initiate.",sp=0},{t="A Crossing to Lordaeron",b="Islen sends the shaman beyond Kalimdor, across the sea to Silverpine Forest, south of the Undercity. Beside an isolated shrine, the initiate must drink the sapta and face the elementals directly. Only then can the shaman earn the right to manifest the Water Totem.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Vial of Purest Water?",a="The Vial of Purest Water holds water gathered from pure springs and consecrated by Brine's rites. It is the essential base for brewing a sapta, which lets a shaman communicate with water spirits.",al={"vial of purest water","brine's water","what did brine give me"},it="item"},{q="Who is Islen Waterseer?",a="Islen Waterseer is an elder shaman who lives on the Barrens' secluded southeastern coast, south of Ratchet. She mentors Horde shamans seeking communion with water and the Water Totem.",al={"islen","who is islen waterseer","islen waterseer lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is a sapta?",a="A sapta is a ceremonial drink prepared by shamanic mentors. It changes a shaman's perception, allowing them to see and meet elemental spirits hidden from mortal sight.",al={"sapta meaning","water sapta","what does sapta do"},it="item"},{q="Why do I have to go to Silverpine Forest next?",a="The shrine for this communion lies in Silverpine Forest's coastal waters, south of the Undercity in the Eastern Kingdoms. The spirits there require a shaman to meet them and face a final trial before gaining mastery over water.",al={"why silverpine","silverpine water totem","shrine in silverpine"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does Brine live?",a="Brine lives in a secluded hut in the southern Barrens, high in the hills west of the road toward the Great Lift and Thousand Needles.",al={"brine location","where is brine","finding brine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can any shaman bypass making the sapta?",a="No. The communion rites require a shaman's spirit to be attuned to the unseen world. Without a sapta to open that way, the water spirits at the shrine cannot be met or challenged.",al={"skip sapta","is sapta required","shaman vision quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Brine send you back to Islen Waterseer?",a="Brine has done her part by purifying the waters you collected across Kalimdor and sealing them into a blessed vial. She knows she is merely a guide on your path, not the seer who initiates you into the deeper mysteries. Islen Waterseer sent you to Brine to prove your endurance, and now that the purest water is prepared, Islen alone possesses the wisdom to brew your sapta and direct the final trial of your communion.",al={"why brine sends you","brine motive call of water","why return to islen"},it="motive",add="5a67c999"},{q="Why does Brine need you to carry the vial instead of delivering it herself?",a="This pilgrimage is your trial as a shaman, not an errand of convenience. The vial holds water that you personally drew from the watering hole below Brine's hut in the Barrens, the well at Tarren Mill, and the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale, blessed through your own labor. Carrying it back across the plains to Islen completes your personal connection to the element before you attempt to commune with the spirits.",al={"why must i deliver the vial","why me brine call of water","why cant brine take it"},it="why_me",add="51ede7cd"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a Horde shaman, you complete the Call of Water rites to commune with the spirits and earn the Water Totem, which governs healing and replenishment.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel from the Barrens in Kalimdor to Silverpine in Lordaeron, crossing lands held by the Forsaken as you undertake the trial."},kw={"brine","call of water","islen waterseer","sapta","silverpine forest","the barrens","vial of purest water","water sapta","water totem"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","npc:brine","zone:barrens","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity","quest:63"},m={start="Brine",["end"]="Islen Waterseer",level="23",faction="Horde",id=220},src={"Call of Water (6)"}}
E["quest:2381"] = {t="quest",n="Plundering the Plunderers",z="barrens",s="Wrenix the Wretched sends new Shattered Hand rogues against the Southsea Freebooters near Ratchet. Aboard the Tide Razor, they face pirates, locked strongboxes, and a dangerous guardian before claiming the Southsea Treasure.",h="Wrenix the Wretched sends new Shattered Hand rogues against the Southsea Freebooters near Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Test of Stealth and Steel",b="Wrenix the Wretched, a goblin contact in Ratchet, tests aspiring Shattered Hand operatives. He sends rogues south along the Barrens coast to a cove where the Tide Razor lies at anchor, crewed by Southsea Freebooters. They must board without being seen, enter the pirates’ den where cutpurses train, pick the strongboxes in the hold, and bring back the plunder.",sp=0},{t="Polly and the Gizmo",b="Wrenix warns that earlier thieves were returned to him in pieces. A savage parrot named Polly guards the vessel’s lowest hold. To help a rogue face the bird, Wrenix provides an experimental E.C.A.C. Hurl it at Polly after cracking the pirate strongbox; the device disorients and weakens the bird, making the fight winnable.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Wrenix the Wretched?",a="Wrenix the Wretched is a goblin rogue contact in Ratchet. He works with operatives linked to Orgrimmar’s Shattered Hand, sending new thieves into pirate territory to practice lockpicking and recover stolen plunder.",al={"wrenix","who is wrenix","ratchet goblin rogue quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Tide Razor located?",a="The Tide Razor is anchored south of Ratchet along the Barrens’ eastern coast, in a Southsea Freebooter cove. The ship is a base and training den for the pirates.",al={"tide razor location","where is pirate ship","where are the southsea pirates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is an E.C.A.C. and how do I use it?",a="The E.C.A.C. is an experimental goblin device dispensed by Wrenix’s Gizmotronic Apparatus. Use it against Polly, the giant parrot guarding the Southsea Treasure in the Tide Razor’s hold, to weaken the bird so it can be defeated.",al={"ecac","what is ecac","how to beat polly"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is the lockpicking area on the ship significant?",a="The Tide Razor’s second deck is the Southsea pirates’ training room. Its lockboxes let rogues practice lockpicking in the field before they try the strongbox below.",al={"lockpicking practice","footpad training ship","picking boxes barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this mission so vital for rogues?",a="Completing the heist proves a rogue’s worth to the Shattered Hand network. Wrenix gives you Thistle Tea as your share, a brew that quickly restores a rogue’s combat energy.",al={"rogue quest thistle tea","why do plundering the plunderers","rogue quest reward"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Polly?",a="Polly is a vicious parrot guarding the lower hold of the Tide Razor for the Southsea Freebooters. Without goblin technology to weaken the bird, it is lethal to inexperienced infiltrators.",al={"polly","giant parrot","tide razor boss"},it="target"},{q="Why does Wrenix the Wretched want the Southsea treasure?",a="Wrenix is a cunning goblin thief and fixer operating out of Ratchet who is after the Southsea Freebooters' illicit hoard as a major payoff. Previous attempts to plunder the pirates' ship proved disastrous, leaving five other rogues dead and dismembered. By sending you to breach the vessel and recover the loot, Wrenix secures a lucrative prize while testing your mettle against cutthroats who stole it first.",al={"wrenix motive","why steal southsea treasure","why does wrenix want this done"},it="motive",add="d00111f9"},{q="Why does Wrenix need you instead of hiring guards or going himself?",a="Stealing from the Southsea Freebooters is delicate, illicit work that cannot be handled by brute force or Ratchet's neutral guards. The pirates train their own thieves aboard the Tide Razor, requiring someone skilled in stealth and lockpicking to slip into the hold undetected. As a goblin operating outside standard trade agreements, Wrenix prefers to hire an expendable, capable operative rather than risk his own skin.",al={"why me wrenix","why send a rogue","why doesn't wrenix get the treasure"},it="why_me",add="abe44597"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you learn to pick locks under pressure and receive Thistle Tea, a prized brew for operatives serving the Horde.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a rogue with an interest in cooking, you can earn Thistle Tea, an herbal tonic valued for restoring energy.",["faction:Horde"]="The Shattered Hand uses goblin contacts in Ratchet to test prospective agents against the Southsea Freebooters, who menace the Barrens coast."},kw={"e.c.a.c.","lockpicking","plundering the plunderers","polly","ratchet","southsea freebooters","southsea treasure","thistle tea","tide razor","wrenix the wretched"},rel={"npc:wrenix-the-wretched","quest:2382","quest:2379","quest:2378","quest:2380","quest:1858","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Wrenix the Wretched",level="18",faction="Horde",id=2381,ri={"Southsea Treasure"}},src={"Plundering the Plunderers"}}
E["quest:3001"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking Strahad",z="barrens",s="Carendin Halgar sends Horde warlocks across the Great Sea to seek Strahad Farsan. Above Ratchet, a human sorcerer offers a path beyond basic shadowcraft toward the difficult art of summoning a felhunter.",h="Carendin Halgar sends Horde warlocks across the Great Sea to seek Strahad Farsan.",sec={{t="A Master Across the Sea",b="Carendin Halgar, a Forsaken warlock trainer in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, knows when an initiate has outgrown basic instruction. He sends his pupils beyond Lordaeron's ruins to find Strahad Farsan. Halgar warns that Strahad is a living human, but no weakling, and says not to treat him as an enemy. For warlocks, the pursuit of demonic mastery often crosses racial and factional lines.",sp=0},{t="The Overlook at Ratchet",b="Strahad works from the bluffs above Ratchet, the goblin port in the Barrens. Near a stone watchtower, he looks down on the sailors, mercenaries, and merchants below, whose blissful ignorance of the Twisting Nether amuses him. Horde warlocks who reach him may bring distrust and simmering hatred in their eyes. Strahad accepts that raw malice as fuel to shape into dark authority.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is an Undercity warlock sending me to a human?",a="Warlocks often set aside factional divisions to pursue rare and potent dark lore. Carendin Halgar says Strahad Farsan has a specialized command of greater demonic summonings that Halgar cannot teach. In the pursuit of demonic power, an instructor's knowledge matters more than their bloodline.",al={"why human trainer","why send to human","carendin sending to strahad"},it="motive"},{q="Where exactly is Strahad Farsan located?",a="Strahad Farsan is in the Barrens, on the high cliffs above the goblin port of Ratchet. He stands near a stone tower overlooking the bay and the busy harbor docks.",al={"strahad location","where is strahad","how to find strahad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of power does Strahad teach?",a="Strahad guides experienced warlocks through the complex rituals for binding greater demons from the Twisting Nether. His instruction leads toward the dangerous trials of summoning and commanding a felhunter.",al={"what does strahad teach","what is this quest for","felhunter quest"},it="power"},{q="Is Strahad allied with the Alliance?",a="Though human, Strahad works from neutral goblin territory in Ratchet and is unaffiliated with the Grand Alliance. He is an independent practitioner who deals freely with Horde and Alliance warlocks able to endure his instruction.",al={"is strahad alliance","strahad faction","is strahad friendly"},it="allies"},{q="What happens after reaching Strahad?",a="When you arrive, Strahad tests your resolve and enlists you to recover the scattered fragments and components of the Tome of the Cabal. The search ranges far as you seek the ritual for summoning a felhunter.",al={"what next after strahad","tome of the cabal","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Strahad welcome hatred in his students?",a="Demonic magic feeds on intense emotion, dominance, and willpower. Hatred can be focused and disciplined, helping a summoner bind chaotic beings from the Nether before they consume someone who lacks discipline.",al={"why does strahad like hatred","hatred in your eyes"}},{q="Why does Carendin send you instead of going himself?",a="Carendin Halgar serves as a resident warlock mentor in the Undercity, guiding novitiates as far as his instruction permits. You have advanced beyond the basic arts he imparts to beginners, proving ready for greater summonings. Rather than a diplomatic errand, this journey is a rite of passage for your own growth. He sends you out to seek Strahad Farsan because it is your own mastery over dark magic that must be tested and expanded.",al={"why send me seeking strahad","why not go himself carendin","why does carendin need me"},it="why_me",add="c0e56201"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, this marks a rite of passage around your thirtieth circle of power. You leave minor imp and voidwalker bindings behind as you turn toward command of the predatory felhunter.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warlock, you set aside your usual hostility toward humans and travel to neutral Ratchet to learn from a living sorcerer.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you are among the Forsaken disciples Carendin Halgar sends from the Undercity. His choice shows that even Sylvanas's loyalists use living masters to expand their arsenal."},kw={"barrens","carendin halgar","felhunter","ratchet","seeking strahad","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal","undercity","warlock"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1758","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",["end"]="Strahad Farsan",level="30",faction="Horde",id=3001},src={"Seeking Strahad (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:3261"] = {t="quest",n="Jorn Skyseer",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, seasoned Horde hunters seek guidance from Jorn Skyseer. After you hunt local raptors for Sergra Darkthorn, she sends you south to Camp Taurajo, where an elder tracker offers deeper lessons.",h="In the southern Barrens, seasoned Horde hunters seek guidance from Jorn Skyseer.",sec={{t="Passing the Mantle",b="You have hunted the cunning sunscale and scytheclaw raptors stalking the northern savannah, earning Sergra Darkthorn's respect at the Crossroads. She knows martial skill must be joined with understanding of the land's great beasts. With her mentorship complete, she sends you south.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Taurajo",b="Follow the Gold Road south through increasingly rugged plains to Camp Taurajo, a vital tauren settlement near the southern wilds. Jorn Skyseer waits there, an elder tracker ready to teach hunters how to pursue elusive, legendary quarry across the Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Jorn Skyseer?",a="After you hunt the local scytheclaws, Sergra Darkthorn, the raptor hunter at the Crossroads, sends you south. Your hunts prove your tracking and hunting prowess.",al={"who gives jorn skyseer","who starts jorn skyseer","sergra darkthorn quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Jorn Skyseer located?",a="Jorn Skyseer is at Camp Taurajo, far south along the main road through the Barrens.",al={"where is jorn skyseer","jorn skyseer location","find jorn skyseer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reaching Jorn Skyseer?",a="When you report to him, Jorn welcomes you to the hunter's path and begins directing you to track and hunt elusive beasts across the southern Barrens. The first is the legendary raptor Ishamuhale.",al={"what does jorn teach","jorn skyseer followup","next quest after jorn skyseer"},it="next_step"},{q="Do I need to be a hunter class to do this quest?",a="No. Any Horde adventurer who completes Sergra Darkthorn's raptor hunts can follow this path of learning how to track the plains, whatever their class.",al={"is this hunter only","class requirement jorn skyseer"},gp=true},{q="Why does Sergra stop teaching you herself?",a="Sergra Darkthorn works among the northern raptor nests near the Crossroads. Once you master those hunts, she sends you south to Jorn Skyseer, who oversees deeper expeditions into southern game.",al={"why does sergra send you away","sergra guidance finished"},it="motive"},{q="What is Camp Taurajo?",a="Camp Taurajo is a tauren encampment in the southern Barrens. It is a hunting post, trading hub, and cultural waystation for travelers journeying between the northern plains and Mulgore or Thousand Needles.",al={"about camp taurajo","what is taurajo"},it="place"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you meet Jorn Skyseer, who tests your ability to outsmart and conquer the legendary apex predators of the central and southern plains.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren returning south toward Camp Taurajo, you reconnect tribal huntsmanship with the spiritual guardianship of the Barrens' wilderness.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel from the Crossroads to Camp Taurajo, deeper into the contested southern Barrens."},kw={"camp taurajo","hunter's path","jorn skyseer","scytheclaws","sergra darkthorn","the barrens","the crossroads"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:crossroads","quest:860","quest:905","zone:barrens","topic:tauren","quest:6065"},m={start="Sergra Darkthorn",["end"]="Jorn Skyseer",level="18",faction="Horde",id=3261},src={"Jorn Skyseer (quest)"}}
E["quest:3281"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Silver",z="barrens",s="Gazrog at the Crossroads sends you after payroll silver stolen by raptors. Rumors of their cunning lead you south of Ratchet, into the Raptor Grounds. The garrison needs its wages back.",h="Gazrog at the Crossroads sends you after payroll silver stolen by raptors.",sec={{t="A Beastly Heist",b="Gazrog needs the Crossroads guards paid, and the raptors have taken their wages. You are sent to recover the stolen coin, not simply punish the beasts. When raptors ambushed the payroll shipment, Gazrog first sought vengeance. But killing the pack would not restore the missing money. The Horde must learn how the raptors carried off heavy crates of coin, and where they took them.",sp=0},{t="The Raptor Grounds",b="Scouts found a raptor nest between two craggy peaks, south of Ratchet and northwest of Northwatch Hold. The creatures dragged the intact lockbox into their territory, where they guard it alongside eggs and fresh kills. Tales of raptor cunning and hoarding now seem true to Gazrog. Ordinary beasts rarely stash metallic valuables.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did raptors steal silver in the first place?",a="Barrens raptors show startling cunning and curious scavenging habits. They dragged the intact strongbox to their communal nests in the Raptor Grounds, perhaps drawn by its shine, the treated leather on the chest, or a hoarding instinct.",al={"why do raptors want silver","why silver raptors","raptor coin motive"}},{q="Who is Gazrog?",a="Gazrog is an orc officer stationed in the Crossroads' main bunker. He manages security and logistics, including threats from local wildlife, centaur incursions, and payroll disruptions.",al={"gazrog","who gives stolen silver","crossroads questgiver gazrog"},it="people"},{q="Where are the Raptor Grounds located?",a="The Raptor Grounds lie in eastern Barrens, south of Ratchet and northwest of Northwatch Hold. Their nests fill a rugged passage between two mountains.",al={"raptor grounds location","where to find stolen silver","stolen silver chest location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens if the silver is not recovered?",a="The stolen silver holds a month's wages for the Crossroads guards. Without it, the outpost's defenders face working without pay, and morale may suffer at a fortress beset by quilboar, centaur, and Alliance raiders.",al={"why is stolen silver important","crossroads guards pay"}},{q="Is this part of a longer quest chain?",a="Before you search for the cache, you must complete Raptor Thieves for Gazrog. There, you cull the raptors that attacked the first transport and track down the stash's location.",al={"stolen silver prerequisites","raptor thieves follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is the Alliance involved in the theft?",a="No. Northwatch Hold lies southeast of the Raptor Grounds, but native raptors carried out the theft. Their thievery and hoarding surprised even veteran Horde commanders.",al={"did northwatch steal silver","alliance raptors barrens"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Gazrog want the silver recovered?",a="The stolen silver constitutes the upcoming month's pay for the Crossroads guards. As a vital Horde outpost facing threats from centaur, quilboar, and the nearby Alliance, the Crossroads depends heavily on these sentries. Without their wages, morale and the settlement's defense could crumble, leaving Gazrog determined to retrieve every coin.",al={"gazrog stolen silver motive","why does gazrog need the silver","why recover stolen silver"},it="motive",add="f31163b7"},{q="What is the Stolen Silver?",a="The silver is payroll meant for the Crossroads sentries, secured within a lockbox until clever raptors made off with it. Stashed deep inside the Raptor Grounds south of Ratchet, this chest of coins represents the livelihood of the outpost's protectors and the security of the Barrens' most crucial crossroads.",al={"what is stolen silver","stolen silver quest item","who does the silver belong to"},it="item",add="b903b9d8"},{q="What are you sent against at the Raptor Grounds?",a="You are dispatched into the Raptor Grounds, a rugged nesting haven south of Ratchet and northwest of Northwatch Hold. The area is teeming with fierce Sunscale raptors, surprisingly cunning beasts known to hoard shiny valuables in their nests and aggressively defend the stolen lockbox from any intruders.",al={"who guards the stolen silver","raptor grounds enemies","what lives at raptor grounds"},it="target",add="03250c10"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the Crossroads keeps its guards paid and fed to hold the Kalimdor frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see Barrens raptors nesting in complex social groups and drawn to artificial, shiny cargo."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","gazrog","payroll","raptor grounds","raptor thieves","ratchet","stolen silver"},rel={"quest:869","npc:gazrog","subzone:raptor-grounds","subzone:crossroads","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Gazrog",level="18",faction="Horde",id=3281,ri={"Stolen Silver"}},src={"Stolen Silver (quest)"}}
E["quest:3301"] = {t="quest",n="Mura Runetotem",z="barrens",s="You carry a snapjaw shell from the Barrens across the sea to Mura Runetotem in Silverpine Forest. Its strange vitality may help the tauren healer aid the Forsaken.",h="You carry a snapjaw shell from the Barrens across the sea to Mura Runetotem in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Bridge Across Seas",b="Tonga Runetotem notices something peculiar about altered snapjaws while investigating the magically changed wildlife around the Barrens oases. Their shells pulse with resilient energy despite their corruption. He asks you to carry one across the Great Sea to his clanmate, Mura Runetotem, who is stationed in the Eastern Kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="Aiding the Forsaken",b="Mura Runetotem is at the Sepulcher, a Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest. She made the arduous journey there to help the Horde's newest allies cleanse and renew their ailing, blighted woodland. Mura hopes the shell's inner glow and enduring spark of life will reveal ways to restore vitality to the northern continent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mura Runetotem?",a="Mura Runetotem is a tauren druid and Tonga Runetotem's clanmate. She traveled across the sea and established herself at the Sepulcher to aid the Forsaken by studying ways to heal their dying forest.",al={"mura","who is mura","runetotem silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Mura Runetotem located?",a="Mura Runetotem is at the Sepulcher, a Forsaken town along the road in central Silverpine Forest, in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"mura location","where is mura","find mura runetotem"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tonga want a snapjaw shell sent to Silverpine?",a="Altered snapjaw shells near the Barrens oases show unnatural vitality and an inner glow. Tonga believes studying that resilient life force may give Mura insights into healing Silverpine Forest's blighted, dying ecology.",al={"why send shell","snapjaw shell purpose","why mura needs shell"},it="motive"},{q="Why are the tauren trying to heal Forsaken lands?",a="Tauren hold a sacred duty to nurture and mend the natural world. Mura sees that Silverpine Forest is decaying and blighted, and hopes to use the earth's healing traditions to aid the Horde's new allies and restore balance to the soil.",al={"tauren helping undead","why heal silverpine","druids in silverpine"}},{q="How does this quest connect the Barrens to Silverpine?",a="The shell's journey connects early Horde territories, carrying you from Kalimdor's plains to the forests of the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"barrens to silverpine quest","cross continent quest"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after giving Mura the shell?",a="Mura is fascinated by the shell's lingering inner glow and resolves to study it closely as she seeks a remedy for Silverpine's blighted woodlands.",al={"mura follow up","what comes next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem ask you to deliver the shell?",a="Tonga Runetotem is stationed at the Crossroads, consumed with investigating the bizarre mutations afflicting the Barrens' oases. Traveling across the sea to the distant continent of Lordaeron would take him away from his urgent duties in Kalimdor, making an adventurous messenger the ideal choice to carry his sample to Mura.",al={"why send me","why can't tonga deliver it","why me mura runetotem"},it="why_me",add="10ada1ab"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the Runetotem clan's dedication to nurturing the natural world reach across the sea to Silverpine's withered groves.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you may see the forest around the Sepulcher as lost to rot and blight, but tauren druids such as Mura Runetotem seek to renew it.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you study unusual returns of nature, even those born of strange mutations, to help restore balance to broken lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see its growing bond in the cooperation between Kalimdor's defenders and the Forsaken in Lordaeron."},kw={"barrens","mura runetotem","oases","sepulcher","silverpine","snapjaw shell","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:sepulcher","zone:barrens","quest:6381"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",["end"]="Mura Runetotem",level="15",faction="Horde",id=3301},src={"Mura Runetotem (quest)"}}
E["quest:3513"] = {t="quest",n="The Runed Scroll",z="barrens",s="A silvery ribbon marks the Runed Scroll found in Kalimdor's wilds as a formal message from across the border. Finding it sends Horde scouts to the Mor'shan Rampart to warn its guards of activity to the north.",h="A silvery ribbon marks the Runed Scroll found in Kalimdor's wilds as a formal message from across the border.",sec={{t="A Silvery Ribbon",b="A fine silvery ribbon binds the scroll, unlike the rough leathers and parchment common in the Barrens. Its craft and script point to the night elves beneath Ashenvale's canopies to the north. With every ridge and road contested, a message taken from the enemy could matter greatly to the Horde's front lines.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Northern Border",b="The scroll belongs with local command, not at the Warchief's hall in Orgrimmar. Kadrak, an orc warrior, watches the border from the Mor'shan Rampart, where the Barrens' red earth meets Ashenvale's forests. Bringing the scroll to this outpost gives its guards word of night elf troop movements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Runed Scroll?",a="The Runed Scroll is a finely made document bound with a silvery ribbon, and its form points to night elf origins. It carries intelligence about their movements or plans along the Barrens border.",al={"what is this scroll","runed scroll lore","silver ribbon scroll"}},{q="Where should I take the scroll?",a="Take the scroll to Kadrak at the Mor'shan Rampart, the northern border post between the Barrens and Ashenvale.",al={"where do i take the runed scroll","scroll turn in","who wants the scroll"}},{q="Who is Kadrak?",a="Kadrak is a Horde scout and guard atop a defensive tower at the Mor'shan Rampart, where he watches for threats from Ashenvale.",al={"kadrak","orc at the tower"}},{q="Why would the night elves drop a scroll in the Barrens?",a="Night elf sentinels and scouts patrol Ashenvale's borders and fringes, sometimes venturing south to test Horde defenses or ambush supply lines headed north.",al={"why is the scroll here","night elves in the barrens"}},{q="What happens after giving the scroll to Kadrak?",a="After reading the scroll, Kadrak names its author as Rynthariel, a dryad and Keymaster of the Talon Den. He sends you to Stonetalon Peak to kill her and plant a Horde flag in the den.",al={"horde presence quest","what comes next"}},{q="Why does the scroll matter to the Horde?",a="Tensions between the Horde and night elves simmer over logging and borders. Intercepted messages can warn the Horde of Alliance ambushes against the Mor'shan Rampart.",al={"importance of runed scroll","horde interest in scroll"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Each intercepted piece of Alliance intelligence helps protect the lumber crews and border sentries guarding the gateway into Ashenvale.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Warsong Clan's expansion into Ashenvale relies on the Mor'shan Rampart's defenses, so night elf messages carry vital news."},kw={"ashenvale","horde border","kadrak","mor'shan rampart","night elf scroll","runed scroll","the barrens"},rel={"npc:kadrak","quest:3514","subzone:mor-shan-rampart","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},m={start="Runed Scroll",["end"]="Kadrak",level="25",faction="Horde",id=3513},src={"The Runed Scroll"}}
E["quest:3514"] = {t="quest",n="Horde Presence",z="barrens",s="At the Barrens border, Kadrak sends a Horde champion into Stonetalon Peak after a missive is intercepted. The champion is to kill the dryad Rynthariel and plant a Horde banner inside the Talon Den.",h="At the Barrens border, Kadrak sends a Horde champion into Stonetalon Peak after a missive is intercepted.",sec={{t="A Message Intercepted",b="Kadrak watches the Barrens' northern boundary for Alliance and night elf incursions. After a messenger carrying a runed scroll is cut down, he decodes the missive and traces it to Rynthariel the Keymaster, an influential dryad in Stonetalon Peak. Kadrak chooses to strike rather than simply guard the mountain passes, hoping to deter future scouts from probing Horde territory.",sp=0},{t="Defiance in the Den",b="Horde warriors enter the Talon Den, a cavern overlooking Stonetalon Peak. Killing Rynthariel deals a blow to local night elf coordination. Kadrak's banner is planted inside the cave, its red standard marking the heart of dryad territory with a warning: incursions into the Barrens will meet decisive violence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kadrak and why does he order this strike?",a="Kadrak is an orc warrior stationed at the northern border outpost between the Barrens and Ashenvale. He orders the strike after discovering Alliance messengers slipping through nearby passes, and seeks to secure Horde lands against foreign encroachment.",al={"kadrak","who is kadrak","kadrak purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Rynthariel the Keymaster?",a="Rynthariel is a dryad leader in the Talon Den atop Stonetalon Peak. She wrote the runed scroll carried by the intercepted messenger, coordinating Alliance and sentinel movements through the mountain corridors.",al={"rynthariel","rynthariel the keymaster","talon den boss"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Talon Den located?",a="The Talon Den is a subterranean cavern complex on the western slopes of Stonetalon Peak, high in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"talon den location","where is talon den","rynthariel location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of planting Kadrak's flag?",a="Kadrak plants the flag as a warning. He wants the night elves and the Alliance to see the red Horde banner over their fallen leader and hesitate before sending more scouts through the Barrens.",al={"why plant the flag","kadrak's flag","horde flag purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="How does this quest connect to 'The Runed Scroll'?",a="Horde Presence follows The Runed Scroll. The mission begins after a player finds the intercepted parchment on an Alliance messenger and brings it to Kadrak for translation.",al={"runed scroll connection","previous quest","horde presence prerequisite"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about Alliance runners in the Barrens?",a="The Barrens links Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, and surrounding settlements. Alliance messengers and night elf allies traveling freely through mountain gaps threaten Horde supply lines and border security.",al={"alliance in barrens","why fight dryads","barrens threat"},it="threat"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, securing the Barrens' northern border helps hold Kalimdor's central plains and protect its fledgling settlements from night elf incursions.",["class:Druid"]="As a Horde druid, you face the bitter pull between faction allegiance and sacred ties to nature when you march into Stonetalon Peak to strike down a dryad child of Cenarius.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Kadrak's offensive as a show of strength and an answer to territorial intrusion, leaving the Alliance no room to maneuver."},kw={"barrens","dryad","horde presence","kadrak","kadrak's flag","rynthariel","stonetalon peak","talon den","the runed scroll"},rel={"quest:3513","npc:kadrak","subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:stonetalon","zone:barrens","quest:1089","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Kadrak",level="29",faction="Horde",id=3514,ri={"Rynthariel the Keymaster"}},src={"Horde Presence"}}
E["quest:3921"] = {t="quest",n="Wenikee Boltbucket",z="barrens",s="Near the Mor'shan Rampart, Wenikee Boltbucket may be able to mend a broken samophlange. Sputtervalve tinkered with the device after it was retrieved from the Sludge Fen, and now needs an expert hand before his colleagues in Undermine demand results.",h="Near the Mor'shan Rampart, Wenikee Boltbucket may be able to mend a broken samophlange.",sec={{t="A Delicate Mishap",b="Sputtervalve's claims to his fellow engineers in Undermine now hang on a broken machine. An adventurer retrieved the mysterious samophlange from the Venture Company's control console at the Sludge Fen, and Sputtervalve could not resist showing it off. His tinkering damaged the delicate contraption. He needs someone with sharper skill to diagnose the damage and repair it.",sp=0},{t="The Tinkerer by the Rampart",b="Wenikee Boltbucket camps beside the road just south of the Mor'shan Rampart. The rampart divides the northern Barrens from Ashenvale. Her inquisitive mind is drawn to intricate machinery, and the broken samophlange quickly captures her attention. Its internal gears hold her curiosity, and she sets to work figuring out how to rebuild it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the samophlange broken?",a="Sputtervalve damaged the samophlange while examining and tinkering with it after it was recovered from the Sludge Fen control console.",al={"why broke","how did it break","sputtervalve broke it"},it="item"},{q="Who is Wenikee Boltbucket?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket is an inventive goblin tinkerer camped just south of the Mor'shan Rampart, on the border between the northern Barrens and Ashenvale. She is known for her skill with complex machinery.",al={"who is wenikee","boltbucket location","where is wenikee"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Sputtervalve care so much about fixing it?",a="Sputtervalve bragged to his colleagues in Undermine that he had secured the device. If he cannot deliver a working samophlange, his reputation and professional standing will suffer.",al={"why fix samophlange","sputtervalve undermine","why does he care"},it="motive"},{q="Does Wenikee know what a samophlange actually does?",a="No. When Wenikee first sees the samophlange, she asks what it is. Its intricate gears fascinate her, and she wants to repair it to see what it does.",al={"does she know what it is","what is a samophlange to her"},it="power"},{q="Where is the Mor'shan Rampart located?",a="The Mor'shan Rampart is a fortified Horde outpost on the northern edge of the Barrens, guarding the pass into Ashenvale.",al={"mor'shan rampart location","where is rampart","barrens ashenvale border"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Wenikee examines the broken device?",a="Wenikee agrees to repair the samophlange, intrigued by its construction. She needs specific mechanical parts, beginning with nugget slugs kept in Venture Company tool buckets at the Sludge Fen, to get the gears working again.",al={"what next","nugget slugs","samophlange next step"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can understand why the samophlange stirs such curiosity. Neither Sputtervalve nor Wenikee knows its original purpose, but its complex gears invite investigation.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Wenikee's camp lies in the shadow of the Mor'shan Rampart, a fortified choke point protecting Horde territory in the northern Barrens from incursions out of Ashenvale."},kw={"broken samophlange","mor'shan rampart","samophlange","sludge fen","sputtervalve","the barrens","undermine","wenikee boltbucket"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","quest:894","subzone:mor-shan-rampart","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},m={start="Sputtervalve",["end"]="Wenikee Boltbucket",level="14",faction="Horde",id=3921},src={"Wenikee Boltbucket (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3922"] = {t="quest",n="Nugget Slugs",z="barrens",s="At the Sludge Fen, Wenikee Boltbucket needs parts for a recovered samophlange. The eccentric tinkerer sends you to the nearby Venture Company drilling crews for spare hardware.",h="At the Sludge Fen, Wenikee Boltbucket needs parts for a recovered samophlange.",sec={{t="Wenikee's Engineering Needs",b="Wenikee Boltbucket has a recovered samophlange and wants to learn how the intricate machine works. Its goblin mechanisms need exact parts, so she sends you to the Venture Company crews at the Sludge Fen. Their heavy tool buckets hold the seventeen-point-five gauge nugget slugs she needs.",sp=0},{t="A Volatile Breakthrough",b="You gather fifteen nugget slugs while Venture Company operators and deforesters work the marsh east of the road. When you bring the parts back, Wenikee sets the samophlange on the ground and begins adjusting it at once. The mismatched parts and rushed assembly end in a sudden explosion. Wenikee is shaken, but her resolve to tinker holds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a nugget slug?",a="A nugget slug is a small metal fastener or ammunition component used in goblin engineering. Wenikee needs seventeen-point-five gauge slugs for the delicate gears inside her samophlange.",al={"nugget slug","nugget slugs","what are nugget slugs"},it="item"},{q="Who is Wenikee Boltbucket?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket is an independent tinkerer camped beside the main trail in the northern Barrens. She is fascinated by intricate machines, especially samophlanges, despite the danger they bring.",al={"wenikee","who is wenikee","wenikee boltbucket"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the nugget slugs found?",a="You can find nugget slugs in tool buckets at the Sludge Fen, a Venture Company camp east of Wenikee's small roadside campsite. The company works there logging and extracting oil.",al={"where are tool buckets","find nugget slugs","sludge fen buckets"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when Wenikee repairs the samophlange?",a="When Wenikee begins adjusting the samophlange with the parts you bring, the machine overloads and explodes in front of her. The poorly calibrated machine proves dangerous.",al={"does the samophlange work","samophlange explosion","wenikee explosion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Venture Company at the Sludge Fen?",a="The Venture Company works at the Sludge Fen to strip-mine the Barrens marshes and extract oil and other natural resources. Its drill rigs and refineries pollute the surrounding landscape.",al={"why venture co sludge fen","sludge fen purpose","venture company barrens"},it="conflict"},{q="Does this quest unlock any further tasks?",a="After the repair attempt goes badly, Wenikee sends you to Orgrimmar to consult Rilli Greasygob, a former Venture Company engineer. She names the next task Rilli Greasygob.",al={"what comes next","follow up quest","after nugget slugs"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="Why does Wenikee Boltbucket want nugget slugs?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket is an eager tinker determined to repair the mysterious samophlange recovered from the Venture Company's control console. To get the complex machine running, she needs seventeen-point-five gauge nugget slugs, a specific mechanical component she lacks. Driven purely by curiosity and the irresistible urge to tinker with intricate machinery, she wants to get the device back into working order to see what it actually does.",al={"why does wenikee need nugget slugs","wenikee boltbucket motive","why fix the samophlange"},it="motive",add="af90a96f"},{q="Why are you sent to steal from the Venture Company at the Sludge Fen?",a="The Venture Company established an extensive oil-drilling operation at the Sludge Fen, complete with drilling rigs and heavy mechanical workshops. Because of their industrial scale, their workers keep tool buckets stocked with the precise seventeen-point-five gauge nugget slugs Wenikee requires. Rather than manufacturing her own or bartering with the hostile operators, she sends you to scavenge the components directly from their work sites.",al={"why sludge fen","why venture company","who has nugget slugs"},it="target",add="8f6d1935"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may recognize the warning signs of goblin handiwork before Wenikee's rushed repairs end in an explosion.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the Venture Company's work at the Sludge Fen harms the marshes. Stealing its supplies gives you reason to strike back."},kw={"barrens","nugget slugs","samophlange","sludge fen","tool buckets","venture company","wenikee boltbucket"},rel={"quest:3921","quest:894","subzone:sludge-fen","topic:venture-company","zone:barrens"},m={start="Wenikee Boltbucket",level="15",faction="Horde",id=3922,ri={"Nugget Slug"}},src={"Nugget Slugs (Classic)"}}
E["quest:4021"] = {t="quest",n="Counterattack!",z="barrens",s="At Regthar Deathgate’s outpost west of the Crossroads, Kolkar warriors strike back after their leaders fall. They have crossed from Desolace, and Warlord Krom'zar leads their charge.",h="At Regthar Deathgate’s outpost west of the Crossroads, Kolkar warriors strike back after their leaders fall.",sec={{t="Vengeance from Desolace",b="The Kolkar have suffered a deep humiliation in the Barrens. Barak Kodobane, Verog the Dervish, and Hezrul Bloodmark are dead, leaving the remaining centaur shattered and without direction. Word of their defeat travels west across the mountains to their ancestral homeland in Desolace. There, a fresh force of hardened Kolkar warriors rallies instead of scattering into the scrubland. Burning for blood and retribution, they cross into the Barrens and march against the young Horde encampments.",sp=0},{t="Defense of the Bunkers",b="Kolkar warriors assault the fortified Horde bunkers west of the Crossroads, where Regthar Deathgate commands the defense. Waves of invaders clash with the Horde grunts stationed there. Warlord Krom'zar leads the warband, his banner rallying the centaur as they charge. The defenders must hold the line, fell Krom'zar, and tear down his war banner to break the centaur threat across the central plains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the Kolkar attacking this specific outpost?",a="Regthar Deathgate arranged the killings of Kolkar leaders around the Barrens’ oases. Humiliated by their fallen chieftains, the centaur march on his fortified bunkers west of the Crossroads to strike the Horde command post responsible.",al={"why attack regthar","why barrens bunker attacked","centaur counterattack reason"},it="place"},{q="Where did these centaur reinforcements come from?",a="The reinforcements cross the western mountain passes from Desolace, the rugged homeland where most centaur clans dwell.",al={"where do kolkar come from","kolkar reinforcements source","desolace centaur"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Warlord Krom'zar?",a="Warlord Krom'zar leads the Kolkar warband from Desolace. He charges Regthar’s bunkers beneath his war banner, which Horde defenders tear down after killing him.",al={"who is kromzar","krom'zar lore","warlord kromzar"},it="target"},{q="Does Thrall learn about this battle?",a="Yes. Regthar Deathgate promises to send formal word of the battle directly to Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar. He honors the defense of the Barrens.",al={"thrall counterattack","does thrall hear about this","warchief reward"},sp=1},{q="What happens to the Kolkar presence after this battle?",a="Krom'zar’s defeat breaks the Kolkar’s last organized force in the central Barrens. Trade routes around the Crossroads are secured, while the remaining tribes are left fragmented and leaderless.",al={"are kolkar defeated","barrens centaur fate","end of kolkar questline"},sp=1},{q="What is the piece of Krom'zar's banner used for?",a="A torn piece of Krom'zar’s banner is physical proof that the warlord is dead. It also marks the collapse of the centaur invasion.",al={"kromzar banner","banner piece quest item","why take banner"},it="item"},{q="Why does Regthar Deathgate want this done?",a="Your relentless campaign against the Kolkar leaders pushed the centaur to the brink, provoking a retaliatory invasion straight from Desolace. Regthar Deathgate knows that if this vengeance force overruns the forward bunkers west of the Crossroads, the Horde's foothold across the northern Barrens could unravel. Crushing their counterattack and slaying their warlord ends their organized threat once and for all, securing the territory for the Horde and ensuring your prior victories were not in vain.",al={"why does regthar need this done","regthar deathgate motive","why stop the kolkar counterattack"},it="motive",add="f1fed609"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help defend the bunkers and secure Horde territory in the central Barrens. The defense protects supply lines between Durotar, Mulgore, and the Crossroads.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you help drive back the centaur threat that has hounded your people for generations. Krom'zar’s defeat brings greater security to the plains.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you stand with the outpost grunts against repeated centaur charges. The defense demands endurance on the front line and discipline in battle."},kw={"barrens","bunkers","centaur","counterattack","crossroads","desolace","kolkar","kromzar","regthar deathgate","warlord krom'zar"},rel={"quest:852","quest:851","quest:850","quest:1361","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:desolace","npc:thrall"},m={start="Regthar Deathgate",level="20",faction="Horde",id=4021,ri={"Piece of Krom'zar's Banner"}},src={"Counterattack! (Classic)"}}
E["quest:4736"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of Menara Voidrender",z="barrens",s="Across the sea, Alliance warlocks seek Menara Voidrender in the Barrens. From Strahad Farsan's tower above Ratchet, she teaches seasoned practitioners to craft tools and garments that strengthen their control of demons.",h="Across the sea, Alliance warlocks seek Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Summons from Ironforge",b="Briarthorn sees when a warlock has moved beyond basic demonology and resisted corruption. He sends those pupils beyond Ironforge, across the sea to Kalimdor, instead of keeping them beneath the mountain. There, they can learn practical felcraft from an artisan with greater skill.",sp=0},{t="The Enclave Above Ratchet",b="Strahad Farsan keeps a solitary tower on the bluffs above Ratchet. Warlocks often set aside racial and political borders to survive in a world wary of dark magic. Menara Voidrender stays at Strahad's sanctuary and works with warlocks of every allegiance, helping them sharpen their craft and keep their summoned fiends bound.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest 'In Search of Menara Voidrender'?",a="Briarthorn sends disciplined Alliance warlocks who have advanced beyond basic demonology to seek instruction.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","briarthorn location"},gp=true},{q="Where can Menara Voidrender be found?",a="Menara Voidrender is at Strahad Farsan's tower on the bluffs above Ratchet in the Barrens.",al={"menara voidrender location","where is menara voidrender","strahad farsan tower location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does an Alliance warlock have to travel to Horde territory?",a="Warlocks often cross faction lines because their craft puts them in danger. Ratchet is a neutral port run by the Steamwheedle Cartel, and Strahad's tower gives practitioners of forbidden magic a secluded place to gather and study.",al={"why go to the barrens","why travel to ratchet","barrens dangerous for alliance"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Menara offer upon completion?",a="Menara offers the chance to craft powerful warlock attire, beginning with gathering the components for an Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe.",al={"what does menara teach","quest reward","next quest after menara"},gp=true},{q="Is Menara Voidrender Alliance or Horde?",a="Menara Voidrender aids disciplined warlocks regardless of their origins. She is stern and prickly, but treats practitioners of the dark arts without regard to faction.",al={"menara faction","is menara friendly"},it="side"},{q="Why do warlocks congregate across racial lines?",a="Demons can strike back at careless summoners of any race. Warlocks share knowledge and seek mutual survival as they master the Twisting Nether.",al={"warlock unity","why do warlocks work together"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Briarthorn send you to Menara Voidrender?",a="Briarthorn recognizes that your warlock training has progressed remarkably well, and particularly notes that you have managed to avoid corruption by the fel and arcane arts thus far. Believing your dedication and discipline deserve reward, he directs you to Menara Voidrender above Ratchet. Menara possesses advanced knowledge and the expertise required to craft specialized robes and implements to further bolster a rising warlock's burgeoning power.",al={"why does briarthorn want this done","why send me to menara voidrender","briarthorn motive"},it="motive",add="34d3d012"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you seek advanced spellcraft that leads to crafting your Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance warlock, you cross hostile Barrens territory and rely on Ratchet's tenuous neutrality to reach Strahad's tower.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnomish warlock, your restraint against arcane and fel corruption matters to Menara, who values practical control over theory.",["race:Human"]="As a human warlock, you leave behind the hidden cults of Stormwind and Ironforge for Ratchet's secluded summit."},kw={"briarthorn","enchanted gold bloodrobe","ironforge","menara voidrender","ratchet","strahad farsan","the barrens","warlock"},rel={"npc:menara-voidrender","npc:strahad-farsan","quest:1796","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Briarthorn",["end"]="Menara Voidrender",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=4736},src={"In Search of Menara Voidrender (Ironforge)"}}
E["quest:4738"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of Menara Voidrender",z="barrens",s="An Alliance warlock seeking to craft powerful vestments is directed by the Mage Quarter's covert practitioners to seek out Menara Voidrender across the Great Sea. Stationed high above the neutral port of Ratchet, Menara trains dark spellcasters across faction divides in the dangerous arts of binding and artifact creation.",h="An Alliance warlock seeking to craft powerful vestments is directed by the Mage Quarter's covert...",sec={{t="A Reluctant Recommendation",b="Within the dark crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, warlock trainer Demisette Cloyce is known for her strict, unsparing standards. When an aspiring warlock reaches the threshold of weaving significant items of power, Demisette rarely believes they are truly ready. Nevertheless, higher authorities within the cabal mandate the student's advancement, dispatching them far from the safety of the capital to prove their mettle.",sp=0},{t="The Tower Above Ratchet",b="The destination is the arid hills overlooking the goblin port of Ratchet in the Barrens. There, Menara Voidrender maintains her laboratory in a stone tower. Isolated from the strict laws of Stormwind and the watchful eyes of Orgrimmar, Menara accepts apprentices regardless of race or political allegiance, knowing that the fiends and demonic entities warlocks contend with harbor equal malice toward every mortal soul.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is an Alliance warlock sent all the way to the Barrens?",a="Few practitioners in the Alliance possess the arcane knowledge or freedom to craft advanced fel vestments like the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe. Menara Voidrender operates out of a secluded tower above the neutral port of Ratchet, providing a rare sanctuary where warlocks of all backgrounds can study dangerous crafts beyond the reach of capital guards and inquisitors.",al={"why ratchet","why go to barrens","why menara voidrender"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Demisette Cloyce?",a="Demisette Cloyce is a senior human warlock trainer who conducts clandestine operations beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Stern and protective of dangerous knowledge, she sends students to Menara only when ordered by the unseen powers guiding the warlock enclave.",al={"demisette cloyce lore","who starts in search of menara"},it="identity"},{q="Does Menara Voidrender care about the Alliance or Horde conflict?",a="No. Menara openly explains that warlocks must look past racial and factional boundaries. The demons and extraplanar forces they summon display equal savagery to all who falter, making mutual survival and shared dark arts far more vital than mortal wars.",al={"is menara horde or alliance","does menara hate alliance"},it="conflict"},{q="What item is Menara Voidrender preparing the warlock to make?",a="Reaching Menara is the first step toward forging the Robe of Arcana into the fabled Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe, a potent garment infused with rare reagents, fine tailoring, and bound demonic energies.",al={"what does menara teach","what robe is this for","bloodrobe quest"},it="item"},{q="Is traveling to Ratchet dangerous for an Alliance warlock?",a="The Barrens is primarily Horde territory populated by hostile wildlife, centaur, and orc patrols. However, Ratchet itself is a neutral port run by the Steamwheedle Cartel, making Menara's tower accessible if an Alliance traveler sticks to the coast or arrives safely by boat from Booty Bay.",al={"how dangerous is ratchet","is the barrens safe"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Demisette Cloyce think the player isn't ready?",a="Demisette views the creation of fel-infused power items as reckless for untested novices. Warlock artifacts demand strict discipline; minor errors in binding reagents or demonic essences can destroy the practitioner or loose horrors into the world.",al={"why demisette doubts player","demisette warning"},it="motive"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This rite of passage bridges the hidden warrens of Stormwind to the open frontiers of Kalimdor, teaching that the pursuit of demonic mastery transcends mortal factions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Undertaking this journey forces Alliance casters out of their familiar eastern territories and into the untamed wilderness of the Barrens to find specialized instruction."},kw={"bloodrobe","demisette cloyce","enchanted gold bloodrobe","menara voidrender","ratchet","slaughtered lamb","the barrens","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:menara-voidrender","npc:demisette-cloyce","quest:1796","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Demisette Cloyce",["end"]="Menara Voidrender",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=4738},src={"In Search of Menara Voidrender (Stormwind)"}}
E["quest:4739"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of Menara Voidrender",z="barrens",s="Menara Voidrender awaits Horde warlocks ready for deeper study in Ratchet. From the Undercity, they cross the Great Sea to her hilltop refuge above the port.",h="Menara Voidrender awaits Horde warlocks ready for deeper study in Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Shadows",b="Kaal Soulreaper watches warlocks grow more skilled in the Undercity. When one outgrows simple hexes and impish thralls, he sends them across the Great Sea for specialized instruction. Demonic control leaves little room for error. A skilled mentor can help a warlock survive the volatile powers of the Nether.",sp=0},{t="The Tower Above Ratchet",b="Strahad Farsan’s tower rises from a high bluff above Ratchet. Away from the scrutiny of city guards, practitioners such as Menara Voidrender teach younger initiates. Warlocks from different backgrounds set aside tribal and political rivalries. The demons they bargain with will consume human, orc, or Forsaken alike if their summoner’s will falters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Kaal Soulreaper sends warlocks from the Undercity to Menara Voidrender when they have grown skilled enough for advanced instruction.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest","kaal soulreaper location"},gp=true},{q="Where can Menara Voidrender be found?",a="Menara Voidrender lives in the Barrens, in the stone tower above Ratchet with Strahad Farsan.",al={"where is menara","find menara voidrender","menara location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must Horde warlocks travel all the way to the Barrens?",a="Horde warlocks travel to the Barrens for secluded instruction in demonic arts. Menara Voidrender teaches and crafts robes from Strahad’s tower, where warlocks of every background study away from civic and religious authorities.",al={"why ratchet","why travel to barrens","why go to menara"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after reaching Menara Voidrender?",a="Menara acknowledges your training and offers to guide you in making an Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe. The work begins a journey to gather rare and dangerous components across Azeroth.",al={"quest continuation","what does menara give me","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do warlocks of different races share knowledge?",a="Demons show no mercy based on race when a summoner loses control. To survive, warlocks share techniques and protect their craft from disaster.",al={"warlock cooperation","why work together warlock","menara warlock lore"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Strahad Farsan?",a="Strahad Farsan is a master warlock who keeps the stone tower above Ratchet. It offers practitioners a remote place to learn demonic arts, away from major faction strongholds.",al={"strahad tower","who owns the tower in ratchet","strahad farsan"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Kaal Soulreaper send you to Menara Voidrender?",a="Kaal recognizes that your burgeoning power and confidence have outgrown basic instruction. Warlocks operate under constant peril from the demonic forces they summon; without advanced discipline and proper arcane instruments, an ambitious practitioner risks utter destruction. Menara Voidrender specializes in testing rising warlocks and crafting powerful implements to anchor their craft, making her guidance essential for your continued survival and mastery.",al={"why does kaal send me","kaal soulreaper motive","why go to menara voidrender"},it="motive",add="09af788d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you begin advanced practice and can pursue specialized vestments attuned to the Nether’s energies.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you leave the Undercity’s grim depths for Kalimdor’s sunlit wastes to continue your studies.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you see warlock factions maintain a hidden network between Lordaeron and Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","enchanted gold bloodrobe","kaal soulreaper","menara voidrender","ratchet","strahad's tower","undercity","warlock"},rel={"npc:menara-voidrender","npc:kaal-soulreaper","quest:1796","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Kaal Soulreaper",["end"]="Menara Voidrender",level="31",faction="Horde",id=4739},src={"In Search of Menara Voidrender (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:5041"] = {t="quest",n="Supplies for the Crossroads",z="barrens",s="Thork needs supplies back at the Crossroads after Razormane quilboar raids. The stolen crates hold provisions the outpost needs amid conflict across the Barrens.",h="Thork needs supplies back at the Crossroads after Razormane quilboar raids.",sec={{t="A Lifeline Under Siege",b="Thork needs provisions restored to the Crossroads after a supply caravan is ambushed. The outpost links Horde travel, trade, and defense across the Barrens, and cargo arrives from Durotar and Mulgore. Without it, shortages of provisions, tools, and arms threaten daily life in the harsh wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Thieving Quilboar",b="Razormane quilboar have taken the crates. These swine-beasts contest Horde control across central Kalimdor. They hauled the cargo to their thorn-bush camps and keep it there. Thork sends trusted warriors into Razormane territory to recover the supplies for the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Thork, the Horde officer overseeing the Crossroads' defense and operations, gives the request.",al={"quest giver","thork quest","who starts supplies for the crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="Why were the supplies stolen in the first place?",a="Razormane quilboar ambushed a supply caravan headed toward the Crossroads and hauled the crates to their nearby camps.",al={"caravan raid","why stolen","what happened to the supplies"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can the stolen crates be found?",a="Crossroads Supply Crates lie scattered on the ground throughout Razormane camps east and northeast of the Crossroads.",al={"crate locations","where are supplies","find crates"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is recovering these supplies so important to Thork?",a="Thork needs the supplies to keep the Crossroads operating and secure. Lost caravans leave soldiers and travelers without necessities at this isolated outpost.",al={"why care","crossroads importance","importance of supplies"},it="motive"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="This follows 'Disrupt the Attacks', in which adventurers struck at Razormane forces to weaken their attacks on Horde travel routes.",al={"prerequisite","prev quest","disrupt the attacks"},it="history"},{q="Who are the Razormane?",a="The Razormane are a fierce, territorial tribe of quilboar native to the Barrens. They raid caravans and contest the Horde's presence on their ancestral lands.",al={"razormane quilboar","who are quilboar","razormane"},it="target"},{q="What are the Crossroads Supply Crates?",a="These crates contain vital provisions and materials intended for the Crossroads settlement, recently ransacked from a supply caravan by marauding Razormane quilboar. Positioned at the arid heart of the Barrens, the settlement relies heavily on these regular shipments to sustain its defenders and daily life.",al={"crossroads supply crates","what is in the supply crates","stolen crates thork"},it="item",add="1af261a6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, holding the Crossroads links the capitals in Durotar and Mulgore. Recovering ambushed freight keeps the frontier outpost supplied.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, protecting Horde supply lines from quilboar helps guard the new Horde's expanding settlements."},kw={"barrens","caravan","crates","crossroads","quilboar","razormane","supplies","thork"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","npc:thork","quest:871","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},m={start="Thork",level="14",faction="Horde",id=5041,ri={"Crossroads Supply Crates"}},src={"Supplies for the Crossroads (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5042"] = {t="quest",n="Agamaggan's Strength",z="barrens",s="In Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers Horde travelers Agamaggan's Strength in return for Blood Shards. The captive Razormane shaman draws on his people's reverence for the ancient boar demigod and his hatred of the rival Bristleback tribe.",h="In Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers Horde travelers Agamaggan's Strength in return for Blood Shards.",sec={{t="Power of the Great Boar",b="The quilboar honor Agamaggan, an ancient boar demigod whose spilled blood is said to have formed the red Blood Shards scattered across the Barrens. They treat the crystals as sacred, drawing on their power to strengthen their front-line fighters. Mangletooth, an elder Razormane shaman held captive in Camp Taurajo, offers this strength to Horde champions. He claims your foes will cower as they do before the Razormane's mightiest champions.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Shaman's Vengeance",b="Mangletooth offers his strength out of spite. The orcs and tauren captured and caged the old quilboar, whose Razormane tribe is at war with the rival Bristleback. Unable to break his chains and slaughter them himself, he trades Agamaggan's gifts for help against them. He rewards those who destroy Bristleback tribes and take the sacred Blood Shards from their lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Agamaggan's Strength grant?",a="Agamaggan's Strength grants enhanced physical prowess through the power of Blood Shards. It lends the recipient the brutal might of the Razormane's fiercest fighters.",al={"what does agamaggan's strength do","agamaggans strength buff","strength blessing barrens"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Who is Mangletooth?",a="Mangletooth is an imprisoned Razormane quilboar held in Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He hates the rival Bristleback and trades quilboar secrets and blessings for Blood Shards.",al={"who is mangletooth","caged quilboar taurajo","taurajo prisoner"},it="identity"},{q="What are Blood Shards?",a="Blood Shards are reddish, crystal-like minerals found across the Barrens. Quilboar tradition says they formed where the blood of their patron demigod, the Great Boar Agamaggan, fell during the ancient War of the Ancients.",al={"what are blood shards","blood shard lore","where do blood shards come from"},it="item"},{q="Why does Mangletooth help the Horde?",a="Mangletooth helps the Horde because he hates the rival Bristleback quilboar. Though caged at Camp Taurajo and abandoned by his own people, he grants Horde champions Agamaggan's blessings if they butcher his rivals and take their sacred Blood Shards.",al={"why is mangletooth helping us","mangletooth motives","why help horde"},it="motive"},{q="Can you receive this blessing more than once?",a="Yes. After you complete Mangletooth's introductory trial, he continues to weave Agamaggan's Strength and other boons when you bring him four more Blood Shards.",al={"is agamaggan's strength repeatable","repeatable blood shards","turn in more blood shards"},gp=true},{q="What is the difference between the Bristleback and Razormane tribes?",a="The Bristleback and Razormane are rival quilboar tribes competing for the Barrens. Mangletooth belongs to the Razormane, despises the Bristleback, and boasts that his tribe is stronger.",al={"bristleback vs razormane","quilboar tribes barrens","why does mangletooth hate bristleback"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you to collect Blood Shards instead of doing it himself?",a="Mangletooth cannot hunt for Blood Shards himself because he is trapped in a cage at Camp Taurajo. While he dreams of taking vengeance on the people who turned their backs on him, he remains a captive of the Horde. Since he cannot leave his prison, he relies on you to hunt down his enemies across the Barrens, gleefully offering the ancient blessings of his patron in return for every shard you harvest.",al={"why does mangletooth need me","why cant mangletooth get the shards","mangletooth why me"},it="why_me",add="3f27ba18"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can draw on the raw vigor Mangletooth channels from the boar-god for a physical edge in battle across Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Camp Taurajo's guards keep Mangletooth locked up, but Horde commanders exploit the old shaman's thirst for vengeance against hostile quilboar.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you help maintain Camp Taurajo and watch Mangletooth warily. Your shamans recognize Agamaggan as an ancient guardian spirit of the land, though quilboar zealotry has corrupted his memory."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","blood shards","bristleback","camp taurajo","mangletooth","quilboar","razormane"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","quest:5052","topic:agamaggan","zone:barrens","quest:5046","quest:5043","quest:5044","quest:889"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5042,ri={"Blood Shard"}},src={"Agamaggan's Strength"}}
E["quest:5043"] = {t="quest",n="Agamaggan's Agility",z="barrens",s="In Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers travelers a blood shard ritual. The captive quilboar channels the power of his ancient boar god, blessing those who bring him shards from the Barrens with swift movement and sure aim.",h="In Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers travelers a blood shard ritual.",sec={{t="The Power of Blood Shards",b="Crimson blood shards jut from the Barrens soil, especially near quilboar encampments and colossal brambles. Quilboar tradition says the crystals formed from Agamaggan's spilled blood. The Great Boar Ancient fell fighting the Burning Legion in the War of the Ancients. Even locked in a wooden cage at Camp Taurajo, the elder quilboar Mangletooth knows how to channel the stones' dormant divine power for anyone who brings them.",sp=0},{t="Blessing of the Boar Scouts",b="Quilboar hunters and scouts prize ruthless accuracy and blinding quickness in the scrublands. For four blood shards, Mangletooth calls on the fallen demi-god's latent energy, lending the petitioner the instincts and supple grace of his people's best stalkers. He grunts with disdain at outsiders, yet honors his pact and weaves Agamaggan's power into a temporary mantle of agility.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers Agamaggan's Agility?",a="Mangletooth, a Razormane quilboar, offers the ritual from a cage at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. Though the Horde keeps him captive, he bargains with travelers who bring him blood shards.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","where is mangletooth"},it="identity"},{q="What are blood shards?",a="Blood shards are crystalline stones found throughout the Barrens. They are gathered chiefly from slain quilboar and mineral outcrops near thorn thickets. Quilboar lore says they formed millennia ago when the blood of the Great Boar Ancient Agamaggan drenched the earth.",al={"blood shards lore","what is a blood shard","red crystals in barrens"},it="item"},{q="Why is a captive quilboar helping Horde members?",a="Mangletooth serves his god, Agamaggan, and seeks to survive. He snorts at non-quilboar, yet trades Agamaggan's blessings for blood shards, handling his deity's sacred essence from inside an enemy cage.",al={"why help us","mangletooth motives","why does mangletooth talk"},it="motive"},{q="Can you receive this blessing more than once?",a="Yes. You can receive the blessing again by bringing Mangletooth four fresh blood shards. He invokes the Great Boar's blessing anew each time.",al={"is this repeatable","can i redo this","repeatable buff"},gp=true},{q="Who was Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan was a colossal boar Ancient who walked Kalimdor in the ancient mythic era. During the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago, he fought and fell against the demons of the Burning Legion. His blood nourished the Barrens, giving rise to its impenetrable razor thorns and the quilboar race.",al={"who is agamaggan","boar god","great boar"},it="history"},{q="What other blessings does Mangletooth provide?",a="Mangletooth offers rites honoring other aspects of Agamaggan as well. For blood shards, he can bless you with greater physical strength, intellectual wisdom, faster running, or skin as thick as razorhide.",al={"other blood shard quests","other buffs","mangletooth rewards"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you to bring him blood shards?",a="Mangletooth cannot gather the shards himself because he is held captive inside Camp Taurajo by the Horde. Locked away in his cage, he depends on outsiders willing to strike down the quilboar wandering the Barrens, recover the sacred stones from their remains, and bring them back to his cell.",al={"why mangletooth needs me","why ask adventurer blood shards","why cant mangletooth get shards"},it="why_me",add="f192776b"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may hear Mangletooth scoff at the speed of non-quilboar rogues. His ritual lets you turn the beast's sacred speed against the tribes of the scrublands.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you value unerring aim and swift stalking, prized virtues for sharpshooters crossing Kalimdor's open expanses.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you respect the Ancients who died in the War of the Ancients. Bargaining with a caged quilboar in Taurajo may still feel uneasy.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Mangletooth kept at Camp Taurajo, where Horde forces tolerate his presence and blood shard bargains because the boar god's residual power aids their hard-fought campaign across the Barrens."},kw={"agamaggan","agility","barrens","blood shards","mangletooth","quilboar","taurajo"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","quest:5052","quest:5042","quest:5044","quest:5046","topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5043,ri={"Blood Shard"}},src={"Agamaggan's Agility"}}
E["quest:5044"] = {t="quest",n="Wisdom of Agamaggan",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth trades the wisdom of Agamaggan for blood shards. The captive quilboar offers Horde spellcasters a ritual drawn from the ancient boar god’s power.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth trades the wisdom of Agamaggan for blood shards.",sec={{t="Blood Shards and Ancient Power",b="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth is held prisoner by the Horde. The quilboar trades his people’s magical secrets for blood shards, crimson crystals said to have formed from Agamaggan’s spilled blood. The towering boar Demigod died in the War of the Ancients. Mangletooth says the geomancers and shaman of his tribes use the shards to channel divine power in their rituals.",sp=0},{t="Blessing of the Mind",b="Other shard offerings bring physical resilience or swiftness. Mangletooth’s Wisdom ritual instead sharpens intellect and arcane ability. For four blood shards, he calls on Agamaggan’s spirit to grant you cunning in your confrontations, then reminds you of your mortality.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan is an ancient boar Demigod who fought the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago. He fell in the Barrens, where his blood soaked the soil and gave rise to giant thorn vines and crystalline blood shards.",al={"agamaggan lore","who is the boar god","boar ancient"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Mangletooth willing to help the Horde?",a="Mangletooth is a captive quilboar held in a cage at Camp Taurajo. Though his tribe fiercely hates the Horde, he values blood shards and his own survival more than loyalty, and gives sacred tribal blessings in exchange for shards.",al={"why help mangletooth","mangletooth motive","captive quilboar"},it="motive"},{q="What are blood shards?",a="Blood shards are red mineral formations found throughout quilboar lands in the Barrens. Quilboar legend says the crystals formed from drops of blood shed by Agamaggan as he died.",al={"blood shard lore","what are blood shards","red shards barrens"},it="item"},{q="Can I repeat this ritual more than once?",a="Yes. After you first show Mangletooth blood shards and earn his trust, he accepts four at a time whenever you want to renew the blessing.",al={"is wisdom of agamaggan repeatable","repeatable blood shards","turn in again"},gp=true},{q="Do quilboar shaman worship other deities?",a="Quilboar revere Agamaggan above all others and believe they descend directly from him. Their shamans and geomancers draw nature magic and power over the earth from his legacy and remnants.",al={"quilboar religion","geomancer gods","quilboar worship"},it="people"},{q="Where does Mangletooth suggest our next meeting might be?",a="After the ritual, Mangletooth asks you to share tales of your cunning the next time you meet, whether in this life or the next. His words acknowledge the ceaseless bloodshed across the Barrens.",al={"mangletooth next life","mangletooth dialogue"}},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you to bring him blood shards?",a="Mangletooth is held captive in a cage inside Camp Taurajo under the watchful eyes of the Horde. Unable to roam the Barrens to collect blood shards himself, he trades his knowledge of quilboar geomancy and the ancient blessings of the Great Boar in exchange for shards gathered by travelers passing through the camp.",al={"why does mangletooth need me","why bring blood shards to mangletooth","why can't mangletooth get blood shards"},it="why_me",add="daf5c556"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="At Camp Taurajo, the Horde keeps Mangletooth captive, giving you a chance to draw on native Barrens magic against the quilboar tribes.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can recognize how Agamaggan’s essence channels primal geomantic power into raw intellect.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may find the link between Agamaggan’s divine blood and rituals that fortify the mind an intriguing part of primal worship.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may recognize how quilboar geomancy echoes elemental callings, while the boar god’s shard rituals remain uniquely wild."},kw={"barrens","blood shards","boar god","camp taurajo","geomancer","mangletooth","quilboar","wisdom of agamaggan"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","quest:5052","quest:5042","quest:5043","quest:5045","quest:5046"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5044,ri={"Blood Shard"}},src={"Wisdom of Agamaggan"}}
E["quest:5045"] = {t="quest",n="Rising Spirit",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers a ritual blessing drawn from Agamaggan's ancient power. Bring blood shards taken from his Bristleback rivals, and he strengthens your will and spirit.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers a ritual blessing drawn from Agamaggan's ancient power.",sec={{t="Willpower of the Razormane",b="Held in a cage at Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth knows the geomancy and ancestral magic of the quilboar. He takes pride in his people's devotion to their creator, the Great Boar Agamaggan. To Mangletooth, an unbroken spirit carries a warrior onward when strength fails and defeat seems near.",sp=0},{t="The Power of Blood Shards",b="Mangletooth asks for blood shards to raise your spirit. These crystals hold Agamaggan's ancient blood, which seeped into the red earth ten thousand years ago. Bring him shards gathered across the Barrens, especially from his Bristleback enemies, and he can channel their power into a blessing that bolsters your will.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mangletooth?",a="Mangletooth is an elder Razormane quilboar held in a wooden cage at Camp Taurajo. Though the Horde keeps him captive, he shares sacred geomantic rites for blood shards and uses travelers to strike at the rival Bristlebacks.",al={"mangletooth lore","who is the caged boar","taurajo prisoner"},it="identity"},{q="What are blood shards?",a="Blood shards are red mineral crystals formed from the blood of Agamaggan, an Ancient Demigod who died in the Barrens during the War of the Ancients. Quilboar shamans and geomancers draw on their lingering magic for boons and rituals.",al={"what are blood shards","blood shard lore","agamaggan blood"},it="item"},{q="Why does Mangletooth help Horde adventurers?",a="Mangletooth hates the rival Bristleback quilboar. He trades blessings for blood shards to spur powerful travelers to kill Bristlebacks across the Barrens, carrying on his tribe's feud from behind the cage.",al={"why does mangletooth help","why is quilboar helping horde"},it="motive"},{q="What does the Rising Spirit blessing do?",a="The Rising Spirit blessing from Mangletooth strengthens a warrior's spirit and resolve. It draws on Agamaggan's enduring life force to keep hope alive through hard encounters.",al={"rising spirit buff","what is rising spirit"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan is the colossal Boar Ancient who fought the Burning Legion ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients. The quilboar revere him as their creator and believe the Barrens' thorny brambles and red blood shards grew from his fallen body.",al={"agamaggan","the great boar"},it="history"},{q="Is this ritual a one-time trade?",a="No. Bring Mangletooth four blood shards, and he will perform the ritual again to renew your blessing before you venture into the wastes.",al={"repeat rising spirit","is rising spirit repeatable"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you instead of gathering shards himself?",a="Mangletooth is a captive of the Horde, held securely in a cage at Camp Taurajo. Unable to wander the plains or battle his quilboar rivals himself, he must rely on passing adventurers to bring him the sacred blood shards he requires to perform his ancestral rituals.",al={"why mangletooth needs me","why cant mangletooth get shards","why ask me"},it="why_me",add="21d8d0f0"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may recognize the quilboar's communion with Agamaggan as a raw expression of faith and spirit, rivaling the organized devotions of eastern churches.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you understand how ancient bloodlines and earth minerals can bind the spirits of the land to a mortal warrior.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde wanderer in the Barrens, you can turn Mangletooth's hatred of the Bristlebacks into a tactical advantage."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","blood shards","bristleback","camp taurajo","mangletooth","razormane","rising spirit"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","topic:agamaggan","quest:5052","zone:barrens","quest:5042","quest:5043","quest:5046","quest:889"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5045,ri={"Blood Shard"}},src={"Rising Spirit"}}
E["quest:5046"] = {t="quest",n="Razorhide",z="barrens",s="In Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers Razorhide to those who bring him blood shards. The captive quilboar trades Agamaggan’s life essence for a blessing that hardens the skin before battle.",h="In Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers Razorhide to those who bring him blood shards.",sec={{t="Blessings of the Boar God",b="The quilboar trace their power to Agamaggan, the Great Boar who died fighting the Burning Legion thousands of years ago. His blood sank into the Barrens and hardened into crystalline shards, still alive with ancient power. The Horde and quilboar remain sworn enemies, yet Mangletooth, held in a cage at Camp Taurajo, will share sacred knowledge for these fragments.",sp=0},{t="Hardening the Hide",b="Quilboar are born with thick hides and protective quills, but their warriors call on Agamaggan to harden their skin against blades and claws. Mangletooth can perform the rite for outsiders, channeling four blood shards to strengthen their defenses and help keep their bones unbroken in the wilds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the Razorhide ritual?",a="Mangletooth, an imprisoned quilboar in a wooden cage at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, offers the Razorhide ritual. Once you show you know how to handle blood shards, he trades blessings for more.",al={"who gives razorhide","mangletooth quest","who starts razorhide"},it="identity"},{q="What are blood shards?",a="Blood shards are crystals found across the Barrens. Quilboar believe they formed from Agamaggan’s spilled blood during the War of the Ancients and still hold great primal magic.",al={"what are blood shards","blood shard lore","blood of agamaggan"},it="origin"},{q="Why is an imprisoned quilboar helping Horde travelers?",a="Mangletooth is held captive by the tauren at Camp Taurajo. He keeps his rough manner and loyalty to Agamaggan, but his hunger for blood shards leads him to teach outsiders quilboar rites.",al={"why does mangletooth help","why is mangletooth in taurajo","friendly quilboar"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of protection does Razorhide represent?",a="Razorhide is a quilboar warding called upon before battle. It hardens the skin and strengthens the bones with Agamaggan’s supernatural endurance.",al={"what does razorhide do","razorhide lore","protective blessing"},it="power"},{q="Can you receive Razorhide more than once?",a="Yes. Mangletooth can invoke Razorhide again whenever you bring him four blood shards.",al={"is razorhide repeatable","repeat razorhide","how many times can i do razorhide"},gp=true},{q="Where can blood shards be found?",a="Blood shards can be scavenged from geomancers, hunters, and warriors in quilboar encampments, brambles, and crags throughout the Barrens.",al={"blood shard locations","where to get blood shards","farm blood shards"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Mangletooth use the Blood Shards for?",a="Blood shards hold the crystallized power and lifeblood of the quilboar ancestor, the Great Boar Agamaggan. Mangletooth channels the residual divine energy trapped inside four of these stones to invoke the god's favor, hardening your flesh and granting you the supernatural resilience quilboar warriors rely on before marching to battle.",al={"what are blood shards used for","why blood shard razorhide","blood shard purpose razorhide"},it="item",add="f8770fb0"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the hunters of Camp Taurajo watch Mangletooth’s cage closely. Quilboar rites touch sacred Earthmother ground, but their feral practitioners rarely share secrets without a price.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you benefit from magical armor and a hardened hide when you enter the dangerous thorn thickets of the southern Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Camp Taurajo holding ground against quilboar encroachment. Mangletooth’s reverence for Agamaggan gives travelers a way to draw on his rites."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","blood shards","camp taurajo","mangletooth","quilboar","razorhide"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","topic:agamaggan","quest:5052","quest:5042","quest:5043","quest:5044","quest:5045","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5046,ri={"Blood Shard"}},src={"Razorhide"}}
E["quest:5052"] = {t="quest",n="Blood Shards of Agamaggan",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, blood shards carry the power of the fallen boar god Agamaggan. Quilboar say his blood sank into the earth and hardened into red stones. At Camp Taurajo, the captive Mangletooth trades their power to the Horde for his own reasons.",h="Across the Barrens, blood shards carry the power of the fallen boar god Agamaggan.",sec={{t="The Boar God's Legacy",b="Quilboar lore tells how Agamaggan fell ten thousand years ago in the War of the Ancients. His blood raised giant thorn mazes across the plains, then sank beneath the soil and seeped into minerals. In time, it hardened into blood-red stones. The quilboar honor the shards as sacred remnants of their creator. They gather them from mineral seams and holy grounds, then use them as totems for battle and sorcery.",sp=0},{t="Spite from a Wooden Cage",b="Mangletooth is held in a cage at Camp Taurajo by the tauren. He bears a bitter grudge against his own kind, saying his tribe betrayed and cast him out. Without freedom or the magic of his people, he bargains with adventurers for blood shards. Their power lets him reach Agamaggan's magic despite his captivity and channel it to Horde champions. He takes pleasure in turning that power against the quilboar who rejected him.",sp=0},{t="Razorfen's Sacred Roots",b="Mangletooth speaks with reverence of Razorfen, the quilboar's holiest sanctuary to the south. The tribes say the vast briars of Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs grew from Agamaggan's colossal skeleton and tusks. They believe Razorfen Downs lies within the demigod's gaping maw, a holy threshold that devours and crushes any who enter without the Boar God's favor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are blood shards?",a="Blood shards are red stones formed when Agamaggan's blood soaked into the earth during the War of the Ancients. They hold remnants of divine quilboar magic and can be found in mineral veins or carried by quilboar as totems.",al={"what is a blood shard","blood shard lore","where do blood shards come from"},it="item"},{q="Why is Mangletooth willing to help the Horde?",a="Mangletooth is captive at Camp Taurajo, and says his own people turned their backs on him. Bitter over his exile and cut off from his people's sacred power, he offers to empower Horde adventurers against the quilboar who spurned him.",al={"why does mangletooth help","is mangletooth friendly","why help captive quilboar"},it="motive"},{q="What buffs does Mangletooth provide?",a="Mangletooth trades blood shards for temporary primal boons in Agamaggan's honor. They can enhance agility, strength, intellect, spirit, armor, and swift movement across the Barrens.",al={"blood shard buffs","what do i get for blood shards","mangletooth boons"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Where is Razorfen, and what is its significance?",a="Razorfen lies in the southernmost Barrens. Quilboar revere it as their holiest site, believing its towering briars grew from Agamaggan's fallen body and Razorfen Downs is the demigod's colossal maw.",al={"what is razorfen","why is razorfen holy","razorfen downs lore"},it="place"},{q="Who was Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan was an Ancient Guardian, a titanic boar god who died fighting the Burning Legion ten thousand years ago. His spilled blood raised the Barrens' massive razor-sharp brambles and gave the quilboar their birth and mystical strength.",al={"who is agamaggan","boar god","quilboar god"},it="origin"},{q="Can miners find blood shards in the Barrens?",a="Yes. Agamaggan's blood infused the Barrens' rocks and minerals, so miners sometimes find blood shards alongside ordinary tin and copper ore.",al={"mining blood shards","can i mine blood shards","ore blood shards"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you to collect blood shards for him?",a="Mangletooth sits locked inside a cage in Camp Taurajo, kept under close watch by the Horde. Having been severed from his sacred relics and his people, he is physically powerless to venture out into the Barrens and gather the shards himself. By enlisting you, he regains access to the stones of Agamaggan's power while turning an outside champion against the very tribes that betrayed him.",al={"why me mangletooth","why can't mangletooth get shards","why does mangletooth need help"},it="why_me",add="2869bf9b"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Across the Barrens, miners can find blood shards embedded alongside tin and copper ore, drawing the crystallized blood of an Ancient Guardian from the veins.",["race:Tauren"]="The tauren see the quilboar as aggressive rivals over the plains' dwindling water and game. Still, Agamaggan's sacrifice in the ancient war commands their spiritual respect.",["faction:Horde"]="To secure Camp Taurajo, the Horde must suppress the aggressive Bristleback and Razorfen tribes. A caged quilboar's spite can turn their demigod's strength against them.",["class:Shaman"]="Blood shards hold raw, primordial earth and spirit magic. For a shaman, they speak to the deep shaping of Kalimdor by titan-forged and primal spirits."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","blood shard","bristleback","camp taurajo","mangletooth","quilboar","razorfen"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:razorfen","quest:878","zone:barrens","quest:889"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="21",faction="Horde",id=5052},src={"Blood Shards of Agamaggan"}}
E["quest:6127"] = {t="quest",n="The Principal Source",z="barrens",s="Dendrite Starblaze sends Horde druids to Dreadmist Peak for a water sample. From Moonglade, she asks them to bring it to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads, where it can help explain the poison harming wildlife.",h="Dendrite Starblaze sends Horde druids to Dreadmist Peak for a water sample.",sec={{t="A Mountain Tainted",b="Dreadmist Peak rises northwest of the Crossroads, with springs and pools high above the dry northern Barrens. Their waters shape local weather and moisture. The Burning Blade, a cult devoted to demons, has taken hold on the crags. Dendrite Starblaze fears their foul sorcery may taint the basin around this important mountain.",sp=0},{t="A Plague on the Plains",b="Sick gazelles stumble across the northern savanna, north of the main east-west trail through the Crossroads. Tonga Runetotem seeks help for the local tauren and turns to the Cenarion Circle to learn what is poisoning the herd. Druids who reach the peak and bring back a sample of its tainted water give Tonga what he needs to study the sickness and brew an antidote.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I get the water sample for this quest?",a="Draw water from the pool at the summit of Dreadmist Peak, northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. The Burning Blade gathers there, and Dendrite Starblaze provides a sampler for the water.",al={"dreadmist peak pool location","where is the water pool","principal source water sample"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the water on Dreadmist Peak so important to the Barrens?",a="Dreadmist Peak's high pools influence the local weather and mist. When the Burning Blade fouls them, poisoned vapor and runoff spread across the plains below and sicken wildlife in the northern Barrens.",al={"why dreadmist peak matters","barrens weather pool","dreadmist peak pools"},it="place"},{q="Who is Tonga Runetotem?",a="Tonga Runetotem is a tauren druid at the Crossroads in the Barrens. Alarmed by the strange sickness afflicting local gazelles, he asked the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade to help diagnose and cleanse the land.",al={"who is tonga","tonga runetotem role","crossroads druid"},it="identity"},{q="Who is corrupting the water on the peak?",a="The Burning Blade has corrupted the waters. Its demon-worshiping warlocks and fel practitioners occupy the winding paths and summit of Dreadmist Peak.",al={"who tainted the pool","dreadmist cultists","burning blade dreadmist"},it="threat"},{q="What ability does completing this chain teach?",a="The rite of Power over Poison teaches young Horde druids the spiritual and herbal knowledge needed to cure poisons in the field.",al={"power over poison reward","druid poison cure spell","cure poison quest barrens"},gp=true},{q="Can Alliance druids do this quest?",a="No. The Principal Source is the Horde trial, sending druids to the Barrens to help Tonga Runetotem. Alliance druids make a similar journey in Darkshore to learn to cleanse poisons.",al={"alliance equivalent","can night elves do principal source","alliance poison quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze want this done?",a="Tonga Runetotem reached out to the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade seeking aid to halt a spreading malady in the Barrens. Dendrite Starblaze suspects that the demon-worshipping Burning Blade has poisoned the pools atop Dreadmist Peak. Because these high waters influence the region's weather patterns, their corruption threatens the delicate balance of the entire northern Barrens ecosystem.",al={"why does dendrite need this","dendrite starblaze motive","why investigate the water"},it="motive",add="41ffa32f"},{q="What is the Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler for?",a="The filled sampler holds tainted water taken directly from the peak's highest pool. Tonga Runetotem needs this foul specimen at the Crossroads to analyze the foul toxins infecting the local wildlife, allowing him and the Cenarion Circle to study the pollution and brew an effective cure for the stricken gazelles.",al={"filled dreadmist peak sampler use","what is the water sample for","sampler purpose"},it="item",add="54ce2e01"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze send you instead of going himself?",a="As an elder of the Cenarion Circle residing in sacred Moonglade, Dendrite oversees many matters and relies on promising young druids to serve as the Circle's hands across Kalimdor. Answering Tonga's plea provides an essential lesson in cleansing corruption and mastering natural remedies, testing your ability to heal the land.",al={"why send me","why doesn't dendrite go","why a druid student"},it="why_me",add="2b67a7e4"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you trace corruption to its source and isolate magical toxins before they can ruin an ecosystem.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you help protect the gazelle herds of the Barrens, ancestral lands of Kalimdor's tribes, from demonic taint.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help guard the Crossroads, a vital center of Horde life in Kalimdor, from demonic blight that threatens trade and survival."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","crossroads","dendrite starblaze","dreadmist peak","power over poison","principal source","sickly gazelle","tonga runetotem"},rel={"quest:6125","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:dreadmist-peak","subzone:crossroads","topic:cenarion-circle","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Tonga Runetotem",level="14",faction="Horde",id=6127,ri={"Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler"}},src={"The Principal Source (Horde)"}}
E["quest:6128"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering the Cure",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, young tauren druids face a sacred passage under Tonga Runetotem's guidance. You gather earthroot and sturdy kodo horns to make a salve for the poisoned gazelles of the Barrens.",h="At the Crossroads, young tauren druids face a sacred passage under Tonga Runetotem's guidance.",sec={{t="A Recipe for Relief",b="Tonga Runetotem needs raw ingredients to brew an antidote from the water sample you secured at Dreadmist Peak. Natural water forms the salve's base, earthroot supplies its medicinal qualities, and ground kodo horn gives it the strength to drive venom from a creature's system. For a young druid, gathering them means relying on the gifts of the earth and hunting local beasts.",sp=0},{t="Lessons in Cleansing",b="Tonga Runetotem uses the salve's preparation to teach the limits of physical medicine. Herbal lore and alchemy can counter specific toxins, but each poison usually needs its own cure. Rather than carry endless herbs and horns, druids learn to attune to nature's healing energies. That lesson leads to the druidic art of Cure Poison.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What ingredients does Tonga Runetotem require?",a="Tonga asks for five bundles of earthroot and five intact kodo horns. Earthroot brings healing properties, while the horns give the salve potency against the toxins harming local gazelles.",al={"gathering the cure items","what reagents do i need","cure materials"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where can the kodo horns be found?",a="Kodos roam the northern and central Barrens, often grazing near roads around the Crossroads. Tonga needs whole, sturdy horns for the salve, not brittle chips.",al={"where are the kodos","kodo horn location","finding kodos in the barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do I have to be an herbalist to obtain earthroot?",a="No, you do not need herbalism to get earthroot. Herbalists harvest it from cliffs and rocky outcroppings across the Barrens, and druids who cannot gather it themselves can obtain it from fellow travelers or trading posts.",al={"do i need herbalism","gathering earthroot without herbalism","earthroot profession requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why is Tonga preparing a physical salve?",a="Tonga is making a physical antidote for the poisoned gazelles suffering across the northern Barrens. The careful work also shows the advantage of learning innate magical purification spells.",al={"why make an antidote","purpose of the salve","why not use magic"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Tonga Runetotem?",a="Tonga Runetotem is an elder tauren druid at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He investigates corruption spreading through the region's waterways and guides young druids in mastering nature's balance.",al={"who gives gathering the cure","tonga runetotem role","who is tonga"},it="identity"},{q="What comes after gathering these ingredients?",a="After Tonga brews the salve, he sends you into the savannah to apply it to afflicted gazelles and test the remedy. Then he teaches the deeper art of magical purification.",al={"what follows gathering the cure","gathering the cure next quest","after gathering the cure"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem want to gather these cure ingredients?",a="Tonga is striving to save the native gazelle population of the Barrens, which is succumbing to a dangerous affliction. The wildlife cannot recover on their own, threatening the natural balance of the plains. By combining the water sampled from Dreadmist Peak with potent restorative reagents, Tonga intends to brew a curative salve capable of halting the sickness before more herds perish.",al={"why help tonga runetotem","tonga runetotem motive","why make the salve"},it="motive",add="239606af"},{q="What is the Earthroot used for?",a="Earthroot provides the essential healing properties for the salve. Tonga utilizes the resilient herb's natural vitality to infuse the salve's water base with the strength needed to soothe the stricken gazelles and fight off the debilitating poison.",al={"why need earthroot","earthroot purpose","earthroot salve"},it="item",add="eb557efc"},{q="What are the Kodo Horns used for?",a="Tonga requires sturdy kodo horns to give the curative salve sufficient potency. Ground into the mixture, whole and intact horns grant the medicine the strength needed to counteract aggressive toxins effectively.",al={"why need kodo horns","kodo horn purpose","kodo horn salve"},it="item",add="9baa8a2a"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you face trials that teach you to move beyond mortal herbcraft and channel nature's magic to purge venom directly.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you know the value of gathering wild medicinal roots from the rocky hillsides of the savannah.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help Tonga protect the wildlife around the Crossroads and preserve a stable ecosystem for the Horde's heartland outpost."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","druid quest","earthroot","gathering the cure","gazelle","kodo horn","salve","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","quest:6125","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",level="14",faction="Horde",id=6128,ri={"Earthroot","Kodo Horn"}},src={"Gathering the Cure (Horde)"}}
E["quest:6129"] = {t="quest",n="Curing the Sick",z="barrens",s="Curing the Sick is an essential trial for young Horde druids, tasking them with healing afflicted wildlife in the northern Barrens. By applying a freshly concocted herbal salve to ailing gazelles, initiates demonstrate both their practical field medicine and their commitment to preserving natural balance. Completing this duty proves their dedication directly to the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade.",h="Curing the Sick is an essential trial for young Horde druids, tasking them with healing afflicted wildlife in...",sec={{t="A Plague upon the Herds",b="Across the northern savanna of the Barrens, grazing gazelles have begun succumbing to an unnatural affliction. After gathering earthroot and kodo horns to assemble a curative remedy, Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads entrusts a young druid with administering the field treatment. The initiate must search north of the main crossroads to find and minister to ten suffering animals, providing immediate relief before the rot takes further root in the ecosystem.",sp=0},{t="The Circle's Blessing",b="Once the salve is dispensed, the druid's path leads back into the tranquil boughs of Moonglade. There, Dendrite Starblaze recognizes the initiate's compassion and vigilance. He notes that the suffering of the gazelles is merely a symptom of a deeper, insidious corruption stalking Kalimdor's wilderness. By tending to the lowliest beasts, tauren druids demonstrate that reverence for Cenarius transcends tribal boundaries, earning deeper secrets of poison cleansing and nature magic.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the sickly gazelles found?",a="The afflicted gazelles roam the arid plains of the northern Barrens, primarily found north of the main east-west trade road that intersects at the Crossroads.",al={"gazelle location","where are sick gazelles","barrens gazelles"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Tonga Runetotem, a tauren druid stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens, provides the quest and supplies the Curative Animal Salve after you complete his reagent-gathering task.",al={"who gives curing the sick","quest giver","tonga runetotem location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who do I report to after curing the animals?",a="You turn the quest in to Dendrite Starblaze in the druidic sanctuary of Moonglade, using your teleportation magic to reach the sacred grove.",al={"where do i turn this in","quest turn in","dendrite starblaze location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is the Cenarion Circle interested in the Barrens?",a="The Cenarion Circle watches over the land's harmony. The sickness spreading among wild gazelles reflects a pervasive corruption creeping through Kalimdor, threatening to destabilize the natural order if left unchecked.",al={"why druids care about barrens","cenarion circle barrens"},it="purpose"},{q="What ability does this quest chain unlock?",a="This trial forms the second half of the druidic rite of passage that ultimately rewards the initiate with the ability to cleanse venoms and toxins from themselves and their allies.",al={"cure poison quest reward","why do this quest druid"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Can non-druids cure these gazelles?",a="No. This quest line is exclusive to druids, serving as a dedicated class trial supervised directly by the Cenarion Circle.",al={"is this druid only","who can do curing the sick"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem want you to cure the gazelles?",a="A spreading corruption is blighting the wildlife across the northern Barrens, leaving the local gazelles afflicted with a debilitating sickness. Tonga Runetotem has prepared a curative salve to counteract the malaise, but nature cannot wait. He needs you to deliver immediate relief to the suffering animals and stem the taint before it takes a deeper toll on the land's fragile balance.",al={"why cure gazelles","tonga runetotem motive","why help sick gazelles"},it="motive",add="f2ed6f7d"},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem need you instead of curing the gazelles himself?",a="Tonga has only managed to craft enough salve for ten doses and must remain behind at the Crossroads to coordinate with local authorities to prepare more. As an aspiring druid walking the path of Cenarius, you have the bond with nature required to track down the scattered, ailing creatures and administer the remedy without causing them further distress.",al={"why me tonga runetotem","why does tonga need help","why not local guards"},it="why_me",add="f6349169"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This rite of healing marks your transition from a student of herbalism into an active guardian of nature, proving your readiness to wield life magic against lethal poisons.",["race:Tauren"]="As your people rekindle ancient ties to the Cenarion Circle, healing the Barrens proves that the Earth Mother's children are worthy stewards of the balance.",["faction:Horde"]="By treating afflicted wildlife near the Crossroads, tauren druids help protect the essential hunting grounds and travel corridors that support the Horde's foothold in central Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","crossroads","curative animal salve","cure poison","curing the sick","dendrite starblaze","moonglade","sickly gazelle","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:6125","quest:5921","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",["end"]="Dendrite Starblaze",level="14",faction="Horde",id=6129,ri={"Sickly Gazelle"}},src={"Curing the Sick (Horde)"}}
E["quest:63"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="barrens",s="Across the sea, Call of Water carries Barrens shamans to Silverpine Forest. There, an initiate faces the blight on an ancient coastal shrine to earn communion with water spirits.",h="Across the sea, Call of Water carries Barrens shamans to Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Pilgrimage Across the Sea",b="After gathering drops of pure water with help from the hermit Brine, you return to Islen Waterseer on the Barrens coast. She sends you across the sea with the purified essence to Silverpine Forest's haunted shore, just west of the Forsaken refuge called the Sepulcher.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Everfount",b="The Brazier of Everfount is an ancient focus for the elements, but Lordaeron's plague has twisted its waters. The spirits there have fallen silent and turned feral. Defeat the corrupted manifestation bound to the brazier, then offer its bracers and the purest water to the flame. The blight breaks, and an untainted spirit of the tides appears, ready to grant its blessing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does a shaman have to travel all the way to Silverpine Forest?",a="Islen Waterseer sends you to face corruption, not merely study peace. The coastal shrine west of the Sepulcher has been tainted by Lordaeron's plague. Healing it may awaken the water spirits, who refuse to speak to anyone else.",al={"why go to silverpine","why travel across sea","why silverpine water quest"},it="place"},{q="What happens when you use the Brazier of Everfount?",a="Place the defeated elemental's bracers and the remaining purest water on the flame. Islen taught this cleansing ritual, which purges the pool and summons a pure spirit of water willing to grant its blessing.",al={"brazier of everfount event","what does the brazier do","how to cleanse the pool"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is corrupting the water shrine in Silverpine?",a="Lordaeron's lingering plague has twisted the shrine's water. Corruption seeps down from the hills, tainting the spring and turning its native water spirits feral and hostile.",al={"who corrupted the shrine","why is the manifestation corrupted","silverpine water corruption"},it="threat"},{q="What do you receive after completing this trial?",a="Cleansing the Brazier of Everfount lets you commune with a pure spirit of water, willing to grant its blessing. Bring proof of the cleansing to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens to earn your Water Totem and finish the long trial.",al={"call of water reward","water totem unlock","what do i get"},it="next_step"},{q="Where exactly is the shrine located?",a="The shrine stands on Silverpine Forest's western coast, over the blighted ridge just west of the Sepulcher.",al={"brazier of everfount location","where is the shrine","silverpine shrine coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Islen Waterseer?",a="Islen Waterseer is a tauren shaman who lives along the Merchant Coast of the Barrens, south of Ratchet. A revered spiritual guide, she instructs young Horde shamans in the difficult rites that attune them to water.",al={"who is islen","islen waterseer background","barrens water trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Islen Waterseer want this done?",a="Islen Waterseer seeks to restore balance to the elements and expand your connection to the water spirits. The shrine in Silverpine Forest has succumbed to the plague, severing communion with the spirits of the region. By purifying this site, you aid the troubled elementals and prove your worth as a shaman capable of earning your Water Totem.",al={"islen waterseer motive","why cleanse the water shrine","why does islen send you to silverpine"},it="motive",add="43e73964"},{q="What are the Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers for?",a="The bracers serve as a physical tether to the fallen elemental. When placed upon the Brazier of Everfount alongside Brine's purest water, they allow the cleansing ritual to take hold, purging the corruption and coaxing a pure water spirit forth so you may commune with it.",al={"corrupt manifestation bracers use","what to do with bracers","brazier bracers"},it="item",add="4cf42c2b"},{q="What is the Corrupt Manifestation of Water?",a="It is an elemental spirit twisted and sickened by the plague seeping into Silverpine Forest's waterways. Hostile and in agony, it guards the blighted shrine, unable to find peace or commune with shamans until its corrupted physical form is defeated.",al={"corrupt manifestation of water","what are you fighting silverpine","corrupt water elemental"},it="target",add="585e30b0"},{q="Why must you perform this cleansing instead of someone else?",a="This journey is an essential trial of your shamanic path. Common guards cannot commune with the elements or survive spiritual trials, and Islen must remain to guide other initiates. A shaman must face the elemental's wrath and restore balance personally to forge an unbreakable bond with water.",al={"why do i have to cleanse the shrine","why not send guards silverpine water","why must the player go"},it="why_me",add="35c6941a"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you learn that your calling reaches beyond storms: you can heal broken lands and purge spiritual blight.",["faction:Horde"]="As an orc or tauren, you travel from Kalimdor into Silverpine Forest and witness firsthand the grim, plague-ridden hardships your Forsaken allies face."},kw={"brazier of everfount","brine","call of water","corrupt manifestation","islen waterseer","sepulcher","silverpine forest","water totem"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","npc:brine","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","zone:barrens"},m={start="Islen Waterseer",["end"]="Brazier of Everfount",level="23",faction="Horde",id=63,ri={"Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers"}},src={"Call of Water (7)"}}
E["quest:6361"] = {t="quest",n="A Bundle of Hides",z="barrens",s="Jahan Hawkwing sends cured hides from the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff for leatherworking. The delivery takes you across central Kalimdor and introduces the Crossroads wind rider roost.",h="Jahan Hawkwing sends cured hides from the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff for leatherworking.",sec={{t="Trade Across the Savanna",b="Hunters bring game hides and meat to the Crossroads, where Jahan Hawkwing gathers pelts from across the Barrens. The outposts cannot process every raw hide, so he asks travelers to carry them west to Thunder Bluff. Master leatherworkers there can turn the pelts into gear for the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Taking to the Skies",b="The trail across the Barrens and into Mulgore is rough, and quilboar and predators threaten anyone carrying cargo on foot. Jahan sends you to Devrak, the Crossroads wind rider master. He can take the goods by air aboard a trained wyvern, linking the Horde’s scattered settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Bundle of Hides?",a="Jahan Hawkwing, a tauren at the Crossroads in the Barrens, gives you the hides to carry. He has gathered pelts from local beasts and needs a reliable courier to take them toward Thunder Bluff.",al={"quest giver","who starts a bundle of hides","where to get bundle of hides"},gp=true},{q="Who should I bring the bundle of hides to?",a="Bring the bundle to Devrak, the orc wind rider master at the Crossroads perch. He handles air travel between the Crossroads and other major Horde hubs.",al={"turn in npc","where to take hides","who do i talk to"},gp=true},{q="What happens after giving the hides to Devrak?",a="After you give Devrak the hides, he asks you to take a wind rider and fly the cargo to Ahanu, the leatherworker atop Thunder Bluff’s high bluffs.",al={"next quest","what after a bundle of hides","follow up quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are these hides being sent to Thunder Bluff?",a="Jahan Hawkwing works with Ahanu in Thunder Bluff, who turns pelts from Barrens game into leather armor and goods for the tauren and their Horde allies.",al={"why thunder bluff","ahanu hides","what are hides for"},it="motive"},{q="Why use a wind rider instead of walking?",a="Walking across the Barrens and climbing Thunder Bluff’s great mesa takes time and risks danger from wildlife and quilboar packs. A wind rider carries you swiftly above them.",al={"why fly to thunder bluff","wind rider travel"}},{q="Does this require prior flight master experience?",a="You can learn to use the flight master system on this early delivery. Devrak’s roost shows you how wind riders connect distant regions.",al={"flight path requirement","do i need flight path"},gp=true},{q="Why does Jahan Hawkwing ask an adventurer to deliver the hides?",a="Jahan Hawkwing is stationed in the Crossroads to support the settlement's trade and crafts. Rather than abandoning his post to make the long journey across the plains to Mulgore himself, he relies on traveling adventurers to carry goods and connect local hunters with the artisans in Thunder Bluff.",al={"why ask me bundle of hides","why does jahan need me","why cant jahan hawkwing deliver the hides"},it="why_me",add="2d6b34f1"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren traveler, you carry hides between hunters in the ancestral Barrens and craftsmen on Thunder Bluff’s great mesas.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on links between Kalimdor’s bases. Orcish beast masters like Devrak help bridge the distance between allied territories."},kw={"ahanu","bundle of hides","crossroads","devrak","jahan hawkwing","leatherworking","the barrens","thunder bluff","wind rider"},rel={"npc:jahan-hawkwing","npc:devrak","npc:ahanu","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff","quest:4767"},m={start="Jahan Hawkwing",["end"]="Devrak",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6361},src={"A Bundle of Hides (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6365"] = {t="quest",n="Meats to Orgrimmar",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Zargh sends a parcel of Barrens meat toward Orgrimmar. He asks young orc and troll adventurers to carry it to Devrak, the wind rider master, and learn the flight route to the Horde capital.",h="At the Crossroads, Zargh sends a parcel of Barrens meat toward Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Fresh Game from the Barrens",b="Wildlife fills the Barrens, from zhevras and plainstriders to kodos and thunder lizards. Zargh has prepared choice cuts for a personal delivery to Gryshka, the innkeeper in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. Rather than risk the long, dusty trek across the Southfury River into Durotar, he sends runners from the Crossroads to the wind rider perch.",sp=0},{t="Wings Over the Steppes",b="Meeting Devrak gives a young Horde warrior a first look at the wind rider flight network. Wind rider masters connect remote outposts like the Crossroads to the Horde's fortified seat of power in Orgrimmar. Devrak prepares you and the cargo for a swift flight over the savannah.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zargh sending this meat to?",a="Zargh sends the meat to his friend Gryshka, the innkeeper of Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength.",al={"who gets the meat","who is the meat for","zargh meat recipient"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why can only Orcs and Trolls take this quest?",a="This flight introduction links orcs and Darkspear trolls to their shared capital, Orgrimmar. Tauren are directed to Thunder Bluff through A Bundle of Hides, while Forsaken are sent to Silverpine Forest through Supplying the Sepulcher.",al={"why cant tauren get this","undead meats quest","race restriction"},gp=true},{q="Who is Devrak?",a="Devrak is the orc wind rider master stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He oversees the wyverns that carry messages, supplies, and travelers throughout Kalimdor.",al={"devrak crossroads","who is devrak"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after giving the meat to Devrak?",a="Devrak accepts the shipment and arranges a wind rider flight that carries you and the meat to Orgrimmar's Skytower. You then deliver it to Gryshka at her inn through Ride to Orgrimmar.",al={"next quest after meats to orgrimmar","what does devrak do"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is Zargh located?",a="Zargh is at the Crossroads, the central Horde trading hub at the Barrens' main intersection.",al={"zargh location","where is zargh"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why use a wind rider instead of walking?",a="Wind riders carry travelers rapidly across the harsh Barrens and over the river canyon into Durotar, so delicate cargo like fresh meat can reach Orgrimmar before spoiling.",al={"why fly to orgrimmar","wind rider meat"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Zargh want the meat delivered?",a="Zargh has acquired some choice cuts of meat and simply wishes to send them as a gift to his friend Gryshka, the innkeeper at Orgrimmar's central inn. Because fresh meat quickly spoils under the harsh sun of the Barrens and Durotar, getting the cuts into skilled hands quickly matters to him.",al={"why send meat","zargh motive","why zargh sending cuts"},it="motive",add="50e2b3bf"},{q="Why does Zargh need you instead of delivering the meat himself?",a="Zargh has his own duties tending his post at the Crossroads and cannot simply abandon them to make the journey back across Durotar. Rather than leave his duties, he relies on promising Horde travelers heading toward the capital to deliver his parcels via the local wind rider network.",al={"why not zargh himself","why does zargh ask me","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="0b0a203b"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc leaving Durotar to hunt in the Barrens, you can deliver Zargh's parcel and establish an aerial route straight back to the Warchief's capital.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll at the Crossroads, you help tie the expanding wilderness outposts into Orgrimmar's supply lines.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you help bring fresh Barrens cuts to Gryshka's inn in Orgrimmar, keeping the capital's stewpots filled for visiting warriors."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","flight master","gryshka","meat delivery","orgrimmar","wind rider","zargh"},rel={"npc:zargh","npc:devrak","quest:6384","quest:6385","quest:6386","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar","quest:6361"},m={start="Zargh",["end"]="Devrak",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6365},src={"Meats to Orgrimmar (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6541"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Kadrak",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Thork sends proven Horde fighters north to report to Kadrak. The orc holds a watch tower near the Ashenvale border and prepares recruits for the fighting ahead.",h="At the Crossroads, Thork sends proven Horde fighters north to report to Kadrak.",sec={{t="The Road North",b="The Crossroads faces quilboar, centaur, and local brigands, while the Horde looks north to Ashenvale's thick forests. Thork directs fighters who have proved themselves in the central Barrens to the northern border tower, where Kadrak is stationed.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Strategy",b="Kadrak oversees the southern approach to Ashenvale and organizes reinforcements for the Horde's foothold across the border. Splintertree Post and an outpost along the Zoram Strand help the Horde strengthen its presence in the timber-rich woodlands, where native night elves resist them fiercely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thork?",a="Thork is an orc officer at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He helps organize local defense and directs promising fighters toward campaigns such as the push into Ashenvale.",al={"thork crossroads","who gives report to kadrak","thork barrens"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Kadrak located?",a="Kadrak is at the northern watch tower in the Barrens, beside the main road into Ashenvale.",al={"kadrak location","where is kadrak","kadrak watch tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde pushing into Ashenvale?",a="The Horde is pushing into Ashenvale for the lumber and resources needed to build its new cities in Durotar and the Barrens. The timber is vital, but seeking it brings the Horde into direct conflict with the night elves.",al={"why ashenvale","horde in ashenvale","ashenvale invasion"},it="conflict"},{q="What outposts has the Horde established in Ashenvale?",a="The Horde has established Splintertree Post along Ashenvale's central road and another outpost farther west on the Zoram Strand.",al={"horde bases ashenvale","zoram strand base","splintertree"},it="allies"},{q="What comes after reporting to Kadrak?",a="After you report to Kadrak, he briefs you on the local military situation and sends you to gather reports from the Warsong outposts across Ashenvale.",al={"after kadrak","next quest after kadrak","what does kadrak give"},it="next_step"},{q="Can you receive this assignment from anywhere other than the Barrens?",a="Yes. Horde fighters operating from Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains receive a nearly identical summons to report to Kadrak.",al={"alternate kadrak quest","stonetalon kadrak quest"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Thork want me to report to Kadrak?",a="The Horde is actively securing its hold on Ashenvale, having recently carved out outposts like the one on the Zoram Strand. Thork oversees Crossroads defense, but the front lines up north constantly demand fresh recruits to protect these newly claimed territories. He directs capable warriors up to Kadrak, who coordinates the campaign from the northern watch tower and determines where reinforcements are needed most.",al={"why report to kadrak","thork motive report to kadrak","why does thork send me to kadrak"},it="motive",add="d049fa98"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you are moving from the defense of settled Barrens territories toward securing vital resources in the disputed forests to the north.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you are entering a crucial proving ground. Ashenvale's timber can help fortify Orgrimmar and establish a lasting home on Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","crossroads","kadrak","splintertree","thork","watch tower","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:kadrak","npc:thork","quest:6543","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale","subzone:zoram-strand","topic:horde","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Thork",["end"]="Kadrak",level="19",faction="Horde",id=6541},src={"Report to Kadrak (Barrens)"}}
E["quest:6543"] = {t="quest",n="The Warsong Reports",z="barrens",s="Kadrak sends couriers from the northern Barrens to gather reports across Ashenvale. The Warsong Reports carry orders and field observations from outriders near Azshara, Splintertree Post, and the Zoram Strand.",h="Kadrak sends couriers from the northern Barrens to gather reports across Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Frontier Logistics",b="Kadrak watches the mountain pass between the northern Barrens and Ashenvale from a fortified tower. The Horde needs the pass because the Barrens cannot supply the timber Orgrimmar requires. The Warsong clan has pushed into the ancient elven forest to reach those supplies. Couriers carry orders between scattered patrols and help keep them in step, while night elf ambushes threaten the wilderness trails.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Across Ashenvale",b="Warsong scouts watch three parts of Ashenvale. On the western coast, a runner at Zoram'gar Outpost watches naga activity and other coastal threats along the Zoram Strand. At Splintertree Post, a scout coordinates defense against Sentinel raids. Farther east, an outrider watches the road toward the shattered ruins of Azshara. Their reports give Kadrak a view of night elf movements and weaknesses along the frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this mission begin?",a="The reports begin with Kadrak, an orc officer in the wooden watchtower guarding the mountain pass between the northern Barrens and southern Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","kadrak location","who gives the warsong reports","where to start"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde spying on Ashenvale?",a="The Horde seeks Ashenvale's dense timber to build and reinforce settlements such as Orgrimmar. Night elves fiercely defend their sacred groves, and constant scouting helps the Horde maintain its outposts and supply lines in the conflict.",al={"why ashenvale","warsong lumber","ashenvale conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can the three Warsong scouts be found?",a="The Warsong Runner is at Zoram'gar Outpost on the far northwestern Zoram Strand. The Warsong Scout is at Splintertree Post along the main road. The Warsong Outrider patrols the eastern road toward Azshara's border.",al={"scout locations","where are the scouts","outrider runner scout location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who are the Warsong outriders?",a="Warsong outriders are scouts and raiders of the Warsong orc clan. Their cavalry and skirmishing help the Horde expand, harvest lumber, and defend territory in Ashenvale's forests.",al={"warsong clan","who are warsong outriders","warsong clan ashenvale"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after returning the reports?",a="When Kadrak receives the reports, he uses them to plan troop movements, reinforce vulnerable outposts such as Zoram'gar and Splintertree, and strengthen the Horde's presence deeper in the forest.",al={"reports turn in","next move","what does kadrak do"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is the road through Ashenvale safe for low-level couriers?",a="No. Night elf Sentinels often ambush travelers on Ashenvale's main road. Prowlers, bears, and Alliance patrols from settlements such as Astranaar also threaten couriers.",al={"ashenvale danger","is the road safe","night elf ganks"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Why does Kadrak want the reports collected?",a="Kadrak guards the border between the Barrens and the contested forests of Ashenvale. The Horde is actively looking to expand its presence within the canopy, but marching blindly into night elf territory invites disaster. Kadrak deployed reconnaissance scouts deep into the region to monitor enemy activity and terrain. He needs these updates delivered and returned urgently so the Horde leadership can accurately assess their tactical standing and coordinate their next moves in the ongoing campaign.",al={"kadrak motive","why kadrak wants reports","why gather warsong reports"},it="motive",add="197774e3"},{q="What is the Warsong Outrider Update?",a="The Warsong Outrider Update is a tactical intelligence document compiled by the Horde outrider patrolling the eastern stretches of Ashenvale toward the border of Azshara. It contains observations on Alliance movements, sentinel patrols, and local geography along the vital thoroughfare, providing Kadrak with the eastern border overview needed to plan troop maneuvers.",al={"warsong outrider update","what is outrider update","outrider report"},it="item",add="649e115c"},{q="What is the Warsong Runner Update?",a="The Warsong Runner Update contains reconnaissance gathered from the western fringes of the forest, stationed out of Zoram'gar Outpost along the Zoram Strand. This dispatch details coastal threats, local hostile forces, and naval approaches, informing Kadrak about the safety of Horde positions far west of the main road.",al={"warsong runner update","what is runner update","runner report"},it="item",add="f6b4d8ea"},{q="What is the Warsong Scout Update?",a="The Warsong Scout Update is a strategic report sent from Splintertree Post, the primary Horde stronghold in central Ashenvale. Compiled by the forward scout stationed there, it tracks enemy night elf incursions, logistical supplies, and the readiness of the outpost to support further Horde expansion in the surrounding wilderness.",al={"warsong scout update","what is scout update","scout report"},it="item",add="92e54885"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Delivering these reports gives a young Horde warrior an early role in the struggle against the night elves in northern Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, aiding the Warsong clan honors the clan and helps supply the lumber needed to build Orgrimmar.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you test your navigation and survival skills on Ashenvale's dangerous roads, where wild predators and hidden elven archers pose threats."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","kadrak","splintertree post","warsong outrider","warsong reports","warsong runner","warsong scout","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:kadrak","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:zoram-strand","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","npc:warsong-outrider","zone:azshara"},m={start="Kadrak",level="19",faction="Horde",id=6543,ri={"Warsong Outrider Update","Warsong Runner Update","Warsong Scout Update"}},src={"The Warsong Reports"}}
E["quest:79192"] = {t="quest",n="Stepping Stones",z="barrens",s="A weathered note in the Barrens points travelers toward Stepping Stones, a mountain refuge near Desolace. It says two couriers made deliveries for the New Plague, and calls what happened to them simple apothecary accidents.",h="A weathered note in the Barrens points travelers toward Stepping Stones, a mountain refuge near Desolace.",sec={{t="A Note in the Wilds",b="A torn message hangs from a wooden plank at a backcountry camp in the Barrens. Mercenaries, cutthroats, and drifters pass through such camps for brief shelter, far from the eyes of the Crossroads or Ratchet. Among the wilds' ordinary signs, the note offers a reason to look beyond the camp and toward the mountains.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the New Plague",b="The anonymous writer says two agents made deliveries for the New Plague, then calls what happened to them simple apothecary accidents. The note invites you to meet at a mountain refuge between the Barrens and Desolace, where the matter can be discussed in safety.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the note found in Stepping Stones talking about?",a="The note says two couriers making deliveries for the New Plague met sudden ends, which the writer calls simple apothecary accidents. The writer offers a mountain meeting place to discuss what happened.",al={"stepping stones note","what is the note about","stepping stones quest text"}},{q="Where does the note tell you to go?",a="The writer directs you to a secluded refuge in the mountains between the Barrens and Desolace.",al={"where to go stepping stones","cozy spot mountains","stepping stones location"}},{q="What is the New Plague mentioned in the letter?",a="The New Plague is a deadly concoction developed in Undercity by the Forsaken's Royal Apothecary Society. It is meant to destroy both the Scourge and living enemies, and its testing and courier runs across the continents carry secrecy and fatal danger.",al={"what is new plague","royal apothecary plague","apothecary deliveries"}},{q="Who wrote the note pinned to the plank?",a="The note is anonymous and pinned to a rough wooden plank at a backcountry camp. Its writer offers a mountain meeting place between the Barrens and Desolace.",al={"who wrote the note","stepping stones author","who is waiting in the mountains"}},{q="Why would couriers for the Forsaken be in Kalimdor?",a="Forsaken apothecaries gather exotic venoms, spores, and reagents from Kalimdor's flora and fauna, then coordinate shipments through Horde outposts and wilderness routes.",al={"forsaken in barrens","why new plague in kalimdor","apothecaries in the barrens"}},{q="Why are backcountry camps used for notes like this?",a="Outside major settlements, the Barrens is sprawling and loosely governed. Neutral waystations, mercenary rest spots, and rogue camps let travelers, smugglers, and informers leave word discreetly, away from the Horde and regional watch posts.",al={"backcountry camp lore","mercenary camps barrens"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken travelers, a rogue mention of the Royal Apothecary Society and its blight research is an urgent security matter, or a dangerous conspiracy from within.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde wanderer in the Barrens, you must weigh whether reports of lethal plague deliveries on Kalimdor soil threaten your lands and alliances.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know how to track anonymous informants and judge covert messages left between Desolace and the Barrens."},kw={"desolace","mercenaries","mountains","new plague","note","royal apothecary society","stepping stones","the barrens"},rel={"zone:barrens","zone:desolace","quest:255"},m={level="24",id=79192},src={"In-game quest text: Stepping Stones","Stepping Stones"},fv=true}
E["quest:819"] = {t="quest",n="Chen's Empty Keg",z="barrens",s="A keg bearing Chen Stormstout’s mark lies abandoned in the Barrens. Its discovery points toward the wandering brewmaster’s old ties to Durotar.",h="A keg bearing Chen Stormstout’s mark lies abandoned in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Wandering Relic",b="Travelers sometimes find an abandoned wooden barrel across the dry Barrens. Razormane quilboar and Kolkar centaur leave ordinary casks behind, but this barrel is carefully made and bears a plaque: “Chen Stormstout - May your spirit be raised and always raise your spirits.” It is an odd relic beneath Kalimdor’s sun. To learn how it came to the Barrens, you seek someone who knows brewing.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of Durotar's Founding",b="Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet recognizes the keg’s craftsmanship and names Chen Stormstout as its owner. Chen, a wandering Pandaren, traveled with Rexxar during the battles that secured Durotar for Thrall’s Horde. Years have passed since Chen walked Kalimdor’s red earth, yet seasoned brewers still remember his recipes and wandering spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Chen's Empty Keg?",a="It is an abandoned brewing barrel found in the Barrens. Its inscription honors the wandering Pandaren brewmaster Chen Stormstout.",al={"empty keg","chens keg","what is this barrel"},it="item"},{q="Who is Chen Stormstout?",a="Chen Stormstout is a wandering Pandaren brewmaster who traveled across Kalimdor. He is best known for helping Rexxar, a half-ogre beastmaster, defend and establish Durotar.",al={"who is chen","chen lore","pandaren brewmaster"},it="identity"},{q="Who should I take the keg to?",a="Take the keg to Brewmaster Drohn, an orc brewer stationed along the road near Ratchet. He recognizes Chen’s mark and knows how to recreate his recipes.",al={"where to turn in keg","who wants chens keg","keg turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is Chen's keg lying out in the Barrens?",a="Chen roamed Kalimdor years ago in search of exotic brewing ingredients. He traveled while helping the young Horde secure its homeland against Admiral Proudmoore’s forces.",al={"why is keg in barrens","how did keg get here"},it="origin"},{q="Does Chen Stormstout appear in person?",a="No. Chen has left the region and has not been seen in Kalimdor for a long time. His old barrels, recipes, and the fond memories of allies like Drohn and Rexxar remain.",al={"can i find chen","where is chen stormstout","is chen in classic"}},{q="What does Brewmaster Drohn do with the keg?",a="Drohn welcomes the relic and challenges adventurous wanderers to gather local beast ingredients. He plans to use them to recreate Chen’s potent, legendary brews.",al={"drohn quest line","what happens next with keg"},it="purpose"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can remember Chen Stormstout as an honored ally who fought beside Rexxar and Rokhan to establish Durotar and protect the Horde in its earliest days.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can see Chen’s keg as the legacy of an artisan brewer. His palate and search for rare ingredients inspired craftsmen across Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","brewing","brewmaster drohn","chen stormstout","empty keg","pandaren","ratchet","rexxar"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","zone:barrens"},m={start="Chen's Empty Keg",["end"]="Brewmaster Drohn",level="15",faction="Horde",id=819},src={"Chen's Empty Keg (quest)"}}
E["quest:821"] = {t="quest",n="Chen's Empty Keg",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Brewmaster Drohn hopes to revive Chen Stormstout's potent brew with wild ingredients from the Barrens.",h="In Ratchet, Brewmaster Drohn hopes to revive Chen Stormstout's potent brew with wild ingredients from the...",sec={{t="A Legacy in a Keg",b="A marked keg brings Chen Stormstout to mind for Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet. Chen passed the secrets of his namesake brew to Drohn's mentor, who entrusted them to Drohn. The recipe calls for raw, potent elements taken straight from the Barrens' fierce wildlife, an unusual choice to those outside the brewing trade.",sp=0},{t="Harvesting the Savannah",b="To revive Chen's potent draught, you gather plainstrider kidneys, savannah lion tusks, and a thunder lizard horn. The ingredients must come from resilient beasts, so the hunt leads across the dusty plains. When you bring them to Drohn, he fondly recalls earlier batches of trogg brew. Reviving the old formula warms his stomach almost as much as those past brews.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Brewmaster Drohn?",a="Brewmaster Drohn is an orc brewmaster in Ratchet, the port town. His mentor received recipes from the wandering Chen Stormstout and passed the brewing art on to Drohn.",al={"brewmaster drohn","who is drohn","drohn ratchet"},it="identity"},{q="Why does a beer recipe require animal kidneys and horns?",a="Pandaren brewing traditions and frontier adaptations use powerful, esoteric ingredients from local wildlife. They lend vigor, kick, and distinct natural essences to potent draughts.",al={"why animal parts","plainstrider kidneys brew","lion tusks beer"},it="item"},{q="Where can the required ingredients be found?",a="Plainstriders and savannah lions roam the Barrens' open grasslands. Thunder lizards graze in its more arid or rocky stretches.",al={"where to find tusks","where are thunder lizards","finding brew ingredients"},gp=true},{q="Who was Chen Stormstout?",a="Chen Stormstout is a wandering pandaren brewmaster who traveled across Kalimdor during the founding of Durotar. He aided the Horde while seeking rare, exotic ingredients to perfect his potent beers.",al={"who is chen","chen stormstout lore","chen"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after bringing the ingredients to Drohn?",a="When you bring Drohn the lion tusks, plainstrider kidneys, and thunder lizard horn, he is delighted. The ingredients recall his earlier brewing days and lead into the final phase of recreating the draught.",al={"next quest after chens empty keg","drohn reward","whats next"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the trogg brew Drohn mentions?",a="Drohn fondly recalls trogg brew when he sees the wild ingredients. His recollection shows his eccentric history of fermenting harsh, unusual concoctions on the frontier.",al={"trogg brew","drohn trogg brew","trogg beer"},it="history"},{q="Why does Brewmaster Drohn want these ingredients?",a="Brewmaster Drohn wants to recreate the legendary Stormstout brew, an exotic and potent drink passed down from Chen Stormstout to Drohn's mentor and finally to him. Preparing the brew is an act of nostalgia and pride for Drohn, stirring fond memories of famous past concoctions and honoring the techniques left behind by the wandering pandaren master.",al={"why does drohn want this","drohn motive","why make the brew"},it="motive",add="cd71a987"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For a cook, this is an unsettling meeting of frontier butchery and fine brewing in the making of legendary Kalimdor spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="Chen Stormstout fought alongside Rexxar to help establish Durotar, giving remnants of his journey special cultural meaning for the Horde.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Drohn as an example of orcs embracing ancient brewmaster traditions passed down by travelers who walked with the early Horde."},kw={"brewmaster drohn","chen stormstout","keg","plainstrider kidney","ratchet","savannah lion tusk","the barrens","thunder lizard horn","trogg brew"},rel={"quest:819","npc:brewmaster-drohn","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:trogg"},m={start="Brewmaster Drohn",level="15",faction="Horde",id=821,ri={"Plainstrider Kidney","Savannah Lion Tusk","Thunder Lizard Horn"}},src={"Chen's Empty Keg (2)"}}
E["quest:822"] = {t="quest",n="Chen's Empty Keg",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Brewmaster Drohn turns to another recipe shared by Chen Stormstout. Trogg ale calls for rare organs and glands from beasts of the Barrens.",h="In Ratchet, Brewmaster Drohn turns to another recipe shared by Chen Stormstout.",sec={{t="A Second Pandaren Formula",b="After helping Brewmaster Drohn recreate Chen Stormstout's first draught, you learn the wandering pandaren shared more than one brewing secret. Drohn has the formula for trogg ale, a strange brew made not from grain, but from potent parts of the wild beasts of central Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="The Ingredients of Trogg Ale",b="To make trogg ale, Drohn needs lightning glands from stormhides, a thunderhawk saliva gland from greater thunderhawks, and a hearty liver from the plains' roaming kodos. Once distilled, these ingredients make a fiercely stimulating drink for life in the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="An Enduring Partnership",b="Brewmaster Drohn keeps the arrangement open for travelers and mercenaries passing through Ratchet. Bring him another supply of beast organs, and he is willing to brew more trogg ale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Chen Stormstout?",a="Chen Stormstout is an elusive pandaren brewmaster who wandered across Kalimdor during the founding of Durotar. He shared some of his potent brewing methods with Drohn in Ratchet before continuing his travels.",al={"who is chen","chen lore","pandaren chen"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Brewmaster Drohn located?",a="Brewmaster Drohn is in Ratchet, the neutral port on the Barrens' eastern coast. He spends his days refining brews he learned from Chen.",al={"drohn location","where is brewmaster drohn","drohn npc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is trogg ale?",a="Trogg ale is a potent brew Chen taught Drohn to make. It uses beast glands and organ meat in place of ordinary brewing hops, giving it a fierce kick for hardy adventurers.",al={"trogg ale","what is this drink","what does drohn brew"},it="item"},{q="Where do you gather lightning glands?",a="You can gather lightning glands from stormhide beasts roaming the Barrens' arid lands. Their bodies carry natural electrical charges.",al={"lightning gland source","stormhide location","where to get lightning gland"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What beasts drop thunderhawk saliva glands?",a="Greater thunderhawks provide the saliva glands Drohn needs. These avian predators hunt in the open skies across the Barrens.",al={"thunderhawk saliva gland","where are greater thunderhawks","thunderhawk location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Can I brew trogg ale more than once?",a="Yes. Brewmaster Drohn will make more trogg ale when adventurers bring him fresh glands and a kodo liver.",al={"is this repeatable","can i do this again","repeat trogg ale"},gp=true},{q="Why does Brewmaster Drohn want these ingredients?",a="Drohn is eager to share another exotic recipe he learned directly from the wandering brewmaster Chen Stormstout. Having already guided you through recreating Chen's prized stout, Drohn wants to brew a batch of potent trogg ale—a concoction with a fierce kick meant to fortify and aid hearty adventurers who brave the perilous Barrens.",al={"why does drohn want this","brewmaster drohn motive","why make trogg ale"},it="motive",add="72ec56fd"},{q="What is the Lightning Gland for?",a="Lightning glands are one of the ingredients in Chen's trogg ale recipe. Drohn asks for five, gathered from stormhides in the Barrens.",al={"why lightning gland","lightning gland use lore","what are lightning glands used for"},it="item",add="63499675"},{q="What is the Thunderhawk Saliva Gland for?",a="Drohn needs one saliva gland from a greater thunderhawk to make Chen's trogg ale. He does not explain the gland's precise role in brewing the drink.",al={"why thunderhawk saliva gland","thunderhawk saliva gland use","what is thunderhawk saliva for"},it="item",add="4ecc81d9"},{q="What is the Kodo Liver for?",a="A kodo liver is one of the ingredients Drohn needs for Chen's trogg ale. He accepts a liver from any of the Barrens' kodos.",al={"why kodo liver","kodo liver use lore","what is the kodo liver for"},it="item",add="315602f6"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Trogg ale may offend culinary purists, but using rich organ meat and potent glands follows the frontier custom of wasting nothing from a kill.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may find Drohn's path unusual: he chose Chen's exotic brewing methods over the traditional warrior's path and keeps his business in Ratchet.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share a history with Chen Stormstout, who fought alongside the Horde in Durotar's defense. His time there left a lasting impression on orcs like Drohn."},kw={"barrens","brewmaster drohn","chen stormstout","chen's empty keg","kodo liver","ratchet","stormhide","thunderhawk","trogg ale"},rel={"npc:brewmaster-drohn","quest:819","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","topic:trogg"},m={start="Brewmaster Drohn",level="24",faction="Horde",id=822,ri={"Kodo Liver","Lightning Gland","Thunderhawk Saliva Gland"}},src={"Chen's Empty Keg (3)"}}
E["quest:840"] = {t="quest",n="Conscript of the Horde",z="barrens",s="Along Durotar’s western road, Conscript of the Horde sends recruits toward the Barrens. Takrin Pathseeker watches beyond Razor Hill and gives them a letter for Kargal Battlescar, whose outpost guards the crossing.",h="Along Durotar’s western road, Conscript of the Horde sends recruits toward the Barrens.",sec={{t="Crossing the Southfury",b="After proving your strength around Razor Hill, you are called west to serve the wider Horde. Takrin Pathseeker watches the road out of Durotar for his friend, veteran Kargal Battlescar. He gives capable travelers a recruitment letter to carry across the Southfury River. For a recruit, the letter marks a first formal assignment beyond the orcs’ new homeland.",sp=0},{t="Border Defense",b="Kargal Battlescar holds the outpost beyond the bridge, between Durotar’s red canyons and the dry Barrens. He gathers recruits to guard the frontier, where centaur, quilboar, and Alliance expeditions test the border. The Horde needs more than guards there: raw manpower is being sent to the settlement of the Crossroads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I take the recruitment letter?",a="Take the western road out of Razor Hill and cross the wooden bridge over the Southfury River. Kargal Battlescar waits at the Horde watchtower just across the border, on the Barrens side.",al={"where do i go","kargal battlescar location","turn in location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Takrin Pathseeker?",a="Takrin Pathseeker is a Horde scout on the western road outside Razor Hill. He watches the road and sends capable warriors west to his comrade Kargal Battlescar.",al={"takrin role","who gives quest","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Kargal Battlescar?",a="Kargal Battlescar is a gruff veteran officer at the eastern Barrens watchpost. He inspects arriving volunteers, signs their conscription papers, and directs them west across the savanna to aid the Crossroads.",al={"who is kargal","battlescar lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after Kargal signs the letter?",a="After Kargal accepts the letter, he enlists you for further service and sends you west along the main road to report to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.",al={"next quest","what after conscript of the horde","where next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde recruiting soldiers for the Barrens?",a="The Barrens is an open frontier that connects Orgrimmar with Mulgore. Fierce quilboar tribes, centaur marauders, and Alliance incursions threaten supply routes, so the Horde needs every able hand to keep the roads secure.",al={"why conscript","barrens danger","why recruit"},it="purpose"},{q="Is this quest available to Alliance players?",a="No. This service is only for Horde members moving from the early Durotar story into the Barrens.",al={"can alliance do this","is this horde only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Takrin Pathseeker want me to deliver the recruitment letter?",a="Takrin Pathseeker serves as an advanced scout watching the road from Durotar into the arid plains. His old comrade Kargal Battlescar commands the border outpost just across the river and faces a constant shortage of capable warriors. Seeing promise in your strength, Takrin wants to steer fresh blood directly into the Barrens garrison to bolster Horde defense rather than let able hands idle in Razor Hill.",al={"why does takrin send me","takrin pathseeker motive","why recruit for kargal"},it="motive",add="dfa16f64"},{q="Why does Takrin send an adventurer instead of reporting to Kargal himself?",a="Takrin is assigned to watch the vital crossroads between Durotar and the western frontier, keeping eyes on travelers and threats moving along the highway. Leaving his post to ferry individual messages would abandon his duty. More importantly, he is scouting for potential soldiers to aid Kargal, and having you report directly to the outpost commander proves your willingness and initiative to serve the Horde.",al={"why doesn't takrin go","why send me to kargal","why me conscript of the horde"},it="why_me",add="788e36ab"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, this conscription marks your move from protecting Durotar to defending Horde lands across Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc leaving the Valley of Trials and Razor Hill, answering Kargal Battlescar’s call is a rite of passage in service to the Warchief.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you join your orc allies in this deployment to aid the Horde’s expansion and secure the lands bordering the Great Sea."},kw={"barrens","conscript of the horde","crossroads","kargal battlescar","razor hill","recruitment letter","southfury river","takrin pathseeker"},rel={"quest:842","npc:kargal-battlescar","zone:barrens","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:crossroads","topic:horde"},m={start="Takrin Pathseeker",["end"]="Kargal Battlescar",level="12",faction="Horde",id=840},src={"Conscript of the Horde (Classic)"}}
E["quest:842"] = {t="quest",n="Crossroads Conscription",z="barrens",s="Recruits leave the Far Watch Post for duty at Crossroads Conscription. Carrying Kargal Battlescar’s signed letter, you report to Sergra Darkthorn at the Barrens’ central hub.",h="Recruits leave the Far Watch Post for duty at Crossroads Conscription.",sec={{t="Reporting for Duty",b="Kargal Battlescar sends you west from the Far Watch Post after you prove your worth. He gives you a signed recruitment letter to carry along the packed dirt road through the Barrens’ arid brush. The road reaches a central junction, where the Crossroads links northern Kalimdor with the southern wilderness.",sp=0},{t="The Shaman of the Crossroads",b="Sergra Darkthorn receives new arrivals at the Crossroads. Warchief Thrall chose the sharp-tongued orc shaman to oversee its operations. Kargal Battlescar grumbles that she is difficult and talks too much, but Thrall holds her in high esteem. Sergra is fierce and unyielding. She reminds recruits, especially arrogant men, that female warriors and leaders stand as equals in Thrall’s Horde, and she will tolerate no insolence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Kargal Battlescar, an orc veteran at the Far Watch Post just west of the bridge between Durotar and the Barrens, sends you west with a letter for Sergra.",al={"who gives crossroads conscription","quest giver crossroads conscription","kargal quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Sergra Darkthorn located?",a="Sergra Darkthorn is near the road crossing at the center of the Crossroads, where caravans and messengers meet.",al={"sergra darkthorn location","where is sergra","find sergra darkthorn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Kargal complain about Sergra?",a="Kargal finds Sergra aggravating. He calls her a nasty shaman who talks in circles before anyone can get to practical work, though he respects Thrall’s command to send recruits to her.",al={"why does kargal dislike sergra","kargal vs sergra","curse her hide"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Sergra speak differently to male and female characters?",a="Sergra takes pride in Thrall’s mandate of equality for female warriors in the Horde. She encourages female recruits and warns male recruits that she will not tolerate disrespect or insolence.",al={"sergra dialogue male female","sergra darkthorn dialogue","sergra equal footing"},it="people"},{q="What route should I take to reach the Crossroads?",a="Follow the main road west from the Far Watch Post to a T-intersection. Turn left and follow the southern road into the Crossroads.",al={"how to get to crossroads","directions to crossroads","crossroads path"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Sergra Darkthorn?",a="Sergra accepts your help at the Crossroads and sends you to aid with local threats, hunting, and outpost security throughout the central Barrens.",al={"what comes after crossroads conscription","next quest sergra","barrens recruits next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Kargal Battlescar sending me to the Crossroads?",a="As commander of Far Watch Post, Kargal processes fresh conscripts entering the Barrens from Durotar. Rather than keeping every able-bodied fighter at an entry outpost, his duty to the Horde is to forward new recruits deeper into the frontier. The Crossroads serves as the central hub of Horde authority and military mobilization in the Barrens, where manpower is desperately needed to secure surrounding lands under Sergra Darkthorn's oversight.",al={"why send to crossroads","kargal motive crossroads conscription","why report to sergra"},it="motive",add="3243ab88"},{q="Why does Kargal send me instead of sending one of his guards?",a="You are an incoming conscript seeking to prove yourself and earn your keep within the Horde. Kargal's outpost guards are already assigned to garrison the border watch post against local threats. Sending you along with a signed recruitment letter both reinforces the outpost at the Crossroads and tests whether a new recruit has the discipline to navigate the wild plains alone and follow orders.",al={"why does kargal need me","why not send a guard to crossroads","why me kargal"},it="why_me",add="07e83289"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you leave the safety of your homeland to serve in the contested wilderness of the Barrens.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see how Thrall’s Horde is changing, as merit and spiritual insight challenge the old clan ways of traditional grunt work.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see Sergra Darkthorn lead as both a spiritual adviser and a military commander and administrator at a strategic outpost."},kw={"barrens","battlescar","conscription","crossroads","darkthorn","far watch","kargal","sergra","thrall"},rel={"npc:kargal-battlescar","subzone:crossroads","subzone:far-watch-post","quest:840","quest:860","zone:barrens","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},m={start="Kargal Battlescar",["end"]="Sergra Darkthorn",level="12",faction="Horde",id=842},src={"Crossroads Conscription"}}
E["quest:843"] = {t="quest",n="Gann's Reclamation",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Gann Stonespire seeks travelers to strike back at Bael Modan. The wandering tauren exile was driven from his clan’s ancestral home and hunting grounds, and asks you to slay the dig’s workers and bring him its leader’s journal.",h="In the southern Barrens, Gann Stonespire seeks travelers to strike back at Bael Modan.",sec={{t="A Displaced Tribe",b="Gann Stonespire walks alone along the southern road, seeking bloody restitution for his fallen kin. His clan’s ancestral birthplace and hunting grounds lay among the red bluffs south of the Barrens. Dwarves from Ironforge came to build Bael Modan, and drove the tauren out or killed them to make room for quarries and trenches. Gann says peaceful protests and diplomacy failed. Now he seeks vengeance for the clan that was displaced and slain.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Bael Modan",b="At Bael Modan, dwarven excavators tear into the hills with steam engines and explosives. Prospector Khazgorm leads the dig deep into the earth. Gann asks you to thin the ranks of Bael'dun excavators and foremen, kill Khazgorm, and take the prospector’s personal excavation notes. He wants the notes to learn what the Alliance expedition seeks in the sacred soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gann Stonespire?",a="Gann Stonespire is a solitary tauren survivor whose tribe once lived in the southern Barrens. After dwarven excavators drove his people from their land and killed those who resisted, he paces the southern highway, seeking justice and revenge against the Alliance dig site.",al={"gann","who gives gann's reclamation","gann stonespire lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the dwarves in the Barrens?",a="The dwarves are an Ironforge expedition called the Bael'dun. They built a keep and excavation at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens, where their blasting and noisy machines tear apart the hills despite the native tauren inhabitants.",al={"why are dwarves at bael modan","bael modan purpose","ironforge in barrens"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Prospector Khazgorm?",a="Prospector Khazgorm leads the dwarven excavation south of the Bael Modan fortress. Gann holds him responsible for the desecration of his ancestral grounds and demands Khazgorm’s journal as proof of his death.",al={"khazgorm","prospector khazgorm","bael modan leader"},it="target"},{q="Where can Gann Stonespire be found?",a="Gann Stonespire paces along the road in the far southern Barrens, west of the Bael Modan fortress and north of the road toward the Great Lift and Thousand Needles.",al={"gann location","find gann","where is gann"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did Gann try to resolve this peacefully?",a="Yes. Gann says he tried diplomacy and other peaceful avenues to stop the destruction of his ancestral lands. The dwarves dismissed those efforts and kept blasting the hills, so he turned to violence.",al={"did tauren try diplomacy","gann diplomacy"},it="history"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="After Gann receives Khazgorm’s journal, he studies the prospector’s notes to understand the dwarves’ technology and plans. That leads into 'Revenge of Gann', where he seeks to sabotage their heavy machinery.",al={"next quest after gann's reclamation","gann follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gann Stonespire want to drive out the dwarves?",a="Bael Modan sits directly atop the ancestral lands of Gann's tribe. When the dwarves arrived, their relentless digging, loud machinery, and blasting drove the tauren from their home and cost many innocent lives. Having exhausted all peaceful overtures, Gann seeks retribution and aims to reclaim his people's sacred homeland by force.",al={"gann motive","why kill baeldun dwarves","why does gann want revenge"},it="motive",add="5ecef431"},{q="What is Khazgorm's Journal for?",a="The journal belongs to Prospector Khazgorm, the leader overseeing the destructive Bael Modan dig site. Gann wants to study its pages to glean insight into the dwarves' operations, their motives in the region, and how best to halt their ongoing destruction of his ancestral territory.",al={"khazgorm journal use","why collect khazgorm journal","what does gann want with the journal"},it="item",add="fd3e714a"},{q="Why does Gann ask you instead of handling the excavation himself?",a="Gann wanders the southern Barrens entirely alone, an exile whose tribe was slaughtered or scattered by the dwarven arrival. Facing a fortified settlement manned by dozens of armed excavators, foremen, and their leader, he cannot hope to dislodge the invaders without an able champion fighting on his behalf.",al={"why cant gann do it himself","why does gann need help","why me gann"},it="why_me",add="4442e883"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a Shu'halo, Gann’s plight is an infuriating reminder that the Alliance shows little respect for the Earth Mother. Dynamite and iron gears tear apart ancestral burial grounds.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Bael Modan as a fortified Alliance stronghold deep in Kalimdor. Defending Gann’s claim is an act of honor and a way to contain that stronghold.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know that Bael Modan’s blasting and deep trenches wound the surrounding earth spirits. Gann’s campaign is a necessary cleansing of that elemental disruption."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun","dwarf dig site","gann stonespire","khazgorm","southern barrens"},rel={"npc:gann-stonespire","quest:846","subzone:bael-modan","zone:barrens","topic:tauren","topic:dwarf","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic"},m={level="23",faction="Horde",id=843,ri={"Khazgorm's Journal"}},src={"Gann's Reclamation"}}
E["quest:844"] = {t="quest",n="Plainstrider Menace",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends new Horde adventurers after plainstriders east of the outpost. The birds threaten its food supplies, and the hunt gives newcomers a first measure of the Barrens.",h="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends new Horde adventurers after plainstriders east of the outpost.",sec={{t="Securing the Crossroads",b="The Crossroads coordinates supplies across Kalimdor, but plainstriders east of the outpost have begun picking at its food crates. Sergra Darkthorn, an orc shaman, sends newly arrived Horde adventurers to hunt the birds before they damage the stores. Their attacks threaten provisions the settlement depends on.",sp=0},{t="The First Hunt",b="Sergra Darkthorn uses the hunt to measure newcomers as well as protect supplies. She sees the plainstriders as simple prey, fit to teach young hunters to endure the elements and track quarry across the sun-baked plains. Bringing back their sharp beaks shows a hunter has patience and the basic martial skill needed to face fiercer beasts of the Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the plainstriders targeted?",a="Plainstriders east of the Crossroads have grown bold, raiding food supplies and harassing passing supply lines. Sergra Darkthorn orders them hunted to protect the settlement's provisions.",al={"why kill plainstriders","plainstrider problem","what did plainstriders do"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Sergra Darkthorn?",a="Sergra Darkthorn is an experienced orc shaman stationed at the Crossroads. She oversees hunting trials, trains incoming adventurers, and directs them against wild beasts that threaten Horde operations.",al={"who is sergra","sergra darkthorn role","quest giver crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Sergra want their beaks specifically?",a="A plainstrider uses its tough, sharp beak as both its primary weapon and a tool for scavenging. Bringing back the beak proves the bird has been slain.",al={"why plainstrider beaks","plainstrider beak proof"},it="item"},{q="What comes after this hunt?",a="After the plainstriders, Sergra sends you to hunt zhevra, faster and more spirited prey roaming the plains.",al={"what is next","next quest after plainstriders","hunt sequence"},it="next_step"},{q="Where are these plainstriders located?",a="Plainstriders wander the savanna grasslands east and southeast of the Crossroads, foraging along the trade roads.",al={"where are plainstriders","plainstrider locations","hunting grounds"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this part of a larger hunting series?",a="Yes. This begins Sergra Darkthorn's hunting trials in the Barrens, which grow more dangerous as they turn to fiercer beasts across the savanna.",al={"barrens hunting chain","sergra quest chain"},gp=true},{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn need an adventurer instead of the Crossroads guards?",a="The guards stationed at the Crossroads have their hands full maintaining perimeter defenses against quilboar raids and keeping local routes secure. Hunting down nuisance scavengers out in the plains serves a dual purpose for Sergra: it relieves pressure on the settlement's food lines while testing whether fresh arrivals have the tracking and combat skills required to survive out in the Barrens.",al={"why send me","why don't guards kill the plainstriders","why adventurer plainstriders"},it="why_me",add="416dd73a"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a young hunter, you learn to stalk, track, and put down quarry in the wide-open savanna.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect the Crossroads, an essential logistics junction, and secure its food supplies so the Horde can maintain its foothold across Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you honor the discipline of the hunt. Sergra expects you to prove your mettle against local beasts before taking on weightier duties."},kw={"barrens","beak","crossroads","darkthorn","hunt","plainstrider","sergra","supplies"},rel={"quest:860","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},m={start="Sergra Darkthorn",level="12",faction="Horde",id=844,ri={"Plainstrider Beak"}},src={"Plainstrider Menace (Classic)"}}
E["quest:845"] = {t="quest",n="The Zhevra",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends young Horde warriors after the zhevra. Their hunt tests the skills needed to face the Barrens' more dangerous beasts.",h="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends young Horde warriors after the zhevra.",sec={{t="A Step Up in the Savanna",b="After the plainstriders, Sergra Darkthorn sends you after tougher prey. Zhevras run in herds across the northern and southern Barrens. They are not the savanna's fiercest beasts, but they are swift and stubborn, and their kicks can break bone.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of Darkthorn",b="Sergra uses the hunt to test your growing skill. She asks for four intact hooves as proof of the kill and warns that a zhevra's rear kick can knock a grown tauren onto their haunches. Passing this trial brings you closer to facing the plains' predatory prowlers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns this hunt?",a="Sergra Darkthorn, an experienced orc shaman at the Crossroads in the central Barrens, sets this trial to test growing Horde warriors.",al={"who gives the zhevra quest","quest giver zhevra","sergra darkthorn quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the zhevra found?",a="Zhevra runners roam the open plains north and south of the Crossroads in the central Barrens.",al={"where are zhevra runners","zhevra location","barrens zhevra map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Sergra want zhevra hooves?",a="The hooves prove that you killed a zhevra. Bringing back four shows you overcame a beast whose powerful legs can knock down even a mighty tauren.",al={"why zhevra hooves","zhevra hoof proof","why hunt zhevra"},it="item"},{q="What comes after this quest?",a="After you prove yourself against zhevra, Sergra tests you against the Barrens' predators in Prowlers of the Barrens.",al={"next quest after the zhevra","zhevra follow up","darkthorn next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Are zhevras dangerous?",a="Zhevras are usually passive grazers, but their legs are powerful. Sergra warns that a startled or cornered runner can knock even a sturdy tauren flat with one kick.",al={"how dangerous are zhevra","zhevra danger","zhevra kick"},it="threat"},{q="Why were plainstriders hunted before this?",a="Sergra makes her trials harder step by step. Plainstriders are the first target; zhevras are faster and stronger prey, preparing you to face aggressive savanna prowlers.",al={"previous quest","plainstrider menace connection"},it="history"},{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn want the zhevra hunted?",a="Sergra Darkthorn is testing your hunting prowess and seasoning you for the brutal wilderness of the Barrens. While plainstriders offer basic target practice, zhevra are sturdier beasts whose powerful kicks test your reflexes and endurance. By sending you after them, Sergra ensures you can handle dangerous wildlife before dispatching you against the territory's apex predators.",al={"why hunt zhevra","sergra motive","sergra darkthorn reason"},it="motive",add="6d2e3590"},{q="What are the zhevra runners?",a="Zhevra runners are swift, striped equines native to the arid savannahs of the Barrens. Traveling in herds across the plains to the north and south of the Crossroads, they rely on speed and formidable hind legs to survive among prowlers and raptors. While not inherently aggressive predators, their kicks can knock a full-grown tauren off their feet.",al={"what are zhevras","zhevra runners","who are we hunting"},it="target",add="1cbbdcd0"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know how forceful a zhevra's kick can be. Sergra warns that it can knock a full-grown tauren off their hooves.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter learning the Barrens, you can sharpen your tracking and aim by stalking swift zhevra herds.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help the Crossroads manage the surrounding wildlife and keep its supply routes clear."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","hooves","hunting trial","sergra darkthorn","zhevra","zhevra runner"},rel={"quest:860","quest:903","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},m={start="Sergra Darkthorn",level="13",faction="Horde",id=845,ri={"Zhevra Hooves"}},src={"The Zhevra (Classic)"}}
E["quest:846"] = {t="quest",n="Revenge of Gann",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Gann Stonespire prepares to strike back at the Bael Modan dwarves. After Prospector Khazgorm's death, he sends Horde allies into the fortress for volatile munitions to fuel his attack.",h="In the southern Barrens, Gann Stonespire prepares to strike back at the Bael Modan dwarves.",sec={{t="A Taste of Their Own Medicine",b="Gann Stonespire knows Prospector Khazgorm's death only slowed the Bael Modan dig site. Dwarven work will resume, and another foreman will soon oversee the machines tearing through Gann's ancestral land. He refuses to watch the earth suffer more excavation. Instead, Gann plans to turn the invaders' demolitions gear against them and rupture their stronghold from within.",sp=0},{t="Raiding the Keep",b="Bael Modan's fortress holds an excavation base and a garrison of soldiers, riflemen, and officers protecting dwarven interests in the Barrens. Gann has learned that its defenders carry nitroglycerin, wood pulp, and sodium nitrate, materials used in industrial demolition. He sends Horde allies past the perimeter to take these volatile supplies from the dwarves. With enough gathered, he can assemble a powerful satchel charge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Gann Stonespire seeking revenge?",a="The Ironforge dwarves at Bael Modan overran Gann's ancestral homeland, desecrated the soil, and drove his people out to establish their excavation site. After killing the chief prospector and recovering his journal, Gann seeks to stop the destruction for good.",al={"why gann angry","gann stonespire motive","what did dwarves do to gann"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the explosive materials found?",a="Bael Modan's defenders carry the ingredients. Riflemen, soldiers, and officers within and around the fortified dig site in the southern Barrens have nitroglycerin vials, wood pulp bundles, and sodium nitrate samples.",al={"where to get nitroglycerin","how to get wood pulp","where is sodium nitrate"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gann need wood pulp and chemicals?",a="Dwarven excavation schematics show that wood pulp stabilizes volatile nitroglycerin, while sodium nitrate helps make a reliable industrial explosive. Gann plans to shape the mixture into a demolitions charge that can bring down key dwarven structures.",al={"why wood pulp","what does gann make","gann bomb ingredients"},it="item"},{q="What happens after gathering the supplies?",a="When you return the raw components, Gann assembles an explosive charge and sends you to destroy the dwarves' flying machine at the Bael Modan excavation, a key part of the site's infrastructure.",al={"what next revenge of gann","after gathering ingredients"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't slaying Khazgorm end the dwarven threat?",a="Khazgorm was only the lead prospector. Bael Modan's dwarven forces are entrenched behind defensive walls and supply lines, and Ironforge can send another foreman to continue digging unless the base suffers a catastrophic blow.",al={"why didn't khazgorm death work","is bael modan stopped"},it="threat"},{q="What is Bael Modan's strategic threat to the Horde?",a="Bael Modan began as a keep defending the dig site, but it has grown into a heavily manned Alliance stronghold. Its position along the southern Barrens trade routes makes it a military threat to nearby Horde settlements in Kalimdor.",al={"why horde care about bael modan","bael modan threat"},it="conflict"},{q="Who carry the supplies needed for the explosive?",a="The supplies are held by the dwarven garrison stationed at Bael Modan. The riflemen, soldiers, and officers inside the excavation and keep make frequent use of blasting powder and machinery to tear apart the land, meaning they keep ample stockpiles of volatile chemicals and stabilizers close at hand.",al={"who has the explosive materials","bael modan dwarves","revenge of gann targets"},it="target",add="410ab5f4"},{q="Why does Gann need you rather than striking Bael Modan himself?",a="Gann Stonespire is an outcast survivor of a shattered tribe, acting on his own without the backing of a large war party. Slaying an entire fortified garrison of Ironforge dwarves single-handedly is far beyond his reach, so he relies on an able champion of the Horde to infiltrate the keep and gather what he needs.",al={"why does gann need me","why cant gann do it himself","why me revenge of gann"},it="why_me",add="5f27d24f"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see Bael Modan as a grievous wound against the Earth Mother. Sabotaging the dwarven machinery is a duty to your spirit and homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep the Alliance from establishing a military foothold in the southern Barrens that could sever travel between Mulgore, Crossroads, and the southern frontier.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you recognize the classic dwarven industrial formula: nitroglycerin stabilized with pulp and mixed with sodium nitrate. Gann adapts it for an uneven fight."},kw={"bael modan","barrens","dynamite","explosives","gann stonespire","ironforge","khazgorm","nitroglycerin","sodium nitrate","wood pulp"},rel={"npc:gann-stonespire","quest:843","subzone:bael-modan","zone:barrens"},m={start="Gann Stonespire",level="26",faction="Horde",id=846,ri={"Nitroglycerin","Sodium Nitrate","Wood Pulp"}},src={"Revenge of Gann"}}
E["quest:848"] = {t="quest",n="Fungal Spores",z="barrens",s="At the Barrens oases, Horde adventurers gather Fungal Spores for Apothecary Helbrim of the Royal Apothecary Society. Strange, mutative energies flow through the springs and alter the local plants into potent reagents. Helbrim seeks the specimens to brew concoctions for his colleague in Thunder Bluff.",h="At the Barrens oases, Horde adventurers gather Fungal Spores for Apothecary Helbrim of the Royal Apothecary...",sec={{t="Vibrant and Mutated Flora",b="The Barrens is a dry savanna, but the Forgotten Pools, Lushwater Oasis, and Stagnant Oasis brim with unnatural vitality. A curious surge of life energy flows from their waters, warping and invigorating plants and beasts that drink there. Laden mushrooms grow along the muddy banks, absorbing those currents. Their spores hold rare properties that draw the curiosity of passing alchemists.",sp=0},{t="The Royal Apothecary Society in Kalimdor",b="Apothecary Helbrim works at the Crossroads, far from the Undercity, yet remains devoted to the Royal Apothecary Society's research. He gathers the altered spores because Kalimdor's native reagents have strange potency, and he uses them to craft powerful mixtures. The specimens are destined for Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff, part of the Forsaken's scientific work across allied lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do these fungal spores grow?",a="Laden mushrooms grow along the water's edge at Barrens oases, including the Forgotten Pools, the Lushwater Oasis, and the Stagnant Oasis.",al={"where to find fungal spores","fungal spore location","laden mushrooms location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the mushrooms altered near the oases?",a="A powerful surge of life energy flows through the Barrens oasis waters. It vigorously alters nearby wildlife and flora instead of merely sustaining ordinary plant growth.",al={"why are the mushrooms mutated","oases life energy","what is wrong with the oases"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Apothecary Helbrim?",a="Apothecary Helbrim is a Forsaken member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He studies the region's unusual biology and gathers local materials for alchemical study.",al={"helbrim lore","who is helbrim","apothecary at crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="What does Helbrim plan to do with the spores?",a="Helbrim uses the potent spores to brew a specific concoction for his research associate, Apothecary Zamah, in Thunder Bluff.",al={"what are the spores for","fungal spores purpose"},it="item"},{q="Why are Forsaken apothecaries operating in the Barrens?",a="As Horde allies, Forsaken researchers study Kalimdor's foreign environments and unusual flora, seeking new reagents for medicines, toxins, and concoctions.",al={"why are undead in barrens","royal apothecary society in kalimdor"},it="why_here"},{q="Which oasis is safest to collect the spores from?",a="The Forgotten Pools, northwest of the Crossroads, has lower-level wildlife than the Lushwater Oasis or the Stagnant Oasis to the south, making it the safest place to gather mushrooms.",al={"easiest oasis for spores","safest oasis barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Helbrim want the fungal spores collected?",a="Apothecary Helbrim is investigating the strange life energies surging through the Barrens' oases, which are mutating the surrounding flora and fauna. The Royal Apothecary Society finds the potent properties of these altered mushrooms uniquely valuable for their research. Helbrim urgently needs the specimens to prepare a specific concoction that must be sent onward to his associate, Apothecary Zamah, stationed in Thunder Bluff.",al={"why does helbrim want spores","helbrim motive","why collect fungal spores"},it="motive",add="f81deb18"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Far from Lordaeron, Forsaken researchers continue their alchemical work, turning Kalimdor's natural anomalies toward the goals of the Royal Apothecary Society.",["faction:Horde"]="Investigating the disturbed waters of the Barrens helps protect the vital trails connecting Orgrimmar, the Crossroads, and Thunder Bluff.",["class:Druid"]="The oases hold an unnaturally turbulent surge of nature magic that causes aggressive mutations in the surrounding ecosystem.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Laden mushrooms around the Barrens oases show how sudden infusions of environmental energy can transform ordinary plants into potent reagents."},kw={"apothecary helbrim","apothecary zamah","barrens","crossroads","forgotten pools","fungal spores","lushwater oasis","royal apothecary society","stagnant oasis"},rel={"npc:apothecary-helbrim","quest:853","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","subzone:forgotten-pools","subzone:lushwater-oasis","subzone:stagnant-oasis","quest:870"},m={start="Apothecary Helbrim",level="15",faction="Horde",id=848,ri={"Fungal Spores"}},src={"Fungal Spores (Classic)"}}
E["quest:849"] = {t="quest",n="Revenge of Gann",z="barrens",s="At Bael Modan, Gann Stonespire turns the dwarves’ own plans against their flying machine. The Horde agent seeks revenge for the fallen Stonespire tribe.",h="At Bael Modan, Gann Stonespire turns the dwarves’ own plans against their flying machine.",sec={{t="A Symbol of Domination",b="At Bael Modan, the dwarven excavation sits atop the ancestral grounds of the displaced Stonespire tauren. The Prospectors rely on a gyrocopter for their reach and military strength. It is stationed on a watchtower above the dig, where it surveys the surrounding Barrens and protects the dwarves’ supply lines. For Gann, the machine also marks the Alliance’s intrusion into kalimdorian soil.",sp=0},{t="Turned Upon Its Makers",b="After recovering Prospector Khazgorm’s plans, Gann Stonespire makes a specialized charge called the Explosive Stick of Gann. Planting it on the flying machine turns the dwarves’ own invention against them. The blast destroys a vital military asset, humiliates the Bael'dun contingent, and honors the spirits of Gann’s lost tribe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Gann want to destroy the flying machine specifically?",a="The flying machine aids Bael Modan’s infrastructure and gives the dwarves aerial reconnaissance. To Gann, it also embodies dwarven power and looms over land his slaughtered tribe once called home.",al={"why destroy gyrocopter","flying machine purpose","why target flying machine"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the flying machine located at Bael Modan?",a="The flying machine sits on a wooden tower platform halfway down the ramp into the main excavation pit, apart from the primary dwarven fortress.",al={"where is flying machine","flying machine location","bael modan gyrocopter spot"},gp=true},{q="How did Gann create the explosive device?",a="Gann made the Explosive Stick of Gann from technical schematics and engineering plans recovered from Prospector Khazgorm, using the dwarves’ own designs against them.",al={"how made bomb","explosive stick origin","khazgorm plans explosive"},it="item"},{q="What tribe does Gann belong to?",a="Gann belongs to the Stonespire tribe, a tauren clan that once lived in the southern Barrens. The Ironforge dwarven excavation drove them out by force and destroyed their settlement.",al={"gann tribe","what is stonespire tribe","who are stonespire tauren"},it="origin"},{q="Does destroying the machine stop the excavation permanently?",a="Destroying the machine cripples Bael Modan’s air strength and infrastructure and gives Gann personal revenge. The heavily entrenched dwarven diggers and fortress remain an active Alliance stronghold in the region.",al={"is bael modan stopped","does bael modan fall","did gann win"},it="conflict"},{q="What recognition does Gann offer upon finishing this mission?",a="Gann says the hero who destroyed the machine will be revered in Thunder Bluff as a defender of sacred tauren lands and a lasting champion of his lost tribe.",al={"gann completion","gann quest end","what does gann say"},sp=1,it="for_you"},{q="What is the flying machine at Bael Modan?",a="The target is a dwarven gyrocopter stationed within Bael Modan. Built and maintained by the dwarven expedition, this flying machine acts as vital infrastructure for their excavation, serves as an aerial weapon of war, and stands as a looming symbol of the dwarven intrusion that displaced Gann's people from their ancestral home.",al={"bael modan flying machine","what is the target in revenge of gann","dwarven flying machine bael modan"},it="target",add="947c7a95"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Destroying dwarven war machines to avenge the Stonespire clan resonates with any tauren defending their ancestral homeland from desecration.",["faction:Horde"]="Crippling Bael Modan’s flying machine weakens an Alliance aerial weapon that can scout and strike deep into the southern Barrens.",["profession:Engineering"]="The explosive turns Ironforge blueprints against a gyrocopter, making it a clever act of field sabotage."},kw={"bael modan","explosive stick of gann","flying machine","gann stonespire","khazgorm","stonespire tribe","the barrens","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:gann-stonespire","quest:846","quest:843","subzone:bael-modan","topic:tauren","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Gann Stonespire",level="26",faction="Horde",id=849},src={"Revenge of Gann (2)"}}
E["quest:850"] = {t="quest",n="Kolkar Leaders",z="barrens",s="Kolkar Leaders begins a campaign led by the orc Regthar Deathgate to crush rising centaur warlords in the Barrens. The nomadic Kolkar have plagued the tauren for generations, but newly emerged chieftains are organizing their disorganized bands into a genuine military threat. Regthar tasks champions of the Horde with cutting down Barak Kodobane at the Forgotten Pools before his influence can spread.",h="Kolkar Leaders begins a campaign led by the orc Regthar Deathgate to crush rising centaur warlords in the...",sec={{t="A Rising Menace in the Drylands",b="For countless years, the horse-bodied centaur have terrorized Kalimdor, driving the nomadic tauren nearly to extinction before Thrall's Horde arrived to turn the tide. In the Barrens, the dominant Kolkar tribe generally roams in scattered, fractured marauding parties. Recently, however, aggressive chieftains have begun uniting the disparate bands, turning simple raiding parties into a cohesive military threat capable of contesting the Horde's fortified outposts.",sp=0},{t="Decapitating the Beast",b="Stationed in an encampment west of the Crossroads, the orc warrior Regthar Deathgate recognized that the Kolkar rely heavily on sheer bravado and brute force to maintain cohesion. Without strong commanders, their raiders degenerate into infighting. To blunt their advance, Regthar directs Horde adventurers to cut off the head of the snake, starting with Barak Kodobane, an ambitious leader camping near the verdant waters of the Forgotten Pools.",sp=0},{t="The First of Many",b="Slaying Barak Kodobane deals a significant blow to the northern Kolkar encampments, yet Regthar knows Barak is merely the vanguard of a broader movement. His elimination marks the opening salvo of a concerted campaign to dismantle the Kolkar high command, paving the way to hunt down fellow chieftains Verog the Dervish and Hezrul Bloodmark across the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Barak Kodobane?",a="Barak Kodobane is a fierce Kolkar centaur leader who rallied marauders around the Forgotten Pools north of the Crossroads. Known for his wit and cruelty, he proved far more dangerous than ordinary nomadic raiders by organizing disparate clans into an offensive threat against the Horde.",al={"barak","who is barak","barak kodobane lore"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Barak Kodobane?",a="Barak Kodobane maintains a camp at the Forgotten Pools, a lush oasis situated north of the Crossroads in the central Barrens. He is typically surrounded by loyal Kolkar guards.",al={"barak location","where is barak","forgotten pools barak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Regthar Deathgate?",a="Regthar Deathgate is an orc veteran situated at a small bunker camp just west of the Crossroads. He monitors centaur movements in the Barrens and orchestrates pre-emptive strikes to safeguard Horde settlements from organized raids.",al={"regthar","who gives kolkar leaders","regthar deathgate lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Kolkar such a problem for the Horde?",a="The centaur have waged a ruthless, near-genocidal war against the tauren for generations. As full members of the Horde, the tauren rely on their allies to help secure their ancestral hunting grounds and trade routes across the Barrens from continued centaur expansion.",al={"why fight kolkar","kolkar threat","centaur horde rivalry"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after Barak is killed?",a="Defeating Barak Kodobane reveals that other chieftains are marshaling forces elsewhere in the Barrens. Regthar immediately sends you to assassinate Verog the Dervish at the Stagnant Oasis, followed by Hezrul Bloodmark at the Lushwater Oasis, culminating in a defense against a direct Kolkar assault.",al={"next quest after barak","kolkar leaders follow up","what comes next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why do the Kolkar gather around the oases?",a="Water and fertile ground are precious treasures in the arid climate of the Barrens. By seizing natural springs like the Forgotten Pools, the Kolkar secure essential water supplies while denying strategic resting spots to travelers and tauren hunters.",al={"why are centaur at oases","kolkar water","forgotten pools centaur"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Regthar Deathgate want the Kolkar leaders killed?",a="Centaur tribes have harassed the tauren for generations, but the Kolkar in the Barrens are usually fractured and disorganized. Recently, charismatic chieftains have begun rallying the scattered warbands into a unified threat against the Horde's settlements. Regthar knows that if these emerging commanders are allowed to organize, the Horde's foothold across the Barrens could crumble. Eliminating figures like Barak Kodobane strikes at the head of the uprising before it can overwhelm regional defenses.",al={"why kill kolkar leaders","regthar deathgate motive","why does regthar want this done"},it="motive",add="55ee765d"},{q="What is Barak's Head for?",a="Regthar requires undeniable proof that the centaur commander has fallen. In the harsh frontier of the Barrens, rumors and claims are not enough to guarantee safety. Bringing Barak's severed head confirms that the Kolkar warband encamped near the Forgotten Pools has truly lost its leader and its will to coordinate further assaults.",al={"why baraks head","baraks head purpose","what do i do with baraks head"},it="item",add="4347847a"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren, striking down Kolkar commanders is a matter of survival and vengeance. Centaur clans slaughtered tribes and drove the shu'halo from their ancestral pastures for decades before the Horde established a foothold in Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="Thrall pledged the Horde to defend the tauren, and seasoned veterans like Regthar Deathgate take that blood-oath seriously, treating centaur warmongers as immediate strategic threats to orcish sovereignty in the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="The crossroads of the Barrens serve as the vital artery connecting Mulgore, Durotar, and Horde outposts farther afield. Neutralizing Kolkar leadership protects fragile supply caravans from devastating ambushes."},kw={"barak","barrens","centaur","crossroads","deathgate","forgotten pools","kodobane","kolkar","regthar"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","subzone:forgotten-pools","quest:851","quest:852","quest:4021","topic:centaur","topic:tauren"},m={start="Regthar Deathgate",level="16",faction="Horde",id=850,ri={"Barak's Head"}},src={"Kolkar Leaders (Classic)"}}
E["quest:851"] = {t="quest",n="Verog the Dervish",z="barrens",s="Across the southern Barrens, Verog the Dervish keeps moving, and Regthar Deathgate seeks to draw him out. The orc directs Horde champions to attack the Kolkar command tent at the Stagnant Oasis, hoping to force the nomadic leader into the open.",h="Across the southern Barrens, Verog the Dervish keeps moving, and Regthar Deathgate seeks to draw him out.",sec={{t="Drawing Out the Dervish",b="After Barak Kodobane fell, Regthar Deathgate turned to the remaining Kolkar warlords. Barak had stayed near the northern waters of the Forgotten Pools, but Verog the Dervish roams the sun-baked plains and rarely lingers in one camp. Horde scouts cannot easily track him across that wide territory. Their chance is to make the commander come to them.",sp=0},{t="The Stagnant Oasis",b="Verog operates from the Kolkar command post at the Stagnant Oasis, southeast of the Crossroads. Regthar sends you against the camp, where you strike the Kolkar warriors near their command tent. Their alarm calls Verog back to defend the outpost, bringing him within reach of the Horde blades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Verog the Dervish?",a="Verog the Dervish leads the Kolkar centaur in the Barrens. He commands from the Stagnant Oasis but roams the southern wastes, making him hard to corner.",al={"who is verog","verog lore","verog the dervish"},it="target"},{q="Why doesn't Verog stay in his camp?",a="Verog wanders the Barrens rather than remaining in one camp. His movements make it hard for Horde war parties to find him, so his enemies must provoke him to return.",al={"where is verog","why does verog roam","verog missing"}},{q="How do you summon Verog?",a="Threaten Verog's tribe at the Stagnant Oasis command post. Attacking the Kolkar near their command tent raises an alarm that brings him back to defend it.",al={"how to spawn verog","find verog","verog not showing up"},gp=true},{q="Who orders Verog's death?",a="Regthar Deathgate orders Verog's death. The orc veteran camps west of the Crossroads, along the main road to the Stonetalon Mountains, and hunts the Kolkar's regional commanders one by one.",al={"who gives the quest","regthar deathgate"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after Verog falls?",a="After Verog falls, you bring his severed head to Regthar, who adds it beside Barak Kodobane's. Regthar then turns his attention to Hezrul Bloodmark, the centaur warlord at the Lushwater Oasis to the south.",al={"what comes next","after verog"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Kolkar centaur such a problem in the Barrens?",a="The Kolkar threaten the Barrens by claiming its vital water sources and raiding caravans, outposts, and native tauren herds. Their attacks endanger the Horde's fledgling presence in central Kalimdor.",al={"why fight kolkar","kolkar threat"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Regthar Deathgate want Verog killed?",a="Regthar Deathgate is systematically dismantling the Kolkar centaur leadership threatening the northern Barrens and the Crossroads. Verog the Dervish commands the centaur warband based around the Stagnant Oasis. By eliminating him along with the other Kolkar chieftains, Regthar aims to shatter their chain of command and weaken their hold on the vital oases before their forces can overwhelm Horde settlements.",al={"why kill verog","regthar deathgate motive","why does regthar want verog dead"},it="motive",add="42943e7a"},{q="What is Verog's Head used for?",a="Regthar Deathgate takes Verog's severed head as undeniable proof of the dervish's demise. He intends to mount it on a pike alongside Barak Kodobane's head at his outpost, serving both as an accounting of fallen enemy commanders and a grim warning to any Kolkar approaching along the road west of the Crossroads.",al={"verogs head purpose","what does regthar do with verogs head","why take verogs head"},it="item",add="f05e98a6"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know Regthar Deathgate sees the Kolkar warlords' defeat as essential to securing the road between the Crossroads and the Stonetalon Mountains for Durotar's travelers.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the Kolkar hunted and harassed your nomadic people across these plains for generations. Verog's execution brings long-awaited retribution.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the oases are vital to survival in the arid Barrens. Defeating centaur commanders helps keep water routes open to supply caravans."},kw={"barrens","centaur","crossroads","dervish","kolkar","regthar deathgate","stagnant oasis","verog"},rel={"quest:850","quest:852","quest:4021","quest:1361","subzone:stagnant-oasis","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","quest:877"},m={start="Regthar Deathgate",level="18",faction="Horde",id=851,ri={"Verog's Head"}},src={"Verog the Dervish (Classic)"}}
E["quest:852"] = {t="quest",n="Hezrul Bloodmark",z="barrens",s="At Lushwater Oasis, Hezrul Bloodmark directs the Kolkar incursions across the Barrens. Regthar Deathgate sends you to end his command and break the centaur's hold on the region.",h="At Lushwater Oasis, Hezrul Bloodmark directs the Kolkar incursions across the Barrens.",sec={{t="Decapitating the Kolkar",b="After Barak Kodobane and Verog the Dervish fall, Hezrul Bloodmark remains the Barrens Kolkar's paramount chieftain. Regthar Deathgate calls him brutal and cunning, the spearhead behind the centaur incursions across the savanna. The Horde hopes his death will sow chaos and fracture the Kolkar ranks beyond recovery, before they can overwhelm Horde settlements.",sp=0},{t="The Lushwater Stronghold",b="Hezrul commands his warbands from Lushwater Oasis, south of the Crossroads. The few watering holes in the Barrens are vital to survival, making this oasis a strategic hub and a staging ground for Kolkar raiders. On Hezrul's own ground, you deny the centaur their most vital stronghold and sever their hold on the southern trails.",sp=0},{t="A Dangerous Aftermath",b="Regthar commends the victory over Hezrul and notes that the centaur lack the focused discipline of orcs. Yet the Kolkar do not scatter quietly. Enraged, they rally their remaining forces and launch a desperate, full-scale assault on Regthar's encampment for bloody vengeance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Hezrul Bloodmark?",a="Hezrul Bloodmark leads the Kolkar centaur across the Barrens. Fierce, cunning, and brutal, he directs their clans and raiders from Lushwater Oasis.",al={"who is hezrul","hezrul bloodmark lore","centaur leader barrens"},it="target"},{q="Where can Hezrul Bloodmark be found?",a="Hezrul patrols the southern Barrens along the shores of Lushwater Oasis, south of the Crossroads, with Kolkar bodyguards at his side.",al={"where is hezrul","hezrul location","where to find hezrul"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to kill Hezrul?",a="Regthar Deathgate, an orc warrior, gives the order at a small camp west of the Crossroads, on the road toward the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who gives hezrul bloodmark","regthar deathgate quest","quest giver hezrul"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde want Hezrul dead?",a="The Kolkar threaten Horde trade routes and settlements. Regthar believes killing their paramount chieftain will fracture the clan's unity and greatly weaken its ability to wage coordinated war.",al={"why kill hezrul","hezrul bloodmark purpose","kolkar threat barrens"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after Hezrul is slain?",a="The surviving Kolkar refuse to surrender. They unite in fury and launch an immediate counterattack against Regthar Deathgate's outpost west of the Crossroads.",al={"counterattack after hezrul","what happens next","consequences of killing hezrul"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How does Hezrul relate to Barak and Verog?",a="Barak Kodobane and Verog the Dervish led individual oases and warbands as Kolkar subordinates. Hezrul Bloodmark commanded the entire clan across the Barrens.",al={"barak verog hezrul","kolkar chieftains","three centaur leaders"},it="ties"},{q="What is Hezrul's Head for?",a="Regthar Deathgate requires Hezrul's Head as indisputable proof that the supreme leader of the Barrens' Kolkar has fallen. Just as with Barak Kodobane and Verog the Dervish before him, bringing back the severed head confirms to the Horde that the centaur leadership has been broken and the threat disrupted.",al={"hezruls head use","why take hezruls head","hezrul head"},it="item",add="ca31e908"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you hear Regthar Deathgate judge the Kolkar by the ways of orcish warfare. The centaur are fierce, but their wild fury lacks the iron discipline honed by the Horde.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know generations of brutal displacement and bloodshed at centaur hands. Defeating warlords like Hezrul brings hard-earned retribution.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know securing the Crossroads and the Barrens means breaking the centaur's hold on the three major oases that sustain travel through the region."},kw={"bloodmark","centaur","crossroads","deathgate","hezrul","kolkar","lushwater","oasis","regthar"},rel={"quest:851","quest:4021","quest:850","subzone:lushwater-oasis","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:centaur"},m={start="Regthar Deathgate",level="19",faction="Horde",id=852,ri={"Hezrul's Head"}},src={"Hezrul Bloodmark (Classic)"}}
E["quest:854"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to the Crossroads",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Kirge Sternhorn sends travelers north to aid Thork at the Crossroads. The journey carries them from Mulgore into the Barrens and the wider struggles of the Horde.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Kirge Sternhorn sends travelers north to aid Thork at the Crossroads.",sec={{t="Leaving the Cradle",b="Camp Taurajo is where many tauren first face the Barrens beyond Mulgore. Just past the mountain pass, mystic Kirge Sternhorn watches travelers descend into the dry grasslands. When Sternhorn sees that a traveler is ready to go farther, Kirge points north along the dusty trade route toward the Crossroads.",sp=0},{t="A Shared Bond",b="The tauren of Thunder Bluff and Thrall's new Horde now share their fortunes. Kirge says the two peoples' fates are bound together, and orcs at the Crossroads need reinforcements as they struggle to establish an outpost. At the settlement, Thork welcomes travelers from even the high bluffs, ready to test their strength against the dangers of the savanna.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts Journey to the Crossroads?",a="Kirge Sternhorn, a tauren mystic at Camp Taurajo, sends travelers north. The camp lies in the southern Barrens, just east of the mountain pass from Mulgore.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","kirge sternhorn quest"},gp=true},{q="Where is Thork located?",a="Thork is inside the stockade walls at the Crossroads, the Horde settlement in the central Barrens. It lies north of Camp Taurajo along the main road.",al={"where is thork","thork location","find thork"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kirge Sternhorn send travelers to the Crossroads?",a="Kirge Sternhorn sees that a traveler is ready for greater trials and knows tauren and orcs now share an intertwined fate. The orcish garrison at the Crossroads faces constant pressure from local threats and needs capable allies.",al={"why go to crossroads","crossroads purpose","why send me to orcs"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Crossroads?",a="The Crossroads is the Horde's main strategic hub and trading post in central Kalimdor. Major north-south and east-west trails meet there, and the settlement is a base for bringing order to the wild frontier.",al={"what is the crossroads","crossroads settlement","barrens hub"},it="place"},{q="Do only tauren receive this task?",a="Yes. Kirge Sternhorn sends only tauren on this journey, welcoming kin from as far as Thunder Bluff and directing them to report to Thork.",al={"is this quest tauren only","horde breadcrumb"},gp=true},{q="What threats await along the road to the Crossroads?",a="The road north crosses dry plains where aggressive plainstriders, prowling savanna lions, and roaming bands of Razormane quilboar roam. Keeping to the beaten path helps travelers avoid the more territorial predators of the central savanna.",al={"is the road dangerous","taurajo to crossroads path"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Kirge Sternhorn choose you for this journey?",a="Kirge Sternhorn foresees your coming and recognizes that you have grown beyond local trials. Sensing that you are destined for greater deeds across the lands of the Horde, he sees you as the right emissary to step forward and aid your orc allies.",al={"why me journey crossroads","why does kirge pick me","why send me to crossroads"},it="why_me",add="fc69c860"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you leave the shelter of the Earthmother's sacred mesa and enter the wider struggles of the Horde.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know Thork needs reinforcements from the south to hold the ground Thrall's scouts have secured across the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see cooperation grow between the tribes of Thunder Bluff and the warchief's vanguard in central Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","crossroads","earthmother","kirge sternhorn","thork","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:thork","npc:kirge-sternhorn","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Kirge Sternhorn",["end"]="Thork",level="12",faction="Horde",id=854},src={"Journey to the Crossroads"}}
E["quest:855"] = {t="quest",n="Centaur Bracers",z="barrens",s="West of the Crossroads, Regthar Deathgate calls for Centaur Bracers. Kolkar centaurs contest the central Barrens, threatening Horde control of the plains.",h="West of the Crossroads, Regthar Deathgate calls for Centaur Bracers.",sec={{t="Securing the Plains",b="The young Horde is fighting to secure territory across Kalimdor. The Barrens lie between Durotar and Mulgore, but Kolkar centaurs contest its watering holes and open plains. They attack supply trains and scouting parties. Regthar Deathgate, an orc warrior, directs the defense from his bunker west of the Crossroads.",sp=0},{t="A Gruesome Accounting",b="Regthar asks for proof that Kolkar warriors have fallen. Soldiers who enter Kolkar territory bring back bracers taken from slain centaurs. The trophies verify claims for Horde bounties and are meant to frighten surviving Kolkar raiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Regthar Deathgate?",a="Regthar Deathgate is an orc commander in a fortified bunker west of the Crossroads. He leads the Horde's efforts to suppress centaur raiders across the Barrens.",al={"who is regthar","regthar deathgate lore","who gives centaur bracers"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Horde want centaur bracers?",a="Centaur bracers prove that enemy warriors were slain in the field. Regthar uses them to ensure bounties go only to those who inflict actual casualties on the hostile Kolkar tribes.",al={"why bracers","what are centaur bracers for","why collect bracers"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Kolkar attacking the Horde?",a="The Kolkar are a brutal centaur clan native to central Kalimdor, and they seek to expand. They claim the Barrens as hunting grounds and fight the new settlements, camps, and alliances formed by orcs and tauren.",al={"why do centaur hate horde","centaur conflict","kolkar aggression"},it="conflict"},{q="Where are the Kolkar centaurs located in the Barrens?",a="Kolkar raiding camps lie around oases and rugged ridges across the central and southern Barrens. The centaurs often dispute access to water and routes through the region.",al={"where to find centaurs","kolkar locations","centaur camps"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does collecting these bracers stop the Kolkar attacks?",a="No. Regthar hopes the losses will frighten surviving raiders, but he doubts the Kolkar will willingly stop their attacks.",al={"did centaur bracers work","do the centaur stop"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the strategic value of the Crossroads?",a="The Crossroads links Durotar, the tauren plains of Mulgore, and northern routes into Ashenvale. Defeating nearby centaur war parties helps keep Horde supply lines intact.",al={"why defend crossroads","crossroads importance"},it="place"},{q="Why does Regthar Deathgate want centaur bracers collected?",a="Regthar Deathgate views the Kolkar centaur as a direct threat to the Horde's foothold across the Barrens. By offering a bounty on their bracers, he aims to thin their fighting ranks through sheer attrition, hoping the heavy losses will strike fear into the surviving clans and blunt their ongoing assaults.",al={"why does regthar want bracers","regthar deathgate motive","why centaur bracers"},it="motive",add="5627e76a"},{q="Who are the Kolkar centaurs you are sent to fight?",a="You are dispatched against the Kolkar clan, a brutal breed of centaur that dominates key oases throughout the central and southern Barrens. Fiercely territorial and bloodthirsty, they wage war against both the tauren and the newly arrived orcs to drive the Horde completely from Kalimdor's plains.",al={"who are the kolkar","what centaurs are in the barrens","who is the target centaur bracers"},it="target",add="566bd14b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing Kolkar protects supply links between Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the centaur have devastated and committed genocide against tauren tribes for centuries. Thinning their numbers in the Barrens is personal retribution.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, securing Durotar's borders against nomadic raiders helps establish a permanent, stable homeland."},kw={"barrens","bounty","bracers","centaur","crossroads","horde","kolkar","regthar deathgate"},rel={"quest:1361","topic:centaur","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:horde"},m={start="Regthar Deathgate",level="14",faction="Horde",id=855,ri={"Centaur Bracers"}},src={"Centaur Bracers (Classic)"}}
E["quest:857"] = {t="quest",n="The Tear of the Moons",z="barrens",s="At Bael Modan, a relic called the Tear of the Moons has left Feegly the Exiled mad and obsessed. General Twinbraid has locked it away as a curse, but Feegly still demands its return.",h="At Bael Modan, a relic called the Tear of the Moons has left Feegly the Exiled mad and obsessed.",sec={{t="Unearthed at Bael Modan",b="The dwarves found the Tear of the Moons while cutting into the southern Kalimdor hills for Bael Modan. It was their first major discovery, and its strange influence fell at once on Feegly, one of the expedition's workers.",sp=0},{t="Twinbraid's Quarantine",b="Feegly claimed the Tear granted him immense power and turned violently on his comrades to protect it. General Twinbraid saw the relic's corrupting hold, called it cursed, took it from Feegly, and secured it in the keep. Banished from the excavation camp, Feegly took refuge among the cliffs. Bitter and obsessed, he begs passing travelers to steal the Tear back.",sp=0},{t="The Terrible Cost",b="General Twinbraid's warnings prove true when Feegly recovers the Tear of the Moons. The relic's hidden transformative magic consumes him, changing the dwarf into a feral trogg. His life ends seconds after he reclaims the prize.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tear of the Moons?",a="The Tear of the Moons is a potent relic found by dwarven excavators during their early digs at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens. It corrupts those who handle it and fills them with an intoxicating desire for power.",al={"what is tear of the moons","tear of the moons relic","bael modan artifact"},it="item"},{q="Who is Feegly the Exiled?",a="Feegly the Exiled was an excavator with General Twinbraid's expedition at Bael Modan. After the Tear of the Moons was found, he grew obsessed and violent, and Twinbraid cast him out of the keep.",al={"who is feegly","feegly lore","feegly dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="Why does General Twinbraid lock the Tear away?",a="General Twinbraid locked the Tear away because he recognized it as a dangerous curse. After Feegly turned on his fellow excavators, Twinbraid secured the relic inside Bael Modan's keep.",al={"why twinbraid locked tear","twinbraid curse","bael modan keep relic"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens when you return the Tear to Feegly?",a="Returning the Tear satisfies Feegly's demand, but what follows is not yet known.",al={"what happens to feegly","feegly ending","return the tear"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is the Tear's magic fully understood?",a="General Twinbraid calls the Tear cursed, while Feegly craves the power he believes it grants. Its magic remains unexplained.",al={"tear magic","tear of the moons curse","how does the tear work"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="Why is this a Horde quest if Feegly is a dwarf?",a="Feegly is an outcast hiding in the Barrens, where he despises the Alliance forces occupying Bael Modan. He appeals to Horde adventurers, who are hostile to Twinbraid's excavation, to raid the keep and recover the relic.",al={"why horde quest","is feegly horde","bael modan horde"},it="side"},{q="Why does Feegly the Exiled want the Tear of the Moons returned?",a="Feegly is completely obsessed with the Tear of the Moons. Unearthed at Bael Modan, the artifact imparted a strange, intoxicating power to him before General Twinbraid declared it cursed and took it away. Twinbraid banished Feegly from the excavation site entirely after violent disputes broke out over the relic. Consumed by paranoia and craving the power he briefly held, Feegly is desperate to reclaim what he believes is rightfully his.",al={"why does feegly want the tear","feegly motive","why feegly the exiled wants the tear"},it="motive",add="76d5a92c"},{q="Why does Feegly ask you instead of retrieving the Tear of the Moons himself?",a="General Twinbraid forcibly banished Feegly from Bael Modan and locked the artifact deep inside the fortress. Feegly is an outcast and persona non grata to his fellow dwarves; the moment he stepped foot back inside the keep, Twinbraid's guards would arrest or strike him down. Unable to infiltrate his former home alone, he turns to an outside adventurer to sneak in and steal it for him.",al={"why feegly needs you","why can't feegly get the tear himself","why does feegly need my help"},it="why_me",add="7effe162"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Striking Bael Modan to recover the relic gives the Horde a chance to disrupt dwarven operations that infringe on the Barrens."},kw={"bael modan","barrens","dwarf curse","feegly","feegly the exiled","general twinbraid","tear of the moons"},rel={"npc:feegly-the-exiled","subzone:bael-modan","topic:trogg","zone:barrens"},m={start="Feegly the Exiled",level="30",faction="Horde",id=857,ri={"Tear of the Moons"}},src={"The Tear of the Moons"}}
E["quest:858"] = {t="quest",n="Ignition",z="barrens",s="At a Venture Company camp in the northern Barrens, a trapped pilot needs an ignition key before their cover fails. The operative hijacked a shredder without its key and needs someone to fetch it from the site supervisor.",h="At a Venture Company camp in the northern Barrens, a trapped pilot needs an ignition key before their cover...",sec={{t="A Heist Gone Sideways",b="A spy sent by Sputtervalve has slipped into a Venture Company shredder at the northern Barrens drilling grounds. The operative means to seize the machine and study how it works. But the steering and movement column stays locked without its ignition key.",sp=0},{t="Bluffing Under Pressure",b="A goblin worker has noticed the shredder sitting idle, so the hijacker bluffs that its engine has failed. Trapped beneath the glass canopy with workers nearby, the operative points you toward the central derrick. The supervisor keeps spare ignition keys in the upper control office, the only way out before the bluff fails.",sp=0},{t="Corporate Jealousy",b="The key turns, and the thief studies the shredder's controls. Its precise arm levers, rotation controls, and stability dampeners surpass the clumsy machines operating out of Ratchet. The machine is now a prize of industrial espionage as well as the pilot's way to survive.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is inside the shredder?",a="An operative connected to Sputtervalve, an engineer in Ratchet, is inside the shredder. The pilot entered the Venture Company operation to steal one of its advanced wood-clearing machines.",al={"shredder pilot","who is in wizzlecrank shredder","wizzlecrank"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't the shredder simply drive away?",a="The shredder's movement column is locked without its ignition key. The hijacker reached the cockpit, but the machine cannot move until the key unlocks its drive controls.",al={"why need key","why stuck","shredder locked"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Ignition Key found?",a="The Venture Company supervisor has the ignition key. The supervisor is in the control room atop the nearby wooden derrick.",al={"ignition key location","where is supervisor","how to find key"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ratchet want a Venture Company shredder?",a="Ratchet wants a Venture Company shredder because its engineering outclasses the standard models used there. An intact machine could let local tinkerers study its arm controls, speed regulators, and stability systems.",al={"why steal shredder","ratchet shredder","sputtervalve shredder"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin engineer and operative in Ratchet. Sputtervalve watches the Venture Company's expansion and seeks its mechanical innovations.",al={"sputtervalve identity","who sent wizzlecrank","sputtervalve ratchet"},it="people"},{q="What happens after the shredder is started?",a="Turning the key unlocks the shredder's movement systems. The pilot then tries to drive the hijacked machine out of the hostile drilling camp and back to safety, with an escort operation underway.",al={"what next ignition","after ignition key","ignition follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizzlecrank need this done right away?",a="Wizzlecrank snuck into the Venture Company drill site to commandeer one of their advanced shredders for Ratchet, only to find himself trapped in the cockpit without the starting mechanism. Worse, when another operator approached him, he panicked and bluffed that the machine had suffered mechanical failure. It is only a matter of time before the crew returns or sees through his lie, turning a quiet heist into an execution if he cannot start the engine and flee immediately.",al={"wizzlecrank motive","why hurry ignition","why does wizzlecrank need the key"},it="motive",add="52fc6a42"},{q="Who holds the key to the shredder?",a="The key is kept by the Venture Company supervisor stationed high in the control room atop the derrick. The Venture Company maintains ruthless oversight across their logging and drilling operations in the Barrens, keeping critical controls out of ordinary laborers' hands to prevent theft and sabotage. Taking the key means infiltrating their command post and confronting the supervisor managing the entire site.",al={"who has the ignition key","venture co supervisor key","who holds ignition key"},it="target",add="edef521b"},{q="Why does Wizzlecrank need you to get the key instead of retrieving it himself?",a="Wizzlecrank is trapped inside the cockpit surrounded by suspicious Venture Company workers. If he climbs out and scurries across the camp toward the command derrick, he will immediately blow his cover and alert the entire work site. He has to stay inside and pretend to inspect the broken controls while relying on an outsider capable of carving a path up to the supervisor's perch.",al={"why can't wizzlecrank get the key","why does wizzlecrank need help","why me wizzlecrank"},it="why_me",add="e6f51bdb"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Venture Company's shredder uses precise arm controls and responsive rotation governors, beyond the usual tinkering in Ratchet.",["faction:Horde"]="The Venture Company's reckless deforestation threatens the northern Barrens. Sabotaging or stealing its heavy machinery disrupts that work."},kw={"derrick","ignition","ignition key","ratchet","shredder","sputtervalve","the barrens","venture company","wizzlecrank"},rel={"npc:wizzlecrank-s-shredder","quest:114","npc:sputtervalve","topic:venture-company","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Wizzlecrank's Shredder",level="18",id=858,ri={"Ignition Key"}},src={"Ignition (Classic)"}}
E["quest:862"] = {t="quest",n="Dig Rat Stew",z="barrens",s="Grub waits east of the Crossroads, hungry for a pot of dig rat stew. He sends travelers to Bael Modan in the southern Barrens to bring back dig rats for his recipe.",h="Grub waits east of the Crossroads, hungry for a pot of dig rat stew.",sec={{t="Barrens Delicacies",b="Across the dry Barrens, hunters bring down zhevras, plainstriders, and raptors. Grub, an orc camping east of the Crossroads, craves something different: dig rats. He says he is hungry all day and offers to share his recipe with any traveler willing to catch the burrowing rodents.",sp=0},{t="The Dwarven Vermin",b="Bael Modan lies deep in the southern Barrens, where dwarven prospectors dig into the red earth. Their work has disturbed nests of dig rats. The dwarves see the small rodents as an infestation, while Grub sees a feast close to the excavation.",sp=0},{t="A Matter of Flavor",b="Grub says dig rats taste best after rotting for several weeks. For a hungry traveler who wants food now, he accepts fresher meat. His recipe shows how forgiving roadside cooking can be on Kalimdor's frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grub?",a="Grub is an orc camping along the trail east of the Crossroads in the Barrens. He is always hungry, has peculiar tastes, and will teach travelers to cook local vermin.",al={"grub","who is grub","orc east of crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="Where do dig rats come from?",a="Dig rats infest Bael Modan, an Alliance excavation in the far southern Barrens, south of Camp Taurajo and north of Razorfen Kraul. The dwarves' mining disturbed the ground and brought swarms of the small creatures.",al={"where are dig rats","dig rat location","find dig rats"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Grub want dig rats specifically?",a="Grub calls dig rats everyone's favorite feast and says hunting vermin is a rite of passage for seasoned travelers. They are the main ingredient in his hearty, pungent stew.",al={"why rats","why dig rats","grub motivation"},it="motive"},{q="Is Dig Rat Stew actually good to eat?",a="Grub calls it delicious, though his taste is extreme. He prefers the meat after it has rotted for a few weeks, making the stew an acquired taste even by rugged Horde standards.",al={"does the stew taste good","eating dig rats","grub recipe flavor"}},{q="Why are there dwarves in Bael Modan?",a="The dwarves of Bael Modan are an Ironforge expedition. They built a keep and excavation in the southern Barrens, blasting and digging deep into the land; their presence has heightened tensions with the Horde and stirred up native vermin.",al={"dwarves in the barrens","why bael modan","alliance southern barrens"},it="place"},{q="Do you need special culinary training to make the stew?",a="Grub's method calls for basic hearthcraft and field dressing. Anyone with rudimentary cooking experience can learn to simmer the rodents into a sustaining meal.",al={"cooking requirement","do i need cooking skill"},gp=true},{q="What is the Dig Rat used for?",a="Dig rats are the key ingredient in Grub's savory concoction. While most folk turn up their noses at vermin, Grub considers them prime culinary fare and simmers them down into a thick stew. Though he privately prefers letting them rot for a few weeks to draw out their ripe, pungent flavor, he will happily cook fresh catches on the spot for hungry wanderers across the arid Barrens.",al={"dig rat use","what is dig rat for","why collect dig rats"},it="item",add="76cb3c44"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Preparing dig rat stew teaches frontier foraging: quarry vermin become a filling, foul-smelling campfire meal.",["faction:Horde"]="Taking dig rats from Bael Modan offers a way to mock the dwarven excavation while gathering rations in the southern Barrens.",["race:Undead"]="Grub likes to let meat rot for weeks before boiling it, a taste few living cooks share with the Forsaken."},kw={"bael modan","barrens","cooking","crossroads","dig rat stew","dwarves","grub","rats"},rel={"npc:grub","subzone:bael-modan","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:razorfenkraul","topic:horde"},m={start="Grub",level="23",faction="Horde",id=862,ri={"Dig Rat (item)"}},src={"Dig Rat Stew (quest)"}}
E["quest:863"] = {t="quest",n="The Escape",z="barrens",s="You help Wizzlecrank flee the Venture Company drill site at the Sludge Fen in the northern Barrens. Trapped in a stolen prototype shredder, the goblin pilot needs protection from company mercenaries as he climbs from the industrial pit. Afterward, you report to his contact, Sputtervalve, in Ratchet.",h="You help Wizzlecrank flee the Venture Company drill site at the Sludge Fen in the northern Barrens.",sec={{t="A Clumsy Getaway",b="Wizzlecrank struggles to control the stolen shredder at the Sludge Fen. He has lit the prototype deep inside the Venture Company drill site, but knows little of its levers and switches. The heavy machine lurches across the muddy quarry floor, and its erratic driving and roaring joints alert nearby laborers and armed guards. A stealthy escape becomes a running battle up the excavation pit’s western ramp.",sp=0},{t="Venture Company Pursuit",b="The Venture Company sends mercenaries to stop the stolen prototype. As the machine claws up the slope toward open ground, squads move to intercept and disable it. The shredder lashes out, but cannot withstand their sabotage without your protection. It clears the rim and staggers from the main drilling depression, though the machine soon suffers a critical failure.",sp=0},{t="Salvage and Payoff",b="Wizzlecrank escapes the wrecked prototype shredder alive. Once clear of immediate danger, the machine breaks down and collapses on the savanna turf. Wizzlecrank scrambles out and tells you to report to Sputtervalve in Ratchet while he stays with the wreckage. Eager to study the Venture Company's designs before his opportunity closes, Sputtervalve immediately sends a goblin salvage squad to haul the intact mechanisms back to port.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Wizzlecrank and why is he inside a shredder?",a="Wizzlecrank is an operative and mechanic working with Sputtervalve in Ratchet. He entered the Venture Company's northern drill site to steal its latest experimental shredder prototype, then became trapped while learning its unfamiliar cockpit controls.",al={"who is wizzlecrank","why is goblin in shredder","wizzlecrank shredder"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this escape take place?",a="The escape begins deep inside the Sludge Fen, a fouled industrial drilling site run by the Venture Company in the northern Barrens, just north of the dry savanna basin.",al={"where is the escape quest","escape location","sludge fen escort"},it="place"},{q="Do you have to escort the shredder all the way to Ratchet?",a="No. You escort Wizzlecrank out of the drill pit depression and up the western ramp. Once clear of the quarry rim, the machine breaks down, and Wizzlecrank tells you to report to Ratchet on your own.",al={"how far do i walk","escort path","do you go to ratchet"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin technician stationed near Ratchet's docks. He gathers industrial intelligence against the rival Venture Company and seeks its mechanical designs to profit from its technological innovations.",al={"who is sputtervalve","turn in npc sputtervalve","sputtervalve lore"},it="people"},{q="Why does the shredder fall over at the end?",a="Wizzlecrank barely knows the controls, and the experimental machine is pushed to its limits in the ambush. It suffers severe mechanical strain breaking through the perimeter, then gives out as soon as it clears the drill site.",al={"why shredder break","shredder wrecked","prototype failure"},sp=1},{q="What happens after the prototype crashes?",a="Wizzlecrank stays with the downed machine while you report to Sputtervalve in Ratchet. Sputtervalve immediately prepares a goblin salvage team to harvest the prototype's valuable components before the Venture Company can reclaim them.",al={"salvage crew","what happens next","escape quest conclusion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizzlecrank need to escape the Sludge Fen?",a="Wizzlecrank stole an experimental prototype shredder right from under the noses of the Venture Company. Trapped deep inside hostile territory at the drill site, he has to pilot the unfamiliar, clunky war machine through rings of angry mercenaries and drudges to survive and deliver the stolen technology to his partner in Ratchet.",al={"why escape sludge fen","wizzlecrank motive","why flee venture co"},it="motive",add="07b3d38e"},{q="Why does Wizzlecrank rely on you to escort him out?",a="Operating the stolen prototype takes all of Wizzlecrank's focus—he barely knows which levers and buttons make it move, let alone fight effectively. Surrounded by hostile Venture Company forces and unable to defend himself while steering the lumbering contraption out of the drill site, he relies entirely on your blade and spellcraft to keep attackers at bay.",al={"why does wizzlecrank need me","why cant wizzlecrank escape alone","why an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="fce70664"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The prototype shredder shows Venture Company pneumatics and cockpit designs, giving engineers valuable insight to study in its salvage.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize Wizzlecrank's willingness to pilot a volatile machine on guesswork. Goblin tinkerers, like gnomish ones, often tinker first and ask questions later.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can welcome disruption to the Venture Company's polluting oil operations at the Sludge Fen, an eyesore on the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","escort","ignition","prototype","ratchet","shredder","sludge fen","sputtervalve","venture co","wizzlecrank"},rel={"quest:858","npc:wizzlecrank-s-shredder","npc:sputtervalve","subzone:sludge-fen","subzone:ratchet","quest:764","topic:goblin","zone:barrens"},m={start="Wizzlecrank's Shredder",["end"]="Sputtervalve",level="18",id=863},src={"The Escape (Classic)"}}
E["quest:865"] = {t="quest",n="Raptor Horns",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix wants intact raptor horns for a scheme of his own. The goblin believes the cunning of Barrens raptors lies in their horns and hires travelers to hunt Sunscale Scytheclaws.",h="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix wants intact raptor horns for a scheme of his own.",sec={{t="Goblin Entrepreneurship",b="Mebok Mizzyrix looks for fortune in Ratchet, where goblins chase one scheme after another. He has watched the Barrens raptors act with unusual craft and coordination compared with beasts elsewhere. Mebok decided their intelligence must be held in their horns. He has no formal inquiry in mind; he wants to put this idea to profit.",sp=0},{t="The Sunscale Scytheclaws",b="Mebok wants undamaged horns from Sunscale Scytheclaws, among the Barrens' deadliest predators. They prowl the southern stretches of the Barrens and the northern borders near Ashenvale. The raptors hunt in packs and defend their territory fiercely, so bringing down one and taking its horns intact calls for considerable skill in battle.",sp=0},{t="A Recipe for Riches",b="Mebok plans to grind the intact horns into fine powder and brew the powder into drinks. He calls the concoctions “smart drinks” and hopes to sell them to patrons eager to buy wit in a bottle. Mebok is convinced the scheme will make him wealthy overnight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix want raptor horns?",a="Mebok believes the cunning of Barrens raptors is stored in their horns. He plans to grind them into powder, brew “smart drinks,” and sell them for profit.",al={"why raptor horns","mebok goal","what does mebok want"},it="motive"},{q="Where are Sunscale Scytheclaws located?",a="Sunscale Scytheclaws roam the southern Barrens and the northern stretches near the Ashenvale border.",al={"where are scytheclaws","sunscale scytheclaw location","raptor horn location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are raptor horns actually magical or mind-enhancing?",a="Mebok's claim that raptor horns hold their wit is goblin pseudoscience driven by profit. The Barrens raptors are cunning, but the entry gives no grounds to call their horns magical or mind-enhancing.",al={"do smart drinks work","are raptors smart","raptor intelligence lore"},it="power"},{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is an ambitious goblin merchant in Ratchet, the port town. He pursues dubious schemes and concoctions to make a fortune from travelers passing through.",al={"who is mebok","mebok mizzyrix lore","mebok ratchet"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after collecting the horns?",a="Mebok plans to grind the intact horns into powder and brew them into drinks he calls “smart drinks.”",al={"next quest after raptor horns","smart drinks quest","raptor horns chain"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can Alliance players help Mebok with this task?",a="Yes. Ratchet is an open port managed by the Steamwheedle Cartel, and Mebok is a neutral goblin who does business with both the Horde and the Alliance.",al={"is this quest horde only","alliance raptor horns","can alliance do raptor horns"},gp=true},{q="What is the Intact Raptor Horn for?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix intends to grind the intact horns down into fine powder and mix them with wine. Convinced that the Barrens raptors store their cunning intellect directly inside their horns, he plans to bottle and sell the concoction as an intellectual booster called a 'smart drink,' aiming to make a massive profit off gullible buyers.",al={"intact raptor horn use","why intact raptor horns","raptor horn purpose"},it="item",add="3bee14c6"},{q="What are Sunscale Scytheclaws and why hunt them?",a="Sunscale scytheclaws are aggressive, cunning raptors native to the arid expanses of the Barrens, roaming both the southern reaches and the northern plains near the border of Ashenvale. Known for exceptional coordination and viciousness compared to other wild beasts, their remarkable sharpness makes them Mebok's prime target for harvesting intellect-boosting horn powder.",al={"sunscale scytheclaws","why sunscale raptors","sunscale scytheclaw lore"},it="target",add="5cf02a79"},{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix hire you instead of hunting the raptors himself?",a="Mebok is an ambitious goblin entrepreneur, not a seasoned tracker or big-game hunter. Venturing into the harsh plains of the Barrens to duel deadly, razor-clawed beasts is far too risky when he can simply pay an adventurer to brave the wilderness and fetch pristine specimens while he keeps his hands clean and concocts his product in safety.",al={"why me mebok","why does mebok need me","why hire an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="57350450"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter familiar with Kalimdor's raptor packs, you know their deadly cunning. Mebok's belief that their wit can be bottled is goblin quackery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can find a neutral foothold in the Horde-dominated Barrens at Ratchet. Odd jobs like Mebok's offer a chance to earn coin and Steamwheedle favor."},kw={"barrens","intact raptor horn","mebok mizzyrix","raptor horns","ratchet","smart drinks","steamwheedle cartel","sunscale scytheclaw"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","quest:1491","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale"},m={level="18",id=865,ri={"Intact Raptor Horn"}},src={"Raptor Horns"}}
E["quest:867"] = {t="quest",n="Harpy Raiders",z="barrens",s="Witchwing harpies strike supply caravans on the northwestern trails of the Barrens. Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads sends you to hunt their raiders and roguefeathers, taking their talons as proof.",h="Witchwing harpies strike supply caravans on the northwestern trails of the Barrens.",sec={{t="Threat from Above",b="Witchwing harpies strike caravans crossing the Barrens. From rocky crags in the northwest, they swoop on merchant trains and supply wagons. They kill pack animals and seize goods bound for orcish outposts, making each journey through the region dangerous.",sp=0},{t="Darsok's Plan",b="Darsok Swiftdagger, an orc rogue, has spent days watching the flock's habits and ranks. He believes an unfocused assault on their mountain roosts would scatter them. His plan is to break the Witchwing from the lowest rank upward, starting with the raiders before turning to their commanders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde targeting the Witchwing harpies?",a="Witchwing harpies nest in the northwestern crags of the Barrens and regularly attack Horde supply caravans traveling the main trails.",al={"why kill harpies","witchwing problem","why attack harpies"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Darsok Swiftdagger?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger is an orc scout and rogue stationed at the Crossroads. He watches local threats and has studied the harpy flock's chain of command to plan a deliberate attack.",al={"darsok","darsok swiftdagger lore","who is darsok"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Darsok want Witchwing talons?",a="Darsok wants the severed talons as proof of each kill. He collects them as trophies and to confirm that the flock's lowest raiding ranks are shrinking.",al={"why talons","harpy talons purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where are these harpies located?",a="The harpies roost in thorn-choked bluffs and ravines in the far northwestern Barrens, north of the road to Stonetalon.",al={"where to find harpies","witchwing location","harpy raiders location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after culling these raiders?",a="After the raiders and roguefeathers are thinned, Darsok directs you toward higher ranks in the flock, including its lieutenants and matron.",al={"next quest","after harpy raiders","what comes next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are the harpies working for anyone else?",a="The Witchwing harpies are wild, territorial scavengers who answer to their roost matron, Serena Bloodfeather, rather than an outside faction.",al={"who leads the harpies","harpy allegiance","witchwing leaders"},it="allies"},{q="Who are the Witchwing harpies?",a="The Witchwing are a flock of vicious, avian humanoids nesting in the crags and canyons of the northwest Barrens. Known for their shrieking savagery, they descend from the bluffs to ambush travelers and loot Horde caravans passing through the dry plains. Darsok has identified their rank-and-file raiders, including the Witchwing Roguefeathers, as the foundation of their flock's raiding power.",al={"witchwing harpies target","who are the harpies","witchwing roguefeathers"},it="target",add="8e2506f2"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Keeping the Barrens' interior routes secure helps supply the newly established outposts and keep them united under Orgrimmar's banners.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can appreciate Darsok Swiftdagger's method: scout the target, study its ranks, and eliminate its leadership piece by piece."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","darsok","harpy","roguefeather","swiftdagger","talons","witchwing"},rel={"quest:875","quest:876","quest:1060","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:harpy"},m={start="Darsok Swiftdagger",level="15",faction="Horde",id=867,ri={"Witchwing Talon"}},src={"Harpy Raiders (Classic)"}}
E["quest:868"] = {t="quest",n="Egg Hunt",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, Korran seeks silithid eggs for study. The Horde scholar at the Crossroads has heard of intelligent insect creatures in the south and wants intact eggs brought to Orgrimmar.",h="Across the Barrens, Korran seeks silithid eggs for study.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Crossroads",b="Korran watches the Barrens from the Crossroads and reports to Orgrimmar. While the Horde faces tribal conflicts and Alliance incursions, he studies strange changes in the land. Intelligent, hive-minded insect creatures have begun burrowing into the southern Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Excavating the Swarm",b="Korran needs samples to learn where the silithid come from and what drives them. With an excavation claw, you go to the Field of Giants and take intact eggs from the dirt mounds. Disturbing a mound draws the nearby brood to defend it, showing the swarm's uncanny coordination.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Egg Hunt quest?",a="Korran gives the work at the Crossroads in the Barrens. The troll watches the region's plants, animals, and strange changes for his patrons in Orgrimmar.",al={"quest giver","korran location","who starts egg hunt"},gp=true},{q="Where are the silithid eggs found?",a="Silithid eggs lie in dirt mounds at the Field of Giants in the southern Barrens. The mounds gather around hive tunnels in the land.",al={"egg location","where to find eggs","field of giants eggs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tool is needed to collect the eggs?",a="Korran provides a Digging Claw to lift the eggs without breaking their shells. You return it with twelve undamaged eggs.",al={"digging tool","digging claw","how to get eggs"},gp=true},{q="What makes these insects different from typical beasts?",a="Silithid act with eerie coordination and cunning. Korran has found their intelligence far beyond that of ordinary animals, as if they share a purpose.",al={"why are silithid special","insect intelligence","silithid nature"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Orgrimmar want silithid eggs?",a="Orgrimmar wants to learn about unknown threats near Horde lands. Studying the eggs can reveal how silithid grow, their strengths, and their biology before the infestation spreads.",al={"orgrimmar silithid study","why study eggs","korran purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you disturb an egg mound?",a="Disturbing a silithid mound agitates the swarm. Nearby silithid attack to protect the brood.",al={"mound ambush","silithid defenders"},gp=true},{q="What is the Silithid Egg used for?",a="Korran was stationed at the Crossroads by his superiors in Orgrimmar to observe the Barrens and report on its emerging threats. Little is known about the insectoid silithid swarming the southern reaches, and whole intact eggs provide the raw biological material required to study their growth, physiology, and origins before the colony spreads further.",al={"silithid egg use","why collect silithid eggs","silithid egg barrens purpose"},it="item",add="cd75534e"},{q="What are the silithid in the Field of Giants?",a="The silithid are an alien, highly aggressive breed of insectoid creatures burrowing across the southern Barrens. Unlike ordinary beasts that act purely on animal instinct, these creatures demonstrate an unsettling collective intelligence and organized hives, making their sudden presence in the Field of Giants a severe concern for the Horde.",al={"what are the silithid","field of giants bugs","silithid barrens target"},it="target",add="2bb4e4c0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde depends on scouts like Korran to watch Kalimdor's harsh lands. Their reports help uncover strange threats before they endanger Durotar and Mulgore.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you know primeval creatures can be dangerous. The silithid are no ordinary bugs, and Korran is wary of their calculating minds."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","digging claw","egg hunt","field of giants","korran","silithid"},rel={"npc:korran","subzone:field-of-giants","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Korran",level="22",faction="Horde",id=868,ri={"Silithid Egg (The Barrens)"}},src={"Egg Hunt (Classic)"}}
E["quest:8680"] = {t="quest",n="Windtotem the Elder",z="barrens",s="During the Lunar Festival, Windtotem the Elder receives travelers on a bluff above Ratchet. She welcomes those who honor the wisdom of ages past and offers an ancestral blessing and guidance to other elders across Kalimdor.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Windtotem the Elder receives travelers on a bluff above Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Vigil Over the Bay",b="On a grassy hill just northwest of Ratchet’s flight master, Windtotem the Elder watches over the goblin docks and open sea. Iron, gunpowder, and coin pass through the harbor below, while quiet Barrens winds and a shaft of celestial light reach the elder.",sp=0},{t="Wisdom Across the Barrens",b="During the Lunar Festival, Windtotem the Elder guides wandering mortals, as do the other ancestral spirits. Those who seek her receive her blessing and a token of her favor, along with whispers pointing to nearby elders across the continent, including Elder Runetotem and Elder Bloodhoof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Windtotem located?",a="Windtotem the Elder stands on a hill just northwest of Ratchet’s flight master, overlooking the harbor in the Barrens.",al={"windtotem location","where is windtotem","elder windtotem ratchet map"}},{q="What is the purpose of seeking out Elder Windtotem?",a="During the Lunar Festival, travelers seek Windtotem the Elder to honor an ancestor. She grants you a Coin of Ancestry and tells you where to find other spirits across the land.",al={"why talk to windtotem","windtotem elder purpose","what does windtotem do"}},{q="Why is there a beam of light shining down on her?",a="The Lunar Festival’s manifested ancestors each stand in a distinct pillar of celestial moonlight, marking their presence between the ancestral realm and the living world.",al={"beam of light elder","why is windtotem glowing","light shining on elder"}},{q="Can Alliance and Horde players both speak to Elder Windtotem?",a="Yes. Ratchet is a neutral port administered by the Steamwheedle Cartel, and the Lunar Festival elders welcome both Alliance and Horde members.",al={"can alliance talk to windtotem","is windtotem neutral","horde and alliance elder"}},{q="Which other elders does Elder Windtotem tell you about?",a="Windtotem the Elder gives guidance about nearby ancestors, including Elder Bloodhoof, Elder Runetotem, Elder Morningdew, Elder Darkhorn, Elder High Mountain, Elder Moonwarden, and Elder Proudhorn.",al={"elders windtotem mentions","who does windtotem point to"}},{q="What happens when you complete homage to the elder?",a="When you approach and honor Windtotem the Elder, she praises your spirit for burning brightly with life, accepts your respect, and gives you a Coin of Ancestry.",al={"elder windtotem turn in","what does elder windtotem say"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor an ancestor of the ancient Windtotem lineage above the goblin harbor, connecting you to the ancestral memory of the plains.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share in the Lunar Festival’s celebration of communion with the natural and celestial cycles guarded by the Cenarion Circle.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you honor the dead and tend the land’s spiritual health when you speak with ancestor spirits near elemental crossings."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","elder windtotem","lunar festival","ratchet","the barrens","windtotem the elder"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","npc:elder-runetotem","npc:elder-bloodhoof","npc:elder-morningdew","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Windtotem",id=8680},src={"Windtotem the Elder"}}
E["quest:869"] = {t="quest",n="Raptor Thieves",z="barrens",s="A raptor has stolen the guards' payroll from the Crossroads tower, leaving the defenders baffled. Gazrog calls for a cull to keep the beasts from striking again.",h="A raptor has stolen the guards' payroll from the Crossroads tower, leaving the defenders baffled.",sec={{t="A Baffling Heist",b="The Crossroads depends on mercenary and grunt guards to keep trade routes open across the Barrens. Their pay matters to morale and discipline. When silver vanished from the guard tower, leaders expected Centaur raiders or Quilboar scavengers. Instead, a raptor was caught stealing in the dead of night, leaving the settlement stunned and short of coin.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance on the Pack",b="Gazrog does not know why wild beasts would hoard shiny coins, and he has no interest in studying their behavior. The guards are restless without their pay, so he calls for blood and deterrence. He sends hunters to take a dozen raptor heads from across the savannah, hoping to curb the predators' boldness before a full search for the silver begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why would raptors steal silver coins?",a="Even Gazrog admits the theft sounds unbelievable. Raptors are known for keen intelligence and hunting skill, but wild predators are not known to hoard refined currency. Gazrog is more concerned with punishing them before they raid the outpost again.",al={"why do raptors want silver","raptors stealing money","why silver"}},{q="Who is Gazrog?",a="Gazrog is an orc officer stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He maintains defense and order, overseeing guard logistics, outrunner bounties, and local threats to the Horde's central hub.",al={"gazrog","who gives raptor thieves"},it="identity"},{q="What was the stolen silver meant for?",a="The stolen chest held the payroll for the guards defending the Crossroads. Without it, keeping watch across the dangerous Barrens becomes much harder.",al={"what was the silver for","stolen shipment"}},{q="Where did the theft take place?",a="The silver was stolen from the guard tower at the Crossroads under cover of darkness. The theft shocked defenders who thought their central post was secure.",al={"where was silver stolen","theft location"},it="place"},{q="Where are these raptors found?",a="Raptor packs roam the central and southern Barrens savannah. Those closer to the Crossroads tend to be less seasoned and easier for travelers to confront.",al={"raptor locations","where to find raptors"},gp=true},{q="Does this quest recover the stolen silver?",a="No. Gazrog calls for a punitive cull to kill the offending beasts and thin their numbers. He organizes the search for the stolen coin chest only after the raptor threat is beaten back.",al={"do i get the silver back","where is the silver"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gazrog want this done?",a="A shipment of silver meant for the Crossroads guard payroll was stolen right out of their guard tower, and a raptor was caught at the scene. Gazrog refuses to let beasts plunder Horde coin and wants the local raptor population culled to prevent future thefts.",al={"gazrog motive","why kill raptors gazrog","why does gazrog want raptors dead"},it="motive",add="f8fd5498"},{q="What are the Raptor Heads for?",a="The severed heads serve as undeniable proof that you have hunted down and slain the raptors prowling near the Crossroads. Gazrog demands twelve of them to ensure the pack has been properly thinned before dealing with the missing silver.",al={"raptor head use","why collect raptor heads","what are raptor heads for"},it="item",add="ea8fb216"},{q="What raptors are you hunting?",a="You are sent to hunt the wild raptors wandering the savannah around the Crossroads. While they are natural predators native to the Barrens, their recent coordinated raid on the guard tower has turned them into an active threat to Horde operations.",al={"which raptors","raptor thieves target","what raptors to kill"},it="target",add="12d6b84d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Crossroads is the Horde's logistical spine in Kalimdor. An unpaid or humiliated garrison threatens every caravan crossing the savannah.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face Barrens raptors known for cunning, pack coordination, and speed. They are formidable targets in the harsh ecology you must master."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","gazrog","guard tower","payroll","raptor","raptor heads","silver"},rel={"quest:3281","npc:gazrog","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},m={start="Gazrog",level="13",faction="Horde",id=869,ri={"Raptor Head"}},src={"Raptor Thieves"}}
E["quest:870"] = {t="quest",n="The Forgotten Pools",z="barrens",s="At the Forgotten Pools, life surges through the dry Barrens for reasons the Cenarion Circle cannot explain. Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads sends Horde adventurers to inspect the oasis northwest of the settlement, where druids sense unseen forces beneath the earth.",h="At the Forgotten Pools, life surges through the dry Barrens for reasons the Cenarion Circle cannot explain.",sec={{t="Stirrings in the Savannah",b="The Barrens once flourished as fertile land before ages of war and the Sundering shattered the continent. The region became sun-baked scrubland, but lush oases have recently begun taking root in its dry basin. Druids of the Cenarion Circle find this sudden growth unnatural. They sense powers beneath the earth pressing upward, stirring vegetation and wildlife into life in scattered pockets across the wastes.",sp=0},{t="The Murky Depths",b="Tonga Runetotem sends you to the Forgotten Pools, just northwest of the Crossroads, to learn more about the new growth. Beneath the water, a fissure in the earth vents strange, bubbling gases into the pool. Tonga cannot yet say what this means, but the fissure gives him a tangible clue as the Barrens changes around you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tonga Runetotem?",a="Tonga Runetotem is a tauren druid of the Cenarion Circle stationed at the Crossroads. He studies the strange changes in the Barrens and seeks the reason oases are appearing across its dry plains.",al={"tonga runetotem","who gives the quest","quest giver crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Cenarion Circle investigating the Forgotten Pools?",a="The Cenarion Circle investigates because its druids sense concentrated energy forcing life to the surface. They want to find the power feeding the new oases before it grows out of control.",al={"why investigate oases","druids barrens oases","what is wrong with the pools"},it="motive"},{q="What is found at the bottom of the Forgotten Pools?",a="An underwater fissure vents bubbling gases into the pool. Tonga thinks it may reveal the force rising to the surface, though he cannot yet be sure.",al={"what is in the water","forgotten pool fissure","what bubbles in the pool"},it="place"},{q="Where are the Forgotten Pools located?",a="The Forgotten Pools lie northwest of the Crossroads in the central Barrens. Palms and water mark the oasis amid the dry land.",al={"forgotten pools location","where is forgotten pools"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Was the Barrens always a desert?",a="No. Druidic lore says the Barrens was once lush and full of life. Ancient wars and cataclysms scorched the land, leaving the arid savannah seen today.",al={"was barrens always dry","ancient barrens","barrens history"},it="history"},{q="What comes after investigating the Forgotten Pools?",a="Tonga Runetotem sends you southeast to inspect another Barrens oasis, the Stagnant Oasis.",al={"next quest","what to do after forgotten pools"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you encounter the Cenarion Circle's watch over the strange forces changing the Barrens' natural growth.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the Barrens matters to the nomadic tribes of the Earth Mother. Understanding and preserving its water sources matters to tauren travelers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you have reason to safeguard the water near the Crossroads, a junction between Durotar, Mulgore, and Ashenvale."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","crossroads","fissure","forgotten pools","oasis","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:forgotten-pools","quest:886","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",level="13",faction="Horde",id=870},src={"The Forgotten Pools (Classic)"}}
E["quest:871"] = {t="quest",n="Disrupt the Attacks",z="barrens",s="Thork needs the Crossroads defended as Razormane quilboar cut its supply roads. Their ambushes have halted caravans from Durotar, and the outpost is running short on food and gear. You strike at the quilboar while scouts search for the one directing their warband.",h="Thork needs the Crossroads defended as Razormane quilboar cut its supply roads.",sec={{t="A Severed Lifeline",b="The Crossroads guards a key junction for Horde traffic through central Kalimdor. Freight wagons and caravans bring food, iron, and equipment west from Durotar, and the outpost depends on those supplies. Razormane ambushes along the northeast trails have stopped the deliveries. Stores are running low, and Thork cannot wait for peaceful talks.",sp=0},{t="Pruning the Brambles",b="Thork sends you against the quilboar bramble dens northeast of the settlement before they can assault the town walls. Striking their Water Seekers, Thornweavers, and Hunters weakens the Razormane scouting perimeter and deprives raiding parties of magical and logistical support. These skirmishes buy time while Horde trackers search the brush for the one organizing the raids.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Razormane raiding caravans?",a="The Razormane see the Barrens as their ancestral homeland. They regard the Crossroads and Horde caravans crossing their hunting grounds as intolerable trespasses, so they ambush the supply wagons.",al={"why quilboar attack","razormane motivation","why attack durotar road"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Thork?",a="Thork is an orc commander stationed at the Crossroads. He oversees the outpost's daily defense, coordinates scouts, and sends warriors to secure trade roads from hostile centaur, harpies, and quilboar.",al={"who is thork","thork lore","crossroads leader"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these quilboar located?",a="The Razormane encampments lie east and northeast of the Crossroads, along the foot of the mountains separating the Barrens from Durotar. Towering briar vines surround their camps.",al={"where are razormane","razormane location","where are thornweavers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after disrupting their attacks?",a="After the first force is driven back and scouts identify who commands the raiders, Thork immediately sends you after their chieftain in The Disruption Ends.",al={"what next after disrupt attacks","next quest after disrupt the attacks"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What role do Water Seekers play in the tribe?",a="Water is the Barrens' rarest and most prized resource. Water Seekers find wells, oases, and hidden underground springs to supply the tribe and its war parties.",al={"what is a water seeker","razormane water seeker lore"},it="people"},{q="What are Thornweavers?",a="Thornweavers are quilboar geomancers and spellcasters who shape earth and grow the massive, impenetrable briars guarding their dens. In battle, they wield the region's nature magic against intruders.",al={"what is a thornweaver","quilboar thornweaver"},it="people"},{q="Why does Thork want the Razormane attacked?",a="The Razormane quilboar have been raiding the Horde's vital supply lines coming in from Durotar. If these ambushes continue unchecked, the outpost at the Crossroads will run out of essential provisions. While Thork awaits word from his scouts on who leads the raids, he needs you to strike their dens to relieve immediate pressure on the supply routes.",al={"why does thork want this","thork motive","why disrupt the attacks"},it="motive",add="9ca32dc5"},{q="Who are you being sent against?",a="You are sent to cull the Razormane quilboar—specifically their Water Seekers, Thornweavers, and Hunters—in their thorny dens to the northeast toward Durotar. Indigenous to the Barrens, the quilboar claim the region as their ancestral territory and fiercely contest the Horde's presence, violently ambushing caravans traveling between the settlements.",al={"who am i fighting","what are the targets","disrupt the attacks targets"},it="target",add="8c137a48"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The route between Durotar and the Crossroads is the Horde's main supply artery in central Kalimdor. If the quilboar close it, the whole outpost risks going hungry.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc settling Durotar, you need room to expand into the Barrens. The quilboar's relentless ambushes stand in your way and must be met with force.",["class:Hunter"]="Taking down Razormane Hunters in the scrub tests your tracking against native skirmishers who know the terrain intimately."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","durotar","quilboar","razormane","thork","thornweaver","water seeker"},rel={"quest:872","npc:thork","subzone:crossroads","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Thork",level="12",faction="Horde",id=871},src={"Disrupt the Attacks"}}
E["quest:8717"] = {t="quest",n="Moonwarden the Elder",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Moonwarden the Elder receives travelers beneath a beam of light. During the Lunar Festival, people honor ancestral spirits and seek his wisdom and directions to elders across Kalimdor.",h="At the Crossroads, Moonwarden the Elder receives travelers beneath a beam of light.",sec={{t="A Celestial Presence in the Barrens",b="At the Crossroads, a column of light falls around Elder Moonwarden. He is one of the ancient spirits honored during the Lunar Festival, when mortals set aside their conflicts to seek the wisdom of generations past.",sp=0},{t="Guidance to the Ancestors",b="Elder Moonwarden looks to the stars for answers to earthly mysteries. He offers ancestral blessings and directs seekers to other elders across Kalimdor, including Elder Bloodhoof, Elder High Mountain, Elder Morningdew, and Elder Runetotem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Moonwarden?",a="Elder Moonwarden stands at the Crossroads in the Barrens, beneath a bright column of starlight.",al={"elder moonwarden location","where is moonwarden","moonwarden crossroads"}},{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Moonwarden?",a="During the Lunar Festival, travelers honor ancestral spirits, receive tokens of ancestry, and seek directions to other elders.",al={"why talk to moonwarden","moonwarden quest","lunar festival moonwarden"}},{q="Which other elders can Moonwarden direct you to?",a="Elder Moonwarden can direct you to Elder Bloodhoof, Elder High Mountain, Elder Morningdew, and Elder Runetotem.",al={"other elders","moonwarden elder directions","who does moonwarden mention"}},{q="Can Alliance adventurers speak with Elder Moonwarden?",a="Alliance travelers can speak with Elder Moonwarden, though he stands in the Horde settlement of the Crossroads, where local guards make the visit dangerous.",al={"can alliance talk to moonwarden","crossroads elder alliance"}},{q="Why is there a beam of light shining on Elder Moonwarden?",a="The beam of light marks Elder Moonwarden's connection to the stars and the ancestral realm during the Lunar Festival.",al={"light beam elder","pillar of light moonwarden"}},{q="What does Elder Moonwarden say about the stars?",a="Elder Moonwarden says the stars hold answers to earthly mysteries, and asks whether the wise and lucky might look up and find truth.",al={"moonwarden dialogue","moonwarden quote"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you must enter the Horde settlement of the Crossroads to visit Elder Moonwarden, where the guards make the journey perilous.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler crossing central Kalimdor, you can conveniently honor Elder Moonwarden as part of the Lunar Festival tradition.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find Elder Moonwarden's focus on celestial mysteries and starry portents familiar through your attunement to nature and lunar cycles."},kw={"ancestor","crossroads","elder","elder moonwarden","elders","lunar festival","moonwarden","the barrens"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","npc:elder-bloodhoof","npc:elder-runetotem","npc:elder-morningdew","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Moonwarden",id=8717},src={"Moonwarden the Elder"}}
E["quest:872"] = {t="quest",n="The Disruption Ends",z="barrens",s="Thork orders a strike against the Razormane raids on the Horde road. Kreenig Snarlsnout leads the attacks from the northern Barrens, and his death is meant to break the warband's hold on the route between Durotar and the Crossroads.",h="Thork orders a strike against the Razormane raids on the Horde road.",sec={{t="Cutting the Head",b="The road between Durotar and the Crossroads carries provisions and reinforcements through the northern Barrens. Razormane quilboar ambushes have kept it under threat. Scout reports name their leader as Kreenig Snarlsnout, whose raiding party organizes the attacks. Thork orders a strike against Kreenig, hoping to break the warband's unity and secure the road.",sp=0},{t="Breaching the Encampment",b="Kreenig's war party is entrenched in craggy hills northeast of the Crossroads. Hardy Razormane Defenders and geomancers who manipulate the arid earth shield his position. Thork's order is to break through that guard and strike Kreenig in his redoubt, sending a warning across the plains. His tusk will prove the leader's death and show that the Horde will not accept attacks on its lifelines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kreenig Snarlsnout?",a="Kreenig Snarlsnout is a Razormane quilboar raid leader northeast of the Crossroads. He organized attacks on Horde caravans traveling the main road from Durotar, leading Thork to order his execution.",al={"who is kreenig","kreenig snarlsnout lore","who leads the razormane raiders"},it="target"},{q="Where is Kreenig Snarlsnout located?",a="Kreenig Snarlsnout is in the quilboar encampments northeast of the Crossroads, against the mountain foothills just south of the main road from Durotar.",al={"where is kreenig","kreenig location","find kreenig snarlsnout"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thork want Kreenig's tusk?",a="A tusk carries cultural weight among orcs and quilboar. Kreenig's tusk proves his death and insults his defeat, demoralizing the remaining Razormane fighters.",al={"why kreenigs tusk","why take the tusk","thork tusk trophy"},it="item"},{q="How does killing Kreenig help the Crossroads?",a="Thork believes quilboar warbands fall into chaos without strong leadership. Kreenig's death disrupts their coordination and curbs caravan ambushes, making the road from Durotar safer for travelers.",al={"why kill kreenig","strategic value of killing kreenig","crossroads caravan defense"},it="motive"},{q="What role do Razormane Geomancers play in the tribe?",a="Razormane Geomancers are quilboar spellcasters who commune with earth and stone spirits. They use nature magic to raise jagged thorn barriers and shape the rugged terrain around their bramble encampments to repel invaders.",al={"what are geomancers","razormane geomancer lore","quilboar earth magic"}},{q="What quest precedes this assignment?",a="The assignment follows Disrupt the Attacks, when scouts first identified the Razormane tribe's role in caravan raids along the eastern frontier.",al={"prerequisite quest","what comes before the disruption ends","previous quest"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The road between Durotar and the Crossroads is vital to Horde expansion in Kalimdor. Keeping it open helps inland outposts survive.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know Thork's approach: break the enemy's resolve by cutting down its chieftain in front of its warriors."},kw={"barrens","caravans","crossroads","defender","durotar","geomancer","kreenig snarlsnout","quilboar","razormane","thork"},rel={"npc:thork","quest:871","topic:quilboar","subzone:crossroads","quest:5041","zone:barrens","zone:durotar"},m={start="Thork",level="15",faction="Horde",id=872,ri={"Kreenig Snarlsnout's Tusk"}},src={"The Disruption Ends"}}
E["quest:873"] = {t="quest",n="Isha Awak",z="barrens",s="Along the Merchant Coast, Mahren Skyseer calls you to a hunt in the Great Sea. You are to slay Isha Awak, the Deep Doom, and bring back its heart for a rite of spirit and respect.",h="Along the Merchant Coast, Mahren Skyseer calls you to a hunt in the Great Sea.",sec={{t="The Deep Doom",b="South of Ratchet, Isha Awak prowls beneath the waves. Known as the Deep Doom, this immense sea creature commands the coastal waters with great strength. Human forces camped along the shore fear those waters after losing many scouts and soldiers to the predator's hunger.",sp=0},{t="A Hunt of Spirit",b="Mahren Skyseer reveres the leviathan, unlike the humans who fear it. To the tauren mystic, Isha Awak is no curse or mere pest, but a worthy foe whose might tests a hunter's resolve. Slaying the beast is an act of spiritual communion. Its heart holds the beast's essence, and claiming it lets the hunter carry that untamed spirit forward.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Isha Awak?",a="Known as the Deep Doom, Isha Awak prowls the waters off the eastern Barrens, south of Ratchet. The powerful sea beast rules those coastal waters and preys on nearby human sailors and soldiers.",al={"what is isha awak","isha awak lore","deep doom"},it="target"},{q="Why does Mahren Skyseer want Isha Awak slain?",a="Mahren Skyseer sees Isha Awak as a worthy, honorable opponent and a spiritual challenge. She believes that overcoming the beast lets a hunter absorb its strength and commune with its wild spirit.",al={"why kill isha awak","mahren skyseer motivation"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Isha Awak be found?",a="Isha Awak swims in the Great Sea along the Merchant Coast in the eastern Barrens, south of Ratchet and near the human-inhabited shore.",al={"isha awak location","where to find isha awak","isha awak spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when you bring back the heart?",a="Mahren Skyseer believes the creature's essence and fate rest in its heart. By bringing it to her, you bind yourself in spirit to the fallen leviathan and carry a portion of Isha Awak's strength and predatory sight.",al={"heart of isha awak purpose","why heart of isha awak"},it="item"},{q="Who are the humans mentioned by Mahren?",a="Mahren speaks of the Theramore and Kul Tiras forces along the Barrens coast, especially around Northwatch Hold and nearby outposts. They have lost many sailors and shore-dwellers to the beast's jaws.",al={"which humans","humans on the coast","who fears isha awak"},it="people"},{q="Is Isha Awak considered an elemental or a natural animal?",a="Isha Awak is a natural aquatic beast of the Great Sea, though exceptionally large and powerful. Local tauren revere its primal spirit and skill as a hunter.",al={"is isha awak a beast","isha awak creature type"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you follow a tradition that respects prey rather than despising it. Taking a life can bring communion with the creature's spirit.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you track a legendary aquatic beast into the Great Sea, testing your patience, cunning, and marksmanship in its own territory.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the Deep Doom along the Merchant Coast, where it has terrorized local Alliance outposts."},kw={"deep doom","heart of isha awak","isha awak","mahren skyseer","merchant coast","ratchet","sea beast"},rel={"quest:874","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet"},m={start="Mahren Skyseer",level="27",faction="Horde",id=873,ri={"Heart of Isha Awak"}},src={"Isha Awak (quest)"}}
E["quest:874"] = {t="quest",n="Mahren Skyseer",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, hunters who have mastered the plains are sent east to Mahren Skyseer. Jorn Skyseer sends them to his sister to learn coastal tracking along the Barrens shore.",h="At Camp Taurajo, hunters who have mastered the plains are sent east to Mahren Skyseer.",sec={{t="A Hunt Beyond the Plains",b="Jorn Skyseer tests hunters at Camp Taurajo against the dangerous beasts of the southern Barrens. Once they have proved themselves on the red plains, he points them beyond dry earth and open savanna. A tracker must learn to follow prey through swamps, over sheer crags, and beside the crashing waves of the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="The Eastern Shore",b="Mahren Skyseer keeps a camp far east along the coast. While Jorn studies thunderhawks and plains stalkers, his sister follows creatures that live in the salt spray. Reaching her means crossing dangerous ground. Kul Tiras marines and Theramore expedition forces hold fortified outposts and watchtowers across the coastal lowlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Mahren Skyseer?",a="Jorn Skyseer sends you from Camp Taurajo after you complete his hunt for the thunderhawks.",al={"who starts mahren skyseer","jorn skyseer quest giver"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where is Mahren Skyseer located?",a="Mahren Skyseer camps along the Barrens' eastern coast, south of Ratchet, near coastal wildlife and Theramore troops.",al={"where is mahren skyseer","mahren skyseer location","find mahren"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="You go from Jorn Skyseer's hunting trials at Camp Taurajo to Mahren's coastal hunts for sea creatures.",al={"why do i need to find mahren","mahren skyseer objective"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Jorn send hunters to Mahren?",a="Jorn believes a hunter must master every environment, including the sea. His sister Mahren specializes in tracking and confronting aquatic beasts, so she can teach you.",al={"why does jorn send me to his sister","lore behind mahren skyseer"},it="motive"},{q="What dangers lie along the way to Mahren?",a="Theramore and Kul Tiras expedition forces occupy the eastern coast, alongside aggressive coastal raptors and marine predators.",al={"dangers reaching mahren","who holds the coast"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="What comes after finding Mahren Skyseer?",a="After you introduce yourself and earn her trust, Mahren sends you to track Isha Awak, a massive, ferocious sea creature haunting the waters.",al={"next quest after mahren","what does mahren give you"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer choose you to seek out Mahren?",a="You have earned Jorn's deep respect by mastering the beasts of the Barrens and proving the strength of your spirit. Jorn believes a true hunter cannot limit themselves to familiar dry dirt, mountains, or swamps—they must learn to master every terrain, including the open ocean. Because you demonstrated such exceptional hunting prowess in Camp Taurajo, he trusts you alone are ready to undertake advanced training under his sister.",al={"why me mahren skyseer","why does jorn send me","why send player to mahren"},it="why_me",add="d516f680"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you move from stalking savanna game to pursuing fierce aquatic beasts under the guidance of seasoned tauren stalkers.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you follow the Skyseer siblings' hunting traditions and face trials across every ecosystem as a child of the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel to the eastern coast, close to hostile Alliance footholds spreading from Theramore."},kw={"camp taurajo","hunting trial","isha awak","jorn skyseer","mahren skyseer","sergra darkthorn","the barrens"},rel={"quest:3261","quest:913","quest:860","zone:barrens"},m={start="Jorn Skyseer",["end"]="Mahren Skyseer",level="27",faction="Horde",id=874},src={"Mahren Skyseer (quest)"}}
E["quest:875"] = {t="quest",n="Harpy Lieutenants",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger sends Horde champions against the Witchwing coven in the northern Barrens. In the Dry Hills, the aim is to kill the flock’s front-line officers and break its chain of command.",h="At the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger sends Horde champions against the Witchwing coven in the northern...",sec={{t="Targeting the Officers",b="After the first clashes with Witchwing raiders, Darsok Swiftdagger turns the offensive toward the harpies roosting in the Dry Hills. Horde scouts are sent after the Witchwing Slayers who lead the flock. These officers keep the lesser harpies in line and coordinate raids against Horde supply paths. Their deaths are critical to securing the northern approaches of the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Rank",b="Witchwing Slayers lead through strength and dominance, and only the most vicious among them carry ornate rings that mark their authority within the matriarchy. Taking the rings proves the lieutenants are dead, disrupts the roost’s coordination, and sends the coven a clear message: attacks on Horde territory will meet decisive retribution.",sp=0},{t="A Path to the Matriarch",b="Killing the officers throws the lower flock into disarray and serves a broader strategic purpose. Removing the Witchwing roost’s field commanders weakens the perimeter around the heights of the Dry Hills, opening a path toward the inner sanctum of their matriarch, Serena Bloodfeather.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find the harpy lieutenants?",a="Find the harpy lieutenants in the Dry Hills, a jagged canyon region in the far north of the Barrens, northwest of the Crossroads. Witchwing Slayers patrol the hills.",al={"lieutenant location","where are witchwing slayers","harpy lieutenant rings location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How are these lieutenants identified among the flock?",a="Witchwing Slayers are the lieutenants of the Witchwing coven. Their distinctive harpy rings mark their authority over lesser scouts and raiders.",al={"which harpies have rings","witchwing slayer identification"},gp=true},{q="Who issues this bounty?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger, an orc scout and coordinator stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens, assigns the contract to protect Horde interests and punish harpy incursions.",al={"who gives harpy lieutenants","darsok swiftdagger role"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does the Horde want to kill the lieutenants instead of just regular harpies?",a="The lieutenants direct the lower harpies and organize predatory strikes. Killing them breaks the matriarchy’s leadership and leaves the remaining harpies disorganized and vulnerable.",al={"why kill lieutenants","harpy chain of command"},it="purpose"},{q="What comes after eliminating the lieutenants?",a="After the lieutenants are slain, Darsok Swiftdagger directs champions to hunt the flock’s matriarch, Serena Bloodfeather, atop the highest bluffs of the Dry Hills.",al={"next quest after lieutenants","what to do next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Witchwing harpies a threat to the Crossroads?",a="The Witchwing coven infests the northern passes of the Barrens, preying on travelers, supply caravans, and patrols traveling between the Crossroads, Durotar, and Ashenvale.",al={"why fight harpies","witchwing threat"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Darsok Swiftdagger want this done?",a="Darsok wants vengeance and security for the Horde after the harpies launched vicious attacks against travelers and outposts in the Barrens. To him, cutting down their commanders teaches the flock the cost of picking a fight with the Horde.",al={"darsok motive","why kill harpy lieutenants","darsok swiftdagger goal"},it="motive",add="7731c688"},{q="What is the Harpy Lieutenant Ring for?",a="The rings serve as badges of authority among the Witchwing harpies, worn exclusively by the slayers who lead underlings in the field. Darsok requires them as undeniable proof that you eliminated genuine field commanders rather than common flock raiders.",al={"harpy ring purpose","harpy lieutenant ring lore","why collect harpy rings"},it="item",add="bdc3a4da"},{q="Who are the Witchwing Slayers?",a="The Witchwing Slayers are the veteran enforcers and battlefield lieutenants of the Witchwing matriarchy. Stationed throughout the Dry Hills, they organize hunting parties and direct common harpies in raids against the Northern Barrens.",al={"witchwing slayers lore","who are the lieutenants","witchwing slayer targets"},it="target",add="090c4b20"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Securing the northern corridors of the Barrens helps keep communication lines open between Durotar, Mulgore, and the Ashenvale logging camps.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the value of striking high-value officers with precision. Darsok Swiftdagger relies on such assassinations instead of costly open warfare."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","darsok swiftdagger","dry hills","harpy lieutenant ring","harpy lieutenants","serena bloodfeather","witchwing slayer"},rel={"quest:867","quest:876","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","subzone:dry-hills","subzone:crossroads","topic:harpy","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},m={start="Darsok Swiftdagger",level="16",faction="Horde",id=875,ri={"Harpy Lieutenant Ring"}},src={"Harpy Lieutenants (Classic)"}}
E["quest:876"] = {t="quest",n="Serena Bloodfeather",z="barrens",s="Across the northern Barrens, harpy raids threaten the Crossroads supply lines. Serena Bloodfeather leads the Witchwing flock, driven by a blood feud with the Horde after Rexxar slew her sister. Ending her campaign could break the harpies’ coordination.",h="Across the northern Barrens, harpy raids threaten the Crossroads supply lines.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Vengeance",b="Witchwing harpies strike the trails northwest of the Crossroads under Serena Bloodfeather’s command. Their attacks are driven by more than hunger: Serena seeks vengeance against the Horde. During Durotar’s founding, the beastmaster Rexxar slew her sister, the notorious matriarch Bloodfeather. Serena has rallied her flock to attack supply trains, scouts, and merchants traveling the arid trails.",sp=0},{t="Cutting Off the Head",b="Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads has led the effort to cull the harpies, from petty raiders to seasoned lieutenants. He now calls for Serena’s head as proof of her death and as a trophy for the next outgoing caravan. The Horde hopes that showing the surviving harpies their matriarch’s fate will frighten them away from the Barrens’ supply lines.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Serena Bloodfeather attacking Horde caravans?",a="Serena attacks Horde caravans to avenge her sister. The beastmaster Rexxar slew the harpy matriarch Bloodfeather during Durotar’s founding, and Serena now turns her flock against Horde supply wagons and travelers.",al={"why do harpies attack caravans","serena motivation","why serena mad"},it="target"},{q="Who was Bloodfeather?",a="Bloodfeather was a notorious harpy leader who terrorized the borders of Durotar and the Barrens. Rexxar slew her while serving Warchief Thrall. Serena, her surviving sister, took up her mantle and grudge.",al={"serena sister","original bloodfeather","rexxar bloodfeather"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Darsok Swiftdagger want her head?",a="Darsok wants Serena’s head to confirm her death and display it on an outgoing caravan wagon. He hopes the sight will warn surviving harpies away from Horde supply lines.",al={"why darsok wants head","darsok swiftdagger head caravan"},it="item"},{q="Where can Serena Bloodfeather be found?",a="Serena is among the rugged cliffs and wind-carved crags northwest of the Crossroads, surrounded by Witchwing lieutenants and guards.",al={"serena bloodfeather location","where is serena","serena spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Serena is defeated?",a="After Serena falls, Darsok sends reliable mercenaries to help other allies in need. He dispatches them with a letter to Jin'Zil, the witch doctor in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"what next after serena","quest chain after serena"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who assigned this bounty?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger, an orc scout stationed at the Crossroads, assigns the bounty. He oversees efforts against wild threats along trade routes and issues it after the flock’s lower ranks have been cleared.",al={"who gives serena quest","darsok role"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Darsok Swiftdagger want Serena Bloodfeather killed?",a="Serena Bloodfeather and her flock have been relentlessly raiding Horde supply caravans moving through the northern Barrens. By cutting down their matriarch, Darsok intends to break the back of the local harpy menace, avenge the fallen caravan crews, and secure vital trade and travel routes connecting the Crossroads to the rest of Kalimdor.",al={"darsok motive","why kill serena","why does darsok want her dead"},it="motive",add="469ae7c3"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The northern trade routes through the Crossroads supply orcish outposts and connect Durotar with Mulgore and Stonetalon. Putting down organized harpy raiders keeps those routes open.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you’ll find Darsok Swiftdagger values cold efficiency. He calls for Serena’s throat to be slit swiftly, without a prolonged fight.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you face unfinished business tied to Rexxar’s deeds and the fierce struggles on Durotar’s early frontier."},kw={"barrens","bloodfeather","crossroads","darsok","harpy","rexxar","serena","swiftdagger"},rel={"quest:875","quest:867","quest:1060","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:harpy","topic:horde"},m={start="Darsok Swiftdagger",level="20",faction="Horde",id=876,ri={"Serena's Head"}},src={"Serena Bloodfeather (Classic)"}}
E["quest:877"] = {t="quest",n="The Stagnant Oasis",z="barrens",s="Tonga Runetotem sends you southeast from the Crossroads to search the Stagnant Oasis. He wants to know if the hidden fissure beneath the Forgotten Pools has a match in its murky waters.",h="Tonga Runetotem sends you southeast from the Crossroads to search the Stagnant Oasis.",sec={{t="A Search for Hidden Waters",b="Tonga Runetotem sends you to the Stagnant Oasis after a strange fissure is found beneath the Forgotten Pools. He suspects the sudden patches of lush growth across the Barrens have a cause beneath the earth. You search the oasis's murky shallows for another opening, among predators that haunt the water.",sp=0},{t="The Spark of Vitality",b="Tonga Runetotem gives you dried seeds that cannot sprout on their own. When you place them in the bubbling fissure, they surge into growth. The spring beneath the oasis can give life to dead matter, revealing an extraordinary power at work below the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest The Stagnant Oasis?",a="Tonga Runetotem, a tauren druid at the Crossroads, sends you to investigate after the search of the Forgotten Pools.",al={"quest giver","where to get","tonga quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What do the dried seeds do?",a="Tonga gives you dead, infertile seeds to test. Place them in a fissure beneath the Stagnant Oasis and watch for any change in the water.",al={"dried seeds","seeds use","seeds test"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Stagnant Oasis located?",a="The Stagnant Oasis lies southeast of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Rocky bluffs surround its waters, where snapjaw turtles, kolkar centaur, and other water-dwelling beasts live.",al={"oasis location","where is stagnant oasis","map location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the significance of the underwater fissures?",a="The fissures are mysterious cracks beneath the oasis waters. Tonga suspects they may give life to the oases and asks you to test that idea.",al={"oasis fissures","underwater crack","bubbling fissure"},it="power"},{q="What quest comes next in the chain?",a="When you return to Tonga Runetotem with your findings, he sends you on to investigate the mutations and aggressive behavior of wildlife around the pools.",al={"next quest","followup","after stagnant oasis"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is the Cenarion Circle interested in these pools?",a="Cenarion druids have long sought ways to heal the Barrens' dry savanna. Springs that create life would bring hope, but the strange, sudden changes also raise concern that an unnatural force is disturbing the land.",al={"why care about pools","cenarion interest","druid oasis"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem want to investigate the Stagnant Oasis?",a="Following your earlier discovery at the Forgotten Pools, Tonga suspects that fissures bubbling beneath the Barrens' waters might be the secret source of life transforming the arid landscape. By testing whether dead, infertile seeds can be revitalized within the bubbling fissure of the Stagnant Oasis, he hopes to prove if an unknown power beneath the oases is actively creating life from barren earth.",al={"tonga runetotem motive","why investigate stagnant oasis","tonga oasis seeds why"},it="motive",add="4e43e800"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the Cenarion Circle, you test the oasis with lifeless seeds to learn whether hidden forces are restoring life to the Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor the Earth Mother by seeking to understand sudden changes in the natural balance of your ancestral hunting grounds.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that freshwater oases near the Crossroads help protect trade caravans and military outposts across the harsh Barrens."},kw={"cenarion circle","crossroads","dried seeds","fissure","forgotten pools","stagnant oasis","the barrens","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:stagnant-oasis","quest:870","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","subzone:forgotten-pools"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",level="16",faction="Horde",id=877},src={"The Stagnant Oasis (Classic)"}}
E["quest:878"] = {t="quest",n="Tribes at War",z="barrens",s="Mangletooth bargains for help against the Bristleback from his cage in Camp Taurajo. The captive Razormane quilboar offers intelligence about quilboar incursions in exchange for the deaths of rival spiritual leaders.",h="Mangletooth bargains for help against the Bristleback from his cage in Camp Taurajo.",sec={{t="A Prisoner's Bargain",b="Mangletooth, a Razormane quilboar, is held in Camp Taurajo by the tauren. The Barrens has long been contested by two powerful quilboar tribes, the Razormane and the Bristleback. The Horde struggles to secure its settlements and supply lines against sudden ambushes. Mangletooth offers insight into who is tormenting Thork's outpost, but he asks a Horde champion to kill the Bristleback's most revered casters.",sp=0},{t="Targeting the Earthweavers",b="Mangletooth sends you north to strike at the Bristleback's spiritual heart: its Water Seekers, Thornweavers, and Geomancers. Both tribes revere the earth and draw power from ancient magic tied to their demigod progenitor, Agamaggan. Killing the casters weakens Bristleback rituals, leaves the tribe vulnerable to Razormane rivals, and eases pressure on nearby trails.",sp=0},{t="Bitter Revelations",b="Mangletooth finds no peace in vengeance after the Bristleback losses. Rage replaces any celebration as he faces his own abandonment. Though he has arranged strikes to aid his tribe from behind iron bars, the Razormane have sent no rescue party to Camp Taurajo. Spurned and forgotten, Mangletooth turns to deeper quilboar secrets and the power of Agamaggan's blood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Mangletooth locked in a cage at Camp Taurajo?",a="Mangletooth is a Razormane quilboar captured by Horde forces at Camp Taurajo. The tauren keep him caged to prevent raids and learn about quilboar incursions across the southern Barrens.",al={"why is mangletooth caged","who captured mangletooth","mangletooth cage"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the feud between the Razormane and the Bristleback?",a="The Razormane and Bristleback are rival quilboar tribes fighting for territory, scarce water, and the Barrens' sacred thorn-covered grounds. Though both share a spiritual lineage tied to the Great Boar Agamaggan, they despise each other and clash over control of the plains.",al={"bristleback vs razormane","why do quilboar fight each other","quilboar war"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Mangletooth want their spiritual leaders dead specifically?",a="Geomancers, Thornweavers, and Water Seekers sustain quilboar life, call stone and brambles into battle, and guide their warriors. Killing these casters breaks morale and weakens the tribe's fighting power.",al={"why kill geomancers","bristleback casters","water seekers and thornweavers"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Thork, and why does Mangletooth mention him?",a="Thork is an orc officer overseeing Horde efforts and security at the Crossroads and throughout the Barrens. His forces face relentless pressure from quilboar war bands, so intelligence on their movements is valuable.",al={"who is thork","thork camp taurajo","thork horde"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Mangletooth, embittered by his tribe's failure to rescue him, offers to reveal the secret of Blood Shards. This opens the way to Blood Shards of Agamaggan, where you can trade shards found on quilboar for tribal spirit blessings.",al={"tribes at war follow up","what unlocks after tribes at war","next quest after mangletooth"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where do I find the Bristleback spiritualists?",a="Bristleback Water Seekers, Thornweavers, and Geomancers live in the tribe's thorny thickets, camps, and ravines in the southern Barrens, just north of Camp Taurajo.",al={"bristleback water seeker location","where are thornweavers","bristleback geomancers location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the Bristlebacks you are sent to hunt?",a="You are sent to cull the spiritual caste of the northern Bristleback quilboar tribe—specifically their Water Seekers, Thornweavers, and Geomancers. Like their Razormane rivals, the Bristlebacks draw martial power directly from the earth and their reverence for the Ancient boar god Agamaggan. By targeting their mystics, you sever the magic and spiritual guidance that give them the upper hand in their bloody territorial war across the Barrens.",al={"who are the bristlebacks","bristleback quillboar barrens","bristleback target"},it="target",add="43fd17a8"},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you to do this instead of doing it himself?",a="Mangletooth cannot strike his rivals himself because he is trapped in an iron cage at Camp Taurajo, held captive by the Horde. His own tribe, the Razormane, has abandoned him to rot without sending a rescue party. With no freedom and no loyal allies of his own within reach, he relies on traveling adventurers willing to do his violent bidding in exchange for valuable intelligence about quilboar aggression.",al={"why does mangletooth need me","why me tribes at war","why ask me mangletooth"},it="why_me",add="db148a16"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Camp Taurajo is ringed by hostile brush. Turning the savage quilboar tribes against each other helps protect Horde supply lines.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see how quilboar geomancers bend earth and stone through ancient pacts with spirits, a crude but potent distortion of elemental reverence.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you help keep Camp Taurajo secure. Mangletooth remains there only while his grudges serve the southern frontier."},kw={"barrens","bristleback","camp taurajo","geomancer","mangletooth","razormane","thork","thornweaver","tribes at war","water seeker"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","subzone:camp-taurajo","quest:5052","zone:barrens","npc:thork","topic:agamaggan","quest:889","quest:5042"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="21",faction="Horde",id=878},src={"Tribes at War"}}
E["quest:879"] = {t="quest",n="Betrayal from Within",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Betrayal from Within begins with Mangletooth's offer of bloody vengeance. Imprisoned in a cage, the quilboar says his kin left him for dead. He offers Horde travelers knowledge of the three Razormane warlords who emerged from Razorfen Kraul to organize assaults across the Barrens.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Betrayal from Within begins with Mangletooth's offer of bloody vengeance.",sec={{t="A Grudge in a Cage",b="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth has lost all loyalty to his Razormane kin. They left him behind in defeat, and he faces execution in his cage. Now he wants vengeance against the leaders who abandoned him. He offers Horde travelers knowledge of the true architects behind the ruthless raids across the plains.",sp=0},{t="The Warlords of the Kraul",b="Razormane attacks keep troubling the Horde, and Thork at the Crossroads struggles to curb them. Mangletooth names three commanders from deep within Razorfen Kraul: Lok Orcbane, a formidable warrior, and his companions Nak, a tracker, and Kuz, a spellcaster. They direct Razormane raiders from encampments far to the south. Mangletooth demands their severed skulls as proof that his betrayers have fallen before his own end arrives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a quilboar helping the Horde?",a="Mangletooth helps the Horde for revenge, not friendship. His brethren turned their backs on him and left him to die in a cage at Camp Taurajo. Since he believes his own death is inevitable, he wants his betrayers dead first.",al={"why mangletooth helps","mangletooth motive","why quilboar betraying kin"},it="motive"},{q="Who are Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane?",a="Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane are three Razormane leaders who emerged from Razorfen Kraul to organize raids across the Barrens. Lok Orcbane is a vicious warrior, joined by Nak the tracker and Kuz the spellcaster.",al={"who are the targets","razormane leaders","lok orcbane lore"},it="target"},{q="Where are the three targets found?",a="They make their camps far to the south of the Barrens, within Razormane territories near the southern brushlands.",al={"where is lok orcbane","where are nak and kuz","target locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Mangletooth mean about Thork being wrong?",a="Thork manages defenses from the Crossroads and believes he knows who directs the quilboar attacks on Horde supply lines. Mangletooth says Thork is wrong: Lok Orcbane, Nak, and Kuz are behind the attacks.",al={"thork mistake","what did thork get wrong","thork and mangletooth"}},{q="Will killing these leaders truly bring peace with the Razormane?",a="Mangletooth claims that killing the three will ease Razormane raids on the Crossroads and much of the Barrens. Their fall would break the immediate southern leadership, but quilboar hostility across the Barrens would remain.",al={"will barrens have peace","end of razormane","razormane defeated"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens to Mangletooth after this?",a="Mangletooth believes his death is inescapable while he is locked in a Horde encampment. He seeks neither escape nor mercy, only the satisfaction of bringing down his treacherous tribe mates before his end.",al={"does mangletooth go free","mangletooth fate","is mangletooth executed"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you to kill the Razormane leaders?",a="Mangletooth cannot strike back himself because he is locked in a cage inside Camp Taurajo, awaiting execution by the Horde. His own kin abandoned him to die in captivity, leaving him powerless to seek vengeance with his own hands. The tauren guards have no reason to do his personal bidding, so he relies on an ambitious adventurer willing to carry out his vendetta against those who betrayed him.",al={"why does mangletooth need me","why cant mangletooth kill them","why send player betryal from within"},it="why_me",add="ad7243f0"},{q="Why does Mangletooth want the skulls of Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane?",a="Mangletooth demands their skulls as undeniable trophies and physical proof that his traitorous rivals are dead. Knowing that his own death in the cage is inevitable, seeing the severed heads of the kin who betrayed and abandoned him grants him satisfaction and closure before his time is up.",al={"what are the skulls for","why mangletooth wants skulls","lok nak kuz skulls purpose"},it="item",add="e94be914"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Stopping Lok Orcbane and his cohorts strikes at the leaders responsible for brutalizing Horde caravans and outposts across the southern Barrens.",["race:Orc"]="Lok Orcbane bears that name for his prowess and hatred in slaughtering orcish travelers across the territory.",["race:Tauren"]="Camp Taurajo lies along the southern corridor where Razormane aggression runs hottest, making these warlords' deaths critical to local security."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","kraul","kuz","lok orcbane","mangletooth","nak","razormane","thork"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","subzone:camp-taurajo","npc:thork","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:horde"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="25",faction="Horde",id=879,ri={"Kuz's Skull","Lok's Skull","Nak's Skull"}},src={"Betrayal from Within (1)"}}
E["quest:880"] = {t="quest",n="Altered Beings",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem studies strange changes in the Barrens' oasis waters. Fissures beneath the pools may be changing the creatures that live there, and he asks you to bring him shells from altered snapjaws.",h="At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem studies strange changes in the Barrens' oasis waters.",sec={{t="Unnatural Waters",b="Tonga Runetotem is searching for the cause of strange changes in the Barrens' oases. Though the savanna is dry, a handful of pools support fertile ground. Tonga found peculiar fissures beneath those waters, sending out potent energies. He does not know whether the force came from outside or rose from deep within the earth. Now he studies the creatures that drink from and live in the pools, hoping to learn what the fissures are doing to them.",sp=0},{t="Signs in the Shell",b="You are sent to the Lushwater Oasis and the Stagnant Oasis to gather altered snapjaw shells. Snapjaws live in the shallows, where they take in the strange essence through food and exposure. Their carapaces have changed, offering Tonga a sign of how the fissures affect local wildlife. He hopes the shells will help him understand the disturbance before it spreads farther across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Altered Beings?",a="Tonga Runetotem, a tauren druid at the Crossroads in the central Barrens, gives this work.",al={"quest giver","where to get altered beings","who starts altered beings"},gp=true},{q="What creatures need to be hunted for this task?",a="You hunt oasis snapjaws around the waters of the Lushwater Oasis and the Stagnant Oasis in the Barrens.",al={"which mobs drop shells","altered snapjaw targets","what to kill"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why are the snapjaws altered?",a="Fissures beneath the oases send strange energies into the water. Animals that live in or drink from the pools have developed mutations, including visible changes to their shells.",al={"why are snapjaws mutated","what altered the turtles","what is wrong with the oasis beasts"}},{q="Where are the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases?",a="Both oases lie south of the Crossroads in the Barrens. The Stagnant Oasis is southeast, toward the border of Dustwallow Marsh, while the Lushwater Oasis is southwest, near the entrance to the Wailing Caverns.",al={"oasis locations barrens","lushwater location","stagnant oasis location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing Altered Beings?",a="Tonga Runetotem finds the mystery runs deeper than the wild beasts. He sends you to report your findings to higher-ranking druidic elders, Hamuul Runetotem or Mura Runetotem.",al={"next quest after altered beings","where does the chain go","altered beings follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is Tonga Runetotem studying the oases?",a="Tonga Runetotem studies the oases to understand nature's balance in the Barrens. Unnatural growth around the pools hints at forces beneath the earth that could disrupt the savanna ecosystem.",al={"tonga runetotem motive","why investigate the oasis","cenarion circle barrens"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Altered Snapjaw Shell for?",a="Tonga Runetotem needs the carapaces of the oasis snapjaws as physical evidence for his research. By examining how the strange energies of the oasis waters have seeped into the creatures' shells, he hopes to understand the unnatural force welling up from the fissures.",al={"altered snapjaw shell use","why snapjaw shells","tonga snapjaw shells"},it="item",add="7a1a1371"},{q="What are the oasis snapjaws you are hunting?",a="Oasis snapjaws are large, aggressive turtles dwelling within the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases of the Barrens. Because they spend their lives immersed in these waters, they directly absorb whatever unnatural properties are leaking through the aquatic fissures, making them prime specimens for druidic study.",al={"oasis snapjaws","what are the snapjaws","why kill snapjaws"},it="target",add="4a9a27cc"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see how close natural vitality can lie to corrupted mutation. The snapjaws offer a view of the disturbance beneath the Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see the Earthmother's balance shaken in the Barrens. Tonga Runetotem's work touches your people's ancestral lands and their search for harmony.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the Crossroads depends on safe, pure water. Its sources must be guarded against unexpected magical dangers."},kw={"altered beings","altered snapjaw shell","crossroads","lushwater oasis","snapjaws","stagnant oasis","the barrens","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",level="16",faction="Horde",id=880,ri={"Altered Snapjaw Shell"}},src={"Altered Beings (Classic)"}}
E["quest:881"] = {t="quest",n="Echeyakee",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, hunters prepare to face Whitemist in the northern Barrens. Sergra Darkthorn sends young Horde hunters to summon the legendary white lion and test their strength.",h="At the Crossroads, hunters prepare to face Whitemist in the northern Barrens.",sec={{t="Whitemist of the Savannah",b="Across the central plains, a white-maned lion rules the savannah cats. Taur-ahe speakers call him Echeyakee, or Whitemist. Legend says he moves so silently that he seems like morning mist gliding over the red earth. His strikes come swiftly, leaving prey no time for fear or suffering. Local hunters revere him as a sign of mercy and swift death.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of the Horn",b="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn trains fledgling warriors. The experienced orc shaman sends her pupils to challenge the king of beasts after they have proven themselves against lesser savannah prowlers. With a special horn, you travel northeast past the mountain ridges to a graveyard of massive kodo bones. Sound the horn to challenge Echeyakee and draw the elusive predator from hiding for a test of strength and cunning.",sp=0},{t="The Lion's Legacy",b="When you return Echeyakee's hide, Sergra says his hunting days are over, though his spirit is with the victor. She teaches that his example joins strength in subtlety with honor in mercy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does the name Echeyakee mean?",a="In Taur-ahe, Echeyakee means “Whitemist.” The name honors his pale pelt and the silent, mist-like way he stalks across the plains.",al={"echeyakee translation","meaning of echeyakee","tauren name echeyakee"},it="name"},{q="Where is Echeyakee summoned?",a="You summon Echeyakee northeast of the Crossroads, past the mountain ridge, among giant kodo skeletons. He appears when you sound the horn Sergra Darkthorn provides.",al={"where is echeyakee","echeyakee location","how to find echeyakee"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Echeyakee described as both mercy and death?",a="Tauren hunting tradition sees Echeyakee as both mercy and death because his strikes are swift and sure. His prey suffers no prolonged agony or fear.",al={"why mercy and death","echeyakee lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends hunters after Echeyakee?",a="Sergra Darkthorn, an orc shaman at the Crossroads, sends hunters after Echeyakee to test their grasp of a predator's subtlety and balance.",al={"who gives echeyakee quest","sergra darkthorn quest"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after Echeyakee is slain?",a="After Echeyakee is slain, Sergra asks you to bring his hide to her at the Crossroads as proof of the hunt.",al={"what happens to echeyakee","echeyakee spirit"},it="next_step"},{q="What follows the hunt of Echeyakee?",a="After you overcome Echeyakee with patience and lethal skill, Sergra Darkthorn sends you after more volatile quarry: the vicious raptors called scytheclaws.",al={"quest after echeyakee","what is next after echeyakee"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn send you to hunt Echeyakee?",a="Sergra is testing your worth and honing your discipline as a hunter of the Horde. She sends you to face Echeyakee, the legendary king of the savannah cats, and learn why the tauren describe him as both mercy and death. Bringing back his hide provides proof that you have met the challenge.",al={"why kill echeyakee","sergra motive echeyakee","why hunt echeyakee"},it="motive",add="04f9f29c"},{q="What is Echeyakee's Hide used for?",a="The hide serves as physical proof of your kill. Bringing the pristine pelt back to Sergra Darkthorn shows that you summoned and bested the elusive white lion in fair combat, demonstrating to the Crossroads shaman that you have mastered the lesson of the hunt.",al={"what is echeyakee hide for","echeyakees hide purpose","why take echeyakee hide"},it="item",add="543d0f76"},{q="Who is Echeyakee?",a="Known in the Tauren tongue as Whitemist, Echeyakee is the legendary king of the Barrens savannah cats. He stalks near the ancient kodo graveyards northeast of the Crossroads, famed for moving like pale fog and delivering strikes so swift that his prey feels no agony before death.",al={"who is echeyakee","what is echeyakee","echeyakee lore"},it="target",add="f8cfac92"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know Echeyakee as Whitemist, a sacred figure of the clean, painless kill and an example of the Earth Mother's fierce balance.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter in the Barrens, you face a test of patience and stealth in Echeyakee, famed among the savannah beasts for his pale fur and legendary name.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion at the Crossroads, you face the harsh Barrens wildlife in a rite of passage that proves your survival skills."},kw={"crossroads","echeyakee","kodo bones","savannah lion","sergra darkthorn","the barrens","whitemist"},rel={"quest:860","quest:903","quest:905","subzone:crossroads","topic:tauren","zone:barrens"},m={start="Sergra Darkthorn",level="16",faction="Horde",id=881,ri={"Echeyakee's Hide"}},src={"Echeyakee (Classic)"}}
E["quest:882"] = {t="quest",n="Ishamuhale",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Jorn Skyseer sends you to face Ishamuhale, the fiercest sunscale raptor in the Barrens. The hunt tests your skill and respect for nature's deadliest predators.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Jorn Skyseer sends you to face Ishamuhale, the fiercest sunscale raptor in the Barrens.",sec={{t="The Nature of Speartooth",b="Sunscale raptors hunt the Barrens in cunning, vicious packs, but none inspires more dread than Speartooth. Jorn Skyseer says Ishamuhale kills by instinct and passion, not for food or territory. He hunts because killing is his nature. To face him is to test whether you can withstand a predator's unbridled ferocity.",sp=0},{t="Baiting the Beast",b="Ishamuhale will not be found resting in a nest. To draw him out, you follow the plains' natural rhythm. Jorn tells you to kill a fresh zhevra and carry its carcass to a lone, withered dead tree on the plains northwest of Ratchet. The scent of blood on the arid wind brings Ishamuhale swiftly to claim his prey.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of Strength",b="When you bring Ishamuhale's fang back to Camp Taurajo, Jorn Skyseer sees it as a profound spiritual milestone, not merely a sign of victory. Tauren belief holds that overcoming so fierce a predator lets you absorb some of its raw strength. The test then turns inward: you must carry that might with temperance, honor, and restraint, rather than surrender to blind bloodlust.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ishamuhale?",a="Ishamuhale, known as Speartooth, is an exceptionally fierce sunscale raptor prowling the Barrens. He hunts relentlessly from instinct and passion, not merely from hunger.",al={"what is ishamuhale","who is speartooth","ishamuhale raptor lore"},it="target"},{q="How do you summon Ishamuhale?",a="To lure Ishamuhale out, you need a freshly slain zhevra. Hang its carcass at the designated dead tree northwest of Ratchet, the goblin port, and its scent will draw him from hiding.",al={"how to spawn ishamuhale","where is ishamuhale","bait ishamuhale"},gp=true},{q="Where does this quest start and end?",a="Jorn Skyseer, a tauren hunter, gives you this hunt at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. After you slay Ishamuhale, you return his fang to Jorn at the camp.",al={"ishamuhale quest giver","who gives ishamuhale","where to turn in ishamuhale"},gp=true},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer want Ishamuhale dead?",a="Jorn does not seek Ishamuhale's extermination out of malice. Tracking and besting him is a spiritual trial that tests you against nature's raw aggression and teaches temperance in bearing such ferocity.",al={"why kill ishamuhale","jorn skyseer motivation"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after completing Ishamuhale?",a="After you prove yourself against Ishamuhale, Jorn directs you toward greater threats disturbing the Barrens' balance. The next hunt concerns the Enraged Thunder Lizards to the south.",al={"quest after ishamuhale","next quest after raptor"},it="next_step"},{q="How does this quest fit into Sergra Darkthorn's chain?",a="Ishamuhale continues the grand hunting trials begun by Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads. After you prove your skill in the northern plains, Sergra sends you south to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo to face apex beasts.",al={"sergra darkthorn connection","crossroads hunting chain"},it="history"},{q="What is Ishamuhale's Fang for?",a="The fang is brought back to Jorn Skyseer as proof that you tracked and overcame the legendary raptor. To the tauren seer, it is far more than a simple hunting trophy; it represents Ishamuhale's indomitable spirit and predatory strength passing on to you. Jorn asks for it so he may recognize your completion of the trial and remind you to wield that acquired power with temperance.",al={"ishamuhale fang purpose","why keep ishamuhale's fang","what does the fang represent"},it="item",add="d2296b8f"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter, you learn that taking a mighty predator's life calls for discipline to control the fierce spirit you inherit.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you use fresh bait and terrain to draw an elusive predator out, practicing the patient, cunning art of the stalk.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you prove your worth by facing a legendary menace like Ishamuhale and make the roads between Ratchet and Taurajo marginally safer for Horde travelers."},kw={"camp taurajo","ishamuhale","jorn skyseer","ratchet","speartooth","sunscale raptor","the barrens","zhevra carcass"},rel={"quest:3261","quest:907","quest:860","subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Jorn Skyseer",level="19",faction="Horde",id=882,ri={"Ishamuhale's Fang"}},src={"Ishamuhale (quest)"}}
E["quest:883"] = {t="quest",n="Lakota'mani",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, hunters bring Lakota'mani's hoof to Jorn Skyseer after the hunt. The offering honors the mighty kodo's spirit and marks the hunter as an equal to its strength.",h="At Camp Taurajo, hunters bring Lakota'mani's hoof to Jorn Skyseer after the hunt.",sec={{t="The Earthshaker",b="Among the Barrens herds, Lakota'mani is a kodo of great size and endurance. In Taur-ahe, the tauren tongue, his name means “Earthshaker,” and his steps rumble across the plains. Tauren hunters track and defeat such a beast not for slaughter, but to meet the raw vigor of Kalimdor's wildlife in a sacred hunt.",sp=0},{t="A Hunt Honored at Camp Taurajo",b="When you bring Lakota'mani's hoof to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo, the hunt reaches its close. Jorn sees a new power and stride in hunters who return from the encounter. Presenting the trophy earns his blessing, honoring Lakota'mani's courage and primal spirit as companions on your path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the name Lakota'mani mean?",a="Lakota'mani means “Earthshaker” in Taur-ahe, the tauren tongue. The name fits the beast's immense size and the thunderous rumble of his steps across the plains.",al={"meaning of lakotamani","lakota'mani translation","what does lakotamani mean in taurahe"},it="name"},{q="Who is Jorn Skyseer?",a="Jorn Skyseer is a tauren elder and spiritual guide at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He reads signs, guides young hunters, and honors the great beasts slain across the plains.",al={"who is jorn","jorn skyseer role","where is jorn skyseer"},it="identity"},{q="Why do tauren collect the hooves of great beasts?",a="Tauren hunters carry a great beast's hoof as a token of its power. Presenting it to an elder honors the fallen beast's spirit and fortitude alongside the hunter's own.",al={"why take the hoof","hoof of lakota'mani meaning","kodo hoof trophy"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the beast Lakota'mani roam?",a="Lakota'mani roams the open savanna of the central and southern Barrens, among the lesser kodo herds, until an attentive hunter tracks him down.",al={"where is lakotamani","lakota'mani location","how to find lakotamani"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Jorn call the hunter 'Earthshaker'?",a="Jorn Skyseer calls the hunter “Earthshaker” because besting Lakota'mani joins the beast's spirit and courage with the hunter's own. The hunter takes on the name and walks with the same thunderous resolve.",al={"why am i called earthshaker","earthshaker title lore"}},{q="Does this hunt have spiritual significance beyond Camp Taurajo?",a="Yes. The hunt reflects the tauren belief in the Earthmother and the natural balance. By testing themselves against nature's greatest avatars, hunters prove their strength and carry that spiritual strength into future conflicts.",al={"lakotamani spiritual meaning","is this a tauren rite"}},{q="Why take the Hoof of Lakota'mani to Jorn Skyseer?",a="The hoof serves as proof that you faced and conquered the great kodo. Among the tauren, felling such a massive beast is a profound spiritual trial rather than mere slaughter. Presenting it to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo allows the elder to recognize your deed, helping you integrate the beast's thunderous strength and courage into your own spirit.",al={"why bring hoof to jorn","hoof of lakotamani purpose","why take lakotamani hoof to taurajo"},it="motive",add="3a1c6579"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter, defeating Lakota'mani fulfills an ancient hunting tradition and earns reverence and the proud title of Earthshaker from your elders.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking a legendary solitary kodo across the vast savanna tests your tracking skill, endurance, and field combat in the heart of Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Camp Taurajo is a hunting hub for the Horde. Claiming the plains' spoils helps build your reputation among the tribes."},kw={"camp taurajo","earthshaker","hoof of lakota'mani","jorn skyseer","kodo","lakota'mani","the barrens"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:barrens","quest:3261"},m={start="Hoof of Lakota'mani",["end"]="Jorn Skyseer",level="22",faction="Horde",id=883},src={"Lakota'mani (quest)"}}
E["quest:884"] = {t="quest",n="Owatanka",z="barrens",s="Across the southern Barrens, Owatanka roams as a swift thunder lizard known to the tauren as Bluebolt. Slaying the beast yields a crackling tailspike, carried to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo in honor of the elders’ tradition of learning from Kalimdor’s primordial beasts.",h="Across the southern Barrens, Owatanka roams as a swift thunder lizard known to the tauren as Bluebolt.",sec={{t="The Beast Called Bluebolt",b="Owatanka prowls the southern Barrens, where tauren hunters speak of him with reverence. Unlike his massive, plodding kin, he moves with blinding speed. The tauren call him Bluebolt, for the storm changed him.",sp=0},{t="Fed by the Sky's Rage",b="Tauren lore says lightning struck Owatanka long ago. The thunder lizard survived, and the strike filled him with unending energy and fury. Even after his death, his tailspike crackles with stray sparks when handled, a remnant of the storm’s power.",sp=0},{t="Trophy of Taurajo",b="Taking Owatanka's Tailspike to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo marks a hunter’s prowess and spirit. Jorn recognizes the encounter in the eyes of any hunter who has outmatched the beast’s speed. Presenting the trophy honors Bluebolt’s enduring swiftness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Owatanka?",a="Owatanka roams the Barrens as a swift thunder lizard known to the tauren as Bluebolt. He crackles with lightning energy.",al={"who is owatanka","what kind of beast is owatanka","owatanka lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Owatanka spark with lightning?",a="Tauren legend says lightning struck Owatanka long ago. The strike left him filled with endless energy and fury.",al={"why is owatanka electric","bluebolt lore","why sparks fly"},it="power"},{q="Who is Jorn Skyseer?",a="Jorn Skyseer is a tauren elder and spiritual guide at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He recognizes the power of the region’s great beasts and accepts trophies such as Owatanka's tailspike.",al={"where do i turn in owatanka","who is jorn","camp taurajo questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Owatanka wander?",a="Owatanka wanders the arid flatlands of the southern Barrens, through scrub and dirt pathways south of Camp Taurajo.",al={"owatanka location","where is owatanka","where to find bluebolt"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when you deliver Owatanka's Tailspike?",a="Jorn Skyseer commends you for outmatching the swift thunder lizard. He says keeping pace with Owatanka leaves a lasting spark of energy and power within you.",al={"owatanka turn in","what does jorn say","owatanka reward lore"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Owatanka dangerous compared to normal thunder lizards?",a="Yes. Owatanka is swift and carries innate electrical power from the lightning strike of legend, as well as the toughness of a thunder lizard.",al={"is owatanka hard","bluebolt danger","owatanka fight"},it="danger"},{q="Why bring Owatanka's Tailspike to Jorn Skyseer?",a="The tailspike still crackles with wild lightning even after the beast falls. Taking such a trophy to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo allows the elder tauren to recognize your triumph over Bluebolt and honor the endless energy gifted by the sky's wrath.",al={"why jorn skyseer tailspike","owatanka tailspike purpose","why bring tailspike to camp taurajo"},it="motive",add="f7b04852"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, hunting Bluebolt honors your people’s tradition of respecting wild spirits and claiming the vitality of the Barrens’ enduring beasts.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, besting Owatanka tests your stalking and speed against one of nature’s swiftest giants.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, Owatanka's tailspike shows how the sky’s elemental forces can reshape living creatures on Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, culling this unpredictable, lightning-charged predator protects the vulnerable supply trails near Camp Taurajo."},kw={"barrens","bluebolt","camp taurajo","jorn skyseer","owatanka","tailspike","thunder lizard"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","quest:3261","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},m={start="Owatanka's Tailspike",["end"]="Jorn Skyseer",level="24",faction="Horde",id=884},src={"Owatanka (quest)"}}
E["quest:885"] = {t="quest",n="Washte Pawne",z="barrens",s="Across the southern Barrens, Washte Pawne's quill leaves a sting that hunters carry to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo. Its pain makes the hunt a trial of regret for the tauren.",h="Across the southern Barrens, Washte Pawne's quill leaves a sting that hunters carry to Jorn Skyseer at Camp...",sec={{t="The Spirit Biter",b="Thunderhawks are elusive creatures of the Barrens, and wandering nomadic tribes treat them with reverence. Washte Pawne means “Spirit Biter” in Taurahe and holds a special place among them. Its death is no ordinary hunt: shamans whisper that striking down a thunderhawk can bring omens of triumph or misfortune.",sp=0},{t="A Lesson in Regret",b="After Washte Pawne falls, its feather burns with a pain that lingers on the skin. Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo explains that the ache is not poison, but regret. Taking a magnificent life bears a burden. The hunter must face that sorrow and turn it into lasting wisdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Washte Pawne mean?",a="In Taurahe, the language spoken by the tauren, Washte Pawne means “Spirit Biter.” It is the name of a rare thunderhawk that soars over the southern Barrens.",al={"washte pawne meaning","what is washte pawne","taurahe meaning spirit biter"},it="name"},{q="Why does Washte Pawne's feather cause pain?",a="Jorn Skyseer says the feather’s sting is the sharp pain of regret. It reflects the spiritual cost of ending the life of a magnificent creature.",al={"why does feather hurt","washte pawne feather sting"},it="power"},{q="Who do I bring Washte Pawne's Feather to?",a="Bring the feather to Jorn Skyseer, a tauren elder at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens.",al={"who takes washte pawne feather","feather turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What omen does slaying a thunderhawk bring?",a="Tauren tradition says a thunderhawk’s death can herald great fortune or immense doom. Jorn says Washte Pawne’s fall brings neither fate on its own; the hunter must make wisdom from remorse.",al={"thunderhawk omen","is killing thunderhawks bad"},it="history"},{q="Where is Washte Pawne found?",a="Washte Pawne roams the skies of the southern Barrens, often circling the savannah near Camp Taurajo.",al={"washte pawne location","where does spirit biter spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Jorn Skyseer think of you after slaying it?",a="Jorn does not condemn you. He sees that enduring the quill’s pain means you have mastered regret, turning spiritual grief into strength and understanding.",al={"jorn skyseer reaction","does jorn get mad"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the Shu'halo, taking Spirit Biter's life is a sacred lesson in respecting nature's balance. It teaches you to turn regret into inner wisdom.",["class:Hunter"]="Facing Washte Pawne tests your motives as a hunter. Taking a beast's life carries weight beyond a trophy.",["class:Shaman"]="The lingering sting of the thunderhawk's feather reveals the wild's spiritual force, a resonance you can recognize as a shaman who studies elemental harmonies.",["faction:Horde"]="At Camp Taurajo, you find a spiritual and hunting crossroads for the Horde, where young warriors face tests of conscience and martial skill."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","feather","jorn skyseer","spirit biter","taurahe","thunderhawk","washte pawne"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","quest:3261","zone:barrens"},m={start="Washte Pawne's Feather",["end"]="Jorn Skyseer",level="25",faction="Horde",id=885},src={"Washte Pawne (quest)"}}
E["quest:887"] = {t="quest",n="Southsea Freebooters",z="barrens",s="Along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet, Southsea Freebooters strike goblin trading vessels. Gazlowe hires adventurers to attack their camp and curb the raids.",h="Along the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet, Southsea Freebooters strike goblin trading vessels.",sec={{t="A Thorn in Gazlowe's Side",b="Ratchet's trade suffers from pirates on the Merchant Coast. The port sits in central Kalimdor, where merchant vessels travel between Kalimdor and the eastern continents. South of town, Southsea Freebooters hold a fortified beach camp. From there, they attack goblin cargo ships arriving and departing, cutting into profits and disrupting local shipping lanes.",sp=0},{t="Neglect from Undermine",b="Gazlowe blames the pirates and the Steamwheedle Cartel's naval leaders. The Trade Princes have spent immense sums on defensive fleets, yet Vice Admiral Grezzlik has failed to patrol the waters effectively. Frustrated by Undermine's slow response, Gazlowe hires independent mercenaries to thin the pirate brigands and cannoneers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Southsea Freebooters?",a="The Southsea Freebooters are pirates who operate across the southern oceans and the Great Sea. In the Barrens, they hold an armed beach camp south of Ratchet and raid merchant ships, plundering trade goods bound for Kalimdor.",al={"southsea pirates","who are southsea freebooters","freebooters lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gazlowe care so much about these pirates?",a="Gazlowe oversees Ratchet's port for the Steamwheedle Cartel. Each merchant ship the Freebooters intercept or plunder cuts into cartel revenue and weakens Ratchet's reputation as a secure trading haven.",al={"why gazlowe want pirates dead","gazlowe motivation","ratchet pirate problem"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the pirate camp located?",a="The Southsea camp lies along the Merchant Coast, down the shoreline south of Ratchet. Fortified tents, beached dinghies, and artillery positions manned by Southsea Cannoneers mark the camp.",al={"where are southsea brigands","cannoneer location","where is pirate camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Vice Admiral Grezzlik?",a="Vice Admiral Grezzlik oversees the Steamwheedle Cartel's trade fleets and protects its sea lanes. Gazlowe considers him ineffective, given the pirates operating brazenly off the Barrens coast.",al={"who is grezzlik","vice admiral grezzlik lore","steamwheedle admiral"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after culling the camp?",a="Culling the camp's defenders solves only part of the problem. After the brigands and cannoneers are routed, Gazlowe turns to tracking down the valuable cargo they hijacked, leading to investigations into his missing shipments.",al={"what comes next","southsea freebooters follow up","missing shipment"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are the Southsea Freebooters affiliated with the Alliance or Horde?",a="No. The Southsea Freebooters operate outside both factions and prey on Alliance vessels, Horde supply craft, and neutral goblin freighters alike.",al={"are freebooters horde","are pirates alliance","southsea faction"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Gazlowe hire an adventurer instead of using his own forces?",a="Ratchet is a bustling neutral port, but its defense forces are stretched thin maintaining order among rival Alliance and Horde travelers in town. The Steamwheedle Cartel's trade fleets, overseen by Vice Admiral Grezzlik, are supposed to handle maritime security, but Grezzlik has failed to check the pirate threat. With Undermine slow to act and his own Bruisers tied down guarding merchant docks, Gazlowe turns to independent, capable mercenaries like you to handle problems outside town limits without spending cartel military capital.",al={"why hire me","why not use ratchet guards","why doesn't gazlowe send his own guards"},it="why_me",add="56366fb6"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find opportunities for cutpurses in the Southsea Freebooters' camp, if you can slip past alert watchmen and heavy coastal artillery.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on Ratchet as a vital resupply corridor in Kalimdor. Clear sea routes protect supplies moving inland across the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","brigands","cannoneers","freebooters","gazlowe","grezzlik","pirates","ratchet","southsea","steamwheedle"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","quest:890","quest:888","zone:barrens","topic:pirate"},m={start="Gazlowe",level="14",id=887},src={"Southsea Freebooters (Classic)"}}
E["quest:888"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Booty",z="barrens",s="Pirate cargo off Ratchet’s coast has left Gazlowe choosing what matters most. Stolen Booty brings him two vital goods: boots for local laborers and a delicate telescopic lens needed to complete his observatory.",h="Pirate cargo off Ratchet’s coast has left Gazlowe choosing what matters most.",sec={{t="Pirate Hijacking",b="The Southsea Freebooters have troubled merchant lanes across the Great Sea for years. Their fortified camp just south of Ratchet brought them into direct conflict with Gazlowe. Pirates intercepted merchant vessels bound for the port and took valuable supplies from the Steamwheedle Cartel. Some goods could be written off as a cost of shipping. Specialized cargo mattered enough for Gazlowe to hire mercenaries to break into the pirate stronghold.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Pieces",b="Gazlowe has two practical priorities. Drizzlik sent a needed shipment of boots from Booty Bay for local laborers. The other item is specialized: a ground telescopic lens made for the observatory tower overlooking Ratchet. Its twin arrived safely by caravan through Durotar, but pirates seized this lens at sea. Until it is recovered, the observatory remains an empty frame.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gazlowe care so much about these two specific items?",a="Gazlowe cannot recover all the cargo, but the boots from Drizzlik in Booty Bay and the telescopic lens are irreplaceable. Local workers need the boots, and the precision lens is needed to complete the observatory overlooking Ratchet.",al={"why boots and lens","gazlowe items","what was stolen"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the two observatory lenses come from?",a="The observatory needs two lenses. The larger arrived safely with an overland caravan through Durotar. Southsea Freebooters intercepted the smaller lens, sent by sea, off the Barrens coast.",al={"telescopic lens origin","observatory lenses","how did gazlowe get the lenses"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Drizzlik?",a="Drizzlik is a goblin cobbler in Booty Bay, in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. He made and sent boots for Gazlowe’s crews in Ratchet before pirates seized the ship carrying them.",al={"drizzlik booty bay","who sent the boots","drizzlik"},it="people"},{q="Where are the stolen items hidden?",a="The crates of boots and the telescopic lens are hidden in the Southsea pirate camp on the Merchant Coast, just south of Ratchet.",al={"where are the boots","pirate camp location","where is the lens"},gp=true},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Gazlowe thanks you and praises your reliability once you return the items. He invites you to keep working for his commercial enterprise in Ratchet.",al={"stolen booty followup","next quest","what is next after stolen booty"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Ratchet have an observatory?",a="Goblin engineering depends on observation, navigation, and surveying the land and sea lanes nearby. A completed observatory tower lets Ratchet’s leaders watch merchant fleets, rival vessels, and threats along the Merchant Coast.",al={"ratchet telescope","gazlowe observatory","why does gazlowe want a telescope"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Shipment of Boots for?",a="The shipment contains boots crafted by Drizzlik down in Booty Bay, intended for Gazlowe's commercial operations in Ratchet. Running a busy neutral port and coordinating trade across Kalimdor takes plenty of gear, and Gazlowe cannot afford to let valuable imported footwear sit in pirate hands.",al={"why does gazlowe need boots","what are the boots for","shipment of boots"},it="item",add="7e99fee8"},{q="What is the Telescopic Lens for?",a="The telescopic lens is the crucial second optic Gazlowe requires to finish the Ratchet observatory. While the larger lens already arrived safely overland by caravan from Durotar, this smaller sea-bound lens was intercepted by the Southsea Freebooters, leaving the entire facility incomplete until you retrieve it.",al={"what is the lens for","telescopic lens use","why does gazlowe need the lens"},it="item",add="f85d62c5"},{q="Who are you sent against to recover the booty?",a="You are sent against the Southsea Freebooters encamped along the coast south of Ratchet. These cutthroats plundered the merchant vessel carrying Gazlowe's imported cargo and stashed the spoils around their shore camps.",al={"who has gazlowes booty","who stole the lens and boots","what pirates took the shipment"},it="target",add="2f3767f4"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Gazlowe’s observatory brings goblin precision optics into coastal construction. Practical infrastructure needs both heavy building and delicate glasswork.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Boots sent from Drizzlik in Booty Bay show how finished leather goods and cobbling move through Steamwheedle ports."},kw={"barrens","booty bay","drizzlik","gazlowe","ratchet","southsea freebooters","stolen booty","telescopic lens"},rel={"quest:890","quest:887","subzone:ratchet","topic:pirate","zone:barrens","subzone:booty-bay","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gazlowe",level="16",id=888,ri={"Shipment of Boots","Telescopic Lens"}},src={"Stolen Booty"}}
E["quest:889"] = {t="quest",n="Spirit of the Wind",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers travelers a burst of speed drawn from Agamaggan's blood shards. The captive quilboar's ritual helps them cross the Barrens swiftly.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth offers travelers a burst of speed drawn from Agamaggan's blood shards.",sec={{t="A Gift from Blood Shards",b="Crossing the Barrens quickly can help you avoid its beasts and centaur warbands. At Camp Taurajo, the captive quilboar Mangletooth draws on red crystalline blood shards scattered across the region. Give him ten, and he channels their lingering power into a burst of swiftness called the Spirit of the Wind.",sp=0},{t="Agamaggan's Ancient Breath",b="Quilboar honor Agamaggan, the Great Boar whose blood was spilled across central Kalimdor during the ancient War of the Ancients. Mangletooth knows the rites that channel that spilled blood, even in captivity. The ritual stirs wild vigor, lending a runner speed to match the zhevra herds. Though quilboar are bitter enemies of the Horde, Mangletooth shares Agamaggan's boons with travelers who bring him fresh shards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Spirit of the Wind?",a="The Spirit of the Wind is a brief blessing Mangletooth grants at Camp Taurajo. For ten blood shards, he lends travelers speed to cross the Barrens.",al={"what is spirit of the wind","spirit of the wind buff","speed buff mangletooth"},it="purpose"},{q="Who offers the Spirit of the Wind?",a="Mangletooth offers the blessing. He is a quilboar held prisoner by the Horde at Camp Taurajo, and performs the ritual when you earn his cooperation.",al={"who gives spirit of the wind","mangletooth","who turns in blood shards for speed"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mangletooth require blood shards?",a="Blood shards are crystalline fragments of Agamaggan's spilled blood. Mangletooth draws on the ancient demi-god's primal power within them to weave his boons.",al={"why blood shards","blood shard purpose","what does mangletooth do with shards"},it="motive"},{q="Can I receive this blessing more than once?",a="Yes. Bring Mangletooth ten blood shards each time, and he can channel the blessing whenever you return.",al={"is spirit of the wind repeatable","can i do this quest again","repeatable buff"},gp=true},{q="Why would a quilboar help members of the Horde?",a="Mangletooth is captive in Taurajo. He bargains his ancestral knowledge of Agamaggan's magic to secure his survival, dealing with travelers who gather the sacred shards he values.",al={"why does mangletooth help","friendly quilboar","why help horde"},it="side"},{q="How long does the blessing last?",a="The blessing fades before long, but Mangletooth's enchantment lends enough swiftness to ease travel across the Barrens for a time.",al={"how long is the buff","spirit of the wind duration","does speed buff last"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mangletooth need you instead of gathering Blood Shards himself?",a="Mangletooth is a captive of the Horde, kept under close watch in a cage within Camp Taurajo. Unable to roam the plains or harvest the fallen god's crystallized essence on his own, he must rely on passing adventurers to gather the shards in exchange for Agamaggan's ancient blessings.",al={"why cant mangletooth get shards","why does mangletooth need me","why me mangletooth"},it="why_me",add="c2e92fc0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="At Camp Taurajo, guards watch Mangletooth closely. Horde scouts use his knowledge of blood shard magic to cross the southern plains faster.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find the lingering power of the Wild God Agamaggan in these rites a fascinating, raw expression of primeval nature.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may hear an echo of your traditions in communing with the wind through crystallized divine essence, with its reverence for elemental and ancestral forces."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","blood shards","camp taurajo","mangletooth","quilboar","speed","spirit of the wind"},rel={"npc:mangletooth","quest:5052","topic:agamaggan","zone:barrens","quest:5043","quest:5042","quest:5046","quest:5045"},m={start="Mangletooth",level="20",faction="Horde",id=889,ri={"Blood Shard"}},src={"Spirit of the Wind"}}
E["quest:890"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Shipment",z="barrens",s="In Ratchet, Gazlowe waits for goods sent from Booty Bay across the Great Sea. He sends couriers to Wharfmaster Dizzywig to check the dock records, while the Southsea Freebooters remain a possible cause of the delay.",h="In Ratchet, Gazlowe waits for goods sent from Booty Bay across the Great Sea.",sec={{t="Ratchet's Vital Lifeline",b="Ratchet is the Steamwheedle Cartel's trading port on Kalimdor. Ships cross the Great Sea from Booty Bay with manufactured goods, exotic supplies, and heavy freight for the town's building and trade. When cargo goes missing, business suffers. Chief Engineer Gazlowe keeps close track of every crate brought into port.",sp=0},{t="Cross-Referencing the Cargo",b="The Southsea Freebooters haunt the coast south of Ratchet and often intercept merchant ships. Gazlowe checks his records before accusing the pirates or sending anyone into a fight. He sends his inventory ledger to Wharfmaster Dizzywig at the docks. Dizzywig oversees the unloading and storage of ship cargo, and can check whether goods were lost at sea or misplaced in a warehouse.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is in the missing shipment?",a="Gazlowe speaks of vital goods from Booty Bay, but Wharfmaster Dizzywig thinks the chief engineer is fretting over a custom order of boots from Drizzlek.",al={"gazlowe cargo","what was stolen","missing shipment goods"},it="item"},{q="Who is Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig oversees shipping records on Ratchet's docks. He manages cargo transfers between ships crossing the ocean and local warehouses for the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"dizzywig","who is dizzywig","ratchet dockmaster"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gazlowe suspect the Southsea Freebooters?",a="The Southsea Freebooters have camps along the Merchant Coast, just south of Ratchet. They prey on trade routes between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, making them suspects when merchant cargo disappears.",al={"freebooters role","pirate thieves","why pirates"},it="conflict"},{q="Where did the shipment originate?",a="The shipment came from Booty Bay, the goblin port at the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"shipment origin","where did it come from","booty bay cargo"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after giving the ledger to Dizzywig?",a="Dizzywig compares his shipping records with Gazlowe's ledger to see whether the cargo reached Ratchet's warehouses or was seized before unloading.",al={"dizzywig next steps","ledger follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't Gazlowe check the docks himself?",a="As Ratchet's Chief Engineer and leader, Gazlowe runs town affairs and expansion projects from his central office. He prefers to pay traveling adventurers to carry paperwork across town.",al={"why send me","gazlowe laziness"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Gazlowe want you to check on the shipment?",a="Gazlowe has been waiting ages for vital goods arriving from Booty Bay across the Great Sea. As the Chief Engineer and boss of Ratchet, keeping local trade moving and his warehouse stocked is central to his business and influence. He strongly suspects the nearby Southsea Freebooters intercepted the cargo, but he needs Wharfmaster Dizzywig to cross-reference his ledger against dock logs first so he can confirm whether the crates were stolen or simply misplaced among Ratchet's chaotic docks.",al={"why does gazlowe care about the shipment","gazlowe motive missing shipment","why find missing shipment"},it="motive",add="cd1ef655"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Gazlowe's need for spare parts, exotic imports, and custom gear from Booty Bay shows the difficulty of keeping Ratchet's machinery running far from goblin industrial centers.",["faction:Horde"]="Ratchet remains neutral and offers Horde travelers a port between Kalimdor and Stranglethorn Vale. Trade at its docks matters to both."},kw={"booty bay","dizzywig","drizzlek","freebooters","gazlowe","ledger","ratchet","shipment"},rel={"quest:887","quest:888","quest:1492","subzone:booty-bay","zone:barrens"},m={start="Gazlowe",["end"]="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",level="14",id=890},src={"The Missing Shipment"}}
E["quest:891"] = {t="quest",n="The Guns of Northwatch",z="barrens",s="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun in Ratchet wants the guns at Northwatch Hold silenced. Alliance gunners there have been blasting merchant vessels, so he sends you down the Merchant Coast to strike the artillery officers and bring back badges from fallen infantry.",h="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun in Ratchet wants the guns at Northwatch Hold silenced.",sec={{t="A Threat Along the Coast",b="Northwatch Hold guards the southern Barrens coast for the humans of Theramore. Its soldiers watch Horde activity in Kalimdor, but fear has made them see every unfamiliar sail as a threat. The guns on the ramparts fire without warning at passing ships, endangering Ratchet's merchant traffic and its privateering vessels.",sp=0},{t="Silencing the Ramparts",b="Captain Brightsun wants the attacks on his ships answered. Captain Fairmount commands Northwatch, with Whessan and Smythe directing its guns. Defeating them and taking Theramore medals from the garrison throws the artillery into disarray and gives Ratchet's ships room to travel along the Merchant Coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Northwatch Hold shooting at ships from Ratchet?",a="Northwatch's human soldiers fear attacks from the Horde and regional pirates. Their gunners fire on nearly every vessel passing the Merchant Coast, whether it flies a neutral or hostile flag.",al={"why are they shooting ships","why northwatch attacking ratchet","northwatch cannons firing"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun?",a="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun is a high elf privateer captain based in Ratchet. He commands a merchant fleet and protects local shipping from rivals, including the Alliance forces at Northwatch Hold.",al={"who gives this quest","thalo'thas brightsun","quest giver ratchet"},it="identity"},{q="Who are Captain Fairmount, Cannoneer Whessan, and Cannoneer Smythe?",a="Captain Fairmount commands Northwatch Hold's garrison. Whessan and Smythe direct the artillery batteries overlooking the sea. Defeating them disrupts the fortress's command and takes its heavy guns out of action.",al={"fairmount whessan smythe","northwatch officers","gun targets northwatch"},it="target"},{q="What are Theramore Medals?",a="Theramore Medals are military insignias carried by the human foot soldiers and guards at Northwatch Hold. Captain Brightsun asks for them as proof that the privateers' deaths have been avenged and the garrison decimated.",al={"theramore medal","why collect medals","what drops medals"},it="item"},{q="Where is Northwatch Hold located?",a="Northwatch Hold sits on the southeastern bluffs of the Barrens, south of Ratchet along the Merchant Coast.",al={"where is northwatch","northwatch location","where are the guns of northwatch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Northwatch Hold officially part of Theramore?",a="Yes. Theramore established Northwatch Hold to secure a military foothold on mainland Kalimdor. Its isolated garrison acts with fierce aggression and suspicion toward those traveling through the Barrens.",al={"is northwatch theramore","alliance faction northwatch","jaina northwatch"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun want Northwatch Hold attacked?",a="Captain Brightsun commands a merchant fleet out of Ratchet, and Northwatch Hold has been devastating his livelihood. Paralyzed by suspicion, the Alliance gunners in the fortress blast away at virtually any vessel sailing past the Merchant Coast, treating neutral privateers and trading ships like hostile raiders. Having lost yet another ship and its crew to Northwatch's cannons, Brightsun wants direct vengeance against the officers responsible and an end to the bombardment threatening his entire fleet.",al={"why attack northwatch","brightsun motive","why does brightsun want northwatch destroyed"},it="motive",add="30184c04"},{q="Why does Captain Brightsun need you instead of handling Northwatch himself?",a="Ratchet thrives on neutrality, relying on an open harbor that welcomes Horde and independent travelers alike without formally declaring war on Theramore or the Alliance. A direct military strike led by Ratchet's goblin authorities or Brightsun's surviving privateers could provoke an open conflict with Jaina Proudmoore's forces across the sea. By hiring an independent adventurer, Brightsun can silence the guns and avenge his lost vessels without dragging the port into formal warfare.",al={"why hire me","why doesnt ratchet attack northwatch","why doesn't brightsun attack"},it="why_me",add="f93e1604"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can strike Northwatch Hold and blunt an aggressive Alliance fortification in the Barrens, securing Kalimdor's borders for your people.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how isolation far from home strains Theramore's frontier garrisons and feeds reckless hostility."},kw={"barrens","brightsun","cannons","fairmount","merchant coast","northwatch","ratchet","smythe","theramore","whessan"},rel={"npc:captain-thalo-thas-brightsun","subzone:ratchet","subzone:merchant-coast","zone:barrens","topic:alliance"},m={start="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun",level="20",faction="Horde",id=891,ri={"Theramore Medal"}},src={"The Guns of Northwatch (Classic)"}}
E["quest:892"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Shipment",z="barrens",s="At Ratchet’s docks, Dizzywig’s ledger points away from harbor graft and toward the Southsea Freebooters. Gazlowe receives the records and prepares to reclaim his lost cargo.",h="At Ratchet’s docks, Dizzywig’s ledger points away from harbor graft and toward the Southsea Freebooters.",sec={{t="Books Balanced at the Docks",b="Ratchet’s trade and its port bring constant logistical headaches. When a shipment fails to arrive, Gazlowe suspects bad harbor accounts or foul play on the piers. Wharfmaster Dizzywig examines the manifest and insists his books are clean. The intake records account for everything, so the missing merchandise never made it onto the dock.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Freebooters",b="With Dizzywig clearing the port’s own operations of embezzlement, the Southsea Freebooters camped down the coast remain the plausible culprits. Dizzywig returns the ledger and mentions separate crates waiting from Undermine. He sends you back to Gazlowe, Ratchet’s chief engineer. Convinced of Dizzywig’s loyalty, Gazlowe turns from supply ledgers to organizing an expedition to reclaim his stolen booty.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is in Gazlowe's ledger?",a="Gazlowe’s ledger holds shipping manifests, cargo inventories, and port intake logs for goods arriving in Ratchet. Dizzywig reviews the records to see whether the missing crates were checked in from the ships.",al={"what is the ledger","gazlowes ledger","dock manifest"},it="item"},{q="Who actually stole Gazlowe's shipment?",a="Gazlowe suspects the Southsea Freebooters, pirates camped along the coast south of Ratchet. Dizzywig’s records show no discrepancy at the docks, so Gazlowe turns his attention to the raiders.",al={"who stole the shipment","who took the cargo","who has the shipment"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Gazlowe trust Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="Gazlowe trusts Dizzywig, who is on his payroll and has served him reliably. Gazlowe believes the wharfmaster knows better than to cheat him and accepts his word that the books are clean.",al={"is dizzywig lying","does gazlowe trust dizzywig","dizzywig honest"},it="ties"},{q="What are the items from Undermine that Dizzywig mentions?",a="Dizzywig mentions separate goods from Undermine, the goblin capital, waiting for Gazlowe to collect when he has a moment away from managing the town.",al={"undermine shipment","what is coming from undermine","undermine goods"},it="item"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Returning the ledger to Gazlowe leads to Stolen Booty. You are hired to infiltrate the Southsea Freebooter camps along the southern coast of the Barrens and take back the lost cargo.",al={"what quest is next","next step after missing shipment","where to go next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Wharfmaster Dizzywig located?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig oversees the Ratchet docks, near the pier platforms where merchant vessels load and unload their cargo.",al={"where is dizzywig","dizzywig location","find wharfmaster"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wharfmaster Dizzywig send you back to Gazlowe?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig is responsible for managing the incoming and outgoing cargo along the docks. Gazlowe sent you to audit Dizzywig's records regarding the missing crates, and by handing back the ledger, Dizzywig clears his own name. His shipping manifests prove the goods never officially cleared his port, shifting the blame away from the docks and pointing the finger squarely at the local Southsea Freebooters.",al={"why does dizzywig want this","dizzywig motive","why send ledger to gazlowe"},it="motive",add="96f6dc82"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Harbor paperwork shows how easily goods can vanish between sea and shore, a classic smugglers’ trick.",["faction:Horde"]="Ratchet is neutral, and keeping Gazlowe happy helps maintain steady trade routes and goblin neutrality that benefits the Horde.",["faction:Alliance"]="Operating in the Barrens calls for careful alliances. Helping Ratchet’s leadership supports a reliable foothold in central Kalimdor for the Alliance."},kw={"barrens","dizzywig","freebooters","gazlowe","ledger","pirates","ratchet","shipment","undermine"},rel={"quest:890","quest:888","quest:887","quest:1492","subzone:ratchet","topic:pirate","zone:barrens"},m={start="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",["end"]="Gazlowe",level="14",id=892},src={"The Missing Shipment (2)"}}
E["quest:893"] = {t="quest",n="Weapons of Choice",z="barrens",s="At Camp Taurajo, Tatternack Steelforge investigates reports of sturdy Razormane weapons. He sends travelers past the Field of Giants to recover them, so the Horde can judge the threat.",h="At Camp Taurajo, Tatternack Steelforge investigates reports of sturdy Razormane weapons.",sec={{t="A Curious Advancement",b="The Razormane are making unusually durable weapons in the southern Barrens. Most quilboar are dismissed as crude fighters with tools of wood, bone, and stone, so the reports have caught the Horde’s attention. Tatternack Steelforge, an orc smith at Camp Taurajo, is investigating under orders from Warchief Thrall. He doubts the quilboar know proper metalwork and wants proof of whether they have learned new techniques or found better supplies.",sp=0},{t="Armaments of the Razormane",b="Tatternack needs weapons from different parts of the Razormane arsenal to study their craft. South of the Field of Giants, scouts face Razormane war camps and seize weapons from their fighters. Razormane Stalkers carry backstabber daggers, Razormane Seers wield charred wands, and frenzied shock troops bear heavy war shields. Each item offers a glimpse of the martial and mystic arts behind the Razormane push against Horde territory.",sp=0},{t="Underestimating the Enemy",b="Tatternack finds the recovered weapons far better made and stronger than the Horde expected. Their quality shows that the Horde has underestimated the Razormane. Tatternack sets aside his forge work to study the materials, suspecting an outside influence or a newly found resource is helping their war effort.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tatternack Steelforge?",a="Tatternack Steelforge is an orc blacksmith and armorer stationed at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. Under orders from Warchief Thrall, he studies enemy weapons and makes gear for local forces.",al={"tatternack steelforge","who gives weapons of choice","taurajo blacksmith"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tatternack want quilboar weapons?",a="Reports say the southern Razormane have unusually durable weapons despite no known tradition of skilled smithing. Tatternack wants to study their daggers, wands, and shields to learn how they are made and whether they pose a greater threat.",al={"why collect quilboar weapons","reason for weapons of choice","tatternack motives"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Razormane quilboar located for this task?",a="The Razormane camps lie in the far southern Barrens, past the Field of Giants and west of the road toward the Great Lift and Thousand Needles.",al={"where are the quilboar","weapons of choice location","where to find razormane"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Which quilboar carry the required weapons?",a="Razormane Stalkers carry Razormane Backstabber daggers, Razormane Seers wield Charred Razormane Wands, and Razormane Warfrenzies carry sturdy Razormane War Shields.",al={"who drops backstabber","who drops wand","who drops war shield"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What does Tatternack discover from the weapons?",a="Tatternack finds the weapons remarkably well made, far beyond what the Horde expected from quilboar. He investigates their raw materials in the follow-up, A New Ore Sample.",al={"what does tatternack find out","weapons of choice outcome","are quilboar smiths"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde worried about quilboar manufacturing weapons?",a="The Horde depends on strong metalwork and disciplined fighters to hold the vast Barrens against its many local threats. If the prolific Razormane can make sturdy iron or steel weapons in great numbers, they could overwhelm frontier outposts such as Camp Taurajo.",al={"why do quilboar weapons matter","quilboar threat level"},it="threat"},{q="Who are you sent against for Weapons of Choice?",a="You are sent against the Razormane quilboar entrenched in southern Barrens, south past the Field of Giants. Long considered crude, primitive scavengers by the Horde, specific ranks among them—their stalkers, seers, and warfrenzies—have begun wielding unexpectedly sturdy and refined armaments that threaten nearby settlements.",al={"who are the targets","which quilboar do i fight","weapons of choice enemies"},it="target",add="17648e33"},{q="What is the Razormane Backstabber for?",a="The Razormane Backstabber is carried by Razormane Stalkers. Tatternack Steelforge requires it as an example of the tribe's bladed craft, seeking to examine its metalwork and edge to determine whether quilboar smiths are truly capable of forging tempered steel.",al={"what is the dagger for","razormane backstabber purpose","why collect the backstabber"},it="item",add="3f25a614"},{q="What is the Charred Razormane Wand for?",a="Carried by Razormane Seers, the Charred Razormane Wand serves as proof of the quilboar's blending of crude implements with arcane or elemental power. Tatternack intends to inspect its construction to see how the tribe channels magic through their manufactured tools.",al={"charred wand purpose","why collect charred razormane wand","what does tatternack do with the wand"},it="item",add="5a3ff8c6"},{q="What is the Razormane War Shield for?",a="Wielded by frontline Razormane Warfrenzies, this heavy bulwark offers Tatternack direct insight into quilboar defensive armor. Inspecting its plating and structural reinforcement allows him to judge whether their crafting methods pose a significant threat to Horde warriors.",al={"razormane war shield purpose","why collect razormane shield","what is the shield for"},it="item",add="d1102a3e"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="For a smith, these recovered weapons show how an enemy’s materials shape its readiness on the frontier.",["faction:Horde"]="Camp Taurajo is vulnerable on the southern frontier, so knowledge of Razormane military advances helps defend the Barrens’ trade routes.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know honor calls for respect for martial strength. Tatternack’s duty to Thrall means recognizing when an enemy is becoming dangerous."},kw={"backstabber","barrens","quilboar","razormane","steelforge","tatternack","taurajo","wand","war shield"},rel={"npc:tatternack-steelforge","quest:1153","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:quilboar","subzone:field-of-giants","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},m={start="Tatternack Steelforge",level="24",faction="Horde",id=893,ri={"Charred Razormane Wand","Razormane Backstabber","Razormane War Shield"}},src={"Weapons of Choice"}}
E["quest:894"] = {t="quest",n="Samophlange",z="barrens",s="At a Venture Company outpost in the northern Barrens, Sputtervalve wants a device called a samophlange. He sends you southwest of the Sludge Fen to find it.",h="At a Venture Company outpost in the northern Barrens, Sputtervalve wants a device called a samophlange.",sec={{t="A Peculiar Contraption",b="In the northern Barrens, Sputtervalve cannot explain what the Venture Company is building. The goblin engineer and tinker works in Ratchet, while the rival company experiments southwest of the Sludge Fen. Its people call one device a samophlange. Sputtervalve does not know its purpose or value, but wants to study its design before his competitors can profit from it.",sp=0},{t="Infiltrating the Rig",b="The Venture Company guards its research site with armed overseers, deforesters, and machinery. Sputtervalve gives you an intercepted operating manual to help shut down the rig safely. At the central control station, you find a locked console with levers, lights, and gauges. Three control valves keep the rig's pressure in order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a samophlange?",a="Sputtervalve does not know exactly what the samophlange is or does. The Venture Company made it as an experimental mechanical component at its site southwest of the Sludge Fen.",al={"what is a samophlange","samophlange purpose","what does a samophlange do"},it="item"},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin engineer and tinker in Ratchet. He is interested in Venture Company trade secrets and hires adventurers to disrupt its works and seize its inventions.",al={"who is sputtervalve","sputtervalve location","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the control console located?",a="The control console is inside the Venture Company research site north of the Crossroads and southwest of the polluted Sludge Fen in the Barrens.",al={"console location","where is console","where to find samophlange"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Venture Company in the Barrens?",a="The Venture Company is a cartel that exploits Kalimdor's natural resources for profit. In the Barrens, its workers clear forests, drill for oil, and build experimental rigs near the Sludge Fen.",al={"venture co barrens","why are venture co here","sludge fen operation"},it="why_here"},{q="How do you disengage the samophlange safely?",a="The console has three open control valves and a keyhole. You use Sputtervalve's retrieved manual to bypass the safety locks and manipulate the valves to detach the module.",al={"how to use console","control console operating manual","manual instructions"},gp=true},{q="Does Sputtervalve work for the Venture Company?",a="No. Sputtervalve works independently of the Venture Company and seeks to steal its engineering discoveries so he can examine them.",al={"is sputtervalve venture co","sputtervalve faction"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Sputtervalve want the samophlange?",a="Sputtervalve is driven by professional curiosity and goblin ingenuity. He discovered that the Venture Company has established a secretive research operation near the Sludge Fen to experiment with a strange device called a samophlange. Not even knowing what such an apparatus actually is or does, he is determined to get his hands on it and dismantle its engineering secrets for himself.",al={"why does sputtervalve want this done","sputtervalve motive","why get the samophlange"},it="motive",add="122be8ea"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can recognize Sputtervalve's interest in a rival's designs. His pursuit shows how fiercely goblins compete over engineering discoveries.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you have reason to oppose the Venture Company's work. Its exploitation and chemical runoff threaten the Barrens, and its facilities endanger the land you defend."},kw={"barrens","control console","goblin engineering","samophlange","sludge fen","sputtervalve","venture company"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","topic:venture-company","subzone:sludge-fen","zone:barrens"},m={start="Sputtervalve",["end"]="Control Console",level="14",id=894},src={"Samophlange (Classic)"}}
E["quest:895"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Baron Longshore",z="barrens",s="On Ratchet's docks, Chief Engineer Gazlowe posts a bounty for Baron Longshore. The pirate captain hails from Gilneas and commands vessels of the Southsea Freebooters. His presence along the Merchant Coast threatens goblin merchant shipping across the region.",h="On Ratchet's docks, Chief Engineer Gazlowe posts a bounty for Baron Longshore.",sec={{t="Piracy on the Merchant Coast",b="South of Ratchet, the Southsea Freebooters hold fortified camps along the Merchant Coast. Their pirates harass merchant vessels and disrupt the sea lanes the Steamwheedle Cartel relies on between Ratchet, Booty Bay, and points beyond. Under captains such as Baron Longshore, the raids drain the local goblin administration and threaten trade along the coast.",sp=0},{t="A Captain from Gilneas",b="Baron Longshore comes from Gilneas, the isolated human kingdom across the sea. On Kalimdor, he commands the pirate vessel Heedless and leads crews ashore just north of Northwatch Hold. Chief Engineer Gazlowe answers with a bounty, calling for Longshore's identifiable head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Baron Longshore?",a="Baron Longshore is a pirate captain from Gilneas who commands the Heedless for the Southsea Freebooters. He raids shipping lanes along the shore south of Ratchet.",al={"baron longshore","who is longshore","captain longshore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gazlowe want him dead?",a="Longshore's piracy threatens merchant shipping out of Ratchet. Gazlowe has placed a bounty on his head to protect trade and Steamwheedle profits.",al={"why kill longshore","gazlowe bounty reason","why is longshore wanted"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Baron Longshore be found?",a="Baron Longshore frequents Southsea Freebooter camps along the Merchant Coast, south of Ratchet and just north of Northwatch Hold.",al={"longshore location","where is longshore","baron longshore spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What ship does Baron Longshore captain?",a="Baron Longshore captains the Heedless, a feared pirate ship on the open seas around the Merchant Coast.",al={"longshore ship","name of longshore boat","heedless ship"}},{q="Is Baron Longshore an Alliance noble?",a="Baron Longshore bears the title of Baron and comes from Gilneas, but he leads the Southsea Freebooters as a renegade corsair, unaffiliated with the current Alliance leadership.",al={"is longshore alliance","gilneas noble pirate","longshore gilneas"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the bounty poster located?",a="The wanted poster hangs on the boards near the bank in Ratchet's port town.",al={"where is wanted poster","longshore poster location","how to start longshore quest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Baron Longshore's Head for?",a="Gazlowe's bounty notice specifically demands that the remains of the infamous pirate captain be identifiable before a reward is paid. Severing Baron Longshore's head provides irrefutable physical proof that the captain of the Heedless has met his end and will no longer prey upon Ratchet's merchant vessels.",al={"baron longshores head","why take baron longshore head","proof of baron longshore kill"},it="item",add="65a73854"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how far deserters and outcasts from the Eastern Kingdoms have scattered across the seas when a Gilnean baron commands cutthroats on Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you benefit when Southsea Freebooters near Ratchet are cleared out and the port stays open for Horde supplies moving into the Barrens.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you rely on neutral shipping between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, which Longshore's piracy disrupts."},kw={"baron longshore","gazlowe","gilneas","heedless","merchant coast","pirate bounty","ratchet","southsea freebooters"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","subzone:merchant-coast","quest:887","zone:barrens"},m={start="WANTED",["end"]="Gazlowe",level="16",id=895,ri={"Baron Longshore's Head"}},src={"WANTED: Baron Longshore"}}
E["quest:896"] = {t="quest",n="Miner's Fortune",z="barrens",s="Wharfmaster Dizzywig has heard of a fist-sized emerald at the Venture Company's Boulder Lode Mine. He hires you to take the Cats Eye Emerald from the mine's supervisors and share the profits.",h="Wharfmaster Dizzywig has heard of a fist-sized emerald at the Venture Company's Boulder Lode Mine.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Docks",b="Wharfmaster Dizzywig hears the merchants who pass through Ratchet's harbor on the routes between Ratchet and Booty Bay. Word reaches him of a huge gem found deep in the Boulder Lode Mine. The Venture Company strips the northern Barrens for its own gain, so few are likely to ask questions if its finest recent find disappears.",sp=0},{t="A Cut of the Lode",b="Northeast of the Sludge Fen, laborers fill the Boulder Lode Mine's rocky shaft. The Venture Co. Overseers and Enforcers have taken the Cats Eye Emerald, and an ordinary digger cannot claim a prize so rare. You need to face the armed managers, secure the stone, and bring it to Dizzywig. He can judge its value against the market in Undermine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig is a goblin dock official in Ratchet. He oversees cargo and passengers traveling by sea to and from Booty Bay, and trades in gossip, rumors, and merchant information.",al={"dizzywig","who gives miners fortune","ratchet wharfmaster"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Boulder Lode Mine located?",a="The Boulder Lode Mine lies in the northern Barrens, in the hills just northeast of the Sludge Fen's oil operation.",al={"boulder lode mine location","where is the emerald","venture co mine barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who holds the Cats Eye Emerald at the mine?",a="The Venture Co. Overseers and Venture Co. Enforcers hold the Cats Eye Emerald. They direct and guard the mining work at the Boulder Lode Mine.",al={"who drops cats eye emerald","cats eye emerald drop","where is cats eye emerald"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the Venture Company's interest in the Barrens?",a="The Venture Company is a goblin trade syndicate that rapidly exploits resources. In the northern Barrens, it drills at the Sludge Fen and digs at Boulder Lode Mine for timber, oil, and minerals, with little regard for local ecology.",al={"why is venture co in barrens","venture company barrens"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Dizzywig reference Undermine?",a="Undermine is the goblin cartels' underground island city and ancestral capital. Its markets set prices for precious gems and rare goods across Azeroth.",al={"undermine mention","gem rates undermine"},it="history"},{q="Does Dizzywig actually share the profits?",a="Dizzywig promises you half the estimated Undermine market value when you deliver the Cats Eye Emerald, and he honors the bargain.",al={"does dizzywig split 50 50","dizzywig payout"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Why does Wharfmaster Dizzywig want the Cats Eye Emerald?",a="As the wharfmaster of Ratchet, Dizzywig monitors trade passing between Kalimdor and Booty Bay and keeps an ear to the ground for lucrative opportunities. When word reached him that a massive gem was unearthed at the Venture Company's Boulder Lode Mine, he saw a chance for personal enrichment. By using an independent mercenary to slip in and lift the prize, he can sell it to wealthy private buyers and pocket a fortune without entangling port authorities.",al={"why does dizzywig want the emerald","dizzywig emerald motive","why steal the cats eye emerald"},it="motive",add="b052118f"},{q="What is the Cats Eye Emerald for?",a="The Cats Eye Emerald is a fist-sized, exceptionally rare gemstone with no inherent magical purpose mentioned in Dizzywig's scheme. Its value lies entirely in its sheer size, purity, and astronomical market worth among gem brokers and collectors in places like Undermine.",al={"cats eye emerald use","what is the cats eye emerald","why is the emerald valuable"},it="item",add="0186bc21"},{q="Who are you sent against at the Boulder Lode Mine?",a="You are sent into the Boulder Lode Mine against the Venture Company, an unscrupulous goblin mining conglomerate aggressively stripping the northern Barrens of resources. Their Enforcers and Overseers guard the dig site, run the labor crews, and have taken possession of the extraordinary emerald discovered by their miners.",al={"who holds the emerald","venture co boulder lode mine","boulder lode mine overseers"},it="target",add="bd4101f7"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can recognize how rare a whole emerald the size of a fist is. Gems of that size almost never survive excavation without cracking or breaking.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know how to slip into a hostile camp and take a guarded gemstone from greedy overseers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde member, you strike at the Venture Company's managers at Boulder Lode Mine and disrupt an industrial cartel encroaching on Horde-held Barrens lands."},kw={"boulder lode mine","cats eye emerald","dizzywig","enforcer","overseer","ratchet","sludge fen","venture co"},rel={"subzone:boulder-lode-mine","subzone:ratchet","topic:venture-company","subzone:sludge-fen","quest:1492","quest:764","subzone:booty-bay","zone:barrens"},m={start="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",level="18",id=896,ri={"Cats Eye Emerald"}},src={"Miner's Fortune (Classic)"}}
E["quest:897"] = {t="quest",n="The Harvester",z="barrens",s="A severed head found in the southern Barrens brings The Harvester’s strange presence to Camp Taurajo. Jorn Skyseer examines the remains, and the creature’s intrusion raises concerns for the land’s spiritual and ecological balance.",h="A severed head found in the southern Barrens brings The Harvester’s strange presence to Camp Taurajo.",sec={{t="An Unnatural Intruder",b="In the southern Barrens, you find the severed head of a silithid called the Harvester. Lions, raptors, and kodos roam these grasslands, but this chitinous insectoid is unlike the native wildlife. Its presence suggests an alien ecology has reached the open plains of Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Jorn Skyseer's Premonition",b="At Camp Taurajo, tauren mystic Jorn Skyseer examines the Harvester’s head. The creature’s spirit has already fled, so Jorn cannot divine its origin. He recognizes the remains as a profound threat and fears its intrusion may herald a grim future for the Horde. Darker mysteries are brewing beneath the sands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Harvester?",a="The Harvester is a large silithid insectoid prowling the southern Barrens. Its chitinous form is unlike the region’s native wildlife.",al={"who is the harvester","what kind of bug is the harvester","harvester creature"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Jorn Skyseer?",a="Jorn Skyseer is a respected tauren elder and spiritual guide at Camp Taurajo. He watches over the plains’ spiritual health and counsels others when the land’s balance is threatened.",al={"jorn skyseer","who is the turn in npc","jorn taurajo"},it="people"},{q="Where does the Harvester come from?",a="Jorn Skyseer cannot divine the Harvester’s exact origin from its severed head. The creature comes from the silithid hives spreading up from the deep deserts to the south.",al={"where do silithid come from","harvester origin","silithid source"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the creature disturb Jorn Skyseer?",a="The Harvester’s unnatural form and foreign spirit deeply disturb Jorn. He senses its presence in the Barrens is no random occurrence, but a warning of an unnatural threat to come.",al={"why is jorn worried","jorn skyseer reaction","grim future"},it="threat"},{q="How do you start this quest?",a="You begin by slaying the rare silithid called the Harvester in the southern Barrens and taking its severed head. Then you seek the elders’ guidance at Camp Taurajo.",al={"how to get quest","harvester head drop","start harvester"},gp=true},{q="What does Jorn tell you to do next?",a="Jorn offers no immediate counterattack. He believes the Horde must prepare and stay vigilant as the mystery of the encroaching silithid slowly unfolds.",al={"follow up quest","what after harvester head","jorn next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Why bring the Harvester's Head to Jorn Skyseer?",a="The severed head belongs to a bizarre, insect-like monstrosity completely alien to the natural balance of the Barrens. Anyone gazing upon its unnatural form can sense that something deeply wrong has intruded upon the plains. Bringing it directly to Jorn Skyseer, a wise tauren seer attuned to the land and the spirits at Camp Taurajo, is an effort to discern what the terrifying creature was and understand what threat it might pose to the realm.",al={"why bring the head to camp taurajo","why show harvester head to jorn","harvester head purpose"},it="motive",add="5f65deeb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a Shu'halo, you know the Earth Mother’s harmony is paramount. An entity that defies the natural order signals deep spiritual disharmony.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you understand Jorn Skyseer’s frustration: the spirit has fled the head, preventing communion with the elemental forces to discover the creature’s true origin.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the corruptive, parasitic nature of these alien burrowers invading the savannah.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Camp Taurajo guards the Barrens’ southern reaches. An invasive predator in the surrounding bluffs threatens the area’s security."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","harvester","harvester's head","insectoid","jorn skyseer","silithid"},rel={"quest:3261","zone:barrens"},m={start="Harvester's Head",["end"]="Jorn Skyseer",level="24",faction="Horde",id=897},src={"The Harvester (quest)"}}
E["quest:898"] = {t="quest",n="Free From the Hold",z="barrens",s="Gilthares Firebough is held at Northwatch Hold after Alliance forces sink his ship off the Barrens coast. The elf deckhand wants to reach his captain in Ratchet.",h="Gilthares Firebough is held at Northwatch Hold after Alliance forces sink his ship off the Barrens coast.",sec={{t="Imprisoned at Northwatch",b="Gilthares Firebough is held in the dungeons at Northwatch Hold. Theramore uses the fortress as its military foothold on the Barrens coast, where its garrison watches for threats. Gilthares had been aboard a ship carrying moonshine along the trade route between Ratchet and Booty Bay when Alliance forces bombarded it and sent it beneath the sea. He alone survived the wreck. The soldiers took him to Northwatch and accused him of being an enemy agent conspiring against the Alliance.",sp=0},{t="A Smuggler's Flight",b="Gilthares says he is only a deckhand who was carrying illicit liquor. With help from Horde forces, he fights his way out of Northwatch Hold and flees north along the shore toward Ratchet. Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun welcomes him back to the crew of the Thalo'dan Privateers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gilthares Firebough?",a="Gilthares Firebough is an elf deckhand sailing under Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun. He served aboard a transport carrying moonshine between Ratchet and Booty Bay before Theramore troops sank the vessel and imprisoned him.",al={"gilthares","who is gilthares firebough","who is the prisoner in northwatch hold"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Gilthares arrested by Theramore forces?",a="Alliance soldiers at Northwatch Hold intercepted Gilthares's ship off the Barrens coast and blasted it into the sea. Wary of maritime traffic near their stronghold, they condemned him as an operative hostile to the Alliance.",al={"why did theramore arrest him","why is gilthares in jail","why was the ship sunk"},it="origin"},{q="Where does Gilthares go once freed?",a="Gilthares flees north from Northwatch Hold along the Barrens' eastern shore to Ratchet. There, he rejoins Captain Brightsun by the docks.",al={"where to escort gilthares","gilthares destination","where does the escort go"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are the Thalo'dan Privateers?",a="The Thalo'dan Privateers are a maritime crew led by Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun and based in Ratchet. They ship goods and smuggle bootleg moonshine across the sea between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"thalodan privateers","captain brightsun crew","who does brightsun lead"},it="people"},{q="Why is Northwatch Hold attacking civilian or smuggler ships?",a="Northwatch Hold is Theramore's fortress in the Barrens, between Horde territory and key sea routes. Its commanders' paranoia and strict military orders lead them to see nearly any non-Alliance ship as a Horde operation or pirate threat.",al={"why is northwatch hostile","theramore aggression barrens","northwatch hold purpose"},it="conflict"},{q="What cargo was the sunken ship carrying?",a="The sunken vessel carried illicit moonshine for distribution between Ratchet and Booty Bay, not weapons or military supplies.",al={"what was on the ship","gilthares cargo","what were they transporting"},it="item"},{q="Why does Gilthares Firebough want to escape Northwatch Hold?",a="Gilthares is the sole survivor of a sunken smuggling vessel, branded an enemy and threat to the Alliance by overzealous Theramore soldiers at Northwatch Hold. Trapped in their dungeons, his life is on the line unless someone breaks him out so he can safely return to Ratchet and Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun.",al={"gilthares motive","why escape northwatch hold","why help gilthares firebough"},it="motive",add="6c76d4e5"},{q="Why does Gilthares Firebough need your help escaping?",a="Gilthares is a mere deckhand, currently locked deep inside an enemy stronghold crawling with hostile Theramore troops. Having lost his entire crew when their ship was destroyed, he has no weapons, allies, or means to fight his way past the guards without an able adventurer clearing a path to freedom.",al={"why does gilthares need help","why can't gilthares escape alone","why me gilthares"},it="why_me",add="153b57ec"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can strike at Theramore's foothold on the Barrens coast by freeing a smuggler held at Northwatch Hold."},kw={"booty bay","captain brightsun","escort","gilthares firebough","moonshine","northwatch hold","privateers","ratchet","smuggler","theramore"},rel={"npc:gilthares-firebough","npc:captain-thalo-thas-brightsun","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:alliance","subzone:booty-bay"},m={start="Gilthares Firebough",["end"]="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun",level="20",faction="Horde",id=898},src={"Free From the Hold"}}
E["quest:899"] = {t="quest",n="Consumed by Hatred",z="barrens",s="Mankrik turns his grief at the Crossroads into a campaign against the Bristleback quilboar. The orc was separated from his wife in a violent ambush, and now he calls on Horde travelers to kill the creatures and bring back their tusks.",h="Mankrik turns his grief at the Crossroads into a campaign against the Bristleback quilboar.",sec={{t="A Husband's Vengeance",b="Mankrik carries the grief of a quilboar ambush that left him battered and his wife missing. At the Crossroads, he watches the arid horizon, still thirsting for the blood of the Bristlebacks despite the many he has killed himself. He calls on fellow Horde travelers to help him continue the fight.",sp=0},{t="Tusks of the Bristleback",b="Mankrik demands sixty Bristleback quilboar tusks. Each one is a measure of suffering returned to the creatures that tore his life apart. The trophies cannot heal his grief or end his desire for revenge, but seeing the Bristlebacks bleed brings the wounded warrior a fleeting, bitter satisfaction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Mankrik want sixty quilboar tusks?",a="Mankrik wants sixty tusks because grief and anger drive him after a quilboar ambush separated him from his wife. The tally calls for heavy losses among the Bristlebacks, and their suffering offers him a little solace.",al={"why 60 tusks","mankrik tusks quest","why so many tusks"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="Mankrik asks for the tusks at the Crossroads in the central Barrens. The Bristleback quilboar live in nearby scrublands and thorned redoubts.",al={"where is consumed by hatred","consumed by hatred location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does turning in the tusks satisfy Mankrik's revenge?",a="No. Mankrik's desire for revenge remains, though the quilboar's losses bring a grim smile and make him feel they have finally felt his pain.",al={"does mankrik stop hating quilboar","mankrik quest ending"}},{q="Why does Mankrik mention Camp Taurajo?",a="Mankrik wonders whether fleeing south toward Camp Taurajo instead of north to the Crossroads after the ambush might have changed the battle's outcome and his search.",al={"why taurajo","camp taurajo mankrik"}},{q="Who are the Bristlebacks?",a="The Bristlebacks are an aggressive quilboar tribe native to the Barrens. They are intensely territorial and xenophobic, clash constantly with the Horde, and attack travelers from thorn-choked encampments across the plains.",al={"what are bristlebacks","bristleback tribe"},it="target"},{q="Is this connected to finding Mankrik's wife?",a="Yes. Mankrik's hatred began with the ambush that overwhelmed him and his wife. As you search the plains for her fate in Lost in Battle, his demand for tusks is a call for revenge against her attackers.",al={"lost in battle connection","mankriks wife quest"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Mankrik need you to kill the Bristlebacks instead of doing it himself?",a="Mankrik is already fighting a one-orc war, slaying every quilboar he encounters between sunrise and sunset. Yet his grief and fury are too vast for a single blade. Rooted at the Crossroads while scouring the horizon and agonizing over the unknown, he enlists capable travelers to expand the slaughter far beyond what he can reach alone.",al={"why me mankrik","why does mankrik need help","why can't mankrik hunt quilboars himself"},it="why_me",add="69927be8"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may recognize Mankrik's grief and his drive to avenge fallen kin in the traditions of orcish honor and the harsh work of making a home in Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face quilboar threats to travel routes between Durotar, Mulgore, and the southern Barrens. Mankrik's fight also protects Horde territory.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know a wound to the heart cannot always be bandaged. Mankrik seeks his remedy in steel against steel across the thorned plains."},kw={"barrens","bristleback","consumed by hatred","crossroads","mankrik","quilboar","taurajo","tusks"},rel={"npc:mankrik","topic:quilboar","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mankrik",level="20",faction="Horde",id=899,ri={"Bristleback Quilboar Tusk"}},src={"Consumed by Hatred (Classic)"}}
E["quest:900"] = {t="quest",n="Samophlange",z="barrens",s="At the Sludge Fen, Samophlange machinery keeps the Venture Company's digging rig running. Three valves must be sealed before the central apparatus can be shut down safely.",h="At the Sludge Fen, Samophlange machinery keeps the Venture Company's digging rig running.",sec={{t="Taming the Apparatus",b="At the Sludge Fen, the Venture Company's machinery is complex and dangerous. The central console makes clear that the core cannot be stopped with a single switch. Its feed lines must be handled by hand first, or the apparatus could fail or explode.",sp=0},{t="The Three Valves",b="Three valves control the flow into the rig: the Main Control Valve, the Fuel Control Valve, and the Regulator Valve. Each must be sealed by hand against high pressure. As they close, the console's green indicators fade to yellow, making it safe to engage the central shutoff.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of shutting off these valves?",a="The valves seal the pressure and fuel lines before the apparatus is shut down. Closing them first helps prevent damage to the machine or a disaster.",al={"why shut valves","samophlange valves purpose","what do valves do"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens once all three valves are closed?",a="With all three valves closed, the pressure falls and the fuel stops flowing. The console's blinking lights dim from green to yellow, and the main shutoff switch can move freely.",al={"console lights","valves closed what next"},it="next_step"},{q="Who built this machine?",a="The Venture Company built the apparatus. The goblin trading cartel extracts oil and raw resources from the northern Barrens.",al={"who made the samophlange","venture co machine"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the valves located?",a="The three valves are near the central control console and main machinery at the Venture Company dig site in the Barrens.",al={"valve location","where are the valves"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde interested in this device?",a="The Venture Company's heavy industry damages the Barrens and encroaches on Horde lands. Understanding and sabotaging its machinery can curb that exploitation.",al={"why does horde care","horde samophlange"},it="motive"},{q="What is a samophlange?",a="A samophlange is an obscure technical goblin component. Non-engineers rarely understand its exact function, but it appears essential to high-pressure drilling equipment.",al={"samophlange meaning","what is a samophlange"},it="item"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will recognize a classic goblin design: overpowered, volatile fuel lines and few automatic failsafes. Manual shutoffs help prevent a catastrophic pressure backfire.",["faction:Horde"]="Stopping the Venture Company's machines protects the northern Barrens from unchecked industrial exploitation."},kw={"barrens","control console","fuel valve","regulator valve","samophlange","sludge fen","venture company"},rel={"zone:barrens"},m={start="Control Console",level="14",id=900},src={"Samophlange (Classic 2)"}}
E["quest:901"] = {t="quest",n="Samophlange",z="barrens",s="At the Sludge Fen, the Venture Company’s machinery waits with its valves shut and its pressure relieved. Tinkerer Sniggles holds the key to open the control unit and free the samophlange within.",h="At the Sludge Fen, the Venture Company’s machinery waits with its valves shut and its pressure relieved.",sec={{t="Unlocking the Mechanism",b="You have relieved the pressure by turning the auxiliary valves, and the dials and gauges have settled. The housing remains locked against tampering. Its key rests with the goblin engineer overseeing the drilling site.",sp=0},{t="Tinkerer Sniggles",b="Tinkerer Sniggles oversees the Venture Company’s equipment at the Sludge Fen. He keeps the console key in a hut just northeast of the main rig. You need that key to open the housing and reach the samophlange.",sp=0},{t="Power Drain",b="Turning Sniggles’ key in the console unlatches the housing. The red beacon goes dark, and the electrical hum fades. With the console’s safeguards disengaged, the core is ready to be removed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Tinkerer Sniggles located?",a="Tinkerer Sniggles is in a goblin hut just northeast of the main control console at the Sludge Fen in the northern Barrens.",al={"find sniggles","sniggles location","where is tinkerer sniggles"},gp=true},{q="What is the Console Key used for?",a="The Console Key unlocks the main control terminal at the Sludge Fen and cuts the remaining power, allowing you to remove the samophlange inside.",al={"console key use","what does key open","how to use console key"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why did the console need to be shut down before using the key?",a="First, the apparatus valves had to be vented so the machinery would idle. Handling it under full pressure would be hazardous.",al={"why shut down first","valves before key"},it="motive"},{q="Who does Tinkerer Sniggles work for?",a="Tinkerer Sniggles works for the Venture Company, which trades and extracts resources across the northern Barrens.",al={"sniggles faction","is sniggles venture co"},it="target"},{q="What is a samophlange?",a="A samophlange is a complex engineering component used in the Venture Company’s heavy drilling and pumping machinery.",al={"what does samophlange mean","what is a samophlange"}},{q="What happens after using the key on the console?",a="Using the key unlocks the terminal and cuts its power. The warning lights go dark, and you can remove the samophlange.",al={"what happens next","after console key"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do you need the Console Key?",a="Even with the apparatus shut down and its pressure valves safely vented, the control console remains physically locked tight. The Console Key is required to unlock the housing, cutting the final power to the terminal so the samophlange inside can be safely extracted without damaging the delicate mechanism.",al={"what is the console key for","console key purpose","why console key"},it="item",add="50a822cb"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how idling the gauges before opening the housing follows goblin mechanical safety practice.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help slow the Venture Company’s exploitation and toxic runoff across northern Kalimdor by sabotaging its equipment at the Sludge Fen."},kw={"barrens","console key","samophlange","sludge fen","sniggles","venture company"},rel={"quest:894","zone:barrens"},m={start="Control Console",level="14",id=901,ri={"Console Key"}},src={"Samophlange (Classic 3)"}}
E["quest:902"] = {t="quest",n="Samophlange",z="barrens",s="At the Venture Company console, you uncover the elusive samophlange and carry it to Ratchet. You have shut down the controls and their defenses; now the delicate device is ready for Sputtervalve to examine.",h="At the Venture Company console, you uncover the elusive samophlange and carry it to Ratchet.",sec={{t="Unearthing the Core",b="Behind the Venture Company console's faceplate, wiring and purposeless tubing crowd around strange engineering. Deep inside lies the samophlange, a core component that has baffled engineers across the region. With a firm tug, you free the device from its housing and carry it back to the goblin who began the recovery effort.",sp=0},{t="Fragile Innovations",b="Back in Ratchet, Sputtervalve takes the curious device and plans to send it to the Tinkers' Union headquarters in Undermine for study. Goblin curiosity gets the better of him. When he sets the samophlange down for a closer look, its delicate mechanism shatters on the floor, and he scrambles to save what he can of the research.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What actually is a samophlange?",a="Even experienced mechanics cannot make sense of the samophlange's jumble of wires, pipes, and odd trinkets. It is the key component inside the Venture Company's control console, though neither Sputtervalve nor the scavengers understand how it works.",al={"what is samophlange","samophlange purpose","what does it do"},it="item"},{q="Why does Sputtervalve want the samophlange?",a="Sputtervalve plans to send the component to the Tinkers' Union headquarters in Undermine. Goblin inventors there study and reverse-engineer rival designs, if the device survives inspection.",al={"why sputtervalve wants it","who wants samophlange"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when you hand the samophlange over?",a="Sputtervalve plans to send the samophlange to the Tinkers' Union in Undermine, but first he wants to inspect it himself.",al={"does the samophlange break","what does sputtervalve do with it"},sp=1},{q="Who built the control console housing the device?",a="The Venture Company built the console and samophlange at its Sludge Fen operation in the northern Barrens. Its technological experiments are notorious for slapdash work and pollution.",al={"who made samophlange","console creator"},it="origin"},{q="Where does Sputtervalve send you after this?",a="Sputtervalve sends you to his associate Wenikee Boltbucket, another engineer in the Barrens.",al={"next quest after samophlange","what to do next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Sputtervalve located?",a="Sputtervalve works on the docks and in the workshops of Ratchet, the port town on the Barrens' eastern coast.",al={"sputtervalve location","where is sputtervalve","where to turn in samophlange"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For an engineer, the samophlange is a Venture Company machine packed with dense wiring, tubing, and unfamiliar parts that invite careful study.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you deal with volatile Venture Company scrap in Ratchet's goblin ports, where neutral goblin enterprise can bring explosive incompetence."},kw={"control console","ratchet","samophlange","sputtervalve","the barrens","tinkers' union","undermine","venture company"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","quest:894"},m={start="Control Console",["end"]="Sputtervalve",level="16",id=902},src={"Samophlange (Classic 4)"}}
E["quest:903"] = {t="quest",n="Prowlers of the Barrens",z="barrens",s="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends you after the savannah prowlers. Their claws will show whether you can face the Barrens' greatest beasts.",h="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends you after the savannah prowlers.",sec={{t="A True Predator",b="Sergra Darkthorn tests hunters who have already faced the plainstriders and zhevras. Southwest of the Crossroads, savannah prowlers vanish into the central Barrens' gold and ochre scrub. These great cats hunt instead of grazing with the herds. They wait in tall grass, then ambush their prey, and unwary travelers can fall to them.",sp=0},{t="Predator or Prey",b="Sergra warns you that prowlers know how to hunt. Read the grasses and strike before a cat leaps if you mean to claim its paws and claws. Bring back seven prowler claws to show you have the cunning and quick reflexes to survive against Kalimdor's deadliest wildlife.",sp=0},{t="Stepping Toward the Champion",b="Your fistful of claws proves you have learned to survive on the open savannah. Sergra is pleased with your martial skill and prepares a test of valor: summon and slay Echeyakee, the white lion revered as a champion among the Barrens' predators.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers this hunt?",a="Sergra Darkthorn, an experienced orc at the Crossroads in the Barrens, assigns the hunt as one step in a traditional series of hunting rites.",al={"quest giver","who gives prowlers quest","sergra darkthorn"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the savannah prowlers located?",a="Savannah prowlers stalk the tall grasses southwest of the Crossroads, where they blend into the veldt and hunt zhevra and unsuspecting travelers.",al={"where are prowlers","prowler locations","where to find savannah prowler"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What trophies are required by Sergra?",a="Sergra requires seven Prowler Claws, taken from the cats in direct combat, to prove you have bested them.",al={"what do i need","prowler quest items","claws"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What does this hunt lead to?",a="Slaying the prowlers proves you are ready to challenge Echeyakee, the renowned white lion of the Barrens.",al={"next quest","what comes after prowlers","echeyakee"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sergra have travelers hunt predators?",a="Sergra's trials cull dangerous beasts that threaten the roads and test whether hunters understand the balance between predator and prey. They weed out the reckless before greater threats await.",al={"why hunt prowlers","purpose of hunt","lore reason"},it="motive"},{q="Are savannah prowlers dangerous to the settlement?",a="Prowlers rarely attack fortified camps like the Crossroads, but they lurk near the southern roads and prey on travelers, messengers, and pack animals.",al={"do prowlers attack crossroads","threat to crossroads"},it="threat"},{q="What are the Prowler Claws for?",a="Sergra Darkthorn demands the claws as physical proof of your kill. Hunting savannah prowlers is a test of your cunning and resilience against the Barrens' genuine predators. Bringing back their deadly claws demonstrates that you mastered the hunt and did not end up as their prey among the tall grasses.",al={"why collect prowler claws","prowler claws purpose","what does sergra do with prowler claws"},it="item",add="52f28747"},{q="What are the savannah prowlers you are hunting?",a="Savannah prowlers are predatory big cats native to the open plains of the Barrens. Stalking through the tall grasses, they are tough, resourceful, sly, and dangerous to travelers. Sergra directs you against them to move past docile quarry and test your survival against beasts that can turn the tables and hunt you.",al={"what are savannah prowlers","who are you hunting prowlers","savannah prowler target"},it="target",add="6a79a965"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, stalking savannah prowlers through tall scrub trains you to track them, spot them before they strike, and subdue aggressive cats.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, helping tame the wilds around the Crossroads keeps supply convoys safe on the routes between Durotar, Mulgore, and the southern outposts.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, culling rogue predators honors the natural balance and protects vulnerable caravans crossing your ancestral hunting lands."},kw={"crossroads","echeyakee","hunting","prowler claws","prowlers","savannah prowler","sergra darkthorn","the barrens"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","quest:845","zone:barrens","quest:860"},m={start="Sergra Darkthorn",level="15",faction="Horde",id=903,ri={"Prowler Claws"}},src={"Prowlers of the Barrens"}}
E["quest:905"] = {t="quest",n="The Angry Scytheclaws",z="barrens",s="South of the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends hunters to face the savage scytheclaws stalking the Barrens. Bring sunscale raptor feathers to their breeding nests, and prove your courage in a land that gives little quarter.",h="South of the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn sends hunters to face the savage scytheclaws stalking the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Test of Nerve",b="Sergra Darkthorn tests hunters against the beasts of the Barrens. After lesser trials, she sends you south of the Crossroads to hunt vicious sunscale raptors and take their feathers. Then you carry those feathers southwest of the Stagnant Oasis, into the heart of raptor territory. Placing them in the nests is the true test: it shows you can face the scytheclaws without fear.",sp=0},{t="The Scytheclaw Nests",b="Three raptor nests lie southwest of the Stagnant Oasis, near the Gold Road. Red, blue, and yellow eggs mark the separate clutches. Scytheclaws defend their nests fiercely against anything that comes near. Place the feathers of fallen raptors among the eggs, and you make your challenge clear to the beasts.",sp=0},{t="Tempered by the Savanna",b="Return to the Crossroads after entering the nests, and Sergra can see you have faced the danger and lived. Walking out of a raptor den takes raw courage. The Barrens test every hunter; each fight may harden you, or leave your bones among the kodo ribs scattered across the dirt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn want me to put feathers in the raptor nests?",a="Sergra Darkthorn asks you to show courage and dominance. Kill sunscale raptors, then place their feathers in the colored clutches to show their pack and kin that you do not fear them.",al={"why scytheclaw nests","purpose of feathers in nests","why defile nests"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the scytheclaw nests located?",a="The nests are south of the Crossroads and southwest of the Stagnant Oasis, near the Gold Road. They lie beside a small hill marked by giant kodo bones, just east of the roadway ditch.",al={"where are nests","scytheclaw nest location","blue yellow red nest location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kinds of raptors live in this part of the Barrens?",a="Sunscale scytheclaws and their kin live here. These cunning, aggressive reptilian predators hunt in packs and fiercely defend their clutches around the Gold Road and nearby Raptor Grounds.",al={"barrens raptor types","sunscale raptors","what are scytheclaws"},it="target"},{q="Where do I collect the Sunscale Feathers?",a="Sunscale raptors and scytheclaws across the plains south of the Crossroads and the nearby Raptor Grounds toward the eastern hills carry Sunscale Feathers.",al={"where to get feathers","sunscale feather drops","how to get raptor feathers"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Sergra Darkthorn?",a="Sergra Darkthorn is an experienced orc stationed at the Crossroads. She tests arriving Horde adventurers with trials across the Barrens, measuring their survival instincts and fighting discipline.",al={"who is sergra","sergra darkthorn lore"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest lead to other hunts?",a="Yes. Sergra Darkthorn's hunts continue across the Barrens, ending with the hunt for Isha Awak, the legendary sea beast off the Barrens coast.",al={"what comes after angry scytheclaws","hunt chain crossroad","next quest after nests"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sergra Darkthorn have you hunt the raptors instead of doing it herself?",a="Sergra Darkthorn is not just managing pests; she is mentoring you in the ways of the hunt. Stationed at the Crossroads, her role is to test the mettle of rising Horde champions against the harsh wilderness of the Barrens. By sending you to harvest the feathers and deliberately intrude upon the raptors' nests, she is shaping your courage and endurance through real danger, watching to see if the unforgiving land will forge you into a tougher survivor.",al={"why send me","why not sergra","why doesnt sergra hunt them"},it="why_me",add="95d43724"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you test your wilderness mastery when you enter a territorial predator's den and challenge its dominance.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know that surviving Durotar and the Barrens takes strength, fortitude, and unwavering nerve.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the raptor packs along the Gold Road threaten caravans and lone messengers traveling between the Crossroads and southern outposts."},kw={"crossroads","eggs","gold road","nests","raptor grounds","raptors","scytheclaws","sergra darkthorn","stagnant oasis","sunscale"},rel={"quest:860","quest:873","quest:877","subzone:stagnant-oasis","subzone:crossroads","subzone:raptor-grounds","subzone:gold-road","zone:barrens"},m={start="Sergra Darkthorn",level="16",faction="Horde",id=905},src={"The Angry Scytheclaws"}}
E["quest:906"] = {t="quest",n="Betrayal from Within",z="barrens",s="In the central Barrens, the hunt for Lok Orcbane reaches its end. His fall will weaken the Razormane raids, and you carry his severed head to Thork at the Crossroads.",h="In the central Barrens, the hunt for Lok Orcbane reaches its end.",sec={{t="A Traitor's Head",b="Mangletooth, a captured Razormane quilboar held in a cage at Camp Taurajo, names Lok Orcbane as the chieftain directing attacks on Horde caravans. After you slay Lok deep in the southern thorn mazes, Mangletooth gives you the chieftain's skull. He finds it amusing that the orcs will benefit from betrayal within the tribe without knowing a captive quilboar helped them.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Crossroads",b="You bring Lok's head north to Thork at the Crossroads, easing the pressure on Horde supply lines across the central savannah. Thork is astonished that one traveler felled so formidable a leader; he had expected another mastermind behind the organized strikes. Lok's death leaves the Razormane offensive fractured and its fighters disorganized.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mangletooth?",a="Mangletooth is a captured Razormane quilboar kept in a wooden cage at Camp Taurajo. Bitter that his tribe abandoned him, he guides Horde adventurers against its warlords for revenge.",al={"mangletooth","captive quilboar","taurajo prisoner"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Lok Orcbane?",a="Lok Orcbane was a prominent Razormane chieftain who coordinated fierce ambushes against Horde outposts and supply lines across the Barrens.",al={"lok","lok orcbane","razormane leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thork care about Lok's death?",a="Thork commands the defense of the Crossroads against persistent thorn-dwelling raiders. Lok Orcbane directed attacks along the Gold Road, and his death removes their primary tactician.",al={"why thork wants lok dead","crossroads supply raids"},it="purpose"},{q="Why did Mangletooth help eliminate his own chieftain?",a="Mangletooth is deeply bitter toward his tribe's leadership and respects raw strength above kin. He guides Horde champions to execute Lok, indulging his hatred while keeping his mystical connection to Agamaggan from behind bars.",al={"why did mangletooth betray","mangletooth motive"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead?",a="You bring Lok's head to mark the end of the immediate assassination chain. Mangletooth still trades Agamaggan's elemental blessings for Blood Shards gathered from quilboar across the Barrens.",al={"next quest after betrayal from within","what follows betrayal from within"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is Thork located?",a="Thork is on guard inside the Crossroads settlement in the northern central Barrens, overseeing defense and logistics.",al={"thork location","where is thork"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mangletooth have you deliver Lok's skull instead of doing it himself?",a="Mangletooth is trapped inside a Horde cage at Camp Taurajo. Even if he could walk free, the guards at the Crossroads would strike down a Razormane quilboar on sight rather than negotiate with him. By sending you with Lok Orcbane's skull, he ensures the Horde learns of the chieftain's downfall while letting you claim the credit and whatever reward Thork offers.",al={"why mangletooth needs you","why does mangletooth send you to thork","why cant mangletooth deliver the skull"},it="why_me",add="1320d8a4"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure the travel corridors between Camp Taurajo and the Crossroads. Lok Orcbane's death blunts the Razormanes' threat to new settlements in Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you hear a warning in Lok's surname: Orcbane. He has long butchered orcish settlers and supply convoys in the arid flats."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","camp taurajo","crossroads","lok orcbane","mangletooth","quilboar","razormane","thork"},rel={"npc:thork","npc:mangletooth","topic:quilboar","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:agamaggan"},m={start="Mangletooth",["end"]="Thork",level="25",faction="Horde",id=906},src={"Betrayal from Within (2)"}}
E["quest:907"] = {t="quest",n="Enraged Thunder Lizards",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, thunder lizards roam the plains around Camp Taurajo. Jorn Skyseer calls hunters to face the great beasts and bring back their blood as part of a wider rite of passage.",h="In the southern Barrens, thunder lizards roam the plains around Camp Taurajo.",sec={{t="A Test of the Southern Plains",b="After defeating the raptor Ishamuhale, you return to Camp Taurajo. The tauren elder Jorn Skyseer now tests your strength against the largest grazers of the land. Stormsnouts and Thunderheads roam the southern Barrens, their heavy strides able to crush an unwary hunter beneath them.",sp=0},{t="The Way of the Predator",b="Tauren and orc hunters prize poise, position, and strength when facing a thunder lizard. Jorn asks you to bring back samples of their potent blood, proof that you stood in the path of the rumbling beasts and survived with your bones unbroken. The trophy opens the way to Jorn's final quarry in the skies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find the thunder lizards for this hunt?",a="Thunder lizards roam the plains around Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. Stormsnouts, Stormhides, and Thunderheads graze north, east, and south of the camp.",al={"thunder lizard location","where are stormsnouts","where to find thunder lizards"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends me on this hunt?",a="Jorn Skyseer, a tauren elder and hunter at Camp Taurajo, sends you after the thunder lizards. The hunt follows your encounter with the swift raptor Ishamuhale.",al={"quest giver","who gives enraged thunder lizards","jorn skyseer"},it="identity"},{q="What makes thunder lizards particularly dangerous?",a="Their great size and electrical nature make thunder lizards dangerous. A careless hunter can be crushed underfoot or stunned by their storm-charged stomps.",al={"why are they dangerous","thunder lizard combat"},it="danger"},{q="What does Jorn do with the blood collected?",a="Jorn uses the blood as proof that you faced and felled the creatures in close combat. He inspects it to see whether you survived their trampling with your bones intact.",al={"why thunder lizard blood","blood purpose"},it="item"},{q="What comes after this quest?",a="Bring the blood to Jorn Skyseer, and he sends you after the winged predators of the plains in Cry of the Thunderhawk, the next stage of the southern hunting trials.",al={"next quest","what after enraged thunder lizards"},it="next_step"},{q="How does this fit into Sergra Darkthorn's trials?",a="Sergra Darkthorn starts your hunting progression near the Crossroads in the northern Barrens. She sends you after plainstriders, zhevras, and raptors, then sends you south to Taurajo to learn from Jorn Skyseer against heavier game.",al={"crossroads hunting trials","sergra darkthorn questline"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer want me to hunt thunder lizards?",a="Jorn Skyseer guides promising hunters through the rites of the plains, building upon the hunting trials begun by Sergra Darkthorn. Facing the colossal thunder lizards proves your courage, agility, and resilience against some of the southern Barrens' most dangerous and physically overwhelming beasts.",al={"why hunt thunder lizards","jorn skyseer motive","why does jorn want thunder lizard blood"},it="motive",add="0ee753a7"},{q="What are the thunder lizards in the southern Barrens?",a="Thunder lizards—known across the southern plains as Stormsnouts, Stormhides, and Thunderheads—are enormous reptilian behemoths native to the Barrens. Their massive bodies make the earth tremble as they stomp across the grasslands, easily capable of crushing unwary hunters beneath their feet.",al={"what are thunder lizards","stormsnouts and stormhides","barrens thunderheads"},it="target",add="5ef19b55"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a Shu'halo, you honor the ancestral plains through the traditional hunt for great thunder lizards around Camp Taurajo. It tests your fortitude and balance.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you test your footwork against a thunder lizard, keeping clear of its crushing stomps while wearing down its immense hide.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help clear enraged beasts from the paths around Camp Taurajo, protecting caravans and traveling warriors in the southern Barrens."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","enraged thunder lizards","jorn skyseer","stormhide","stormsnout","thunderhead"},rel={"quest:3261","quest:913","subzone:camp-taurajo","quest:860","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},m={start="Jorn Skyseer",level="18",faction="Horde",id=907,ri={"Thunder Lizard Blood"}},src={"Enraged Thunder Lizards"}}
E["quest:913"] = {t="quest",n="Cry of the Thunderhawk",z="barrens",s="Cry of the Thunderhawk is the culmination of Jorn Skyseer's hunting trials in the southern Barrens. Entrusted by the elders at Camp Taurajo, a hunter must seek out a winged serpent soaring through the scrublands and bring back its wings to prove their mastery over the savanna's fiercest beasts.",h="Cry of the Thunderhawk is the culmination of Jorn Skyseer's hunting trials in the southern Barrens.",sec={{t="The Culmination of the Trial",b="After proving their mettle against prowling plainstriders, prowlers, and agitated thunder lizards, hunters in the Barrens are directed toward their ultimate challenge by Jorn Skyseer. The thunderhawk is considered one of the most fierce aerial predators inhabiting the scrublands surrounding Camp Taurajo. Slaying one requires patience, sharp aim, and an awareness of the sky that few landbound predators possess.",sp=0},{t="A Hunter's Walk",b="Returning with the thunderhawk's wings marks the end of a novice's tutelage under Camp Taurajo's watchful eyes. For the tauren, hunting is not mere slaughter but an ongoing spiritual walk in harmony with the Earthmother and the natural hierarchy of the wild. Besting such a proud creature shows that the hunter acts with strength, courage, and honor—virtues required before stepping out into harsher wildernesses beyond the central plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a thunderhawk?",a="Thunderhawks are winged, serpentine predators native to the Barrens. They glide over the arid plains hunting smaller prey from above, using their lightning-quick strikes and aerial mobility to dominate the skies around Camp Taurajo.",al={"what are thunderhawks","thunderhawk creature","flying serpent barrens"},it="target"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Jorn Skyseer, a respected tauren hunter stationed at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, issues this trial once you have proven yourself against the region's enraged thunder lizards.",al={"who starts cry of the thunderhawk","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where are thunderhawks found?",a="They roam the open skies and rocky crags across the southern Barrens, primarily hovering in the plains flanking the roads north and west of Camp Taurajo.",al={"where to find thunderhawks","thunderhawk location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does claiming the wings signify to the tauren?",a="Presenting the severed wings serves as tangible proof of a clean and honorable kill. In tauren culture, harvesting tokens from dangerous quarry demonstrates mastery over the beast while acknowledging the pride and ferocity of the fallen creature.",al={"why bring wings","thunderhawk wings meaning"},it="item"},{q="Where does this hunting trial lead next?",a="Completing Jorn Skyseer's trials concludes your training at Camp Taurajo, prompting Jorn to send you toward his sister, Mahren Skyseer, who hunts along the eastern coast of the Barrens south of Ratchet.",al={"what comes after cry of the thunderhawk","next quest after thunderhawk"},it="next_step"},{q="How does this connect to Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads?",a="This trial forms the southern chapter of the overarching hunting rites that began under Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads. After mastering the northern beasts, promising hunters are sent south to Camp Taurajo to continue their training under Jorn Skyseer.",al={"sergra darkthorn connection","crossroads hunting chain"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer want this done?",a="Jorn Skyseer is testing your strength, courage, and honor as a hunter. Having guided you through the trials of the southern Barrens, he sets the fierce thunderhawk before you as the final culmination of your training under his watch. Taking down such a proud predator proves that you are ready to conclude your time at Camp Taurajo and walk the wider path of a true hunter.",al={"jorn skyseer motive","why kill thunderhawk","purpose of thunderhawk hunt"},it="motive",add="2e0d4fa8"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the Shu'halo, tracking the soaring thunderhawk is a sacred trial of respect and honor, proving the hunter's ability to commune with and test themselves against the swiftest children of the Earthmother.",["class:Hunter"]="Taking down an aerial serpent like the thunderhawk tests your ranged discipline and patience, serving as a formal rite of passage into true mastery of the plains.",["faction:Horde"]="Taming and securing the dangerous frontier around Camp Taurajo ensures the safety of Horde travelers journeying along the high road through the Barrens."},kw={"barrens hunt","camp taurajo","cry of the thunderhawk","jorn skyseer","thunderhawk","thunderhawk wings","winged serpent"},rel={"quest:3261","quest:907","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:barrens","quest:860","subzone:crossroads"},m={start="Jorn Skyseer",level="20",faction="Horde",id=913,ri={"Thunderhawk Wings"}},src={"Cry of the Thunderhawk"}}
E["quest:924"] = {t="quest",n="The Demon Seed",z="barrens",s="Neeru Fireblade's orders reach Ak'Zeloth, who sends Horde travelers to destroy the Demon Seed atop Dreadmist Peak. An unstable Flawed Power Stone can break the Burning Legion's conduit before its influence spreads farther through the Barrens.",h="Neeru Fireblade's orders reach Ak'Zeloth, who sends Horde travelers to destroy the Demon Seed atop Dreadmist...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Crags",b="High in a cave on Dreadmist Peak, the Demon Seed hangs above an altar of fire. The artifact anchors demonic power in the heart of the Barrens for the Burning Legion. The orc Ak'Zeloth prepares specialized power stones to break its link to the Nether. One must reach the peak before the stone's unstable energy runs out.",sp=0},{t="Shattering the Tether",b="The Flawed Power Stone loses power as it crosses Dreadmist Peak's craggy slopes. Set against the altar of fire, it overloads the Demon Seed and shatters its connection. The destruction sends powerful shockwaves through the ether, alerting unseen masters that their device has been compromised.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Demon Seed?",a="The Demon Seed is a Burning Legion artifact in a cavern atop Dreadmist Peak. It hangs above an altar of fire and draws demonic power and influence into the Barrens.",al={"demon seed purpose","what is demon seed","demon seed lore"},it="item"},{q="Who orders the destruction of the Demon Seed?",a="The orc Ak'Zeloth orders the Demon Seed destroyed, following instructions and receiving rewards through Neeru Fireblade, a warlock in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow.",al={"who wants demon seed destroyed","neeru demon seed","akzeloth questgiver"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does the Flawed Power Stone have a time limit?",a="Ak'Zeloth's Flawed Power Stone is unstable. Its imperfect magical containment makes its disruptive energy burn out, so it must reach the demonic altar quickly.",al={"flawed power stone timer","why does stone expire","stone disappearing"},it="power"},{q="Where is the altar of fire located?",a="The altar of fire lies in a cavern near the summit of Dreadmist Peak, northwest of the Crossroads in the northern Barrens.",al={"altar of fire location","demon seed cave","dreadmist peak cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when the Demon Seed is destroyed?",a="Destroying the Demon Seed severs its link to the Burning Legion, and the release sends immense ripples through the ether. Ak'Zeloth warns that powerful demonic entities will sense the disruption and investigate the ruin of their tool.",al={"demon seed shockwave","consequences of demon seed","waves of power"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="How does this connect to Neeru Fireblade?",a="Neeru Fireblade coordinates with Ak'Zeloth against rival or disruptive demonic artifacts across the Barrens. Neeru supplies the coin and equipment given once the Demon Seed is destroyed.",al={"neeru connection","is neeru good","neeru involvement"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Ak'Zeloth want the Demon Seed destroyed?",a="Ak'Zeloth acts on direct instructions from Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar. The Demon Seed serves as an active conduit for the Burning Legion on Dreadmist Peak. By neutralizing it with a flawed power stone, they sever that specific demonic connection to Azeroth, striking a blow against Legion instruments operating in the Barrens.",al={"akzeloth motive","why destroy demon seed","why does akzeloth want this"},it="motive",add="f2c946bb"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you recognize the delicate craft of power stones that disrupt Legion tethers without causing a catastrophic demonic implosion.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect the Barrens' vital caravan crossroads and the trade routes that sustain the young Horde by eliminating Legion footholds.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you have endured Draenor's ruin under demonic corruption and have little tolerance for Legion altars near Durotar's borders."},kw={"ak'zeloth","altar of fire","barrens","burning legion","demon seed","dreadmist peak","flawed power stone","neeru fireblade"},rel={"quest:809","quest:829","quest:926","subzone:dreadmist-peak","topic:burning-legion","zone:barrens"},m={start="Ak'Zeloth",level="14",faction="Horde",id=924},src={"The Demon Seed (quest)"}}
E["quest:926"] = {t="quest",n="Flawed Power Stone",z="barrens",s="Across the Barrens, Flawed Power Stone rests on arcane tables, charged with arcane energy. Its makers left it fatally flawed, so it consumes its own power soon after it is moved.",h="Across the Barrens, Flawed Power Stone rests on arcane tables, charged with arcane energy.",sec={{t="Volatile Craftsmanship",b="In the Barrens, flawed power stones hold arcane essence within compromised structures. Their makers deliberately left them unstable, so they decay into inert matter moments after someone handles them.",sp=0},{t="Self-Consuming Energy",b="A stone begins consuming its power as soon as it leaves the ritual table where it rests. Its energy burns away too quickly for anyone to carry it far.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Flawed Power Stone?",a="Flawed Power Stone holds raw magical power, but its deliberate flaws make it consume itself rapidly once moved.",al={"flawed power stone","what is this stone","power stone lore"},it="item"},{q="Can the stones be preserved permanently?",a="No. Once separated from the tables that stabilize them, the stones' magical matrices collapse and their energy quickly runs out.",al={"keep flawed stone","can i store it","preserving stone"},it="power"},{q="Who uses these stones?",a="The orc Ak'Zeloth prepares the stones, and Horde adventurers carry them to the altar of fire on Dreadmist Peak. There, they disrupt the Demon Seed's connection to the Burning Legion.",al={"who made power stones","who crafted them","stone creators"},it="people"},{q="Why does the Horde care about them?",a="The Horde uses the stones against the Burning Legion. Ak'Zeloth prepared them for Neeru Fireblade, so carrying one to the altar of fire on Dreadmist Peak can break the Demon Seed's connection to the Legion.",al={"horde interest","why does horde want this"},it="conflict"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you keep watch over arcane oddities scattered across the Barrens, wary of rogue sorcery that could threaten your supply routes."},kw={"arcane","barrens","flawed power stone","power stones","ritual table","volatile magic"},rel={"zone:barrens"},m={start="Flawed Power Stones",["end"]="Flawed Power Stones",level="14",faction="Horde",id=926},src={"Flawed Power Stone (quest)"}}
E["quest:92706"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Bruuz",z="barrens",s="Bruuz threatens the harbor traffic that keeps Ratchet busy. Gazlowe has posted a bounty for the huge shark prowling the docks and disrupting coastal trade.",h="Bruuz threatens the harbor traffic that keeps Ratchet busy.",sec={{t="A Terror in the Bay",b="Ratchet is the primary neutral gateway between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, and its trade depends on merchant ships. Lately, a huge shark called Bruuz has been prowling the bay. Dockworkers gave the shark its name after it began attacking small skiffs, sailors, and cargo being unloaded near the docks. Its presence disrupts the port and puts the ships that keep Ratchet supplied at risk.",sp=0},{t="Gazlowe's Bounty",b="Gazlowe has posted a public bounty to keep ships from avoiding his port for fear of the shark. The notice calls on anglers and promises a hefty reward. To claim it, you need to slay Bruuz and bring back the shark's dorsal fin as proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bruuz?",a="Bruuz is a huge, aggressive shark hunting near Ratchet's shipping docks. Dockworkers gave it that name after attacks on sailors and small vessels.",al={"what is bruuz","bruuz shark","who is bruuz the shark"}},{q="Why did Gazlowe post a bounty on Bruuz?",a="Bruuz disrupts the shipping and trade that fuel Ratchet's economy. Gazlowe offers a cash reward for the shark's carcass to protect business at the docks.",al={"why kill bruuz","gazlowe shark quest","why want bruuz fin"}},{q="Where is Bruuz usually found?",a="Bruuz prowls the waters off Ratchet in the Barrens, often near the main shipping piers and harbor entrance.",al={"bruuz location","where is bruuz","find bruuz"}},{q="What proof does Gazlowe require for the kill?",a="Gazlowe requires Bruuz's dorsal fin as proof that the shark has been slain before he pays the bounty.",al={"bruuz turn in","what do you bring gazlowe","bruuz dorsal fin"}},{q="Can both Alliance and Horde adventurers take this bounty?",a="Yes. Ratchet is run by the neutral Steamwheedle Cartel, and Gazlowe welcomes capable adventurers from either faction to deal with the shark.",al={"is wanted bruuz neutral","can horde do wanted bruuz","can alliance do bruuz"}},{q="Why does the bounty specifically call for anglers?",a="The notice does not explain why it calls for anglers. It opens with “Calling all anglers!” and promises a hefty reward for Bruuz's fin.",al={"calling all anglers bruuz","is this a fishing quest"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can test your patience and aim against Bruuz, a huge predator of the waters.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you could make use of the fresh coastal meat from a shark as large as Bruuz. Gazlowe wants only the dorsal fin as proof of the kill."},kw={"barrens","bounty","bruuz","dorsal fin","gazlowe","ratchet","shark","steamwheedle"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={level="20",id=92706},src={"In-game quest text: WANTED: Bruuz"},fv=true}
E["quest:96"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="barrens",s="You carry the Shard of Water back to Islen Waterseer along the Barrens coast. Your journey proves your harmony with restorative energies and earns you a Water Totem.",h="You carry the Shard of Water back to Islen Waterseer along the Barrens coast.",sec={{t="A Long Journey Home",b="You carry a gift from the Minor Manifestation of Water back across the sea. To earn it, you crossed continents to the tainted shores of Silverpine Forest and faced the corruption there. Water gives life, adapts, and heals, yet its pliant nature leaves it open to blight and dark magic. Before the Minor Manifestation, you witnessed pure elemental will and received the Shard of Water. Now, as you return to the sun-scorched Barrens, the shard reminds you that water connects distant corners of the world.",sp=0},{t="The Water Totem",b="When you give Islen Waterseer the shard, she weighs more than proof of your journey. She tests whether you have learned the balance between preservation and renewal. Lordaeron's spreading rot can hide small victories, yet cleansing even one wellspring matters to the spirits. Islen recognizes your offering and gives you a Water Totem. Through it, you can channel cleansing, healing, and mana-restoring streams into the mortal realm, binding you to the tide.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shard of Water?",a="The Shard of Water is an elemental remnant given by the Minor Manifestation of Water. It shows that you understand water's life-giving power and have opposed the corruption threatening elemental streams.",al={"shard of water","water shard","what is the shard"},it="item"},{q="Where do I take the Shard of Water?",a="Bring the Shard of Water to Islen Waterseer at her secluded camp on the Barrens' eastern shore, south of Ratchet.",al={"where to turn in","who gets the shard","turn in location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What do I receive for completing this trial?",a="You receive a Water Totem, the conduit shamans need to call water-based elemental totems for healing and restorative magic.",al={"quest reward","totem reward","what do i get"},it="power"},{q="Why was the trial set in Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine Forest's waters suffer heavy corruption from plague and shadow magic. There, you witnessed water's fragility and defended its natural purity against decay.",al={"why silverpine","why eastern kingdoms","silverpine water"},it="place"},{q="Who is Islen Waterseer?",a="Islen Waterseer is a tauren shaman at the Barrens' eastern coast. She oversees the shamanic trials of water and teaches initiates to commune with fluid spirits and master restorative arts.",al={"islen","who is islen waterseer"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Minor Manifestation of Water send you back to Islen?",a="The elemental manifestation serves as the living voice of pure water, tested and summoned through your rituals. By granting you the Shard of Water, it entrusts you with the fundamental truth of its nature: water brings life, while corruption extinguishes it. It sends you back to Islen Waterseer so the shaman can confirm your communion with the spirits, recognize your success in confronting corruption, and grant you the water totem you have proven worthy to wield.",al={"minor manifestation motive","why take shard to islen","why manifestation of water wants this"},it="motive",add="352084e3"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you receive your Water Totem and gain the restorative wellsprings and cleansing fountains central to your role as a spiritual healer.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share responsibility for the spirits of the land. Young shamans are called to cleanse blighted lands across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"call of water","islen waterseer","minor manifestation of water","shard of water","silverpine forest","the barrens","water totem"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","npc:minor-manifestation-of-water","zone:barrens"},m={start="Minor Manifestation of Water",["end"]="Islen Waterseer",level="23",faction="Horde",id=96},src={"Call of Water (9)"}}
E["quest:97005"] = {t="quest",n="Chol'aruk the Ravener",z="barrens",s="A horror stalks a cave on Thorn Hill in the Barrens, where the Razormane call it Chol'aruk the Ravener. Bainham seeks its severed head to avenge comrades lost to similar beasts.",h="A horror stalks a cave on Thorn Hill in the Barrens, where the Razormane call it Chol'aruk the Ravener.",sec={{t="Terror of Thorn Hill",b="Northwest of Bainham's camp in the Barrens, Thorn Hill rises above the Savannah. Razormane tribes have long fought over the plateau. Now rumors speak of a monstrous abomination in one of its caves, called Chol'aruk or the Ravener by the Razormane. Some travelers dismiss tales that it can swallow an armored orc whole. Those who have seen the carnage know the danger is real.",sp=0},{t="A Grudge Repaid",b="Bainham knows Chol'aruk is no campfire tale. He has fought similar horrors and bears scars from those encounters, while mourning comrades who fell to such beasts. He fears the abomination threatens everyone crossing the Savannah. Bainham asks seasoned champions to climb Thorn Hill, enter its underground lair, slay Chol'aruk, and bring back its massive head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Chol'aruk?",a="Chol'aruk is a monstrous abomination in a cave on Thorn Hill. Rumors say it is large enough to swallow a grown orc whole, and the local Razormane call it the Ravener.",al={"what is cholaruk","cholaruk monster type","who is the ravener"}},{q="Where is Chol'aruk's lair located?",a="Chol'aruk lairs in a cave on the high plateau of Thorn Hill, northwest in the Barrens.",al={"where is cholaruk","cholaruk location","thorn hill cave"}},{q="Who is Bainham and why does he want Chol'aruk dead?",a="Bainham lives in the Barrens and has fought similar beasts. He wants Chol'aruk dead because he lost allies to such abominations and seeks vengeance for his fallen comrades.",al={"who gives cholaruk quest","why kill cholaruk","bainham lore"}},{q="What does 'The Ravener' mean?",a="The local Razormane quilboar call Chol'aruk the Ravener, a name tied to its ravenous nature. Rumors say it devours full-grown warriors whole.",al={"meaning of cholaruk","why called ravener","razormane cholaruk"}},{q="Do the Razormane quilboar worship or fear Chol'aruk?",a="Whether the Razormane quilboar fear or worship Chol'aruk is unknown. They call it Chol'aruk or the Ravener, but nothing more is known of their feelings toward the abomination in Thorn Hill's cave.",al={"do quilboar like cholaruk","razormane and cholaruk"}},{q="What proof is required to confirm Chol'aruk's death?",a="Bainham asks you to bring back Chol'aruk's severed head as proof of its death.",al={"cholaruk quest turn in","what do i bring bainham"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Unchecked monsters on the high plateaus threaten travelers and caravans crossing the Barrens. Slaying the beast would help protect the region.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking a predator rumored to swallow fully armored warriors whole tests your skill and nerve.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can answer Bainham's call by facing a towering horror in its underground lair and avenging fallen comrades."},kw={"abomination","bainham","barrens","chol'aruk","razormane","the ravener","thorn hill"},rel={"subzone:thorn-hill","zone:barrens"},m={level="21",id=97005},src={"In-game quest text: Chol'aruk the Ravener"},fv=true}
E["quest:972"] = {t="quest",n="Water Sapta",z="barrens",s="At Islen Waterseer's shore, a young Horde shaman receives Water Sapta for a journey across the Great Sea. The trial leads from the Barrens to Silverpine Forest, where a spring has been corrupted.",h="At Islen Waterseer's shore, a young Horde shaman receives Water Sapta for a journey across the Great Sea.",sec={{t="A Vision of Water",b="Among Horde shaman, a sapta is a draught made to open the senses to the world's spirits. To ordinary eyes, a stream may look calm and a pond still. Drink a sapta, and the veil of the physical world parts, showing the elementals that dwell in the water.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Silverpine",b="Islen Waterseer gives the shaman the draught after they have shown their devotion to the spirits. She lives alone on the barren shore south of Ratchet. She sends the initiate across the Great Sea, away from Kalimdor's dry valleys, to Silverpine Forest. There, an elemental corruption is poisoning Lordaeron's streams, and the shaman must face it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a water sapta?",a="A sapta is a ceremonial draught prepared by shamanic mentors. Drinking it sharpens spiritual sight, so the shaman can see and speak with elementals hidden from mortal eyes.",al={"what is sapta","water sapta meaning","what does sapta do"},it="item"},{q="Who is Islen Waterseer?",a="Islen Waterseer is a master shaman who lives alone on the Barrens' eastern coast, south of the Merchant Coast. She guides young Horde shaman on the hard path to commune with and bind the element of water.",al={"islen waterseer lore","who is islen"},it="identity"},{q="Why must the shaman travel to Silverpine Forest?",a="Water's elementals are suffering from a widespread affliction in Silverpine Forest. To complete their initiation, shaman carry the sapta across the sea and see a corrupted water source firsthand, then cleanse its taint.",al={"why silverpine","why go to eastern kingdoms"},it="place"},{q="What happens after drinking the sapta?",a="After drinking the sapta, shaman can see the corrupted water elementals in Silverpine's tainted pools. That sight opens the way to confront the source of the decay.",al={"drinking sapta","sapta effect"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this trial required for all Horde shaman?",a="Yes. Orc, tauren, and troll shaman all heed the Call of Water and receive the sapta as a rite of passage before earning their Water Totem.",al={"who takes this quest","is this class quest"}},{q="Where in Silverpine is the corrupted pool located?",a="The corrupted spring lies on Silverpine Forest's coast, west of the Sepulcher.",al={"silverpine pool location","where is the water pool"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Islen Waterseer send you to Silverpine?",a="Islen Waterseer seeks to guide you through your spiritual rite of passage, helping you attune yourself to the elemental forces of water. To earn communion with the spirits of water and complete the Call of Water, you must face and cleanse the taint plaguing the world's waterways. She has entrusted you with a prepared water sapta so you can perceive hidden elemental corruption firsthand and prove your devotion as a burgeoning shaman.",al={"why does islen want this done","islen waterseer motive","why clean the corrupted water"},it="motive",add="c8d11240"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you take a turning step in your elemental trials with the Water Sapta. It opens your eyes to the spirit world before you gain command of your healing Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see this trial send initiates from Kalimdor's sun-bleached plains to Lordaeron's haunted woods."},kw={"call of water","islen waterseer","shaman trial","silverpine forest","the barrens","totem quest","water sapta"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","zone:barrens"},m={start="Islen Waterseer",level="20",faction="Horde",id=972},src={"Water Sapta (quest)"}}
E["subzone:agama-gor"] = {t="subzone",n="Agama'gor",z="barrens",s="Agama'gor stands north of the road from Camp Taurajo toward Mulgore. Bristleback quilboar hold this encampment in the southern Barrens, keeping pressure on the nearby Horde outpost.",h="Agama'gor stands north of the road from Camp Taurajo toward Mulgore.",sec={{t="A Bristleback Stronghold",b="Agama'gor is a Bristleback stronghold in the southern Barrens. Its huts, brambles, and crude totems lie close to Camp Taurajo. The quilboar threaten travelers moving between the Barrens and Mulgore’s grassy hills, and Horde scouts and hunters fight to contain them.",sp=0},{t="Blood Shards and Exile",b="Bristleback quilboar in Agama'gor carry crimson stones called Blood Shards. Mangletooth, an exiled quilboar held captive at Camp Taurajo, seeks these stones because of ancient beliefs about Agamaggan’s sacred essence. Horde adventurers raid the encampment for shards and trade them to Mangletooth for tribal charms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Agama'gor?",a="Agama'gor is a large Bristleback quilboar settlement in the southern Barrens, directly north of the road west from Camp Taurajo toward Mulgore.",al={"agamagor overview","what is this quilboar place","quilboar camp near taurajo"},it="place"},{q="Why are the Bristleback quilboar here so hostile?",a="Quilboar believe all land touched by the fallen Ancient boar god Agamaggan belongs to them. The Bristlebacks see the nearby tauren and orcs of Camp Taurajo as invaders on their ancestral soil.",al={"why do quilboar attack","quilboar hostility","why are bristlebacks angry"},it="conflict"},{q="What can you find in Agama'gor?",a="Bristleback quilboar in Agama'gor carry Blood Shards, crystallized deposits of primal power. You can trade them to Mangletooth, an exiled quilboar in Camp Taurajo.",al={"what to get here","agamagor drops","why kill bristlebacks here"},gp=true},{q="Who is Mangletooth and how does he relate to this place?",a="Mangletooth is an exiled quilboar held in a cage at Camp Taurajo. He resents his kin and offers Horde adventurers protective charms in exchange for Blood Shards taken from the Bristlebacks of Agama'gor.",al={"mangletooth connection","who is mangletooth","pig prisoner taurajo"},it="people"},{q="Who lives in Agama'gor?",a="Agama'gor is inhabited by the Bristleback quilboar. They have turned this territory north of Camp Taurajo into an entrenched settlement, ferociously defending their ground against any outsiders who approach their thorns and dwellings.",al={"who lives in agamagor","agamagor residents","who is at agamagor"},it="residents",add="62d1d1e5"},{q="Is Agama'gor dangerous?",a="Yes. Agama'gor teems with hostile Bristleback quilboar who attack travelers on sight. Its proximity to the western road from Camp Taurajo makes straying off the beaten path perilous for any wanderer unprepared for swarms of quilboar defenders.",al={"how dangerous is agamagor","is agamagor safe","agamagor danger"},it="danger",add="def0ef2e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As Horde defenders pass through Camp Taurajo, keeping the Bristlebacks of Agama'gor in check helps protect the outpost. Their warriors remain a priority.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you face danger from Agama'gor's marauders along the path to the Great Gate and Mulgore. They threaten supply lines and pilgrims."},kw={"agama'gor","agamagor","barrens","blood shards","bristleback","camp taurajo","mangletooth","quilboar"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","npc:mangletooth","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},src={"Agama'gor"}}
E["subzone:bael-dun-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Bael'dun Keep",z="barrens",s="Dwarven forces hold Bael'dun Keep above the Bael Modan excavation in the southern Barrens. Under General Twinbraid, this imposing fortification anchors the Alliance's controversial presence in the region and brings it into violent conflict with the surrounding Horde territories.",h="Dwarven forces hold Bael'dun Keep above the Bael Modan excavation in the southern Barrens.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Stronghold in Kalimdor",b="Bael'dun Keep rises over the Bael Modan excavation as the fortified military heart of Ironforge's presence in the southern Barrens. Dwarven architect Haggis Boatmurder designed the stronghold to protect the Prospectors and archaeologists searching the trenches for ancient titan artifacts. Ironworks and artillery arm its garrison, which keeps a vigilant watch, secures dwarven supply lines, and projects Alliance military power into Kalimdor's heartland.",sp=0},{t="A Flashpoint of Bloodshed",b="The keep and its adjoining digsite displaced the local Stonespire tribe of tauren from their ancestral home. Bael'dun remains a flashpoint in the Barrens, and nearby Horde outposts see it as a flagrant military intrusion. Gann Stonespire wages a personal war of vengeance against the invaders. Aggrieved tauren, opportunistic scouts, and suspicious outposts such as Camp Taurajo keep the fortress under threat of raids and sabotage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Bael'dun Keep?",a="Dwarven soldiers garrison Bael'dun Keep under the Alliance and Ironforge's Explorers' League. Their steadfast commander is General Twinbraid.",al={"who runs bael'dun keep","who leads baeldun","general twinbraid"},it="residents"},{q="Why is Bael'dun Keep built in the southern Barrens?",a="The Alliance established Bael'dun Keep to defend Bael Modan, a massive archaeological expedition seeking titan relics and ancient dwarven origins in Kalimdor.",al={"why are dwarves in the barrens","purpose of bael'dun keep","why did dwarves build here"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the local tauren attacking Bael'dun Keep?",a="The excavation and fortress displaced the Stonespire tauren from their ancestral grounds. Survivors such as Gann Stonespire seek vengeance and the destruction of the dwarven invaders.",al={"gann stonespire revenge","why do tauren hate baeldun","stonespire feud"},it="conflict"},{q="Who was the architect of the fortress?",a="Dwarven architectural records name Haggis Boatmurder as the architect who designed and constructed the fortress.",al={"who built bael'dun keep","haggis boatmurder","baeldun schematics"}},{q="What is Bael'dun Keep?",a="Bael'dun Keep is a heavily fortified dwarven stronghold erected in the southern Barrens. Towering over the Bael Modan excavation site, it serves as the military headquarters and defensive anchor for the Prospectors and soldiers dispatched by the Explorers' Guild and the Alliance. From behind its stone battlements and artillery, the dwarves protect their ongoing archaeological endeavors and secure an armed foothold right in the heart of Kalimdor.",al={"bael'dun keep","baeldun fortress","what is bael modan keep"},it="place",add="c3860f97"},{q="What happened at Bael'dun Keep?",a="Dwarven expedition forces pushed deep into the Barrens to unearth ancient titan artifacts, claiming the high ground at Bael Modan and erecting the fortified keep. In doing so, their excavation and military presence violently displaced the indigenous Stonespire tauren tribe from their ancestral sacred grounds. This sparked an open and bitter conflict, prompting surviving tauren to enlist the aid of the Horde to strike back and destroy the stronghold.",al={"baeldun history","bael'dun keep history","what happened at baeldun"},it="history",add="5592ca31"},{q="Is Bael'dun Keep dangerous?",a="Yes, especially if you pledge allegiance to the Horde. Bael'dun Keep is garrisoned by heavily armed dwarven riflemen, officers, and sentries commanded by General Twinbraid, who are aggressively hostile to any Horde trespassers approaching their dig. Between formidable defensive walls, heavy ordnance, and concentrated Alliance firepower, wandering near its gates is an invitation to be shot on sight.",al={"is baeldun dangerous","bael'dun keep threats","is bael modan hostile"},it="danger",add="223c6b8e"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Bael'dun Keep occupies grounds taken from the Stonespire tribe, a reminder of Alliance encroachment on your homeland.",["faction:Alliance"]="Bael'dun Keep is your primary military foothold in the southern Barrens, guarding the Explorers' League's vital discoveries against hostile Horde forces."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun keep","baeldun","explorers' league","gann stonespire","general twinbraid","haggis boatmurder","southern barrens"},rel={"subzone:bael-modan","npc:gann-stonespire","npc:feegly-the-exiled","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:tauren","topic:horde","zone:barrens"},src={"Bael'dun Keep"}}
E["subzone:bael-modan"] = {t="subzone",n="Bael Modan",z="barrens",s="Dwarven crews blast into the red earth at Bael Modan, searching for Titan relics. Their fortified outpost has driven the Stonespire tauren from their sacred land and kindled a bitter fight.",h="Dwarven crews blast into the red earth at Bael Modan, searching for Titan relics.",sec={{t="Unearthed Secrets and Bloodshed",b="Bael Modan's walls guard Bael'dun Keep, siege cannons, gyrocopter landing pads, and a deep excavation pit. Dwarven prospectors came to Kalimdor convinced an ancient Titan facility lay beneath the red earth. Their blasting tore through sacred ground of the Stonespire tauren. The expedition answered no call to negotiate. Gunfire and explosives drove the tribe from its ancestral lands, leaving survivors scattered and vengeful.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Unearthed Relics",b="The diggers have uncovered more than old stonework. Among their finds is the Tear of the Moons, an artifact that brings paranoia and madness to those near it. Feegly the Exiled, a prospector banished from the camp, fell wholly under its sway. When the stone returned to his grasp, he became a trogg. Outside the gates, enraged tauren seek retribution, while deadly relics threaten the dwarves within.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are dwarves digging in the Barrens?",a="Dwarven crews search Kalimdor for ancient Titan structures and relics buried beneath the earth. They believe buried Titan research facilities hold clues to the origins of their race.",al={"why are dwarves here","bael modan purpose","what are dwarves digging for"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the tauren who used to live here?",a="The Stonespire tribe once held these hills as holy ground. When the dwarves arrived, they blasted open the dig site with explosives, killing some tauren and driving others away while destroying their village.",al={"stonespire tauren","who lived at bael modan","tauren village"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gann Stonespire?",a="Gann Stonespire is one of the few Stonespire survivors. After peaceful efforts failed, he made camp by the road outside Bael Modan and calls on Horde travelers to sabotage the dwarven flying machines and kill the officers who destroyed his people's home.",al={"gann","gann questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Tear of the Moons?",a="The Tear of the Moons is a mysterious artifact found by the excavators. It drives mortals who handle it mad, and the exiled dwarf Feegly is obsessed with reclaiming it.",al={"tear of the moons relic","feegly artifact"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="What is Bael Modan?",a="Bael Modan is a heavily fortified dwarven excavation site and stronghold situated in the southern reaches of the Barrens. Dominated by mighty fortifications, towering cannons, and massive mechanical diggers, the facility was established by the Explorer's League to unearth ancient Titan secrets buried deep beneath the earth. It serves as the primary base of Alliance power and archaeological ambition in the region.",al={"bael modan info","what is this place bael modan","dwarf base southern barrens"},it="place",add="85aa09cd"},{q="What happened at Bael Modan?",a="Before the dwarves arrived, these lands were the ancestral territory of the Stonespire tauren. Driven by archaeological ambition, dwarven expedition forces tore into the earth with heavy explosives and siege machinery. The encroachment sparked a violent conflict that devastated the peaceful Stonespire tribe, scattering the survivors and turning the sacred grounds into an active, fortified war zone carved open by mining trenches.",al={"bael modan history","history of bael modan","what happened here bael modan"},it="history",add="8ce94b36"},{q="Who runs Bael Modan?",a="The stronghold and its archaeological diggings operate under the joint authority of Ironforge military officers and Prospectors. Key figures overseeing operations include General Twinbraid, Heggin Stonewhisker, Prospector Khazgorm, Malgin Barleybrew, Captain Gerogg Hammertoe, and the famed flying machine pilot Lord Cyrik Blackforge.",al={"who leads bael modan","bael modan leaders","who is in charge of bael modan"},it="residents",add="f7e6e142"},{q="Is Bael Modan dangerous?",a="Yes, especially if you walk under the banner of the Horde. The dwarves garrisoned here are on high alert, equipped with rifle squads, siege engines, flying machines, and massive fortifications. Furthermore, their subterranean excavations risk disturbing buried relics and volatile curses best left forgotten in the deep dark of the earth.",al={"bael modan danger","is bael modan hostile","can i go to bael modan"},it="danger",add="e130d5b0"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see Bael Modan as an open wound, built over the Stonespire tribe's sacred grounds. Helping Gann Stonespire seek vengeance honors the tribe.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see the Explorers' League pressing on to uncover Titan history. Its commanders' harsh tactics have earned the local tribes' fierce hatred."},kw={"bael modan","bael'dun","barrens excavation","feegly","gann stonespire","stonespire","tear of the moons","twinbraid"},rel={"zone:barrens","npc:gann-stonespire","quest:843","quest:857","npc:feegly-the-exiled","subzone:bael-dun-keep","subzone:bael-dun-digsite","topic:titan"},src={"Bael Modan"}}
E["subzone:blackthorn-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackthorn Ridge",z="barrens",s="At Blackthorn Ridge, Razormane quilboar guard the southern Barrens north of Razorfen Kraul. Brine, an orc shaman, keeps watch from a camp above a pool of unusually pure mountain water.",h="At Blackthorn Ridge, Razormane quilboar guard the southern Barrens north of Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="A Thorn-Choked Redoubt",b="Blackthorn Ridge rises beside Razorfen Kraul, its slopes crowded with dense thickets of sharp briars. The Razormane quilboar claim the ground as ancestral territory, using the thorny barriers to ambush outsiders and skirmish across the southern Barrens. Travelers seek out the ridge despite the danger, drawn to Brine, a hermit orc shaman. His camp sits above a spring famed across Kalimdor for its clear, spiritually pure water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Blackthorn Ridge?",a="Blackthorn Ridge lies in the far southern Barrens, just north of the briars around Razorfen Kraul and south of Camp Taurajo.",al={"blackthorn ridge location","where is blackthorn","how to find blackthorn ridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives at Blackthorn Ridge?",a="Hostile Razormane quilboar occupy the valley floor. Brine, an orc shaman, lives on a rocky perch above their brambles and watches over the nearby mountain spring.",al={"who is at blackthorn ridge","blackthorn ridge inhabitants","quilboar blackthorn"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the pool beneath Brine's camp special?",a="A hidden pool beneath the ridge holds exceptionally pure, clear water, despite the dry plains and the quilboar thornbrakes around it. Shamans use the pool as a sacred focus for their rituals.",al={"brine pool","water of blackthorn","blackthorn ridge spring"}},{q="What is Blackthorn Ridge?",a="Blackthorn Ridge is a jagged, bramble-choked valley situated in the southern Barrens, just north of the massive quilboar redoubt known as Razorfen Kraul. The area takes its name from the high ridge rising above the valley, where massive briars twist across the arid rock. It serves as an entrenched outpost for local quilboar tribes, set apart from the open plains.",al={"what is blackthorn ridge","blackthorn ridge overview","tell me about blackthorn ridge"},it="place",add="a60eac08"},{q="Is Blackthorn Ridge dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely perilous for unwary travelers. The valley floor and surrounding paths are heavily prowled by hostile Razormane quilboar guarding the approaches to Razorfen Kraul. Aside from an isolated orc shaman named Brine encamped on the high ridge, there are no friendly outposts or safe paths through the thickets.",al={"is blackthorn ridge safe","danger blackthorn ridge","how dangerous is blackthorn ridge"},it="danger",add="4cf5ece9"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Young Horde shamans seek out Brine at the ridge to learn about the purity of natural water elements amid the harsh, dry plains.",["faction:Horde"]="Razormane quilboar threaten Horde supply lines through the southern Barrens toward Thousand Needles, so passing caravans must stay vigilant."},kw={"barrens","blackthorn ridge","brine","pure water","quilboar","razorfen kraul","razormane"},rel={"npc:brine","zone:razorfenkraul","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","topic:razorfen"},src={"Blackthorn Ridge"}}
E["subzone:boulder-lode-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulder Lode Mine",z="barrens",s="In the northeastern Barrens, the Venture Company tears into Boulder Lode Mine for its riches. Orcish banners and watchtowers mark a claim the Horde once held.",h="In the northeastern Barrens, the Venture Company tears into Boulder Lode Mine for its riches.",sec={{t="Corporate Claim",b="Weathered orcish works frame the mine mouth, signs that the Horde once held or founded the claim. Now Venture Company overseers and enforcers answer to Boss Copperplug. The goblin syndicate strips the canyon for minerals, gems, and machinery, with little care for the land or its workers.",sp=0},{t="Gems and Schematics",b="Riches from the mine have drawn attention from Ratchet. Wharfmaster Dizzywig has sent mercenaries after a rumored massive emerald found in the tunnels. Engineers seeking to understand goblin machinery also know that Boss Copperplug keeps key operating manuals in his camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Boulder Lode Mine?",a="The Venture Company runs Boulder Lode Mine under Boss Copperplug, with armed enforcers and overseers guarding its work.",al={"who runs boulder lode mine","boulder lode boss","who is in boulder lode"},it="in_charge"},{q="Did the Horde originally own this mine?",a="Weathered orcish woodwork, watchtowers, and Horde banners suggest the Horde first established or claimed the site before the Venture Company took control.",al={"orc banners at boulder lode","horde mine","why are there horde flags"},it="history"},{q="Why is Wharfmaster Dizzywig interested in this place?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig heard that a miner unearthed an unusually large emerald in the tunnels. He hires cutthroats to steal it for a share of the profits.",al={"dizzywig mine quest","emerald quest barrens","miners fortune"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Boss Copperplug's connection to the samophlange?",a="Boss Copperplug holds the operating manual for the nearby samophlange machinery. Engineers in Ratchet send adventurers to recover the book and its scattered pages from his crew.",al={"samophlange manual boulder lode","copperplug manual","rilli greasygob mine"},it="item"},{q="What is Boulder Lode Mine?",a="Boulder Lode Mine is a mining operation nestled in the rocky hills of northeastern Barrens. Though built with unmistakable orcish timber and banners suggesting it was once established by the Horde, the mine has been taken over by the Venture Company. Today, goblin overseers and hired enforcers drive frantic excavation efforts deep into the rock, scouring the earth for valuable ores and precious gems.",al={"what is boulder lode mine","boulder lode mine barrens","about boulder lode mine"},it="place",add="60cbae83"},{q="Who lives in or runs Boulder Lode Mine?",a="The mine is currently occupied by the Venture Company, under the ruthless supervision of Boss Copperplug. He oversees a labor force guarded by Venture Company overseers and enforcers, driving continuous excavation into the hills while keeping a tight grip on proprietary machinery manuals and valuable discoveries.",al={"who runs boulder lode mine","who is at boulder lode mine","boulder lode mine inhabitants"},it="residents",add="97c77cb5"},{q="Is Boulder Lode Mine dangerous?",a="Yes. The Venture Company does not welcome visitors or trespassers poking around their enterprise. The mine crawls with armed enforcers and vigilant overseers who will attack anyone threatening their claims or attempting to plunder the precious mineral veins and treasures hidden inside.",al={"is boulder lode mine dangerous","boulder lode mine dangers","venture co danger boulder lode"},it="danger",add="a11a7920"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, seeing Venture Company crews work from fortifications marked with Horde standards is a bitter reminder of the cartel's reach across Kalimdor.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can see rich veins in the deep tunnels cut into the arid hills, where the Venture Company strips the earth without mercy."},kw={"boss copperplug","boulder lode mine","dizzywig","miner's fortune","samophlange manual","the barrens","venture company"},rel={"topic:venture-company","zone:barrens","quest:896","quest:3924","quest:1492","quest:3923","quest:894","topic:horde"},src={"Boulder Lode Mine"}}
E["subzone:bramblescar"] = {t="subzone",n="Bramblescar",z="barrens",s="Across the southern Barrens, Bramblescar's Razormane wage war with the Bristleback across the Gold Road. Thick brambles fortify their settlement.",h="Across the southern Barrens, Bramblescar's Razormane wage war with the Bristleback across the Gold Road.",sec={{t="A Thorned Redoubt",b="Bramblescar is carved into the jagged briars of the southern Barrens. The thick, sharp thorns make a vital redoubt for the Razormane quilboar and deter casual wanderers. The tribe is fiercely territorial and hostile to outsiders. They skirmish with anyone who approaches, treating all who are not quilboar as intruders on land blessed by their ancient boar gods.",sp=0},{t="Tribal Blood Feud",b="Bramblescar sits in perpetual tension with Agama'gor, the Bristleback encampment directly across the Gold Road. The rival tribes wage an unrelenting war for dominion over the southern Barrens. Razormane warriors fight Horde travelers along the highway and repel Bristleback raiding parties, keeping them on constant, violent alert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Bramblescar?",a="The Razormane tribe of quilboar lives in Bramblescar. They defend their thorn-choked encampment from rival quilboar and travelers passing through.",al={"who is here","bramblescar mobs","bramblescar quilboar"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the quilboar here fighting each other?",a="The Razormane of Bramblescar and the Bristleback across the road at Agama'gor are bitter enemies, locked in a fierce territorial feud for control of the southern Barrens.",al={"why are they at war","razormane vs bristleback","quilboar war"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Bramblescar located?",a="Bramblescar lies in the southern plains of the Barrens, just east of the main Gold Road and across from Agama'gor.",al={"bramblescar location","where is bramblescar","how to find bramblescar"},gp=true},{q="Are the quilboar here hostile to the Horde?",a="Yes. The Razormane view the Horde as invaders on their sacred tribal lands and attack any traveler who wanders close.",al={"is bramblescar friendly","horde reputation bramblescar"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Bramblescar?",a="Bramblescar is an encampment and lair of the Razormane quilboar in the southern Barrens. It sits along the main roadway, directly opposite the Bristleback quilboar holding of Agama'gor. The settlement serves as a fortified base for the Razormane in their relentless territorial war against their Bristleback rivals.",al={"what is bramblescar","bramblescar info","about bramblescar"},it="place",add="86a75fd0"},{q="Is Bramblescar dangerous?",a="Yes, Bramblescar is exceptionally hazardous to any traveler. The Razormane quilboar who dwell here are fiercely aggressive and will readily ambush anyone who wanders close to their lair, regardless of who they are, all while waging a violent war with the nearby Bristleback tribe.",al={"is bramblescar dangerous","bramblescar danger","how safe is bramblescar"},it="danger",add="f9fc9349"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you need the Gold Road clear of raids from Bramblescar to travel safely between Crossroads, Camp Taurajo, and the southern frontier."},kw={"agama'gor","barrens","bramblescar","bristleback","gold road","quilboar","razormane"},rel={"subzone:agama-gor","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},src={"Bramblescar"}}
E["subzone:camp-taurajo"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp Taurajo",z="barrens",s="Camp Taurajo holds the eastern mouth of the pass into Mulgore. The tauren camp offers travelers an inn, supplies, mentors, and wind rider routes across the plains and central Kalimdor.",h="Camp Taurajo holds the eastern mouth of the pass into Mulgore.",sec={{t="Frontier of the Red Rocks",b="At Camp Taurajo, you reach the eastern mouth of the pass into Mulgore. For young tauren leaving Bloodhoof Village, the camp is often their first glimpse of the wider Barrens. Dry scrubland and rugged mesas surround this outpost and trading hub. Hunters, leathercrafters, and field herbalists find shelter here, while wind riders connect the camp to Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, and Freewind Post deeper south.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camp Taurajo?",a="Camp Taurajo is a tauren settlement and outpost in the southern Barrens, between Mulgore and the Barrens' arid scrublands.",al={"camp taurajo overview","what is taurajo","taurajo lore"},it="place"},{q="Where does the road west lead?",a="The dirt trail west from Camp Taurajo crosses the mountain pass into Mulgore, toward Bloodhoof Village and Thunder Bluff.",al={"taurajo west pass","road west of camp taurajo","path to mulgore"},gp=true},{q="Where do the wind riders from Camp Taurajo fly?",a="Wind riders from Camp Taurajo travel to the Crossroads to the north, Thunder Bluff to the west, and Freewind Post in Thousand Needles to the south.",al={"taurajo flight master","taurajo flight paths","flight connections taurajo"},gp=true},{q="Is Camp Taurajo dangerous?",a="The camp itself is a secure settlement protected by tauren braves, but the surrounding wilderness of the southern Barrens is treacherous. Aggressive quilboar tribes contest the scrublands nearby, while prowling beasts and roaming predators make straying far from the road a perilous venture.",al={"is camp taurajo safe","dangers near camp taurajo","threats around taurajo"},it="danger",add="9a32993c"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren leaving Mulgore for the first time, you find Camp Taurajo as the first friendly shelter on the Barrens' harsh plains.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can use Camp Taurajo's overland junction and flight path to connect Mulgore with the rest of Horde-controlled central Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","bloodhoof village","camp taurajo","mulgore pass","southern barrens","taurajo","tauren outpost"},rel={"zone:barrens","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren","subzone:crossroads","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:bloodhoof-village","subzone:freewind-post"},src={"Camp Taurajo"}}
E["subzone:crossroads"] = {t="subzone",n="Crossroads",z="barrens",s="At Crossroads, Horde travelers meet where the Gold Road crosses the route from Ratchet to the Stonetalon Mountains. The outpost handles trade, military staging, and travel between Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern frontlines.",h="At Crossroads, Horde travelers meet where the Gold Road crosses the route from Ratchet to the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Vital Junction in the Savannah",b="Crossroads sits where the Gold Road meets the route from the goblin port of Ratchet into the Stonetalon Mountains. Its lodgings are modest, but travelers find wind rider masters, merchants, blacksmiths, and trainers beneath the watchtowers. For young warriors from Durotar or Mulgore, the outpost reveals how the new Horde links its far-flung fronts and supplies.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Outpost Under Siege",b="Keeping order at Crossroads is a constant struggle. Plains raptors prowl close enough to steal payroll silver from the guard towers, while harpies, quilboar, and centaur tribes press against the perimeter. Neutral Ratchet lies nearby, and Ashenvale's contested forests are within reach. Alliance scouts often strike near the outpost's defensive barricades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Crossroads so important to the Horde?",a="Crossroads anchors central Kalimdor's main routes. Travelers moving overland between Durotar, Mulgore, Ratchet, Stonetalon, or Ashenvale pass through or near the outpost, making it a key point for supplies and reinforcements.",al={"why is crossroads important","crossroads purpose","why crossroads matters"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides flight transport at the Crossroads?",a="Devrak manages the wind rider roost at Crossroads. He connects travelers to outposts across Kalimdor, including Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff.",al={"crossroads flight master","who has wyverns here","flight master crossroads"},gp=true},{q="Why does the Alliance attack the Crossroads so frequently?",a="Crossroads lies at the heart of Horde travel, within striking distance of Ashenvale and Ratchet. Alliance raiding parties target the outpost to disrupt Horde supply lines.",al={"why alliance raids crossroads","alliance pvp crossroads","crossroads attacks"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to the outpost's payroll silver?",a="Barrens raptors stole a shipment of silver from the Crossroads guard tower. The silver was meant to pay the defending guards, and the raptors scattered it across the surrounding savannah.",al={"stolen payroll crossroads","who took the silver","crossroads silver stolen"}},{q="What is the Crossroads?",a="The Crossroads is the largest and most central Horde settlement in the Barrens. Built around a fortified watchtower and inn, it serves as the primary waystation and supply depot connecting Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, Ratchet, and the frontier in Stonetalon and Ashenvale. For travelers across central Kalimdor, it is a bustling hub for rest, trade, and regional defense.",al={"what is crossroads","crossroads barrens","what is the crossroads town"},it="place",add="2f66b0ff"},{q="Why is it called the Crossroads?",a="The outpost takes its name directly from geography: it sits squarely where the main north-south Gold Road intersects the east-west route running from the neutral port of Ratchet into the Stonetalon Mountains. Because nearly every overland journey through the Barrens crosses here, the settlement grew naturally around that crucial junction.",al={"why crossroads","crossroads name origin","how did crossroads get its name"},it="name",add="6d918d5a"},{q="Is the Crossroads dangerous?",a="While the interior is secured by Horde guards, the settlement faces constant peril. Its close proximity to Ashenvale and Ratchet makes it a frequent target for daring Alliance incursions, while the surrounding plains are plagued by aggressive raptors, harpy raiders, and hostile quilboar tribes looking to sever the Horde's vital supply lines.",al={"is crossroads safe","crossroads dangers","threats to crossroads"},it="danger",add="9b710adc"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Crossroads linking the homelands of orcs, tauren, and trolls while coordinating supplies across Kalimdor. It is a proving ground for your fledgling nation.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can strike Crossroads to disrupt Horde reinforcements moving between Orgrimmar, Mulgore, and Ashenvale's disputed borders."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","gold road","raptors","ratchet","stonetalon","wind rider"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:gold-road","npc:devrak","subzone:ratchet","zone:orgrimmar","zone:thunderbluff","quest:869","quest:3281"},src={"Crossroads"}}
E["subzone:dreadmist-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmist Den",z="barrens",s="In the northern Barrens, Burning Blade cultists keep their rites beneath Dreadmist Peak. Red haze fills the cavern they use as a shrine to demons.",h="In the northern Barrens, Burning Blade cultists keep their rites beneath Dreadmist Peak.",sec={{t="A Den of Wicked Shadows",b="Dreadmist Den cuts into the jagged slopes of Dreadmist Peak, where Burning Blade cultists gather in a dark sanctuary. Thick crimson vapor hangs through its stone tunnels, dimming the cavern in red twilight. Away from the Horde's watch in the plains below, the cult performs demonic rites, guards its blasphemous relics, and plots to spread corruption across Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="The Demon Seed",b="Deep in Dreadmist Den, the Demon Seed rests above the Altar of Fire. The cult prizes the artifact for its fel power, and it is connected to the Burning Legion. Ak'Zeloth prepares a power stone to disrupt that connection. Horde scouts and aspiring warlocks who follow the Burning Blade's activity face danger in the cavern as they seek to learn how far demonic influence reaches in the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Dreadmist Den?",a="Dreadmist Den cuts beneath Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens. Burning Blade cultists use its caves as an enclave and a place for their rites.",al={"dreadmist den","what is dreadmist den","barrens dreadmist cave"},it="place"},{q="What causes the red mist inside the den?",a="Red haze shrouds Dreadmist Den and the peak above it. Burning Blade cultists perform demonic rites there, but the haze's exact cause is unknown.",al={"red haze dreadmist","crimson fog barrens","red mist dreadmist den"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Demon Seed found inside?",a="The Demon Seed is a dark artifact kept deep within Dreadmist Den. The Burning Blade cult prizes it as a powerful focus for fel magic.",al={"demon seed","what is demon seed","artifact in dreadmist den"},it="item"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this cave?",a="The Horde fears the Burning Blade's demon worship and its efforts to undermine the Horde across Kalimdor. A stronghold near Crossroads and Orgrimmar threatens the security of the Barrens.",al={"horde dreadmist den","why clear dreadmist den","orcs burning blade barrens"},it="purpose"},{q="Who lives in Dreadmist Den?",a="The cave is occupied by cultists of the Burning Blade. These demonic worshippers use the secluded mountain cavern as a hidden sanctuary and ritual redoubt, dwelling under the perpetual twilight cast by the unnatural red vapors within.",al={"dreadmist den residents","who is in dreadmist den","who controls dreadmist den"},it="residents",add="43f375e7"},{q="Is Dreadmist Den dangerous?",a="The den is dangerous because Burning Blade cultists defend their demonic shrine. A red haze shrouds the cavern, and intruders must contend with its hostile occupants.",al={"dreadmist den danger","is dreadmist cave safe","how dangerous is dreadmist den"},it="danger",add="bcbe1c71"},{q="Why is it called Dreadmist Den?",a="The cavern takes its name from the dark red mist that perpetually cloaks the interior. This noxious fog seeps through the peak, casting everything inside in eerie twilight and lending its sinister moniker to both the mountain and the den beneath it.",al={"why dreadmist den","dreadmist den name origin","meaning of dreadmist den"},it="name",add="5db705cc"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may be drawn to the demonic relics and volatile fel energies within Dreadmist Den, and to the Burning Blade's dark secrets.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face danger from the Burning Blade den overlooking the Barrens. Its presence threatens nearby trade routes and settlements, calling for swift action from Horde defenders."},kw={"barrens","burning blade","cultists","demon seed","dreadmist den","dreadmist peak","red mist"},rel={"subzone:dreadmist-peak","quest:924","zone:barrens"},src={"Dreadmist Den"}}
E["subzone:dreadmist-peak"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmist Peak",z="barrens",s="Red haze cloaks Dreadmist Peak, northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. The Burning Blade cult keeps a hidden refuge on its crags.",h="Red haze cloaks Dreadmist Peak, northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Den of Corruption",b="Dreadmist Peak rises above the Barrens, its crags swallowed by a dense red haze that dims the sky. At the crest and in the hollows below, Burning Blade cultists shelter warlocks and toxicologists. They poison nearby water and scheme against the new powers claiming central Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Convergence of Schemes",b="Dreadmist Peak draws more than the Burning Blade. Sarilus Foulborne, a rogue Forsaken mage, has made camp on its heights. He bends elemental forces to corrupt water spirits as far north as Ashenvale.",sp=1,bt={"q1016.2"}}},faq={{q="Why is the air red and foggy around Dreadmist Peak?",a="No one knows where the reddish-orange fog around Dreadmist Peak comes from. It covers the trails and Dreadmist Den, where Burning Blade warlocks perform their rituals.",al={"red mist dreadmist","orange fog dreadmist peak","why is dreadmist red"},it="name"},{q="Who controls Dreadmist Peak?",a="The Burning Blade cult controls Dreadmist Peak, watches its trails, and guards Dreadmist Den below. Sarilus Foulborne, a renegade undead mage, also occupies the mountain.",al={"who lives on dreadmist peak","dreadmist peak enemies","burning blade dreadmist"},it="residents"},{q="How do you reach Dreadmist Peak?",a="Follow the main road north from the Crossroads to the fork for Ashenvale and Stonetalon. Turn northwest toward the looming crag, then climb the path up its northern face for the safest route to the top.",al={"getting to dreadmist peak","dreadmist peak location","dreadmist path"},gp=true},{q="What is Dreadmist Peak?",a="Dreadmist Peak is a jagged, ominous mountain rising northwest of the Crossroads in the northern Barrens. Shrouded in an eerie red-orange fog, it serves as a notorious stronghold for the shadowy Burning Blade cult. Its heights conceal treacherous caves like the Dreadmist Den, where warlocks and cultists conduct foul rituals to blight the surrounding savanna.",al={"what is dreadmist peak","dreadmist peak lore","tell me about dreadmist peak"},it="place",add="225dd39b"},{q="Is Dreadmist Peak dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The mountain crawls with fanatical Burning Blade acolytes, bruisers, toxicologists, and dark summoners who fiercely guard their ritual sites. Beyond the hostile cultists, the water of the peak is believed to be poisoning the wildlife of the Barrens below.",al={"is dreadmist peak dangerous","dreadmist peak threats","dangers of dreadmist peak"},it="danger",add="9aed69cf"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, you investigate Dreadmist Peak's water sources from Camp Taurajo, seeking the unnatural toxins poisoning the gazelles and wildlife of the plains.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance agent near Ashenvale, you trace the magic corrupting water elementals to Sarilus Foulborne, an undead summoner on the peak."},kw={"barrens","burning blade","dreadmist den","dreadmist peak","miasma","sarilus foulborne"},rel={"subzone:dreadmist-den","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","quest:6122","quest:1017","topic:druid","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Dreadmist Peak"}}
E["subzone:dry-hills"] = {t="subzone",n="Dry Hills",z="barrens",s="Witchwing harpies menace the Dry Hills, where greener slopes rise above the Barrens.",h="Witchwing harpies menace the Dry Hills, where greener slopes rise above the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Green Haven for Harpies",b="The Dry Hills grow greener than the dry plains below, on the Barrens' northwestern edge beneath the Stonetalon Mountains. Travelers find little safety among the bluffs. Serena Bloodfeather leads the Witchwing harpies from their roosts along the crags. Their raiding parties swoop down on supply caravans along the northern Gold Road. Abandoned orcish fortifications and derelict siege engines lie rotting in the brush.",sp=0},{t="Threat to the Crossroads",b="Witchwing harpies strike out from the hills to bleed trade routes and harass nearby settlements, so the Horde keeps a standing bounty on their feathers. In the rocky ravines, their nests and roosts are heavily defended. Hecklefang hyenas prowl there, and fierce Sunscale raptors hunt across the highlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Dry Hills if it's so green?",a="Despite their name, the Dry Hills are noticeably greener than the surrounding Barrens. No record explains the name or this local contrast.",al={"why called dry hills","dry hills green","dry hills terrain"},it="name"},{q="Who lives in the Dry Hills?",a="The Witchwing tribe of harpies controls almost all of the hills, under Serena Bloodfeather's rule. Hecklefang hyenas and Sunscale raptors also roam the rocky slopes.",al={"who is in dry hills","dry hills inhabitants","harpies dry hills"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in this area?",a="Witchwing raiders strike out from the hills to plunder supply caravans along the northern Gold Road. Horde commanders issue bounties to cull their numbers and eliminate their leaders.",al={"horde dry hills","why fight harpies here","dry hills quests"},it="motive"},{q="What are the ruined towers and catapults in the middle of the hills?",a="The towers and catapults are remains of an abandoned orcish outpost. The surviving structures do not establish its original mission or why it was deserted.",al={"orc tower dry hills","abandoned catapults dry hills","orc ruins dry hills"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the Dry Hills?",a="The Dry Hills are a lush, verdant pocket nestled in the northwestern reaches of the Barrens, resting right along the foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains. In stark contrast to the parched savannahs stretching to the south and east, this area flourishes with green brush and tall bluffs. However, its tranquil appearance is deceptive, as the slopes have become the roost of dangerous creatures and a contested highland on the border of Horde lands.",al={"what are the dry hills","dry hills lore","dry hills info"},it="place",add="06447f2d"},{q="Is the Dry Hills dangerous?",a="Venturing into the Dry Hills is perilous. The crags are fiercely guarded by the Witchwing harpies, led by Serena Bloodfeather, who actively raid supply caravans traveling along the northern Gold Road. Beyond the harpies and their ambushers, aggressive Hecklefang hyenas and Sunscale raptors prowl the ridges, ready to tear apart anyone who wanders off the beaten path without preparation.",al={"are dry hills safe","dry hills threats","danger in dry hills"},it="danger",add="9a122504"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Witchwing harpies nesting in the Dry Hills threaten the northern trade routes linking the Crossroads to Stonetalon and Ashenvale. Horde champions must regularly cull them.",["class:Hunter"]="The rugged uplands offer rich hunting grounds, with swift Hecklefang hyenas, predatory Sunscale scytheclaws, and fierce harpies."},kw={"barrens","dry hills","gold road","harpies","serena bloodfeather","stonetalon","witchwing"},rel={"zone:barrens","topic:harpy","quest:867","quest:876","zone:stonetalon","subzone:gold-road"},src={"Dry Hills"}}
E["subzone:far-watch-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Far Watch Post",z="barrens",s="Horde defenders hold Far Watch Post west of the Southfury River bridge, guarding the homeland's frontier. The outpost protects vital trade caravans from quilboar packs and Alliance incursions.",h="Horde defenders hold Far Watch Post west of the Southfury River bridge, guarding the homeland's frontier.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Border",b="Far Watch Post guards the western foot of the bridge from Durotar into the Barrens. You enter a vast, arid savannah, where this is the first sign of Horde authority. The settlement is spare but built for readiness, with an orcish watchtower, a burrow, and siege catapults aimed across the plains. South of the main road, peons tend riding wolves for messengers or reinforcements. The post keeps the supply road to Crossroads secure, screening travelers and turning back raids by roaming quilboar tribes and Alliance scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Far Watch Post?",a="Far Watch Post guards the border between Durotar and the Barrens. Its defenders protect vital Horde supply caravans and keep quilboar tribes and Alliance trespassers from crossing the Southfury River into Durotar.",al={"why is far watch post here","purpose of far watch","far watch outpost role"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="The Horde mans Far Watch Post as an active military camp. Orc grunts garrison the tower and maintain the siege engines, while peons tend the riding wolves.",al={"who runs far watch post","far watch post faction"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats does the outpost face?",a="Quilboar packs harass Far Watch Post from nearby scrubland, and Alliance forces may strike across the Barrens toward Orgrimmar.",al={"far watch post enemies","dangers at far watch"},it="threat"},{q="What is Far Watch Post?",a="Far Watch Post is a fortified Horde outpost situated just west of the bridge linking Durotar to the Barrens. Marked by a sturdy watchtower, an orc burrow, catapults, and wolf pens to the south, it serves as the primary gateway defending Durotar's western frontier and securing passage for travelers and supply caravans entering the wild plains.",al={"what is far watch post","far watch post lore","explain far watch post"},it="place",add="c35ec5b1"},{q="Is Far Watch Post dangerous?",a="For Horde travelers, the post itself offers safety under the vigilant guard of seasoned warriors and peons. Beyond its perimeter, however, the area remains hazardous. Hostile quilboar prowl the surrounding scrublands, and potential Alliance incursions threaten the open road, requiring travelers and sentries alike to stay constantly on guard.",al={"is far watch post safe","danger far watch post","far watch post danger"},it="danger",add="d7c9315a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For a young Horde warrior leaving Durotar, Far Watch Post marks the last familiar ground before the rugged, dangerous heartland of Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Across the bridge from Durotar, Far Watch Post blocks Alliance scouts and saboteurs from easily approaching the orcish capital."},kw={"barrens","burrow","durotar","far watch post","peons","quilboar","southfury river","watchtower","wolves"},rel={"zone:barrens","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:quilboar","topic:alliance"},src={"Far Watch Post"}}
E["subzone:field-of-giants"] = {t="subzone",n="Field of Giants",z="barrens",s="The Field of Giants spreads across the southern Barrens, from Camp Taurajo to Dustwallow's marshes. Towering kodo, thunder lizards, and other great beasts graze its dry scrub, while silithids make the plain more dangerous.",h="The Field of Giants spreads across the southern Barrens, from Camp Taurajo to Dustwallow's marshes.",sec={{t="A Wild Frontier in the South",b="The Field of Giants follows the southern Gold Road, far from the Barrens' better-defended north. Wooden watchtowers along the road sit largely abandoned, while great herds roam the open flats. Hunters and naturalists come to see Kalimdor's enormous beasts, but the land is not safe. Dwarven excavators from Bael Modan dig aggressively to the south, and a more sinister threat has begun burrowing underground.",sp=0},{t="The Creeping Swarm",b="Silithid hives have recently broken through the ground across the Field of Giants. They mark the northernmost known sighting of these ravenous creatures in Kalimdor. Their strange mounds and aggressive swarms have alarmed the Horde. Korran, a troll scout from the Crossroads, and Ruga Ragetotem, a tauren warrior at Camp Taurajo, urge adventurers to investigate the hives and learn what draws these horrors so far from the deep deserts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Field of Giants?",a="The plain takes its name from its enormous wildlife. Great herds of towering kodo and thunder lizards graze here, alongside other massive Kalimdorean beasts.",al={"field of giants name origin","why field of giants"},it="name"},{q="What are those bug mounds in the ground?",a="Those mounds belong to silithids, insectoid predators that have tunneled up from deep underground. Their hives are the northernmost discovered in Kalimdor, and they threaten travelers and local wildlife.",al={"bug mounds barrens","insects in southern barrens","what are the silithid"},it="threat"},{q="Who lives near the Field of Giants?",a="Few settlements lie on the plain itself, but the tauren shaman Brine lives on a southern ridge. Nearby, the displaced exile Gann Stonespire watches and plots against the dwarven excavation at Bael Modan.",al={"who lives here","field of giants npcs"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the watchtowers along the road abandoned?",a="The Horde concentrates its forces along the northern Gold Road near the Crossroads, so the southern reaches receive fewer patrols. The towers have been neglected amid silithid threats and aggressive wildlife.",al={"abandoned towers gold road","southern barrens watchtowers"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the Field of Giants?",a="The Field of Giants is an expansive expanse in the southern Barrens, situated between Camp Taurajo and the road leading toward Dustwallow Marsh. Straddled by the southern stretch of the Gold Road, these sunbaked plains are famed for the massive herds of thunder lizards, kodos, and other colossal Kalimdorean beasts that roam freely across the savanna.",al={"field of giants overview","what is this place field of giants","about field of giants"},it="place",add="c3e59f7c"},{q="What is the history of the Field of Giants?",a="Long a wild stomping ground for Kalimdor's greatest megafauna, the Field of Giants once saw regular watch along the southern Gold Road before its defense towers fell into neglect. In recent days, the landscape has grown unsettled as encroaching silithid swarms have dug massive hives beneath the soil, and nearby dwarven excavators at Bael Modan displaced local tribes like Gann Stonespire's people.",al={"field of giants history","what happened at field of giants","field of giants past"},it="history",add="2ebbbb7d"},{q="Is the Field of Giants dangerous?",a="It is quite perilous. Beyond the towering, aggressive thunder lizards and heavy kodo herds that stampede across the plains, an aggressive silithid hive has recently erupted from beneath the red dirt. Travelers along the southern Gold Road find little shelter, as the regional watchtowers stand empty and unguarded.",al={"field of giants danger","how dangerous is field of giants","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="b9c947c6"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Thunder lizards and massive kodo roam the Field of Giants, making it one of the Barrens' premier hunting grounds for hunters seeking formidable beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="Silithid hives near the road between Camp Taurajo and Dustwallow Marsh threaten travel through the Barrens. Leaders across the region are calling for scouts."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","field of giants","gold road","kodo","korran","ruga ragetotem","silithid","thunder lizard"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:gold-road","quest:1824","npc:korran","npc:ruga-ragetotem","npc:brine","subzone:bael-modan","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Field of Giants"}}
E["subzone:forgotten-pools"] = {t="subzone",n="Forgotten Pools",z="barrens",s="The Forgotten Pools draw wildlife, Kolkar centaur, and the Horde into a contest for water in the northern Barrens. Northwest of the Crossroads, subterranean springs feed an oasis amid the dry savanna.",h="The Forgotten Pools draw wildlife, Kolkar centaur, and the Horde into a contest for water in the northern...",sec={{t="An Oasis in the Wastes",b="Fresh water gathers in the Forgotten Pools, where thick reeds, palm trees, and Laden Mushrooms grow beside the parched Barrens. Plainstriders, snapjaw turtles, and zhevras come to drink. Kolkar centaur keep a camp along the banks and guard the water from travelers, bringing them into conflict with Horde travelers from the Crossroads. Wildlife, Kolkar, and the Horde all contend for the oasis.",sp=0},{t="Ecological Mysteries",b="Deviate Fish thrive in the Forgotten Pools, one of the region’s rare surface waters where they can be found. Their presence hints at deeper ties to the strange transformative energies altering the Barrens’ water table. Horde naturalists and scouts watch the waters and unusual fungi along the banks, wary of what may be seeping into the soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Forgotten Pools located?",a="The Forgotten Pools lie in the northern Barrens, directly northwest of the Crossroads and just north of the road that branches west toward the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"forgotten pools location","where is forgotten pools","find forgotten pools"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Kolkar centaur here?",a="Water sustains life in the arid Barrens, so the Kolkar aggressively claim every oasis they can reach. They sustain their warbands and deny vital resources to traveling Horde caravans and nearby settlements.",al={"centaur at forgotten pools","why are kolkar here","kolkar forgotten pools"},it="why_here"},{q="What makes the fish and plants here unusual?",a="The Forgotten Pools are one of the few places above ground where Deviate Fish thrive, and unusual Laden Mushrooms grow along the banks. These mutations point to subterranean disturbances influencing the Barrens’ underground aquifers.",al={"deviate fish forgotten pools","laden mushrooms","why are fish weird here"},it="power"},{q="Did Thrall pass through this oasis?",a="No record says which oases Thrall’s Horde rested at during its long march across the Barrens, so whether the Forgotten Pools was among them is unknown.",al={"thrall forgotten pools","did orcs camp here","warcraft 3 oasis"},it="history"},{q="What is the Forgotten Pools?",a="The Forgotten Pools is a lush oasis nestled in the Northern Barrens, located just northwest of the Crossroads. Unlike the surrounding arid scrubland, its fresh waters foster dense vegetation, including peculiar laden mushrooms along the shores and strange, mutated deviate fish swimming in its depths.",al={"what is forgotten pools","forgotten pools barrens","about forgotten pools"},it="place",add="670d71f6"},{q="Who lives at the Forgotten Pools?",a="The oasis is claimed by hostile Kolkar centaur, who aggressively guard its vital waters alongside indigenous snapping turtles and beasts.",al={"who controls forgotten pools","who is at forgotten pools","forgotten pools residents"},it="residents",add="a5a5def4"},{q="Is the Forgotten Pools dangerous?",a="Yes, traveling here requires caution. Fierce Kolkar stormers and wranglers fiercely patrol the banks, attacking anyone who draws near their water supply. In addition to the centaur, vicious predatory wildlife prowls the perimeter and mutated creatures dwell within the oasis waters.",al={"is forgotten pools dangerous","forgotten pools threats","danger forgotten pools"},it="danger",add="62a6fb30"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Holding the Forgotten Pools helps secure the trade routes out of the Crossroads and keep the Kolkar from choking the Horde’s western supply lines.",["class:Druid"]="The rapid growth of mutated vegetation and Deviate Fish around the Forgotten Pools gives Cenarion researchers evidence as they investigate unnatural shifts across the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","centaur","crossroads","deviate fish","forgotten pools","kolkar","laden mushrooms","oasis"},rel={"quest:870","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:centaur","npc:thrall","subzone:forgotten-pool"},src={"Forgotten Pools"}}
E["subzone:fray-island"] = {t="subzone",n="Fray Island",z="barrens",s="Warriors gather on Fray Island, just off the Merchant Coast of the Barrens. The rocky islet holds a rough training ring where fighters from across Azeroth test their skill.",h="Warriors gather on Fray Island, just off the Merchant Coast of the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Proving Ground for Brawlers",b="Fray Island lies off the eastern bluffs of the Barrens, beyond the watchful eyes of Orgrimmar and Theramore. Warriors of every race and creed train here. At the island's heart, Klannoc Macleod oversees a fighting arena where seasoned fighters and raw recruits meet in brutal brawls.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of the Affray",b="The ring on Fray Island follows a simple code of martial combat, despite the hostile waters around it. Warriors come at their trainers' direction to face The Affray, a grueling gauntlet against waves of challengers that ends with a bout against champion Big Will. Here, Horde and Alliance allegiance gives way to strength and martial discipline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Fray Island used for?",a="Fray Island is a training ground for warriors and the site of The Affray, a brutal combat trial. Warriors from both factions come to test their endurance and master advanced stances.",al={"why go to fray island","fray island purpose","what is on fray island"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls Fray Island?",a="No kingdom or faction rules Fray Island. Warriors of every race and creed train there, and Klannoc Macleod oversees the combat ring.",al={"who runs fray island","who lives on fray island","fray island faction"},it="in_charge"},{q="How do I reach Fray Island?",a="Fray Island lies in the Great Sea, off the Barrens' eastern coast and south of Ratchet. Reaching it means swimming a long way from shore through waters filled with sharks and frenzy.",al={"getting to fray island","where is fray island","how to get to fray island"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What is The Affray?",a="The Affray is an endurance trial held in Fray Island's fighting cage. A warrior stands atop the grate and defeats successive waves of challengers before facing brawler Big Will.",al={"the affray","fray island arena","big will fight"}},{q="What is Fray Island?",a="Fray Island is a small, arid isle situated off the eastern coast of the Barrens, south of Ratchet. It serves as an isolated proving ground and fighting ring for warriors of all races and creeds seeking to test their martial mettle.",al={"fray island lore","what is fray island","fray island barrens"},it="place",add="0872188f"},{q="What happened at Fray Island?",a="Fray Island was established as a martial proving ground, led by the trainer Klannoc Macleod. It has long stood outside faction politics, drawing fighters and brawlers from across Azeroth to test their combat skills in the ring.",al={"history of fray island","fray island past","what happened here"},it="history",add="122aa5b5"},{q="Is Fray Island dangerous?",a="Yes, for the unprepared. The fighting ring tests every challenger against waves of fierce brawlers, and reaching the island at all means a long swim through waters full of hostile muck frenzies.",al={"is fray island safe","fray island threats","danger on fray island"},it="danger",add="d609582c"},{q="Why is it called Fray Island?",a="The island earns its name from The Affray, the brutal combat contest and fighting pit maintained on the grounds. Warriors and combatants travel from far and wide to clash in these brawls, giving the entire isle its combative reputation.",al={"fray island name meaning","why fray island","why is it named fray island"},it="name",add="b15eb391"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can test your discipline and strength at Fray Island's training ground. Klannoc Macleod and The Affray test whether you can adopt the Berserker Stance.",["race:Human"]="Klannoc Macleod is human, but the warriors who gather in his ring share a bond of combat across racial lines."},kw={"affray","barrens","berserker stance","big will","fray island","klannoc macleod"},rel={"npc:klannoc-macleod","quest:887","zone:barrens","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Fray Island"}}
E["subzone:gold-road"] = {t="subzone",n="Gold Road",z="barrens",s="Horde caravans and warriors travel the Gold Road through the Barrens. It runs from Mor'shan Rampart on the border of Ashenvale, past the Crossroads, toward the south.",h="Horde caravans and warriors travel the Gold Road through the Barrens.",sec={{t="The Artery of the Barrens",b="The Gold Road is a long dirt highway through the center of the Barrens. Near its northern end, Mor'shan Rampart and Mor'shan Base Camp guard against night elf incursions from Ashenvale. Farther south, an eastern roadway connects directly to Durotar before the Gold Road reaches the Crossroads. Beyond the settlement, it passes the waters of local oases and the foothills near the Wailing Caverns. The northern span ends at a dried-up riverbed, where travelers enter the more dangerous southern Barrens.",sp=0},{t="A Vital and Dangerous Path",b="The Gold Road carries Horde trade and military movements between Kalimdor's central territories, but danger follows its length. Quilboar tribes, centaur warbands, plainstriders, and lions threaten supply caravans and lone messengers. The Horde spends considerable resources placing scouts and warriors along the road. Even so, travelers leave the safety of major outposts armed and alert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Gold Road begin and end?",a="The Gold Road begins at Mor'shan Rampart on the border of Ashenvale. Its northern section runs south through the Crossroads to a dried-up riverbed dividing the northern and southern Barrens. From there, the Southern Gold Road continues past Camp Taurajo toward the Great Lift.",al={"gold road route","where does the gold road go","gold road length"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Gold Road so important to the Horde?",a="The Gold Road connects the Horde's major territories in central Kalimdor. It links supply lines from Durotar and the port of Ratchet to the tauren homelands in Mulgore and the northern military front against the Night Elves in Ashenvale.",al={"why is gold road important","importance of gold road"},it="purpose"},{q="What threats wander near the road?",a="Razormane and Bristleback quilboar raiding parties, Kolkar centaur, and wild beasts such as savanna prowlers and thunder lizards roam near the road. Outside the Crossroads' perimeter, the road is far from secure.",al={"is gold road safe","enemies on gold road","gold road dangers"},it="threat"},{q="How does the Gold Road connect to Durotar?",a="North of the Crossroads, an eastward fork branches from the Gold Road and crosses the Southfury River by a wooden bridge into Durotar.",al={"road to durotar","turn off to durotar"}},{q="Is the Gold Road dangerous to travel?",a="While it serves as the primary thoroughfare through the Barrens, stepping even slightly off the path invites peril. The northern stretches brush against fierce quilboar dens, aggressive plains beasts, and wandering centaur marauders. Further south, the road cuts through contested territory rife with hostile razormane tribes, silithid hives, and aggressive wildlife lurking near the oases. Sticking closely to the road and traveling in numbers offers your best chance of survival.",al={"is gold road dangerous","gold road danger","gold road safe"},it="danger",add="5bf25b24"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Gold Road is the backbone of Horde logistics in Kalimdor, tying Durotar's orcish capital to the tauren lands in Mulgore and the northern forward camps near Ashenvale.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can follow plains beasts along the savanna road and track or tame early companions such as lions and raptors."},kw={"caravan","crossroads","gold road","highway","mor'shan","the barrens"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","subzone:southern-gold-road","subzone:mor-shan-rampart","zone:durotar","subzone:ratchet"},src={"Gold Road"}}
E["subzone:grol-dom-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Grol'dom Farm",z="barrens",s="Along the road from Durotar to the Crossroads, Grol'dom Farm raises swine in the northern Barrens. Kranal Fiss and his family work the homestead, despite constant harassment from aggressive local quilboars.",h="Along the road from Durotar to the Crossroads, Grol'dom Farm raises swine in the northern Barrens.",sec={{t="A Swine Farm in the Savannah",b="Established after Durotar was settled, Grol'dom Farm is an early Horde effort to farm the dry Barrens. Kranal Fiss and his children tend the homestead and raise pigs, while Razormane quilboar raiders prowl the nearby ridges. The farm supplies sustenance to the emerging orcish nation, though life here remains lonely and rugged.",sp=0},{t="A Beacon for Young Shaman",b="Grol'dom Farm is a pig farm, but its purpose reaches beyond that daily work. Kranal Fiss knows the elemental rites and plays a key part in guiding young shaman through their trials. Horde initiates on the spiritual path hold the farm in quiet regard, and seekers traveling west from Orgrimmar are regularly directed here to learn how to commune with the primal spirits of fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Grol'dom Farm?",a="Grol'dom Farm is an orcish swine farm in the northern Barrens, along the road between Durotar and the Crossroads. Established after Orgrimmar was founded, it is a remote homestead worked by Kranal Fiss and his children.",al={"groldom farm info","what is this place barrens","orc pig farm"},it="place"},{q="Who lives at Grol'dom Farm?",a="Kranal Fiss and his children live at the farm. They tend the pens, herd the pigs, and defend their meager livelihood against roving beasts and quilboar raiders.",al={"who is at groldom farm","who lives here","kranal fiss home"},it="residents"},{q="Why do shamans come to Grol'dom Farm?",a="Kranal Fiss knows the elemental rites, and orc and tauren shaman are routinely sent to speak with him during their early training. He guides them through trials needed to earn their Call of Fire and manifest the Fire Totem.",al={"shaman fire quest","why come to groldom","kranal fiss shaman"},it="purpose"},{q="What threats face the farm?",a="Razormane quilboars from the surrounding savannah constantly harass the farm. Their raids threaten the livestock and endanger Kranal's family.",al={"why are there quillboars","who attacks groldom","farm enemies"},it="danger"},{q="What is the history of Grol'dom Farm?",a="Grol'dom Farm is one of several orcish pig farms established in the northern Barrens following the founding of Orgrimmar and Durotar. Seeking to carve out an honest livelihood in the arid plains, Kranal Fiss settled here with his children to raise swine and live quietly under the protection of the new Horde.",al={"groldom farm history","how was groldom farm founded","what happened at groldom farm"},it="history",add="571c8690"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman initiate walking the elemental path, you come to Grol'dom Farm to face the dangerous rites Kranal Fiss guides you through, rites needed to commune with the spirits of fire.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see in Grol'dom Farm the grit early settlers need to make a sustainable life in the harsh, untamed Barrens."},kw={"barrens","fire totem","grol'dom farm","groldom","kranal fiss","pig farm","razormane","swine"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Grol'dom Farm"}}
E["subzone:lushwater-oasis"] = {t="subzone",n="Lushwater Oasis",z="barrens",s="South of the Crossroads, Lushwater Oasis is one of three life-giving watering holes in the Barrens. Kolkar centaur threaten travelers who come for its water, while the tainted pools draw anglers seeking Deviate Fish.",h="South of the Crossroads, Lushwater Oasis is one of three life-giving watering holes in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Precarious Sanctuary",b="Lushwater Oasis lies a short march south of the Crossroads, beneath the Barrens sun. Its palms and springs draw thirsty beasts, but Kolkar centaur hold the banks and ambush wildlife and travelers. The oasis also marks the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. Energies from its underground passages taint the pools, where unnatural creatures and strange mutations take hold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to the Wailing Caverns located?",a="The entrance to the Wailing Caverns lies in the natural rock faces overlooking the eastern side of Lushwater Oasis.",al={"where is wc","wc cave entrance","wailing caverns entrance"},gp=true},{q="Who controls Lushwater Oasis?",a="Kolkar centaur dominate Lushwater Oasis. They use its cover to hunt wildlife and attack travelers coming from the Crossroads.",al={"who lives at lushwater oasis","lushwater enemies","centaur at the oasis"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are the fish here strange?",a="Energies from the Wailing Caverns taint the oasis waters, mutating local fish into unusual Deviate Fish.",al={"deviate fish location","why deviate fish","mutated fish oasis"}},{q="Did Thrall's Horde travel through here?",a="During the orcs' Long March through the Barrens with the tauren, Thrall led his troops through the scattered oases for drinking water while they fought off centaur ambushes.",al={"thrall long march oasis","orcs in barrens oasis"},it="history"},{q="What is Lushwater Oasis?",a="Lushwater Oasis is one of three major oases found within the dry plains of the Barrens, lying just south of the Crossroads. Fed by deep subterranean springs, it provides crucial water and vegetation amidst an otherwise arid savanna. It is also renowned and feared for sheltering the entrance to the enigmatic subterranean labyrinth known as the Wailing Caverns.",al={"what is lushwater oasis","lushwater oasis lore","about lushwater oasis"},it="place",add="cb9dfd73"},{q="Is Lushwater Oasis dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers should tread carefully around the waters. Savage Kolkar centaur stalk between the palm trees to hunt wild beasts that gather to drink, attacking any outsiders on sight. Furthermore, the proximity to the corrupted Wailing Caverns exerts an unnatural influence on the area, spawning aggressive creatures and mutate beasts around its shores.",al={"lushwater oasis dangers","is lushwater oasis safe","what threats are at lushwater oasis"},it="danger",add="fd829a06"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Anglers can catch Deviate Fish in these pools. The fish are a vital ingredient in Savory Deviate Delights, prized across Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see troubling overgrowth at Lushwater Oasis, driven by twisted energies escaping the nearby Wailing Caverns."},kw={"crossroads","deviate fish","kolkar","lushwater oasis","the barrens","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","subzone:crossroads","topic:centaur","zone:barrens","npc:thrall"},src={"Lushwater Oasis"}}
E["subzone:merchant-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Merchant Coast",z="barrens",s="Trade and piracy shape the Merchant Coast along the Barrens' eastern shore. Ratchet handles sea trade, while pirates contest the coast.",h="Trade and piracy shape the Merchant Coast along the Barrens' eastern shore.",sec={{t="A Gateway for Commerce and Conflict",b="The Merchant Coast runs along the Barrens' eastern edge, where ships link central Kalimdor with the Eastern Kingdoms and Theramore. The Steamwheedle Cartel's neutral port of Ratchet takes cargo from anyone with coin. Southsea Freebooters also haunt the sands and nearby waters, preying on merchant ships and setting up illicit operations along the beaches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Merchant Coast?",a="The coast takes its name from the profitable trade passing through Ratchet. Steamwheedle merchants carry cargo across the Great Sea to ports throughout Azeroth.",al={"merchant coast name origin","why called merchant coast"},it="name"},{q="What major settlements are on the Merchant Coast?",a="Ratchet, a neutral goblin port run by Gazlowe, is the coast's main settlement. Farther south, Northwatch Hold is an Alliance stronghold, and Fray Island lies just offshore.",al={"towns on merchant coast","what is on merchant coast"},it="place"},{q="Who controls the beaches around here?",a="Ratchet controls its harbor, while Southsea Freebooters camp along nearby beaches. The pirates disrupt trade, rob goblin convoys, and challenge Ratchet's authority.",al={"pirates on merchant coast","who is attacking merchant coast"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Merchant Coast?",a="The Merchant Coast is the stretch of eastern shoreline where the arid Barrens meets the waters of the Great Sea. Dominated by the bustling goblin port of Ratchet to the north and the towering ramparts of Northwatch Hold to the south, this coastline serves as a vital maritime trade corridor connecting central Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"what is merchant coast","merchant coast overview","barrens coast"},it="place",add="bb3cbd28"},{q="Is the Merchant Coast dangerous?",a="While the harbor of Ratchet maintains a guarded neutrality, the surrounding shoreline is fraught with peril. South of the goblin docks, the beaches are heavily infested with Southsea Freebooters—ruthless pirates who raid passing vessels and salvage sunken wrecks. Venturing further south brings you into the shadow of Northwatch Hold, where vigilant Theramore soldiers fiercely defend their garrison.",al={"merchant coast dangers","is it safe here","merchant coast threats"},it="danger",add="c3eb7a38"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the Merchant Coast is the Barrens' chief commercial link to the sea. Securing Ratchet and suppressing local pirates matters to regional supply lines.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance keeps a naval presence at nearby Northwatch Hold. Its forces watch the goblin trade through Ratchet and the unruly Southsea pirates along the shore."},kw={"barrens","great sea","merchant coast","ratchet","southsea freebooters","steamwheedle cartel"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","subzone:fray-island","quest:887","topic:goblin","topic:pirate","subzone:longshore"},src={"Merchant Coast"}}
E["subzone:raptor-grounds"] = {t="subzone",n="Raptor Grounds",z="barrens",s="In the southern Barrens, Sunscale raptors claim a secluded valley in the rocky hills west of Northwatch Hold. Their eerie, tool-using cunning and obsessive theft of bright trinkets set them apart from ordinary beasts.",h="In the southern Barrens, Sunscale raptors claim a secluded valley in the rocky hills west of Northwatch Hold.",sec={{t="Uncanny Beasts of the Southern Wastes",b="West of Northwatch Hold, Sunscale raptors make their home in the Raptor Grounds. Eerie and far from ordinary beasts, they fashion crude shelters, make primitive tools, and coordinate their hunts. Their obsessive fascination with shiny or unusual things drives them to raid passing caravans and Horde encampments. Coins, trinkets, and supplies disappear into their canyon dens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Raptor Grounds?",a="The Raptor Grounds is a small, sunken valley in the southern Barrens, in the rocky hills west of Northwatch Hold.",al={"raptor grounds location","where are the raptor grounds","raptor grounds map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the raptors here different from normal beasts?",a="Sunscale raptors show an unnatural degree of intelligence. They assemble primitive tools and build crude huts to shelter their pack and hide stolen goods.",al={"sunscale raptor intelligence","why do raptors have huts","smart raptors barrens"}},{q="Why do the raptors attack caravans and steal items?",a="The pack has an obsessive attraction to shiny, glittering, or unusual objects. That fascination drives the raptors to ambush travelers and raid Horde settlements, hoarding stolen coin and metal deep in their valley.",al={"stolen silver raptors","why do raptors steal","raptor shiny things"},it="motive"},{q="Who controls this valley?",a="Neither faction holds the valley. It remains the untamed hunting and nesting ground of the wild Sunscale raptors, who fiercely defend it against intruders.",al={"who owns raptor grounds","is raptor grounds horde"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Raptor Grounds?",a="The Raptor Grounds is a secluded, tucked-away valley nestled in the southern reaches of the Barrens, lying just west of the Alliance stronghold Northwatch Hold. Unlike typical stretches of the savannah, this valley is entirely overrun by Sunscale raptors that have claimed the rocky hollow as their personal breeding ground and territory.",al={"what is raptor grounds","raptor grounds info","about raptor grounds"},it="place",add="5f1076b0"},{q="Is the Raptor Grounds dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally perilous for unwary travelers. The valley is densely packed with Sunscale raptors displaying unnerving coordination and cunning. Rather than behaving like simple predators, they craft crude huts and tools, ambushing passing trade convoys and aggressively defending their nesting territory against any trespassers.",al={"is raptor grounds dangerous","raptor grounds danger","how dangerous is raptor grounds"},it="danger",add="7bb1fdc9"},{q="Why is it called the Raptor Grounds?",a="The valley takes its name directly from the overwhelming concentration of Sunscale raptors dwelling within it. Because the beasts have thoroughly taken over the enclosed hollow, raising their young and establishing crude communal camps there, locals simply know it as their grounds.",al={"why called raptor grounds","raptor grounds name meaning","raptor grounds name origin"},it="name",add="fd15f683"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Sunscale raptors threaten Horde caravans and outposts across the southern Barrens, prompting bounties and expeditions to recover stolen wealth.",["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, you may find the Sunscale pack’s unusual cunning, coordinated hunts, and rudimentary shelters fascinating to study as a tracker."},kw={"northwatch hold","raptor grounds","raptors","stolen silver","sunscale raptor","the barrens"},rel={"quest:3281","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Raptor Grounds"}}
E["subzone:ratchet"] = {t="subzone",n="Ratchet",z="barrens",s="Ships crowd Ratchet's docks on the eastern coast of the Barrens. The Steamwheedle Cartel runs this neutral port, linking central Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms by sea.",h="Ships crowd Ratchet's docks on the eastern coast of the Barrens.",sec={{t="The Crossroads of the Great Sea",b="Ratchet gives shelter to anyone who can pay, on the dry coast between Durotar and Dustwallow Marsh. After the Third War, chief engineer Gazlowe founded the port, drawing smugglers, exiles, and daring traders to Kalimdor's frontier. The Steamwheedle Cartel runs the town, which keeps strict neutrality between the Horde and the Alliance. Ships such as The Maiden's Fancy cross the Great Sea to Booty Bay with goods, mercenaries, and raw materials. Ratchet Bruisers watch the docks and beat anyone who starts a fight and disrupts trade.",sp=0},{t="Shadows Above the Docks",b="Ratchet's docks, taverns, and workshops serve a town with dealings beyond trade. A secluded tower overlooks the harbor from the hills, where warlocks including Strahad Farsan and Menara Voidrender gather. While townsfolk and sailors tend to cargo and goblin engineering, the warlocks commune with demonic forces without interference. The Steamwheedle Cartel does not enforce the moral restrictions found in traditional faction capitals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Ratchet?",a="Chief Engineer Gazlowe runs Ratchet for the neutral Steamwheedle Cartel. He founded the town after Warchief Thrall paid him well to direct the construction of Orgrimmar's infrastructure.",al={"ratchet leader","who is in charge of ratchet","gazlowe ratchet"},it="residents"},{q="Can Alliance players visit Ratchet safely?",a="Yes. Ratchet is a neutral goblin port where Alliance and Horde travelers can use the inn, bank, vendors, flight paths, and ferry, as long as they remain on good terms with the Steamwheedle Cartel and attack no one in town.",al={"is ratchet safe for alliance","alliance in ratchet","can alliance go to ratchet"},gp=true},{q="Where does the boat in Ratchet go?",a="The Maiden's Fancy, docked at the southern pier, sails across the Great Sea to Booty Bay at the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale. It is a major sea link between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"ratchet boat destination","where does the ratchet ship go","boat to eastern kingdoms"},gp=true},{q="Why are there warlocks in the hills above the town?",a="Warlocks gather in the tower overlooking Ratchet under figures such as Strahad Farsan and Menara Voidrender. The Steamwheedle Cartel's indifference to dark magic lets them teach apprentices and bind demons without interference from religious or civil authorities.",al={"ratchet warlocks","strahad farsan tower","warlock tower ratchet"}},{q="What happens if I start a fight in Ratchet?",a="Ratchet Bruisers attack anyone who starts a fight, using heavy clubs and nets. Fighting disrupts business and quickly damages your standing with the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"ratchet guards","attacking players in ratchet","ratchet bruisers"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is Ratchet?",a="Ratchet is a bustling goblin port nestled on the eastern coast of the Barrens, positioned midway between Orgrimmar and Theramore Isle. Run by the Steamwheedle Cartel, it serves as Kalimdor's premier neutral harbor, connecting commerce and travelers across the Great Sea directly to Booty Bay.",al={"what is this place","ratchet overview","about ratchet"},it="place",add="45ea181b"},{q="What happened at Ratchet?",a="Ratchet was founded by Gazlowe shortly after the Third War, financed by the handsome payment he earned overseeing the construction of Orgrimmar. Run by the Steamwheedle Cartel, it has grown into Kalimdor's busiest neutral port, open to Horde and Alliance traders alike.",al={"ratchet history","how was ratchet founded","who built ratchet"},it="history",add="0458c752"},{q="Is Ratchet dangerous?",a="Within town limits, peace is ruthlessly enforced by Gazlowe's heavy-handed goblin bruisers, making violence ill-advised for anyone wishing to keep their teeth. However, the surrounding territory teems with hostile quilboar, roving pirates along the coast, and a shadowy coven of warlocks practicing dark arts in the hills just above.",al={"is it safe here","danger in ratchet","threats in ratchet"},it="danger",add="42d2f24d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can train in the tower on the bluffs above Ratchet, where warlocks of many origins gather under Strahad Farsan and Menara Voidrender to master advanced demonic summoning.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can find a safe landing point in the hostile central Barrens at Ratchet, with boat transport and flight connections."},kw={"barrens","booty bay","gazlowe","maiden's fancy","ratchet","steamwheedle cartel","strahad farsan"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:booty-bay","topic:steamwheedle-cartel","npc:strahad-farsan","npc:menara-voidrender","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:crossroads"},src={"Ratchet"}}
E["subzone:razorfen-downs-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Razorfen Downs (Classic)",z="barrens",s="Deep in the southern Barrens, the Scourge now holds Razorfen Downs, the quilboar's ancestral burial ground and capital. Led by the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer, its agents have raised the quilboar dead and threaten to spread their power across central Kalimdor.",h="Deep in the southern Barrens, the Scourge now holds Razorfen Downs, the quilboar's ancestral burial ground...",sec={{t="Capital of Thorns",b="Razorfen Downs shares the towering, petrified vines of nearby Razorfen Kraul. It lies where the boar demigod Agamaggan fell in the War of the Ancients. For generations, this thorn labyrinth was the quilboar's sacred burial ground and seat of power, guarded by mystics of the Death's Head tribe. The quilboar hold its dense briars holy, for they were soaked in their divine progenitor's blood.",sp=0},{t="A Scourge Bastion in Kalimdor",b="The Scourge has broken the sanctity of Razorfen Downs. Amnennar the Coldbringer, a powerful lich who serves the Lich King, subdued the Death's Head quilboar and made their ancestral resting ground an undead stronghold. Reanimated quilboar skeletons and corpses, along with shrieking banshees, prowl the Spiral of Thorns. The Horde in the nearby Barrens and emissaries from Stormwind's Cathedral of Light both see this Scourge power as a grave threat to Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Downs is the quilboar's ancestral capital and burial ground, cut through massive briars in the southern Barrens. The Scourge now controls it.",al={"what is rfd","razorfen downs lore","downs background"},it="place"},{q="Why are there undead inside a quilboar city?",a="Amnennar the Coldbringer, a Scourge lich, invaded Razorfen Downs, subdued the local Death's Head tribe, and raised dead quilboar to build an undead stronghold on Kalimdor.",al={"why scourge in downs","why undead in barrens","who brought the scourge here"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the difference between Razorfen Downs and Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs share Agamaggan's brambles. Charlga Razorflank leads the living quilboar stronghold at Kraul, while the Scourge now holds the Downs, their ancestral burial ground.",al={"downs vs kraul","rfk vs rfd","difference between downs and kraul"}},{q="Who rules Razorfen Downs right now?",a="Amnennar the Coldbringer, a Scourge lich, commands Razorfen Downs from deep within the Spiral of Thorns.",al={"rfd final boss","who leads razorfen downs","boss of downs"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happened to Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Downs long served as the capital city and sacred burial grounds of the quilboar, tended by the priests of the Death's Head tribe. Recently, agents of the Scourge arrived in Kalimdor under the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer. Amnennar infiltrated the thorny stronghold, corrupted the quilboar priesthood, and raised their honored dead into a shambling army. The sacred tombs have now been twisted into a fortified necropolis, forcing surviving quilboar into a desperate struggle to reclaim their ancestral home before the undead plague spreads across the Barrens.",al={"what happened at razorfen downs","razorfen downs history","story of razorfen downs"},it="history",add="537e8490"},{q="How dangerous is Razorfen Downs?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. Unlike the feral quilboar found elsewhere in the Barrens, Razorfen Downs is held by the undead Scourge. You will face not only fanatic Death's Head necromancers and geomancers, but also legions of reanimated quilboar corpses, banshees, and skeletal summoners. Deep within, the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer commands the dark magic infesting the brambles, threatening to use the stronghold as a staging ground to overwhelm central Kalimdor with undeath.",al={"is razorfen downs dangerous","danger in razorfen downs","threat of razorfen downs"},it="danger",add="4edae968"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="A Scourge stronghold on the Barrens' southern border threatens the Horde's heartland and supply routes.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you may draw the Royal Apothecary Society's and Undercity's Forsaken leadership's interest in investigating and purging the rival necromantic magic growing within the Downs."},kw={"agamaggan","amnennar","barrens","death's head","quilboar","razorfen downs","rfd","scourge"},rel={"zone:barrens","zone:razorfenkraul","topic:scourge","topic:quilboar","topic:agamaggan","zone:undercity","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:horde"},src={"Razorfen Downs (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:razorfen-kraul-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Razorfen Kraul (Classic)",z="barrens",s="Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heartland of the quilboar, carved deep into the colossal thorns that sprang from the blood of the fallen boar demigod Agamaggan. Ruled by the ruthless crone Charlga Razorflank, this fortified labyrinth serves as a staging ground for bloody raids across the southern Barrens.",h="Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heartland of the quilboar, carved deep into the colossal thorns that sprang...",sec={{t="Blood of the Boar God",b="Ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, the colossal boar demigod Agamaggan perished battling the Burning Legion to save Azeroth. Wherever his sacred blood seeped into the soil of southern Kalimdor, massive, impenetrable thorn vines erupted from the earth. The quilboar, believing themselves the mortal progeny of the Great Boar, gathered within these dense briars to dwell and venerate his sacrifice. The dense mass known as Razorfen Kraul stands as their most revered redoubt, thick with quilboar warriors, beast trainers, and earth-shaping shamans.",sp=0},{t="The Crone's Ambition",b="Control over the Kraul has fallen to the aging geomancer Charlga Razorflank. Under her iron rule, the Razorfen tribe has waged merciless war against rival quilboar bands and nearby Horde encampments alike. Far more chilling than mere territorial raiding, however, are reports from watchful scouts noting undead figures lurking around the thorny briars. Whispers suggest that Charlga has begun bargaining with agents of the Scourge, endangering not only the Barrens but threatening to open a grim foothold for undeath on Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What created the giant thorns around Razorfen Kraul?",a="According to legend, the colossal thorn vines sprouted wherever the blood of the boar demigod Agamaggan struck the ground during the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago.",al={"why are there thorns here","giant thorn vines barrens","agamaggan thorns lore"},it="origin"},{q="Who rules Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul is commanded by Charlga Razorflank, a ruthless quilboar crone and geomancer who directs raids against neighboring tribes and settlements.",al={"razorfen kraul leader","who leads the kraul","charlga razorflank"},it="leader"},{q="Why are there undead near the Kraul?",a="Charlga Razorflank has reportedly entered secret negotiations with agents of the Scourge, seeking an unholy alliance that could bring the power of undeath into the quilboar folds.",al={"scourge in razorfen","undead quilboar","why scourge barrens"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Where is Razorfen Kraul located?",a="Razorfen Kraul is situated in the southernmost reaches of the Barrens, nestled on the western side of the colossal thorn thickets just north of the Great Lift.",al={"where is rfk","rfk entrance","razorfen kraul location"},gp=true},{q="What is Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heartland and heavily fortified stronghold of the quilboar, nestled deep inside the colossal brambles of the southern Barrens. Believed to be the mortal offspring of the fallen boar demigod Agamaggan, the quilboar revere the dense briars as holy ground and their rightful domain.",al={"what is razorfen kraul","razorfen kraul lore","about razorfen kraul"},it="place",add="6f44c4ee"},{q="What happened at Razorfen Kraul?",a="Ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, the boar demigod Agamaggan fell fighting the Burning Legion. His spilled blood caused massive, thorn-ridden briars to erupt across the land. The quilboar claimed the central bramble as their ancestral home, but the crone Charlga Razorflank recently seized dominion over the Kraul, turning its defenders against both rival tribes and neighboring settlements.",al={"history of razorfen kraul","razorfen kraul history","what happened in the kraul"},it="history",add="8546d87b"},{q="Is Razorfen Kraul dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the fierce quilboar warriors, tamed beasts, and geomancers that fiercely defend their sacred briars, the Kraul has grown aggressively hostile under Charlga Razorflank's command. More troubling still are whispers of Scourge agents walking within, raising fears of an unholy presence taking root in Kalimdor.",al={"is razorfen kraul safe","razorfen kraul danger","threat of razorfen kraul"},it="danger",add="2a3e9319"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Charlga Razorflank's aggressive raids directly threaten southern settlements and trade routes, making pacifying the Kraul an urgent security priority for the Horde.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren hunters and shamans hold deep historical enmity with the quilboar, and the rumors of unholy Scourge corruption taking root in the revered earth of Agamaggan demand their swift intervention."},kw={"agamaggan","agathelos","barrens","charlga razorflank","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen kraul","rfk","scourge"},rel={"topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","npc:charlga-razorflank","npc:overlord-ramtusk","npc:agathelos-the-raging","zone:barrens","topic:scourge","quest:1101"},src={"Razorfen Kraul (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:shrine-of-the-fallen-warrior"] = {t="subzone",n="Shrine of the Fallen Warrior",z="barrens",s="Perched upon a secluded ridge west of the Crossroads lies the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior, a quiet memorial overlooking the sweeping red savannahs of the Barrens. Marked by a stone plinth bearing the initials 'MK' and the body of a fallen orc warrior, it is watched over by the gentle presence of a Spirit Healer named Koiter.",h="Perched upon a secluded ridge west of the Crossroads lies the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior, a quiet memorial...",sec={{t="A Silent Vigil",b="Tucked away high upon the hills northwest of the Crossroads, the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior stands as an unusually solemn haven amidst the dust and peril of the Barrens. To find it, travelers must scale a winding ridge pathway southwest of the summit until they reach a gentle mound. Upon the summit rests a carved stone monument, its plinth carved with the initials 'MK'. Before it lies the armored form of an orc warrior at rest, watched over day and night by a named Spirit Healer known as Koiter. There are no battle horns here, only quiet contemplation honoring a champion who walked Kalimdor's lands.",sp=0},{t="The Meaning of the Memorial",b="Within the world, the shrine stands as an enduring tribute to a departed champion of the Horde whose soul lingers in the care of the spirits. Outside the realm, the monument serves as a heartfelt tribute created by the game's artists to honor Michel Koiter, a beloved illustrator who passed away during the development of the world. The resting warrior is modeled precisely after Koiter's own beta character, Twincruiser, immortalizing his presence forever beneath Kalimdor's open skies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior located?",a="The shrine sits atop a hill west of the Crossroads in the northern Barrens. Travelers can reach it by locating the base of a ridge southwest of the elevation and following a winding path up to the grassy knoll.",al={"shrine location","where is the shrine","how to get to shrine of fallen warrior"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is the orc lying upon the plinth?",a="In-game, he represents a revered fallen warrior. In reality, he is modeled directly after Twincruiser, the orc warrior character played by late Blizzard artist Michel Koiter during early development.",al={"who is the dead orc","fallen warrior identity","twincruiser"},it="identity"},{q="What does the 'MK' carved into the stone mean?",a="The runic initials 'MK' honor Michel Koiter, a senior artist who passed away in 2004 during the development of the world.",al={"mk initials","what does mk stand for","letters on the stone"},it="name"},{q="Who is the Spirit Healer standing beside the shrine?",a="The Spirit Healer is named Koiter. Unlike ordinary Spirit Healers that only appear to spirits walking in death, Koiter stands in vigil and can be seen clearly by living wanderers who make the trek up the hill.",al={"spirit healer koiter","angel at the shrine","who is the ghost"},it="identity"},{q="Are there any quests associated with this shrine?",a="No. The Shrine of the Fallen Warrior is not part of any questline or faction conflict. It exists purely as a solemn place of reflection, remembrance, and tribute.",al={"shrine quest","quest for fallen warrior","is there a quest here"},gp=true},{q="What is the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior?",a="The Shrine of the Fallen Warrior is a peaceful, solemn monument perched high atop a hill west of the Crossroads. It features an ornate stone plinth bearing the resting form of an honored orcish warrior, overseen by an obelisk and a spectral guardian. Travelers from all corners of Azeroth journey here to pay quiet respects away from the conflicts consuming the Barrens.",al={"what is shrine of the fallen warrior","shrine fallen warrior barrens","monument on hill barrens"},it="place",add="7e92bc4e"},{q="Is the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior dangerous?",a="No. The shrine itself is a sacred sanctuary untouched by hostile creatures or warring factions. While the Barrens below teem with prowling beasts, quilboars, and rival soldiers, the hilltop monument remains completely peaceful and safe for any traveler who makes the climb.",al={"is shrine of the fallen warrior safe","shrine dangerous","enemies at the shrine"},it="danger",add="a34bf1b4"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Warriors of all races often make a quiet pilgrimage to this hill, paying respects to a fallen brother-in-arms who fought bravely before passing into legend.",["faction:Horde"]="Set right in the heartland of Horde territory, this solitary resting place captures the honor, duty, and sacrifice at the core of the shamanic and warrior traditions of Kalimdor."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","koiter","memorial","michel koiter","shrine of the fallen warrior","twincruiser"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens"},src={"Shrine of the Fallen Warrior"}}
E["subzone:sludge-fen"] = {t="subzone",n="Sludge Fen",z="barrens",s="In northeastern the Barrens, Sludge Fen's clear pool has become an oily industrial field run by the Venture Company. Supervisor Lugwizzle oversees the drilling, while rivals in Ratchet seek to sabotage the operation.",h="In northeastern the Barrens, Sludge Fen's clear pool has become an oily industrial field run by the Venture...",sec={{t="Industrial Devastation",b="Sludge Fen once held a clear pool fed by natural springs in the arid Barrens. The Venture Company built oil-drilling platforms and machinery over the basin, turning the wetland into a reservoir of sludge and industrial waste. Supervisor Lugwizzle oversees goblin drillers, engineers, and overseers as they pump crude oil around the clock. Runoff and toxic byproducts coat the water, choking the native aquatic life beneath the grease.",sp=0},{t="Corporate Rivalry and Espionage",b="Sludge Fen's machinery and shredder designs have drawn industrial thieves. In nearby Ratchet, Tinkers' Union engineer Sputtervalve faced pressure to match the Venture Company's logging and excavation technology. Instead of making his own designs, Sputtervalve sent Wizzlecrank to seize a Venture Company shredder from the fen. Wizzlecrank took the machine without its ignition key, leaving it stranded. Mercenaries are often drawn into the mire to pry the keys from Lugwizzle and escort the shredder through furious Venture Co. employees.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Sludge Fen like before the Venture Company arrived?",a="Before the Venture Company arrived, Sludge Fen was a crystal-clear pool fed by natural springs. The company's oil rig and refining operation covered the basin in crude oil and chemical refuse.",al={"sludge fen past","was sludge fen always polluted","sludge fen history"},it="history"},{q="Who runs the operation at Sludge Fen?",a="Supervisor Lugwizzle runs the oil field for the Venture Company. He oversees the drillers, engineers, and overseers, with lieutenants including Overseer Glibby and Foreman Grills.",al={"sludge fen boss","who leads sludge fen","supervisor lugwizzle"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is there a hijacked shredder parked in the middle of the fen?",a="Sputtervalve sent Wizzlecrank from Ratchet to steal the Venture Company's shredder design. Wizzlecrank entered the cockpit without the ignition key and became stranded among hostile Venture Co. workers.",al={"wizzlecrank shredder","goblin in shredder sludge fen","why is shredder stuck"}},{q="Why do druids dive into these polluted waters?",a="Horde druids on the Trial of the Sea Lion dive to the bottom of the contaminated pool to retrieve the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility from a submerged lockbox. The foul water tests their endurance.",al={"druid quest sludge fen","aquatic agility half pendant","aquatic form trial"}},{q="What is Sludge Fen?",a="Sludge Fen is an oil drilling field run by the Venture Company in northeastern Barrens. Dominated by an industrial drilling platform erected straight out of the muck, the compound serves as a hub of resource extraction and machinery testing, surrounded by toxic runoff, grinding shredders, and company personnel.",al={"what is sludge fen","tell me about sludge fen","sludge fen overview"},it="place",add="35534ec0"},{q="Is Sludge Fen dangerous?",a="Yes. The Venture Company employs aggressive overseers, foremen, and engineers who actively guard their operations with shredders and heavy tools, attacking any trespassers on sight. In addition, the waters themselves are choked with toxic industrial waste and unnatural sludge anomalies created by the pollution.",al={"is sludge fen dangerous","sludge fen dangers","sludge fen threats"},it="danger",add="537e9a89"},{q="Why is it called Sludge Fen?",a="The site earned its name from the sheer volume of toxic runoff and industrial waste dumped by the Venture Company's drilling operations. What was once a pristine natural pool has been thoroughly choked into a filthy, oil-slicked marsh of black sludge.",al={"why is it called sludge fen","sludge fen name meaning","how did sludge fen get its name"},it="name",add="8087f29c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Horde druid, you enter Sludge Fen's oily depths during the Trial of the Sea Lion to retrieve the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Venture Company operates advanced shredders and machinery at Sludge Fen. Blueprints, specialized components, and trade theft orchestrated from Ratchet draw interest to the site."},kw={"oil rig","shredder","sludge fen","sputtervalve","supervisor lugwizzle","the barrens","venture co","wizzlecrank"},rel={"topic:venture-company","npc:sputtervalve","quest:114","quest:858","quest:31","subzone:boulder-lode-mine","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Sludge Fen"}}
E["subzone:southern-gold-road"] = {t="subzone",n="Southern Gold Road",z="barrens",s="Caravans and travelers crowd the Southern Gold Road as it runs through the Barrens toward the Great Lift. Trade links the central plains with distant reaches of Kalimdor.",h="Caravans and travelers crowd the Southern Gold Road as it runs through the Barrens toward the Great Lift.",sec={{t="Artery of the South",b="At the stone bridge between the northern and southern Barrens, the Southern Gold Road turns south toward the Great Lift and Thousand Needles. Like the northern stretch, simply called the Gold Road, it takes its name from the lucrative merchant caravans that travel its length. Quilboar tribes and prowling predators harass those who use it, yet the road remains one of the continent’s busiest long-distance routes. Goods pass along it between remote outposts and ports.",sp=0},{t="A Crossroads of Distant Lands",b="Horde couriers and patrols share the Southern Gold Road with merchants and explorers bound for distant lands. Travelers journey between Gadgetzan in the southern deserts of Tanaris, Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore, and Nighthaven, among the sacred groves of Moonglade. For those crossing Kalimdor’s interior on foot, surviving the journey down this sun-baked road is a grueling rite of passage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Southern Gold Road start and end?",a="The Southern Gold Road begins at the bridge between the northern and southern Barrens and runs south to the Great Lift at the edge of Thousand Needles.",al={"southern gold road path","southern gold road route","where is southern gold road"},it="place"},{q="Why is it called the Gold Road?",a="The road takes its name from the valuable trade caravans that carry precious goods, ore, and coin across Kalimdor.",al={"why called gold road","gold road name origin","gold road meaning"},it="name"},{q="What is the difference between the Gold Road and the Southern Gold Road?",a="The bridge between the two halves of the Barrens divides the routes: north of it is the Gold Road, while the stretch south to the Great Lift is the Southern Gold Road.",al={"gold road vs southern gold road","two gold roads"},it="place"},{q="Who travels along this stretch of road?",a="Horde couriers and patrols use the road, as do merchants and explorers traveling between Gadgetzan to the south and Darkshore and Moonglade to the north.",al={"who uses southern gold road","caravans southern gold road"},it="people"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on the Southern Gold Road to carry supplies between the Barrens’ central crossway and the southern outposts near Thousand Needles."},kw={"barrens","caravans","gold road","great lift","southern gold road","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:gold-road","zone:barrens","subzone:great-lift","subzone:gadgetzan","zone:tanaris","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:nighthaven"},src={"Southern Gold Road"}}
E["subzone:stagnant-oasis"] = {t="subzone",n="Stagnant Oasis",z="barrens",s="Kolkar centaur guard the Stagnant Oasis in the dry heart of the Barrens. Its waters lie between the Gold Road and Merchant Coast, drawing wildlife to its banks.",h="Kolkar centaur guard the Stagnant Oasis in the dry heart of the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Murky Haven in the Drought",b="East of the Gold Road, inland from the Merchant Coast, the Stagnant Oasis breaks up the dusty scrub of the Barrens. Dense foliage grows around the pool, where aggressive snapjaw turtles prowl. Weakened kodos often stray here from the great herds of the Field of Giants. Kolkar centaur keep camps along the banks and fiercely guard the water from anyone entering their territory.",sp=0},{t="Strange Waters",b="Strange life stirs in the pool, though its waters look still. Deviate Fish swim among other unusual creatures. Scholars and shamans watch the Barrens oases closely, studying the strange forces that affect local springheads and the wildlife that drinks from them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stagnant Oasis located?",a="The Stagnant Oasis lies in the central-southern Barrens, east of the Gold Road and west of the cliffs along the Merchant Coast.",al={"stagnant oasis location","where is stagnant oasis","how to find stagnant oasis"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who controls the Stagnant Oasis?",a="Kolkar centaur have camps around the pool. Oasis Snapjaws and solitary, wandering kodos also roam the greenery nearby.",al={"who lives at stagnant oasis","stagnant oasis centaur","enemies at stagnant oasis"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the kodos here easier to hunt?",a="Kodos near the Stagnant Oasis are often solitary, weakened, or lost, unlike the great, coordinated herds farther south in the Field of Giants. That makes them easier prey for hunters and travelers.",al={"lost barrens kodo","kodos stagnant oasis","hunting kodos barrens"}},{q="What kind of fish can be caught in the pool?",a="Anglers can catch Deviate Fish in the murky pool. The fish can be cooked into delicacies prized across Kalimdor.",al={"stagnant oasis fishing","deviate fish stagnant oasis","fishing in stagnant oasis"},gp=true},{q="Did Thrall visit this oasis during the Long March?",a="No record confirms whether Thrall visited the Stagnant Oasis. It may have been one of the three watering holes Thrall and the newly arrived Horde secured while marching across the Barrens with Cairne Bloodhoof.",al={"thrall stagnant oasis","long march oasis","warcraft 3 oasis"},it="history"},{q="What is the Stagnant Oasis?",a="The Stagnant Oasis is one of the lush watering holes dotting the arid expanse of the Barrens, situated between the Gold Road and the Merchant Coast. Filled with freshwater pools, towering palms, and indigenous greenery, it serves as a critical refuge for wildlife amidst the surrounding savanna, though it harbors its own lurking perils.",al={"what is stagnant oasis","stagnant oasis info","about stagnant oasis"},it="place",add="9f5a622c"},{q="Is the Stagnant Oasis dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers must tread carefully. Fierce Kolkar centaur maintain encampments along its perimeter, violently claiming the precious water for themselves. In addition to the hostile raiders, aggressive oasis snapjaws prowl the muddy banks, posing a deadly hazard to unwary wanderers seeking respite from the harsh sun.",al={"is stagnant oasis safe","stagnant oasis danger","threats at stagnant oasis"},it="danger",add="f4d964bf"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The Stagnant Oasis yields rare Deviate Fish, the essential ingredient for Savory Deviate Delights.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde couriers and scouts traveling between Crossroads and Taurajo face a constant threat from the centaur camps at the oasis, which menace supply traffic on the Gold Road."},kw={"barrens","centaur","deviate fish","gold road","kodo","kolkar","snapjaw","stagnant oasis"},rel={"quest:877","zone:barrens","topic:centaur","subzone:gold-road","subzone:merchant-coast","subzone:field-of-giants","npc:thrall"},src={"Stagnant Oasis"}}
E["subzone:thorn-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Thorn Hill",z="barrens",s="Razormane warbands strike Horde supply lines from Thorn Hill, east of the Crossroads. The fortified quilboar camp holds the high ridges between Durotar and the Barrens interior.",h="Razormane warbands strike Horde supply lines from Thorn Hill, east of the Crossroads.",sec={{t="A Thorn in the Horde's Side",b="Thorn Hill overlooks the roads between Durotar and the Crossroads. The Razormane gather here with hunters, trained wolves, and geomancers who shape the earth. Elder Mystic Razorsnout guides the quilboar as their attacks on Horde supply caravans grow bolder. The camp sits close to vital routes, making it one of the Crossroads guards' most immediate threats in the central savanna.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Thorn Hill?",a="Thorn Hill is a Razormane camp on the northern Barrens ridges between the Crossroads and Durotar.",al={"thorn hill location","where is thorn hill","what is this camp"},it="place"},{q="Who leads the quilboar at Thorn Hill?",a="Elder Mystic Razorsnout guides the Razormane warbands at Thorn Hill.",al={"thorn hill boss","who rules thorn hill"},it="leader"},{q="Why is the Horde fighting the quilboar here?",a="Razormane warbands ambush Horde supply caravans traveling from Durotar to the Crossroads, so Horde authorities send warriors to clear the ridges.",al={"why attack thorn hill","horde caravan raids","crossroads quilboar"},it="conflict"},{q="What kinds of enemies live in Thorn Hill?",a="Razormane geomancers, hunters, trained wolves, and berserkers defend the camp.",al={"thorn hill mobs","quilboar types thorn hill"},it="residents"},{q="Is Thorn Hill dangerous?",a="Thorn Hill poses a serious threat to anyone traveling between Durotar and the Crossroads. The mountainside settlement is heavily defended by hostile Razormane geomancers, hunters, and trained wolves, guided by mystics like Elder Mystic Razorsnout. Because these quilboar actively raid passing Horde caravans, unwary travelers face immediate attack when stepping onto their fortified grounds.",al={"is thorn hill dangerous","thorn hill dangers","how dangerous is thorn hill"},it="danger",add="e0126d7b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior, you can help secure the road between the Crossroads and Durotar by confronting the raiders at Thorn Hill."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","quilboar","razormane","razorsnout","thorn hill"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:quilboar","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Thorn Hill"}}
E["subzone:tidus-stair"] = {t="subzone",n="Tidus Stair",z="barrens",s="At Tidus Stair, two tauren shamans seek insight from the coastal water spirits. Broad stone terraces rise above the Merchant Coast southeast of Ratchet, sheltered beside the Great Sea.",h="At Tidus Stair, two tauren shamans seek insight from the coastal water spirits.",sec={{t="Steps to the Sea",b="Waves crash below the weathered stone terraces of Tidus Stair, cut into the coastal bluffs southeast of Ratchet. The Barrens around you are arid and dusty, and skirmishes trouble the region, but this stretch above the Merchant Coast is quiet. A modest hut stands on the terraces, home to the tauren Islen Waterseer and Mahren Skyseer. Far from the goblin trade docks, they spend their days fishing, watching the horizon, and seeking insight from the coastal water spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tidus Stair located?",a="Tidus Stair lies along the eastern coast of the Barrens, directly southeast of the goblin port of Ratchet. It overlooks the waters of the Merchant Coast.",al={"tidus stair location","where is tidus stair","how to get to tidus stair"},it="place"},{q="Who lives at Tidus Stair?",a="Islen Waterseer and Mahren Skyseer, two tauren, live here in a simple seaside hut on the terraces. They spend their time fishing and communing with nature.",al={"who is at tidus stair","tidus stair npcs","who lives here"},it="residents"},{q="Why is Tidus Stair significant to shamans?",a="Horde shamans seeking to master water are guided across Kalimdor to find Islen Waterseer at Tidus Stair. Beside the open ocean, initiates learn to commune with the tides and seek pure waters to bind their water totem.",al={"shaman tidus stair","water totem tidus stair","why do shamans come here"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Tidus Stair aligned with the Horde or neutral?",a="The tauren who live at Tidus Stair are loyal to the Horde and guide Horde shamans. The remote terraces lie outside formal military borders.",al={"is tidus stair horde","tidus stair faction"},it="side"},{q="What is Tidus Stair?",a="Tidus Stair is a striking natural geological formation along the Merchant Coast, southeast of Ratchet. Several broad rock terraces descend down toward the Great Sea like a massive set of stone stairs. Perched peacefully upon these terraces sits a humble seaside shelter overlooking the waves, creating a quiet sanctuary along the otherwise bustling and dry Barrens coast.",al={"what is tidus stair","tidus stair overview","tidus stair lore"},it="place",add="95879c45"},{q="Is Tidus Stair dangerous?",a="The stair itself is a calm haven, shielded from the immediate perils of the open plains. However, the surrounding Merchant Coast is often prowled by coastal wildlife and dangerous pirates from the nearby Southsea holdouts, so travelers should remain vigilant while making the trek south along the shore.",al={"is tidus stair safe","danger at tidus stair","tidus stair threats"},it="danger",add="4cc68021"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a Horde shaman, you eventually journey down these coastal steps to seek Islen Waterseer during your trials to bind the water totem.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see in Islen Waterseer and Mahren Skyseer how tauren seers keep a spiritual vigil far beyond Mulgore's borders."},kw={"barrens","islen waterseer","mahren skyseer","merchant coast","ratchet","tidus stair","water totem"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","quest:874","subzone:merchant-coast","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},src={"Tidus Stair"}}
E["subzone:wailing-caverns"] = {t="subzone",n="Wailing Caverns",z="barrens",s="Steam wails through the bluffs above Lushwater Oasis, where the Wailing Caverns twist beneath the Barrens. Naralex, a night elf druid, entered the springs hoping to restore life to the arid plains, but mutations and agitated wildlife now haunt the caverns.",h="Steam wails through the bluffs above Lushwater Oasis, where the Wailing Caverns twist beneath the Barrens.",sec={{t="The Druids of the Fang",b="Naralex's sleeping followers guard him in the Wailing Caverns. His closest disciples were driven mad by the Emerald Nightmare and abandoned their old traditions. Under leaders such as Lady Anacondra, they formed the Druids of the Fang and took on venomous snake aspects. They defend their master from anyone who might break his trance. The waterways now threaten to poison oases across the Barrens. Cenarion Circle allies in Thunder Bluff are concerned, while goblins in Ratchet see an opportunity.",sp=1,bt={"q886.5","q886.6"}},{t="The Dream Curdled",b="Steam bursts from underground geysers and escapes through cracks in the rock, sending mournful wails through the caverns. The night elf druid Naralex entered these deep waterways with his faithful followers. He hoped to draw on the subterranean springs and channel the Emerald Dream, bringing bloom to the barren savannas. Instead, the Emerald Nightmare trapped his consciousness. Corruption seeps from the sleeping druid, warping the springs and changing local beasts into deviate horrors.",sp=1,bt={"q886.5"}}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Wailing Caverns?",a="The Wailing Caverns take their name from shrieks of steam bursting through narrow cracks in the rock ceiling. The cries echo through the stone chambers.",al={"why wailing","wailing caverns name meaning","why does it wail"},it="name"},{q="Who is Naralex and why is he sleeping here?",a="Naralex is a night elf druid who sought to turn the Barrens into lush woodland by joining its underground springs to the Emerald Dream. The Emerald Nightmare overwhelmed him in trance, and corruption now flows through him.",al={"who is naralex","sleeping druid","why is naralex asleep"},sp=1,it="purpose",bt={"q886.5"}},{q="What are the Druids of the Fang?",a="The Druids of the Fang are Naralex's former disciples, driven mad by the Emerald Nightmare while he slept. They took on serpent aspects, defend the corrupted caverns, and seek to spread their warped vision of nature.",al={"druids of the fang lore","who are the fang druids","snake druids"},sp=1,it="residents",bt={"q886.5","q886.6"}},{q="Why are the beasts inside called 'deviate'?",a="Naralex's corruption has tainted the springs, changing ordinary raptors, crocolisks, and vipers into deviate forms. Their strange coloring, heightened aggression, and unusual scales and hides mark the change.",al={"deviate beasts","what is a deviate","why deviate"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What is Wailing Caverns?",a="The Wailing Caverns are a subterranean network of waterways and grottos nestled within the Lushwater Oasis in the Barrens. Its underground rivers feed the oases that dot the arid plains above. Once a natural wonder of mist and rushing subterranean currents, it has become an epicenter of rampant corruption spreading throughout the heart of the savannah.",al={"what is wailing caverns","wailing caverns overview","about wailing caverns"},it="place",add="0897dbe4"},{q="What happened at Wailing Caverns?",a="The night elf druid Naralex brought his followers into these caverns with a grand ambition: to tap into the subterranean waters and channel the Emerald Dream, restoring lush fertility to the Barrens. Instead, his slumber was snared by the Emerald Nightmare. The dark corruption seeped from his dreaming mind into the underground springs, warping the local wildlife and driving his acolytes mad.",al={"history of wailing caverns","what happened in wailing caverns","wailing caverns lore"},it="history",add="2a1640a8"},{q="Is Wailing Caverns dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The waters within are infested with mutated, aggressive beasts, including venomous deviate serpents, mutated raptors, and ravenous crocolisks. Beyond the beasts lurk the Druids of the Fang, who attack any trespassers on sight, channeling nightmarish energies to protect the trapped, slumbering master whose dreams fuel the corruption.",al={"how dangerous is wailing caverns","is it safe in wailing caverns","threats in wailing caverns"},it="danger",add="fdd3771a"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid, the Wailing Caverns show how good intentions can be corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare. Naralex must be awakened, or his twisted disciples put to rest.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the tainted waters threaten the fragile oases that sustain life and travel across the Barrens. Cleansing the caves is urgent for the safety of nearby settlements."},kw={"barrens","cavern of mists","deviate","druids of the fang","emerald nightmare","lushwater oasis","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","subzone:lushwater-oasis","npc:lady-anacondra","npc:mutanus-the-devourer","quest:914","zone:barrens"},src={"Wailing Caverns"}}
E["zone:barrens"] = {t="zone",n="The Barrens",z="barrens",s="Across The Barrens, Horde outposts hold the roads while rival forces press in from every side. Once a forest before the Great Sundering, the central Kalimdor plain is now dry country of red dust, scrub, and wandering wildlife. The Crossroads anchors Horde traffic, but quilboar, centaur, and creeping corruption threaten its hold.",h="Across The Barrens, Horde outposts hold the roads while rival forces press in from every side.",sec={{t="Heart of the New Horde",b="For generations, tauren nomads hunted kodo and zhevra across the plains and fought a repeating defensive war against Kolkar centaur. During the Third War, Thrall led the orcs to Kalimdor and helped Cairne Bloodhoof drive back the centaur and cross the savanna into Mulgore. The Barrens now links Durotar, Mulgore, and Ashenvale. The Crossroads and Camp Taurajo guard trade along the Gold Road, while orcish homesteads endure the harsh climate as they build a lasting home.",sp=0},{t="A Land Under Siege",b="Horde control of the savanna remains contested. Razormane quilboar, with their porcupine-like bristles, raid farms and supply lines from thorn-choked strongholds. Razorfen Kraul's dens loom to the south. On the eastern coast, Theramore forces hold Northwatch Hold, while dwarven prospectors dig into the titan complex of Bael Modan. Ratchet's goblins keep an uneasy neutrality in trade, welcoming travelers who bring coin.",sp=0},{t="The Emerald Corruption",b="Several oases break up the northern plains, their waters surging with unnatural vigor. The source lies in the Wailing Caverns, where the night elf druid Naralex tried to reach the Emerald Dream and restore the Barrens to its ancient forested state. A nightmare twisted his vision. Now corrupted water flows through the Forgotten Pools and Stagnant Oasis, giving rise to strange deviate plants, unnatural beasts, and the rogue Druids of the Fang.",sp=1,bt={"q886.5","q886.6"}}},faq={{q="Why are there lush oases in the middle of a desert?",a="The Forgotten Pools and Lushwater Oasis draw water from underground springs flowing out of the Wailing Caverns. The night elf druid Naralex tried to channel the springs through the Emerald Dream and green the dry land, but the effort went awry, filling the northern Barrens with potent, volatile natural magic.",al={"barrens oases","why is there water in barrens","wailing caverns water"},sp=1,it="place",bt={"q886.5"}},{q="Who controls the Crossroads?",a="The Horde garrisons the Crossroads, chiefly with orc and tauren warriors who serve Warchief Thrall. Its place where the main trade routes meet makes it the Horde's chief military and transit hub in central Kalimdor, linking Durotar, Mulgore, and Ashenvale.",al={"who runs crossroads","crossroads horde","crossroads guards"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are the quilboar attacking everyone?",a="The quilboar claim the Barrens as their ancestral birthright. They believe its great brambles grew from the blood of their demigod, Agamaggan, during the War of the Ancients. They see the arriving Horde and native tauren as trespassers taking their sacred foraging grounds and hunting territory.",al={"quilboar lore","why quilboar aggressive","razormane motive"},it="threat"},{q="Why are Alliance soldiers in the Barrens?",a="The Alliance holds to the savanna's edges. Human troops from Theramore garrison Northwatch Hold to watch Horde movements, while dwarves at Bael Modan and Bael'dun Keep dig for ancient titan artifacts buried in the southern hills.",al={"northwatch hold alliance","bael modan dwarves","alliance in barrens"},it="conflict"},{q="Is Ratchet part of the Horde?",a="No. Ratchet is an independent goblin port run by Gazlowe. It welcomes Horde and Alliance travelers, smugglers, and adventurers for maritime trade, so long as they respect goblin commerce and keep weapons sheathed in town.",al={"is ratchet horde","ratchet faction","gazlowe ratchet"},it="side"},{q="What is going on with the silithid in the south?",a="Silithid, insect-like creatures, have emerged from earthen hives in the southern Barrens, especially around the Field of Giants. Their sudden arrival and fast-growing colonies threaten travelers and nearby outposts, and the Horde is investigating their origins.",al={"barrens bugs","field of giants bugs","silithid south barrens"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Barrens?",a="The Barrens is a vast, sun-scorched savanna dominating central Kalimdor. Bound by low mountains, it forms the territorial heartland of the Horde, linking Durotar, Mulgore, Ashenvale, and regions south. While mostly arid plains and dry grasslands, it is dotted with occasional oases fed by underground waters, as well as sprawling trade routes that connect distant settlements.",al={"what is the barrens","barrens zone","tell me about the barrens"},it="place",add="08031609",nx={8,9}},{q="Why is the Barrens so dry and empty?",a="Long ago, this expanse was a lush, verdant forest tended by the night elves. Ten thousand years ago, the catastrophic devastation of the Great Sundering and the wars surrounding the Burning Legion tore the woodlands apart. Disasters and fires ravaged the landscape, stripping away its rich soil and leaving behind the arid, sun-baked plains seen today.",al={"why is it barren","why is it dry and empty","barrens origin"},it="history",add="d0091816"},{q="Who lives in the Barrens?",a="For generations, nomadic tauren tribes were the primary inhabitants, roaming alongside kodo and zhevra. Today, the Horde maintains major settlements like the Crossroads and Camp Taurajo, alongside scattered orc farming families. The wild plains are also populated by hostile quilboar tribes, Kolkar centaur clans, harpies, neutral goblins in Ratchet, and dwarven archaeological expeditions.",al={"who lives here","barrens inhabitants","who lives in the barrens"},it="residents",add="d67a8142"},{q="Is the Barrens dangerous?",a="Extremely so. Aside from ferocious native predators like raptors and thunder lizards, travelers face relentless raids from Razormane and Bristleback quilboar defending their thorned dens. Marauding Kolkar centaur and vicious harpies ambush travelers along the ridges, while Alliance forces and armed dwarven digs fiercely contest Horde territory in the south.",al={"is the barrens dangerous","threats in the barrens","barrens danger"},it="danger",add="8675aa57"},{q="Why did the Horde send me to the Crossroads?",a="The Crossroads is the central staging ground for all Horde operations in central Kalimdor. Adventurers arriving from Durotar or Mulgore are directed here to support supply lines, defend vulnerable outposts from aggressive local tribes, and establish a firm military presence across the vast wilderness.",al={"why send me to crossroads","why am i at the crossroads","crossroads purpose"},it="arrival",add="ba0a3e81"},{q="What is the Crossroads for?",a="It serves as the bustling commercial and logistical nexus of the Barrens. Situated squarely at the intersection of the north-south Gold Road and the east-west route between Ratchet and the Stonetalon Mountains, it provides vital trade stalls, wyvern flight routes, and defensive barracks connecting nearly every Horde outpost on the continent.",al={"what is the crossroads","what is crossroads for","purpose of crossroads"},it="place",add="2ec69a3c",nx={13}},{q="Who built the Crossroads?",a="The Horde established the outpost following the Third War. As Thrall led the orcs and Darkspear trolls to build Durotar and secure central Kalimdor, they erected the settlement at the convergence of ancient trade routes to anchor their supply chains and defend against roaming centaur and quilboar.",al={"who built crossroads","crossroads origin","how was crossroads built"},it="history",add="23c4dfc8"},{q="Who are the centaur and why do they hate us?",a="The centaur are aggressive, four-legged marauders that have clashed with the tauren across these plains for generations. Tribes like the local Kolkar view other races as intruders or prey to be hunted for sport. Their ancestral blood feuds with the tauren ensure constant bloodshed wherever their raiding parties encounter the Horde.",al={"why do centaur hate us","who are the centaur","centaur threat"},it="threat",add="e472d007"},{q="What are the harpies doing out here?",a="Vicious avian humanoids nest along the northern ridges and canyons of the Barrens. They strike without warning, scavenging carrion and ambushing passing caravans along the roads. Under leaders like Serena Bloodfeather, their organized raids represent a persistent threat to Horde supply lines traversing northern passes.",al={"harpies barrens","why are harpies here","barrens harpies"},it="threat",add="e2564dbf"},{q="Who are the dwarves at Bael Modan and what are they digging for?",a="They are an expedition from Ironforge operating under General Twinbraid, fortified inside Bael'dun Keep. They are excavating a buried titan research complex deep beneath the earth, seeking ancient relics and historical knowledge. Their extensive use of blasting powder and machinery displaced the native Stonespire tauren.",al={"bael modan dwarves","what are dwarves digging for","bael modan digsite"},it="threat",add="909ebb4b",nx={17}},{q="Why is Gann Stonespire so angry at the dwarves?",a="Bael Modan was constructed directly over ancestral land that the Stonespire tauren held sacred. When the dwarves arrived, they drove off or slaughtered the tribe and tore apart the village with heavy excavation machines. After diplomatic attempts completely failed, Gann dedicated himself to taking bloody vengeance against the digsite.",al={"gann stonespire mad","why does gann hate dwarves","gann stonespire revenge"},it="conflict",add="52bcea79"},{q="What's Ratchet and why are goblins neutral?",a="Ratchet is a bustling harbor town on the Merchant Coast founded by Gazlowe following his engineering work in Orgrimmar. The Steamwheedle Cartel runs the port strictly for commerce and maritime trade with places like Booty Bay. They maintain neutrality to profit off trade with everyone, welcoming both Horde and Alliance travelers so long as gold flows.",al={"what is ratchet","why are ratchet goblins neutral","ratchet goblins"},it="place",add="918bbb4f"},{q="Where does all this lead after the Barrens?",a="The Barrens acts as the crossroads for all Kalimdor. Trails to the north climb through the Mor'shan Rampart into the dense, contested forests of Ashenvale. Mountain passes to the west wind toward the Stonetalon Mountains, while the Southern Gold Road leads past Camp Taurajo toward the swamplands of Dustwallow Marsh and the towering bluffs of Thousand Needles.",al={"where to go after barrens","next zone after barrens","what comes after barrens"},it="next_step",add="50dbd02f",nx={20}},{q="What's south past Camp Taurajo?",a="Heading south down the Gold Road brings you past the massive dwarven fortifications of Bael Modan and into the disputed borderlands. Further south lie the thorned fortresses of Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs, followed by the Great Lift that descends into the canyons of Thousand Needles.",al={"south of camp taurajo","what is south of taurajo","past camp taurajo"},it="place",add="06412399"},{q="How did I end up in The Barrens?",a="You followed the natural roads leading out of your people's homelands. Orcs and Darkspear trolls crossed westward out of Durotar, passing the Far Watch Post across the Southfury River. Tauren ventured east through the mountain pass from Mulgore, arriving first at Camp Taurajo. Travelers from further lands, including the Forsaken and rare Alliance interlopers, often arrive by sea through the goblin port of Ratchet. However you arrived, the vast savanna opens before you at the heart of central Kalimdor.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to the barrens","why am i in the barrens"},it="arrival",add="9b9beaa0"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in The Barrens?",a="As a member of the Horde, you are here to secure and tame this sprawling frontier. Orcs and tauren have established settlements like the Crossroads and Camp Taurajo, but they are constantly besieged. You are tasked with driving back aggressive Razormane and Bristleback quilboar, battling centaur marauders, and investigating the bizarre, corrupted life springing up around the desert oases. You must also keep watch against encroaching Alliance outposts at Northwatch Hold and Bael Modan to keep the heartland safe.",al={"what do i do here","what is my goal in the barrens","what am i doing here"},it="purpose",add="f4aa7870"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Barrens is your realm's supply road. Holding the Crossroads and guarding convoys along the Gold Road help Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff endure.",["race:Tauren"]="Your nomadic ancestors roamed these savannas for generations before the orcs reached Kalimdor. They hunted sacred game and struggled to survive against the ruthless Kolkar centaur.",["class:Druid"]="The altered waters from the Wailing Caverns mark a tragedy: Naralex's attempt to restore the Barrens fell to a nightmare.",["class:Shaman"]="These dry plains test your bond with the elements, from the spirits of the parched earth to the enchanted waters bubbling up in isolated oases."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","gold road","kolkar","naralex","quilboar","ratchet","taurajo","wailing caverns"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:wailing","subzone:ratchet","subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:gold-road","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:bael-modan","npc:naralex"},m={levels="10-25"},src={"Barrens"}}
